window.L4_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"abandon – adopt","cards":[{"w":"abandon","p":"v.","d":"to leave a person, place, or thing and never come back","c":"放棄；遺棄","s":"When the river rose quickly during the typhoon, the villagers had to abandon their homes and run to higher ground.","t":"颱風期間河水迅速上漲時，村民們不得不放棄家園，跑到較高的地方。","h":1},{"w":"abandoned","p":"adj.","d":"left behind and no longer used or cared for","c":"被遺棄的；廢棄的","s":"The children found an abandoned house at the end of the street, and nobody had lived there for twenty years.","t":"孩子們在街尾發現一間廢棄的房子，已經二十年沒有人住在那裡了。"},{"w":"abandon a plan","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop a plan and not do it anymore","c":"放棄計畫","s":"Because the weather report said heavy rain was coming, we decided to abandon our plan to climb the mountain this weekend.","t":"因為氣象報告說大雨即將來臨，我們決定放棄這個週末爬山的計畫。","a":"abandon our plan"},{"w":"abandonment","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving someone or something behind","c":"遺棄；放棄","s":"The abandonment of pets is a serious problem in big cities, so the government now fines owners who leave animals on the street.","t":"遺棄寵物在大城市是個嚴重的問題，所以政府現在會對把動物丟在街上的飼主開罰。"},{"w":"absolute","p":"adj.","d":"complete and total; without any limit","c":"絕對的；完全的","s":"The teacher asked for absolute silence during the listening test, so even the sound of a pencil seemed very loud.","t":"老師要求聽力測驗期間要絕對安靜，所以連鉛筆的聲音都顯得很大。","h":1},{"w":"absolutely","p":"adv.","d":"completely; used to agree strongly","c":"絕對地；完全地","s":"You are absolutely right about the schedule, and I think we should tell the rest of the team as soon as possible.","t":"關於時間表你完全正確，我認為我們應該儘快告訴團隊其他人。"},{"w":"absolutely not","p":"phr.","d":"a strong way to say no","c":"絕對不行","s":"When my little brother asked if he could ride his bike on the highway, my father said, \"Absolutely not, it is far too dangerous.\"","t":"當我弟弟問他能不能在高速公路上騎腳踏車時，我爸爸說：「絕對不行，那太危險了。」","a":"Absolutely not"},{"w":"absorb","p":"v.","d":"to take in a liquid, heat, or information","c":"吸收","s":"Plants absorb water through their roots, and that is why you should water the soil instead of the leaves.","t":"植物透過根部吸收水分，這就是為什麼你應該澆土壤而不是澆葉子。","h":1},{"w":"be absorbed in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give all your attention to something","c":"專注於；沉浸於","s":"My sister was absorbed in her new novel last night, so she did not even hear the phone ring three times.","t":"我姐姐昨晚沉浸在她的新小說裡，所以連電話響了三次她都沒聽到。","a":"was absorbed in"},{"w":"absorbent","p":"adj.","d":"able to take in liquid easily","c":"吸水的","s":"This towel is very absorbent, so it dries your hair much faster than the thin one we used before.","t":"這條毛巾非常吸水，所以它比我們以前用的那條薄毛巾更快把你的頭髮弄乾。"},{"w":"absorption","p":"n.","d":"the process of taking something in","c":"吸收","s":"Eating vegetables with a little oil helps the absorption of some vitamins, which is good news for people who love salad.","t":"吃蔬菜時加一點油有助於某些維生素的吸收，對愛吃沙拉的人來說是好消息。"},{"w":"abstract","p":"adj.","d":"based on ideas, not on real things you can see or touch","c":"抽象的","s":"Words like \"freedom\" and \"happiness\" are abstract, so it is often hard for young children to understand them.","t":"像「自由」和「快樂」這樣的字是抽象的，所以年幼的孩子常常很難理解它們。","h":1},{"w":"abstract","p":"n.","d":"a short summary of an article or report","c":"摘要","s":"Before you read the whole report, look at the abstract on the first page because it tells you the main findings.","t":"在你閱讀整份報告之前，先看第一頁的摘要，因為它會告訴你主要的發現。"},{"w":"abstract art","p":"n.phr.","d":"art that uses shapes and colors, not real objects","c":"抽象藝術","s":"Many visitors say they do not understand abstract art, but the museum guide explained that the colors show the artist's feelings.","t":"許多參觀者說他們不懂抽象藝術，但博物館導覽員解釋說那些顏色表現了藝術家的感受。"},{"w":"abstraction","p":"n.","d":"a general idea that is not about one real thing","c":"抽象概念","s":"To a hungry child, \"the economy\" is just an abstraction, but the price of a lunch box is something very real.","t":"對一個飢餓的孩子來說，「經濟」只是個抽象概念，但便當的價格卻非常真實。"},{"w":"academic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with studying, schools, and universities","c":"學術的；學業的","s":"Her academic results improved a lot this year because she started studying with a group of friends every weekend.","t":"她今年的學業成績進步很多，因為她開始每個週末和一群朋友一起讀書。","h":1},{"w":"academic year","p":"n.phr.","d":"the school year, usually from September to June","c":"學年","s":"The new academic year begins in September, so students have about two months to rest and travel before classes start.","t":"新的學年從九月開始，所以學生在開學前有大約兩個月可以休息和旅行。"},{"w":"academy","p":"n.","d":"a school or college for special training","c":"學院；專科學校","s":"After high school, my cousin joined a music academy in Taipei, where he practices the violin for six hours every day.","t":"高中畢業後，我表哥進入台北的一所音樂學院，他每天在那裡練六小時小提琴。"},{"w":"academically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with study","c":"在學業上","s":"Although Tom is not strong at sports, he does very well academically and always gets the top grade in math.","t":"雖然湯姆運動不強，但他在學業上表現很好，數學總是拿最高分。"},{"w":"accent","p":"n.","d":"the way people from a place or country say words","c":"口音","s":"You can tell that the new teacher is from Australia because she speaks English with a strong accent.","t":"你可以聽出新老師來自澳洲，因為她說英文帶著濃厚的口音。","h":1},{"w":"accent","p":"n.","d":"the stress put on one part of a word","c":"重音","s":"In the word \"banana,\" the accent is on the second syllable, so you should say it a little louder than the others.","t":"在 banana 這個字裡，重音在第二個音節，所以你應該把它說得比其他音節大聲一點。"},{"w":"have a strong accent","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak in a way that clearly shows where you are from","c":"口音很重","s":"My grandfather has a strong accent because he grew up in the countryside, but everyone in the family understands him perfectly.","t":"我爺爺口音很重，因為他在鄉下長大，但家裡每個人都完全聽得懂他說的話。","a":"has a strong accent"},{"w":"acceptance","p":"n.","d":"the act of agreeing to take or receive something","c":"接受；錄取","s":"Her acceptance letter from the university arrived this morning, and the whole family cheered when she opened it.","t":"她大學的錄取通知今天早上寄到了，當她打開信時全家人都歡呼起來。","h":1},{"w":"accept","p":"v.","d":"to say yes to an offer or take something that is given","c":"接受","s":"I was happy to accept the invitation to her birthday party because we had not seen each other for a year.","t":"我很高興接受她生日派對的邀請，因為我們已經一年沒見面了。"},{"w":"acceptable","p":"adj.","d":"good enough to be allowed or agreed to","c":"可接受的","s":"Wearing jeans is acceptable at our office on Fridays, but on other days we have to wear more formal clothes.","t":"在我們辦公室，星期五穿牛仔褲是可接受的，但其他日子我們必須穿比較正式的衣服。"},{"w":"unacceptable","p":"adj.","d":"so bad that it cannot be allowed","c":"無法接受的","s":"Arriving thirty minutes late without calling is unacceptable, so the manager asked him to explain what had happened.","t":"沒有打電話就遲到三十分鐘是無法接受的，所以經理要他解釋發生了什麼事。"},{"w":"accept an offer","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say yes to a job or a deal someone offers you","c":"接受提議／工作邀約","s":"After thinking about it for a week, she decided to accept the offer from the company in Taichung because the pay was better.","t":"考慮了一週後，她決定接受台中那家公司的工作邀約，因為薪水比較好。","a":"accept the offer"},{"w":"access","p":"n.","d":"the right or chance to use, enter, or see something","c":"使用權；進入；通道","s":"Students need a library card to get access to the computer room, which is open until nine every evening.","t":"學生需要借書證才能進入電腦教室，那裡每天晚上開放到九點。","h":1},{"w":"gain access to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get the right or a way to enter or use something","c":"取得使用／進入權","s":"The thief tried to gain access to the building at night, but the new security camera recorded everything he did.","t":"小偷試圖在夜裡進入那棟大樓，但新的監視器錄下了他做的每件事。"},{"w":"have access to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be able to use or get something","c":"能夠使用／取得","s":"In many poor villages, children do not have access to clean water, so they often get sick after drinking from the river.","t":"在許多貧窮的村莊，孩子們無法取得乾淨的水，所以喝了河水後常常生病。"},{"w":"access","p":"v.","d":"to open or use information, especially on a computer","c":"存取；使用","s":"You can access your test results online by typing your student number and password on the school website.","t":"你可以在學校網站輸入學號和密碼，在線上查看你的考試成績。"},{"w":"accessible","p":"adj.","d":"easy to reach, enter, or use","c":"容易到達的；無障礙的","s":"The new MRT station is accessible to people in wheelchairs because there are elevators at every exit.","t":"新的捷運站對坐輪椅的人來說很方便進出，因為每個出口都有電梯。"},{"w":"inaccessible","p":"adj.","d":"very hard or impossible to reach or use","c":"難以到達的；無法使用的","s":"The small temple on the mountain is inaccessible in winter, since snow and ice cover the only road that leads there.","t":"山上的小寺廟在冬天難以到達，因為冰雪覆蓋了通往那裡唯一的道路。"},{"w":"accidental","p":"adj.","d":"happening by chance, not planned","c":"偶然的；意外的","s":"The fire was accidental, and the police believe it started when someone forgot to turn off the stove.","t":"這場火災是意外的，警方認為是有人忘了關爐火才引起的。","h":1},{"w":"accidentally","p":"adv.","d":"by chance; without meaning to","c":"不小心地；偶然地","s":"I accidentally deleted all the photos from our trip, so now I have to ask my friends to send me their copies.","t":"我不小心刪掉了我們旅行的所有照片，所以現在我得請朋友把他們的照片傳給我。"},{"w":"accident","p":"n.","d":"something bad that happens by chance, like a car crash","c":"意外；事故","s":"There was a serious car accident on the highway this morning, and the traffic was stopped for almost two hours.","t":"今天早上高速公路上發生了一起嚴重的車禍，交通停滯了將近兩個小時。"},{"w":"by accident","p":"phr.","d":"by chance, not on purpose","c":"偶然地；無意中","s":"We met our old English teacher by accident at the night market, and she still remembered all of our names.","t":"我們在夜市偶然遇到以前的英文老師，她還記得我們每個人的名字。"},{"w":"accompany","p":"v.","d":"to go somewhere with someone","c":"陪伴；陪同","s":"My mother asked me to accompany my grandmother to the hospital because she does not feel comfortable going alone.","t":"我媽媽要我陪奶奶去醫院，因為她一個人去會不安心。","h":1},{"w":"be accompanied by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have someone or something go together with you","c":"由…陪同；伴隨著","s":"Children under twelve must be accompanied by an adult when they swim in this pool, even if they can swim well.","t":"十二歲以下的兒童在這個泳池游泳時必須由成人陪同，即使他們會游泳。"},{"w":"accompaniment","p":"n.","d":"music played to support a singer; something served with food","c":"伴奏；配菜","s":"She sang the song beautifully with a simple piano accompaniment, and the audience stood up to clap at the end.","t":"她在簡單的鋼琴伴奏下把這首歌唱得很美，最後觀眾都起立鼓掌。"},{"w":"keep sb company","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay with someone so they are not alone","c":"陪伴某人","s":"My dog always keeps me company while I do my homework, and he sleeps next to my desk until I finish.","t":"我做功課時我的狗總是陪著我，牠睡在我桌子旁邊直到我做完。","a":"keeps me company"},{"w":"accomplish","p":"v.","d":"to finish something successfully","c":"完成；達成","s":"If we work together as a team and plan carefully, we can accomplish this project before the end of the month.","t":"如果我們團隊合作並仔細規劃，就能在月底前完成這個專案。","h":1},{"w":"accomplishment","p":"n.","d":"something difficult that you have done successfully","c":"成就","s":"Finishing a full marathon at the age of sixty is a great accomplishment, and my uncle is very proud of it.","t":"六十歲跑完全程馬拉松是一項了不起的成就，我叔叔對此感到非常自豪。"},{"w":"a sense of accomplishment","p":"n.phr.","d":"the good feeling you have after finishing something hard","c":"成就感","s":"After she fixed the old bicycle by herself, she felt a sense of accomplishment that no new toy could ever give her.","t":"她自己修好那台舊腳踏車之後，感受到任何新玩具都無法給她的成就感。"},{"w":"accomplished","p":"adj.","d":"very skilled at something","c":"有造詣的；技藝精湛的","s":"My aunt is an accomplished pianist who has played in concerts in Japan, Korea, and several European countries.","t":"我阿姨是一位技藝精湛的鋼琴家，曾在日本、韓國和幾個歐洲國家演出。"},{"w":"accountant","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to keep and check money records","c":"會計師","s":"My father works as an accountant for a large company, so he is always very busy at the end of the year.","t":"我爸爸在一家大公司當會計師，所以每到年底他總是非常忙碌。","h":1},{"w":"account","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement with a bank to keep your money","c":"帳戶","s":"I opened a bank account when I started my part-time job, and now I save a little money every month.","t":"我開始打工時開了一個銀行帳戶，現在我每個月都存一點錢。"},{"w":"account for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to explain the reason for something; to make up a part of","c":"說明…的原因；佔…比例","s":"Heavy rain and strong wind accounted for most of the delays at the airport last week, according to the news report.","t":"根據新聞報導，上週機場大多數的延誤都是大雨和強風造成的。","a":"accounted for"},{"w":"take ... into account","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think about something when making a decision","c":"考慮到；把…納入考量","s":"When you choose a university, you should take into account the cost of living in that city, not just the school's name.","t":"選大學時，你應該考慮到那個城市的生活費，而不只是學校的名氣。","a":"take into account"},{"w":"accounting","p":"n.","d":"the job or study of keeping money records","c":"會計學；會計","s":"She is studying accounting at university because she is good with numbers and wants a stable job after graduation.","t":"她在大學讀會計，因為她擅長數字，而且想在畢業後有份穩定的工作。"},{"w":"accuracy","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being correct and exact","c":"準確性；精確度","s":"The weather app is popular because of its accuracy; it told us the rain would stop at three, and it did.","t":"這個天氣 App 因為它的準確性而受歡迎；它說雨會在三點停，結果真的停了。","h":1},{"w":"accurate","p":"adj.","d":"correct and exact in every detail","c":"準確的；精確的","s":"Please make sure the address on the package is accurate, or the gift may be sent to the wrong house.","t":"請確認包裹上的地址是正確的，否則禮物可能會被送到錯的房子。"},{"w":"accurately","p":"adv.","d":"in a correct and exact way","c":"準確地","s":"The new machine can measure your height and weight accurately in less than ten seconds without any help from a nurse.","t":"這台新機器可以在十秒內準確地測量你的身高和體重，不需要護士幫忙。"},{"w":"inaccurate","p":"adj.","d":"not correct or exact","c":"不準確的","s":"The old map was inaccurate because several new roads had been built after it was printed ten years ago.","t":"那張舊地圖不準確，因為它十年前印好後又建了幾條新路。"},{"w":"accuse","p":"v.","d":"to say that someone has done something wrong","c":"指控；控告","s":"You should not accuse your classmate of cheating unless you actually saw him copy the answers during the test.","t":"除非你真的看到同學在考試中抄答案，否則你不應該指控他作弊。","h":1},{"w":"be accused of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be blamed for doing something wrong","c":"被指控…","s":"The shop owner was accused of selling fake brand-name bags, so the police came to check every item in his store.","t":"那位店主被指控販賣假名牌包，所以警察來檢查他店裡的每一件商品。","a":"was accused of"},{"w":"accusation","p":"n.","d":"a statement that someone has done something wrong","c":"指控；控訴","s":"The player strongly denied the accusation that he had taken drugs before the race, and he asked for another test.","t":"那位選手強烈否認他在比賽前服用禁藥的指控，並要求再做一次檢測。"},{"w":"the accused","p":"n.","d":"the person who is on trial for a crime","c":"被告","s":"In court, the accused sat quietly beside his lawyer while the judge read the long list of charges against him.","t":"在法庭上，被告安靜地坐在律師旁邊，法官則讀出對他的一長串罪名。"},{"w":"acid","p":"n.","d":"a chemical that can burn things and tastes sour","c":"酸","s":"Be careful with that bottle in the science lab because the acid inside can burn your skin in seconds.","t":"小心理化實驗室裡的那個瓶子，因為裡面的酸幾秒鐘就能灼傷你的皮膚。","h":1},{"w":"acid","p":"adj.","d":"sour; containing acid","c":"酸的；酸性的","s":"Lemons and limes have an acid taste, which is why people add sugar when they make juice from them.","t":"檸檬和萊姆有酸味，這就是為什麼人們用它們做果汁時會加糖。"},{"w":"acid rain","p":"n.phr.","d":"rain that has chemicals from pollution in it","c":"酸雨","s":"Smoke from factories and cars causes acid rain, which slowly damages trees, rivers, and even old stone buildings.","t":"工廠和汽車排放的煙造成酸雨，它會慢慢破壞樹木、河流，甚至古老的石造建築。"},{"w":"acidic","p":"adj.","d":"containing acid; sour","c":"酸性的","s":"Soft drinks are highly acidic, so dentists warn that drinking them every day can slowly damage your teeth.","t":"汽水是高度酸性的，所以牙醫警告每天喝汽水會慢慢損害你的牙齒。"},{"w":"acquaintance","p":"n.","d":"a person you know a little but who is not a close friend","c":"熟人；認識的人","s":"He is just an acquaintance from my old job, so I was surprised when he invited me to his wedding.","t":"他只是我以前工作上的一個熟人，所以當他邀請我參加他的婚禮時，我很驚訝。","h":1},{"w":"acquaint","p":"v.","d":"to make someone know about something","c":"使認識；使熟悉","s":"The first week of the job is designed to acquaint new workers with the company rules and the people they will work with.","t":"工作的第一週是為了讓新員工熟悉公司規定以及將一起工作的同事。"},{"w":"be acquainted with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to know a person or a subject a little","c":"認識；熟悉","s":"Are you acquainted with the new manager, or would you like me to introduce you before the meeting starts?","t":"你認識新經理嗎？還是你希望我在會議開始前介紹你們認識？","a":"acquainted with"},{"w":"make sb's acquaintance","p":"v.phr.","d":"to meet someone for the first time","c":"結識某人","s":"I first made his acquaintance at a summer camp ten years ago, and we have stayed in touch ever since.","t":"我十年前在夏令營第一次結識他，從那時起我們就一直保持聯絡。","a":"made his acquaintance"},{"w":"acquire","p":"v.","d":"to get or buy something; to learn a skill","c":"獲得；取得；學會","s":"Children acquire language quickly when they hear it every day, which is why many families speak two languages at home.","t":"孩子每天聽到語言時會很快學會，這就是為什麼許多家庭在家裡說兩種語言。","h":1},{"w":"acquisition","p":"n.","d":"the act of getting something; something you have got","c":"獲得；收購；取得物","s":"The acquisition of the small company by the big one was announced on the news, and many workers worried about their jobs.","t":"大公司收購小公司的消息在新聞上公布了，許多員工擔心自己的工作。"},{"w":"acquire a skill","p":"v.phr.","d":"to learn how to do something well","c":"學會一項技能","s":"It takes years of practice to acquire a skill like playing the piano, so do not give up after only one month.","t":"要學會一項技能，像是彈鋼琴，需要多年的練習，所以不要才一個月就放棄。"},{"w":"adapt","p":"v.","d":"to change so that you fit a new situation","c":"適應；改編","s":"Animals that cannot adapt to a warmer climate may disappear, so scientists are watching polar bears very closely.","t":"無法適應較暖氣候的動物可能會消失，所以科學家正密切觀察北極熊。","h":1},{"w":"adapt to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get used to a new place or situation","c":"適應…","s":"It took my cousin about half a year to adapt to life in Canada, especially the long, cold winter.","t":"我表姐花了大約半年才適應加拿大的生活，尤其是漫長寒冷的冬天。"},{"w":"adaptation","p":"n.","d":"a film or play made from a book; the process of changing to fit","c":"改編作品；適應","s":"The movie is an adaptation of a famous novel, but many readers say the book is much better than the film.","t":"這部電影是一部著名小說的改編作品，但許多讀者說書比電影好得多。"},{"w":"adaptable","p":"adj.","d":"able to change easily to fit new situations","c":"適應力強的","s":"Employers like adaptable workers who can learn new software quickly and stay calm when plans suddenly change.","t":"雇主喜歡適應力強的員工，他們能快速學會新軟體，並在計畫突然改變時保持冷靜。"},{"w":"addict","p":"n.","d":"a person who cannot stop doing or taking something","c":"上癮的人；癮君子","s":"My brother jokes that he is a coffee addict because he cannot start his morning without at least two cups.","t":"我哥哥開玩笑說他是咖啡癮君子，因為他早上至少要喝兩杯才能開始一天。","h":1},{"w":"be addicted to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be unable to stop doing or taking something","c":"對…上癮","s":"Some teenagers are addicted to online games, so they stay up late every night and feel tired at school the next day.","t":"有些青少年對線上遊戲上癮，所以他們每晚熬夜，第二天在學校覺得很累。","a":"are addicted to"},{"w":"addiction","p":"n.","d":"the state of not being able to stop doing or taking something","c":"上癮；癮","s":"Smartphone addiction is becoming a serious problem, and some schools now ask students to lock their phones away during class.","t":"手機上癮正成為一個嚴重的問題，有些學校現在要求學生上課時把手機鎖起來。"},{"w":"addictive","p":"adj.","d":"making you want more and more of it","c":"令人上癮的","s":"This new game is so addictive that I played it for five hours yesterday without noticing the time.","t":"這款新遊戲太令人上癮了，我昨天玩了五個小時都沒注意到時間。"},{"w":"adequate","p":"adj.","d":"enough or good enough for a purpose","c":"足夠的；適當的","s":"The small apartment is adequate for one person, but it would feel very crowded if a whole family lived there.","t":"這間小公寓對一個人來說是足夠的，但如果一整家人住在那裡會覺得很擠。","h":1},{"w":"adequately","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is enough or good enough","c":"足夠地；適當地","s":"The hikers were not adequately prepared for the cold, so the rescue team had to bring them warm clothes and hot drinks.","t":"那些登山客沒有為寒冷做好足夠的準備，所以救難隊必須帶保暖衣物和熱飲給他們。"},{"w":"inadequate","p":"adj.","d":"not enough or not good enough","c":"不足的；不適當的","s":"The old school building has inadequate lighting, and students often complain that they cannot see the board clearly.","t":"舊校舍的照明不足，學生常抱怨看不清楚黑板。"},{"w":"adjust","p":"v.","d":"to change something a little so it works better","c":"調整；調節","s":"If the picture on the screen looks too dark, you can adjust the brightness by pressing the button on the side.","t":"如果螢幕上的畫面看起來太暗，你可以按側邊的按鈕來調整亮度。","h":1},{"w":"adjust to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get used to a new situation","c":"適應…","s":"After moving from a small town to Taipei, it took me several months to adjust to the noise and the fast pace of life.","t":"從小鎮搬到台北後，我花了幾個月才適應噪音和快速的生活步調。"},{"w":"adjustment","p":"n.","d":"a small change that makes something better","c":"調整；調節","s":"The dentist made a small adjustment to my braces, and now my teeth do not hurt when I eat.","t":"牙醫對我的牙套做了一點小調整，現在我吃東西時牙齒不會痛了。"},{"w":"make adjustments","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change some things a little","c":"做調整","s":"The coach had to make adjustments to the team's plan at halftime because the other side was playing much better than expected.","t":"教練在半場時必須對球隊的計畫做調整，因為對方的表現比預期好很多。"},{"w":"adjustable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be changed to fit different needs","c":"可調整的","s":"This office chair is adjustable, so both tall and short people can sit comfortably by moving the seat up or down.","t":"這張辦公椅是可調整的，所以高個子和矮個子的人都能透過上下移動座椅坐得舒服。"},{"w":"admirable","p":"adj.","d":"deserving respect and praise","c":"令人欽佩的","s":"It is admirable that the young nurse worked twelve hours a day during the outbreak without ever complaining.","t":"那位年輕護士在疫情期間每天工作十二小時卻從不抱怨，這真是令人欽佩。","h":1},{"w":"admiration","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great respect and liking","c":"欽佩；讚賞","s":"The students watched with admiration as the firefighter climbed the ladder and carried the frightened cat down safely.","t":"學生們欽佩地看著消防員爬上梯子，安全地把受驚的貓抱下來。","h":1},{"w":"admire","p":"v.","d":"to respect and like someone or something very much","c":"欽佩；欣賞","s":"I really admire my grandmother because she learned to use a smartphone at the age of eighty and now video-calls us every week.","t":"我真的很欽佩我奶奶，因為她八十歲學會用智慧型手機，現在每週都和我們視訊。"},{"w":"admirer","p":"n.","d":"a person who likes and respects someone very much","c":"欽佩者；愛慕者","s":"The famous writer has thousands of admirers around the world, and many of them wait for hours to get her signature.","t":"這位知名作家在世界各地有成千上萬的欽佩者，許多人等好幾個小時只為了她的簽名。","a":"admirers"},{"w":"admission","p":"n.","d":"the right to enter a place; the money you pay to enter","c":"入場；入場費；入學許可","s":"Admission to the museum is free on the first Sunday of every month, so the place is always crowded with families then.","t":"每個月第一個星期日博物館的入場是免費的，所以那時候總是擠滿了家庭。","a":"Admission","h":1},{"w":"admission","p":"n.","d":"a statement that something bad is true","c":"承認","s":"His quiet admission that he had broken the window surprised everyone, because we had all blamed the neighbor's kids.","t":"他默默承認是他打破窗戶，讓大家都很驚訝，因為我們都怪到鄰居的小孩身上。"},{"w":"admit","p":"v.","d":"to agree that something bad is true","c":"承認","s":"You have to admit that the new restaurant is better than the old one, even though it costs a little more.","t":"你必須承認新餐廳比舊的好，即使它貴了一點。"},{"w":"admit","p":"v.","d":"to allow someone to enter a place or school","c":"准許進入；錄取","s":"The university will admit only two hundred new students this year, so the competition is going to be very strong.","t":"這所大學今年只會錄取兩百名新生，所以競爭將會非常激烈。"},{"w":"admission fee","p":"n.phr.","d":"the money you pay to enter a place","c":"入場費","s":"The admission fee for the amusement park is 800 dollars, but children under six can enter for free.","t":"遊樂園的入場費是八百元，但六歲以下的兒童可以免費進入。"},{"w":"adopt","p":"v.","d":"to start using a new idea, plan, or method","c":"採用；採納","s":"Many schools have decided to adopt a new teaching method that lets students learn through games and group work.","t":"許多學校決定採用一種新的教學法，讓學生透過遊戲和小組活動學習。","h":1},{"w":"adopt","p":"v.","d":"to legally take a child into your family as your own","c":"收養","s":"My neighbors could not have children of their own, so they decided to adopt a baby girl from an orphanage.","t":"我的鄰居無法生育自己的孩子，所以他們決定從孤兒院收養一個女嬰。"},{"w":"adoption","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking a child into your family; the act of starting to use something","c":"收養；採用","s":"The adoption of electric buses in the city has helped make the air cleaner over the past three years.","t":"這座城市採用電動公車，在過去三年幫助空氣變得更乾淨。"},{"w":"adopted","p":"adj.","d":"taken into a family legally as their own child","c":"被收養的","s":"Although she is an adopted child, her parents have always treated her exactly the same as her two brothers.","t":"雖然她是被收養的孩子，但她的父母一直待她和她兩個哥哥完全一樣。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"agency – appreciation","cards":[{"w":"agency","p":"n.","d":"a business or office that provides a service for people","c":"機構；代辦處","s":"My parents booked our trip to Japan through a travel agency because they did not want to plan every hotel themselves.","t":"我爸媽透過旅行社訂了我們的日本之旅，因為他們不想自己規劃每一家飯店。","h":1},{"w":"agent","p":"n.","d":"a person who acts for another person or company","c":"代理人；經紀人","s":"The real estate agent showed us three apartments in one afternoon, and the last one was exactly what we wanted.","t":"那位房地產仲介一個下午帶我們看了三間公寓，最後一間正是我們想要的。","h":1},{"w":"travel agency","p":"n.phr.","d":"a company that arranges trips, tickets, and hotels for people","c":"旅行社","s":"If you book through a travel agency, they will arrange your flights and hotels, so you only need to pack your bags.","t":"如果你透過旅行社訂購，他們會安排機票和飯店，你只需要打包行李就好。"},{"w":"secret agent","p":"n.phr.","d":"a spy who works secretly for a government","c":"特務；間諜","s":"In the movie, the secret agent changed his name three times and traveled across Europe to find the stolen plans.","t":"電影裡，那位特務改了三次名字，穿越歐洲尋找被偷走的計畫書。"},{"w":"agenda","p":"n.","d":"a list of things to be discussed at a meeting","c":"議程","s":"The first item on today's agenda is the school trip, so please share your ideas about where we should go.","t":"今天議程的第一項是校外教學，所以請分享你們覺得應該去哪裡的想法。"},{"w":"aggressive","p":"adj.","d":"angry and ready to attack or argue","c":"好鬥的；有攻擊性的","s":"The dog became aggressive when a stranger walked into the yard, so the owner quickly put it on a leash.","t":"當陌生人走進院子時，那隻狗變得很有攻擊性，所以主人趕快幫牠繫上牽繩。","h":1},{"w":"aggressive","p":"adj.","d":"very determined to succeed; forceful","c":"積極進取的；強勢的","s":"The company started an aggressive advertising campaign, and its new phone was sold in every store within a month.","t":"這家公司展開了強勢的廣告活動，一個月內它的新手機在每家商店都有販售。"},{"w":"aggressively","p":"adv.","d":"in an angry or forceful way","c":"好鬥地；積極地","s":"The driver behind us honked aggressively and tried to pass on the narrow road, which frightened everyone in our car.","t":"我們後面的駕駛兇狠地按喇叭，還想在狹窄的路上超車，嚇壞了我們車上的每個人。"},{"w":"aggression","p":"n.","d":"angry or violent behavior toward others","c":"侵略；攻擊行為","s":"Teachers are trained to deal with aggression between students calmly, instead of shouting at the children who are fighting.","t":"老師受過訓練，能冷靜處理學生之間的攻擊行為，而不是對打架的孩子大吼。"},{"w":"agreeable","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant and nice; willing to agree","c":"令人愉快的；欣然同意的","s":"Our new neighbor is an agreeable old man who always says good morning and helps carry our heavy bags upstairs.","t":"我們的新鄰居是位和藹可親的老先生，總是跟我們道早安，還幫忙把重袋子搬上樓。","h":1},{"w":"agree","p":"v.","d":"to have the same opinion; to say yes","c":"同意","s":"I agree with my sister that we should give Mom a surprise party instead of just buying her a gift.","t":"我同意姐姐的看法，我們應該幫媽媽辦驚喜派對，而不是只買禮物給她。"},{"w":"agree to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say yes to a plan or request","c":"同意（做某事）","s":"After a long talk, my father finally agreed to let me go camping with my classmates during the summer vacation.","t":"經過長談後，我爸爸終於同意讓我暑假和同學去露營。","a":"agreed to"},{"w":"agreement","p":"n.","d":"a decision or promise that two sides accept","c":"協議；同意","s":"The two countries signed a trade agreement last week, so it will become cheaper to buy fruit from each other.","t":"兩國上週簽署了貿易協定，所以互相購買水果會變得比較便宜。"},{"w":"disagree","p":"v.","d":"to have a different opinion","c":"不同意","s":"My brother and I often disagree about which movie to watch, so we take turns choosing every Friday night.","t":"我和哥哥常常對看哪部電影意見不同，所以我們每個星期五晚上輪流選。"},{"w":"alcohol","p":"n.","d":"drinks such as beer and wine that can make you drunk","c":"酒；酒精","s":"In Taiwan, stores are not allowed to sell alcohol to anyone under eighteen, so the clerk asked to see my ID.","t":"在台灣，商店不能賣酒給未滿十八歲的人，所以店員要求看我的身分證。","h":1},{"w":"alcoholic","p":"adj.","d":"containing alcohol","c":"含酒精的","s":"The restaurant serves both alcoholic and non-alcoholic drinks, so children and their parents can all find something to enjoy.","t":"這家餐廳同時供應含酒精和不含酒精的飲料，所以孩子和父母都能找到喜歡的。"},{"w":"alcoholic","p":"n.","d":"a person who cannot stop drinking alcohol","c":"酗酒者","s":"His uncle was an alcoholic for many years, but he stopped drinking after his doctor warned him about his liver.","t":"他叔叔酗酒多年，但在醫生警告他肝臟的問題後就戒酒了。"},{"w":"drink alcohol","p":"v.phr.","d":"to drink beer, wine, or other strong drinks","c":"喝酒","s":"You should never drink alcohol before driving, because even one glass of wine can slow down your reaction time.","t":"開車前絕對不要喝酒，因為即使一杯葡萄酒也會讓你的反應變慢。"},{"w":"alert","p":"adj.","d":"watching carefully and ready to notice anything","c":"警覺的；機警的","s":"Lifeguards must stay alert all afternoon, because a swimmer can get into trouble in just a few seconds.","t":"救生員整個下午都必須保持警覺，因為游泳的人可能幾秒內就發生危險。","h":1},{"w":"alert","p":"v.","d":"to warn someone about a danger or problem","c":"警告；通知","s":"The smoke detector will alert the whole building if there is a fire, so everyone can leave quickly and safely.","t":"如果發生火災，煙霧偵測器會警示整棟大樓，讓大家能快速安全地離開。"},{"w":"alert","p":"n.","d":"a warning that something dangerous may happen","c":"警報","s":"The government sent a typhoon alert to every phone this morning, and all the schools were closed for the day.","t":"政府今天早上向每支手機發送了颱風警報，所有學校都停課一天。"},{"w":"on the alert","p":"phr.","d":"ready to deal with danger or problems","c":"保持警戒","s":"After several bikes were stolen, the guards at our school are on the alert for anyone who looks suspicious near the bike racks.","t":"在幾輛腳踏車被偷之後，我們學校的警衛對停車架附近任何可疑的人都保持警戒。"},{"w":"allowance","p":"n.","d":"money that parents give a child regularly","c":"零用錢","s":"My parents give me a weekly allowance of three hundred dollars, and I have to pay for my own snacks and games with it.","t":"我爸媽每週給我三百元零用錢，我得用它買自己的零食和遊戲。","h":1},{"w":"allowance","p":"n.","d":"an amount of money given for a special purpose","c":"津貼；補助","s":"The company pays a travel allowance to workers who visit customers in other cities, so they do not lose money on train tickets.","t":"公司付差旅津貼給去其他城市拜訪客戶的員工，這樣他們不會在火車票上賠錢。"},{"w":"allow","p":"v.","d":"to let someone do something","c":"允許","s":"Our teacher does not allow us to use phones in class, but we can use them during the lunch break.","t":"老師不允許我們上課用手機，但午休時可以使用。"},{"w":"be allowed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have permission to do something","c":"被允許做…","s":"Students are allowed to bring one dictionary into the exam room, but it must be a paper one, not an electronic one.","t":"學生可以帶一本字典進考場，但必須是紙本的，不能是電子的。","a":"are allowed to"},{"w":"make allowances for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be less strict because of a special situation","c":"體諒；考慮到","s":"The coach made allowances for the new player's mistakes because it was his first game with the team.","t":"教練體諒新球員的失誤，因為那是他和球隊的第一場比賽。","a":"made allowances for"},{"w":"alternative","p":"n.","d":"something you can choose instead of another thing","c":"替代方案；另一個選擇","s":"If the train is full, taking the bus is a good alternative, although the trip will take about an hour longer.","t":"如果火車客滿，搭公車是不錯的替代方案，雖然車程會多大約一小時。","h":1},{"w":"alternative","p":"adj.","d":"different from the usual way; that can be used instead","c":"替代的；另類的","s":"Because the main road was closed for repairs, the police showed drivers an alternative route through the old town.","t":"因為主要道路封閉維修，警察指引駕駛走穿過舊城區的替代路線。"},{"w":"have no alternative but to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have no other choice","c":"別無選擇只能…","s":"When the last bus left without us, we had no alternative but to walk home in the rain for forty minutes.","t":"當最後一班公車沒載到我們就開走時，我們別無選擇只能在雨中走四十分鐘回家。","a":"had no alternative but to"},{"w":"alternatively","p":"adv.","d":"used to suggest another possibility","c":"或者；要不然","s":"We can take the MRT to the museum, or alternatively, we can ride our bikes along the river, which is more fun.","t":"我們可以搭捷運去博物館，或者沿著河騎腳踏車，那樣更好玩。"},{"w":"alternate","p":"v.","d":"to happen or do one thing after another, in turns","c":"交替；輪流","s":"My grandmother likes to alternate between walking and swimming, so she goes to the pool every other day.","t":"我奶奶喜歡交替散步和游泳，所以她每隔一天去一次游泳池。"},{"w":"amateur","p":"n.","d":"a person who does something for fun, not as a job","c":"業餘愛好者","s":"Although she is only an amateur, her photos of the night market look as good as the ones in travel magazines.","t":"雖然她只是個業餘愛好者，她拍的夜市照片卻和旅遊雜誌裡的一樣好。","h":1},{"w":"amateur","p":"adj.","d":"done for pleasure, not as a job; not very skilled","c":"業餘的","s":"My uncle plays in an amateur baseball team every Sunday morning, and the whole family goes to cheer for him.","t":"我叔叔每週日早上在一支業餘棒球隊打球，全家人都會去幫他加油。"},{"w":"amateurish","p":"adj.","d":"not done well, like the work of someone without skill","c":"外行的；拙劣的","s":"The poster looked amateurish because the letters were different sizes and the picture was not in the center.","t":"那張海報看起來很外行，因為字母大小不一，圖片也沒有放在中間。"},{"w":"ambiguous","p":"adj.","d":"having more than one possible meaning; not clear","c":"模稜兩可的；含糊的","s":"The sign at the station was so ambiguous that half of the tourists walked the wrong way and missed their train.","t":"車站的指示牌含糊到一半的遊客走錯方向，錯過了火車。","h":1},{"w":"ambiguity","p":"n.","d":"the state of having more than one possible meaning","c":"模糊；歧義","s":"To avoid any ambiguity, the teacher wrote the exact date and time of the test on the board in large letters.","t":"為了避免任何模糊不清，老師用大字把考試的確切日期和時間寫在黑板上。"},{"w":"unambiguous","p":"adj.","d":"completely clear, with only one possible meaning","c":"明確的；毫不含糊的","s":"The doctor gave us an unambiguous answer: Grandpa must stop smoking today if he wants to stay healthy.","t":"醫生給了我們一個明確的答案：爺爺如果想保持健康，今天就必須戒菸。"},{"w":"ambitious","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong wish to be successful or powerful","c":"有野心的；雄心勃勃的","s":"My cousin is so ambitious that she plans to open her own restaurant before she turns twenty-five.","t":"我表姐非常有野心，她計劃在二十五歲前開自己的餐廳。","h":1},{"w":"ambitious","p":"adj.","d":"difficult and needing a lot of effort to achieve","c":"艱鉅的；宏大的","s":"Building a new library in only six months is an ambitious plan, but the mayor believes the workers can do it.","t":"只用六個月蓋一座新圖書館是個宏大的計畫，但市長相信工人們做得到。"},{"w":"ambition","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to achieve something","c":"抱負；志向","s":"Her greatest ambition is to become a doctor and work in poor villages where there are no hospitals.","t":"她最大的抱負是成為醫生，到沒有醫院的貧窮村莊工作。"},{"w":"ambitiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows a strong wish to succeed","c":"野心勃勃地","s":"The young company ambitiously promised to sell its cars in fifty countries within five years.","t":"這家年輕的公司野心勃勃地承諾五年內要在五十個國家販售它的汽車。"},{"w":"amuse","p":"v.","d":"to make someone laugh or smile","c":"逗樂；使發笑","s":"My little brother tried to amuse the baby by making funny faces, and soon the whole family was laughing too.","t":"我弟弟做鬼臉想逗寶寶笑，很快全家人也都笑了。","h":1},{"w":"amusement","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being entertained or made to laugh","c":"樂趣；娛樂","s":"To everyone's amusement, the cat jumped into the empty box and refused to come out for the rest of the party.","t":"令大家覺得好笑的是，那隻貓跳進空箱子裡，派對剩下的時間都不肯出來。"},{"w":"amusement park","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large place with rides and games for fun","c":"遊樂園","s":"We spent the whole day at the amusement park, and my sister rode the roller coaster five times without feeling sick.","t":"我們在遊樂園待了一整天，我妹妹坐了五次雲霄飛車都沒有不舒服。"},{"w":"amused","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you think something is funny","c":"覺得好笑的","s":"The teacher looked amused when she read my excuse for being late, but she still gave me extra homework.","t":"老師讀我遲到的理由時看起來覺得很好笑，但她還是多給了我功課。"},{"w":"amusing","p":"adj.","d":"funny and enjoyable","c":"有趣的；好笑的","s":"The speaker told an amusing story about his first day at work, and nobody in the room could stop laughing.","t":"講者說了一個關於他上班第一天的好笑故事，房間裡沒有人能停止大笑。"},{"w":"analysis","p":"n.","d":"a careful study of something to understand it","c":"分析","s":"After a careful analysis of the test results, the teacher found that most students had trouble with the listening part.","t":"仔細分析考試結果後，老師發現大多數學生在聽力部分有困難。","h":1},{"w":"analyze","p":"v.","d":"to study something carefully in order to understand it","c":"分析","s":"Scientists analyze the water from the river every month to make sure it is still safe for the fish and the farmers.","t":"科學家每個月分析河裡的水，以確保它對魚和農民仍然安全。","h":1},{"w":"analyst","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to study data or situations","c":"分析師","s":"My aunt works as a data analyst for a bank, and she uses computers to find out what customers like to buy.","t":"我阿姨在銀行當資料分析師，她用電腦找出顧客喜歡買什麼。"},{"w":"analytical","p":"adj.","d":"using careful thinking to understand something","c":"分析的；善於分析的","s":"Students with strong analytical skills can break a difficult math problem into small steps and solve it one by one.","t":"有強大分析能力的學生能把困難的數學題拆成小步驟，一步步解決。"},{"w":"ancestor","p":"n.","d":"a family member who lived a long time ago","c":"祖先","s":"During the Tomb Sweeping Festival, Taiwanese families clean the graves of their ancestors and offer them food and flowers.","t":"清明節時，台灣的家庭會清掃祖先的墳墓，並供上食物和鮮花。","a":"ancestors","h":1},{"w":"ancestry","p":"n.","d":"the family members who lived before you; your family origin","c":"祖籍；血統","s":"My friend is proud of his Hakka ancestry, and he is learning the language so he can talk with his grandmother.","t":"我朋友以他的客家血統為榮，他正在學客語，好跟他奶奶聊天。"},{"w":"ancestral","p":"adj.","d":"connected with your ancestors","c":"祖先的；祖傳的","s":"Every year, my father takes us back to our ancestral home in Tainan, where his grandfather built the house a century ago.","t":"每年爸爸都會帶我們回台南的祖厝，那是他祖父一個世紀前蓋的房子。"},{"w":"anniversary","p":"n.","d":"the date each year when something special happened before","c":"週年紀念日","s":"My parents celebrated their twentieth wedding anniversary at the same restaurant where they had their first date.","t":"我爸媽在他們第一次約會的那家餐廳慶祝結婚二十週年。","h":1},{"w":"wedding anniversary","p":"n.phr.","d":"the date on which a couple got married, each year","c":"結婚週年紀念日","s":"For their wedding anniversary, my grandfather bought my grandmother the same kind of flowers he gave her fifty years ago.","t":"為了結婚週年紀念日，我爺爺買了和五十年前送給奶奶一樣的花。"},{"w":"celebrate an anniversary","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something special on an anniversary","c":"慶祝週年","s":"The school will celebrate its anniversary next month, because it was built exactly one hundred years ago.","t":"學校下個月將慶祝校慶週年，因為它正好是一百年前建立的。","a":"celebrate its anniversary"},{"w":"annoy","p":"v.","d":"to make someone a little angry","c":"惹惱；使煩躁","s":"Loud phone calls on the MRT really annoy the other passengers, so please speak quietly or send a message instead.","t":"在捷運上大聲講電話真的會惹惱其他乘客，所以請小聲說話或改傳訊息。","h":1},{"w":"annoyed","p":"adj.","d":"a little angry","c":"惱怒的；生氣的","s":"My mother was annoyed because I forgot to take out the trash again, even though she had reminded me twice.","t":"我媽媽很生氣，因為我又忘了倒垃圾，即使她已經提醒我兩次了。"},{"w":"annoying","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel a little angry","c":"令人討厭的；煩人的","s":"The most annoying thing about my new neighbor is that he practices the drums at eleven o'clock every night.","t":"我新鄰居最煩人的地方是他每晚十一點練鼓。"},{"w":"annoyance","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being a little angry; something that annoys you","c":"惱怒；煩擾","s":"To my great annoyance, the printer ran out of ink just as I was printing the last page of my report.","t":"令我非常惱怒的是，我正在印報告最後一頁時，印表機沒墨水了。"},{"w":"annual","p":"adj.","d":"happening once a year","c":"每年的；年度的","s":"Our school holds its annual sports day in November, and every class practices for weeks to win the relay race.","t":"我們學校在十一月舉辦年度運動會，每個班級都練習好幾週想贏得接力賽。","h":1},{"w":"annually","p":"adv.","d":"once a year; every year","c":"每年；一年一次","s":"The famous lantern festival is held annually in a different city, and it brings millions of visitors to Taiwan.","t":"這個著名的燈會每年在不同城市舉辦，為台灣帶來數百萬遊客。"},{"w":"annual report","p":"n.phr.","d":"a report a company gives every year about its business","c":"年度報告","s":"The company's annual report showed that it sold more electric bikes this year than in the past three years combined.","t":"該公司的年度報告顯示，今年賣出的電動腳踏車比過去三年的總和還多。"},{"w":"anxiety","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry or fear about what may happen","c":"焦慮；擔憂","s":"Many students feel anxiety before a big exam, but a good night's sleep helps more than studying until midnight.","t":"許多學生在大考前感到焦慮，但睡個好覺比讀到半夜更有幫助。","h":1},{"w":"anxious","p":"adj.","d":"worried and nervous","c":"焦慮的；擔心的","s":"My mother gets anxious when I come home late without calling, so now I always send her a message.","t":"我沒打電話就晚回家時，媽媽會很擔心，所以現在我都會傳訊息給她。"},{"w":"be anxious about","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to be worried about something","c":"對…感到焦慮","s":"He is anxious about his job interview tomorrow, so he practiced answering questions in front of the mirror all evening.","t":"他對明天的工作面試感到焦慮，所以整個晚上都在鏡子前練習回答問題。","a":"is anxious about"},{"w":"anxiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a worried way","c":"焦急地","s":"The parents waited anxiously outside the operating room until the doctor came out and told them the surgery went well.","t":"父母焦急地在手術室外等候，直到醫生出來告訴他們手術很順利。"},{"w":"apology","p":"n.","d":"words that say you are sorry for something you did","c":"道歉","s":"The restaurant manager offered us an apology and a free dessert after we waited forty minutes for our food.","t":"我們等了四十分鐘才上菜之後，餐廳經理向我們道歉並送了免費甜點。","h":1},{"w":"apologize","p":"v.","d":"to say you are sorry","c":"道歉","s":"You should apologize to your sister for breaking her headphones, even if you did not do it on purpose.","t":"你應該為弄壞耳機向姐姐道歉，即使你不是故意的。"},{"w":"apologize to sb for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell someone you are sorry for something","c":"為…向某人道歉","s":"Tom apologized to Amy for missing her birthday party, and he promised to take her to the movies next weekend.","t":"湯姆為錯過生日派對向艾咪道歉，並答應下週末帶她去看電影。","a":"apologized to Amy for"},{"w":"make an apology","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say sorry formally","c":"正式道歉","s":"The airline had to make an apology to hundreds of passengers after their flights were delayed for more than six hours.","t":"在班機延誤超過六小時後，航空公司必須向數百名乘客正式道歉。"},{"w":"apparent","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see or understand; clear","c":"明顯的","s":"It was apparent from her red eyes that she had been crying, so I sat down next to her and asked what was wrong.","t":"從她泛紅的眼睛可以明顯看出她哭過，所以我坐到她旁邊問她怎麼了。","h":1},{"w":"apparently","p":"adv.","d":"it seems that; according to what you have heard","c":"顯然；據說","s":"Apparently, the concert has been moved to next Saturday, because the singer caught a bad cold during her trip.","t":"據說演唱會已經改到下週六，因為歌手在旅途中得了重感冒。","a":"Apparently"},{"w":"for no apparent reason","p":"phr.","d":"without any clear reason","c":"毫無明顯原因地","s":"The baby started crying for no apparent reason in the middle of the night, and nothing we did could make him stop.","t":"寶寶半夜毫無明顯原因地哭了起來，我們做什麼都無法讓他停下來。"},{"w":"applicant","p":"n.","d":"a person who asks for a job, a place at a school, etc.","c":"申請人","s":"More than two hundred applicants wanted the job at the new café, but the owner could only hire five of them.","t":"超過兩百名申請者想要新咖啡廳的工作，但老闆只能錄用五個人。","a":"applicants","h":1},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a written request for a job, a place at a school, etc.","c":"申請；申請書","s":"You must send your application for the summer camp before May 1, or there will be no places left for you.","t":"你必須在五月一日前寄出夏令營的申請，否則就沒有名額了。","h":1},{"w":"application","p":"n.","d":"a computer program for phones or computers; the use of something","c":"應用程式；應用","s":"This new application helps students learn English words by turning every lesson into a short game on their phones.","t":"這個新的應用程式把每一課變成手機上的小遊戲，幫助學生學英文單字。"},{"w":"apply","p":"v.","d":"to ask officially for a job, a place, etc.","c":"申請","s":"My sister plans to apply to three universities in Taipei, because she wants to stay close to our family.","t":"我姐姐計劃申請三所台北的大學，因為她想離家人近一點。"},{"w":"apply for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask officially for a job, a card, or a place","c":"申請（工作、證件等）","s":"I want to apply for a part-time job at the bookstore, since I love reading and the shop is near my house.","t":"我想申請書店的兼職工作，因為我喜歡閱讀，而且店就在我家附近。"},{"w":"applicable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be used in a particular situation","c":"適用的","s":"The student discount is applicable only on weekdays, so we have to pay full price if we go on Saturday.","t":"學生優惠只在平日適用，所以如果我們星期六去就得付全額。"},{"w":"appoint","p":"v.","d":"to choose someone for a job or position","c":"任命；指派","s":"The principal decided to appoint Ms. Lin as the new head of the English department because of her great teaching record.","t":"校長因為林老師優秀的教學紀錄，決定任命她為新的英文科主任。","h":1},{"w":"appointment","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to meet someone at a particular time","c":"預約；約會","s":"I have a dentist appointment at three o'clock tomorrow, so I will have to leave school a little early.","t":"我明天三點有牙醫預約，所以得提早一點離開學校。"},{"w":"make an appointment","p":"v.phr.","d":"to arrange a time to see someone, like a doctor","c":"預約；約時間","s":"If your tooth still hurts next week, you should make an appointment with the dentist instead of just taking more medicine.","t":"如果下週你的牙齒還在痛，你應該預約牙醫，而不是只吃更多藥。"},{"w":"appointed","p":"adj.","d":"chosen officially for a job; (of a time) agreed in advance","c":"被任命的；約定的","s":"The newly appointed manager called a meeting on her first day to learn about the problems in each department.","t":"新任命的經理在上任第一天就召開會議，了解各部門的問題。"},{"w":"appreciation","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of being thankful; understanding how good something is","c":"感激；欣賞","s":"The students made a big card to show their appreciation for everything their teacher had done for them during the year.","t":"學生們做了一張大卡片，表達對老師這一年為他們所做一切的感激。","h":1},{"w":"appreciate","p":"v.","d":"to be thankful for something; to understand the value of something","c":"感激；欣賞","s":"I really appreciate your help with my science project, because I could never have finished it alone before the deadline.","t":"我真的很感激你幫忙我的科學專題，因為我自己絕對無法在期限前完成。"},{"w":"show appreciation for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to let someone know you are thankful","c":"表達對…的感謝","s":"On Teachers' Day, we showed appreciation for our homeroom teacher by cleaning the classroom and singing her favorite song.","t":"教師節那天，我們打掃教室並唱導師最喜歡的歌，表達對她的感謝。","a":"showed appreciation for"},{"w":"appreciative","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or showing thanks","c":"感激的；讚賞的","s":"The appreciative audience clapped for five minutes after the young pianist finished her last piece.","t":"年輕鋼琴家演奏完最後一曲後，讚賞的觀眾鼓掌了五分鐘。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"appropriate – attraction","cards":[{"w":"appropriate","p":"adj.","d":"right or suitable for a particular situation","c":"合適的；適當的","s":"Shorts and sandals are not appropriate for a job interview, so my brother borrowed a suit from our father.","t":"短褲和涼鞋不適合工作面試，所以我哥哥向爸爸借了一套西裝。","h":1},{"w":"appropriately","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is suitable for the situation","c":"適當地","s":"The students dressed appropriately for the graduation ceremony, and even the boys who hate ties wore them that day.","t":"學生們為畢業典禮得體地穿著，連討厭領帶的男生那天也打了領帶。"},{"w":"inappropriate","p":"adj.","d":"not suitable or right for the situation","c":"不合適的；不恰當的","s":"Telling jokes during a funeral is inappropriate, so please stay quiet and show respect to the family.","t":"在葬禮上講笑話是不恰當的，所以請保持安靜，對家屬表示尊重。"},{"w":"be appropriate for","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to be suitable for someone or something","c":"適合…","s":"This movie is not appropriate for young children because it has many scary scenes, so parents should check the rating first.","t":"這部電影不適合幼童，因為有許多恐怖場面，所以家長應該先看分級。","a":"is not appropriate for"},{"w":"approval","p":"n.","d":"the act of agreeing that something is good or can be done","c":"贊同；批准","s":"The students need the principal's approval before they can hold a concert in the school gym next month.","t":"學生們需要校長的批准才能下個月在學校體育館舉辦音樂會。","h":1},{"w":"approve","p":"v.","d":"to officially agree to something; to think something is good","c":"核准；贊成","s":"The city council will approve the plan for the new park if enough people support it at the meeting tonight.","t":"如果今晚會議上有足夠的人支持，市議會將核准新公園的計畫。"},{"w":"approve of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think that someone or something is good or acceptable","c":"贊成；認可","s":"My parents do not approve of my plan to travel alone this summer, so I am trying to find a friend to go with me.","t":"我父母不贊成我今年夏天獨自旅行的計畫，所以我正試著找朋友一起去。"},{"w":"disapprove","p":"v.","d":"to think that something is bad or wrong","c":"不贊成；反對","s":"Although my grandmother disapproves of tattoos, she still loves my cousin and never says anything about his arm.","t":"雖然我奶奶不贊成刺青，但她還是很愛我表哥，從不對他手臂上的刺青說什麼。","a":"disapproves"},{"w":"approving","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you think something is good","c":"贊許的","s":"The coach gave the new player an approving nod after she scored her first goal in the final minute.","t":"新球員在最後一分鐘踢進第一球後，教練對她讚許地點了點頭。"},{"w":"aquarium","p":"n.","d":"a building where people can see fish and sea animals","c":"水族館","s":"On our school trip to the aquarium, we watched a diver feed the sharks while hundreds of fish swam around him.","t":"我們校外教學去水族館時，看到潛水員餵鯊魚，數百條魚在他周圍游來游去。","h":1},{"w":"aquarium","p":"n.","d":"a glass tank where fish are kept at home","c":"水族箱；魚缸","s":"My father cleans the aquarium in our living room every Sunday, and the goldfish always seem happier afterwards.","t":"我爸爸每週日清洗客廳的魚缸，之後金魚看起來總是比較快樂。"},{"w":"aquatic","p":"adj.","d":"living or happening in water","c":"水生的；水上的","s":"Frogs are aquatic animals when they are young, but as adults they can live both in water and on land.","t":"青蛙幼年時是水生動物，但成年後牠們可以同時生活在水中和陸地上。"},{"w":"arch","p":"n.","d":"a curved shape over a door, window, or bridge","c":"拱門；拱形","s":"The old stone bridge has a beautiful arch in the middle, and boats pass under it every afternoon.","t":"那座古老的石橋中間有一個美麗的拱形，每天下午都有船從它下面經過。","h":1},{"w":"arch","p":"v.","d":"to form a curved shape","c":"拱起；彎成弓形","s":"The cat will arch its back and make a loud hissing sound whenever a strange dog comes near our yard.","t":"每當陌生的狗靠近我們的院子，那隻貓就會拱起背，發出大聲的嘶嘶聲。"},{"w":"architect","p":"n.","d":"a person who designs buildings","c":"建築師","s":"The architect showed us a model of the new library, which will have a glass roof and a garden on the top floor.","t":"那位建築師給我們看新圖書館的模型，它將有玻璃屋頂和頂樓花園。"},{"w":"architecture","p":"n.","d":"the art of designing buildings; the style of a building","c":"建築學；建築風格","s":"Tourists love the architecture of the old town, where every house has red bricks and wooden windows.","t":"遊客喜愛舊城區的建築風格，那裡每棟房子都有紅磚和木窗。"},{"w":"arise, arose, arisen","p":"v.","d":"to happen or appear, especially a problem","c":"出現；發生","s":"If any problems arise during the trip, please call the office immediately so that we can help you.","t":"如果旅途中出現任何問題，請立刻打電話到辦公室，這樣我們才能幫助你。","a":"arise","h":1},{"w":"arise from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be caused by something","c":"起因於；由…引起","s":"Most of the arguments between my sister and me arise from small things, like who gets to use the bathroom first.","t":"我和姐姐之間大多數的爭吵都起因於小事，像是誰先用浴室。"},{"w":"rise, rose, risen","p":"v.","d":"to go up; to increase","c":"上升；升起","s":"The price of eggs has risen again this month, so my mother started buying them from a farmer near our town.","t":"這個月蛋價又上漲了，所以我媽媽開始向我們鎮附近的農夫買蛋。","a":"risen"},{"w":"give rise to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause something to happen","c":"引起；導致","s":"The long, hot summer gave rise to a serious water shortage, and many farmers lost their rice crops.","t":"漫長炎熱的夏天引起嚴重的缺水，許多農民失去了他們的稻作。","a":"gave rise to"},{"w":"arms","p":"n.","d":"weapons such as guns","c":"武器","s":"The two countries finally agreed to stop selling arms to each other and to work together for peace.","t":"兩國終於同意停止互相販售武器，並一起為和平努力。","h":1},{"w":"arm","p":"v.","d":"to give someone weapons","c":"武裝；裝備","s":"The government decided to arm the police officers with new equipment after several attacks in the city.","t":"在市內發生幾起攻擊事件後，政府決定為警察配備新裝備。"},{"w":"armed","p":"adj.","d":"carrying a weapon","c":"武裝的；持有武器的","s":"Two armed robbers ran into the bank this morning, but the police caught them before they could escape.","t":"今天早上兩名持械搶匪衝進銀行，但警察在他們逃走前就抓到了他們。"},{"w":"army","p":"n.","d":"a large group of soldiers who fight on land","c":"軍隊；陸軍","s":"My brother joined the army after high school, and now he sends us photos from the training camp every week.","t":"我哥哥高中畢業後加入軍隊，現在他每週都從訓練營寄照片給我們。"},{"w":"arm in arm","p":"phr.","d":"with arms linked together","c":"臂挽著臂","s":"The old couple walked arm in arm along the beach every evening, watching the sun go down over the sea.","t":"那對老夫婦每天傍晚手挽著手沿著海灘散步，看著太陽落入海中。"},{"w":"artificial","p":"adj.","d":"made by people, not natural","c":"人造的；人工的","s":"The flowers on the table looked so real that I did not notice they were artificial until I tried to smell them.","t":"桌上的花看起來很真，我直到想聞聞看才發現它們是人造的。","h":1},{"w":"artificial intelligence","p":"n.phr.","d":"computer systems that can learn and make decisions like people","c":"人工智慧","s":"Many companies now use artificial intelligence to answer customers' questions online, so you may be chatting with a computer.","t":"現在許多公司用人工智慧在線上回答顧客的問題，所以你可能正在和電腦聊天。"},{"w":"artificially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is made by people, not natural","c":"人為地；人工地","s":"The strawberries were artificially colored to look fresh, which is why my mother refuses to buy them from that store.","t":"那些草莓被人工染色讓它們看起來新鮮，這就是為什麼我媽媽拒絕在那家店買。"},{"w":"artistic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with art; good at creating art","c":"藝術的；有藝術天分的","s":"My sister is very artistic, and she painted a huge picture of the sea on the wall of her bedroom last summer.","t":"我姐姐很有藝術天分，去年夏天她在臥室牆上畫了一幅巨大的海景。","h":1},{"w":"artist","p":"n.","d":"a person who creates art, such as paintings","c":"藝術家","s":"A street artist drew my portrait in ten minutes at the night market, and it looked exactly like me.","t":"一位街頭藝術家在夜市十分鐘內畫了我的肖像，畫得跟我一模一樣。"},{"w":"art","p":"n.","d":"paintings, drawings, and other beautiful things people make","c":"藝術","s":"We visited the museum of modern art on Saturday, and some of the paintings were bigger than my classroom.","t":"我們星期六參觀了現代藝術博物館，有些畫比我的教室還大。"},{"w":"work of art","p":"n.phr.","d":"a painting, statue, or other object made by an artist","c":"藝術品","s":"The cake she made for the wedding was a real work of art, with tiny sugar flowers on every layer.","t":"她為婚禮做的蛋糕是一件真正的藝術品，每一層都有小小的糖花。"},{"w":"ashamed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling bad because you did something wrong","c":"羞愧的；慚愧的","s":"Tom felt ashamed after he shouted at his mother, so he cleaned the whole kitchen to say sorry.","t":"湯姆對媽媽大吼之後感到很羞愧，所以他把整個廚房打掃乾淨來表示道歉。","h":1},{"w":"be ashamed of","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to feel bad about something you did or about someone","c":"對…感到羞愧","s":"You should not be ashamed of your mistakes; instead, learn from them and try to do better next time.","t":"你不應該為自己的錯誤感到羞愧；相反地，要從中學習，下次努力做得更好。"},{"w":"shame","p":"n.","d":"the bad feeling you have when you did something wrong","c":"羞愧；恥辱","s":"He hung his head in shame when the teacher found the test answers hidden inside his pencil case.","t":"當老師發現藏在他鉛筆盒裡的考試答案時，他羞愧地低下了頭。"},{"w":"What a shame!","p":"phr.","d":"used to say that something is disappointing","c":"真可惜！","s":"\"What a shame\" said my aunt when she heard that the concert was canceled because of the typhoon.","t":"當我阿姨聽說演唱會因為颱風取消時，她說：「真可惜！」","a":"What a shame"},{"w":"shameful","p":"adj.","d":"very bad and making people feel ashamed","c":"可恥的","s":"It is shameful that some people leave their trash on the beach after a picnic and expect others to clean it up.","t":"有些人野餐後把垃圾留在海灘上，還期待別人清理，這真是可恥。"},{"w":"aspect","p":"n.","d":"one part or side of a situation, idea, or problem","c":"方面；層面","s":"Before you choose a university, think about every aspect of student life there, not only the classes.","t":"在你選大學之前，想想那裡學生生活的每一個方面，而不只是課程。","h":1},{"w":"in every aspect","p":"phr.","d":"in all ways or parts","c":"在各方面","s":"The new phone is better than the old one in every aspect: the camera, the battery, and even the price.","t":"新手機在各方面都比舊的好：相機、電池，甚至價格。"},{"w":"aspect of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a particular part of something","c":"…的方面","s":"The most difficult aspect of living abroad, my cousin says, is missing family dinners on holidays.","t":"我表姐說，在國外生活最困難的方面是錯過節日的家庭聚餐。"},{"w":"aspirin","p":"n.","d":"a common medicine that reduces pain and fever","c":"阿斯匹靈","s":"My father takes an aspirin whenever he has a headache, but the doctor told him not to take too many.","t":"我爸爸每次頭痛都會吃一顆阿斯匹靈，但醫生告訴他不要吃太多。","h":1},{"w":"take aspirin","p":"v.phr.","d":"to swallow aspirin as medicine","c":"服用阿斯匹靈","s":"You should not take aspirin on an empty stomach, because it can hurt your stomach and make you feel sick.","t":"你不應該空腹服用阿斯匹靈，因為它會傷胃，讓你覺得不舒服。"},{"w":"painkiller","p":"n.","d":"a medicine that reduces pain","c":"止痛藥","s":"After the dentist pulled out my tooth, she gave me a painkiller and told me to rest for the whole afternoon.","t":"牙醫拔掉我的牙齒後，給了我一顆止痛藥，並要我整個下午休息。"},{"w":"assemble","p":"v.","d":"to come together in one place as a group","c":"集合；聚集","s":"All the students will assemble in the playground at eight o'clock before we leave for the museum.","t":"所有學生將在八點於操場集合，然後我們再出發去博物館。","h":1},{"w":"assemble","p":"v.","d":"to put the parts of something together","c":"組裝","s":"It took my father three hours to assemble the new bookshelf because the instructions were only in Swedish.","t":"我爸爸花了三個小時組裝新書架，因為說明書只有瑞典文。","h":1},{"w":"assembly","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of a large group of people, such as a whole school","c":"集會；朝會","s":"During the morning assembly, the principal announced that the school would get a new swimming pool next year.","t":"在早上的朝會上，校長宣布學校明年將有新的游泳池。"},{"w":"assembly line","p":"n.phr.","d":"a line of workers and machines that put a product together","c":"裝配線；生產線","s":"Each worker on the assembly line adds one small part to the car, and a finished car comes out every two minutes.","t":"裝配線上的每位工人為汽車加上一個小零件，每兩分鐘就有一輛完成的車出來。"},{"w":"assign","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a job or task to do","c":"指派；分配","s":"Our teacher will assign each group a different country to study, and we will present our findings next Friday.","t":"老師會分配給每一組一個不同的國家研究，我們下週五要報告研究結果。","h":1},{"w":"assignment","p":"n.","d":"a piece of work that a student or worker is given to do","c":"作業；任務","s":"The history assignment is due on Monday, so I plan to spend the whole weekend reading about the Qing Dynasty.","t":"歷史作業星期一要交，所以我打算整個週末都在讀清朝的資料。"},{"w":"be assigned to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be given a particular job, place, or group","c":"被分配到…","s":"My cousin was assigned to the Taichung office after only one year, so now he takes the train home every weekend.","t":"我表哥才工作一年就被分配到台中辦公室，所以現在他每個週末搭火車回家。","a":"was assigned to"},{"w":"hand in an assignment","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give finished homework to the teacher","c":"繳交作業","s":"If you hand in an assignment late, the teacher will take ten points off your grade for each day it is late.","t":"如果你遲交作業，老師會每遲一天就扣十分。"},{"w":"assistance","p":"n.","d":"help or support","c":"協助；幫助","s":"The old man asked the station staff for assistance because he could not read the small letters on the ticket machine.","t":"那位老先生向車站人員尋求協助，因為他看不清楚售票機上的小字。","h":1},{"w":"assist","p":"v.","d":"to help someone do something","c":"協助","s":"The nurse will assist the doctor during the operation by handing her the tools she needs.","t":"手術期間護士會把醫生需要的工具遞給她，協助醫生。"},{"w":"assistant","p":"n.","d":"a person who helps someone in their work","c":"助理；助手","s":"My aunt works as a dental assistant, and her job is to prepare the tools and calm down nervous patients.","t":"我阿姨是牙醫助理，她的工作是準備工具和安撫緊張的病人。"},{"w":"with the assistance of","p":"phr.","d":"with help from someone or something","c":"在…的協助下","s":"The students finished the science project with the assistance of their teacher, who stayed after school every day for a week.","t":"學生們在老師的協助下完成了科學專題，老師整整一週每天放學後都留下來。"},{"w":"associate","p":"v.","d":"to connect one thing with another in your mind","c":"聯想；把…聯繫起來","s":"Most people associate the color red with good luck in Taiwan, which is why there are red envelopes at New Year.","t":"在台灣大多數人把紅色聯想到好運，這就是為什麼過年時有紅包。","h":1},{"w":"be associated with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be connected with something","c":"與…有關","s":"Smoking is associated with many serious diseases, so the government puts warning pictures on every cigarette box.","t":"吸菸與許多嚴重疾病有關，所以政府在每個菸盒上放警告圖片。","a":"is associated with","h":1},{"w":"associate","p":"n.","d":"a person you work with or do business with","c":"同事；夥伴","s":"My father is having dinner with a business associate from Japan tonight, so we will eat without him.","t":"我爸爸今晚要和一位來自日本的生意夥伴吃晚餐，所以我們要自己吃。"},{"w":"association","p":"n.","d":"a group of people with the same interest or job","c":"協會；聯盟","s":"The parents' association raised enough money to buy new computers for every classroom in the school.","t":"家長協會募到足夠的錢，為學校每間教室購買新電腦。"},{"w":"association","p":"n.","d":"a connection between things in your mind","c":"聯想；關聯","s":"For me, the smell of fresh bread has a strong association with my grandmother's kitchen on Sunday mornings.","t":"對我來說，新鮮麵包的香味與奶奶週日早晨的廚房有強烈的關聯。"},{"w":"assurance","p":"n.","d":"a promise that something is true or will happen","c":"保證；擔保","s":"The shop gave us an assurance that the new phone would be repaired for free if it broke within one year.","t":"店家給我們保證，如果新手機在一年內壞掉會免費維修。","h":1},{"w":"assure","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone that something is true so they stop worrying","c":"向…保證；使確信","s":"The doctor tried to assure my mother that the operation was simple and that I would be home in two days.","t":"醫生試著向我媽媽保證手術很簡單，我兩天內就能回家。","h":1},{"w":"assure sb that","p":"v.phr.","d":"to promise someone that something is true","c":"向某人保證…","s":"The travel agent assured us that our hotel was right next to the beach, and she was telling the truth.","t":"旅行社人員向我們保證飯店就在海灘旁邊，而她說的是實話。","a":"assured us that"},{"w":"self-assurance","p":"n.","d":"confidence in yourself","c":"自信","s":"She walked onto the stage with great self-assurance, and nobody could tell it was her first time giving a speech.","t":"她帶著十足的自信走上舞台，沒有人看得出那是她第一次演講。"},{"w":"assured","p":"adj.","d":"confident; certain to happen","c":"有自信的；確定的","s":"After months of practice, the young singer gave an assured performance and won first prize in the contest.","t":"經過幾個月的練習，這位年輕歌手給了一場自信的演出，贏得比賽第一名。"},{"w":"athletic","p":"adj.","d":"physically strong and good at sports","c":"運動的；擅長運動的","s":"My brother is very athletic; he runs every morning, plays basketball after school, and swims on weekends.","t":"我哥哥非常擅長運動；他每天早上跑步，放學後打籃球，週末游泳。","h":1},{"w":"athlete","p":"n.","d":"a person who is good at sports or competes in sports","c":"運動員","s":"The young athlete broke the national record in the 100-meter race and became famous overnight.","t":"這位年輕運動員打破了一百公尺賽跑的全國紀錄，一夜之間成名。"},{"w":"athletics","p":"n.","d":"sports such as running and jumping","c":"田徑運動","s":"Our school is famous for athletics, and three of its runners have competed in international games.","t":"我們學校以田徑聞名，有三位跑者曾參加國際比賽。"},{"w":"athletic shoes","p":"n.phr.","d":"shoes made for running and sports","c":"運動鞋","s":"You need to wear athletic shoes in the gym because leather shoes can damage the wooden floor.","t":"在體育館你需要穿運動鞋，因為皮鞋會損壞木地板。"},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the feeling or mood of a place","c":"氣氛","s":"The small café has a warm and friendly atmosphere, so many students go there to study on rainy afternoons.","t":"這家小咖啡館有溫暖友善的氣氛，所以很多學生在下雨的午後去那裡讀書。","h":1},{"w":"atmosphere","p":"n.","d":"the layer of air around the Earth","c":"大氣層","s":"Factories send a lot of smoke into the atmosphere, and scientists say this is making the Earth warmer every year.","t":"工廠把大量的煙排入大氣層，科學家說這讓地球每年變得更暖。"},{"w":"atmospheric","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the atmosphere; creating a special mood","c":"大氣的；有氣氛的","s":"Scientists measure atmospheric pressure every hour to predict whether a storm is coming toward the island.","t":"科學家每小時測量大氣壓力，以預測是否有暴風雨正朝島嶼而來。"},{"w":"atom","p":"n.","d":"the smallest part of a chemical element","c":"原子","s":"Everything around us, from water to gold, is made of tiny pieces called atoms, which are too small to see.","t":"我們周圍的一切，從水到黃金，都是由叫做原子的微小粒子組成，小到看不見。","a":"atoms","h":1},{"w":"atomic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with atoms or the energy from them","c":"原子的","s":"The first atomic bomb was dropped in 1945, and the world has been worried about such weapons ever since.","t":"第一顆原子彈在 1945 年投下，從那時起全世界就一直擔心這類武器。","h":1},{"w":"atomic energy","p":"n.phr.","d":"the power produced by splitting atoms","c":"原子能；核能","s":"Some countries use atomic energy to make electricity, but many people worry about what happens if something goes wrong.","t":"有些國家利用核能發電，但許多人擔心出問題時會發生什麼事。"},{"w":"attach","p":"v.","d":"to fasten or join one thing to another","c":"附上；繫上","s":"Please attach a recent photo to your application form before you send it to the school office.","t":"請在把申請表寄到學校辦公室之前，附上一張近照。","h":1},{"w":"attachment","p":"n.","d":"a file sent with an email","c":"附件","s":"I could not open the attachment in your email, so could you send the report again as a PDF file?","t":"我打不開你電子郵件裡的附件，你可以把報告再用 PDF 檔寄一次嗎？"},{"w":"attachment","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of love or connection","c":"依戀；依附","s":"My little sister has a strong attachment to her old teddy bear and cannot sleep without it, even on trips.","t":"我妹妹對她的舊泰迪熊有強烈的依戀，沒有它就睡不著，即使旅行時也是。"},{"w":"be attached to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to like someone or something very much; to be joined to","c":"依戀；附在…上","s":"My grandfather is attached to his old bicycle, so he refuses to buy a new one even though it is thirty years old.","t":"我爺爺很捨不得他的舊腳踏車，所以即使它已經三十年了，他還是拒絕買新的。","a":"is attached to"},{"w":"attach importance to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think that something is important","c":"重視…","s":"Our school attaches importance to reading, so every student must read at least one English book each month.","t":"我們學校重視閱讀，所以每位學生每個月至少要讀一本英文書。","a":"attaches importance to"},{"w":"attraction","p":"n.","d":"an interesting place that people visit","c":"景點","s":"Taipei 101 is the most popular tourist attraction in the city, and the view from the top is amazing at night.","t":"台北 101 是這座城市最受歡迎的觀光景點，晚上從頂樓看的景色非常壯觀。","h":1},{"w":"attraction","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of liking someone or something very much","c":"吸引力","s":"I do not understand the attraction of horror movies, but my friends line up to watch every new one.","t":"我不懂恐怖電影的吸引力，但我的朋友們每部新片都排隊去看。"},{"w":"attract","p":"v.","d":"to make someone come to a place or be interested in something","c":"吸引","s":"The night market's cheap and tasty food attracts thousands of tourists every weekend, especially in summer.","t":"夜市便宜又美味的食物每個週末吸引數千名遊客，尤其是在夏天。","a":"attracts"},{"w":"attractive","p":"adj.","d":"pleasant to look at; interesting","c":"吸引人的；漂亮的","s":"The job offer was very attractive because it came with a high salary and three weeks of vacation every year.","t":"這份工作邀約非常吸引人，因為它有高薪，而且每年有三週的假期。"},{"w":"attract attention","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people notice you or something","c":"引起注意","s":"The little boy banged on the drum to attract attention, and soon everyone at the party was watching him.","t":"小男孩敲鼓引起注意，很快派對上的每個人都在看他。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"audio – blossom","cards":[{"w":"audio","p":"adj.","d":"connected with sound, especially recorded sound","c":"聲音的；音訊的","s":"The audio quality of the old recording was so poor that we could hardly hear what the singer was saying.","t":"那段舊錄音的音訊品質太差了，我們幾乎聽不清楚歌手在說什麼。","h":1},{"w":"audio file","p":"n.phr.","d":"a computer file that contains sound","c":"音訊檔","s":"Our teacher sends us an audio file every week, and we listen to it on the bus to practice our English.","t":"我們老師每週傳一個音訊檔給我們，我們在公車上聽來練習英文。"},{"w":"audiovisual","p":"adj.","d":"using both sound and pictures","c":"視聽的","s":"The library has a new audiovisual room where students can watch movies and listen to music with headphones.","t":"圖書館有一間新的視聽室，學生可以在那裡戴著耳機看電影和聽音樂。"},{"w":"audience","p":"n.","d":"the people who watch or listen to a show","c":"觀眾；聽眾","s":"When the band finished its last song, the audience stood up and clapped for almost five minutes.","t":"樂團唱完最後一首歌時，觀眾起立鼓掌了將近五分鐘。"},{"w":"auditorium","p":"n.","d":"a large hall where people sit to watch a performance","c":"禮堂；觀眾席","s":"The school auditorium can hold eight hundred people, so every student can attend the graduation ceremony.","t":"學校禮堂可容納八百人，所以每位學生都能參加畢業典禮。"},{"w":"authentic","p":"adj.","d":"real and true, not a copy","c":"真正的；真實的","s":"This small restaurant serves authentic Thai food because the cook grew up in Bangkok and uses her mother's recipes.","t":"這家小餐廳提供道地的泰國菜，因為廚師在曼谷長大，而且用的是她母親的食譜。","h":1},{"w":"authenticity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being real and true","c":"真實性；真品","s":"Before the museum bought the old painting, experts spent six months checking its authenticity very carefully.","t":"博物館買下那幅古畫之前，專家花了六個月非常仔細地檢查它的真實性。"},{"w":"author","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes books","c":"作者；作家","s":"The author of this popular novel will visit our school next month to talk about how she writes her stories.","t":"這本暢銷小說的作者下個月會來我們學校，談談她是如何寫故事的。"},{"w":"authority","p":"n.","d":"the power to give orders and make decisions","c":"權力；權威","s":"The new manager has the authority to hire and fire workers, so everyone in the office is a little nervous.","t":"新經理有雇用和解僱員工的權力，所以辦公室裡每個人都有點緊張。","h":1},{"w":"the authorities","p":"n.","d":"the people or organizations in charge, such as the police or the government","c":"當局；有關單位","s":"After the bridge was damaged by the earthquake, the authorities closed the road and sent engineers to check it.","t":"橋被地震損壞後，當局封閉了道路，並派工程師去檢查。"},{"w":"authorize","p":"v.","d":"to give official permission for something","c":"授權；批准","s":"Only the principal can authorize a school trip abroad, so the teachers must send her the plan a month early.","t":"只有校長能批准出國的校外教學，所以老師們必須提前一個月把計畫交給她。"},{"w":"authoritative","p":"adj.","d":"trusted and respected as true or correct","c":"權威的；可信的","s":"This dictionary is the most authoritative one for English learners, and many teachers in Taiwan recommend it.","t":"這本字典是英語學習者最權威的一本，台灣許多老師都推薦它。"},{"w":"autobiography","p":"n.","d":"a book that someone writes about his or her own life","c":"自傳","s":"In her autobiography, the famous singer describes how she grew up in a poor village and sang in the streets.","t":"這位知名歌手在她的自傳中描述她如何在一個貧窮的村莊長大，並在街頭唱歌。","h":1},{"w":"autobiographical","p":"adj.","d":"about the writer's own life","c":"自傳的；自傳性質的","s":"Although the movie is called a love story, it is actually autobiographical and shows the director's own childhood.","t":"雖然這部電影被稱為愛情故事，但它其實是自傳性質的，呈現了導演自己的童年。"},{"w":"automatic","p":"adj.","d":"working by itself without a person controlling it","c":"自動的","s":"The automatic doors at the supermarket open when you walk near them, which is very helpful when your hands are full.","t":"超市的自動門會在你走近時打開，當你雙手都拿滿東西時非常方便。"},{"w":"automatically","p":"adv.","d":"by itself, without a person doing anything","c":"自動地","s":"My phone automatically saves every photo to the cloud, so I did not lose anything when it fell into the river.","t":"我的手機會自動把每張照片存到雲端，所以它掉進河裡時我沒有丟失任何東西。"},{"w":"autograph","p":"n.","d":"a famous person's name written by himself or herself","c":"（名人的）親筆簽名","s":"After the baseball game, hundreds of fans waited outside the stadium hoping to get an autograph from the star player.","t":"棒球賽結束後，數百名球迷在球場外等候，希望得到明星球員的親筆簽名。","h":1},{"w":"autograph","p":"v.","d":"to sign your name on something for a fan","c":"親筆簽名於","s":"The writer kindly agreed to autograph my copy of her book, and she even wrote a short message for me.","t":"那位作家很親切地答應在我那本她的書上簽名，甚至還為我寫了一段簡短的話。"},{"w":"ask for sb's autograph","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask a famous person to sign his or her name for you","c":"向某人索取簽名","s":"My little sister was too shy to ask for his autograph, so I walked up to the actor and asked him for her.","t":"我妹妹太害羞不敢向他索取簽名，所以我走到那位演員面前替她開口。","a":"ask for his autograph"},{"w":"await","p":"v.","d":"to wait for something (more formal than wait)","c":"等待；等候","s":"Thousands of students across the country await the results of the big exam, which will be announced tomorrow morning.","t":"全國成千上萬的學生正在等待大考的結果，成績將在明天早上公布。","h":1},{"w":"wait","p":"v.","d":"to stay in a place until something happens","c":"等待","s":"Please wait outside the office for a few minutes because the doctor is still talking with another patient.","t":"請在辦公室外面等幾分鐘，因為醫生還在和另一位病人談話。"},{"w":"wait for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay where you are until a person or thing arrives","c":"等候…","s":"We had to wait for the bus for forty minutes in the rain, so everyone was wet and unhappy when it finally came.","t":"我們在雨中等公車等了四十分鐘，所以當車終於來時，大家都淋濕了，心情很差。"},{"w":"long-awaited","p":"adj.","d":"that people have waited for a long time","c":"期待已久的","s":"The long-awaited new MRT line finally opened last week, and now my trip to school takes only fifteen minutes.","t":"期待已久的捷運新路線上週終於開通了，現在我上學只要十五分鐘。"},{"w":"waiting room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room where people sit until it is their turn","c":"候診室；等候室","s":"The waiting room at the clinic was full of sick children, so we sat on the floor until our number was called.","t":"診所的候診室擠滿了生病的孩子，所以我們坐在地板上，直到叫到我們的號碼。"},{"w":"bald","p":"adj.","d":"having little or no hair on the head","c":"禿頭的","s":"My uncle started to go bald in his thirties, so now he always wears a cap when he goes outside.","t":"我叔叔三十幾歲就開始禿頭，所以現在他出門總是戴著帽子。","h":1},{"w":"go bald","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lose the hair on your head","c":"變禿頭","s":"Many men worry that they will go bald like their fathers, and some of them spend a lot of money on special shampoo.","t":"許多男人擔心會像父親一樣變禿頭，有些人花大錢買特殊的洗髮精。"},{"w":"baldness","p":"n.","d":"the state of having no hair on the head","c":"禿頭；掉髮","s":"Doctors say that baldness is often passed down in families, so there is no need to feel ashamed about it.","t":"醫生說禿頭常常是家族遺傳，所以不需要為此感到羞愧。"},{"w":"bald eagle","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large American bird with a white head","c":"白頭海鵰","s":"The bald eagle is the national bird of the United States, and you can see it on coins and government buildings.","t":"白頭海鵰是美國的國鳥，你可以在硬幣和政府建築上看到它。"},{"w":"ballet","p":"n.","d":"a kind of dancing that tells a story with music and careful movements","c":"芭蕾舞","s":"My cousin has studied ballet since she was five, and she practices for three hours after school every day.","t":"我表妹從五歲起就學芭蕾舞，她每天放學後練習三個小時。","h":1},{"w":"ballet dancer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who performs ballet","c":"芭蕾舞者","s":"A professional ballet dancer must be very strong, because jumping and standing on your toes is much harder than it looks.","t":"專業的芭蕾舞者必須非常強壯，因為跳躍和用腳尖站立比看起來難得多。"},{"w":"ballerina","p":"n.","d":"a female ballet dancer","c":"芭蕾女舞者","s":"The young ballerina moved so lightly across the stage that she seemed to be flying rather than dancing.","t":"那位年輕的芭蕾女舞者在舞台上移動得如此輕盈，看起來像在飛而不是在跳舞。"},{"w":"ballroom","p":"n.","d":"a very large room used for dancing","c":"舞廳；宴會廳","s":"The hotel ballroom was decorated with flowers and lights for the wedding, and more than two hundred guests danced all night.","t":"飯店的宴會廳為婚禮佈置了花和燈飾，兩百多位賓客跳舞跳了整晚。"},{"w":"bandage","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of cloth that you tie around a hurt part of the body","c":"繃帶","s":"The nurse cleaned the cut on my knee and wrapped a clean bandage around it before I went back to class.","t":"護士清理了我膝蓋上的傷口，並在我回教室前用乾淨的繃帶包好。","h":1},{"w":"bandage","p":"v.","d":"to tie a bandage around a hurt part of the body","c":"用繃帶包紮","s":"My father knows how to bandage a wound properly because he worked as a volunteer at the fire station for years.","t":"我爸爸知道如何正確地包紮傷口，因為他在消防隊當志工好幾年了。"},{"w":"band","p":"n.","d":"a thin flat strip of material; a group of musicians","c":"帶子；樂團","s":"She tied her long hair back with a simple black band before she started running on the school track.","t":"她在開始到學校操場跑步前，用一條簡單的黑色髮帶把長髮綁起來。"},{"w":"rubber band","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin circle of rubber used to hold things together","c":"橡皮筋","s":"I put a rubber band around the stack of letters so that they would not fall apart in my bag.","t":"我用一條橡皮筋把那疊信綑起來，這樣它們在我的包包裡就不會散開。"},{"w":"bankrupt","p":"adj.","d":"without enough money to pay what you owe","c":"破產的","s":"The toy company was bankrupt by the end of the year because fewer and fewer parents bought its old-fashioned products.","t":"那家玩具公司到年底就破產了，因為買它老式產品的父母越來越少。","h":1},{"w":"go bankrupt","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lose all your money so that your business must close","c":"破產；倒閉","s":"Many small shops in our town may go bankrupt if the new shopping mall takes away all of their customers.","t":"如果新購物中心搶走所有顧客，我們鎮上許多小店可能會倒閉。"},{"w":"bankruptcy","p":"n.","d":"the state of having no money to pay your debts","c":"破產","s":"The airline announced its bankruptcy this morning, and thousands of passengers do not know whether their flights will still take off.","t":"這家航空公司今天早上宣布破產，成千上萬的乘客不知道他們的航班是否還會起飛。"},{"w":"bankrupt","p":"v.","d":"to make a person or company lose all their money","c":"使破產","s":"The huge hospital bills nearly bankrupted the family, so their neighbors started collecting money to help them.","t":"龐大的醫療費用幾乎使這家人破產，所以鄰居們開始募款幫助他們。","a":"bankrupted"},{"w":"bargain","p":"n.","d":"something you buy for much less than its usual price","c":"便宜貨；特價品","s":"This winter coat was a real bargain because the store was closing down and sold everything at half price.","t":"這件冬季大衣真是便宜貨，因為那家店要關門了，所有東西都半價出售。","h":1},{"w":"bargain","p":"v.","d":"to talk with someone to try to get a lower price","c":"討價還價；議價","s":"In many night markets, you can bargain with the sellers, and they will often lower the price if you buy two items.","t":"在許多夜市你可以和攤商討價還價，如果你買兩件，他們通常會降價。"},{"w":"bargain with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to discuss a price or deal with someone","c":"與…議價","s":"My mother loves to bargain with the fruit sellers at the market, and she usually walks home with extra apples for free.","t":"我媽媽喜歡在市場和水果攤商議價，她通常會帶著額外免費的蘋果走回家。"},{"w":"a real bargain","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very good deal","c":"非常划算的交易","s":"The second-hand bike was a real bargain at only five hundred dollars, so my brother bought it without thinking twice.","t":"那輛二手腳踏車只要五百元，真的很划算，所以我哥哥毫不猶豫就買了。"},{"w":"barrier","p":"n.","d":"something that stops people from going somewhere or doing something","c":"障礙；屏障","s":"The police set up a barrier across the road so that the crowd could not get too close to the burning building.","t":"警方在路上設置了屏障，使群眾無法太靠近燃燒中的建築。","h":1},{"w":"language barrier","p":"n.phr.","d":"the problem of not sharing a common language","c":"語言障礙","s":"When my grandmother first moved to Canada, the language barrier made it hard for her to make friends or even buy food.","t":"我奶奶剛搬到加拿大時，語言障礙讓她很難交朋友，甚至很難買食物。"},{"w":"bar","p":"n.","d":"a long piece of metal or wood; a place that sells drinks","c":"條；棒；酒吧","s":"The window had a thick metal bar across it, so the thief could not climb into the house from the garden.","t":"那扇窗戶上有一根粗的金屬欄杆，所以小偷無法從花園爬進屋裡。"},{"w":"bar","p":"v.","d":"to officially stop someone from doing something or entering a place","c":"禁止；阻擋","s":"The school decided to bar students from bringing phones into the exam room after several cases of cheating last year.","t":"去年發生幾起作弊事件後，學校決定禁止學生把手機帶進考場。"},{"w":"basin","p":"n.","d":"a large bowl for holding water, especially for washing","c":"盆；臉盆","s":"My grandmother still washes her face every morning with cold water from a small metal basin in the yard.","t":"我奶奶每天早上仍然用院子裡一個小金屬臉盆裡的冷水洗臉。","h":1},{"w":"basin","p":"n.","d":"a large low area of land where rivers flow into","c":"盆地；流域","s":"Taipei lies in a basin surrounded by mountains, which is one reason the city feels so hot in summer.","t":"台北位於群山環繞的盆地中，這是夏天城市感覺如此炎熱的原因之一。"},{"w":"washbasin","p":"n.","d":"a bowl fixed to the wall in a bathroom for washing your hands and face","c":"洗手台；洗臉盆","s":"Please do not leave the water running in the washbasin while you brush your teeth, because it wastes a lot of water.","t":"刷牙時請不要讓洗手台的水一直流，因為那會浪費很多水。"},{"w":"battery","p":"n.","d":"an object that gives electricity to a phone, toy, or car","c":"電池","s":"The remote control stopped working last night, so I bought a new battery for it at the convenience store this morning.","t":"遙控器昨晚不能用了，所以我今天早上在便利商店買了一顆新電池。","h":1},{"w":"battery life","p":"n.phr.","d":"the length of time a battery can work before it needs charging","c":"電池續航力","s":"I chose this phone mainly because of its long battery life, which lasts two full days without charging.","t":"我選這支手機主要是因為它的電池續航力很長，不用充電可以撐整整兩天。"},{"w":"run out of battery","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have no power left in a battery","c":"電池沒電","s":"My laptop ran out of battery in the middle of the presentation, so I had to finish my talk without any slides.","t":"我的筆電在簡報中途沒電了，所以我只好在沒有任何投影片的情況下講完。","a":"ran out of battery"},{"w":"rechargeable battery","p":"n.phr.","d":"a battery that can be filled with electricity again and again","c":"充電電池","s":"Using a rechargeable battery is better for the environment because you do not have to throw it away after one use.","t":"使用充電電池對環境比較好，因為你不必用過一次就丟掉。"},{"w":"beggar","p":"n.","d":"a very poor person who asks others for money or food","c":"乞丐","s":"An old beggar sat outside the train station every day, and some kind passengers gave him bread and coins.","t":"一位老乞丐每天坐在火車站外面，有些好心的乘客會給他麵包和零錢。","h":1},{"w":"beg","p":"v.","d":"to ask for something in a strong and anxious way","c":"懇求；乞求","s":"The little boy began to beg his mother for one more hour of video games, but she firmly said no.","t":"小男孩開始懇求媽媽再讓他玩一小時電動，但她堅定地拒絕了。"},{"w":"beg for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask for something that you need very much","c":"乞求…；懇求…","s":"The hungry dog followed us down the street and seemed to beg for food with its big sad eyes.","t":"那隻飢餓的狗跟著我們走過街道，用它又大又悲傷的眼睛似乎在乞求食物。"},{"w":"I beg your pardon","p":"phr.","d":"a polite way to say sorry or to ask someone to repeat","c":"對不起；請再說一次","s":"\"I beg your pardon, I did not hear the last part,\" said the student politely, and the teacher repeated the question.","t":"「對不起，請再說一次，我沒聽到最後一部分。」學生客氣地說，老師就重複了問題。"},{"w":"behavior","p":"n.","d":"the way a person or animal acts","c":"行為；舉止","s":"The teacher praised the class for their excellent behavior during the museum visit, so they got extra free time.","t":"老師稱讚全班在參觀博物館時的優良行為，所以他們獲得額外的自由時間。","h":1},{"w":"behave","p":"v.","d":"to act in a particular way","c":"表現；行為","s":"Children often behave badly when they are tired, so we should put them to bed before the guests arrive.","t":"孩子疲倦時常常表現不好，所以我們應該在客人到達前讓他們上床睡覺。"},{"w":"behave yourself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to act politely and not cause trouble","c":"守規矩；表現得體","s":"My mother told me to behave myself at my aunt's house, which meant no running inside and no fighting with my cousins.","t":"我媽媽叫我在阿姨家要守規矩，意思是不能在屋裡跑，也不能和表兄弟姊妹打架。","a":"behave myself"},{"w":"misbehave","p":"v.","d":"to act badly","c":"行為不當；調皮","s":"If students misbehave on the school bus, the driver will report them and they may lose their bus pass.","t":"如果學生在校車上行為不當，司機會通報他們，他們可能會失去乘車證。"},{"w":"behavioral","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the way people act","c":"行為的","s":"The new puppy has some behavioral problems, such as biting shoes, so we are taking it to a training class.","t":"這隻新來的小狗有一些行為問題，比如咬鞋子，所以我們要帶它去上訓練課。"},{"w":"bin","p":"n.","d":"a container for waste, or for storing things","c":"垃圾桶；箱；桶","s":"Please put your empty bottles in the bin by the door instead of leaving them on the classroom desks.","t":"請把空瓶子放進門邊的垃圾桶，不要留在教室的桌子上。","h":1},{"w":"recycling bin","p":"n.phr.","d":"a container for things that can be used again, like paper or plastic","c":"回收桶","s":"Our school has a blue recycling bin on every floor, and the students who sort their waste correctly win a prize each month.","t":"我們學校每層樓都有一個藍色的回收桶，正確分類垃圾的學生每月可以得獎。"},{"w":"trash bin","p":"n.phr.","d":"a container for waste","c":"垃圾桶","s":"The trash bin in the park was so full that paper cups and food boxes were lying all over the grass.","t":"公園裡的垃圾桶太滿了，紙杯和食物盒散落在草地各處。"},{"w":"throw sth in the bin","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put something into the waste container","c":"把某物丟進垃圾桶","s":"After eating lunch, she folded the paper bag and threw it in the bin before walking back to the office.","t":"吃完午餐後，她把紙袋折好丟進垃圾桶，然後走回辦公室。","a":"threw it in the bin"},{"w":"biography","p":"n.","d":"the story of a person's life written by someone else","c":"傳記","s":"For my book report, I read a biography of a famous scientist and learned that she failed many times before she succeeded.","t":"為了寫讀書報告，我讀了一位著名科學家的傳記，得知她成功前失敗了很多次。","h":1},{"w":"biographer","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes the story of someone else's life","c":"傳記作家","s":"The biographer spent ten years talking to the president's friends and family before she finished the book.","t":"那位傳記作家花了十年訪談總統的朋友和家人，才完成這本書。"},{"w":"biographical","p":"adj.","d":"about a particular person's life","c":"傳記的","s":"The film is a biographical drama about a young painter, and most of the events in it really happened.","t":"這部電影是關於一位年輕畫家的傳記劇情片，裡面大部分事件都真實發生過。"},{"w":"biology","p":"n.","d":"the science of living things","c":"生物學","s":"In biology class this week, we looked at tiny plant cells under a microscope and drew what we saw.","t":"這週的生物課，我們用顯微鏡觀察微小的植物細胞，並畫出我們看到的東西。","h":1},{"w":"biologist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies living things","c":"生物學家","s":"The biologist spent two years in the rainforest studying a rare frog that is only as big as a fingernail.","t":"那位生物學家在雨林中花了兩年研究一種只有指甲大小的稀有青蛙。"},{"w":"biological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with living things or with biology","c":"生物的；生物學的","s":"Scientists are developing a biological way to kill insects on farms so that farmers can use fewer dangerous chemicals.","t":"科學家正在研發一種生物方法來消滅農田裡的昆蟲，讓農民可以少用危險的化學藥劑。"},{"w":"biologically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with living things","c":"在生物學上","s":"Although they look very different, dogs and wolves are biologically very close and can even have babies together.","t":"雖然外表差很多，但狗和狼在生物學上非常接近，甚至可以一起生下後代。"},{"w":"blade","p":"n.","d":"the flat sharp part of a knife or tool that cuts","c":"刀刃；刀身","s":"Be careful with that kitchen knife because the blade is extremely sharp and can cut your finger easily.","t":"小心那把菜刀，因為刀刃非常鋒利，很容易割到你的手指。","h":1},{"w":"blade","p":"n.","d":"a single long thin leaf of grass","c":"（草的）葉片","s":"After the rain, every blade of grass in the garden shone with tiny drops of water in the morning sun.","t":"雨後，花園裡每一片草葉都在晨光中閃著小小的水珠。"},{"w":"razor blade","p":"n.phr.","d":"the thin sharp piece of metal used for shaving","c":"刮鬍刀片","s":"My father changes his razor blade every week because an old one can hurt his skin when he shaves.","t":"我爸爸每週更換刮鬍刀片，因為舊刀片在刮鬍子時會傷到皮膚。"},{"w":"shoulder blade","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of the two flat bones at the top of your back","c":"肩胛骨","s":"After carrying the heavy backpack all day, I felt a sharp pain under my right shoulder blade and needed a rest.","t":"背了一整天沉重的背包後，我感到右邊肩胛骨下面一陣劇痛，需要休息。"},{"w":"blend","p":"v.","d":"to mix two or more things together so they become one","c":"混合；調和","s":"To make the sauce, blend the tomatoes, garlic, and olive oil until the mixture is smooth and bright red.","t":"要做這個醬汁，先把番茄、大蒜和橄欖油混合攪打到均勻滑順、顏色鮮紅。","h":1},{"w":"blend","p":"n.","d":"a mixture of different things","c":"混合物","s":"This tea is a special blend of green tea and dried fruit, and it tastes sweet without any sugar.","t":"這款茶是綠茶和果乾的特別混合配方，不加糖就有甜味。"},{"w":"blend in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look or behave like the people or things around you","c":"融入；不顯眼","s":"The new student tried hard to blend in by wearing the same style of clothes and learning the local jokes.","t":"新同學努力融入大家，穿同樣風格的衣服，還學當地的笑話。"},{"w":"blender","p":"n.","d":"an electric machine that mixes food or drinks","c":"果汁機；攪拌機","s":"Every morning my mother puts bananas, milk, and oats into the blender to make a quick breakfast drink for us.","t":"每天早上我媽媽把香蕉、牛奶和燕麥放進果汁機，為我們做快速的早餐飲品。"},{"w":"blessing","p":"n.","d":"something good that you are lucky to have; God's help","c":"祝福；福氣；恩賜","s":"Having a warm house and enough food every day is a blessing that many people in the world do not enjoy.","t":"每天有溫暖的家和足夠的食物是一種福氣，世界上許多人並沒有享有。","h":1},{"w":"bless","p":"v.","d":"to ask God to protect someone; to make someone lucky","c":"祝福；保佑","s":"Before the long journey, the old man asked the temple god to bless his family and keep them safe from harm.","t":"在長途旅行前，老人請求廟裡的神明保佑他的家人，使他們免於傷害。"},{"w":"Bless you!","p":"phr.","d":"what you say when someone sneezes","c":"（別人打噴嚏時說）保重！","s":"When my classmate sneezed loudly in the quiet library, three people around her whispered \"Bless you\" at the same time.","t":"我同學在安靜的圖書館裡大聲打噴嚏時，她周圍三個人同時小聲說「保重」。","a":"Bless you"},{"w":"blessed","p":"adj.","d":"lucky; having good things in your life","c":"有福的；幸運的","s":"I feel truly blessed to have friends who drove two hours just to celebrate my birthday with me.","t":"我覺得真的很幸運，有朋友開了兩小時的車只為了和我一起慶生。"},{"w":"a blessing in disguise","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that seems bad at first but turns out to be good","c":"因禍得福","s":"Losing that job was a blessing in disguise, because it pushed him to start his own small bakery, which is now very successful.","t":"失去那份工作反而是因禍得福，因為這促使他開了自己的小麵包店，現在非常成功。"},{"w":"blink","p":"v.","d":"to close and open your eyes very quickly","c":"眨眼","s":"When the doctor shone the bright light into my eyes, I could not stop myself from trying to blink.","t":"當醫生把亮光照進我的眼睛時，我忍不住想眨眼。","h":1},{"w":"blink","p":"n.","d":"a quick closing and opening of the eyes","c":"眨眼","s":"The magician made the coin disappear in a blink, and none of the children could figure out how he did it.","t":"魔術師在一眨眼間讓硬幣消失了，沒有一個孩子能弄清楚他是怎麼做到的。"},{"w":"in the blink of an eye","p":"phr.","d":"very quickly; in a very short time","c":"一眨眼；轉瞬間","s":"Summer vacation passed in the blink of an eye, and suddenly we were back in the classroom with new books and a new teacher.","t":"暑假一眨眼就過了，我們突然又回到教室，有了新書和新老師。"},{"w":"bloom","p":"v.","d":"to produce flowers","c":"開花","s":"The roses in my grandmother's garden bloom every May, and the whole street smells sweet for two weeks.","t":"我奶奶花園裡的玫瑰每年五月開花，整條街有兩週都香香的。","h":1},{"w":"bloom","p":"n.","d":"a flower, especially on a plant that people admire","c":"花；花朵","s":"The cherry trees along the river were covered in pink blooms, so hundreds of people came to take photos.","t":"河邊的櫻花樹開滿粉紅色的花朵，所以數百人前來拍照。","a":"blooms"},{"w":"in bloom","p":"phr.","d":"with its flowers open","c":"開花中；盛開","s":"The best time to visit the park is in early spring, when the tulips are in bloom and the weather is still cool.","t":"參觀這座公園最好的時間是早春，那時鬱金香正盛開，天氣還很涼爽。"},{"w":"blooming","p":"adj.","d":"full of flowers; healthy and happy","c":"盛開的；容光煥發的","s":"The blooming garden behind the old house attracted so many butterflies that the children spent the whole afternoon chasing them.","t":"老房子後面盛開的花園吸引了許多蝴蝶，孩子們整個下午都在追蝴蝶。"},{"w":"blossom","p":"n.","d":"a flower on a tree or bush, especially a fruit tree","c":"（樹上的）花","s":"In March, the plum trees on the mountain are full of white blossoms, and the farmers know spring has arrived.","t":"三月時，山上的梅樹開滿白色的花，農民就知道春天到了。","a":"blossoms","h":1},{"w":"blossom","p":"v.","d":"to produce flowers; to grow and become more successful","c":"開花；成長茁壯","s":"After she joined the drama club, the shy girl began to blossom and soon became one of the most confident students in class.","t":"加入戲劇社後，那個害羞的女孩開始成長茁壯，很快就成為班上最有自信的學生之一。"},{"w":"cherry blossom","p":"n.phr.","d":"the pink or white flower of a cherry tree","c":"櫻花","s":"Every spring, thousands of tourists travel to Japan to see the cherry blossom season, which lasts only about ten days.","t":"每年春天，成千上萬的遊客到日本看櫻花季，花期只有大約十天。"},{"w":"in full blossom","p":"phr.","d":"with all its flowers open","c":"盛開","s":"The apple trees were in full blossom when we visited the farm, so the whole hillside looked like it was covered in snow.","t":"我們參觀農場時，蘋果樹正盛開，整個山坡看起來像被雪覆蓋一樣。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"boast – carve","cards":[{"w":"boast","p":"v.","d":"to talk too proudly about what you have or can do","c":"自誇；吹噓","s":"Nobody likes to sit next to Kevin at lunch because he always boasts about his expensive shoes and his high test scores.","t":"沒有人喜歡午餐時坐在凱文旁邊，因為他總是吹噓他昂貴的鞋子和很高的考試分數。","a":"boasts","h":1},{"w":"boast about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak too proudly about something","c":"誇耀…","s":"My uncle loves to boast about his new car, and he shows everyone pictures of it on his phone at every family dinner.","t":"我叔叔喜歡誇耀他的新車，每次家庭聚餐都給每個人看手機裡的照片。"},{"w":"boast","p":"n.","d":"a proud statement about yourself","c":"自誇的話；豪語","s":"His boast that he could finish the marathon in three hours made his friends laugh, because he never trains.","t":"他說能在三小時內跑完馬拉松的豪語讓朋友們大笑，因為他從來不訓練。"},{"w":"boastful","p":"adj.","d":"talking too proudly about yourself","c":"自誇的；愛吹噓的","s":"The new player is very talented, but his boastful comments after the game made the rest of the team dislike him.","t":"這位新球員很有天分，但他賽後自誇的言論讓隊上其他人不喜歡他。"},{"w":"bond","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of friendship or love that connects people","c":"情感聯繫；羈絆","s":"The bond between the twins is so strong that they often know what the other is thinking without saying a word.","t":"這對雙胞胎之間的情感聯繫非常強，他們常常不用說話就知道對方在想什麼。","h":1},{"w":"bond","p":"v.","d":"to develop a close relationship with someone","c":"建立感情；培養關係","s":"The new teacher took the class camping for two days so that the students could bond with each other before the school year began.","t":"新老師帶全班去露營兩天，好讓學生在學年開始前彼此建立感情。"},{"w":"bond with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to form a close relationship with a person or animal","c":"與…建立親密關係","s":"It took the shy puppy a few weeks to bond with its new family, but now it follows my little sister everywhere.","t":"那隻害羞的小狗花了幾週才和新家人建立感情，但現在牠到處跟著我妹妹。"},{"w":"a strong bond","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very close connection between people","c":"深厚的感情；緊密的連結","s":"Working together through the typhoon created a strong bond among the volunteers, and they still meet for dinner every month.","t":"在颱風期間一起工作讓志工之間產生了深厚的感情，他們現在每個月仍會聚餐。"},{"w":"bounce","p":"v.","d":"to move up or away quickly after hitting a surface","c":"彈起；反彈","s":"The basketball hit the edge of the ring and bounced off the court, so the other team got the ball.","t":"籃球打到籃框邊緣，彈出了球場，所以球權歸另一隊。","a":"bounced","h":1},{"w":"bounce","p":"n.","d":"a movement of something hitting a surface and moving away again","c":"彈跳；反彈","s":"The tennis ball took a strange bounce on the wet ground, and the player missed it completely.","t":"網球在濕地上出現奇怪的反彈，球員完全沒接到。"},{"w":"bounce back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become healthy or successful again after a difficult time","c":"恢復；東山再起","s":"After losing the first three games of the season, the team managed to bounce back and win the championship in the end.","t":"球隊在本季前三場輸球後，設法東山再起，最後贏得冠軍。"},{"w":"bouncy","p":"adj.","d":"able to bounce well; full of energy","c":"有彈性的；活潑的","s":"The children spent the whole afternoon jumping on the bouncy castle at the birthday party and did not want to go home.","t":"孩子們在生日派對上整個下午都在充氣城堡上跳來跳去，不想回家。"},{"w":"bracelet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of jewelry that you wear around your wrist","c":"手鐲；手鍊","s":"My grandmother gave me a silver bracelet for my sixteenth birthday, and I wear it on my left wrist every day.","t":"我奶奶在我十六歲生日時送我一條銀手鍊，我每天都戴在左手腕上。","h":1},{"w":"friendship bracelet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a simple bracelet made of thread that friends give each other","c":"友誼手環","s":"The girls made a colorful friendship bracelet for each other at summer camp and promised to keep in touch after they went home.","t":"女孩們在夏令營互相做了彩色的友誼手環，並答應回家後保持聯絡。"},{"w":"brace","p":"n.","d":"something that holds a weak part of the body in place and supports it","c":"支架；護具","s":"After the accident, the doctor told him to wear a neck brace for six weeks so that the bones could heal properly.","t":"意外之後，醫生要他戴六週的頸部護具，讓骨頭能好好癒合。"},{"w":"braces","p":"n.","d":"metal wires that straighten teeth","c":"牙套；牙齒矯正器","s":"My brother has to wear braces for two years, and he cannot eat hard candy or chew gum during that time.","t":"我哥哥必須戴兩年的牙套，在那段期間他不能吃硬糖或嚼口香糖。"},{"w":"breed","p":"n.","d":"a particular type of animal, especially a dog, cat, or horse","c":"品種","s":"The golden retriever is a popular breed of dog in Taiwan because it is friendly and gentle with small children.","t":"黃金獵犬是台灣受歡迎的狗品種，因為牠對小孩友善又溫和。","h":1},{"w":"breed, bred, bred","p":"v.","d":"to keep animals so that they produce young; (of animals) to have babies","c":"飼養；繁殖","s":"My uncle has bred horses on his farm for twenty years, and some of them have won prizes in national races.","t":"我叔叔在農場飼養馬匹已經二十年了，其中有些還在全國賽馬中得過獎。","a":"bred"},{"w":"breeder","p":"n.","d":"a person who keeps animals to produce young ones","c":"飼養者；培育者","s":"We bought our cat from a breeder who takes good care of her animals and lets buyers visit the kittens first.","t":"我們的貓是向一位飼養者買的，她把動物照顧得很好，還讓買家先來看小貓。"},{"w":"breeding","p":"n.","d":"the keeping of animals or plants to produce young","c":"繁殖；飼養","s":"Spring is the breeding season for many birds, so visitors to the park are asked not to go near the nests.","t":"春天是許多鳥類的繁殖季節，所以公園請遊客不要靠近鳥巢。"},{"w":"bridegroom","p":"n.","d":"a man on the day he gets married","c":"新郎","s":"The bridegroom looked nervous as he waited at the front of the church, but he smiled widely when the music started.","t":"新郎在教堂前方等待時看起來很緊張，但音樂響起時他露出大大的笑容。","h":1},{"w":"groom","p":"n.","d":"a man who is getting married (short for bridegroom)","c":"新郎","s":"The groom and his friends arrived at the wedding party in a long white car decorated with red ribbons.","t":"新郎和他的朋友們坐著裝飾紅緞帶的白色長禮車抵達婚宴。"},{"w":"groom","p":"v.","d":"to clean and brush an animal; to prepare someone for a job","c":"梳理（動物的毛）；培養","s":"Every Sunday morning, my sister helps groom the horses at the riding club by brushing their coats and cleaning their feet.","t":"每個星期天早上，我姐姐在騎馬俱樂部幫忙梳理馬匹，刷牠們的毛並清潔牠們的腳。"},{"w":"bride","p":"n.","d":"a woman on the day she gets married","c":"新娘","s":"The bride wore a long white dress with small flowers in her hair, and everyone said she looked beautiful.","t":"新娘穿著長長的白色禮服，頭髮上別著小花，每個人都說她看起來很美。"},{"w":"bride and groom","p":"n.phr.","d":"the woman and man who are getting married","c":"新郎新娘；新人","s":"At the end of the wedding dinner, the bride and groom walked from table to table to thank all of their guests.","t":"婚宴結束時，新郎新娘一桌一桌地走去感謝所有賓客。"},{"w":"broke","p":"adj.","d":"having no money","c":"沒錢的；身無分文的","s":"I would love to go to the concert with you, but I am completely broke until I get paid next Friday.","t":"我很想和你一起去聽演唱會，但在下週五領薪水之前我完全沒錢。","h":1},{"w":"go broke","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lose all your money","c":"破產；花光錢","s":"If you keep buying a new phone every six months, you will go broke long before you finish university.","t":"如果你每六個月就買一支新手機，你在大學畢業前很久就會花光錢。"},{"w":"break, broke, broken","p":"v.","d":"to separate into pieces; to stop working","c":"打破；弄壞；故障","s":"My little brother broke the kitchen window with a baseball yesterday, so my parents made him pay for a new one.","t":"我弟弟昨天用棒球打破了廚房的窗戶，所以我父母要他付錢換一扇新的。","a":"broke"},{"w":"broken","p":"adj.","d":"in pieces; not working","c":"破碎的；壞掉的","s":"The elevator in our building has been broken for a week, so my grandmother has to climb six floors every day.","t":"我們大樓的電梯已經壞了一個星期，所以我奶奶每天都得爬六層樓。"},{"w":"broom","p":"n.","d":"a brush with a long handle for cleaning the floor","c":"掃帚","s":"Please take the broom from the corner and sweep up the glass before someone steps on it and gets hurt.","t":"請從角落拿掃帚把玻璃掃起來，免得有人踩到受傷。","h":1},{"w":"broomstick","p":"n.","d":"the long handle of a broom; the broom a witch flies on in stories","c":"掃帚柄；（女巫的）飛天掃帚","s":"In the story, the young witch flies over the city on her broomstick to deliver packages to people who need help.","t":"故事中，年輕的女巫騎著飛天掃帚飛越城市，把包裹送給需要幫助的人。"},{"w":"sweep, swept, swept","p":"v.","d":"to clean a floor with a broom","c":"掃；清掃","s":"Every student has to sweep the classroom floor after school once a week, and the teacher checks the corners carefully.","t":"每位學生每週一次要在放學後掃教室地板，老師會仔細檢查角落。","a":"sweep"},{"w":"brutal","p":"adj.","d":"very cruel and violent","c":"殘忍的；野蠻的","s":"The movie was too brutal for young children, so the parents decided to leave the theater before it ended.","t":"這部電影對幼童來說太殘忍了，所以家長們決定在電影結束前離開戲院。","h":1},{"w":"brutally","p":"adv.","d":"in a very cruel or honest way","c":"殘忍地；毫不留情地","s":"The coach was brutally honest about our poor performance, but his words helped us train harder for the final.","t":"教練對我們糟糕的表現毫不留情地直言，但他的話讓我們更努力為決賽訓練。"},{"w":"brutality","p":"n.","d":"very cruel and violent behavior","c":"殘忍；暴行","s":"The old man still remembers the brutality of the war, and he tells his grandchildren that peace is the most precious thing.","t":"老人仍然記得戰爭的殘酷，他告訴孫子們和平是最珍貴的東西。"},{"w":"brute","p":"n.","d":"a cruel, violent person or animal","c":"殘暴的人；野獸","s":"The man who kicked the stray dog in the park is a real brute, and several people reported him to the police.","t":"那個在公園裡踢流浪狗的男人真是個殘暴的人，好幾個人向警方檢舉了他。"},{"w":"bulletin","p":"n.","d":"a short official news report or announcement","c":"公告；簡報","s":"The school sends out a weekly bulletin to parents with news about tests, trips, and sports events for the coming week.","t":"學校每週寄一份簡報給家長，內容是下週的考試、校外教學和運動賽事消息。","h":1},{"w":"bulletin board","p":"n.phr.","d":"a board on a wall where notices are put up","c":"布告欄","s":"Check the bulletin board outside the office every morning because the teacher posts the new homework and club news there.","t":"每天早上要看辦公室外的布告欄，因為老師會把新的作業和社團消息貼在那裡。"},{"w":"news bulletin","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short news report on TV or radio","c":"新聞快報","s":"We stopped the movie to watch a special news bulletin about the typhoon, which said that schools would be closed tomorrow.","t":"我們停下電影去看一則關於颱風的特別新聞快報，報導說明天學校停課。"},{"w":"burglar","p":"n.","d":"a person who enters a building to steal things","c":"竊賊；闖空門的小偷","s":"A burglar climbed through the open bathroom window while the family was on holiday and took their laptop and jewelry.","t":"一名竊賊趁這家人度假時從打開的浴室窗戶爬進去，偷走了他們的筆電和珠寶。","h":1},{"w":"burglary","p":"n.","d":"the crime of entering a building to steal","c":"入室竊盜","s":"There have been three cases of burglary on our street this month, so the neighbors are planning to install more cameras.","t":"我們這條街這個月發生了三起入室竊盜案，所以鄰居們打算裝更多攝影機。"},{"w":"burglarize","p":"v.","d":"to enter a building and steal things from it","c":"闖入…行竊","s":"Someone tried to burglarize the corner shop last night, but the alarm went off and the thief ran away empty-handed.","t":"昨晚有人試圖闖入轉角那家店行竊，但警報響了，小偷空手逃走。"},{"w":"burglar alarm","p":"n.phr.","d":"a device that makes a loud noise when someone breaks into a building","c":"防盜警報器","s":"My parents had a burglar alarm installed after the robbery next door, and now it rings loudly if any window is opened at night.","t":"隔壁遭竊後，我父母裝了一個防盜警報器，現在晚上任何窗戶被打開它都會大聲響。"},{"w":"cabinet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of furniture with shelves or drawers for storing things","c":"櫥櫃；櫃子","s":"Please put the clean plates back in the cabinet above the sink, and make sure you close the door tightly.","t":"請把乾淨的盤子放回水槽上方的櫥櫃，並確定把門關緊。","h":1},{"w":"cabinet","p":"n.","d":"the group of top government ministers who advise the leader","c":"內閣","s":"The president met with her cabinet this morning to discuss how to help farmers after the terrible flood.","t":"總統今天早上和她的內閣開會，討論如何在嚴重水災後幫助農民。"},{"w":"kitchen cabinet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cupboard in a kitchen for storing food or dishes","c":"廚房櫥櫃","s":"My mother keeps the snacks in the highest kitchen cabinet so that my little brother cannot reach them without asking.","t":"我媽媽把零食放在最高的廚房櫥櫃裡，這樣我弟弟不問就拿不到。"},{"w":"filing cabinet","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tall metal cupboard with drawers for storing papers","c":"檔案櫃","s":"The secretary keeps every student's records in a locked filing cabinet in the corner of the school office.","t":"秘書把每位學生的資料都放在學校辦公室角落一個上鎖的檔案櫃裡。"},{"w":"calculate","p":"v.","d":"to find a number or amount by using math","c":"計算","s":"Before we order the pizzas, let me calculate how much each person needs to pay so that nobody has to pay extra.","t":"在我們訂披薩之前，讓我計算一下每個人要付多少錢，這樣就沒有人需要多付。","h":1},{"w":"calculation","p":"n.","d":"the act of using math to find a number; the result you get","c":"計算；計算結果","s":"According to my calculation, we will need about forty bottles of water for the twenty students on the two-day trip.","t":"根據我的計算，兩天的旅行中二十名學生大約需要四十瓶水。","h":1},{"w":"calculator","p":"n.","d":"a small electronic machine that does math","c":"計算機","s":"You may use a calculator in the science exam, but you still have to show how you got each answer on the paper.","t":"你可以在理化考試中使用計算機，但你仍然必須在考卷上寫出每個答案是怎麼算出來的。"},{"w":"miscalculate","p":"v.","d":"to make a mistake when working out a number or judging a situation","c":"算錯；誤判","s":"The builders miscalculated the amount of wood they needed, so the work stopped for a week while they waited for more.","t":"建築工人算錯了需要的木材量，所以工程停了一週等待更多木材送來。","a":"miscalculated"},{"w":"calorie","p":"n.","d":"a unit for measuring how much energy food gives you","c":"卡路里；熱量","s":"A can of soda has about one hundred and forty calories, which is more than many people expect for a single drink.","t":"一罐汽水大約有一百四十卡路里，比許多人對單一飲料的預期還多。","a":"calories","h":1},{"w":"low-calorie","p":"adj.","d":"containing only a small amount of energy","c":"低熱量的","s":"My aunt only buys low-calorie snacks now because her doctor told her to lose some weight before the operation.","t":"我阿姨現在只買低熱量的零食，因為醫生要她在手術前減重。"},{"w":"burn calories","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use up energy by moving your body","c":"消耗熱量","s":"Riding a bicycle to school is a fun way to burn calories every morning, and it saves money on bus tickets too.","t":"騎腳踏車上學是每天早上消耗熱量的有趣方式，而且也能省下公車錢。"},{"w":"count calories","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep a record of how much energy you eat","c":"計算熱量","s":"Some people count calories with a phone app at every meal, but my doctor says eating more vegetables is a simpler plan.","t":"有些人每餐都用手機應用程式計算熱量，但我的醫生說多吃蔬菜是更簡單的方法。"},{"w":"campaign","p":"n.","d":"a series of planned activities to achieve a goal, such as winning an election","c":"活動；運動；競選活動","s":"The city started a campaign to get people to use less plastic, and now many shops no longer give out free bags.","t":"市政府發起了一項減少塑膠使用的運動，現在許多商店不再提供免費袋子。","h":1},{"w":"campaign","p":"v.","d":"to take part in planned activities to achieve a goal","c":"參加競選；發起運動","s":"The students decided to campaign for a longer lunch break, so they collected signatures and spoke to the principal.","t":"學生們決定為了延長午休時間發起運動，所以他們收集簽名並和校長談話。"},{"w":"election campaign","p":"n.phr.","d":"the activities a politician does to win votes","c":"競選活動","s":"During the election campaign, the candidates visited markets and temples every day to shake hands with voters.","t":"在競選活動期間，候選人每天到市場和廟宇與選民握手。"},{"w":"advertising campaign","p":"n.phr.","d":"a series of advertisements to sell a product","c":"廣告宣傳活動","s":"The company spent millions of dollars on an advertising campaign for its new phone, with posters in every MRT station.","t":"這家公司花了數百萬元為新手機做廣告宣傳活動，每個捷運站都有海報。"},{"w":"campaigner","p":"n.","d":"a person who works to achieve social or political change","c":"活動人士；倡導者","s":"The young campaigner has spent five years asking the government to build safer bicycle paths in the city.","t":"這位年輕的倡導者花了五年時間要求政府在市內建造更安全的自行車道。"},{"w":"candidate","p":"n.","d":"a person who is trying to get a job or be elected","c":"候選人；應徵者","s":"Over fifty people applied for the job, but only three candidates were invited to the final interview with the manager.","t":"有五十多人應徵這份工作，但只有三位應徵者被邀請參加和經理的最後面試。","a":"candidates","h":1},{"w":"presidential candidate","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is trying to be elected president","c":"總統候選人","s":"Each presidential candidate was given ten minutes on TV last night to explain how he or she would improve the economy.","t":"昨晚每位總統候選人在電視上有十分鐘說明他或她將如何改善經濟。"},{"w":"job candidate","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is trying to get a particular job","c":"求職者；應徵者","s":"A good job candidate should arrive early, dress neatly, and be ready to talk about why he or she wants the position.","t":"好的求職者應該提早到、穿著整齊，並準備好說明為什麼想要這個職位。"},{"w":"candidacy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a candidate in an election","c":"候選人資格；參選","s":"The mayor announced her candidacy for a second term at a big party in the city square last Saturday.","t":"市長上週六在市區廣場的大型活動上宣布參選連任。"},{"w":"cane","p":"n.","d":"a long stick that helps a person walk","c":"手杖；拐杖","s":"Since his knee operation, my grandfather has walked with a wooden cane, but he still goes to the park every morning.","t":"自從膝蓋手術後，我爺爺走路要用木製手杖，但他每天早上仍然去公園。","h":1},{"w":"cane","p":"n.","d":"the long hard stem of some plants, such as sugar cane or bamboo","c":"莖；藤條","s":"The farmers cut the tall cane by hand and loaded it onto trucks that took it to the sugar factory.","t":"農民用手砍下高高的甘蔗莖，裝上卡車運到糖廠。"},{"w":"sugar cane","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tall plant from which sugar is made","c":"甘蔗","s":"In southern Taiwan, fields of sugar cane used to stretch for miles, and children loved to chew the sweet stems.","t":"在台灣南部，甘蔗田曾經綿延數英里，孩子們喜歡嚼甜甜的莖。"},{"w":"candy cane","p":"n.phr.","d":"a hard red and white stick-shaped candy for Christmas","c":"拐杖糖","s":"My aunt hangs a candy cane on every branch of the Christmas tree, and the children are allowed to eat them on Christmas morning.","t":"我阿姨在聖誕樹的每根樹枝上掛一支拐杖糖，孩子們可以在聖誕節早上吃。"},{"w":"canoe","p":"n.","d":"a light narrow boat that you move with a paddle","c":"獨木舟","s":"We rented a canoe at the lake and paddled slowly along the shore, watching the birds in the tall grass.","t":"我們在湖邊租了一艘獨木舟，沿著岸邊慢慢划，看著高草叢中的鳥。","h":1},{"w":"canoe","p":"v.","d":"to travel in a canoe","c":"划獨木舟","s":"My father and I plan to canoe down the river this summer, camping on the sandbanks each night along the way.","t":"我爸爸和我計畫今年夏天沿河划獨木舟而下，沿途每晚在沙洲上露營。"},{"w":"canoeing","p":"n.","d":"the sport or activity of traveling in a canoe","c":"划獨木舟（運動）","s":"Canoeing is my favorite summer activity because it is quiet, it is good exercise, and you can see wildlife up close.","t":"划獨木舟是我最喜歡的夏季活動，因為它很安靜、是很好的運動，而且可以近距離看野生動物。","a":"Canoeing"},{"w":"go canoeing","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spend time traveling in a canoe for fun","c":"去划獨木舟","s":"If the weather is fine this weekend, we will go canoeing on the lake and have a picnic on the small island.","t":"如果這個週末天氣好，我們會到湖上去划獨木舟，並在小島上野餐。"},{"w":"capacity","p":"n.","d":"the largest amount that something can hold or produce","c":"容量；容納量","s":"The new stadium has a capacity of forty thousand people, and every seat was sold for the opening game.","t":"新體育場的容納量是四萬人，開幕賽的每個座位都賣光了。","h":1},{"w":"capacity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do or understand something","c":"能力","s":"Young children have an amazing capacity for learning languages, so many parents start English lessons early.","t":"幼童有驚人的語言學習能力，所以許多家長很早就開始讓孩子上英語課。"},{"w":"capable","p":"adj.","d":"able to do something well","c":"有能力的；能幹的","s":"Although she is only twenty-three, the new manager is very capable and has already solved several problems that worried the staff.","t":"雖然她只有二十三歲，新經理非常能幹，已經解決了幾個讓員工擔心的問題。"},{"w":"capability","p":"n.","d":"the ability or power to do something","c":"能力；性能","s":"This small camera has the capability to record clear videos at night, which is perfect for watching animals in the forest.","t":"這台小相機有夜間錄製清晰影片的能力，非常適合觀察森林裡的動物。"},{"w":"incapable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to do something","c":"無能力的；不會…的","s":"My grandfather is incapable of using a smartphone, so we still call him on the old telephone in his living room.","t":"我爺爺不會使用智慧型手機，所以我們仍然打他客廳裡的老電話給他。"},{"w":"capital","p":"n.","d":"the most important city of a country, where the government is","c":"首都","s":"Taipei is the capital of Taiwan, and it is home to the government offices, many museums, and the tallest building on the island.","t":"台北是台灣的首都，政府機關、許多博物館和島上最高的建築都在這裡。","h":1},{"w":"capitalist","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns a business and uses money to make more money","c":"資本家","s":"The old capitalist built his first factory with a small loan and later owned more than twenty companies around the world.","t":"這位老資本家用一筆小貸款建立了第一家工廠，後來在世界各地擁有二十多家公司。","h":1},{"w":"capital","p":"n.","d":"money that is used to start or grow a business","c":"資本；資金","s":"My cousin needs more capital to open a second coffee shop, so she is asking the bank for a loan.","t":"我表姐需要更多資金來開第二家咖啡店，所以她正向銀行申請貸款。"},{"w":"capitalism","p":"n.","d":"an economic system in which businesses are owned by people, not the government","c":"資本主義","s":"Under capitalism, companies compete with each other for customers, and the government owns very few businesses.","t":"在資本主義下，公司彼此競爭顧客，而政府擁有的企業非常少。"},{"w":"capital letter","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large letter such as A, B, or C used at the start of a sentence or name","c":"大寫字母","s":"Remember to begin every sentence with a capital letter, and use one for names of people, cities, and countries as well.","t":"記得每個句子開頭要用大寫字母，人名、城市和國家的名稱也要用大寫。"},{"w":"capitalist","p":"adj.","d":"connected with capitalism","c":"資本主義的","s":"In a capitalist economy, prices usually go up when many people want the same product and only a few are available.","t":"在資本主義經濟中，當很多人想要同一產品而數量很少時，價格通常會上漲。"},{"w":"cargo","p":"n.","d":"goods that are carried by a ship, plane, or truck","c":"貨物","s":"The ship arrived at Kaohsiung port with a cargo of bananas from the Philippines, and workers unloaded it before dark.","t":"那艘船載著從菲律賓來的一批香蕉貨物抵達高雄港，工人在天黑前卸完貨。","h":1},{"w":"cargo ship","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large ship that carries goods","c":"貨船","s":"From the beach, we could see a huge cargo ship waiting outside the harbor for its turn to enter and unload.","t":"從海灘上我們可以看到一艘巨大的貨船在港外等待，輪到它進港卸貨。"},{"w":"cargo plane","p":"n.phr.","d":"a plane that carries goods instead of passengers","c":"貨機","s":"After the earthquake, a cargo plane full of tents, blankets, and medicine landed at the airport within twelve hours.","t":"地震後，一架載滿帳篷、毛毯和藥品的貨機在十二小時內降落機場。"},{"w":"carrier","p":"n.","d":"a company that transports goods or people; a person or animal that passes on a disease","c":"運輸公司；帶原者","s":"The package was late because the carrier lost it at the airport, and the company gave us our money back.","t":"包裹遲到是因為貨運公司在機場弄丟了它，公司把錢退還給我們。","h":1},{"w":"carry","p":"v.","d":"to hold something and take it somewhere","c":"攜帶；搬運","s":"My mother asked me to carry the heavy bags of rice from the car to the kitchen while she parked.","t":"我媽媽在停車時要我把沉重的米袋從車上搬到廚房。"},{"w":"carry out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do a task or plan","c":"執行；進行","s":"The scientists will carry out a series of tests on the river water to find out why so many fish have died.","t":"科學家將對河水進行一系列檢測，找出為什麼這麼多魚死亡。"},{"w":"carry on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to continue doing something","c":"繼續","s":"Even though it started to rain, the players decided to carry on with the game until the lightning began.","t":"雖然開始下雨了，球員們決定繼續比賽，直到開始打閃電。"},{"w":"aircraft carrier","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very large warship that planes can take off from and land on","c":"航空母艦","s":"An aircraft carrier is like a floating airport, and more than five thousand people can live and work on it at sea.","t":"航空母艦像一座漂浮的機場，五千多人可以在海上的艦上生活和工作。"},{"w":"carve","p":"v.","d":"to make an object or pattern by cutting wood or stone; to cut cooked meat into pieces","c":"雕刻；切（肉）","s":"The old man can carve a small bird out of a piece of wood in less than an hour, using only a simple knife.","t":"那位老人只用一把簡單的刀，不到一小時就能用一塊木頭雕刻出一隻小鳥。","h":1},{"w":"carving","p":"n.","d":"an object or pattern made by cutting wood or stone","c":"雕刻品；雕刻","s":"My grandfather bought a beautiful wooden carving of a dragon in Sanyi, and it now sits on the table in our living room.","t":"我爺爺在三義買了一件美麗的木雕龍，現在放在我們客廳的桌上。"},{"w":"wood carving","p":"n.phr.","d":"the art of cutting shapes out of wood; an object made this way","c":"木雕","s":"The small town is famous for its wood carving, and tourists can watch the artists at work in the shops along the main street.","t":"這個小鎮以木雕聞名，遊客可以在大街沿線的店裡觀看藝術家工作。"},{"w":"carved","p":"adj.","d":"cut into a shape or pattern from wood or stone","c":"雕刻的；刻有花紋的","s":"The temple doors are covered with carved flowers and animals that were made by hand more than two hundred years ago.","t":"廟門上布滿了雕刻的花朵和動物，是兩百多年前手工製作的。"}]},{"unit":6,"theme":"catalogue – cliff","cards":[{"w":"catalogue","p":"n.","d":"a list of all the things you can buy, see, or borrow from a place","c":"目錄","s":"Before we visited the furniture store, my mother looked through the catalogue and marked the sofas she liked.","t":"在我們去家具店之前，媽媽先翻閱了目錄，並標出她喜歡的沙發。","h":1},{"w":"catalogue","p":"v.","d":"to make a complete list of things in order","c":"編目；列入目錄","s":"The librarian spent the whole summer trying to catalogue the old books that were donated by a retired professor.","t":"圖書館員花了整個夏天，努力把一位退休教授捐贈的舊書編目。"},{"w":"catalog","p":"n.","d":"the American spelling of catalogue","c":"目錄（美式拼法）","s":"The university sends a course catalog to every new student, so they can choose their classes before the semester starts.","t":"大學會寄一本課程目錄給每位新生，讓他們在學期開始前選課。"},{"w":"category","p":"n.","d":"a group of people or things that are similar in some way","c":"類別；種類","s":"Movies in this category are only for adults, so the cinema staff checked our ID cards at the door.","t":"這個類別的電影只限成人觀看，所以電影院員工在門口檢查了我們的身分證。","h":1},{"w":"categorize","p":"v.","d":"to put people or things into groups by type","c":"分類","s":"The teacher asked us to categorize the animals into three groups: those that fly, swim, or walk.","t":"老師要我們把動物分類成三組：會飛的、會游的和會走的。"},{"w":"fall into a category","p":"v.phr.","d":"to belong to a certain group or type","c":"屬於某一類別","s":"Whales fall into the category of mammals rather than fish, even though they live in the sea and look like huge fish.","t":"鯨魚屬於哺乳動物的類別而不是魚類，即使它們生活在海裡，看起來像巨大的魚。","a":"fall into the category"},{"w":"cease","p":"v.","d":"to stop happening or stop doing something","c":"停止","s":"The heavy rain finally began to cease at midnight, and the workers were able to repair the broken bridge the next morning.","t":"大雨終於在午夜開始停止，工人隔天早上才得以修理損壞的橋。","h":1},{"w":"cease to do sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to no longer do something","c":"不再做某事","s":"After the factory closed, the small town slowly ceased to be a busy place, and many young people moved to the city.","t":"工廠關閉後，這個小鎮慢慢地不再是個熱鬧的地方，許多年輕人搬到城市去了。","a":"ceased to"},{"w":"ceaseless","p":"adj.","d":"never stopping; continuing all the time","c":"不停的；不斷的","s":"The ceaseless noise from the construction site next door made it impossible for me to study for my final exams.","t":"隔壁工地不停的噪音讓我根本無法為期末考讀書。"},{"w":"ceasefire","p":"n.","d":"an agreement to stop fighting for a period of time","c":"停火","s":"Both sides agreed to a ceasefire so that doctors could enter the city and help the people who were hurt.","t":"雙方同意停火，這樣醫生才能進入城市幫助受傷的人。"},{"w":"celebration","p":"n.","d":"a party or special event for an important day","c":"慶祝活動；慶典","s":"The celebration of my grandparents' fiftieth wedding anniversary was held in a big restaurant, and over a hundred relatives came.","t":"我爺爺奶奶金婚五十週年的慶祝活動在一家大餐廳舉行，來了一百多位親戚。","h":1},{"w":"celebrate","p":"v.","d":"to do something special and enjoyable for an important event","c":"慶祝","s":"We are going to celebrate my sister's graduation by having dinner at her favorite Japanese restaurant this Saturday.","t":"這個星期六我們要到我姐姐最愛的日本餐廳吃晚餐，來慶祝她畢業。"},{"w":"celebrated","p":"adj.","d":"famous and praised by many people","c":"著名的；備受讚譽的","s":"The celebrated chef opened a new restaurant in Taipei, and people waited in line for three hours to taste his food.","t":"這位著名的廚師在台北開了一家新餐廳，人們排隊三小時只為品嚐他的料理。"},{"w":"celebrity","p":"n.","d":"a famous person, especially in entertainment","c":"名人","s":"When the celebrity walked into the shopping mall, hundreds of fans ran toward her and asked for photos.","t":"當那位名人走進購物中心時，數百名粉絲衝向她要求合照。"},{"w":"in celebration of","p":"phr.","d":"in order to celebrate something","c":"為了慶祝…","s":"The city held a huge fireworks show in celebration of its one hundredth birthday, and the sky was bright for twenty minutes.","t":"這座城市為了慶祝一百歲生日舉辦了盛大的煙火秀，天空亮了二十分鐘。"},{"w":"chamber","p":"n.","d":"a room used for a special purpose; a closed space inside something","c":"房間；室；腔","s":"The king's secret chamber was hidden behind a large painting, and only his most trusted servants knew about it.","t":"國王的秘密房間藏在一幅大畫後面，只有他最信任的僕人知道。","h":1},{"w":"chamber music","p":"n.phr.","d":"classical music played by a small group of musicians","c":"室內樂","s":"My aunt plays the cello in a chamber music group, and they perform in small halls where the audience can sit very close.","t":"我阿姨在一個室內樂團裡拉大提琴，他們在觀眾可以坐得很近的小廳演出。"},{"w":"chamber of commerce","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of business people who work together to help local business","c":"商會","s":"The local chamber of commerce organized a night market festival to bring more visitors to the shops in the old town.","t":"當地商會舉辦了夜市節，為老城區的商店帶來更多遊客。"},{"w":"championship","p":"n.","d":"a competition to find the best player or team","c":"錦標賽；冠軍賽","s":"Our school basketball team won the national championship last year, and the whole town celebrated with a big parade.","t":"我們學校的籃球隊去年贏得全國錦標賽，全鎮舉辦了一場大遊行來慶祝。","h":1},{"w":"champion","p":"n.","d":"a person or team that wins a competition","c":"冠軍","s":"The young tennis player became the youngest champion in the history of the tournament when she was only seventeen.","t":"這位年輕的網球選手在十七歲時成為該賽事史上最年輕的冠軍。"},{"w":"defending champion","p":"n.phr.","d":"the player or team that won the last competition","c":"衛冕冠軍","s":"Nobody expected the defending champion to lose in the first round, so the fans in the stadium were shocked and silent.","t":"沒有人預料到衛冕冠軍會在第一輪就輸掉，所以體育場裡的球迷震驚又沉默。"},{"w":"champion","p":"v.","d":"to support or fight for an idea or a group of people","c":"擁護；支持","s":"The famous actress has used her fame to champion the rights of children who cannot afford to go to school.","t":"這位知名女演員利用她的名氣來擁護無法負擔上學費用的孩子的權利。"},{"w":"characteristic","p":"n.","d":"a typical quality or feature of a person or thing","c":"特徵；特色","s":"Patience is an important characteristic of a good teacher, because students do not always understand things the first time.","t":"耐心是好老師的重要特徵，因為學生不一定第一次就能理解。","h":1},{"w":"characteristic","p":"adj.","d":"typical of a particular person or thing","c":"典型的；特有的","s":"With his characteristic big smile, the host welcomed every guest at the door and remembered all of their names.","t":"主持人帶著他特有的大笑容在門口歡迎每位來賓，而且記得他們所有人的名字。"},{"w":"character","p":"n.","d":"the qualities that make a person who they are; a person in a story","c":"性格；人物；角色","s":"My favorite character in the novel is the brave little girl who saves her village from the dragon.","t":"這本小說裡我最喜歡的角色是那個勇敢的小女孩，她從惡龍手中救了她的村子。"},{"w":"characterize","p":"v.","d":"to describe the typical qualities of something","c":"描繪…的特性；是…的特徵","s":"Heavy rain and strong winds characterize the typhoon season in Taiwan, so people always prepare extra food and water.","t":"大雨和強風是台灣颱風季節的特徵，所以人們總是會準備額外的食物和水。"},{"w":"charity","p":"n.","d":"an organization that helps poor or sick people; the act of giving to them","c":"慈善機構；慈善","s":"Every winter, my family gives warm clothes to a charity that takes care of homeless people in the city.","t":"每年冬天，我們家都會把保暖衣物送給一個照顧城裡無家可歸者的慈善機構。","h":1},{"w":"charitable","p":"adj.","d":"kind and generous in helping people who need it","c":"慈善的；仁慈的","s":"The charitable businessman donated half of his money to build free hospitals for children in poor villages.","t":"這位慈善的企業家捐出一半的財產，為貧窮村莊的孩子蓋免費醫院。"},{"w":"for charity","p":"phr.","d":"in order to raise money to help people in need","c":"為了慈善；為公益","s":"The students sold homemade cookies at the school fair for charity, and they raised twenty thousand dollars in one day.","t":"學生們在園遊會上為公益販售自製餅乾，一天就募到了兩萬元。"},{"w":"chemistry","p":"n.","d":"the science that studies what things are made of and how they change","c":"化學","s":"In our chemistry class today, we mixed two clear liquids together, and they suddenly turned bright blue.","t":"今天的化學課上，我們把兩種透明液體混合在一起，它們突然變成了亮藍色。","h":1},{"w":"chemical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to chemistry or produced by it","c":"化學的","s":"The chemical smell in the swimming pool was so strong that some of the children started coughing and had to leave.","t":"游泳池裡的化學味太重了，有些孩子開始咳嗽，不得不離開。"},{"w":"chemical","p":"n.","d":"a substance made by or used in chemistry","c":"化學物質；化學品","s":"Farmers should be careful when they spray this chemical on their fruit trees, because it can be harmful to bees.","t":"農民在果樹上噴灑這種化學藥劑時應該小心，因為它可能對蜜蜂有害。"},{"w":"chemist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies chemistry; a pharmacist (UK)","c":"化學家；藥劑師","s":"The chemist worked in her laboratory for ten years before she finally discovered a safer way to clean drinking water.","t":"這位化學家在實驗室裡工作了十年，終於找到一種更安全的淨化飲用水的方法。"},{"w":"cherish","p":"v.","d":"to love and take great care of someone or something","c":"珍惜；珍愛","s":"I will always cherish the handmade scarf my grandmother gave me, even though it is old and a little torn now.","t":"我會一直珍惜奶奶送我的手織圍巾，雖然它現在已經舊了，還有點破。","h":1},{"w":"cherished","p":"adj.","d":"loved and very important to someone","c":"珍愛的；珍視的","s":"Her most cherished dream is to open a small bookstore by the sea, where people can read all day.","t":"她最珍視的夢想是在海邊開一家小書店，讓人們可以整天閱讀。"},{"w":"cherish the memory of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep a happy memory of someone or something in your heart","c":"珍藏…的回憶","s":"Even after fifty years, my grandfather still cherishes the memory of the summer he spent fishing with his brothers by the river.","t":"即使過了五十年，我爺爺仍然珍藏著他和兄弟們在河邊釣魚的那個夏天的回憶。","a":"cherishes the memory of"},{"w":"chew","p":"v.","d":"to bite food several times with your teeth before swallowing","c":"咀嚼；咬","s":"The dentist told me to chew my food slowly on both sides, because my new tooth is still a little weak.","t":"牙醫告訴我要用兩側慢慢咀嚼食物，因為我的新牙還有點脆弱。","h":1},{"w":"chewing gum","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soft sweet that you chew but do not swallow","c":"口香糖","s":"You are not allowed to eat chewing gum in class, because some students stick it under the desks when they finish.","t":"上課時不可以吃口香糖，因為有些學生吃完後會把它黏在桌子底下。"},{"w":"chew on/over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think carefully about something for a long time","c":"仔細考慮；反覆思量","s":"The job offer sounds good, but let me chew on it for a few days before I give you my final answer.","t":"這份工作機會聽起來不錯，但在給你最後答覆之前，讓我仔細考慮幾天。","a":"chew on"},{"w":"chewy","p":"adj.","d":"needing to be chewed a lot before you can swallow it","c":"有嚼勁的；耐嚼的","s":"The bread at this bakery is soft on the outside but chewy inside, which is why my brother buys it every week.","t":"這家麵包店的麵包外軟內有嚼勁，這就是我哥哥每週都去買的原因。"},{"w":"choke","p":"v.","d":"to be unable to breathe because something is blocking your throat","c":"窒息；噎住；使窒息","s":"The thick smoke from the fire made the people in the building choke and cough as they ran toward the exit.","t":"火災產生的濃煙使大樓裡的人們在跑向出口時窒息咳嗽。","h":1},{"w":"choke on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have trouble breathing because of something in your throat","c":"被…噎住","s":"My little cousin almost choked on a piece of candy, so now my aunt only gives him soft food to eat.","t":"我的小表弟差點被一顆糖果噎住，所以現在我阿姨只給他吃軟的食物。","a":"choked on"},{"w":"choke back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop yourself from showing a strong feeling such as tears","c":"強忍（淚水、情緒）","s":"At the end of the graduation ceremony, the teacher had to choke back her tears as she said goodbye to the students.","t":"畢業典禮結束時，老師在向學生道別時不得不強忍淚水。"},{"w":"chorus","p":"n.","d":"the part of a song that is repeated after each verse","c":"合唱部分；副歌","s":"Most people cannot remember the words to the whole song, but everyone sings along when the chorus begins.","t":"大多數人記不住整首歌的歌詞，但副歌一開始大家就會跟著唱。","h":1},{"w":"chorus","p":"n.","d":"a large group of people who sing together","c":"合唱團","s":"My brother joined the school chorus this year, and they will perform at the Christmas concert in December.","t":"我哥哥今年加入了學校的合唱團，他們將在十二月的聖誕音樂會上表演。"},{"w":"in chorus","p":"phr.","d":"said or sung by many people at the same time","c":"齊聲；一致地","s":"When the teacher asked who wanted to go on the field trip, the whole class shouted \"Yes!\" in chorus.","t":"當老師問誰想去校外教學時，全班齊聲大喊：「要！」"},{"w":"choir","p":"n.","d":"a group of people who sing together, especially in a church or school","c":"合唱團；唱詩班","s":"The church choir practices every Thursday evening, and their beautiful singing can be heard from the street.","t":"教堂的唱詩班每週四晚上練習，從街上就能聽到他們美妙的歌聲。"},{"w":"circular","p":"adj.","d":"shaped like a circle; moving around in a circle","c":"圓形的；環形的","s":"The new library has a circular reading room in the center, so sunlight comes in from windows on every side.","t":"新圖書館中央有一間圓形的閱覽室，所以陽光能從四面的窗戶照進來。","h":1},{"w":"circulate","p":"v.","d":"to move around freely; to pass from person to person","c":"循環；流通；傳播","s":"Open the windows for a few minutes so that fresh air can circulate through the classroom before the test begins.","t":"把窗戶打開幾分鐘，讓新鮮空氣在考試開始前能在教室裡流通。","h":1},{"w":"circulation","p":"n.","d":"the movement of blood around the body; the movement of air, money, or news","c":"循環；流通；發行量","s":"Regular exercise improves your blood circulation, which is why your hands and feet feel warmer after a long walk.","t":"規律運動能改善血液循環，這就是為什麼長時間散步後你的手腳會覺得比較暖。","h":1},{"w":"circle","p":"n.","d":"a round shape; a group of people who know each other","c":"圓圈；圈子","s":"The children sat in a circle on the floor while the teacher read them a story about a clever fox.","t":"孩子們在地板上坐成一圈，老師則念一個關於聰明狐狸的故事給他們聽。"},{"w":"in circulation","p":"phr.","d":"being used or passed around among people","c":"在流通中；在使用中","s":"The old five-dollar bills are no longer in circulation, so you should take them to the bank and exchange them.","t":"舊的五元紙鈔已經不再流通，所以你應該拿去銀行兌換。"},{"w":"circumstance","p":"n.","d":"the facts or conditions that affect a situation","c":"情況；環境","s":"The police are still looking into the exact circumstances of the accident, so they have not told the family anything yet.","t":"警方仍在調查這場意外的確切情況，所以還沒有告訴家屬任何事。","a":"circumstances","h":1},{"w":"under the circumstances","p":"phr.","d":"because of the particular situation","c":"在這種情況下","s":"Our best player was sick and it rained all afternoon, so under the circumstances, a tied game was actually a good result.","t":"我們最好的球員生病了，而且整個下午都在下雨，所以在這種情況下，打成平手其實算是好結果。"},{"w":"under no circumstances","p":"phr.","d":"never, whatever happens","c":"無論如何都不","s":"Under no circumstances should you open the door to a stranger when your parents are not at home, even if he says he is a police officer.","t":"父母不在家時，無論如何都不可以幫陌生人開門，即使他說他是警察。","a":"Under no circumstances"},{"w":"civilian","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not a member of the army or police","c":"平民；百姓","s":"During the war, thousands of civilians left the city on foot, carrying only what they could hold in their hands.","t":"戰爭期間，數千名平民徒步離開這座城市，只帶著手裡拿得動的東西。","a":"civilians","h":1},{"w":"civilian","p":"adj.","d":"not belonging to the army or police","c":"平民的；民用的","s":"After twenty years as a soldier, my uncle returned to civilian life and opened a small coffee shop near the station.","t":"當了二十年軍人之後，我叔叔回到平民生活，在車站附近開了一家小咖啡店。","h":1},{"w":"civilization","p":"n.","d":"a society with its own culture, laws, and way of life, especially an advanced one","c":"文明","s":"The ancient Egyptian civilization built huge pyramids thousands of years ago, and people still wonder how they did it.","t":"古埃及文明在數千年前建造了巨大的金字塔，人們至今仍在猜想他們是如何做到的。"},{"w":"civil","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the people of a country; polite","c":"公民的；國內的；有禮的","s":"The two neighbors do not like each other, but they always stay civil and say good morning when they meet.","t":"這兩個鄰居彼此不喜歡，但見面時總是保持有禮，互道早安。"},{"w":"civilize","p":"v.","d":"to teach people to live in a more organized and polite way","c":"使文明；開化","s":"Some people believed that building schools and roads would civilize the villagers, but the villagers already had a rich culture.","t":"有些人認為蓋學校和道路會開化村民，但村民們本來就擁有豐富的文化。"},{"w":"civilized","p":"adj.","d":"having a well-developed society; polite and reasonable","c":"文明的；有教養的","s":"In a civilized society, people solve their problems by talking and voting rather than by fighting in the streets.","t":"在文明的社會裡，人們透過對話和投票來解決問題，而不是在街上打架。"},{"w":"clarify","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier to understand by explaining it","c":"澄清；闡明","s":"Could you clarify the homework rules, please, because half of the class is not sure when the report is due?","t":"可以請你說明清楚作業規定嗎？因為全班有一半的人不確定報告什麼時候要交。","h":1},{"w":"clarification","p":"n.","d":"an explanation that makes something clearer","c":"澄清；說明","s":"The students asked for clarification after reading the exam notice, because the time and the room number did not match.","t":"學生們讀完考試公告後要求澄清，因為時間和教室號碼對不起來。"},{"w":"clarity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being clear and easy to understand or see","c":"清晰；清楚","s":"The speaker explained the difficult science topic with such clarity that even the youngest children in the room understood it.","t":"講者把困難的科學主題講得非常清楚，連現場最小的孩子都聽懂了。"},{"w":"clear","p":"adj.","d":"easy to understand, see, or hear; without doubt","c":"清楚的；清晰的","s":"The teacher's instructions were so clear that nobody had to ask any questions before starting the group project.","t":"老師的指示非常清楚，所以開始小組專題之前沒有人需要提問。"},{"w":"clash","p":"n.","d":"a short fight or a strong disagreement between people or groups","c":"衝突；爭執","s":"There was a clash between the two groups of fans outside the stadium, and the police had to separate them.","t":"體育場外兩群球迷之間發生了衝突，警察不得不把他們分開。","h":1},{"w":"clash","p":"v.","d":"to fight or argue; to look bad together (of colors)","c":"衝突；不相配","s":"The bright pink curtains clash with the green walls, so my mother decided to paint the whole room white.","t":"亮粉色的窗簾和綠色的牆壁不相配，所以媽媽決定把整個房間漆成白色。"},{"w":"clash with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to happen at the same time as something else, so you cannot do both","c":"與…時間衝突","s":"Unfortunately, the piano concert clashes with my cousin's wedding, so I had to give my ticket to a friend.","t":"很不巧，鋼琴音樂會與我表姊的婚禮時間衝突，所以我只好把票送給朋友。","a":"clashes with"},{"w":"classification","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting things into groups; a group in such a system","c":"分類；類別","s":"Scientists use a system of classification to group millions of living things by how they look and how they are related.","t":"科學家使用一套分類系統，依據外觀和親緣關係把數百萬種生物分組。","h":1},{"w":"classify","p":"v.","d":"to put things into groups according to their type","c":"分類；歸類","s":"Librarians classify books by subject, so all the cookbooks sit together on the same shelf near the window.","t":"圖書館員按主題分類書籍，所以所有的食譜書都放在靠窗的同一個書架上。","h":1},{"w":"classified","p":"adj.","d":"officially secret; (of ads) arranged in groups in a newspaper","c":"機密的；分類的","s":"The report was marked classified, so only three people in the whole company were allowed to read it.","t":"這份報告被標記為機密，所以全公司只有三個人可以閱讀。"},{"w":"class","p":"n.","d":"a group of students; a group of things of the same type; a social group","c":"班級；類；階級","s":"In the hotel's top class of rooms, every guest gets a private pool and a view of the whole bay.","t":"在這家飯店最高等級的房型裡，每位客人都有私人泳池，而且能看到整個海灣。"},{"w":"claw","p":"n.","d":"a sharp curved nail on the foot of an animal or bird","c":"爪；爪子","s":"The kitten dug her sharp claws into the sofa, and my mother shouted that we had to buy a scratching post.","t":"小貓把尖尖的爪子扎進沙發裡，媽媽大喊我們必須買一個貓抓板。","a":"claws","h":1},{"w":"claw","p":"v.","d":"to tear or pull at something with claws or fingers","c":"用爪抓；抓住","s":"The trapped dog tried to claw its way out of the hole, and its paws were covered with mud when we found it.","t":"被困住的狗努力用爪抓著想爬出洞口，我們找到它時，它的腳掌滿是泥巴。"},{"w":"claw one's way","p":"v.phr.","d":"to succeed only by working extremely hard against difficulties","c":"艱苦地奮鬥向上","s":"After losing everything in the fire, the family clawed their way back to a normal life over the next five years.","t":"在火災中失去一切之後，這家人在接下來的五年裡艱苦地奮鬥，重新回到正常生活。","a":"clawed their way"},{"w":"cliff","p":"n.","d":"a high, steep rock face, especially by the sea","c":"懸崖；峭壁","s":"From the top of the cliff, we could see the waves hit the rocks far below, so we stayed behind the fence.","t":"從懸崖頂端，我們可以看到海浪撞擊遠處下方的岩石，所以我們待在圍欄後面。","h":1},{"w":"cliffhanger","p":"n.","d":"an exciting story or situation whose ending is unknown until the last moment","c":"懸疑結局；扣人心弦的情節","s":"The season ended with a cliffhanger, and now we have to wait six months to find out whether the hero survived.","t":"這一季以一個懸疑結局收尾，現在我們得等六個月才能知道主角是否活了下來。"},{"w":"fall off a cliff","p":"v.phr.","d":"to drop from a high rock face; (informal) to decrease suddenly and sharply","c":"從懸崖掉落；驟降","s":"The hiker nearly fell off a cliff when the wet path gave way, but his friend grabbed his backpack just in time.","t":"當濕滑的小路塌陷時，那位登山客差點從懸崖掉下去，但他的朋友及時抓住了他的背包。","a":"fell off a cliff"}]},{"unit":7,"theme":"clumsy – concerning","cards":[{"w":"clumsy","p":"adj.","d":"moving or doing things in a careless way, often dropping or breaking things","c":"笨拙的；笨手笨腳的","s":"I am so clumsy in the kitchen that my mother does not let me carry the soup to the table anymore.","t":"我在廚房裡太笨手笨腳了，所以媽媽不再讓我把湯端到桌上。","h":1},{"w":"clumsily","p":"adv.","d":"in a careless and awkward way","c":"笨拙地","s":"The new waiter clumsily dropped the tray of glasses, and the whole restaurant turned to look at him.","t":"新來的服務生笨拙地打翻了一整盤玻璃杯，整間餐廳的人都轉頭看他。"},{"w":"clumsiness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being careless and awkward with your body","c":"笨拙","s":"Because of his clumsiness, my little brother has broken three phones this year, so Dad bought him a strong case.","t":"由於他的笨拙，我弟弟今年已經摔壞三支手機，所以爸爸幫他買了一個堅固的手機殼。"},{"w":"coarse","p":"adj.","d":"rough and not smooth or fine","c":"粗糙的；粗的","s":"The coarse sand on this beach hurts your feet, so most visitors wear sandals when they walk to the water.","t":"這片海灘上粗糙的沙子會弄痛你的腳，所以大多數遊客走到海邊時都會穿涼鞋。","h":1},{"w":"coarse","p":"adj.","d":"rude and not polite, especially in the way you speak","c":"粗俗的；粗魯的","s":"The old man's coarse jokes made several guests at the dinner feel uncomfortable, and his wife told him to stop.","t":"那位老先生粗俗的笑話讓晚宴上好幾位客人感到不自在，他太太叫他別再說了。"},{"w":"coarsely","p":"adv.","d":"in large, rough pieces; in a rude way","c":"粗略地；粗糙地","s":"For this salad, you should chop the carrots coarsely instead of cutting them into very thin slices.","t":"做這道沙拉時，你應該把紅蘿蔔粗略地切塊，而不是切成很薄的片。"},{"w":"code","p":"n.","d":"a set of rules; a system of letters, numbers, or signs that carries a message","c":"規範；密碼；代碼","s":"The spy wrote the message in a secret code so that nobody else could read it if the letter was stolen.","t":"間諜用秘密密碼寫下訊息，這樣即使信被偷了，也沒有人能讀懂。","h":1},{"w":"code","p":"v.","d":"to write instructions for a computer","c":"寫程式；編碼","s":"My cousin learned to code when she was twelve, and now she builds simple games on her laptop every weekend.","t":"我表妹十二歲就學會寫程式，現在她每個週末都在筆電上做簡單的遊戲。"},{"w":"dress code","p":"n.phr.","d":"the rules about what clothes people must wear in a place","c":"服裝規定","s":"The company has a strict dress code, so employees are not allowed to wear shorts or sandals even in summer.","t":"這家公司有嚴格的服裝規定，所以員工即使在夏天也不能穿短褲或涼鞋。"},{"w":"zip code","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of numbers that shows the area where you live (US)","c":"郵遞區號","s":"Please write your zip code clearly on the package, or the post office may send it to the wrong part of the city.","t":"請在包裹上清楚寫下你的郵遞區號，否則郵局可能會把它送到城市裡錯誤的地區。"},{"w":"decode","p":"v.","d":"to find the meaning of a message written in code","c":"解碼；破解","s":"It took the scientists several months to decode the strange signals that came from deep space.","t":"科學家花了好幾個月才破解來自深太空的奇怪訊號。"},{"w":"collapse","p":"v.","d":"to fall down suddenly; to fail completely","c":"倒塌；崩潰；昏倒","s":"The old bridge might collapse in the next big earthquake, so the city has closed it to all cars and buses.","t":"這座老橋可能會在下一次大地震中倒塌，所以市政府已禁止所有汽車和公車通行。","h":1},{"w":"collapse","p":"n.","d":"a sudden fall or failure of something","c":"倒塌；崩潰；瓦解","s":"The sudden collapse of the company left two thousand workers without jobs just before the new year.","t":"這家公司突然倒閉，讓兩千名員工在新年前夕失去工作。"},{"w":"collapsible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be folded into a smaller shape","c":"可折疊的","s":"We bought a collapsible table for camping, because it fits easily in the back of our small car.","t":"我們買了一張可折疊的露營桌，因為它可以輕鬆放進我們小車的後車廂。"},{"w":"colleague","p":"n.","d":"a person you work with, especially in a professional job","c":"同事","s":"My mother's colleague drove her home from the office last night because her car would not start in the rain.","t":"我媽媽的同事昨晚開車送她從公司回家，因為她的車在雨中發不動。","h":1},{"w":"co-worker","p":"n.","d":"a person who works with you at the same company","c":"同事","s":"A friendly co-worker showed me how to use the copy machine on my first day, which saved me a lot of time.","t":"一位友善的同事在我上班第一天教我怎麼用影印機，幫我省了很多時間。"},{"w":"a colleague of mine","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of the people I work with","c":"我的一位同事","s":"A colleague of mine is giving a talk about healthy eating tomorrow, so I will go to the hall to support her.","t":"我的一位同事明天要做一場關於健康飲食的演講，所以我會去會堂支持她。","a":"A colleague of mine"},{"w":"combination","p":"n.","d":"two or more things put together; the numbers that open a lock","c":"結合；組合；密碼組合","s":"The restaurant is popular because of its combination of good food, friendly service, and low prices.","t":"這家餐廳很受歡迎，因為它結合了美食、親切的服務和實惠的價格。","h":1},{"w":"combine","p":"v.","d":"to join two or more things together","c":"結合；混合","s":"If you combine flour, eggs, milk, and a little sugar, you can make simple pancakes in about ten minutes.","t":"如果你把麵粉、雞蛋、牛奶和一點糖混合在一起，大約十分鐘就能做出簡單的鬆餅。"},{"w":"combined","p":"adj.","d":"put together; total","c":"聯合的；總共的","s":"The combined efforts of the teachers and the parents helped the school raise enough money for a new library.","t":"老師和家長共同的努力幫助學校募到足夠的錢，蓋了一座新圖書館。"},{"w":"in combination with","p":"phr.","d":"together with something else","c":"與…結合；搭配","s":"This medicine works best in combination with plenty of rest, so the doctor told me to stay home for three days.","t":"這種藥搭配充分的休息效果最好，所以醫生要我在家待三天。"},{"w":"comedy","p":"n.","d":"a funny film, play, or TV show that makes people laugh","c":"喜劇","s":"After a long week of exams, we watched a comedy together, and we laughed so hard that our stomachs hurt.","t":"經過一週漫長的考試之後，我們一起看了一部喜劇，笑到肚子都痛了。","h":1},{"w":"comedian","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to make people laugh","c":"喜劇演員","s":"The comedian told funny stories about his family, and even the serious old man in the front row could not stop laughing.","t":"那位喜劇演員說了關於他家人的好笑故事，連前排嚴肅的老先生都笑個不停。"},{"w":"comic","p":"adj.","d":"funny; connected with comedy","c":"滑稽的；喜劇的","s":"The actor is famous for his comic roles, but in his new movie he plays a sad father who loses his son.","t":"這位演員以喜劇角色聞名，但在他的新電影裡，他飾演一位失去兒子的悲傷父親。"},{"w":"comical","p":"adj.","d":"funny in a strange or silly way","c":"好笑的；滑稽的","s":"It was comical to watch my grandfather try to dance to pop music at my sister's wedding party.","t":"看我爺爺在姊姊的婚宴上努力跟著流行音樂跳舞，真是好笑。"},{"w":"commander","p":"n.","d":"an officer who is in charge of a group of soldiers or a ship","c":"指揮官；司令","s":"The commander ordered his soldiers to stop and rest for the night because the road ahead was too dangerous in the dark.","t":"指揮官命令士兵停下來休息過夜，因為前方的路在黑暗中太危險了。","h":1},{"w":"command","p":"n.","d":"an order that must be obeyed; control over a group","c":"命令；指揮","s":"The dog sat down at once when it heard its owner's command, which showed how well it had been trained.","t":"那隻狗一聽到主人的命令就立刻坐下，顯示牠受過良好的訓練。"},{"w":"command","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone to do something; to be in charge of","c":"命令；指揮","s":"The captain will command the ship for the next two weeks while the main officer recovers from his illness.","t":"在主要軍官養病期間，船長將在接下來兩週指揮這艘船。"},{"w":"in command of","p":"phr.","d":"in charge of a group of people","c":"指揮；掌管","s":"The young teacher was in command of forty excited children on the field trip, and she did not lose a single one.","t":"這位年輕老師在校外教學時掌管四十個興奮的孩子，一個都沒弄丟。"},{"w":"comment","p":"n.","d":"something you say or write that gives your opinion","c":"評論；意見","s":"The teacher wrote a kind comment at the end of my essay, saying that my ideas were clear and interesting.","t":"老師在我的作文結尾寫了一句親切的評語，說我的想法清楚又有趣。","h":1},{"w":"comment","p":"v.","d":"to give your opinion about something","c":"評論；發表意見","s":"The coach refused to comment on the game until he had watched the video of the last ten minutes again.","t":"教練拒絕對這場比賽發表意見，直到他再看一次最後十分鐘的影片。"},{"w":"comment on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say or write what you think about something","c":"對…發表評論","s":"Many people commented on her new haircut, and most of them said it made her look younger and more confident.","t":"很多人對她的新髮型發表意見，大多數人說這讓她看起來更年輕、更有自信。","a":"commented on"},{"w":"commentary","p":"n.","d":"a spoken description of an event while it is happening; a set of comments","c":"實況報導；評論","s":"We listened to the radio commentary of the baseball game while we were driving home from the beach.","t":"我們從海邊開車回家時，一邊聽著棒球比賽的廣播實況報導。"},{"w":"commentator","p":"n.","d":"a person who describes a sports event or gives opinions on the news","c":"評論員；播報員","s":"The sports commentator got so excited when the team scored that he nearly fell off his chair.","t":"當球隊得分時，那位體育播報員太興奮了，差點從椅子上摔下來。"},{"w":"commerce","p":"n.","d":"the buying and selling of goods and services","c":"商業；貿易","s":"The old port city grew rich through commerce with countries across the sea, and many traders settled there.","t":"這座古老的港口城市透過與海外國家的貿易變得富裕，許多商人在那裡定居。","h":1},{"w":"commercial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with buying and selling; made to earn money","c":"商業的；商業性的","s":"The movie was not a commercial success, but many critics said it was the best film of the year.","t":"這部電影在商業上並不成功，但許多影評人說它是年度最佳電影。"},{"w":"commercial","p":"n.","d":"an advertisement on TV or radio","c":"（電視、廣播）廣告","s":"My little sister can sing every word of the toothpaste commercial because it is played ten times a day.","t":"我妹妹能唱出那支牙膏廣告的每一個字，因為它一天播十次。"},{"w":"e-commerce","p":"n.","d":"the business of buying and selling things on the internet","c":"電子商務","s":"Thanks to e-commerce, my aunt sells her handmade soap to customers all over the world without leaving her village.","t":"多虧了電子商務，我阿姨不用離開村子就能把手工肥皂賣給世界各地的顧客。"},{"w":"commit","p":"v.","d":"to do something wrong or illegal","c":"犯（罪、錯）","s":"The police believe the man did not commit the robbery, because he was at work when it happened.","t":"警方相信那名男子並沒有犯下搶案，因為案發時他正在上班。","h":1},{"w":"commit a crime","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something that is against the law","c":"犯罪","s":"People who commit a crime should be punished fairly, but they should also be given a chance to change.","t":"犯罪的人應該受到公平的懲罰，但也應該被給予改過的機會。"},{"w":"commit to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to promise to do something or to give your time to it","c":"承諾；投入","s":"Before you commit to the swimming team, remember that you will have to practice every morning at six o'clock.","t":"在你承諾加入游泳隊之前，記住你每天早上六點都必須練習。"},{"w":"commitment","p":"n.","d":"a promise to do something; the hard work you give to something","c":"承諾；投入","s":"Learning a musical instrument takes real commitment, so you should practice a little every day instead of once a week.","t":"學樂器需要真正的投入，所以你應該每天練習一點，而不是一週練一次。"},{"w":"committed","p":"adj.","d":"willing to work very hard at something","c":"盡心盡力的；堅定的","s":"She is a committed teacher who stays after school every day to help students who are having trouble with math.","t":"她是一位盡心盡力的老師，每天放學後都留下來幫助數學有困難的學生。"},{"w":"communication","p":"n.","d":"the act of sharing information, ideas, or feelings with others","c":"溝通；通訊","s":"Good communication between parents and teachers helps children do better at school and feel safer in class.","t":"家長與老師之間良好的溝通有助於孩子在學校表現更好，在課堂上也更有安全感。","h":1},{"w":"communicate","p":"v.","d":"to share information, ideas, or feelings with someone","c":"溝通；傳達","s":"Even though they do not speak the same language, the two boys communicate easily by drawing pictures and using hand signs.","t":"雖然他們說的語言不同，這兩個男孩透過畫圖和手勢輕鬆地溝通。"},{"w":"communicate with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to talk or write to someone and share ideas","c":"與…溝通","s":"Nowadays, most teenagers prefer to communicate with their friends through short messages rather than long phone calls.","t":"現在大多數青少年偏好透過簡短的訊息而不是長時間的電話與朋友溝通。"},{"w":"communicative","p":"adj.","d":"willing to talk and share information with people","c":"健談的；善於溝通的","s":"The new student was shy at first, but she became much more communicative after she joined the drama club.","t":"這位新生起初很害羞，但加入戲劇社之後，她變得健談多了。"},{"w":"community","p":"n.","d":"all the people who live in one area; a group of people who share something","c":"社區；社群；群體","s":"Everyone in our small community helped clean up the park after the typhoon, and it looked beautiful again by Sunday.","t":"颱風過後，我們小社區裡的每個人都幫忙清理公園，到星期天它又變得美麗了。","h":1},{"w":"community center","p":"n.phr.","d":"a building where people in an area can meet and do activities","c":"社區活動中心","s":"My grandmother takes a free dance class at the community center every Tuesday morning with her neighbors.","t":"我奶奶每週二早上和鄰居一起在社區活動中心上免費的舞蹈課。"},{"w":"community service","p":"n.phr.","d":"unpaid work that helps the people in an area","c":"社區服務","s":"Our class did community service last weekend by picking up trash along the river and painting the old bus stop.","t":"我們班上週末做了社區服務，沿著河邊撿垃圾，還把舊公車站漆了一遍。"},{"w":"communal","p":"adj.","d":"shared by a group of people","c":"公共的；共用的","s":"The students who live in the dormitory cook together in a communal kitchen on the first floor.","t":"住在宿舍的學生在一樓的共用廚房裡一起煮飯。"},{"w":"companion","p":"n.","d":"a person or animal you spend a lot of time with","c":"同伴；伴侶","s":"My grandfather's dog has been his closest companion since my grandmother passed away three years ago.","t":"自從三年前我奶奶過世後，爺爺的狗就一直是他最親密的同伴。","h":1},{"w":"companionship","p":"n.","d":"the pleasant feeling of being with someone you like","c":"友誼；陪伴","s":"Many elderly people join the morning exercise group not only for their health but also for the companionship.","t":"許多老人家參加晨間運動團體，不只是為了健康，也是為了陪伴。"},{"w":"company","p":"n.","d":"the state of being with someone; a business","c":"陪伴；公司","s":"I enjoy her company because she always listens carefully and makes me laugh when I am feeling sad.","t":"我很享受她的陪伴，因為她總是仔細傾聽，在我難過時逗我笑。"},{"w":"accompany","p":"v.","d":"to go somewhere with someone","c":"陪伴；陪同","s":"My father will accompany me to the interview tomorrow, but he has promised to wait outside the office.","t":"我爸爸明天會陪我去面試，但他答應會在辦公室外面等。"},{"w":"competition","p":"n.","d":"an event in which people try to win; the act of trying to be better than others","c":"比賽；競爭","s":"There is a lot of competition for places at the best high schools, so students start preparing for the exam a year early.","t":"進入最好的高中的競爭非常激烈，所以學生提前一年就開始準備考試。","h":1},{"w":"competitive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting very much to win; involving competition","c":"競爭的；好勝的","s":"My brother is so competitive that he gets upset even when he loses a simple card game with our grandmother.","t":"我哥哥太好勝了，連和奶奶玩簡單的紙牌遊戲輸了都會不高興。","h":1},{"w":"competitor","p":"n.","d":"a person, team, or company that competes with others","c":"競爭者；參賽者","s":"Over two hundred competitors from twelve countries will take part in the speech contest in Taipei next month.","t":"下個月將有來自十二個國家的兩百多名參賽者參加在台北舉辦的演講比賽。","a":"competitors","h":1},{"w":"compete","p":"v.","d":"to try to win or be better than others","c":"競爭；比賽","s":"Small bookstores find it hard to compete with online shops that sell the same books at much lower prices.","t":"小書店很難和以低很多的價格販售同樣書籍的網路商店競爭。"},{"w":"compete against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to beat a particular person or team","c":"與…競爭","s":"Our school team will compete against last year's champions in the final, so we have been practicing twice a day.","t":"我們校隊將在決賽中對上去年的冠軍，所以我們每天練習兩次。"},{"w":"complicate","p":"v.","d":"to make something more difficult to understand or deal with","c":"使複雜化","s":"Please do not complicate the plan by inviting more people; a small dinner with close friends is all she wants.","t":"請不要再邀更多人來把計畫弄得更複雜；她只想要和親近的朋友吃頓小型晚餐。","h":1},{"w":"complicated","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to understand because it has many parts","c":"複雜的","s":"The rules of this board game are so complicated that we spent the first hour just reading the instructions.","t":"這款桌遊的規則太複雜了，我們第一個小時光是讀說明書就過去了。"},{"w":"complication","p":"n.","d":"something that makes a situation more difficult","c":"複雜的問題；併發症","s":"The trip was going well until a complication with our train tickets forced us to stay another night in the city.","t":"這趟旅行原本一切順利，直到火車票出了麻煩，迫使我們在這座城市多住一晚。"},{"w":"complex","p":"adj.","d":"made of many connected parts; not simple","c":"複雜的","s":"The human brain is the most complex organ in the body, and scientists still do not understand how it works.","t":"人腦是身體中最複雜的器官，科學家至今仍不了解它如何運作。"},{"w":"compose","p":"v.","d":"to write music, a poem, or a letter","c":"作曲；創作；撰寫","s":"She began to compose her own songs at the age of ten, and now she writes music for popular singers.","t":"她十歲就開始創作自己的歌曲，現在她為流行歌手寫歌。","h":1},{"w":"composer","p":"n.","d":"a person who writes music","c":"作曲家","s":"The young composer wrote the music for the film in only three weeks, and it later won an important award.","t":"這位年輕的作曲家只用三週就為這部電影寫好配樂，後來還贏得了一個重要獎項。","h":1},{"w":"composition","p":"n.","d":"a piece of music or writing; the way something is made up","c":"作品；作文；組成","s":"For homework, we have to write a composition about a person who changed our life, and it must be at least 200 words.","t":"回家作業是寫一篇關於改變我們人生的人的作文，至少要兩百字。","h":1},{"w":"be composed of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be made up of certain parts","c":"由…組成","s":"The school band is composed of thirty students, and about half of them play some kind of drum.","t":"學校樂隊由三十名學生組成，其中大約一半的人演奏某種鼓。","a":"is composed of"},{"w":"compose oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become calm after being upset or nervous","c":"使自己鎮定下來","s":"The speaker took a deep breath to compose herself before she walked onto the stage in front of a thousand people.","t":"演講者在走上一千人面前的舞台之前，深吸一口氣讓自己鎮定下來。","a":"compose herself"},{"w":"concentrate","p":"v.","d":"to give all your attention to one thing","c":"專心；集中","s":"It is hard to concentrate on my homework when my brother is playing loud video games in the next room.","t":"當我哥哥在隔壁房間大聲玩電動時，我很難專心寫功課。","h":1},{"w":"concentration","p":"n.","d":"the ability to give all your attention to something","c":"專注力；專心","s":"Chess requires great concentration, so the players sat in silence for over three hours without looking up.","t":"下棋需要高度的專注力，所以棋手們安靜地坐了三個多小時，連頭都沒抬。","h":1},{"w":"concentrate on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think very carefully about one thing you are doing","c":"專注於…","s":"This year I want to concentrate on improving my English, so I have decided to read one English book every month.","t":"今年我想專注於提升我的英文，所以我決定每個月讀一本英文書。"},{"w":"concentrated","p":"adj.","d":"strong because water has been removed; done with great attention","c":"濃縮的；集中的","s":"This juice is concentrated, so you need to add three cups of water before you drink it.","t":"這種果汁是濃縮的，所以喝之前你需要加三杯水。"},{"w":"concept","p":"n.","d":"an idea of what something is or how it works","c":"概念；觀念","s":"Young children often do not understand the concept of time, so they ask \"Are we there yet?\" every five minutes.","t":"幼童通常不懂時間的概念，所以他們每五分鐘就問一次「到了沒？」。","h":1},{"w":"conceive","p":"v.","d":"to think of a new idea or plan; to imagine","c":"構想；想像","s":"The engineer first conceived the idea for the folding bicycle while watching his daughter fold a paper crane.","t":"這位工程師第一次構想出折疊腳踏車的點子，是在看女兒摺紙鶴的時候。","a":"conceived"},{"w":"conception","p":"n.","d":"a general idea or understanding of something","c":"概念；理解","s":"Many students have no clear conception of what a scientist's daily work is really like, so the school invited one to speak.","t":"許多學生對科學家的日常工作到底是什麼樣子沒有清楚的概念，所以學校邀請了一位來演講。"},{"w":"conceptual","p":"adj.","d":"based on ideas rather than on real things","c":"概念上的","s":"The artist's conceptual work made some visitors confused, because there was only an empty chair in the middle of the room.","t":"這位藝術家的概念性作品讓一些參觀者感到困惑，因為房間中央只有一張空椅子。"},{"w":"concerning","p":"prep.","d":"about; on the subject of","c":"關於","s":"The principal sent a letter to all parents concerning the new rules for using phones during school hours.","t":"校長寄了一封信給所有家長，關於上課時間使用手機的新規定。","h":1},{"w":"concern","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry; something that worries you","c":"擔心；關心的事","s":"The doctor said my main concern should be getting enough sleep, not the small cut on my hand.","t":"醫生說我主要該擔心的是睡眠是否充足，而不是手上的小傷口。"},{"w":"concern","p":"v.","d":"to worry someone; to be about something","c":"使擔心；與…有關","s":"The news that the river is rising again will concern everyone who lives near the bridge.","t":"河水再次上漲的消息會讓所有住在橋附近的人擔心。"},{"w":"be concerned about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be worried about something","c":"擔心…","s":"My parents are concerned about my grades this semester, so they have asked me to stop playing games on school nights.","t":"我父母擔心我這學期的成績，所以他們要我上課日的晚上不要再打電動。","a":"are concerned about"},{"w":"concerned","p":"adj.","d":"worried; involved in something","c":"擔心的；有關的","s":"The concerned mother called the school three times when her son did not come home by six o'clock.","t":"當兒子六點還沒回家時，那位擔心的母親打了三次電話到學校。"},{"w":"concerning","p":"adj.","d":"causing worry","c":"令人擔憂的","s":"The number of students who skip breakfast is concerning, so the school now sells cheap sandwiches before the first class.","t":"不吃早餐的學生人數令人擔憂，所以學校現在在第一節課前販售便宜的三明治。"}]},{"unit":8,"theme":"concrete – container","cards":[{"w":"concrete","p":"adj.","d":"real and clear, not just an idea; made of concrete","c":"具體的；混凝土製的","s":"Instead of just saying you will study harder, make a concrete plan with the exact hours you will read each day.","t":"與其只是說你會更努力讀書，不如訂一個具體的計畫，寫出你每天要讀書的確切時數。","h":1},{"w":"concrete","p":"n.","d":"a hard building material made from cement, sand, water, and small stones","c":"混凝土","s":"The workers poured wet concrete into the wooden frame, and it became as hard as rock by the next morning.","t":"工人把濕的混凝土倒進木框裡，到第二天早上它就變得像石頭一樣硬。"},{"w":"concrete evidence","p":"n.phr.","d":"clear proof that something is true","c":"具體證據","s":"The police could not arrest the man because they had no concrete evidence that he had taken the money.","t":"警方無法逮捕那名男子，因為他們沒有他拿走錢的具體證據。"},{"w":"concretely","p":"adv.","d":"in a clear and specific way","c":"具體地","s":"The teacher asked us to explain concretely how we would raise money for the trip instead of saying \"we will try our best.\"","t":"老師要我們具體地說明我們要如何為旅行募款，而不是只說「我們會盡力」。"},{"w":"conductor","p":"n.","d":"a person who directs an orchestra; a person who checks tickets on a train or bus","c":"指揮；（火車、公車）車掌","s":"The conductor raised her hands, the hall became silent, and then a hundred musicians began to play together.","t":"指揮舉起雙手，大廳變得安靜，接著一百名樂手開始一起演奏。","h":1},{"w":"conductor","p":"n.","d":"a material that lets heat or electricity pass through it","c":"導體","s":"Copper is a very good conductor of electricity, so most of the wires in your house are made of it.","t":"銅是非常好的電導體，所以你家裡大部分的電線都是用它做的。"},{"w":"conduct","p":"v.","d":"to organize and do something; to direct an orchestra","c":"進行；指揮","s":"The scientists will conduct a survey of five hundred students to find out how many hours they sleep each night.","t":"科學家將對五百名學生進行一項調查，以了解他們每晚睡幾個小時。"},{"w":"conduct","p":"n.","d":"the way a person behaves, especially in public","c":"行為；品行","s":"The school gave him a prize for good conduct because he was always polite, honest, and helpful to others.","t":"學校因為他品行良好而頒獎給他，因為他總是有禮貌、誠實又樂於助人。"},{"w":"conduct oneself","p":"v.phr.","d":"to behave in a particular way","c":"表現；為人處事","s":"The young athlete conducted herself with great calm after losing the final, and she even smiled at the winner.","t":"這位年輕運動員在輸掉決賽後表現得非常冷靜，甚至還對贏家微笑。","a":"conducted herself"},{"w":"conference","p":"n.","d":"a large formal meeting where people discuss a subject","c":"會議；研討會","s":"Over two thousand doctors from thirty countries came to the medical conference in Taipei to share their newest research.","t":"來自三十個國家的兩千多名醫生前來參加在台北舉行的醫學會議，分享他們最新的研究。","h":1},{"w":"conference room","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room in an office used for meetings","c":"會議室","s":"Please move the chairs back into the conference room after the meeting, because another team needs it at three o'clock.","t":"會議結束後請把椅子搬回會議室，因為另一個團隊三點要用。"},{"w":"press conference","p":"n.phr.","d":"a meeting where someone answers questions from reporters","c":"記者會","s":"The mayor held a press conference this morning to explain why the new bridge will open six months late.","t":"市長今天早上舉行記者會，說明為什麼新橋會晚六個月通車。"},{"w":"confer","p":"v.","d":"to discuss something with others before making a decision","c":"商議；協商","s":"The judges will confer for a few minutes before they announce the winner of the singing contest.","t":"評審們會先商議幾分鐘，然後再宣布歌唱比賽的優勝者。"},{"w":"confess","p":"v.","d":"to admit that you have done something wrong or embarrassing","c":"承認；坦白","s":"After the teacher promised not to be angry, the boy finally confessed that he had broken the window with his ball.","t":"在老師保證不會生氣之後，男孩終於承認是他用球打破了窗戶。","a":"confessed","h":1},{"w":"confess to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to admit that you did something","c":"承認（做了）…","s":"I have to confess to eating the last piece of cake, even though I knew my sister was saving it for later.","t":"我必須承認我吃掉了最後一塊蛋糕，雖然我知道姊姊把它留著待會吃。"},{"w":"confession","p":"n.","d":"a statement that you have done something wrong","c":"自白；認罪","s":"The thief made a full confession to the police and told them where he had hidden the stolen jewelry.","t":"小偷向警方完整認罪，並告訴他們他把偷來的珠寶藏在哪裡。"},{"w":"confessed","p":"adj.","d":"having admitted openly that you are something","c":"自己承認的","s":"As a confessed chocolate lover, my aunt cannot walk past a bakery without going in to buy something sweet.","t":"身為一個自己承認的巧克力愛好者，我阿姨經過麵包店時沒辦法不進去買點甜的。"},{"w":"confidence","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you can do something well; trust in someone","c":"信心；自信；信賴","s":"Winning the school speech contest gave Amy the confidence to speak English in front of strangers without fear.","t":"贏得學校演講比賽讓 Amy 有信心在陌生人面前毫不害怕地說英文。","h":1},{"w":"have confidence in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to trust someone or believe in their ability","c":"對…有信心","s":"The coach has confidence in his young players, so he let them make their own decisions during the game.","t":"教練對他的年輕球員有信心，所以他讓他們在比賽中自己做決定。","a":"has confidence in"},{"w":"confident","p":"adj.","d":"sure that you can do something; sure that something is true","c":"有自信的；確信的","s":"She felt confident about the math test because she had finished every practice problem in the book twice.","t":"她對數學考試感到有自信，因為她已經把書上每一道練習題都做過兩遍。"},{"w":"self-confidence","p":"n.","d":"belief in your own ability and value","c":"自信心","s":"Learning to swim at the age of forty gave my father a lot of self-confidence, and he now tries new things all the time.","t":"四十歲學會游泳給了我爸爸很多自信心，現在他總是嘗試新事物。"},{"w":"confide in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell someone a secret because you trust them","c":"向…吐露心事","s":"Teenagers often confide in their friends rather than their parents when they have a problem at school.","t":"青少年在學校遇到問題時，通常向朋友而不是父母吐露心事。"},{"w":"confidential","p":"adj.","d":"meant to be kept secret","c":"機密的","s":"The doctor keeps all patient records confidential, so nobody outside the hospital can see your test results.","t":"醫生把所有病人的紀錄都保持機密，所以醫院以外的人都看不到你的檢查結果。"},{"w":"confusion","p":"n.","d":"a state of not understanding; a situation that is not clear or orderly","c":"困惑；混亂","s":"There was great confusion at the station when all the trains were canceled and nobody told the passengers why.","t":"當所有火車都被取消、又沒有人告訴乘客原因時，車站裡一片混亂。","h":1},{"w":"confuse","p":"v.","d":"to make someone unable to understand; to mix up two things","c":"使困惑；混淆","s":"The two sisters look so alike that even their teachers confuse them on the first day of school every year.","t":"這對姊妹長得太像了，每年開學第一天連老師都會搞混她們。"},{"w":"in confusion","p":"phr.","d":"in a state of not understanding or not knowing what to do","c":"困惑地；混亂地","s":"The children ran around the stage in confusion when the lights suddenly went out in the middle of the school play.","t":"學校話劇演到一半燈光突然熄滅時，孩子們慌亂地在舞台上跑來跑去。"},{"w":"confused","p":"adj.","d":"unable to understand or think clearly","c":"感到困惑的","s":"I was completely confused by the map, so I asked a kind old lady to show me the way to the museum.","t":"我被地圖弄得完全搞不清楚，所以我請一位親切的老太太指引我去博物館的路。"},{"w":"confusing","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to understand","c":"令人困惑的","s":"The instructions for the new washing machine were so confusing that we had to watch a video online to set it up.","t":"新洗衣機的說明書太令人困惑了，我們只好在網路上看影片來設定它。"},{"w":"congratulate","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone you are happy about their success or good luck","c":"恭喜；祝賀","s":"All of her classmates came up to congratulate Lily when the teacher announced that she had won first prize.","t":"當老師宣布 Lily 得到第一名時，她所有的同學都上前恭喜她。","h":1},{"w":"congratulations","p":"n.","d":"words you say to someone who has done well or had good luck","c":"恭喜（用語）","s":"\"Congratulations on your new job!\" my uncle shouted as he walked in with a big cake and a bunch of flowers.","t":"「恭喜你找到新工作！」我叔叔一邊喊著，一邊拿著大蛋糕和一束花走進來。","a":"Congratulations"},{"w":"congratulatory","p":"adj.","d":"expressing congratulations","c":"祝賀的","s":"The team received hundreds of congratulatory messages from fans around the world after they won the championship.","t":"球隊贏得冠軍後，收到來自世界各地球迷數百則祝賀的訊息。"},{"w":"congress","p":"n.","d":"the group of people elected to make laws in some countries, especially the US","c":"國會；議會","s":"The new law about clean air must be passed by Congress before the president can sign it next month.","t":"這項關於清潔空氣的新法必須先由國會通過，總統下個月才能簽署。","a":"Congress","h":1},{"w":"congress","p":"n.","d":"a large formal meeting of people from one profession or organization","c":"大會；代表大會","s":"Teachers from all over Asia will attend the education congress in Singapore to discuss the future of online learning.","t":"來自全亞洲的教師將參加在新加坡舉行的教育大會，討論線上學習的未來。"},{"w":"congressman","p":"n.","d":"a male member of the US Congress","c":"（美國）國會議員","s":"The congressman promised the farmers that he would fight for lower water prices when he returned to Washington.","t":"這位國會議員向農民承諾，他回到華盛頓後會為降低水價而努力。"},{"w":"congressional","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a congress","c":"國會的","s":"A congressional committee is studying whether children under sixteen should be allowed to use social media.","t":"一個國會委員會正在研究是否應該允許十六歲以下的孩子使用社群媒體。"},{"w":"conquer","p":"v.","d":"to take control of a country or city by force; to defeat","c":"征服；攻克","s":"The Roman army was able to conquer most of Europe, and their roads can still be seen in many countries today.","t":"羅馬軍隊得以征服歐洲大部分地區，他們修的道路至今仍可在許多國家看到。","h":1},{"w":"conquer","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in controlling a fear, problem, or difficulty","c":"克服（恐懼、困難）","s":"After years of practice, he finally conquered his fear of speaking in public and gave a speech to five hundred people.","t":"經過多年練習，他終於克服了公開演講的恐懼，對五百人發表演說。","a":"conquered"},{"w":"conqueror","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes control of a place by force","c":"征服者","s":"The conqueror built a huge castle on the hill so that everyone in the valley would remember who ruled them.","t":"征服者在山丘上建了一座巨大的城堡，好讓山谷裡的每個人都記得是誰在統治他們。"},{"w":"conquest","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking control of a place by force","c":"征服；佔領","s":"The conquest of the island took only three days, but the new rulers stayed there for over two hundred years.","t":"征服這座島只花了三天，但新的統治者在那裡待了兩百多年。"},{"w":"conscience","p":"n.","d":"the part of your mind that tells you whether what you are doing is right or wrong","c":"良心","s":"He returned the wallet to the police station because his conscience would not let him keep the money inside.","t":"他把皮夾送回警察局，因為他的良心不允許他留下裡面的錢。","h":1},{"w":"have a guilty conscience","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel bad because you have done something wrong","c":"感到心虛；內疚","s":"Tom had a guilty conscience after he lied to his mother, so he could not sleep until he told her the truth.","t":"Tom 對媽媽說謊之後感到內疚，所以直到他說出實話才能入睡。","a":"had a guilty conscience"},{"w":"conscientious","p":"adj.","d":"careful to do your work well and properly","c":"認真負責的；盡責的","s":"Our class leader is so conscientious that she checks every homework list twice before she hands it to the teacher.","t":"我們的班長非常認真負責，每次交給老師之前都會把作業清單檢查兩遍。"},{"w":"conscious","p":"adj.","d":"awake and able to understand what is happening; aware of something","c":"有意識的；察覺到的","s":"The patient was still conscious when the ambulance arrived, and he was able to tell the doctors his name.","t":"救護車抵達時病人仍然有意識，而且能夠告訴醫生他的名字。"},{"w":"consequence","p":"n.","d":"a result of an action, often a bad one","c":"後果；結果","s":"One consequence of staying up late every night is that you cannot pay attention in your morning classes.","t":"每天熬夜的一個後果就是你早上的課無法專心。","h":1},{"w":"consequent","p":"adj.","d":"happening as a result of something","c":"隨之而來的；因…而起的","s":"The heavy rain and the consequent flooding forced hundreds of families to leave their homes for several days.","t":"大雨和隨之而來的洪水迫使數百個家庭離家好幾天。","h":1},{"w":"as a consequence","p":"phr.","d":"as a result","c":"結果；因此","s":"He forgot to set his alarm, and as a consequence he missed the first twenty minutes of the important exam.","t":"他忘了設鬧鐘，結果錯過了重要考試的前二十分鐘。"},{"w":"face the consequences","p":"v.phr.","d":"to accept the bad results of what you have done","c":"承擔後果","s":"If you break the school rules, you will have to face the consequences, even if you say you are very sorry afterward.","t":"如果你違反校規，就必須承擔後果，即使你事後說你非常抱歉。"},{"w":"consequently","p":"adv.","d":"as a result; therefore","c":"因此；所以","s":"The store raised its prices twice this year, and consequently many customers have started shopping somewhere else.","t":"這家店今年漲價兩次，因此很多顧客已經開始到別處購物。"},{"w":"conservative","p":"adj.","d":"not liking change or new ideas; traditional","c":"保守的；守舊的","s":"My grandfather is quite conservative about clothes, so he always wears a suit and tie even on hot summer days.","t":"我爺爺對穿著相當保守，所以即使在炎熱的夏天他也總是穿西裝打領帶。","h":1},{"w":"conservative","p":"adj.","d":"careful and lower than the real number is likely to be","c":"保守的（估計）","s":"The report says at least ten thousand people joined the parade, but that is a conservative guess; it may have been twice as many.","t":"報告說至少有一萬人參加遊行，但那是個保守的估計；實際人數可能是兩倍。"},{"w":"conservative","p":"n.","d":"a person who does not like change and prefers traditional ways","c":"保守派人士","s":"Many conservatives in the town voted against the plan to replace the old market with a modern shopping center.","t":"鎮上許多保守派人士投票反對把舊市場改建成現代購物中心的計畫。","a":"conservatives"},{"w":"conserve","p":"v.","d":"to use something carefully so that it lasts; to protect nature","c":"節約；保護（自然）","s":"During the dry season, the government asked everyone to conserve water by taking shorter showers and fixing leaking taps.","t":"乾季期間，政府要求大家縮短淋浴時間、修好漏水的水龍頭來節約用水。"},{"w":"conservation","p":"n.","d":"the protection of nature and natural resources","c":"（自然）保護；保育","s":"The conservation of the forest is important because hundreds of rare birds and animals make their homes there.","t":"這座森林的保育很重要，因為數百種稀有的鳥類和動物以那裡為家。"},{"w":"consist","p":"v.","d":"to be made of particular parts or people","c":"組成；構成","s":"Our school band consists mainly of first-year students, so the music teacher is very patient with the beginners.","t":"我們學校的樂隊主要由一年級學生組成，所以音樂老師對初學者非常有耐心。","a":"consists","h":1},{"w":"consistent","p":"adj.","d":"always behaving or happening in the same way; not changing","c":"一致的；穩定的","s":"Her grades have been consistent all year, never dropping below ninety in any subject, which makes her parents proud.","t":"她的成績一整年都很穩定，任何科目都沒低於九十分，這讓她的父母很驕傲。","h":1},{"w":"consist of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be formed from particular things or people","c":"由…組成","s":"A healthy breakfast should consist of some fruit, a glass of milk, and bread or rice rather than just sweet cookies.","t":"健康的早餐應該由一些水果、一杯牛奶和麵包或米飯組成，而不是只有甜餅乾。"},{"w":"be consistent with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to agree with or match something","c":"與…一致；符合","s":"The story the boy told was consistent with what the video camera recorded, so the police believed him.","t":"男孩說的經過與攝影機拍到的畫面一致，所以警方相信了他。","a":"was consistent with"},{"w":"consistency","p":"n.","d":"the quality of always being the same or behaving in the same way","c":"一致性；穩定性","s":"A good basketball player needs consistency; it is not enough to score thirty points one night and only two the next.","t":"一個好的籃球員需要穩定性；某晚得三十分而隔天只得兩分是不夠的。"},{"w":"consistently","p":"adv.","d":"always in the same way; regularly","c":"一貫地；始終","s":"The small restaurant has consistently served fresh and delicious food for twenty years, so it always has a long line outside.","t":"這家小餐館二十年來始終供應新鮮美味的食物，所以外面總是排著長隊。"},{"w":"constitute","p":"v.","d":"to be the parts that form something; to be considered as something","c":"構成；組成；被視為","s":"Women now constitute more than half of the medical students at this university, which was not true thirty years ago.","t":"現在女性佔這所大學醫學院學生的一半以上，三十年前並非如此。","h":1},{"w":"constitution","p":"n.","d":"the set of basic laws by which a country is governed","c":"憲法","s":"According to the constitution of our country, every citizen over twenty has the right to vote in elections.","t":"根據我國憲法，每位二十歲以上的公民都有權在選舉中投票。","h":1},{"w":"constitution","p":"n.","d":"the condition of a person's body and how healthy it is","c":"體質","s":"My grandmother has a strong constitution; she is eighty-five and still walks up five floors every day without resting.","t":"我奶奶體質很好；她八十五歲了，每天還能不休息地爬五層樓。"},{"w":"constitutional","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by or connected with the constitution","c":"憲法的；合憲的","s":"The court must decide whether the new rule about school uniforms is constitutional or goes against students' basic rights.","t":"法院必須判定關於校服的新規定是否合憲，還是違反了學生的基本權利。"},{"w":"construct","p":"v.","d":"to build something large such as a building, bridge, or road","c":"建造；建設","s":"The city plans to construct a new sports center next to the river, and it should be finished before the national games.","t":"市政府計畫在河邊建造一座新的運動中心，應該會在全國運動會之前完工。","h":1},{"w":"construction","p":"n.","d":"the work of building something; the way something is built","c":"建造；建築工程；結構","s":"The construction of the new subway line has made the traffic on Main Street much worse for the past two years.","t":"新地鐵線的興建工程讓主街的交通在過去兩年變得更糟。","h":1},{"w":"constructive","p":"adj.","d":"helpful and useful, especially when giving opinions","c":"有建設性的","s":"Instead of just saying the essay was bad, the teacher gave constructive advice on how to make each paragraph clearer.","t":"老師不是只說這篇作文寫得不好，而是給了有建設性的建議，教我們如何讓每一段更清楚。","h":1},{"w":"under construction","p":"phr.","d":"being built at the moment","c":"興建中","s":"The new library is still under construction, so students have to use the small reading room on the second floor for now.","t":"新圖書館仍在興建中，所以學生目前必須使用二樓的小閱覽室。"},{"w":"reconstruct","p":"v.","d":"to build something again after it has been damaged; to form a picture of past events","c":"重建；重現","s":"It took the village five years to reconstruct the temple after the earthquake destroyed most of its roof.","t":"地震摧毀了廟的大部分屋頂之後，村子花了五年才把它重建起來。"},{"w":"consult","p":"v.","d":"to ask an expert for advice; to look in a book or map for information","c":"諮詢；請教；查閱","s":"You should consult a doctor before you start taking any medicine for your back pain, even if a friend recommends it.","t":"在你開始服用任何治療背痛的藥之前，應該先諮詢醫生，即使是朋友推薦的也一樣。","h":1},{"w":"consultant","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to give expert advice to companies or people","c":"顧問","s":"The company hired a consultant to find out why its sales had dropped so sharply in the past six months.","t":"公司聘請了一位顧問，來找出為什麼過去六個月銷售量下降得這麼厲害。","h":1},{"w":"consult with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to discuss something with someone before deciding","c":"與…商量","s":"Before choosing a university, Kevin decided to consult with his teachers and his parents to hear their opinions.","t":"在選擇大學之前，Kevin 決定與老師和父母商量，聽聽他們的意見。"},{"w":"consultation","p":"n.","d":"a meeting with an expert to get advice; the act of discussing something","c":"諮詢；會診；商議","s":"After a short consultation with the eye doctor, my brother learned that he needed glasses for reading.","t":"跟眼科醫生做了短暫的諮詢之後，我弟弟得知他看書需要戴眼鏡。"},{"w":"consume","p":"v.","d":"to eat, drink, or use something, especially in large amounts","c":"消耗；吃；喝","s":"Teenagers who consume too many sugary drinks every day are more likely to have problems with their teeth and weight.","t":"每天喝太多含糖飲料的青少年，更容易出現牙齒和體重的問題。","h":1},{"w":"consumer","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys goods or uses services","c":"消費者","s":"Smart consumers compare prices in several stores before they buy an expensive item like a laptop or a phone.","t":"聰明的消費者在購買筆電或手機等昂貵的物品之前，會先比較好幾家店的價格。","a":"consumers","h":1},{"w":"time-consuming","p":"adj.","d":"taking a lot of time","c":"耗時的","s":"Making dumplings by hand is time-consuming, but the whole family enjoys sitting around the table and doing it together.","t":"手工包餃子很耗時，但全家人都喜歡圍坐在桌邊一起做。"},{"w":"consumption","p":"n.","d":"the act of eating, drinking, or using something; the amount used","c":"消耗；消費（量）","s":"The consumption of electricity goes up sharply in July and August because almost everyone turns on the air conditioner.","t":"七、八月的電力消耗量會急遽上升，因為幾乎每個人都開冷氣。"},{"w":"container","p":"n.","d":"a box, bottle, or other object used for holding things","c":"容器；貨櫃","s":"Put the leftover soup in a glass container with a tight lid, and it will stay fresh in the fridge for three days.","t":"把剩下的湯放進有緊密蓋子的玻璃容器裡，它在冰箱裡可以保鮮三天。","h":1},{"w":"contain","p":"v.","d":"to have something inside; to include","c":"包含；含有","s":"This cereal contains a lot of sugar, so it is not as healthy as the colorful box makes it look.","t":"這種穀片含有很多糖，所以它並不像彩色包裝盒看起來那麼健康。","a":"contains"},{"w":"contain","p":"v.","d":"to control or stop something from spreading; to control your feelings","c":"控制；遏制；抑制","s":"The firefighters worked all night to contain the forest fire before it could reach the houses at the bottom of the hill.","t":"消防員整晚努力控制森林火勢，以免它蔓延到山腳下的房子。"},{"w":"content","p":"n.","d":"the things that are inside something; the information in a book or website","c":"內容；內容物","s":"She emptied the contents of her school bag onto the bed to look for the lost key, but it was not there.","t":"她把書包裡的東西全倒在床上找遺失的鑰匙，但鑰匙不在裡面。","a":"contents"}]},{"unit":9,"theme":"content – cottage","cards":[{"w":"content","p":"n.","d":"the things that are inside something; the ideas or information in a book, film, or website","c":"內容；內容物","s":"The content of the video was not suitable for young children, so the teacher chose a different one for the class.","t":"這部影片的內容不適合幼童，所以老師為班上選了另一部。","h":1},{"w":"contentment","p":"n.","d":"a quiet feeling of happiness and satisfaction","c":"滿足；知足","s":"After the big family dinner, my grandfather sat in his favorite chair with a look of pure contentment on his face.","t":"吃完家族大餐後，我爺爺坐在他最愛的椅子上，臉上帶著一種純然滿足的神情。","h":1},{"w":"content","p":"adj.","d":"happy and satisfied with what you have","c":"滿足的；滿意的","s":"My aunt does not want a bigger house or a faster car; she is perfectly content with her simple life in the countryside.","t":"我阿姨不想要更大的房子或更快的車；她對鄉下的簡單生活完全滿足。"},{"w":"be content with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be satisfied with something and not want more","c":"對…感到滿足","s":"The coach told the players not to be content with second place, because he believed they could win the whole tournament next year.","t":"教練告訴球員們不要滿足於第二名，因為他相信他們明年可以贏得整個錦標賽。"},{"w":"content","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel satisfied","c":"使滿足","s":"A bowl of warm noodles and a cup of tea were enough to content the tired travelers on that cold rainy night.","t":"在那個寒冷的雨夜，一碗熱麵和一杯茶就足以讓疲憊的旅人滿足了。"},{"w":"table of contents","p":"n.phr.","d":"the list at the front of a book showing its chapters and page numbers","c":"目錄","s":"If you want to find the chapter about volcanoes quickly, look at the table of contents at the beginning of the book.","t":"如果你想快速找到關於火山的那一章，請看書本開頭的目錄。"},{"w":"contest","p":"n.","d":"a competition in which people try to win a prize","c":"比賽；競賽","s":"More than sixty students entered the English speech contest, but only the best ten were chosen for the final round.","t":"六十多名學生報名參加英語演講比賽，但只有最優秀的十位被選進決賽。","h":1},{"w":"contest","p":"v.","d":"to compete for something; to argue that a decision is wrong","c":"角逐；爭辯；質疑","s":"The two brothers decided to contest their father's will in court because they believed it had been changed without his knowledge.","t":"兩兄弟決定在法庭上質疑父親的遺囑，因為他們認為遺囑是在父親不知情的情況下被更改的。"},{"w":"contestant","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a contest","c":"參賽者","s":"Each contestant in the cooking show has only thirty minutes to prepare a dish that will impress the three judges.","t":"烹飪節目裡的每位參賽者只有三十分鐘可以準備一道能讓三位評審驚豔的菜。"},{"w":"beauty contest","p":"n.phr.","d":"a competition in which the most attractive person wins","c":"選美比賽","s":"My cousin won a local beauty contest when she was nineteen, and the photos are still hanging in my aunt's living room.","t":"我表姊十九歲時贏得了當地的選美比賽，那些照片至今還掛在我阿姨的客廳裡。"},{"w":"context","p":"n.","d":"the words around a word that help explain its meaning; the situation in which something happens","c":"上下文；情境；背景","s":"When you meet a new word in a story, try to guess its meaning from the context before you look it up in a dictionary.","t":"當你在故事裡遇到新單字時，先試著從上下文猜它的意思，再查字典。","h":1},{"w":"in context","p":"phr.","d":"together with the words or situation around it","c":"在上下文中；在情境中","s":"Learning a word in context is much better than memorizing a long list, because you can see how it is really used.","t":"在情境中學單字比背一長串的單字表好得多，因為你可以看到這個字真正的用法。"},{"w":"out of context","p":"phr.","d":"without the words or situation that give the real meaning","c":"斷章取義","s":"The reporter took the mayor's words out of context, so many readers thought he had said something he never meant.","t":"記者把市長的話斷章取義，所以很多讀者以為他說了他根本沒有的意思。"},{"w":"contextual","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the context of something","c":"上下文的；情境的","s":"Good readers use contextual clues, such as the pictures and the surrounding sentences, to understand difficult passages.","t":"好的讀者會利用上下文的線索，例如圖片和前後的句子，來理解困難的段落。"},{"w":"continual","p":"adj.","d":"happening again and again, often in an annoying way","c":"連續不斷的；頻頻的","s":"The continual noise from the construction site next door made it impossible for me to study for my exam.","t":"隔壁工地不斷的噪音讓我根本無法準備考試。","h":1},{"w":"continuous","p":"adj.","d":"happening or existing without stopping","c":"連續的；不間斷的","s":"The island has had continuous rain for five days, and the rivers are now dangerously close to flooding the town.","t":"這座島已經連續下了五天雨，河水現在已經危險地接近淹沒城鎮的程度。","h":1},{"w":"continually","p":"adv.","d":"again and again; repeatedly","c":"不斷地；頻頻地","s":"My little brother continually asks \"Why?\" about everything, so a short walk to the park takes us an hour.","t":"我弟弟對每件事都不斷地問「為什麼？」，所以走一小段路到公園就要花我們一個小時。"},{"w":"continuously","p":"adv.","d":"without stopping","c":"連續地；不停地","s":"The machine has been running continuously for forty-eight hours, so the engineers will turn it off tonight to check it.","t":"這台機器已經不停地運轉四十八小時，所以工程師今晚會把它關掉檢查。"},{"w":"continue","p":"v.","d":"to keep doing something; to go on happening","c":"繼續","s":"If the typhoon rains continue through the night, the school will send a message to parents about closing tomorrow.","t":"如果颱風雨整夜持續下，學校會發訊息給家長通知明天是否停課。"},{"w":"continuity","p":"n.","d":"the state of going on without stopping or changing","c":"連續性；連貫性","s":"The old coach stayed with the team for two more years to give the young players some continuity after the owner changed.","t":"老教練在球隊老闆換人後又留了兩年，好讓年輕球員有一些連貫性。"},{"w":"contrary","p":"adj.","d":"opposite or completely different","c":"相反的","s":"Although the two scientists studied the same data, they reached contrary conclusions about whether the medicine was safe.","t":"雖然兩位科學家研究的是同樣的數據，他們對這種藥是否安全卻得出相反的結論。","h":1},{"w":"contrary","p":"n.","d":"the opposite","c":"相反（的事物）","s":"I thought the museum would be boring, but the contrary turned out to be true; we stayed there for five hours.","t":"我以為博物館會很無聊，結果相反的情況才是真的；我們在那裡待了五個小時。"},{"w":"on the contrary","p":"phr.","d":"used to say that the opposite is true","c":"正好相反；恰恰相反","s":"The movie was not a waste of money; on the contrary, it was the best film I have seen this year, and I want to watch it again.","t":"這部電影並不浪費錢；正好相反，它是我今年看過最好的電影，我還想再看一次。"},{"w":"contrary to","p":"phr.","d":"opposite to what someone said or expected","c":"與…相反","s":"Contrary to what the weather report said, it did not rain at all, and we enjoyed a sunny day at the beach.","t":"與氣象報告相反，完全沒有下雨，我們在海邊享受了晴朗的一天。","a":"Contrary to"},{"w":"contrast","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference between two things when they are compared","c":"對比；對照；差異","s":"There is a sharp contrast between the quiet village where I grew up and the busy city where I now live.","t":"我長大的安靜村莊和我現在居住的繁忙城市之間有鮮明的對比。","h":1},{"w":"contrast","p":"v.","d":"to compare two things in order to show how they are different","c":"對比；對照","s":"In your essay, contrast life in the 1950s with life today, and explain which period you would prefer to live in.","t":"在你的作文中，對比一九五〇年代與現今的生活，並說明你比較想生活在哪個時期。"},{"w":"in contrast to","p":"phr.","d":"very different from something else","c":"與…形成對比；相較之下","s":"In contrast to her noisy older brother, Mia is a quiet girl who would rather read a book than play loud games.","t":"相較於她吵鬧的哥哥，Mia 是個安靜的女孩，她寧願看書也不想玩吵鬧的遊戲。","a":"In contrast to"},{"w":"contrasting","p":"adj.","d":"very different from each other","c":"對比的；截然不同的","s":"The designer used contrasting colors, bright yellow and deep blue, so that the poster could be seen from across the street.","t":"設計師使用了對比的顏色——鮮黃和深藍，好讓海報從街道對面就能被看見。"},{"w":"contribute","p":"v.","d":"to give money, help, or ideas to something together with other people","c":"貢獻；捐助","s":"Everyone in the class was asked to contribute at least one idea for the school festival, and we ended up with forty suggestions.","t":"班上每個人都被要求為校慶貢獻至少一個點子，最後我們收到了四十個建議。","h":1},{"w":"contribution","p":"n.","d":"something you give or do to help make something successful","c":"貢獻；捐款","s":"The scientist received a gold medal for her great contribution to the study of the ocean over the past thirty years.","t":"這位科學家因為她過去三十年對海洋研究的重大貢獻而獲頒金牌。","h":1},{"w":"contribute to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help cause something; to give to something","c":"促成；對…有貢獻","s":"Eating too much fast food and sitting all day can contribute to serious health problems when you get older.","t":"吃太多速食和整天久坐，到你年紀大時可能會導致嚴重的健康問題。"},{"w":"make a contribution to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give money or help to a cause","c":"對…做出貢獻；捐款給","s":"Our school decided to make a contribution to the earthquake fund, and students brought coins and bills from home all week.","t":"我們學校決定捐款給地震基金，學生整個星期都從家裡帶零錢和鈔票來。"},{"w":"contributor","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives money, help, or writing to something","c":"貢獻者；捐助者；撰稿人","s":"The magazine thanked every contributor who had sent in stories and photos, and it printed their names on the last page.","t":"雜誌感謝每一位寄來故事和照片的撰稿人，並把他們的名字印在最後一頁。"},{"w":"convenience","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being easy to use or reach and saving you time or effort","c":"方便；便利","s":"Many people pay a little more for the convenience of having their groceries delivered to their door instead of shopping themselves.","t":"很多人願意多付一點錢換取雜貨直接送到家門口的便利，而不用自己去採買。","h":1},{"w":"convenience store","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small shop that sells everyday things and stays open long hours","c":"便利商店","s":"There is a convenience store on almost every corner in Taipei, so you can buy a hot meal or pay a bill at midnight.","t":"台北幾乎每個街角都有便利商店，所以你可以在半夜買熱食或繳帳單。"},{"w":"at your convenience","p":"phr.","d":"at a time that suits you","c":"在您方便的時候","s":"The dentist's office said I could call back at my convenience to change my appointment, as long as it was before Friday.","t":"牙醫診所說我可以在我方便的時候再打電話回去更改預約，只要是在星期五之前就好。","a":"at my convenience"},{"w":"convenient","p":"adj.","d":"easy to use or reach; suiting your needs","c":"方便的；便利的","s":"The new apartment is very convenient for my mother because the subway station and the hospital are both a five-minute walk away.","t":"這間新公寓對我媽媽來說非常方便，因為地鐵站和醫院都只要走五分鐘。"},{"w":"conveniently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is easy or suitable","c":"方便地；便利地","s":"The hotel is conveniently located near the airport, so guests who arrive late at night do not have to travel far.","t":"這家飯店便利地座落在機場附近，所以深夜抵達的客人不必走太遠。"},{"w":"inconvenience","p":"n.","d":"a problem that causes difficulty or extra effort","c":"不便；麻煩","s":"The airline apologized for the inconvenience caused by the delay and gave every passenger a free meal and a hotel room.","t":"航空公司為延誤造成的不便道歉，並提供每位乘客免費餐點和飯店房間。"},{"w":"convention","p":"n.","d":"the usual or accepted way of doing something in a society","c":"習俗；慣例","s":"By convention, the youngest person at the table pours tea for the elders at a traditional Chinese family dinner.","t":"按照慣例，在傳統的中式家庭聚餐上，桌上最年輕的人要為長輩倒茶。","h":1},{"w":"conventional","p":"adj.","d":"following the usual or traditional way; not new or different","c":"傳統的；慣常的","s":"My grandmother prefers conventional medicine, so she visits the doctor instead of trying the new herbal tea my aunt recommends.","t":"我奶奶偏好傳統的醫療，所以她去看醫生，而不是嘗試阿姨推薦的新草藥茶。","h":1},{"w":"convention","p":"n.","d":"a large meeting of people who share a job or interest","c":"大會；會議","s":"Thousands of comic book fans attended the annual convention in Tokyo, and many of them dressed as their favorite characters.","t":"成千上萬的漫畫迷參加了在東京舉行的年度大會，許多人打扮成他們最喜愛的角色。"},{"w":"conventionally","p":"adv.","d":"in the usual or traditional way","c":"按照慣例；傳統上","s":"The bride was conventionally dressed in white, but she surprised everyone by wearing bright red running shoes under her gown.","t":"新娘按照傳統穿著白色禮服，但她在禮服下穿了亮紅色的跑鞋，讓大家都很驚訝。"},{"w":"unconventional","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is usual or traditional","c":"非傳統的；不落俗套的","s":"The young teacher has an unconventional way of teaching history: she turns every lesson into a role-play game.","t":"這位年輕老師有一套非傳統的歷史教學法：她把每堂課都變成角色扮演遊戲。"},{"w":"converse","p":"v.","d":"to talk with someone in a formal or polite way","c":"交談；談話","s":"After studying Japanese for only one year, Linda was able to converse easily with the shopkeepers in Kyoto.","t":"Linda 才學了一年日文，就已經能和京都的店家輕鬆交談了。","h":1},{"w":"converse with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a conversation with someone","c":"與…交談","s":"The old farmer liked to converse with travelers who stopped at his gate, and he always offered them a cup of tea.","t":"老農夫喜歡與在他門口停下來的旅人交談，而且總是請他們喝杯茶。"},{"w":"conversation","p":"n.","d":"an informal talk between two or more people","c":"對話；交談","s":"We had a long conversation about our dreams for the future while we waited for the delayed train.","t":"在等誤點的火車時，我們針對未來的夢想進行了一場很長的對話。"},{"w":"conversational","p":"adj.","d":"relating to or used in informal talk","c":"會話的；口語的","s":"This course focuses on conversational English, so students practice ordering food and asking for directions rather than writing essays.","t":"這門課著重於會話英語，所以學生練習點餐和問路，而不是寫作文。"},{"w":"convey","p":"v.","d":"to express a feeling, idea, or message to someone","c":"傳達；表達","s":"The painter uses dark colors and empty streets to convey the loneliness she felt after moving to a new city.","t":"這位畫家用暗沉的色彩和空蕩的街道來傳達她搬到新城市後感受到的孤獨。","h":1},{"w":"convey","p":"v.","d":"to carry or take something from one place to another","c":"運送；傳送","s":"Hundreds of trucks convey fresh vegetables from the farms in the south to the markets in Taipei every night.","t":"每天晚上有數百輛卡車把新鮮蔬菜從南部的農場運送到台北的市場。"},{"w":"conveyor belt","p":"n.phr.","d":"a moving band that carries things from one place to another","c":"輸送帶","s":"At the sushi restaurant, small plates of fish move slowly past your table on a conveyor belt, and you take the ones you want.","t":"在迴轉壽司店，一小盤一小盤的魚在輸送帶上緩緩經過你的桌子，你拿你想要的就好。"},{"w":"convince","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe that something is true or that they should do something","c":"說服；使相信","s":"It took my sister three weeks to convince our parents that she was old enough to travel to Japan alone.","t":"我姊姊花了三個星期才說服爸媽她已經大到可以一個人去日本旅行。","h":1},{"w":"be convinced of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be completely sure that something is true","c":"確信…；相信…","s":"After watching the video from the store camera, the jury was convinced of the young man's innocence and set him free.","t":"看過商店監視器的影片後，陪審團確信這名年輕人是無辜的，並將他釋放。","a":"was convinced of"},{"w":"convinced","p":"adj.","d":"completely sure about something","c":"確信的；堅信的","s":"I am convinced that our team will win tomorrow, because we have practiced every single day for the past two months.","t":"我確信我們的隊伍明天會贏，因為過去兩個月我們每天都練習。"},{"w":"convincing","p":"adj.","d":"making you believe that something is true","c":"有說服力的；令人信服的","s":"Her excuse for being late was not very convincing, so the teacher asked her to bring a note from her parents.","t":"她遲到的藉口不太有說服力，所以老師要她帶家長的字條來。"},{"w":"unconvinced","p":"adj.","d":"not sure that something is true or right","c":"不相信的；未被說服的","s":"The doctor remained unconvinced by the salesman's claims and refused to buy the expensive machine for his clinic.","t":"醫生對推銷員的說法仍然不相信，拒絕為他的診所購買那台昂貴的機器。"},{"w":"cooperate","p":"v.","d":"to work together with others to achieve something","c":"合作","s":"If the two villages cooperate and share one water system, both of them will have enough clean water during the dry season.","t":"如果兩個村子合作共用一套供水系統，乾季時兩村都能有足夠的乾淨用水。","h":1},{"w":"cooperation","p":"n.","d":"the act of working together for a shared purpose","c":"合作；協力","s":"Thanks to the cooperation of all the parents, the school playground was cleaned and painted in a single weekend.","t":"多虧所有家長的協力，學校的遊樂場在一個週末內就清理並粉刷完成。","h":1},{"w":"cooperative","p":"adj.","d":"willing to help and work with others","c":"合作的；配合的","s":"The new student was so cooperative during the group project that everyone wanted her on their team for the next one.","t":"這位新同學在小組報告時非常配合，大家下一次都想找她同組。","h":1},{"w":"cooperative","p":"n.","d":"a business or farm that is owned and run by the people who work in it","c":"合作社","s":"The farmers formed a cooperative so that they could buy seeds more cheaply and sell their rice at a better price.","t":"農民們成立了一個合作社，這樣他們就能更便宜地買種子，並以更好的價格賣米。"},{"w":"cooperate with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work together with a person or group","c":"與…合作","s":"The police asked the public to cooperate with them by reporting anything unusual they saw near the bank that night.","t":"警方請民眾與他們合作，通報那晚在銀行附近看到的任何異常情況。"},{"w":"in cooperation with","p":"phr.","d":"working together with someone","c":"與…合作","s":"The museum organized the dinosaur exhibition in cooperation with a famous university in Canada, which lent most of the fossils.","t":"博物館與加拿大一所著名大學合作舉辦恐龍展，大部分化石都是該校出借的。"},{"w":"cope","p":"v.","d":"to deal successfully with a difficult situation","c":"應付；處理","s":"When both of her parents got sick at the same time, Jane found it very hard to cope, so her neighbors cooked for the family.","t":"當 Jane 的父母同時生病時，她覺得很難應付，所以鄰居幫她全家煮飯。","h":1},{"w":"cope with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to manage or deal with a problem or difficult situation","c":"應付…；處理…","s":"Many first-year students struggle to cope with the heavy homework, so the school offers free study help after class.","t":"許多一年級學生難以應付繁重的作業，所以學校在課後提供免費的課業輔導。"},{"w":"coping strategy","p":"n.phr.","d":"a way of dealing with stress or problems","c":"應對策略；因應方式","s":"Going for a long run is my favorite coping strategy when I feel stressed about exams and cannot sit still at my desk.","t":"當我因為考試感到壓力大、坐不住時，去長跑是我最喜歡的應對方式。"},{"w":"copper","p":"n.","d":"a soft reddish-brown metal used for making wires, pipes, and coins","c":"銅","s":"The old pot in my grandmother's kitchen is made of copper, and it turns a beautiful red when she polishes it.","t":"我奶奶廚房裡的舊鍋子是銅做的，她擦亮時它會變成漂亮的紅色。","h":1},{"w":"copper","p":"adj.","d":"reddish-brown in color; made of copper","c":"銅製的；銅色的","s":"The dancer's copper hair shone under the stage lights, and every photo in the newspaper the next day showed it.","t":"舞者銅色的頭髮在舞台燈光下閃閃發亮，第二天報紙上的每張照片都拍到了。"},{"w":"copper coin","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small coin made of copper","c":"銅幣","s":"My grandfather keeps a jar of old copper coins from the 1960s, and he says each one has a story behind it.","t":"我爺爺收藏了一罐一九六〇年代的舊銅幣，他說每一枚背後都有一個故事。","a":"copper coins"},{"w":"cord","p":"n.","d":"a thick string or thin rope; a wire that carries electricity to a machine","c":"繩索；電線","s":"Please tie the boxes with a strong cord before you put them in the truck, or they will fall open on the way.","t":"把箱子放上卡車之前，請用牢固的繩子綁好，否則它們會在路上散開。","h":1},{"w":"extension cord","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long electric wire used to connect a machine to a far-away socket","c":"延長線","s":"The socket is too far from the desk, so we need an extension cord to plug in the new printer.","t":"插座離書桌太遠了，所以我們需要一條延長線才能插上新的印表機。"},{"w":"cordless","p":"adj.","d":"working without an electric cord; using a battery","c":"無線的","s":"My father loves his new cordless vacuum cleaner because he can carry it up the stairs without looking for a socket.","t":"我爸爸很喜歡他的新無線吸塵器，因為他可以把它拿上樓而不用找插座。"},{"w":"vocal cords","p":"n.phr.","d":"the two thin bands in your throat that make sound when you speak","c":"聲帶","s":"The singer rested her vocal cords for a whole week before the concert, so she did not speak a single word.","t":"歌手在演唱會前讓聲帶休息了整整一週，所以她一個字都沒說。"},{"w":"correspond","p":"v.","d":"to match or be the same as something; to be equal to","c":"符合；相當於；對應","s":"The numbers on your ticket correspond to the seat numbers in the theater, so please check them before you sit down.","t":"你票上的號碼對應劇院裡的座位號碼，所以坐下前請先核對。","h":1},{"w":"correspond","p":"v.","d":"to write letters or emails to someone regularly","c":"通信","s":"My grandmother and her best friend in Canada have corresponded by letter every month for over fifty years.","t":"我奶奶和她在加拿大的好朋友每個月都寫信通信，已經超過五十年了。","a":"corresponded"},{"w":"correspond with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to match something; to write to someone regularly","c":"與…相符；與…通信","s":"What the witness told the police did not correspond with what the camera recorded, so they questioned her again.","t":"證人告訴警方的話與攝影機拍到的畫面不符，所以警方又再次詢問她。"},{"w":"correspondence","p":"n.","d":"letters or emails sent between people; the act of writing letters","c":"通信；信件往來","s":"The museum displays the correspondence between the two famous writers, including more than two hundred handwritten letters.","t":"博物館展出這兩位名作家之間的書信往來，包括兩百多封手寫信件。"},{"w":"correspondent","p":"n.","d":"a reporter who sends news from a particular place or about a particular subject","c":"特派記者；通訊記者","s":"Our news channel's correspondent in London reported live from outside the palace during the royal wedding.","t":"我們新聞台駐倫敦的特派記者在皇室婚禮期間於皇宮外進行現場報導。"},{"w":"corresponding","p":"adj.","d":"matching or connected with something you have just mentioned","c":"相應的；對應的","s":"As the price of oil went up this year, there was a corresponding rise in the cost of bus and taxi rides across the city.","t":"今年油價上漲時，全市公車和計程車的費用也出現了相應的上漲。"},{"w":"costume","p":"n.","d":"special clothes worn for a play, party, or festival, or typical of a place or time","c":"戲服；服裝；裝扮","s":"For the school play, my mother spent two weekends sewing a king's costume with a long purple cloak and a gold crown.","t":"為了學校的話劇，我媽媽花了兩個週末縫製一套國王的戲服，有長長的紫色披風和金色的王冠。","h":1},{"w":"costume party","p":"n.phr.","d":"a party where everyone dresses up as a character","c":"化裝舞會；變裝派對","s":"Everyone at the costume party laughed when my uncle walked in dressed as a giant banana with sunglasses.","t":"當我叔叔打扮成戴墨鏡的大香蕉走進化裝舞會時，大家都笑了。"},{"w":"in costume","p":"phr.","d":"wearing special clothes for a play or festival","c":"穿著戲服（扮裝）","s":"The actors were already in costume an hour before the show, walking around backstage as kings, witches, and animals.","t":"演出前一小時，演員們就已經穿好戲服，扮成國王、女巫和動物在後台走來走去。"},{"w":"costume jewelry","p":"n.phr.","d":"cheap jewelry made to look like expensive jewelry","c":"人造珠寶；飾品","s":"The actress wore costume jewelry on stage because real diamonds would be too expensive and dangerous to use every night.","t":"女演員在舞台上戴人造珠寶，因為真的鑽石每晚使用太昂貴也太危險。"},{"w":"cottage","p":"n.","d":"a small house, especially an old one in the countryside","c":"小屋；農舍","s":"My grandparents live in a stone cottage by the lake, and we spend every summer holiday swimming and fishing there.","t":"我的祖父母住在湖邊的一間石造小屋，我們每年暑假都在那裡游泳和釣魚。","h":1},{"w":"cottage industry","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small business in which people make things at home","c":"家庭手工業","s":"Making handmade paper used to be a cottage industry in this village, and a few families still do it the old way.","t":"手工造紙曾經是這個村子的家庭手工業，現在仍有幾個家庭用老方法製作。"},{"w":"cottage cheese","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soft white cheese made from milk","c":"茅屋起司；卡達起司","s":"My aunt eats cottage cheese with fruit for breakfast because it is high in protein and low in fat.","t":"我阿姨早餐吃茅屋起司配水果，因為它蛋白質含量高、脂肪含量低。"}]},{"unit":10,"theme":"council – cushion","cards":[{"w":"council","p":"n.","d":"a group of people chosen to make decisions for a town, school, or organization","c":"理事會；議會；委員會","s":"The town council meets every Tuesday evening to talk about local problems such as traffic, parks, and garbage collection.","t":"鎮議會每週二晚上開會，討論交通、公園和垃圾收集等地方問題。","h":1},{"w":"city council","p":"n.phr.","d":"the group of elected people who run a city","c":"市議會","s":"After many parents complained about the dangerous crossing, the city council finally agreed to build a new footbridge near the school.","t":"在許多家長抱怨那個危險的路口之後，市議會終於同意在學校附近建一座新的天橋。"},{"w":"student council","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of students chosen to speak for all students at a school","c":"學生會","s":"Our student council is planning a charity concert next month, and every class has been asked to prepare one performance.","t":"我們的學生會正在規劃下個月的慈善音樂會，每個班級都被要求準備一個表演。"},{"w":"councilor","p":"n.","d":"a member of a council","c":"議員；理事","s":"The young councilor promised to fix the broken streetlights in our neighborhood, and she kept her word within two weeks.","t":"那位年輕的議員承諾修好我們社區壞掉的路燈，而且她在兩週內就實現了承諾。"},{"w":"counter","p":"n.","d":"a long flat surface in a shop or kitchen where people are served or work","c":"櫃檯；流理台","s":"Please pay at the counter near the door, and the clerk will give you a receipt and a bag for your books.","t":"請到門邊的櫃檯付款，店員會給你收據和一個裝書的袋子。","h":1},{"w":"counter","p":"v.","d":"to say or do something in answer to an attack or argument","c":"反駁；反擊；抵銷","s":"When his boss said the plan was too expensive, Tom tried to counter the argument with numbers from last year's report.","t":"當老闆說這個計畫太貴時，湯姆試著用去年報告裡的數字來反駁這個論點。"},{"w":"over the counter","p":"phr.","d":"sold in a shop without a doctor's prescription","c":"不需處方即可購買的","s":"This cold medicine is sold over the counter, so you can buy it at any drugstore without seeing a doctor first.","t":"這種感冒藥是不需處方就能買到的，所以你不用先看醫生就可以在任何藥局買到。"},{"w":"counterpart","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that has the same job or position as another in a different place","c":"相對應的人或物","s":"The Taiwanese minister met her Japanese counterpart in Tokyo, and they discussed how to help students study abroad.","t":"台灣的部長在東京會見了她的日本對應官員，他們討論了如何幫助學生出國留學。"},{"w":"counterclockwise","p":"adv.","d":"in the opposite direction to the hands of a clock","c":"逆時針地","s":"To open the old jar, you need to turn the lid counterclockwise while holding the bottom firmly with your other hand.","t":"要打開這個舊罐子，你需要一手牢牢握住底部，另一手把蓋子逆時針轉開。"},{"w":"courageous","p":"adj.","d":"brave; not afraid to do something difficult or dangerous","c":"勇敢的；有膽量的","s":"The courageous firefighter ran back into the burning house twice, and she carried out two children and an old man.","t":"那位勇敢的消防員兩次跑回燃燒的房子，救出了兩個孩子和一位老人。","h":1},{"w":"courage","p":"n.","d":"the ability to do something dangerous or difficult without fear","c":"勇氣","s":"It took a lot of courage for the shy boy to stand on the stage and sing in front of the whole school.","t":"那個害羞的男孩要站上舞台在全校面前唱歌，需要很大的勇氣。"},{"w":"courageously","p":"adv.","d":"in a brave way","c":"勇敢地","s":"The small dog courageously barked at the snake until its owner came, and nobody in the family was hurt.","t":"那隻小狗勇敢地對著蛇吠叫，直到主人過來，家裡沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone hope or confidence to do something","c":"鼓勵","s":"My teachers always encourage us to ask questions in class, because they believe that is the fastest way to learn.","t":"我的老師總是鼓勵我們在課堂上提問，因為他們相信那是最快的學習方式。"},{"w":"encouragement","p":"n.","d":"words or actions that give someone hope or confidence","c":"鼓勵","s":"With a little encouragement from her coach, the nervous runner found the strength to finish the last two kilometers.","t":"在教練的一點鼓勵下，那位緊張的跑者找到了力量跑完最後兩公里。"},{"w":"courtesy","p":"n.","d":"polite behavior that shows respect for other people","c":"禮貌；謙恭","s":"Out of courtesy, you should always knock on the door before you enter your roommate's bedroom, even when it is open.","t":"出於禮貌，進入室友房間之前你應該先敲門，即使門是開著的。","h":1},{"w":"courteous","p":"adj.","d":"polite and showing respect","c":"有禮貌的；謙恭的","s":"The hotel staff were so courteous that they carried our heavy bags upstairs and brought us hot tea without being asked.","t":"飯店員工非常有禮貌，不用我們開口就把沉重的行李搬上樓，還為我們送上熱茶。"},{"w":"discourteous","p":"adj.","d":"rude; not polite","c":"無禮的；失禮的","s":"It is discourteous to look at your phone while someone is talking to you, so put it away during dinner.","t":"別人跟你說話時看手機是不禮貌的，所以吃晚餐時把手機收起來。"},{"w":"court","p":"n.","d":"the place where legal cases are judged; an area for playing a ball game","c":"法庭；球場","s":"The witness had to appear in court on Monday morning and tell the judge exactly what she had seen that night.","t":"證人必須在週一早上出席法庭，告訴法官她那晚確切看到了什麼。"},{"w":"coward","p":"n.","d":"a person who is not brave and avoids danger or difficulty","c":"懦夫；膽小鬼","s":"He felt like a coward because he ran away when the two older boys started to bully his little brother.","t":"當兩個大男孩開始欺負他弟弟時他跑掉了，所以他覺得自己像個懦夫。","h":1},{"w":"cowardly","p":"adj.","d":"not brave; afraid to face danger or difficulty","c":"膽小的；懦弱的","s":"Leaving a note instead of saying goodbye in person was a cowardly thing to do, and his friends were disappointed in him.","t":"留一張紙條而不是親自道別是一件懦弱的事，他的朋友對他很失望。"},{"w":"cowardice","p":"n.","d":"behavior that shows a lack of courage","c":"膽小；懦弱","s":"The soldier was punished for cowardice because he hid in the forest while his team was fighting the enemy.","t":"那名士兵因為懦弱而受到懲罰，因為他的隊友在和敵人作戰時，他躲在森林裡。"},{"w":"crack","p":"n.","d":"a thin line on a surface where something is broken but not in pieces","c":"裂縫；裂痕","s":"There is a long crack in the bathroom wall, so my father is going to call someone to repair it this weekend.","t":"浴室牆上有一道長裂縫，所以我爸爸這個週末要找人來修理。","h":1},{"w":"crack","p":"v.","d":"to break so that lines appear on the surface; to make a sudden sharp sound","c":"使破裂；裂開；發出爆裂聲","s":"If you pour boiling water into a cold glass, it may crack at once, so let the glass warm up first.","t":"如果你把滾水倒進冰冷的玻璃杯，它可能會立刻裂開，所以先讓杯子回溫。"},{"w":"crack down on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start dealing with bad behavior in a much stricter way","c":"嚴厲打擊；取締","s":"The police have decided to crack down on drunk driving during the holidays, so there are checkpoints on every main road.","t":"警方決定在假期期間嚴厲取締酒駕，所以每條主要道路上都有檢查站。"},{"w":"crack a joke","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell a joke","c":"說笑話","s":"Our science teacher likes to crack a joke at the start of each class, and it helps everyone relax before the hard lesson begins.","t":"我們的理化老師喜歡在每堂課開始時說個笑話，這讓大家在困難的課程開始前放鬆下來。"},{"w":"cracker","p":"n.","d":"a thin, dry, hard biscuit","c":"薄脆餅乾","s":"My grandmother always keeps a box of crackers in her kitchen, and she serves them with cheese when guests visit.","t":"我奶奶廚房裡總是放著一盒薄脆餅乾，有客人來時她會配著起司端出來。","a":"crackers"},{"w":"craft","p":"n.","d":"an activity that needs skill with the hands; a boat, aircraft, or spacecraft","c":"工藝；手藝；船；飛行器","s":"Making paper lanterns is a traditional craft in this village, and children learn it from their grandparents at a young age.","t":"做紙燈籠是這個村子的傳統工藝，孩子們從小就向祖父母學習。","h":1},{"w":"craftsman","p":"n.","d":"a person who is skilled at making things with their hands","c":"工匠；手藝人","s":"The old craftsman spent three months carving the wooden door, and every flower on it looks almost real.","t":"那位老工匠花了三個月雕刻這扇木門，上面的每一朵花看起來幾乎都像真的。"},{"w":"handicraft","p":"n.","d":"something beautiful or useful made by hand","c":"手工藝品","s":"At the weekend market, you can buy local handicrafts such as bamboo baskets, painted fans, and hand-made soap.","t":"在週末市集，你可以買到當地的手工藝品，像是竹籃、彩繪扇子和手工肥皂。","a":"handicrafts"},{"w":"aircraft","p":"n.","d":"a plane, helicopter, or other machine that flies","c":"飛機；航空器","s":"The small aircraft had to land in a field because its engine stopped working, but luckily nobody on board was hurt.","t":"那架小飛機因為引擎停止運轉而不得不降落在田裡，幸好機上沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"crafty","p":"adj.","d":"clever at getting what you want, often by tricking people","c":"狡猾的；詭計多端的","s":"The crafty fox in the story tricks the crow into singing, and then it quickly steals the cheese from her mouth.","t":"故事裡狡猾的狐狸騙烏鴉唱歌，然後迅速從她嘴裡偷走起司。"},{"w":"creation","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something new; something that has been made","c":"創造；創作；作品","s":"The creation of a new school uniform took almost a year, because students, teachers, and parents all wanted different designs.","t":"新校服的設計創作花了將近一年，因為學生、老師和家長都想要不同的款式。","h":1},{"w":"creativity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to think of new ideas and make new things","c":"創造力；創意","s":"Art class is my favorite because the teacher lets us use our creativity instead of copying the pictures in the textbook.","t":"美術課是我最喜歡的課，因為老師讓我們發揮創造力，而不是照著課本的圖畫臨摹。","h":1},{"w":"create","p":"v.","d":"to make something new","c":"創造；創作","s":"The students worked together to create a short film about their town, and it won first prize in the city competition.","t":"學生們合作創作了一部關於他們小鎮的短片，並在市賽中獲得第一名。"},{"w":"creative","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new ideas or making new things","c":"有創意的；有創造力的","s":"My sister is very creative, so she turned our old jeans into a colorful bag that everyone at school admires.","t":"我姐姐非常有創意，她把我們的舊牛仔褲變成一個色彩鮮豔的包包，學校每個人都很欣賞。"},{"w":"creator","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes or invents something","c":"創造者；創作者","s":"The creator of this popular cartoon started drawing it in a tiny apartment when he was still a university student.","t":"這部熱門卡通的創作者還是大學生時，就在一間小公寓裡開始畫它了。"},{"w":"creature","p":"n.","d":"any living thing that is not a plant, especially an animal","c":"生物；動物","s":"Scientists found a strange creature deep in the ocean, and it glows in the dark to attract small fish.","t":"科學家在深海發現了一種奇怪的生物，它會在黑暗中發光以吸引小魚。"},{"w":"creep, crept, crept","p":"v.","d":"to move slowly and quietly so that nobody notices you","c":"悄悄地移動；爬行","s":"The cat crept slowly toward the bird on the fence, but the bird saw it and flew away just in time.","t":"那隻貓慢慢地朝籬笆上的鳥悄悄爬行過去，但鳥看見了它，及時飛走了。","a":"crept","h":1},{"w":"creep up on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to approach someone quietly from behind; to happen gradually without being noticed","c":"悄悄接近；不知不覺地來到","s":"My brother loves to creep up on me while I am studying, and then he shouts loudly to make me jump.","t":"我哥哥喜歡在我讀書時從後面悄悄接近我，然後大聲喊叫讓我嚇一跳。"},{"w":"creepy","p":"adj.","d":"strange and frightening in a way that makes you nervous","c":"令人毛骨悚然的；詭異的","s":"The empty house at the end of the street looks so creepy at night that the children refuse to walk past it alone.","t":"街尾那間空房子晚上看起來非常詭異，孩子們都不敢單獨走過。"},{"w":"critic","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to give opinions about books, films, or art; a person who says something is bad","c":"評論家；批評者","s":"The famous food critic gave our little restaurant five stars, and since then the place has been full every night.","t":"那位知名的美食評論家給我們的小餐廳五顆星，從那時起這裡每晚都客滿。","h":1},{"w":"critical","p":"adj.","d":"saying that something is bad or wrong; very important or serious","c":"批評的；批判性的；關鍵的；危急的","s":"My father is very critical of my cooking, so I was surprised when he asked for a second bowl of my soup.","t":"我爸爸對我的廚藝非常挑剔，所以當他要求再來一碗我煮的湯時，我很驚訝。","h":1},{"w":"criticism","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying what is bad or wrong about something or someone","c":"批評；評論","s":"The new movie received a lot of criticism for its weak story, even though the actors did a very good job.","t":"這部新電影因劇情薄弱而受到許多批評，儘管演員們表現得非常好。","h":1},{"w":"criticize","p":"v.","d":"to say that something or someone is bad or wrong","c":"批評","s":"It is easy to criticize other people's work, but it is much harder to make something good yourself.","t":"批評別人的作品很容易，但自己做出好東西困難得多。","h":1},{"w":"critically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows careful judgment; seriously","c":"批判性地；嚴重地","s":"Good readers think critically about what they read online, because not every website tells the truth.","t":"好的讀者會對網路上讀到的內容進行批判性思考，因為不是每個網站都說真話。"},{"w":"be critical of","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to say that someone or something is bad or wrong","c":"對…持批評態度","s":"Many parents are critical of the new school schedule, because classes now end so late that children get home after dark.","t":"許多家長對新的學校時間表持批評態度，因為現在課程結束得太晚，孩子天黑後才到家。","a":"are critical of"},{"w":"cruelty","p":"n.","d":"behavior that causes pain or suffering to people or animals","c":"殘酷；殘忍","s":"The video of a man kicking a puppy shocked the whole country, and he was later fined for cruelty to animals.","t":"一名男子踢小狗的影片震驚全國，他後來因為對動物殘忍而被罰款。","h":1},{"w":"cruel","p":"adj.","d":"causing pain or suffering to others on purpose","c":"殘忍的；殘酷的","s":"It is cruel to keep a large dog in a tiny cage all day, so the animal group took the dog away from its owner.","t":"整天把大狗關在小籠子裡是殘忍的，所以動保團體把狗從主人那裡帶走了。"},{"w":"cruelly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that causes pain or suffering","c":"殘酷地；殘忍地","s":"The children in the story are treated cruelly by their stepmother, who makes them work from morning till night.","t":"故事裡的孩子被繼母殘酷地對待，她讓他們從早到晚工作。"},{"w":"be cruel to","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to treat someone or something in a way that causes pain","c":"對…殘忍","s":"You should never be cruel to younger students just because they are smaller and cannot fight back.","t":"你絕不應該因為年幼的學生比較小、無法反抗就對他們殘忍。"},{"w":"crunchy","p":"adj.","d":"hard and making a loud sound when you bite it","c":"脆的；鬆脆的","s":"I like my toast crunchy and golden brown, so I always leave it in the toaster a little longer than my sister does.","t":"我喜歡吐司酥脆金黃，所以我總是比姐姐多烤一會兒。","h":1},{"w":"crunch","p":"v.","d":"to make a loud sound when biting hard food or walking on something hard","c":"嘎吱作響地咬或踩","s":"We could hear the dry leaves crunch under our shoes as we walked through the quiet park in late autumn.","t":"我們走過晚秋寧靜的公園時，可以聽到乾葉子在鞋下嘎吱作響。"},{"w":"crunch","p":"n.","d":"a loud sound made when something hard is bitten or crushed; a difficult situation","c":"嘎吱聲；危機","s":"There was a loud crunch when my brother bit into the apple, and everyone in the quiet library turned to look at him.","t":"我哥哥咬下蘋果時發出一聲響亮的嘎吱聲，安靜的圖書館裡每個人都轉頭看他。"},{"w":"crush","p":"v.","d":"to press something so hard that it breaks or becomes flat","c":"壓碎；壓扁","s":"Be careful not to crush the eggs at the bottom of the bag when you put the heavy bottles of milk on top.","t":"把沉重的牛奶瓶放上去時，小心不要壓破袋子底部的雞蛋。","h":1},{"w":"crush","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of love for someone that usually does not last long","c":"迷戀","s":"My cousin has had a crush on the boy next door since summer camp, but she is too shy to talk to him.","t":"我表妹從夏令營以來就一直迷戀隔壁的男孩，但她太害羞，不敢跟他說話。"},{"w":"have a crush on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a strong but usually short feeling of love for someone","c":"迷戀某人","s":"Everyone in class knows that Peter has a crush on the new music teacher, because his face turns red whenever she speaks to him.","t":"班上每個人都知道彼得迷戀新來的音樂老師，因為每當她跟他說話，他的臉就會變紅。","a":"has a crush on"},{"w":"crushed","p":"adj.","d":"pressed into small pieces; extremely sad or disappointed","c":"壓碎的；深受打擊的","s":"Add some crushed garlic and a little salt to the soup, and then let it cook slowly for another twenty minutes.","t":"在湯裡加一些壓碎的大蒜和少許鹽，然後再慢煮二十分鐘。"},{"w":"cube","p":"n.","d":"a solid object with six equal square sides","c":"立方體；方塊","s":"The teacher asked us to count how many small cubes were needed to build the large tower in the picture.","t":"老師要我們算出圖片中建造那座大塔需要多少個小方塊。","a":"cubes","h":1},{"w":"ice cube","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small block of ice used to make drinks cold","c":"冰塊","s":"It was so hot that the ice cubes in my lemonade melted in two minutes, and the drink soon became warm again.","t":"天氣熱到我檸檬水裡的冰塊兩分鐘就融化了，飲料很快又變溫了。","a":"ice cubes"},{"w":"cube","p":"v.","d":"to cut food into small square pieces","c":"把…切成小方塊","s":"First, cube the potatoes and carrots, and then fry them with onions before you add water to the pot.","t":"首先，把馬鈴薯和紅蘿蔔切成小方塊，然後和洋蔥一起炒，再把水加進鍋裡。"},{"w":"cubic","p":"adj.","d":"measured by multiplying length, width, and height","c":"立方的","s":"The new water tank holds about ten cubic meters of water, which is enough for the whole building for one day.","t":"新水塔可容納大約十立方公尺的水，足夠整棟大樓使用一天。"},{"w":"cue","p":"n.","d":"a signal that tells someone to start doing something","c":"提示；暗示；信號","s":"When the lights go down, that is your cue to walk onto the stage and begin the first song of the show.","t":"燈光暗下來時，那就是你走上舞台、開始演出第一首歌的提示。","h":1},{"w":"cue","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a signal to start doing something","c":"給…提示；示意","s":"The director will cue the band with a small wave of his hand, and then the music should start right away.","t":"導演會輕輕揮手示意樂隊，然後音樂應該立刻開始。"},{"w":"on cue","p":"phr.","d":"at exactly the right moment, as if planned","c":"恰好在那時；準時地","s":"Just as the teacher said the word 'rain,' the thunder came right on cue, and the whole class started laughing.","t":"老師剛說出「雨」這個字，雷聲就恰好響起，全班都笑了起來。"},{"w":"take one's cue from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to copy what someone else does because it shows you how to act","c":"以…為榜樣；效法","s":"Young children often take their cue from their parents, so if you read books at home, your kids will probably love reading too.","t":"小孩子常常效法父母，所以如果你在家看書，你的孩子可能也會愛上閱讀。","a":"take their cue from"},{"w":"cunning","p":"adj.","d":"clever at getting what you want, especially by tricking people","c":"狡猾的；精明的","s":"The cunning salesman told us the watch was the last one in the store, but we saw ten more in the back room.","t":"那個狡猾的售貨員告訴我們這是店裡最後一支手錶，但我們在後面房間看到還有十支。","h":1},{"w":"cunning","p":"n.","d":"the ability to get what you want by being clever and tricking people","c":"狡猾；詭計","s":"In the old tale, the small rabbit uses its cunning to escape from the tiger, who is much bigger and stronger.","t":"在古老的故事裡，小兔子用它的狡猾逃離了體型更大更強壯的老虎。"},{"w":"cunningly","p":"adv.","d":"in a clever way that tricks people","c":"狡猾地","s":"The thief cunningly dressed as a repairman, so the guard let him into the building without checking his card.","t":"小偷狡猾地打扮成修理工，所以警衛沒檢查他的證件就讓他進了大樓。"},{"w":"curiosity","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to know or learn about something","c":"好奇心","s":"Her curiosity about space began when she was six, and now she is studying to become an astronomer.","t":"她對太空的好奇心從六歲開始，現在她正在攻讀天文學。","h":1},{"w":"curious","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to know or learn about something","c":"好奇的","s":"The curious puppy sniffed every corner of the new apartment and then fell asleep in a shoe box.","t":"那隻好奇的小狗聞了新公寓的每個角落，然後在鞋盒裡睡著了。"},{"w":"be curious about","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to want to know more about something","c":"對…感到好奇","s":"Many tourists are curious about the night markets in Taiwan, so our teacher asked us to make a video introducing our favorite stalls.","t":"許多觀光客對台灣的夜市感到好奇，所以老師要我們拍影片介紹我們最喜歡的攤位。","a":"are curious about"},{"w":"curiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you want to know more; strangely","c":"好奇地；奇怪地","s":"The little girl looked curiously at the robot, and then she asked whether it could feel happy or sad.","t":"小女孩好奇地看著機器人，然後問它會不會感到快樂或難過。"},{"w":"out of curiosity","p":"phr.","d":"because you want to know something, not for an important reason","c":"出於好奇","s":"Just out of curiosity, I opened the old box in the attic and found hundreds of letters that my grandfather wrote during the war.","t":"只是出於好奇，我打開閣樓裡的舊箱子，發現了幾百封爺爺在戰爭期間寫的信。"},{"w":"curl","p":"v.","d":"to form or make something into a round or curved shape","c":"使捲曲；捲","s":"My hair starts to curl as soon as it gets wet, so I always carry an umbrella on rainy days.","t":"我的頭髮一碰到水就開始捲曲，所以下雨天我總是帶著雨傘。","h":1},{"w":"curl","p":"n.","d":"a piece of hair that forms a round or curved shape","c":"捲髮；捲曲物","s":"The baby has soft golden curls that fall over her eyes, and everyone who meets her wants to touch them.","t":"寶寶有柔軟的金色捲髮垂在眼前，每個見到她的人都想摸一摸。","a":"curls"},{"w":"curly","p":"adj.","d":"having curls or a curved shape","c":"捲的；捲曲的","s":"You can easily find my brother in a crowd because of his thick curly hair and bright red glasses.","t":"你可以輕易在人群中找到我哥哥，因為他有濃密的捲髮和亮紅色的眼鏡。"},{"w":"curl up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to sit or lie with your arms and legs bent close to your body","c":"蜷縮","s":"On cold winter nights, I love to curl up on the sofa with a blanket, a cup of hot cocoa, and a good book.","t":"在寒冷的冬夜，我喜歡裹著毯子、拿著一杯熱可可和一本好書，蜷縮在沙發上。"},{"w":"curse","p":"n.","d":"magic words that are meant to bring bad luck; a cause of trouble","c":"詛咒；禍根","s":"According to the legend, anyone who takes a stone from the temple will suffer a terrible curse for the rest of their life.","t":"根據傳說，任何從寺廟拿走石頭的人都會終生遭受可怕的詛咒。","h":1},{"w":"curse","p":"v.","d":"to say rude words because you are angry; to wish bad luck on someone","c":"咒罵；詛咒","s":"The driver began to curse loudly when he saw that someone had scratched his new car in the parking lot.","t":"那位司機看到有人在停車場刮傷他的新車時，開始大聲咒罵。"},{"w":"cursed","p":"adj.","d":"having a curse on it; bringing bad luck","c":"被詛咒的；倒霉的","s":"The villagers believe the old well is cursed, so nobody dares to drink its water, even on the hottest days.","t":"村民相信那口古井是被詛咒的，所以即使在最熱的日子也沒人敢喝它的水。"},{"w":"curve","p":"n.","d":"a line that bends like part of a circle","c":"曲線；彎道","s":"Slow down before the sharp curve in the mountain road, because many accidents have happened there on rainy nights.","t":"在山路的急彎前要減速，因為雨夜在那裡發生過許多事故。","h":1},{"w":"curve","p":"v.","d":"to bend or move in the shape of a curve","c":"彎曲；呈曲線前進","s":"The river begins to curve to the east after it passes the bridge, and then it flows into the sea.","t":"河流過橋後開始向東彎曲，然後流入大海。"},{"w":"curved","p":"adj.","d":"having a round shape like part of a circle","c":"彎曲的","s":"The new library has a curved glass wall that lets in sunlight all day, so students enjoy reading there.","t":"新圖書館有一面彎曲的玻璃牆，整天都能照進陽光，所以學生們喜歡在那裡閱讀。"},{"w":"curvy","p":"adj.","d":"having many curves","c":"彎彎曲曲的；曲線多的","s":"The curvy road to the beach made my little sister feel sick, so we had to stop the car twice.","t":"通往海灘的彎彎曲曲的路讓我妹妹想吐，所以我們不得不停車兩次。"},{"w":"learning curve","p":"n.phr.","d":"the rate at which someone learns a new skill","c":"學習曲線","s":"There is a steep learning curve when you start using this software, but after a week most people find it easy.","t":"剛開始使用這個軟體時學習曲線很陡，但一週後大多數人覺得它很容易。"},{"w":"cushion","p":"n.","d":"a soft bag filled with material that you sit on or lean against","c":"軟墊；靠墊","s":"Grandma always puts a thick cushion on the wooden chair before she sits down to watch her evening TV shows.","t":"奶奶坐下看晚間電視節目前，總是先在木椅上放一個厚厚的軟墊。","h":1},{"w":"cushion","p":"v.","d":"to make the effect of a fall or a bad situation less serious","c":"緩衝；減輕","s":"The thick snow helped to cushion his fall from the roof, so he only hurt his arm instead of breaking his leg.","t":"厚厚的積雪幫助緩衝了他從屋頂摔落的衝擊，所以他只傷了手臂，沒有摔斷腿。"},{"w":"cushioned","p":"adj.","d":"having a soft layer that protects or makes something comfortable","c":"有軟墊的；有緩衝的","s":"These running shoes are well cushioned, so your feet will not hurt even after running for more than an hour.","t":"這些跑鞋緩衝性很好，所以即使跑超過一小時，你的腳也不會痛。"}]},{"unit":11,"theme":"damp – destruction","cards":[{"w":"damp","p":"adj.","d":"a little wet, often in an unpleasant way","c":"潮濕的","s":"The towels in the bathroom are still damp from this morning, so please hang them outside in the sun to dry.","t":"浴室裡的毛巾從今天早上到現在還是潮濕的，所以請把它們掛到外面曬太陽晾乾。","h":1},{"w":"damp","p":"n.","d":"wetness in the air or on walls, especially inside a building","c":"濕氣","s":"There is a smell of damp in the old basement, and the walls feel cold and wet whenever it rains for several days.","t":"舊地下室裡有一股濕氣的味道，每當連續下雨幾天，牆壁摸起來又冷又濕。"},{"w":"dampen","p":"v.","d":"to make something slightly wet; to make a feeling less strong","c":"弄濕；使減弱","s":"Even the heavy rain could not dampen the fans' excitement, and they kept singing until the concert finally began.","t":"即使是大雨也無法減弱歌迷們的興奮，他們一直唱歌直到演唱會終於開始。"},{"w":"dampness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being slightly wet","c":"潮濕；濕氣","s":"Because of the dampness in our apartment during the rainy season, my mother bought a machine that takes water out of the air.","t":"因為雨季時我們公寓裡的潮濕，我媽媽買了一台從空氣中抽出水分的機器。"},{"w":"deadline","p":"n.","d":"the time or day by which something must be finished","c":"截止日期；最後期限","s":"The deadline for the science report is next Friday, so we need to finish our experiment before the weekend.","t":"科學報告的截止日期是下週五，所以我們需要在週末前完成實驗。","h":1},{"w":"meet the deadline","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finish something by the time it must be done","c":"趕上截止日期","s":"If we want to meet the deadline, everyone in the group has to send their part of the project to me by Wednesday night.","t":"如果我們想趕上截止日期，小組裡每個人都必須在週三晚上前把自己負責的部分寄給我。"},{"w":"miss the deadline","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fail to finish something by the time it must be done","c":"錯過截止日期","s":"Students who miss the deadline will lose ten points, so do not wait until the last day to start writing your essay.","t":"錯過截止日期的學生會被扣十分，所以不要等到最後一天才開始寫作文。"},{"w":"extend the deadline","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give more time for something to be finished","c":"延長截止日期","s":"Because many students were sick last week, the teacher agreed to extend the deadline by three more days for the whole class.","t":"因為上週許多學生生病，老師同意為全班延長截止日期三天。"},{"w":"declare","p":"v.","d":"to say something officially or in public","c":"宣布；宣告；申報","s":"The judge stood up to declare the winner of the speech contest, and the whole hall became completely silent.","t":"評審站起來宣布演講比賽的優勝者，整個大廳變得鴉雀無聲。","h":1},{"w":"declaration","p":"n.","d":"an official or public statement","c":"宣言；聲明；申報","s":"The Declaration of Independence was signed in 1776, and Americans still celebrate that day with fireworks every summer.","t":"獨立宣言於 1776 年簽署，美國人至今每年夏天仍以煙火慶祝那一天。","a":"Declaration"},{"w":"declare war on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to officially announce the start of a war or a fight against something","c":"向…宣戰","s":"The mayor promised to declare war on the rats in the city, and new garbage cans with lids were placed on every street.","t":"市長承諾向城裡的老鼠宣戰，每條街上都放置了有蓋子的新垃圾桶。"},{"w":"have nothing to declare","p":"v.phr.","d":"to carry nothing that you must pay tax on when entering a country","c":"沒有需要申報的物品","s":"At the airport, I walked through the green door because I had nothing to declare; all I carried was some clothes and a few books.","t":"在機場，我走綠色通道，因為我沒有需要申報的物品；我帶的只有一些衣服和幾本書。","a":"had nothing to declare"},{"w":"decoration","p":"n.","d":"something that is added to make a place or thing look more beautiful","c":"裝飾；裝飾品","s":"We hung paper lanterns and red decorations all over the classroom to get ready for the Chinese New Year party.","t":"我們在教室各處掛上紙燈籠和紅色裝飾品，為農曆新年派對做準備。","a":"decorations","h":1},{"w":"decorate","p":"v.","d":"to make something look more beautiful by adding things to it","c":"裝飾；佈置","s":"My sister and I plan to decorate the living room with balloons and flowers before our parents come home for their anniversary.","t":"我和姐姐打算在父母回家慶祝結婚紀念日前，用氣球和鮮花佈置客廳。"},{"w":"decorative","p":"adj.","d":"made to look beautiful rather than to be useful","c":"裝飾性的","s":"The small decorative plates on the wall are not for eating; my grandmother collected them during her trips around Europe.","t":"牆上那些小的裝飾盤子不是用來吃飯的；它們是我奶奶在歐洲旅行時收集的。"},{"w":"decorator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to paint houses or make rooms look beautiful","c":"室內裝潢師；油漆工","s":"The decorator suggested painting the bedroom light blue, because the color would make the small room feel bigger and calmer.","t":"室內裝潢師建議把臥室漆成淺藍色，因為這個顏色會讓小房間感覺更大、更平靜。"},{"w":"defeat","p":"v.","d":"to win against someone in a game, fight, or election","c":"擊敗；打敗","s":"Our school basketball team managed to defeat last year's champions by two points in the final seconds of the game.","t":"我們學校的籃球隊在比賽最後幾秒以兩分之差成功擊敗了去年的冠軍。","h":1},{"w":"defeat","p":"n.","d":"the fact of losing a game, fight, or election","c":"失敗；戰敗","s":"After the painful defeat in the city final, the coach told the players that losing was also part of learning.","t":"在市決賽痛苦的失敗之後，教練告訴球員們，輸球也是學習的一部分。"},{"w":"admit defeat","p":"v.phr.","d":"to accept that you have lost or cannot succeed","c":"認輸","s":"After trying to fix the computer for three hours, my father finally had to admit defeat and call a repair shop.","t":"試著修電腦三個小時後，我爸爸終於不得不認輸，打電話給維修店。"},{"w":"undefeated","p":"adj.","d":"never having lost","c":"不敗的；未被擊敗的","s":"The young boxer has remained undefeated for five years, and she will fight for the world title next month in Tokyo.","t":"這位年輕的拳擊手五年來保持不敗，下個月她將在東京爭奪世界冠軍。"},{"w":"defend","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone or something from attack or harm; to speak in support of","c":"保衛；防守；辯護","s":"The soldiers were ordered to defend the bridge at all costs, because it was the only road into the city.","t":"士兵們奉命不惜一切代價保衛那座橋，因為它是進城唯一的道路。","h":1},{"w":"defense","p":"n.","d":"the act of protecting someone or something from attack; the players who try to stop the other team from scoring","c":"防禦；防守；辯護","s":"Our team has a strong defense, so the other side could not score a single goal during the whole second half.","t":"我們球隊的防守很強，所以對方在整個下半場一球都沒進。","h":1},{"w":"defensible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be protected or supported with good reasons","c":"可防禦的；站得住腳的","s":"The castle was built on a hill with the river on three sides, which made it easily defensible against enemy attacks.","t":"這座城堡建在三面環河的山丘上，使它很容易防禦敵人的攻擊。","h":1},{"w":"defensive","p":"adj.","d":"used or meant to protect; behaving as if someone is attacking you","c":"防禦的；防守的；戒備的","s":"Whenever anyone asks about his grades, Peter gets very defensive and changes the subject as quickly as he can.","t":"每當有人問起他的成績，彼得就變得非常有戒心，並儘快轉移話題。","h":1},{"w":"defender","p":"n.","d":"a person who protects something; a player whose job is to stop the other team from scoring","c":"防守者；後衛；擁護者","s":"The tall defender blocked every shot in the last ten minutes, and his teammates lifted him onto their shoulders after the game.","t":"那位高大的後衛在最後十分鐘擋下了每一次射門，賽後隊友們把他抬到肩上。"},{"w":"self-defense","p":"n.","d":"the act of protecting yourself when someone attacks you","c":"自衛","s":"My mother signed me up for a self-defense class, so now I know what to do if someone tries to grab my bag.","t":"我媽媽幫我報名了一堂自衛課，所以現在如果有人想搶我的包包，我知道該怎麼做。"},{"w":"defenseless","p":"adj.","d":"unable to protect yourself","c":"無防備的；無力自衛的","s":"The defenseless baby birds sat in the nest and cried for their mother while a cat watched them from the tree below.","t":"無力自衛的雛鳥坐在巢裡哭喊著媽媽，而一隻貓從下方的樹上盯著牠們。"},{"w":"definite","p":"adj.","d":"clear and certain; not likely to change","c":"明確的；確定的","s":"We need a definite answer from you by Friday, because the hotel will not hold the rooms any longer than that.","t":"我們需要你在週五前給一個明確的答覆，因為飯店不會再為我們保留房間超過那一天。","h":1},{"w":"definitely","p":"adv.","d":"certainly; without any doubt","c":"肯定地；絕對地","s":"I will definitely come to your birthday party on Saturday, even if I have to finish my homework on the bus.","t":"我週六一定會去你的生日派對，即使我得在公車上寫完功課。"},{"w":"indefinite","p":"adj.","d":"not clear or fixed; without a known end","c":"不明確的；無限期的","s":"The old factory has been closed for an indefinite period, and nobody knows whether the workers will ever get their jobs back.","t":"那家舊工廠已經關閉了一段無限期的時間，沒有人知道工人們是否還能找回工作。"},{"w":"indefinitely","p":"adv.","d":"for a period of time with no fixed end","c":"無限期地","s":"Because of the heavy snow, all flights from the airport have been delayed indefinitely, and hundreds of travelers are sleeping on the floor.","t":"由於大雪，機場所有航班都無限期延誤，數百名旅客睡在地板上。"},{"w":"definition","p":"n.","d":"a statement that explains what a word means","c":"定義","s":"If you do not understand a word in the reading, look up its definition in the dictionary before you ask the teacher.","t":"如果你不懂閱讀中的某個字，在問老師之前先在字典裡查它的定義。"},{"w":"define","p":"v.","d":"to explain exactly what a word or idea means","c":"下定義；界定","s":"It is hard to define the word 'happiness' because it means something different to every person you ask.","t":"很難為「快樂」這個字下定義，因為對你問的每個人來說它的意思都不一樣。"},{"w":"delicate","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged; needing careful treatment; fine and beautiful","c":"精緻的；脆弱的；需小心處理的","s":"These delicate glass cups were a gift from my grandmother, so please wash them by hand instead of putting them in the machine.","t":"這些精緻易碎的玻璃杯是奶奶送的禮物，所以請用手洗，不要放進洗碗機。","h":1},{"w":"delicately","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful or gentle way","c":"精巧地；小心地","s":"The nurse delicately removed the bandage from the little boy's arm, and he did not even feel any pain.","t":"護士小心地拆掉小男孩手臂上的繃帶，他甚至沒感覺到任何疼痛。"},{"w":"delicacy","p":"n.","d":"a special, expensive, or rare food; the quality of being delicate","c":"美味佳餚；精緻；細膩","s":"Stinky tofu is a famous delicacy in Taiwan, but many foreign visitors need some courage to try it for the first time.","t":"臭豆腐是台灣有名的美食，但許多外國遊客第一次嘗試時需要一些勇氣。"},{"w":"delight","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great pleasure; something that gives great pleasure","c":"高興；喜悅；樂事","s":"To the children's great delight, the teacher announced that there would be no homework during the long holiday.","t":"讓孩子們非常高興的是，老師宣布長假期間沒有功課。","h":1},{"w":"delightful","p":"adj.","d":"very pleasant and enjoyable","c":"令人愉快的；宜人的","s":"We spent a delightful afternoon by the lake, eating sandwiches and watching the ducks swim with their babies.","t":"我們在湖邊度過了一個愉快的下午，吃著三明治，看鴨子帶著小鴨游泳。","h":1},{"w":"delight","p":"v.","d":"to give someone great pleasure","c":"使高興；使愉快","s":"The magician's tricks never fail to delight the audience, especially when he pulls a rabbit out of an empty hat.","t":"魔術師的把戲總是能讓觀眾開心，尤其是當他從空帽子裡拉出一隻兔子時。"},{"w":"delighted","p":"adj.","d":"very pleased","c":"高興的；欣喜的","s":"My grandparents were delighted when they heard that my cousin would be visiting them from Canada this summer.","t":"我的祖父母聽說表哥今年夏天會從加拿大來看他們時，非常高興。"},{"w":"be delighted to","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to be very happy to do something","c":"很高興做…","s":"Our principal said she was delighted to welcome the visiting students from Japan, and she even learned a few Japanese words for the speech.","t":"我們校長說她很高興歡迎來自日本的訪問學生，她甚至為演講學了幾個日文單字。","a":"was delighted to"},{"w":"take delight in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get great pleasure from something","c":"以…為樂","s":"My little brother seems to take delight in hiding my shoes before school, and he laughs every time I search for them.","t":"我弟弟似乎以上學前藏我的鞋子為樂，每次我找鞋子他都笑個不停。"},{"w":"demand","p":"n.","d":"a strong request; the wish of people to buy something","c":"要求；需求","s":"There is a huge demand for electric scooters in the city, so the shop sold out of them within a week.","t":"這座城市對電動機車有巨大的需求，所以那家店一週內就賣光了。","h":1},{"w":"demand","p":"v.","d":"to ask for something strongly, as if it is your right","c":"要求；需要","s":"The angry customers began to demand their money back when the concert was cancelled only an hour before it started.","t":"當演唱會在開始前一小時才被取消時，憤怒的顧客開始要求退款。"},{"w":"in demand","p":"phr.","d":"wanted by many people","c":"需求量大的；搶手的","s":"Good English teachers are always in demand in Taiwan, so my cousin found a job only two weeks after she graduated.","t":"好的英文老師在台灣總是很搶手，所以我表姐畢業後只花兩週就找到工作。"},{"w":"demanding","p":"adj.","d":"needing a lot of time, effort, or attention","c":"要求高的；費力的","s":"Being a nurse is a demanding job, because you often have to work at night and stay calm when patients are frightened.","t":"當護士是一份要求很高的工作，因為你常常得在夜裡工作，並在病人害怕時保持冷靜。"},{"w":"on demand","p":"phr.","d":"whenever someone asks for it","c":"隨需；按需求","s":"With this new app, you can watch thousands of movies on demand, so you never have to wait for a TV schedule again.","t":"有了這個新 App，你可以隨時依需求觀看數千部電影，再也不必等電視節目表了。"},{"w":"demonstrate","p":"v.","d":"to show how to do something; to prove that something is true","c":"示範；證明；展示","s":"The chef will demonstrate how to make dumplings from scratch, and then everyone in the class will try to make ten of their own.","t":"主廚將示範如何從頭製作水餃，然後班上每個人都會試著自己做十顆。","h":1},{"w":"demonstration","p":"n.","d":"an act of showing how something works; a march or meeting to protest or support something","c":"示範；展示；示威遊行","s":"The science museum gives a free demonstration of how volcanoes work every afternoon, and children love the fake red lava.","t":"科學博物館每天下午提供免費的火山運作示範，孩子們很喜歡那假的紅色岩漿。","h":1},{"w":"demonstrate","p":"v.","d":"to march or meet in public to protest or support something","c":"示威；遊行","s":"Thousands of workers plan to demonstrate outside the city hall tomorrow, because the company has not paid them for two months.","t":"數千名工人計畫明天在市政府外示威，因為公司已經兩個月沒付他們薪水。"},{"w":"demonstrator","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a protest; a person who shows how something works","c":"示威者；示範者","s":"The demonstrator at the shopping mall showed us how the new vacuum cleaner picks up both dust and water from the floor.","t":"購物中心的示範員向我們展示新的吸塵器如何同時吸起地板上的灰塵和水。"},{"w":"dense","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of things or people close together; thick and hard to see through","c":"稠密的；濃密的","s":"The forest was so dense that the hikers could not see the sky, and they had to use a map to find their way out.","t":"森林茂密到登山客看不見天空，他們必須用地圖才能找到出路。","h":1},{"w":"densely","p":"adv.","d":"with many things or people close together","c":"稠密地","s":"Taipei is a densely populated city, which is why apartments are small and most families do not own a garden.","t":"台北是一個人口稠密的城市，這就是為什麼公寓很小，而且大多數家庭沒有花園。"},{"w":"density","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something in a space; how close together things are","c":"密度","s":"Scientists measure the density of the ice to learn how much weight the frozen lake can hold before it breaks.","t":"科學家測量冰的密度，以了解結冰的湖面在破裂前能承受多少重量。"},{"w":"depart","p":"v.","d":"to leave a place, especially to start a journey","c":"出發；離開","s":"The train to Kaohsiung will depart from Platform 2 at exactly nine o'clock, so we should get to the station by half past eight.","t":"往高雄的火車將於九點整從第二月台出發，所以我們應該在八點半前到車站。","h":1},{"w":"departure","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving a place; a plane or train that leaves","c":"出發；離開；離境","s":"Please arrive at the airport at least two hours before your departure, because the lines at the check-in counter can be very long.","t":"請至少在出發前兩小時抵達機場，因為報到櫃檯的隊伍可能很長。","h":1},{"w":"depart from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave a place; to do something differently from the usual way","c":"從…出發；偏離","s":"The ferry to the island will depart from the old harbor this year, since the new one is still being repaired after the typhoon.","t":"今年往小島的渡輪將從舊港口出發，因為新港口在颱風後仍在修復中。"},{"w":"department","p":"n.","d":"a part of a large organization such as a school, company, or shop","c":"部門；系","s":"My aunt works in the sales department of a toy company, and she often brings home new games for us to try.","t":"我阿姨在一家玩具公司的業務部門工作，她常常帶新遊戲回家給我們試玩。"},{"w":"department store","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large shop that sells many different kinds of things","c":"百貨公司","s":"We went to the department store to buy a winter coat for my father, but we ended up buying shoes for everyone instead.","t":"我們去百貨公司幫爸爸買冬天的外套，結果卻幫每個人買了鞋子。"},{"w":"dependent","p":"adj.","d":"needing someone or something in order to live or succeed","c":"依賴的；取決於…的","s":"Young birds are completely dependent on their parents for food until they learn how to fly and hunt by themselves.","t":"幼鳥在學會飛行和自己覓食之前，食物完全依賴父母。","h":1},{"w":"be dependent on","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to need someone or something; to be decided by something","c":"依賴…；取決於…","s":"Whether we go hiking on Sunday is dependent on the weather, so let's check the forecast again on Saturday night.","t":"我們週日是否去健行取決於天氣，所以我們週六晚上再看一次天氣預報吧。","a":"is dependent on"},{"w":"depend on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to need someone or something; to trust someone to help you","c":"依靠；依賴；取決於","s":"You can always depend on my brother when you need help with math, because he explains things patiently and never laughs at mistakes.","t":"當你需要數學方面的幫助時，你永遠可以依靠我哥哥，因為他會耐心解釋，而且從不嘲笑錯誤。"},{"w":"dependence","p":"n.","d":"the state of needing someone or something","c":"依賴；依靠","s":"Doctors worry about children's growing dependence on smartphones, since many of them cannot sit through a meal without one.","t":"醫生們擔心孩子們對智慧型手機日益增長的依賴，因為很多孩子沒有手機就無法安坐吃完一餐。"},{"w":"independent","p":"adj.","d":"not needing other people; not controlled by another country or group","c":"獨立的；自主的","s":"Living alone in Taichung for university has made my sister much more independent; she now cooks, cleans, and manages her own money.","t":"為了上大學獨自住在台中，讓我姐姐變得獨立多了；她現在會自己煮飯、打掃、管理自己的錢。"},{"w":"independence","p":"n.","d":"freedom from control by other people or another country","c":"獨立；自主","s":"Many teenagers want more independence from their parents, but they also need to show that they can be responsible first.","t":"許多青少年想要從父母那裡得到更多自主權，但他們也需要先證明自己可以負責任。"},{"w":"depression","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great sadness that lasts a long time; a long period when the economy is very bad","c":"沮喪；憂鬱；經濟蕭條","s":"After losing both his job and his dog in the same month, my uncle fell into a deep depression and rarely left his room.","t":"在同一個月失去工作和愛犬之後，我叔叔陷入深深的沮喪，很少離開房間。","h":1},{"w":"the Great Depression","p":"n.phr.","d":"the period in the 1930s when the world economy was very bad","c":"經濟大蕭條","s":"My great-grandfather grew up during the Great Depression, so he never threw away food and always kept some cash hidden at home.","t":"我的曾祖父在經濟大蕭條時期長大，所以他從不浪費食物，而且總是在家裡藏一些現金。"},{"w":"depress","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel very sad; to make something less active or lower","c":"使沮喪；使蕭條","s":"Rainy weekends always depress my mother, because she cannot work in her garden or go for her morning walks.","t":"下雨的週末總是讓我媽媽心情低落，因為她不能在花園裡工作，也不能去晨間散步。"},{"w":"depressed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling very sad and without hope","c":"沮喪的；消沉的","s":"Tom felt depressed after failing his driving test for the third time, but his friends took him out for dinner to cheer him up.","t":"第三次駕照考試失敗後，湯姆感到沮喪，但他的朋友帶他出去吃晚餐讓他開心起來。"},{"w":"depressing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel sad and without hope","c":"令人沮喪的","s":"The news about the forest fires was so depressing that my sister turned off the TV and went to plant some trees in the park.","t":"關於森林大火的新聞令人非常沮喪，所以我姐姐關掉電視，去公園種了幾棵樹。"},{"w":"deserve","p":"v.","d":"to have earned something because of what you have done","c":"應得；值得","s":"After studying every night for three months, Amy truly deserved the first prize, and nobody in the class was surprised.","t":"在每晚苦讀三個月之後，艾咪真的應得第一名，班上沒有人感到意外。","a":"deserved","h":1},{"w":"deserve to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have earned the right to do or get something","c":"應該得到…；有資格…","s":"The workers deserve to be paid for the extra hours they spent fixing the roads after the earthquake last spring.","t":"工人們應該為他們在去年春天地震後花在修路上的額外時數獲得報酬。"},{"w":"well-deserved","p":"adj.","d":"that someone has earned through hard work or good behavior","c":"應得的；理所當然的","s":"After working seven days a week all year, my parents are finally taking a well-deserved vacation in Hualien next month.","t":"在整年每週工作七天之後，我父母下個月終於要去花蓮度一個應得的假期。"},{"w":"deserving","p":"adj.","d":"worthy of help, praise, or a reward","c":"值得的；應受獎賞的","s":"The charity gives free computers to deserving students from poor families, so they can study online like their classmates.","t":"該慈善機構免費提供電腦給來自貧困家庭、值得幫助的學生，讓他們能像同學一樣在線上學習。"},{"w":"desperate","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that you have no hope and will do anything to change the situation; needing something very much","c":"絕望的；不顧一切的；極需要的","s":"The desperate farmers prayed for rain every day, because their rice fields had been dry for more than two months.","t":"絕望的農民每天祈求下雨，因為他們的稻田已經乾了兩個多月。","h":1},{"w":"desperately","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows great need or little hope","c":"拼命地；極度地","s":"The lost hikers shouted desperately for help all night, and a rescue helicopter finally found them at dawn.","t":"迷路的登山客整夜拼命地呼救，救援直升機終於在黎明時找到他們。"},{"w":"desperation","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of having no hope, which makes you do extreme things","c":"絕望；走投無路","s":"In desperation, the man sold his wedding ring to pay for his daughter's medicine before the hospital closed for the night.","t":"在走投無路之下，那名男子賣掉了結婚戒指，以便在醫院晚上關門前為女兒買藥。"},{"w":"be desperate for","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to need or want something very much","c":"極度渴望…；急需…","s":"After running the marathon under the hot sun, the runners were desperate for cold water and a place to sit in the shade.","t":"在烈日下跑完馬拉松後，跑者們急需冰水和一個陰涼的地方坐下。","a":"were desperate for"},{"w":"despite","p":"prep.","d":"without being affected by something; although something is true","c":"儘管；雖然","s":"Despite the heavy rain and strong wind, more than a thousand people came to the night market to celebrate the festival.","t":"儘管大雨和強風，仍有一千多人來到夜市慶祝節日。","a":"Despite","h":1},{"w":"in spite of","p":"prep.","d":"despite; without being stopped by something","c":"儘管；不顧","s":"My grandfather still walks five kilometers every morning in spite of his bad knee, and he says it keeps him young.","t":"儘管膝蓋不好，我爺爺每天早上仍然走五公里，他說這讓他保持年輕。"},{"w":"despite the fact that","p":"phr.","d":"although something is true","c":"儘管…（的事實）","s":"She passed the English exam with a high score despite the fact that she had been sick in bed for the whole week before it.","t":"儘管考前整整一週她都臥病在床，她仍以高分通過了英文考試。"},{"w":"depending on","p":"prep.","d":"decided by or changing according to something","c":"視…而定；取決於","s":"The bus trip to the mountains takes two or three hours, depending on the traffic and the weather on that day.","t":"到山上的巴士車程需要兩到三小時，視當天的交通和天氣而定。"},{"w":"in defense of","p":"prep.","d":"in order to protect or support someone or something","c":"為了保衛…；為…辯護","s":"The lawyer spoke for an hour in defense of her client, and she showed the court three videos that proved he was somewhere else.","t":"律師為她的當事人辯護了一個小時，並向法庭出示三段證明他當時在別處的影片。"},{"w":"to the delight of","p":"prep.","d":"in a way that makes someone very happy","c":"令…高興的是","s":"To the delight of the whole class, the teacher brought in a big birthday cake and let everyone eat it during the last period.","t":"令全班高興的是，老師帶來一個大生日蛋糕，讓大家在最後一節課吃。","a":"To the delight of"},{"w":"destruction","p":"n.","d":"the act of damaging something so badly that it no longer exists or cannot be used","c":"破壞；毀滅","s":"The typhoon caused terrible destruction along the east coast, and it will take months to rebuild the roads and bridges.","t":"颱風在東海岸造成了可怕的破壞，重建道路和橋樑需要好幾個月。","h":1},{"w":"destroy","p":"v.","d":"to damage something so badly that it no longer exists or cannot be used","c":"破壞；摧毀","s":"A single careless cigarette can destroy a whole forest, so never smoke when you go camping in the mountains.","t":"一根不小心的香菸就能摧毀整片森林，所以在山上露營時絕對不要抽菸。"},{"w":"destructive","p":"adj.","d":"causing a lot of damage","c":"破壞性的；毀滅性的","s":"The earthquake was the most destructive one in fifty years, and thousands of families had to sleep in school gyms for weeks.","t":"這場地震是五十年來破壞性最強的一次，數千個家庭必須在學校體育館睡好幾週。"}]},{"unit":12,"theme":"detective – disorder","cards":[{"w":"detective","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to find out who did a crime","c":"偵探","s":"The detective looked carefully at the footprints near the window, and soon he knew who had broken into the shop.","t":"偵探仔細察看窗邊的腳印，很快就知道是誰闖進了那家店。","h":1},{"w":"detective story","p":"n.phr.","d":"a story about solving a crime","c":"偵探小說","s":"My brother loves reading a good detective story before bed because he enjoys guessing who the criminal is before the ending.","t":"我哥哥喜歡睡前讀一本好的偵探小說，因為他喜歡在結局前猜出誰是罪犯。"},{"w":"detect","p":"v.","d":"to notice or find something that is hard to see","c":"察覺；偵測","s":"Smoke alarms can detect even a small fire in the kitchen, so every home should have at least one of them.","t":"煙霧警報器能偵測到廚房裡即使很小的火，所以每個家都應該至少有一個。"},{"w":"detection","p":"n.","d":"the act of finding or noticing something","c":"偵測；發現","s":"Early detection of health problems is important, which is why doctors suggest that adults get a check-up every year.","t":"及早發現健康問題很重要，這就是為什麼醫生建議成人每年做一次健康檢查。"},{"w":"detector","p":"n.","d":"a machine that finds something","c":"探測器","s":"At the airport, everyone must walk through a metal detector before they are allowed to go to the gate.","t":"在機場，每個人都必須走過金屬探測器，才被允許前往登機門。"},{"w":"determination","p":"n.","d":"the strong wish to keep trying until you succeed","c":"決心","s":"With great determination, the young runner finished the race even though her legs were hurting badly in the last two kilometers.","t":"這位年輕的跑者憑著極大的決心跑完比賽，即使在最後兩公里她的腿痛得很厲害。","h":1},{"w":"determine","p":"v.","d":"to decide something; to find out the facts","c":"決定；確定","s":"The doctor ran several tests to determine what was causing the pain in my grandfather's back.","t":"醫生做了幾項檢查來確定是什麼造成我爺爺背部的疼痛。"},{"w":"determined","p":"adj.","d":"having a strong wish to do something","c":"堅決的；下定決心的","s":"She is determined to pass the driving test this time, so she practices with her father every evening after dinner.","t":"她下定決心這次要通過駕照考試，所以每天晚飯後都和爸爸練習。"},{"w":"be determined to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have firmly decided to do something","c":"決心要…","s":"After failing twice, Kevin was determined to learn to swim before the summer ended, and he finally did it.","t":"失敗兩次後，凱文決心要在夏天結束前學會游泳，而他終於做到了。","a":"was determined to"},{"w":"device","p":"n.","d":"a machine or tool made for a special purpose","c":"裝置；設備","s":"Please turn off every electronic device, including your phone and tablet, before the plane takes off.","t":"飛機起飛前，請關掉每一個電子裝置，包括你的手機和平板。","h":1},{"w":"mobile device","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small computer you can carry, such as a phone","c":"行動裝置","s":"Students may use a mobile device in class only when the teacher asks them to look something up online.","t":"學生只有在老師要他們上網查資料時，才可以在課堂上使用行動裝置。"},{"w":"safety device","p":"n.phr.","d":"a tool that keeps people safe","c":"安全裝置","s":"A seat belt is a simple safety device that has saved millions of lives in car accidents around the world.","t":"安全帶是一種簡單的安全裝置，在全世界的車禍中拯救了數百萬人的生命。"},{"w":"devise","p":"v.","d":"to invent a plan or system by thinking carefully","c":"設計；想出","s":"The teacher asked us to devise a plan to raise money for the school trip without asking our parents.","t":"老師要我們想出一個不用向父母要錢就能為校外教學籌款的計畫。","h":1},{"w":"devise a way","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think of a method to do something","c":"想出辦法","s":"The farmers had to devise a way to keep the birds away from the fruit trees without hurting them.","t":"農夫們必須想出辦法讓鳥遠離果樹，又不傷害它們。"},{"w":"devise a strategy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a careful plan to win or succeed","c":"擬定策略","s":"Before the final game, the coach met with the players to devise a strategy that could beat the stronger team.","t":"決賽前，教練和球員開會擬定一套能擊敗較強隊伍的策略。"},{"w":"devote","p":"v.","d":"to give your time or energy to something","c":"奉獻；投入","s":"My aunt decided to devote her weekends to teaching English to children in a poor village near the mountains.","t":"我阿姨決定把她的週末投入在教山區附近貧困村莊的孩子英文。","h":1},{"w":"devote oneself to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spend all your time and effort on something","c":"致力於","s":"After he retired from the bank, Mr. Lin devoted himself to growing roses, and now his garden is famous in town.","t":"從銀行退休後，林先生致力於種植玫瑰，現在他的花園在鎮上很有名。","a":"devoted himself to"},{"w":"devoted","p":"adj.","d":"loving and loyal; caring a lot","c":"忠誠的；深愛的","s":"He is a devoted father who never misses his daughter's school events, even when he is very busy at work.","t":"他是一位深愛孩子的父親，即使工作很忙，也從不錯過女兒學校的活動。"},{"w":"devotion","p":"n.","d":"great love and loyalty; hard work for a cause","c":"奉獻；熱愛","s":"The nurse was given an award for her devotion to her patients during the thirty years she worked at the hospital.","t":"這位護士因為在醫院工作三十年期間對病人的奉獻而獲獎。"},{"w":"dew","p":"n.","d":"small drops of water that form on grass at night","c":"露水","s":"Early in the morning, the grass in the park was wet with dew, and my shoes got soaked as I walked across it.","t":"一大早，公園的草地被露水弄濕了，我走過時鞋子都濕透了。","h":1},{"w":"morning dew","p":"n.phr.","d":"dew that you see at the start of the day","c":"晨露","s":"The spider web shone like silver in the morning dew when the first light of the sun touched the garden.","t":"當第一道陽光照到花園時，蜘蛛網在晨露中閃著銀光。"},{"w":"dewdrop","p":"n.","d":"one small drop of dew","c":"露珠","s":"A single dewdrop hung from the tip of the leaf, and the child watched it until it finally fell to the ground.","t":"一顆露珠掛在葉尖上，孩子看著它直到它終於落到地上。"},{"w":"diagram","p":"n.","d":"a simple drawing that explains how something works","c":"圖表；圖解","s":"The science teacher drew a diagram on the board to show how water moves from the sea to the clouds and back.","t":"自然老師在黑板上畫了一張圖解，說明水如何從海洋到雲再回到海洋。","h":1},{"w":"diagram","p":"v.","d":"to draw a simple picture to explain something","c":"用圖表示","s":"Before building the model bridge, we had to diagram each part carefully so that everyone knew where the pieces went.","t":"建造模型橋之前，我們必須仔細把每個部分畫成圖，讓每個人都知道零件放哪裡。"},{"w":"draw a diagram","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a simple drawing to explain","c":"畫圖解","s":"If the instructions are hard to follow, draw a diagram of the steps, and the whole process will become much clearer.","t":"如果說明很難看懂，就把步驟畫成圖解，整個流程就會清楚很多。"},{"w":"differ","p":"v.","d":"to be not the same as something else","c":"不同；相異","s":"Food habits differ greatly from country to country, so travelers should try to respect the customs of the places they visit.","t":"飲食習慣因國家而大大不同，所以旅客應該盡量尊重所到之地的風俗。","h":1},{"w":"differ from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be unlike something","c":"與…不同","s":"My sister and I differ from each other in many ways, but we both love music and spend hours singing together.","t":"我和我姐姐在很多方面彼此不同，但我們都愛音樂，常花好幾小時一起唱歌。"},{"w":"different","p":"adj.","d":"not the same","c":"不同的","s":"The twins look exactly alike, but their personalities are completely different: one is quiet while the other talks all the time.","t":"這對雙胞胎長得一模一樣，但個性完全不同：一個安靜，另一個總是說話。"},{"w":"difference","p":"n.","d":"the way in which things are not the same","c":"差異；不同","s":"Can you tell the difference between butter and margarine just by tasting them, or do they taste the same to you?","t":"你光靠嘗味道就能分辨奶油和人造奶油的差異嗎，還是它們對你來說味道一樣？"},{"w":"make a difference","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have an important effect","c":"帶來改變；有影響","s":"Small actions like turning off lights and recycling paper can really make a difference to the environment over many years.","t":"像關燈和回收紙張這樣的小行動，多年下來真的能為環境帶來改變。"},{"w":"indifferent","p":"adj.","d":"not interested or not caring","c":"冷漠的；不在乎的","s":"The shop assistant seemed indifferent to our questions and kept looking at her phone, so we left without buying anything.","t":"店員對我們的問題似乎不在乎，一直看著她的手機，所以我們什麼都沒買就走了。"},{"w":"digest","p":"v.","d":"to change food in your stomach so the body can use it","c":"消化","s":"Soup and rice are easy to digest, so my mother always cooks them for me when I have a stomachache.","t":"湯和飯很容易消化，所以我肚子痛時媽媽總是煮這些給我吃。","h":1},{"w":"digest","p":"v.","d":"to think about new information until you understand it","c":"理解；吸收（資訊）","s":"The lecture had so many new ideas that the students needed a few days to digest everything they had heard.","t":"這場演講有太多新觀念，學生需要幾天才能消化他們聽到的一切。"},{"w":"digest","p":"n.","d":"a short version of a long text or news","c":"摘要；文摘","s":"Every Friday the company sends out a news digest so that busy workers can read the week's main events in five minutes.","t":"每週五公司會寄出一份新聞摘要，讓忙碌的員工五分鐘內就能讀完本週大事。"},{"w":"digestion","p":"n.","d":"the process of breaking down food in the body","c":"消化（作用）","s":"Eating slowly and chewing well helps your digestion, and it also stops you from eating more than your body needs.","t":"慢慢吃、好好咀嚼有助於消化，也能防止你吃得比身體需要的多。"},{"w":"digestive","p":"adj.","d":"connected with digesting food","c":"消化的","s":"Yogurt is good for your digestive system because it contains helpful bacteria that keep your stomach healthy.","t":"優格對你的消化系統有益，因為它含有能讓胃保持健康的有益細菌。"},{"w":"digital","p":"adj.","d":"using computer technology; showing numbers instead of hands","c":"數位的","s":"Most people now take digital photos with their phones instead of using film cameras like my parents did.","t":"現在大多數人用手機拍數位照片，而不是像我父母以前那樣用底片相機。","h":1},{"w":"digital camera","p":"n.phr.","d":"a camera that stores pictures as computer files","c":"數位相機","s":"For her birthday, Amy received a digital camera and spent the whole afternoon taking pictures of her cat.","t":"艾咪生日收到一台數位相機，整個下午都在拍她的貓。"},{"w":"digitally","p":"adv.","d":"by using computer technology","c":"以數位方式","s":"The old family photos were scanned and saved digitally, so now every relative can see them on their phones.","t":"這些老家庭照片被掃描並以數位方式儲存，現在每個親戚都能在手機上看到。"},{"w":"digit","p":"n.","d":"any one of the numbers from 0 to 9","c":"數字；位數","s":"A Taiwanese phone number has ten digits, so make sure you write down every single one before you call.","t":"台灣的電話號碼有十個數字，所以打電話前一定要把每一個都寫下來。","a":"digits"},{"w":"dignity","p":"n.","d":"calm and serious behavior that makes people respect you","c":"尊嚴；莊重","s":"Even after losing the election, the mayor spoke with dignity and thanked everyone who had voted for him.","t":"即使選舉落敗，市長仍帶著尊嚴發言，並感謝每一位投票給他的人。","h":1},{"w":"with dignity","p":"phr.","d":"in a calm and proud way","c":"有尊嚴地","s":"The old man accepted the bad news with dignity, without crying or shouting, which made everyone respect him even more.","t":"老先生有尊嚴地接受了壞消息，沒有哭也沒有大喊，這讓大家更加尊敬他。"},{"w":"dignified","p":"adj.","d":"calm and serious in a way that deserves respect","c":"莊重的；有尊嚴的","s":"The queen walked into the hall in a dignified manner, and the whole room became quiet at once.","t":"女王以莊重的姿態走進大廳，整個房間立刻安靜下來。"},{"w":"diligence","p":"n.","d":"careful and continued hard work","c":"勤勉；用功","s":"Thanks to her diligence, Mia finished the long research report two days early and still had time to check every page.","t":"多虧她的勤勉，米亞提早兩天完成了那份長篇研究報告，還有時間檢查每一頁。","h":1},{"w":"diligent","p":"adj.","d":"working hard and carefully","c":"勤奮的","s":"The diligent student reviews her notes every night, so she never has to stay up late before a big test.","t":"這位勤奮的學生每晚複習筆記，所以大考前從不需要熬夜。","h":1},{"w":"diligently","p":"adv.","d":"in a hard-working and careful way","c":"勤奮地","s":"The workers diligently cleaned up the beach for six hours, and by sunset there was not a single plastic bottle left.","t":"工人們勤奮地清理海灘六小時，到日落時已經連一個塑膠瓶都不剩了。"},{"w":"a diligent worker","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who works hard and carefully","c":"勤奮的工作者","s":"The manager said that Jason is a diligent worker who always finishes his tasks on time and helps others when he can.","t":"經理說傑森是一位勤奮的工作者，總是準時完成任務，並在能力範圍內幫助他人。"},{"w":"diploma","p":"n.","d":"an official paper showing you finished a course or school","c":"文憑；畢業證書","s":"After four years of hard work, my cousin finally received her college diploma and hung it proudly on the wall.","t":"經過四年努力，我表姐終於拿到大學文憑，並自豪地把它掛在牆上。","h":1},{"w":"high school diploma","p":"n.phr.","d":"the paper you get when you finish high school","c":"高中文憑","s":"Many jobs require at least a high school diploma, so dropping out of school can make finding work much harder later.","t":"許多工作至少需要高中文憑，所以輟學可能讓以後找工作更困難。"},{"w":"graduate with a diploma","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finish school and receive a certificate","c":"畢業取得文憑","s":"She hopes to graduate with a diploma in nursing next June and then work at the hospital in her hometown.","t":"她希望明年六月畢業取得護理文憑，然後在家鄉的醫院工作。"},{"w":"diplomat","p":"n.","d":"a person who represents their country in another country","c":"外交官","s":"As a diplomat, my uncle has lived in five different countries and can speak four languages fluently.","t":"身為一名外交官，我叔叔曾住過五個不同的國家，能流利地說四種語言。","h":1},{"w":"diplomatic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with relations between countries; good at dealing with people politely","c":"外交的；圓融的","s":"The two countries solved the problem through diplomatic talks instead of going to war, which saved thousands of lives.","t":"兩國透過外交會談而非戰爭解決了問題，拯救了數千人的生命。"},{"w":"diplomacy","p":"n.","d":"the work of managing relations between countries; skill in dealing with people","c":"外交；交際手腕","s":"Good diplomacy is needed when two neighbors argue about a fence, because shouting only makes the problem worse.","t":"當兩個鄰居為圍籬爭吵時，需要良好的交際手腕，因為大吼只會讓問題更糟。"},{"w":"disability","p":"n.","d":"a condition that makes it hard for someone to do some things","c":"身心障礙","s":"The new library has wide doors and low shelves so that people with a disability can use it easily.","t":"新圖書館有寬門和低書架，讓有身心障礙的人也能輕鬆使用。","h":1},{"w":"disabled","p":"adj.","d":"unable to use part of the body or mind fully","c":"身心障礙的","s":"Please leave the front seats on the bus for elderly and disabled passengers who may find it hard to stand.","t":"請把公車前排座位留給可能難以站立的年長者和身心障礙乘客。"},{"w":"learning disability","p":"n.phr.","d":"a problem that makes learning harder than usual","c":"學習障礙","s":"A student with a learning disability may need more time on tests, but that does not mean he is less intelligent.","t":"有學習障礙的學生可能在考試時需要更多時間，但那不代表他比較不聰明。"},{"w":"ability","p":"n.","d":"the power or skill to do something","c":"能力","s":"Dolphins have the amazing ability to find food in dark water by making sounds and listening for the echo.","t":"海豚有驚人的能力，能藉著發出聲音並聆聽回音，在黑暗的水中找到食物。"},{"w":"disadvantage","p":"n.","d":"something that makes a situation harder or less good","c":"劣勢；不利條件","s":"Living far from the MRT station is a disadvantage, but the rent is much cheaper, so we decided to move there anyway.","t":"住得離捷運站遠是個不利條件，但房租便宜很多，所以我們還是決定搬過去。","h":1},{"w":"at a disadvantage","p":"phr.","d":"in a weaker position than others","c":"處於不利地位","s":"Students without a computer at home are at a disadvantage when teachers give homework that must be done online.","t":"當老師出必須在線上完成的作業時，家裡沒電腦的學生就處於不利地位。"},{"w":"disadvantaged","p":"adj.","d":"having less money or fewer chances than most people","c":"弱勢的","s":"The charity gives free lunches and books to disadvantaged children so that they can keep up with their classmates.","t":"這個慈善機構提供免費午餐和書籍給弱勢兒童，讓他們能跟上同學。"},{"w":"advantage","p":"n.","d":"something that helps you do better than others","c":"優勢；好處","s":"Being tall is a big advantage in basketball, but short players can still win if they are fast and smart.","t":"身高在籃球中是很大的優勢，但矮的球員只要夠快、夠聰明還是能贏。"},{"w":"take advantage of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make good use of something","c":"利用；善用","s":"You should take advantage of the free swimming lessons at the community center before the summer program ends next week.","t":"你應該在下週夏季課程結束前，善用社區中心的免費游泳課。"},{"w":"disappoint","p":"v.","d":"to make someone sad because something is not as good as hoped","c":"使失望","s":"I did not want to disappoint my parents, so I studied hard and finally got into the school they hoped for.","t":"我不想讓父母失望，所以努力讀書，終於考上他們期望的學校。","h":1},{"w":"disappointment","p":"n.","d":"the sad feeling when something is not as good as hoped","c":"失望","s":"To our great disappointment, the concert was canceled an hour before it started because the singer was sick.","t":"令我們非常失望的是，演唱會在開始前一小時因為歌手生病而取消了。"},{"w":"disappointed","p":"adj.","d":"sad because something was not as good as hoped","c":"失望的（人）","s":"The kids were disappointed when it rained on Saturday, because they had planned to go to the beach all week.","t":"星期六下雨時孩子們很失望，因為他們整個星期都計畫要去海邊。"},{"w":"disappointing","p":"adj.","d":"not as good as hoped","c":"令人失望的","s":"The new restaurant was disappointing: the food was cold, the service was slow, and the prices were too high.","t":"這家新餐廳令人失望：食物是冷的，服務很慢，價格又太高。"},{"w":"be disappointed with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel let down by something","c":"對…感到失望","s":"The coach was disappointed with the team's performance in the first half, so he gave a serious talk at halftime.","t":"教練對球隊上半場的表現感到失望，所以在半場時認真訓話。","a":"was disappointed with"},{"w":"disaster","p":"n.","d":"a sudden event that causes great damage, like a flood or earthquake","c":"災難","s":"The 1999 earthquake was the worst natural disaster in Taiwan's recent history, and many buildings fell in just a few seconds.","t":"一九九九年的地震是台灣近代史上最嚴重的天然災難，許多建築在幾秒內倒塌。","h":1},{"w":"natural disaster","p":"n.phr.","d":"a disaster caused by nature, such as a typhoon","c":"天災","s":"Taiwan faces more than one natural disaster every year, so schools teach children what to do when the ground starts shaking.","t":"台灣每年面臨不只一次天災，所以學校會教孩子地面開始搖晃時該怎麼做。"},{"w":"disastrous","p":"adj.","d":"causing great damage; very bad","c":"災難性的；慘重的","s":"Forgetting to save the file was disastrous, because Tom lost the whole report he had been writing for three days.","t":"忘了存檔是災難性的，因為湯姆失去了他寫了三天的整份報告。"},{"w":"end in disaster","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finish very badly","c":"以災難收場","s":"The picnic ended in disaster when a sudden storm blew away our tent and soaked all the food we had brought.","t":"野餐以災難收場：一場突來的暴風吹走了帳篷，還淋濕了我們帶的所有食物。","a":"ended in disaster"},{"w":"discipline","p":"n.","d":"training that teaches people to follow rules; self-control","c":"紀律；自律","s":"Learning the piano takes a lot of discipline, because you have to practice every day even when you do not feel like it.","t":"學鋼琴需要很多自律，因為即使不想練，你也必須每天練習。","h":1},{"w":"discipline","p":"v.","d":"to punish someone to teach them to follow rules","c":"懲戒；管教","s":"The school decided to discipline the students who cheated by making them clean the classrooms for a month.","t":"學校決定懲戒作弊的學生，要他們打掃教室一個月。"},{"w":"self-discipline","p":"n.","d":"the ability to make yourself do what you should","c":"自我約束；自律","s":"Studying at home during the holidays requires strong self-discipline, since nobody is there to tell you to put down your phone.","t":"假期在家讀書需要很強的自律，因為沒有人在旁邊叫你放下手機。"},{"w":"disciplined","p":"adj.","d":"able to control your behavior and follow rules","c":"有紀律的","s":"The disciplined soldiers stood perfectly still in the hot sun for an hour without moving or making a sound.","t":"這些有紀律的士兵在烈日下站得筆直一小時，不動也不出聲。"},{"w":"discourage","p":"v.","d":"to make someone lose hope or confidence","c":"使沮喪；打消念頭","s":"Don't let one bad grade discourage you; even the best students fail a test sometimes and then do better next time.","t":"不要讓一次差成績讓你沮喪；就算最好的學生有時也會考砸，然後下次考得更好。","h":1},{"w":"discourage sb from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to stop someone from doing something","c":"勸阻某人做…","s":"The doctor tried to discourage my father from smoking by showing him pictures of damaged lungs.","t":"醫生試圖勸阻我爸爸抽菸，給他看受損肺部的照片。","a":"discourage my father from"},{"w":"discouragement","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of losing hope","c":"沮喪；氣餒","s":"After three failed job interviews, he felt a deep sense of discouragement, but his friends kept telling him not to give up.","t":"三次面試失敗後，他感到深深的氣餒，但朋友們一直告訴他不要放棄。"},{"w":"discouraged","p":"adj.","d":"having lost hope or confidence","c":"氣餒的","s":"Many beginners feel discouraged when they cannot understand English movies, but listening gets easier with daily practice.","t":"許多初學者聽不懂英文電影時會感到氣餒，但每天練習，聽力就會越來越容易。"},{"w":"encourage","p":"v.","d":"to give someone hope or confidence","c":"鼓勵","s":"My teacher always tries to encourage shy students to speak up in class by praising every small effort they make.","t":"我的老師總是藉著稱讚每一個小小的努力，鼓勵害羞的學生在課堂上發言。"},{"w":"disguise","p":"v.","d":"to change how you look so people will not know you","c":"偽裝；假扮","s":"The famous actor tried to disguise himself with a cap and sunglasses, but a fan still recognized him at the market.","t":"那位名演員試圖用帽子和太陽眼鏡偽裝自己，但一位粉絲還是在市場認出了他。","h":1},{"w":"disguise","p":"n.","d":"clothes or make-up that hide who you are","c":"偽裝；掩飾","s":"The police officer wore a disguise and pretended to be a street seller so that he could watch the thieves.","t":"那位警察穿著偽裝，假裝是街頭小販，好監視那些小偷。"},{"w":"in disguise","p":"phr.","d":"wearing a disguise; appearing to be something else","c":"偽裝的；喬裝的","s":"In the fairy tale, the old woman at the door was really a prince in disguise, testing how kind the family was.","t":"在童話裡，門口的老婦人其實是喬裝的王子，正在考驗這家人有多善良。"},{"w":"a blessing in disguise","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that seems bad but turns out good","c":"禍中有福；塞翁失馬","s":"Losing that job was a blessing in disguise, because it pushed me to start my own small business, which I now love.","t":"失去那份工作其實是塞翁失馬，因為它推動我開了自己的小生意，而我現在很喜歡這份事業。"},{"w":"disgust","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of dislike for something very unpleasant","c":"厭惡；反感","s":"She looked at the dirty kitchen with disgust and refused to eat anything cooked in that restaurant.","t":"她厭惡地看著骯髒的廚房，拒絕吃那家餐廳做的任何東西。","h":1},{"w":"disgust","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel strong dislike","c":"使厭惡","s":"The smell of rotten fish from the trash can was enough to disgust everyone who walked past the alley.","t":"垃圾桶傳來的臭魚味足以讓每個經過巷子的人感到厭惡。"},{"w":"disgusting","p":"adj.","d":"extremely unpleasant","c":"令人作噁的；噁心的","s":"The milk had been left out for three days, and it smelled so disgusting that I almost threw up.","t":"牛奶放在外面三天了，聞起來噁心得讓我差點吐出來。"},{"w":"disgusted","p":"adj.","d":"feeling strong dislike","c":"感到厭惡的","s":"The tourists were disgusted to see people throwing plastic bags into the beautiful river right next to the sign that said 'No Littering.'","t":"遊客看到有人就在「禁止亂丟垃圾」的告示牌旁把塑膠袋丟進美麗的河裡，感到很厭惡。"},{"w":"be disgusted by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel sick or angry about something","c":"對…感到厭惡","s":"Many viewers were disgusted by the violent scenes in the movie and left the theater before it ended.","t":"許多觀眾對電影中的暴力場面感到厭惡，在結束前就離開了電影院。","a":"were disgusted by"},{"w":"dismiss","p":"v.","d":"to make someone leave their job","c":"解僱；開除","s":"The company had to dismiss twenty workers last month because it was losing money and could not pay everyone.","t":"公司上個月不得不解僱二十名員工，因為它在虧錢，付不起所有人的薪水。","h":1},{"w":"dismiss","p":"v.","d":"to tell people they can leave; to refuse to consider an idea","c":"讓…離開（下課）；駁回","s":"The teacher will dismiss the class early today because there is a teachers' meeting at three o'clock in the afternoon.","t":"老師今天會提早讓全班下課，因為下午三點有教師會議。"},{"w":"dismiss an idea","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide an idea is not worth considering","c":"否決／不理會一個想法","s":"Don't dismiss an idea just because it sounds strange at first; many great inventions seemed silly in the beginning.","t":"不要只因為一個想法一開始聽起來很奇怪就否決它；許多偉大的發明起初都看起來很傻。"},{"w":"dismissal","p":"n.","d":"the act of removing someone from a job","c":"解僱；開除","s":"His dismissal from the bank shocked his colleagues, because he had worked there for more than fifteen years.","t":"他被銀行解僱讓同事們很震驚，因為他已經在那裡工作了超過十五年。"},{"w":"disorder","p":"n.","d":"a state of confusion with no order","c":"混亂；凌亂","s":"After the party, the living room was in complete disorder, with cups on the floor and chairs turned over everywhere.","t":"派對結束後，客廳一片混亂，杯子掉在地上，椅子到處翻倒。","h":1},{"w":"disorder","p":"n.","d":"an illness that stops part of the body or mind from working normally","c":"失調；疾病","s":"Looking at a bright phone screen late at night can cause a sleep disorder that makes you tired all day.","t":"深夜看明亮的手機螢幕可能造成睡眠失調，讓你整天都很累。"},{"w":"in disorder","p":"phr.","d":"in a messy or confused state","c":"處於混亂中；亂成一團","s":"The papers on his desk were in disorder, so it took him twenty minutes to find the letter he needed.","t":"他桌上的文件亂成一團，所以他花了二十分鐘才找到需要的那封信。"},{"w":"order","p":"n.","d":"the state when everything is neat and in its right place","c":"秩序；整齊","s":"The librarian put the returned books back in order on the shelves so that students could find them easily.","t":"圖書館員把歸還的書依序放回書架，讓學生能輕易找到。"},{"w":"disorderly","p":"adj.","d":"untidy; behaving in a noisy and uncontrolled way","c":"雜亂的；不守秩序的","s":"The police asked the disorderly crowd outside the stadium to calm down and go home after the game ended.","t":"比賽結束後，警察要求體育場外不守秩序的人群冷靜下來回家。"}]},{"unit":13,"theme":"dispute – dynasty","cards":[{"w":"dispute","p":"n.","d":"a serious argument or disagreement","c":"爭論；糾紛","s":"The two neighbors have had a long dispute over the wall between their houses, and now they do not even say hello.","t":"這兩位鄰居為了他們房子之間的牆有了長期的糾紛，現在連招呼都不打了。","h":1},{"w":"dispute","p":"v.","d":"to say that something is not true or correct","c":"爭論；質疑","s":"Nobody can dispute the fact that she is the best singer in the school, since she has won the contest three years in a row.","t":"沒人能質疑她是全校最棒歌手的事實，因為她已經連續三年贏得比賽。"},{"w":"in dispute","p":"phr.","d":"being argued about; not agreed","c":"有爭議的","s":"The border between the two countries is still in dispute, so soldiers from both sides stand guard there day and night.","t":"兩國之間的邊界仍然有爭議，所以雙方的士兵日夜在那裡站崗。"},{"w":"settle a dispute","p":"v.phr.","d":"to end an argument","c":"解決糾紛","s":"The manager called both workers into her office to settle a dispute about who should take the holiday shift.","t":"經理把兩名員工叫進辦公室，解決誰該值假日班的糾紛。"},{"w":"disputed","p":"adj.","d":"argued about; not agreed by everyone","c":"有爭議的","s":"The referee's disputed call at the end of the game made the home fans so angry that they shouted for ten minutes.","t":"裁判在比賽尾聲有爭議的判決讓主場球迷非常生氣，他們大喊了十分鐘。"},{"w":"distinct","p":"adj.","d":"clearly different; easy to see or hear","c":"不同的；清楚的","s":"Each of the three sisters has a distinct voice, so I can always tell who is calling before she says her name.","t":"三姊妹每個人都有明顯不同的聲音，所以她們還沒說名字我就知道是誰打來的。","h":1},{"w":"distinguish","p":"v.","d":"to see or understand the difference between things","c":"分辨；區別","s":"It is hard to distinguish the twins at first, but after a week you will notice that Ben smiles more than Sam.","t":"一開始很難分辨這對雙胞胎，但一週後你會注意到班比山姆更常微笑。","h":1},{"w":"distinguished","p":"adj.","d":"famous and respected for doing something well","c":"傑出的；卓越的","s":"A distinguished scientist from Japan will visit our school next month to talk about her research on clean energy.","t":"一位來自日本的傑出科學家下個月將來我們學校演講她的潔淨能源研究。","h":1},{"w":"distinguish right from wrong","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell what is good from what is bad","c":"分辨是非","s":"Young children sometimes cannot distinguish right from wrong, so parents need to explain things patiently and clearly.","t":"幼童有時無法分辨是非，所以父母需要有耐心且清楚地解釋事情。"},{"w":"distinctly","p":"adv.","d":"clearly","c":"清楚地；明顯地","s":"I distinctly remember locking the door this morning, so I do not understand how the cat got outside.","t":"我清楚地記得今天早上鎖了門，所以不明白貓是怎麼跑到外面的。"},{"w":"distinction","p":"n.","d":"a clear difference between things","c":"區別；差別","s":"There is an important distinction between being alone and being lonely, and many people enjoy quiet time by themselves.","t":"「獨處」和「孤單」之間有重要的區別，許多人很享受自己一個人的安靜時光。"},{"w":"distribute","p":"v.","d":"to give things out to a number of people","c":"分發；分配","s":"The volunteers will distribute free water and bread to the families who lost their homes in the flood last night.","t":"志工們將分發免費的水和麵包給昨晚在水災中失去家園的家庭。","h":1},{"w":"distribution","p":"n.","d":"the act of giving things out; the way things are spread","c":"分發；分布","s":"The distribution of the new textbooks will begin on Monday, so every class should send two students to the office.","t":"新課本的發放將在星期一開始，所以每個班級應該派兩名學生到辦公室。","h":1},{"w":"distributor","p":"n.","d":"a company or person that supplies goods to shops","c":"經銷商；配送商","s":"The small bakery found a distributor who now delivers its cookies to more than fifty convenience stores across the city.","t":"這家小麵包店找到了一位經銷商，現在把它的餅乾送到全市五十多家便利商店。"},{"w":"evenly distributed","p":"adj.phr.","d":"spread out in equal amounts","c":"平均分布的","s":"The chairs should be evenly distributed around the room so that every student can see the screen without turning their head.","t":"椅子應該平均分布在教室各處，讓每個學生不用轉頭就能看到螢幕。"},{"w":"district","p":"n.","d":"an area of a city or country","c":"區；地區","s":"Our school is in the Daan district of Taipei, which is famous for its large park and many good restaurants.","t":"我們學校位於台北的大安區，那裡以大公園和許多好餐廳聞名。","h":1},{"w":"business district","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of a city where offices and shops are","c":"商業區","s":"Rents in the business district are very high, so many young workers live far away and take the MRT every morning.","t":"商業區的租金非常高，所以許多年輕上班族住得很遠，每天早上搭捷運。"},{"w":"school district","p":"n.phr.","d":"an area whose children go to the same schools","c":"學區","s":"Many parents buy a house in a good school district because they want their children to attend the best public schools.","t":"許多父母在好的學區買房子，因為他們希望孩子能上最好的公立學校。"},{"w":"residential district","p":"n.phr.","d":"an area where people live rather than work","c":"住宅區","s":"The streets in this quiet residential district are full of trees, and children play outside until the sun goes down.","t":"這個安靜住宅區的街道滿是樹木，孩子們在外面玩到太陽下山。"},{"w":"disturb","p":"v.","d":"to interrupt someone or stop them from being calm","c":"打擾；干擾","s":"Please do not disturb your father while he is on the phone with his boss; you can ask him later.","t":"爸爸和老闆講電話時請不要打擾他；你可以等一下再問。","h":1},{"w":"Do not disturb","p":"phr.","d":"a sign asking people not to knock or enter","c":"請勿打擾","s":"The hotel guest hung a \"Do not disturb\" sign on the door because she wanted to sleep late after her long flight.","t":"這位飯店客人在門上掛了「請勿打擾」的牌子，因為長途飛行後她想睡晚一點。"},{"w":"disturbing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel worried or upset","c":"令人不安的","s":"The news about the fire at the factory was disturbing, because several of our neighbors work there every day.","t":"工廠失火的消息令人不安，因為我們有好幾位鄰居每天在那裡工作。"},{"w":"disturbance","p":"n.","d":"something that interrupts or upsets people; noisy trouble","c":"干擾；騷動","s":"The loud party next door caused such a disturbance that someone finally called the police at two in the morning.","t":"隔壁吵鬧的派對造成了很大的騷動，終於有人在凌晨兩點報警。"},{"w":"disturbed","p":"adj.","d":"worried or upset","c":"感到不安的","s":"She was deeply disturbed by the strange phone calls she kept receiving late at night from an unknown number.","t":"她對深夜不斷接到來自不明號碼的奇怪電話感到非常不安。"},{"w":"diverse","p":"adj.","d":"including many different kinds","c":"多樣的；各式各樣的","s":"Taipei has a diverse food scene, where you can find Japanese, Thai, Italian, and Indian restaurants on the same street.","t":"台北有多元的飲食景觀，在同一條街上你可以找到日式、泰式、義式和印度餐廳。","h":1},{"w":"diversity","p":"n.","d":"the fact of including many different kinds","c":"多樣性；多元","s":"Our class has students from six countries, and the teacher says this diversity helps us learn about the world.","t":"我們班有來自六個國家的學生，老師說這種多元性幫助我們認識世界。","h":1},{"w":"cultural diversity","p":"n.phr.","d":"the mix of different cultures in a place","c":"文化多樣性","s":"Singapore is proud of its cultural diversity, and its public holidays include festivals from several different religions.","t":"新加坡以其文化多樣性為傲，它的國定假日包括好幾個不同宗教的節日。"},{"w":"diversify","p":"v.","d":"to start to include more different kinds","c":"使多樣化","s":"The farmer decided to diversify his crops, so now he grows vegetables and fruit instead of only rice.","t":"這位農夫決定讓作物多樣化，所以現在他種蔬菜和水果，而不只是種稻米。"},{"w":"divine","p":"adj.","d":"connected with God or a god","c":"神的；神聖的","s":"The ancient Greeks believed that thunder was a divine sign, so they prayed whenever a storm came.","t":"古希臘人相信雷聲是神的徵兆，所以每當暴風雨來臨他們就祈禱。","h":1},{"w":"divine","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good or beautiful (informal)","c":"極美的；絕妙的","s":"The chocolate cake at that café is simply divine; you must try a piece before you leave Tainan.","t":"那家咖啡館的巧克力蛋糕真是絕妙；你離開台南前一定要嚐一塊。"},{"w":"divinity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a god; the study of religion","c":"神性；神學","s":"In many old stories, kings claimed divinity so that the people would obey them without asking questions.","t":"在許多古老的故事裡，國王宣稱擁有神性，好讓人民毫不質疑地服從他們。"},{"w":"divine power","p":"n.phr.","d":"power that comes from a god","c":"神力","s":"The temple visitors asked the god for divine power to protect their families from sickness during the coming year.","t":"廟裡的信眾祈求神明賜予神力，保護他們的家人在來年免於疾病。"},{"w":"divorce","p":"n.","d":"the legal ending of a marriage","c":"離婚","s":"After the divorce, the children lived with their mother during the week and visited their father on weekends.","t":"離婚後，孩子們平日和媽媽住，週末去看爸爸。","h":1},{"w":"divorce","p":"v.","d":"to legally end a marriage","c":"與…離婚","s":"The famous couple decided to divorce after ten years of marriage, and the news was on every website that evening.","t":"這對名人夫妻在結婚十年後決定離婚，當晚每個網站都有這則新聞。"},{"w":"get a divorce","p":"v.phr.","d":"to end your marriage legally","c":"辦理離婚","s":"My aunt and uncle argued all the time, so nobody was surprised when they finally decided to get a divorce.","t":"我阿姨和姨丈總是吵架，所以當他們終於決定離婚時，沒有人感到驚訝。"},{"w":"divorced","p":"adj.","d":"no longer married","c":"離了婚的","s":"Her parents are divorced, but they still have dinner together on her birthday every year because they both love her.","t":"她的父母離婚了，但每年她生日時他們仍會一起吃晚餐，因為兩人都愛她。"},{"w":"dodge","p":"v.","d":"to move quickly to avoid being hit","c":"閃躲；閃避","s":"The boy managed to dodge the ball at the last second, so it hit the wall behind him instead of his face.","t":"那男孩在最後一秒成功閃過球，所以球打到他身後的牆，而不是他的臉。","h":1},{"w":"dodge","p":"v.","d":"to avoid doing or answering something","c":"迴避；逃避","s":"The politician tried to dodge the reporter's question about taxes by talking about the weather instead.","t":"那位政治人物藉著談天氣來迴避記者關於稅的問題。"},{"w":"dodge","p":"n.","d":"a trick to avoid something","c":"伎倆；躲避","s":"Saying he had a stomachache was just a dodge to get out of the math test, and the teacher knew it.","t":"說自己肚子痛只是為了逃避數學考試的伎倆，而老師心知肚明。"},{"w":"dodgeball","p":"n.","d":"a game in which players throw a ball at each other","c":"躲避球","s":"In PE class today we played dodgeball, and our team won because nobody could hit our fastest runner.","t":"今天體育課我們玩躲避球，我們隊贏了，因為沒人打得到我們跑最快的隊員。"},{"w":"dominant","p":"adj.","d":"more powerful or important than others","c":"主導的；佔優勢的","s":"English is the dominant language of the internet, although Chinese websites are growing very quickly these days.","t":"英語是網路上主導的語言，雖然中文網站近來成長得非常快。","h":1},{"w":"dominate","p":"v.","d":"to control or be the most important thing in something","c":"支配；主宰","s":"One strong team has continued to dominate the league for five years, winning the championship every single season.","t":"一支強隊連續五年稱霸聯盟，每一季都贏得冠軍。","h":1},{"w":"domination","p":"n.","d":"control or power over others","c":"支配；統治","s":"The small island was under the domination of a foreign empire for almost a hundred years before it became free.","t":"這座小島在獲得自由之前，曾被一個外國帝國統治了將近一百年。"},{"w":"dominant position","p":"n.phr.","d":"the strongest place in a market or contest","c":"主導地位","s":"The company holds a dominant position in the phone market, selling more than half of all the phones in the country.","t":"這家公司在手機市場擁有主導地位，賣出全國一半以上的手機。"},{"w":"predominantly","p":"adv.","d":"mostly; mainly","c":"主要地；大多","s":"The island's population is predominantly made up of fishermen and their families, who have lived there for generations.","t":"島上的人口主要由漁民和他們的家人組成，他們已在那裡住了好幾代。"},{"w":"draft","p":"n.","d":"an early version of a piece of writing","c":"草稿","s":"The teacher asked us to hand in the first draft of our essay on Friday so that she can give us comments before the final copy.","t":"老師要我們星期五交作文的初稿，這樣她才能在定稿前給我們意見。","h":1},{"w":"draft","p":"v.","d":"to write the first version of something","c":"起草；草擬","s":"The lawyer will draft the contract this week, and both companies will check every detail before they sign it.","t":"律師這週會草擬合約，兩家公司在簽字前會檢查每一個細節。"},{"w":"draft","p":"n.","d":"a current of cold air coming into a room","c":"冷風；氣流","s":"I feel a cold draft coming from under the door, so let's put a towel there until we can fix it.","t":"我感覺有一股冷風從門底下吹進來，在修好之前我們先放條毛巾在那裡吧。"},{"w":"rough draft","p":"n.phr.","d":"a first, unfinished version","c":"初稿；草稿","s":"Don't worry about spelling in your rough draft; just get all your ideas down on paper first and fix the details later.","t":"別擔心初稿的拼字；先把所有想法寫在紙上，細節以後再修。"},{"w":"final draft","p":"n.phr.","d":"the finished version of a piece of writing","c":"定稿","s":"After three weeks of changes, she finally printed the final draft of her story and sent it to the magazine.","t":"經過三週的修改，她終於印出故事的定稿並寄給雜誌社。"},{"w":"dread","p":"v.","d":"to feel very afraid or worried about something that will happen","c":"害怕；畏懼","s":"I dread going to the dentist so much that I always feel sick on the morning of my appointment.","t":"我非常害怕看牙醫，以至於每次預約當天早上都覺得不舒服。","h":1},{"w":"dread","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of fear about the future","c":"恐懼；畏懼","s":"A feeling of dread came over the students when the teacher walked in carrying a thick pile of test papers.","t":"當老師拿著一疊厚厚的考卷走進來時，一股恐懼感籠罩了學生。"},{"w":"dreadful","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or unpleasant","c":"糟糕的；可怕的","s":"The weather was dreadful during our trip: it rained for five days, and we never saw the mountains at all.","t":"我們旅行期間天氣糟透了：下了五天雨，我們完全沒看到山。"},{"w":"dreadfully","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; very badly","c":"非常；極度","s":"I am dreadfully sorry for breaking your vase; please let me pay for a new one as soon as possible.","t":"我非常抱歉打破了你的花瓶；請讓我儘快賠你一個新的。"},{"w":"drift","p":"v.","d":"to be carried slowly by water or air","c":"漂流；飄動","s":"The small boat began to drift away from the beach because the boy had forgotten to tie it to the post.","t":"小船開始從海灘漂走，因為男孩忘了把它綁在柱子上。","h":1},{"w":"drift","p":"v.","d":"to move or change slowly without a plan","c":"漫無目的地移動；游移","s":"During the long lecture, my thoughts started to drift toward what I would eat for dinner that night.","t":"漫長的講課中，我的思緒開始飄向那天晚上要吃什麼。"},{"w":"drift","p":"n.","d":"a pile of snow or sand made by the wind","c":"吹積物；雪堆","s":"After the storm, a deep snow drift blocked the front door, and we had to climb out through the window.","t":"暴風雪過後，一道深深的雪堆擋住了前門，我們只好從窗戶爬出去。"},{"w":"drift apart","p":"v.phr.","d":"to slowly stop being close friends","c":"漸漸疏遠","s":"Lisa and I were best friends in elementary school, but we began to drift apart after she moved to another city.","t":"麗莎和我在小學是最好的朋友，但她搬到另一個城市後我們開始漸漸疏遠。"},{"w":"drift off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fall asleep slowly","c":"慢慢睡著","s":"The baby finally began to drift off after her mother sang the same soft song for the fifth time.","t":"媽媽第五次唱同一首輕柔的歌後，寶寶終於開始慢慢睡著。"},{"w":"drill","p":"n.","d":"a tool for making holes","c":"鑽子；鑽頭","s":"My father used an electric drill to make four holes in the wall so that he could hang the new shelf.","t":"我爸爸用電鑽在牆上鑽了四個洞，好把新架子掛上去。","h":1},{"w":"drill","p":"n.","d":"an exercise that is repeated to practice something","c":"反覆練習；演習","s":"We have a fire drill at school every semester so that everyone knows the fastest way out of the building.","t":"我們學校每學期都有消防演習，讓每個人都知道離開大樓最快的路。"},{"w":"drill","p":"v.","d":"to make a hole with a drill","c":"鑽孔","s":"Be careful when you drill into that wall, because there may be electric wires hidden behind it.","t":"在那面牆上鑽孔時要小心，因為後面可能藏有電線。"},{"w":"drill","p":"v.","d":"to teach by making someone repeat something many times","c":"反覆訓練","s":"The coach will drill the players on passing every afternoon until they can do it without thinking.","t":"教練每天下午會反覆訓練球員傳球，直到他們不用思考就能做到。"},{"w":"fire drill","p":"n.phr.","d":"practice for leaving a building safely during a fire","c":"消防演習","s":"During the fire drill, all students must walk quickly to the playground and wait for their teacher to count them.","t":"消防演習期間，所有學生必須快步走到操場，等老師點名。"},{"w":"drowsy","p":"adj.","d":"tired and almost asleep","c":"昏昏欲睡的","s":"The warm classroom and the teacher's slow voice made everyone drowsy right after lunch on that hot afternoon.","t":"在那個炎熱的下午，溫暖的教室和老師緩慢的聲音讓大家午餐後都昏昏欲睡。","h":1},{"w":"feel drowsy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel sleepy","c":"覺得想睡","s":"Some cold medicines make you feel drowsy, so you should not drive or ride a scooter after taking them.","t":"有些感冒藥會讓你覺得想睡，所以服用後不應該開車或騎機車。"},{"w":"drowsiness","p":"n.","d":"the state of being sleepy","c":"睡意；昏沉","s":"The label on the bottle warns that the medicine may cause drowsiness, so take it only before going to bed.","t":"瓶子上的標籤警告這種藥可能引起睡意，所以只能在睡前服用。"},{"w":"drowse","p":"v.","d":"to sleep lightly for a short time","c":"打瞌睡","s":"Grandpa likes to drowse in his armchair after lunch with the newspaper still open on his lap.","t":"爺爺喜歡午餐後在扶手椅上打瞌睡，報紙還攤開在腿上。"},{"w":"durable","p":"adj.","d":"staying strong and in good condition for a long time","c":"耐用的；持久的","s":"These hiking boots are expensive, but they are so durable that my father has worn his pair for twelve years.","t":"這些登山鞋很貴，但它們非常耐用，我爸爸那雙已經穿了十二年。","h":1},{"w":"durability","p":"n.","d":"the quality of lasting a long time","c":"耐用性；耐久性","s":"Customers choose this brand of phone case because of its durability; it can survive a fall from a second-floor window.","t":"顧客選擇這個牌子的手機殼是因為它的耐用性；它從二樓窗戶掉下來都不會壞。"},{"w":"duration","p":"n.","d":"the length of time that something lasts","c":"持續時間","s":"The duration of the flight to Tokyo is about three hours, so you will have time to watch one movie.","t":"飛往東京的航程時間大約三小時，所以你有時間看一部電影。"},{"w":"endure","p":"v.","d":"to suffer something difficult for a long time","c":"忍受；持續","s":"The hikers had to endure strong winds and freezing rain for six hours before they reached the mountain hut.","t":"登山客必須忍受強風和冰冷的雨六個小時，才抵達山屋。"},{"w":"dusty","p":"adj.","d":"covered with dust","c":"滿是灰塵的","s":"The old books in the attic were so dusty that I started sneezing as soon as I opened the first one.","t":"閣樓裡的舊書滿是灰塵，我一打開第一本就開始打噴嚏。","h":1},{"w":"dust","p":"n.","d":"very small pieces of dry dirt","c":"灰塵","s":"There was a thick layer of dust on the piano because nobody had played it since my grandmother died.","t":"鋼琴上有一層厚厚的灰塵，因為自從我奶奶過世後就沒有人彈過它。"},{"w":"dust","p":"v.","d":"to clean the dust off something","c":"擦去灰塵","s":"Every Saturday morning I dust the shelves and the TV while my brother cleans the floor.","t":"每個星期六早上我擦拭書架和電視的灰塵，我弟弟則負責拖地。"},{"w":"dusty road","p":"n.phr.","d":"a dry road with a lot of dust","c":"塵土飛揚的路","s":"The truck drove down the long dusty road, leaving a brown cloud behind it that took minutes to settle.","t":"卡車沿著漫長塵土飛揚的路駛去，留下一團要好幾分鐘才落定的褐色塵雲。"},{"w":"dye","p":"v.","d":"to change the color of hair or cloth with a special liquid","c":"染色；染","s":"My sister wants to dye her hair purple for the summer, but our mother says she has to wait until after graduation.","t":"我姐姐想在夏天把頭髮染成紫色，但媽媽說她得等到畢業之後。","h":1},{"w":"dye","p":"n.","d":"a substance used to change the color of something","c":"染料","s":"In the old days, people made blue dye from plants and used it to color their cotton clothes.","t":"古時候，人們用植物製作藍色染料，用來為棉衣上色。"},{"w":"hair dye","p":"n.phr.","d":"a product used to change hair color","c":"染髮劑","s":"The hair dye she bought at the drugstore turned her hair orange instead of brown, so she had to visit a salon.","t":"她在藥妝店買的染髮劑把頭髮染成橘色而不是棕色，所以她只好去美髮沙龍。"},{"w":"dyed","p":"adj.","d":"colored with dye","c":"染過的","s":"You can tell her hair is dyed because the roots are black while the rest is bright red.","t":"你看得出她的頭髮是染過的，因為髮根是黑色，其餘是鮮紅色。"},{"w":"dynamic","p":"adj.","d":"full of energy and new ideas; always changing","c":"充滿活力的；動態的","s":"Our new principal is a dynamic leader who has already started three clubs and a school garden in her first month.","t":"我們的新校長是位充滿活力的領導者，上任第一個月就已經成立了三個社團和一座校園菜園。","h":1},{"w":"dynamics","p":"n.","d":"the way people or things act together and change","c":"動態；互動關係","s":"The dynamics of the team changed completely after the new captain joined and started listening to every player.","t":"新隊長加入並開始聆聽每位球員後，球隊的互動關係完全改變了。"},{"w":"dynamically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that keeps changing or is full of energy","c":"動態地；充滿活力地","s":"The weather map updates dynamically, so you can watch the typhoon move closer to Taiwan hour by hour.","t":"氣象圖會動態更新，所以你可以一小時一小時地看著颱風逐漸接近台灣。"},{"w":"a dynamic personality","p":"n.phr.","d":"an energetic and exciting character","c":"充滿活力的個性","s":"Jack has a dynamic personality that makes people want to follow him, so he was elected class leader three times.","t":"傑克有充滿活力的個性，讓大家都想跟隨他，所以他三度當選班長。"},{"w":"dynasty","p":"n.","d":"a series of rulers from the same family","c":"王朝；朝代","s":"The Tang dynasty was a golden age for Chinese poetry, and students in Taiwan still memorize poems from that time.","t":"唐朝是中國詩歌的黃金時代，台灣的學生至今仍背誦那個時代的詩。","h":1},{"w":"the Qing Dynasty","p":"n.phr.","d":"the last ruling family of imperial China","c":"清朝","s":"Many old temples in Tainan were built during the Qing Dynasty, and some of them are more than two hundred years old.","t":"台南許多古廟建於清朝，其中有些已超過兩百年歷史。"},{"w":"found a dynasty","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start a line of rulers","c":"建立王朝","s":"The general won the war and then decided to found a dynasty that would rule the land for the next three hundred years.","t":"將軍打贏了戰爭，然後決定建立一個王朝，統治這片土地接下來三百年。"},{"w":"dynastic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a dynasty","c":"王朝的","s":"The museum's new show explains the dynastic history of China through coins, paintings, and clothes from each period.","t":"博物館的新展覽透過各時期的錢幣、畫作和服飾，說明中國的王朝歷史。"}]},{"unit":14,"theme":"earnest – engineering","cards":[{"w":"earnest","p":"adj.","d":"very serious and sincere","c":"認真的；誠摯的","s":"The young teacher made an earnest effort to learn every student's name during the first week, and the class really appreciated it.","t":"這位年輕老師在第一週認真努力記住每個學生的名字，全班都非常感激。","h":1},{"w":"in earnest","p":"phr.","d":"seriously; in a real and determined way","c":"認真地；正式地","s":"After the holiday, the students began to study in earnest because the big exam was only three weeks away.","t":"假期過後，學生們開始認真地讀書，因為大考只剩三週了。"},{"w":"earnestly","p":"adv.","d":"in a serious and sincere way","c":"認真地；誠摯地","s":"She earnestly asked her parents to let her join the school trip, promising that she would finish all her homework first.","t":"她誠摯地請求父母讓她參加學校旅行，並答應會先完成所有功課。"},{"w":"earphone","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of equipment you put in your ear to listen to sound","c":"耳機","s":"I always wear earphones on the MRT so that my music does not bother the other passengers sitting around me.","t":"我在捷運上總是戴耳機，這樣我的音樂才不會打擾到坐在我周圍的其他乘客。","a":"earphones","h":1},{"w":"a pair of earphones","p":"n.phr.","d":"two earphones that are used together","c":"一副耳機","s":"My brother gave me a pair of earphones for my birthday, and the sound quality is much better than the old ones I had.","t":"我哥哥送我一副耳機當生日禮物，音質比我以前的那副好得多。"},{"w":"headphones","p":"n.","d":"a piece of equipment with two parts that cover your ears to listen to sound","c":"頭戴式耳機","s":"The large headphones in the music room block out all the noise, so students can hear every note clearly.","t":"音樂教室裡的大型頭戴式耳機隔絕了所有噪音，所以學生能清楚聽到每個音符。"},{"w":"economic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with trade, industry, and money","c":"經濟的","s":"The country's economic growth slowed down last year because fewer tourists visited and factories sold fewer products abroad.","t":"這個國家去年的經濟成長放緩，因為來訪的觀光客減少，工廠賣到國外的產品也變少了。","h":1},{"w":"economical","p":"adj.","d":"not using a lot of money, fuel, or time; cheap to use","c":"節省的；經濟實惠的","s":"A small car is more economical than a big one because it uses less gas and costs less to park in the city.","t":"小車比大車更省錢，因為它用的油比較少，在城市停車的費用也比較低。","h":1},{"w":"economics","p":"n.","d":"the study of how money, goods, and services are produced and used","c":"經濟學","s":"My sister studies economics at university because she wants to understand why prices go up and down.","t":"我姐姐在大學讀經濟學，因為她想了解為什麼物價會上漲和下跌。","h":1},{"w":"economist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies or writes about economics","c":"經濟學家","s":"The economist on TV explained that house prices in Taipei will probably keep rising over the next five years.","t":"電視上的經濟學家解釋說，台北的房價在未來五年可能會持續上漲。","h":1},{"w":"economy","p":"n.","d":"the system of money, trade, and industry in a country","c":"經濟","s":"When the economy is strong, more people have jobs and families feel comfortable spending money on travel and new clothes.","t":"當經濟強勁時，更多人有工作，家庭也樂於把錢花在旅遊和新衣服上。","h":1},{"w":"economize","p":"v.","d":"to spend less money or use fewer resources","c":"節省；節約","s":"Since Dad lost his job, our family has had to economize by eating at home and canceling our cable TV.","t":"自從爸爸失業後，我們家不得不節省開支，在家吃飯並取消有線電視。"},{"w":"economically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way connected with the economy; in a way that saves money","c":"在經濟上；節省地","s":"The town has suffered economically since the big factory closed, and many young people have moved away to find work.","t":"自從大工廠關閉後，這個小鎮在經濟上深受其害，許多年輕人搬走去找工作。"},{"w":"efficiency","p":"n.","d":"the quality of doing something well without wasting time or energy","c":"效率","s":"The new computer system improved the efficiency of the office so much that workers now finish their reports in half the time.","t":"新電腦系統大大提升了辦公室的效率，員工現在只需一半的時間就能完成報告。","h":1},{"w":"efficient","p":"adj.","d":"working well without wasting time, money, or energy","c":"有效率的","s":"Taking the MRT is the most efficient way to cross the city during rush hour, since it never gets stuck in traffic.","t":"尖峰時間搭捷運是穿越城市最有效率的方式，因為它永遠不會塞車。"},{"w":"efficiently","p":"adv.","d":"in an efficient way","c":"有效率地","s":"If you plan your homework schedule carefully, you can work more efficiently and still have time to play basketball.","t":"如果你仔細規劃做功課的時間，就能更有效率地工作，而且仍有時間打籃球。"},{"w":"inefficient","p":"adj.","d":"wasting time, money, or energy","c":"效率低的","s":"Heating the whole house with one old stove is inefficient, because most of the warm air escapes through the windows.","t":"用一個舊暖爐為整間房子取暖是效率低的，因為大部分的暖空氣都從窗戶跑掉了。"},{"w":"elastic","p":"adj.","d":"able to stretch and then return to its original shape","c":"有彈性的","s":"The waistband of these pants is elastic, so they still fit comfortably even after a big dinner.","t":"這條褲子的腰帶是有彈性的，所以即使吃了一頓大餐後仍然穿得很舒服。","h":1},{"w":"elastic","p":"n.","d":"a type of rubber material that stretches","c":"鬆緊帶","s":"My mother sewed a piece of elastic into the skirt so that it would not slip down when I run.","t":"我媽媽在裙子裡縫了一條鬆緊帶，這樣我跑步時裙子就不會滑下來。"},{"w":"elastic band","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin circle of rubber used to hold things together","c":"橡皮筋","s":"The teacher used an elastic band to keep the thirty test papers together before putting them in her bag.","t":"老師用一條橡皮筋把三十張考卷綑在一起，然後放進包包。"},{"w":"elasticity","p":"n.","d":"the ability to stretch and return to the original shape","c":"彈性","s":"As people grow older, their skin slowly loses its elasticity, which is why wrinkles appear around the eyes.","t":"隨著年齡增長，人的皮膚會慢慢失去彈性，這就是為什麼眼睛周圍會出現皺紋。"},{"w":"electronics","p":"n.","d":"the science of electronic equipment; electronic devices","c":"電子學；電子產品","s":"The electronics store near the station sells phones, cameras, and laptops at lower prices than the department store.","t":"車站附近的電子產品商店賣的手機、相機和筆電，比百貨公司便宜。","h":1},{"w":"electronic","p":"adj.","d":"using electricity and small parts like chips to work","c":"電子的","s":"Students must turn off all electronic devices, including smartwatches, before the listening test begins in ten minutes.","t":"聽力測驗十分鐘後開始，學生必須在測驗前關掉所有電子裝置，包括智慧手錶。"},{"w":"electricity","p":"n.","d":"energy that gives power to lights and machines","c":"電；電力","s":"During the typhoon, the electricity went out for six hours, so we lit candles and played card games together.","t":"颱風期間電力中斷了六個小時，所以我們點了蠟燭一起玩撲克牌。"},{"w":"electrical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with electricity","c":"電的；與電有關的","s":"Never touch an electrical socket with wet hands, because water makes it much easier for electricity to shock you.","t":"絕對不要用濕手觸碰電插座，因為水會讓電更容易電到你。"},{"w":"electrician","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to fix and connect electrical wires","c":"電工","s":"The lights in our kitchen kept flashing, so my father called an electrician to check the wires behind the wall.","t":"我們廚房的燈一直閃，所以爸爸叫了一位電工來檢查牆後的電線。"},{"w":"elegant","p":"adj.","d":"attractive and graceful in style","c":"優雅的","s":"She looked very elegant in her long black dress at the concert, and many people turned to look at her.","t":"她在音樂會上穿著黑色長禮服看起來非常優雅，許多人都轉頭看她。","h":1},{"w":"elegance","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being graceful and attractive","c":"優雅","s":"The old hotel is famous for its elegance, with high ceilings, soft music, and waiters in white gloves.","t":"這間老飯店以它的優雅聞名，有高高的天花板、輕柔的音樂和戴白手套的服務生。"},{"w":"elegantly","p":"adv.","d":"in a graceful and attractive way","c":"優雅地","s":"The dancer moved so elegantly across the stage that the audience forgot how difficult the steps actually were.","t":"那位舞者在舞台上動作如此優雅，觀眾都忘了那些舞步其實有多困難。"},{"w":"elementary","p":"adj.","d":"basic; connected with the first stages of learning","c":"基礎的；初級的","s":"This book teaches only elementary Japanese, so you will need a harder one after you learn the basic greetings.","t":"這本書只教初級日語，所以學完基本問候語後，你會需要一本更難的書。","h":1},{"w":"elementary school","p":"n.phr.","d":"a school for children aged about six to twelve","c":"小學","s":"My little cousin starts elementary school this September, and she is excited about carrying her new pink backpack.","t":"我的小表妹今年九月開始上小學，她對背她的新粉紅色書包感到很興奮。"},{"w":"element","p":"n.","d":"one basic part of something; a simple chemical substance","c":"元素；要素","s":"Trust is the most important element of a good friendship, because without it people cannot share their real feelings.","t":"信任是良好友誼最重要的要素，因為沒有它，人們無法分享真實的感受。"},{"w":"eliminate","p":"v.","d":"to remove or get rid of something completely","c":"消除；淘汰","s":"The city hopes to eliminate plastic straws from all restaurants by next year in order to protect the ocean.","t":"這座城市希望明年前消除所有餐廳的塑膠吸管，以保護海洋。","h":1},{"w":"be eliminated from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be removed from a competition after losing","c":"從…中被淘汰","s":"Our basketball team was eliminated from the tournament in the second round, so we watched the final from the stands.","t":"我們的籃球隊在第二輪就被淘汰出錦標賽，所以我們只能從看台上觀看決賽。","a":"was eliminated from"},{"w":"elimination","p":"n.","d":"the act of removing something completely","c":"消除；淘汰","s":"The elimination of the entrance fee brought thousands of extra visitors to the museum during the summer holiday.","t":"免除入場費後，暑假期間博物館多了數千名訪客。"},{"w":"elsewhere","p":"adv.","d":"in or to another place","c":"在別處；到別處","s":"The restaurant was full, so we decided to eat elsewhere and found a nice noodle shop around the corner.","t":"那家餐廳客滿了，所以我們決定到別處吃飯，結果在轉角找到一家不錯的麵店。","h":1},{"w":"look elsewhere","p":"v.phr.","d":"to search in other places","c":"另尋他處","s":"If this shop does not have your size, you may have to look elsewhere, perhaps at the bigger store downtown.","t":"如果這家店沒有你的尺寸，你可能得另尋他處，也許去市中心那家更大的店。"},{"w":"nowhere","p":"adv.","d":"not in any place","c":"無處；任何地方都不","s":"I looked for my keys everywhere in the house, but they were nowhere to be found until my brother checked the car.","t":"我在屋裡到處找鑰匙，卻到處都找不到，直到哥哥去車裡查看。"},{"w":"embarrass","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel shy, ashamed, or uncomfortable","c":"使尷尬","s":"Please do not embarrass me by showing my baby photos to my friends when they come over this weekend.","t":"這個週末我朋友來的時候，請不要拿我的嬰兒照片給他們看來讓我尷尬。","h":1},{"w":"embarrassment","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being embarrassed","c":"尷尬","s":"To my great embarrassment, I called the new teacher 'Mom' in front of the whole class on the first day.","t":"讓我非常尷尬的是，第一天我在全班面前把新老師叫成「媽」。"},{"w":"embarrassed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling shy, ashamed, or uncomfortable","c":"感到尷尬的","s":"I felt so embarrassed when my phone rang loudly in the middle of the quiet library that my face turned red.","t":"當我的手機在安靜的圖書館中大聲響起時，我覺得非常尷尬，臉都紅了。"},{"w":"embarrassing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel embarrassed","c":"令人尷尬的","s":"It was really embarrassing to forget my lines on stage, but the audience was kind and clapped anyway.","t":"在台上忘詞真的很令人尷尬，但觀眾很友善，還是給了掌聲。"},{"w":"embassy","p":"n.","d":"the building where officials of a foreign country work","c":"大使館","s":"You must go to the Japanese embassy to get a visa if you plan to stay in Japan for more than ninety days.","t":"如果你打算在日本停留超過九十天，必須去日本大使館辦簽證。","h":1},{"w":"ambassador","p":"n.","d":"the most important official who represents a country abroad","c":"大使","s":"The ambassador gave a speech at our school about the long friendship between Taiwan and her country.","t":"這位大使在我們學校演講，談到台灣和她的國家之間長久的友誼。"},{"w":"diplomat","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to represent their country in another country","c":"外交官","s":"My uncle works as a diplomat in Europe, so he has to speak three languages and attend many formal dinners.","t":"我叔叔在歐洲擔任外交官，所以他必須會說三種語言，還要出席許多正式晚宴。"},{"w":"emerge","p":"v.","d":"to come out from somewhere; to appear","c":"出現；浮現","s":"After the heavy rain stopped, the sun began to emerge from behind the dark clouds and warmed the wet streets.","t":"大雨停後，太陽開始從烏雲後出現，溫暖了潮濕的街道。","h":1},{"w":"emerge from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to come out of a place or a difficult situation","c":"從…出現／走出","s":"The country slowly emerged from the war and began building new schools, roads, and hospitals for its people.","t":"這個國家慢慢從戰爭中走出來，開始為人民建造新的學校、道路和醫院。","a":"emerged from"},{"w":"emergence","p":"n.","d":"the process of appearing or becoming known","c":"出現；興起","s":"The emergence of online shopping has changed the way people buy clothes, especially among young people in big cities.","t":"網路購物的興起改變了人們買衣服的方式，尤其是大城市的年輕人。"},{"w":"emergency","p":"n.","d":"a sudden dangerous situation that needs quick action","c":"緊急情況","s":"In an emergency, call 119 right away and tell the operator exactly where you are and what happened.","t":"遇到緊急情況時，立刻打 119，並告訴接線員你的確切位置和發生了什麼事。"},{"w":"emphasis","p":"n.","d":"special importance given to something","c":"強調；重點","s":"Our school puts a lot of emphasis on reading, so every student must finish at least one English book a month.","t":"我們學校把很多重點放在閱讀上，所以每個學生每個月必須讀完至少一本英文書。","h":1},{"w":"put emphasis on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give special importance to something","c":"強調；重視","s":"The new coach puts emphasis on teamwork rather than individual skill, and the team started winning more games.","t":"新教練重視團隊合作而非個人技巧，球隊開始贏更多比賽。","a":"puts emphasis on"},{"w":"emphasize","p":"v.","d":"to give special importance to something","c":"強調","s":"The doctor emphasized that I should drink more water and sleep at least eight hours every night to recover quickly.","t":"醫生強調我應該多喝水，每晚至少睡八小時才能快速康復。","a":"emphasized"},{"w":"empire","p":"n.","d":"a group of countries ruled by one ruler or government","c":"帝國","s":"The Roman empire was so large that it took weeks for a message to travel from one end to the other.","t":"羅馬帝國如此龐大，一則訊息從一端傳到另一端要花好幾週。","h":1},{"w":"emperor","p":"n.","d":"the ruler of an empire","c":"皇帝","s":"In ancient China, the emperor lived in a huge palace, and ordinary people were not allowed to enter it.","t":"在古代中國，皇帝住在一座巨大的宮殿裡，普通百姓不准進入。"},{"w":"empress","p":"n.","d":"a woman who rules an empire, or the wife of an emperor","c":"女皇；皇后","s":"The empress ruled the country wisely for forty years after her husband died, and people still remember her kindness.","t":"女皇在丈夫死後明智地統治國家四十年，人們至今仍記得她的仁慈。"},{"w":"imperial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with an empire or emperor","c":"帝國的；皇家的","s":"Visitors to the imperial palace in Beijing can see the golden throne where the emperor once sat.","t":"參觀北京皇家宮殿的遊客可以看到皇帝曾經坐過的金色王座。"},{"w":"enclose","p":"v.","d":"to put something inside a letter or package; to surround with a wall or fence","c":"附上；圍住","s":"Please enclose a photo of yourself with the application form and mail it to the office before Friday.","t":"請在申請表中附上一張你的照片，並在星期五前寄到辦公室。","h":1},{"w":"be enclosed by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be surrounded by a wall, fence, etc.","c":"被…圍住","s":"The garden is enclosed by a tall stone wall, so the children can play safely without their parents worrying.","t":"這座花園被高高的石牆圍住，所以孩子們可以安全地玩耍，父母不必擔心。","a":"is enclosed by"},{"w":"enclosed","p":"adj.","d":"surrounded by walls; included in an envelope","c":"封閉的；附上的","s":"Please find the enclosed check for 500 dollars, which covers the cost of the books I ordered last week.","t":"請查收附上的五百元支票，用來支付我上週訂購的書款。"},{"w":"enclosure","p":"n.","d":"an area surrounded by a fence or wall","c":"圍場；圍欄區","s":"The zoo built a larger enclosure for the elephants so they have more space to walk around and cool off in the water.","t":"動物園為大象建了一個更大的圍欄區，讓它們有更多空間走動並在水裡消暑。"},{"w":"encounter","p":"v.","d":"to meet someone or experience something unexpectedly","c":"遭遇；偶遇","s":"Hikers who climb the mountain early in the morning sometimes encounter wild monkeys looking for food near the trail.","t":"早上爬山的登山客有時會遇到在步道附近找食物的野生猴子。","h":1},{"w":"encounter","p":"n.","d":"an unexpected meeting or experience","c":"遭遇；邂逅","s":"My first encounter with a snake was on a camping trip, and I was too frightened to move for a full minute.","t":"我第一次與蛇的遭遇是在一次露營旅行中，我嚇得整整一分鐘動不了。"},{"w":"encounter difficulties","p":"v.phr.","d":"to meet problems","c":"遇到困難","s":"Many students encounter difficulties when they first write a long essay in English, but practice makes it easier.","t":"許多學生第一次用英文寫長篇文章時會遇到困難，但練習會讓它變得更容易。"},{"w":"endanger","p":"v.","d":"to put someone or something in danger","c":"危害；使遭危險","s":"Driving after drinking alcohol can endanger not only your own life but also the lives of other people on the road.","t":"酒後開車不僅會危害你自己的生命，也會危及路上其他人的生命。","h":1},{"w":"endangered","p":"adj.","d":"in danger of disappearing from the world","c":"瀕臨絕種的","s":"The Formosan black bear is an endangered animal, so hunting it is strictly forbidden by law in Taiwan.","t":"台灣黑熊是瀕臨絕種的動物，所以在台灣法律嚴格禁止獵捕它。"},{"w":"endangered species","p":"n.phr.","d":"a type of animal or plant that may soon disappear","c":"瀕危物種","s":"Pandas were once on the list of endangered species, but years of hard work by scientists helped their numbers grow.","t":"熊貓曾經被列為瀕危物種，但科學家多年的努力讓它們的數量增加了。"},{"w":"danger","p":"n.","d":"the possibility of being hurt or harmed","c":"危險","s":"The sign by the river warns swimmers of the danger of strong currents, especially after heavy rain in the mountains.","t":"河邊的告示牌警告游泳的人注意強勁水流的危險，尤其是山區下大雨之後。"},{"w":"dangerous","p":"adj.","d":"likely to hurt or harm you","c":"危險的","s":"It is dangerous to ride a scooter without a helmet, even if you are only going to the convenience store nearby.","t":"不戴安全帽騎機車是很危險的，即使你只是要去附近的便利商店。"},{"w":"endure","p":"v.","d":"to suffer something painful or difficult for a long time","c":"忍受；忍耐","s":"The runners had to endure strong winds and cold rain for over four hours before they finally reached the finish line.","t":"跑者們必須忍受強風和冷雨超過四個小時，才終於抵達終點線。","h":1},{"w":"endurance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to continue doing something difficult for a long time","c":"耐力","s":"Marathon running is a test of endurance more than speed, so most runners train slowly for many months.","t":"跑馬拉松考驗的是耐力而非速度，所以大多數跑者會慢慢訓練好幾個月。"},{"w":"enduring","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a long time","c":"持久的","s":"The two friends have an enduring friendship that began in kindergarten and is still strong forty years later.","t":"這兩位朋友有一段持久的友誼，從幼兒園開始，四十年後依然深厚。"},{"w":"enforce","p":"v.","d":"to make people obey a law or rule","c":"執行；實施","s":"The police will strictly enforce the new speed limit near schools, and drivers who break it will pay a heavy fine.","t":"警方將嚴格執行學校附近的新速限，違規的駕駛將付高額罰款。","h":1},{"w":"enforcement","p":"n.","d":"the act of making people obey a law or rule","c":"執行；實施","s":"Strict enforcement of the no-smoking rule has made the park much cleaner and more pleasant for families with children.","t":"禁菸規定的嚴格執行讓公園變得更乾淨，對有孩子的家庭也更舒適。"},{"w":"law enforcement","p":"n.phr.","d":"the activity of making sure people obey the law; the police","c":"執法","s":"Officers in law enforcement often work at night and on holidays to keep the city safe while everyone else sleeps.","t":"執法人員經常在夜間和假日工作，在大家睡覺時保護城市安全。"},{"w":"force","p":"n.","d":"physical power or strength","c":"力量；武力","s":"The wind was so strong that the force of it pushed the small boat all the way back to the shore.","t":"風太強了，風的力量把小船一路推回岸邊。"},{"w":"force","p":"v.","d":"to make someone do something they do not want to do","c":"強迫；迫使","s":"Heavy snow forced the airport to close for two days, and thousands of travelers slept on the floor.","t":"大雪迫使機場關閉兩天，數千名旅客睡在地板上。","a":"forced"},{"w":"engineering","p":"n.","d":"the work of designing and building machines, roads, bridges, etc.","c":"工程；工程學","s":"My brother studies engineering at university because he has loved building model bridges since he was a child.","t":"我哥哥在大學讀工程，因為他從小就喜歡做橋的模型。","h":1},{"w":"engineer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to design or build machines, roads, bridges, etc.","c":"工程師","s":"The engineer checked the old bridge carefully after the earthquake and said it was still safe for cars to cross.","t":"地震後，工程師仔細檢查了舊橋，說汽車通行仍然安全。"},{"w":"engine","p":"n.","d":"the part of a car or machine that makes it move","c":"引擎","s":"The car engine made a strange noise on the highway, so Dad stopped at the next gas station to check it.","t":"車子的引擎在高速公路上發出奇怪的聲音，所以爸爸在下一個加油站停下來檢查。"},{"w":"software engineer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who designs computer programs","c":"軟體工程師","s":"After graduation, she worked as a software engineer at a game company and helped design a popular mobile game.","t":"畢業後，她在一家遊戲公司擔任軟體工程師，協助設計了一款受歡迎的手機遊戲。"}]},{"unit":15,"theme":"enlargement – explanation","cards":[{"w":"enlarge","p":"v.","d":"to make something bigger","c":"放大；擴大","s":"The photo shop can enlarge this small picture of my grandparents so that we can hang it on the living room wall.","t":"照相館可以把這張我祖父母的小照片放大，這樣我們就能把它掛在客廳牆上。","h":1},{"w":"enlargement","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something bigger; a bigger copy of a photo","c":"放大；擴大","s":"The enlargement of the school library will give students three hundred more seats and a quiet room for group discussion.","t":"學校圖書館的擴建將為學生增加三百個座位和一間安靜的小組討論室。"},{"w":"large","p":"adj.","d":"big in size or amount","c":"大的；大量的","s":"A large number of students stayed after school to practice for the music contest, so the hall was very noisy.","t":"大量學生放學後留下來為音樂比賽練習，所以禮堂非常吵。"},{"w":"largely","p":"adv.","d":"mostly; mainly","c":"大部分；主要地","s":"The success of the school fair was largely due to the parents who cooked, cleaned, and sold tickets all day.","t":"學校園遊會的成功主要歸功於整天煮飯、打掃和賣票的家長們。"},{"w":"enormous","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large","c":"巨大的","s":"The new shopping mall is enormous, with over four hundred stores, two cinemas, and a parking lot for five thousand cars.","t":"新的購物中心非常巨大，有四百多家商店、兩間電影院和可停五千輛車的停車場。","h":1},{"w":"enormously","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; very much","c":"極大地；非常","s":"Online learning has grown enormously in the past few years, and many students now take classes at home.","t":"線上學習在過去幾年大幅成長，許多學生現在在家上課。"},{"w":"an enormous amount of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very large quantity of","c":"大量的","s":"The volunteers collected an enormous amount of food for the families who lost their homes in the flood last month.","t":"志工們為上個月洪水中失去家園的家庭募集了大量的食物。"},{"w":"ensure","p":"v.","d":"to make certain that something happens","c":"確保","s":"Please check the list twice to ensure that every student has a ticket before the bus leaves for the museum.","t":"請在公車出發去博物館前檢查名單兩次，確保每個學生都有票。","h":1},{"w":"make sure","p":"v.phr.","d":"to check so that something is certain","c":"確認；確保","s":"Before you leave the house, make sure that all the windows are closed, because a typhoon is coming tonight.","t":"出門前請確認所有窗戶都關好，因為今晚颱風要來了。"},{"w":"sure","p":"adj.","d":"certain; having no doubt","c":"確定的","s":"Are you sure that the test is on Friday and not Thursday? I want to plan my study time correctly.","t":"你確定考試是星期五而不是星期四嗎？我想正確安排我的讀書時間。"},{"w":"assure","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone that something is true so they stop worrying","c":"向…保證","s":"The doctor assured my mother that the operation was simple and that I would be home in two days.","t":"醫生向我媽媽保證手術很簡單，我兩天後就能回家。","a":"assured"},{"w":"entertain","p":"v.","d":"to amuse people; to have guests at your home","c":"使娛樂；款待","s":"The clown entertained the children at the birthday party with funny jokes and magic tricks for nearly an hour.","t":"小丑在生日派對上用搞笑的笑話和魔術娛樂孩子們將近一個小時。","a":"entertained","h":1},{"w":"entertainment","p":"n.","d":"things like movies, music, and games that amuse people","c":"娛樂","s":"There is not much entertainment in my grandmother's village, so young people usually go to the city on weekends.","t":"我奶奶的村子裡沒有什麼娛樂，所以年輕人週末通常都去城裡。"},{"w":"entertaining","p":"adj.","d":"funny and enjoyable","c":"有趣的；娛樂性的","s":"The science show was so entertaining that even the students who hate physics laughed and asked questions.","t":"這場科學秀太有趣了，連討厭物理的學生都笑了並提出問題。"},{"w":"entertainer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to amuse people, such as a singer","c":"藝人；表演者","s":"The famous entertainer sang, danced, and told jokes on stage, and the audience did not want the show to end.","t":"這位知名藝人在台上唱歌、跳舞、講笑話，觀眾都不希望表演結束。"},{"w":"enthusiasm","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of interest and excitement","c":"熱情；熱忱","s":"The new teacher's enthusiasm for science is catching, and now half the class wants to join the science club.","t":"新老師對科學的熱情很有感染力，現在半個班級都想加入科學社。","h":1},{"w":"enthusiastic","p":"adj.","d":"showing a lot of interest and excitement","c":"熱情的；熱衷的","s":"The fans were so enthusiastic that they waited outside the stadium for six hours in the rain to see the team.","t":"球迷們非常熱情，在雨中在體育場外等了六個小時只為見到球隊。"},{"w":"enthusiastically","p":"adv.","d":"with a lot of interest and excitement","c":"熱情地","s":"The whole class clapped enthusiastically on Friday when Amy finished her speech about protecting sea turtles.","t":"星期五當艾咪結束關於保護海龜的演講時，全班熱情地鼓掌。"},{"w":"equality","p":"n.","d":"the state of having the same rights and chances as others","c":"平等","s":"The school believes in equality, so boys and girls play on the same sports teams and share the same jobs.","t":"這所學校相信平等，所以男生和女生在同樣的運動隊伍打球，並分擔同樣的工作。","h":1},{"w":"equal","p":"adj.","d":"the same in size, amount, or value","c":"相等的；平等的","s":"Cut the cake into eight equal pieces so that every child at the party gets exactly the same amount.","t":"把蛋糕切成八等份，這樣派對上的每個孩子都能拿到完全一樣的量。"},{"w":"equally","p":"adv.","d":"in the same way or to the same degree","c":"同樣地；平等地","s":"Both players performed equally well in the final, so the judges needed ten minutes to decide the winner.","t":"兩位選手在決賽中表現得同樣出色，所以評審花了十分鐘才決定勝者。"},{"w":"be equal to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be the same as; to be able to deal with","c":"等於；勝任","s":"One kilometer is equal to one thousand meters, so the five-kilometer race is five thousand meters long.","t":"一公里等於一千公尺，所以五公里的賽跑長五千公尺。","a":"is equal to"},{"w":"inequality","p":"n.","d":"the unfair situation in which some people have more rights or money than others","c":"不平等","s":"Many people are worried about the growing inequality between rich and poor families in big cities around the world.","t":"許多人擔心世界各大城市中富裕家庭與貧窮家庭之間日益擴大的不平等。"},{"w":"equip","p":"v.","d":"to provide someone or something with what is needed","c":"裝備；配備","s":"The school will equip every classroom with a new projector and a faster computer before the semester starts.","t":"學校會在學期開始前為每間教室配備新的投影機和更快的電腦。","h":1},{"w":"equipment","p":"n.","d":"the tools or machines needed for a job or activity","c":"設備；裝備","s":"The camping equipment is heavy, so we will share the tent, the stove, and the cooking pots among the four of us.","t":"露營裝備很重，所以我們四個人會分攤帳篷、爐子和鍋具。"},{"w":"be equipped with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have the tools or features needed","c":"配備有","s":"The new ambulance is equipped with modern machines, so doctors can begin treating patients on the way to the hospital.","t":"新救護車配備有現代化的儀器，所以醫生能在前往醫院的途中就開始治療病患。","a":"is equipped with"},{"w":"a piece of equipment","p":"n.phr.","d":"one tool or machine","c":"一件設備","s":"A microscope is a piece of equipment that every biology lab needs, because it lets students see tiny living things.","t":"顯微鏡是每間生物實驗室都需要的一件設備，因為它讓學生能看到微小的生物。"},{"w":"era","p":"n.","d":"a period of time in history with a special character","c":"時代；年代","s":"The invention of the smartphone began a new era in which people can work, shop, and study almost anywhere.","t":"智慧型手機的發明開啟了一個新時代，人們幾乎可以在任何地方工作、購物和學習。","h":1},{"w":"a new era","p":"n.phr.","d":"the beginning of a very different period","c":"新時代","s":"The first high-speed train in 2007 marked a new era for travel in Taiwan, cutting the trip from Taipei to Kaohsiung to ninety minutes.","t":"2007年第一班高鐵標誌著台灣旅行的新時代，把台北到高雄的車程縮短到九十分鐘。"},{"w":"the modern era","p":"n.phr.","d":"the period of recent history up to now","c":"現代","s":"In the modern era, most people get their news from phones rather than from newspapers delivered to their doors.","t":"在現代，大多數人從手機而不是從送到家門口的報紙獲得新聞。"},{"w":"essential","p":"adj.","d":"completely necessary; very important","c":"必要的；不可或缺的","s":"Clean water is essential for good health, so remember to carry a bottle with you when you hike in summer.","t":"乾淨的水對健康是不可或缺的，所以夏天爬山時記得帶一瓶水。","h":1},{"w":"essential","p":"n.","d":"something that is necessary (usually plural)","c":"必需品","s":"Before the typhoon arrived, we bought the essentials such as candles, batteries, bread, and bottled water.","t":"颱風來臨前，我們買了蠟燭、電池、麵包和瓶裝水等必需品。","a":"essentials"},{"w":"essentially","p":"adv.","d":"basically; in the most important ways","c":"本質上；基本上","s":"The two phones are essentially the same, although the newer one has a slightly better camera and costs more.","t":"這兩支手機基本上是一樣的，雖然新的那支相機稍微好一點，而且比較貴。"},{"w":"essence","p":"n.","d":"the most important quality of something","c":"本質；精髓","s":"The essence of good teaching is helping students ask their own questions, not just giving them the answers.","t":"良好教學的本質是幫助學生提出自己的問題，而不只是給他們答案。"},{"w":"establish","p":"v.","d":"to start or create an organization, system, or relationship","c":"建立；設立","s":"The two schools decided to establish an exchange program so that students can visit each other's countries every summer.","t":"這兩所學校決定建立一個交換計畫，讓學生每年夏天可以互訪對方的國家。","h":1},{"w":"establishment","p":"n.","d":"the act of starting an organization; a business or organization","c":"建立；機構","s":"The establishment of a free clinic in the village means that sick people no longer have to travel two hours to see a doctor.","t":"村子裡設立免費診所，意味著生病的人不必再花兩小時去看醫生。"},{"w":"be established in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be founded in a certain year","c":"創立於","s":"Our school was established in 1952, so next year we will celebrate its seventy-fifth birthday with a big concert.","t":"我們學校創立於1952年，所以明年我們將以一場盛大的音樂會慶祝它的七十五歲生日。","a":"was established in"},{"w":"well-established","p":"adj.","d":"having existed for a long time and respected","c":"歷史悠久的；穩固的","s":"The bakery is a well-established business in our town, and three generations of the same family have worked there.","t":"這家麵包店是我們鎮上歷史悠久的商店，同一家族的三代人都在那裡工作過。"},{"w":"estimate","p":"v.","d":"to guess the size, amount, or cost of something","c":"估計","s":"Experts estimate that more than two million people will visit the lantern festival during the ten days it is open.","t":"專家估計燈會開放的十天期間將有超過兩百萬人參觀。","h":1},{"w":"estimate","p":"n.","d":"a guess about the size, amount, or cost of something","c":"估計；估價","s":"The repair shop gave us an estimate of 3,000 dollars to fix the scooter, but the final bill was a little higher.","t":"修車行給我們修機車的估價是三千元，但最後的帳單稍微高一點。"},{"w":"estimated","p":"adj.","d":"calculated roughly","c":"估計的","s":"The estimated cost of the new bridge is two billion dollars, and the city hopes to finish it within four years.","t":"新橋的估計成本是二十億元，市政府希望在四年內完工。"},{"w":"underestimate","p":"v.","d":"to think something is smaller or less important than it really is","c":"低估","s":"Never underestimate the power of a good night's sleep, because tired students make many more careless mistakes on tests.","t":"絕不要低估一夜好眠的力量，因為疲倦的學生在考試中會犯更多粗心的錯誤。"},{"w":"ethnic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a group of people who share the same culture, language, or race","c":"種族的；民族的","s":"Taiwan has many ethnic groups, including the Amis and the Atayal, and each one has its own language and festivals.","t":"台灣有許多民族群體，包括阿美族和泰雅族，每一族都有自己的語言和節慶。","h":1},{"w":"ethnic group","p":"n.phr.","d":"people who share the same culture, language, or history","c":"族群","s":"Students learned that the Hakka are an important ethnic group in Taiwan with their own food, songs, and traditional clothes.","t":"學生們了解到客家人是台灣重要的族群，有自己的食物、歌曲和傳統服飾。"},{"w":"ethnicity","p":"n.","d":"the fact of belonging to a particular ethnic group","c":"種族；民族身分","s":"The survey asked people about their age and job, but it did not ask about their ethnicity or religion.","t":"這份問卷詢問了人們的年齡和職業，但沒有問他們的民族身分或宗教。"},{"w":"evaluate","p":"v.","d":"to judge how good, useful, or successful something is","c":"評估；評價","s":"At the end of the course, students are asked to evaluate the teacher by filling out a short online form.","t":"課程結束時，學生會被要求填寫一份簡短的線上表格來評價老師。","h":1},{"w":"evaluation","p":"n.","d":"a judgment about how good or useful something is","c":"評估；評價","s":"The company sends every worker a yearly evaluation that explains what they did well and what they should improve.","t":"公司每年會給每位員工一份評估，說明他們做得好的地方和應該改進的地方。","h":1},{"w":"value","p":"n.","d":"how much something is worth; importance","c":"價值","s":"The value of the old painting went up after the artist died, and it was finally sold for two million dollars.","t":"這幅老畫的價值在畫家去世後上漲，最後以兩百萬元賣出。"},{"w":"valuable","p":"adj.","d":"worth a lot of money; very useful","c":"貴重的；有價值的","s":"Do not leave valuable things like phones and wallets in the classroom when you go to PE class.","t":"去上體育課時，不要把手機和錢包等貴重物品留在教室裡。"},{"w":"eventual","p":"adj.","d":"happening at the end of a process","c":"最終的","s":"The team lost the first two games, but their eventual victory in the final made all the hard training worthwhile.","t":"球隊輸了前兩場比賽，但他們在決賽中的最終勝利讓所有辛苦的訓練都值得了。","h":1},{"w":"eventually","p":"adv.","d":"in the end, after a long time","c":"最後；終於","s":"After waiting for the bus for forty minutes in the rain, we eventually decided to take a taxi home.","t":"在雨中等了四十分鐘的公車後，我們最後決定搭計程車回家。"},{"w":"event","p":"n.","d":"something that happens, especially something important","c":"事件；活動","s":"The school sports day is the biggest event of the year, and parents come to cheer for their children.","t":"學校運動會是一年中最大的活動，家長們都會來為孩子加油。"},{"w":"evidence","p":"n.","d":"facts or signs that show something is true","c":"證據","s":"The police found no evidence that the man had been in the shop, so they had to let him go.","t":"警方找不到那名男子曾在店裡的證據，所以只好放他走。","h":1},{"w":"evident","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see or understand; clear","c":"明顯的","s":"It was evident from her red eyes that she had been crying, so I sat down beside her and waited quietly.","t":"從她紅紅的眼睛可以明顯看出她哭過，所以我在她身邊坐下來安靜地等著。","h":1},{"w":"evidently","p":"adv.","d":"clearly; it seems that","c":"明顯地；顯然","s":"The boy had evidently not done his homework, because he could not answer even the easiest question the teacher asked.","t":"那個男孩顯然沒有做功課，因為他連老師問的最簡單的問題都答不出來。"},{"w":"give evidence","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell a court what you saw or know","c":"作證","s":"The shop owner had to give evidence in court about what she saw on the night of the robbery.","t":"店主必須在法庭上就搶案當晚她所看到的情況作證。"},{"w":"exaggerate","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem bigger or better than it really is","c":"誇大","s":"My uncle likes to exaggerate when he tells stories, so the fish he caught gets bigger every time we hear about it.","t":"我叔叔講故事時喜歡誇大，所以他釣到的魚每次聽起來都變得更大。","h":1},{"w":"exaggeration","p":"n.","d":"a statement that makes something seem bigger or better than it is","c":"誇張；誇大","s":"It is no exaggeration to say that the night market is the most popular place in town on a Saturday evening.","t":"說夜市是週六晚上鎮上最受歡迎的地方，一點也不誇張。"},{"w":"exaggerated","p":"adj.","d":"made to seem bigger or more important than it is","c":"誇大的","s":"The movie poster gives an exaggerated idea of how scary the film is; actually, even my little sister enjoyed it.","t":"電影海報對這部片有多恐怖給了一個誇大的印象；其實連我妹妹都看得很開心。"},{"w":"exception","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that is not included in a rule","c":"例外","s":"Everyone in the class passed the test, and the only exception was Tom, who was sick and missed a week of school.","t":"全班都通過了考試，唯一的例外是湯姆，他生病缺了一週的課。","h":1},{"w":"make an exception","p":"v.phr.","d":"to allow something that is usually not allowed","c":"破例","s":"The library does not usually lend out dictionaries, but the librarian agreed to make an exception for my project.","t":"圖書館通常不外借字典，但圖書館員同意為了我的專題破例。"},{"w":"except","p":"prep.","d":"not including","c":"除了…之外","s":"The museum is open every day except Monday, so let's plan our visit for the weekend instead.","t":"博物館除了星期一每天都開放，所以我們改計畫週末去參觀吧。"},{"w":"exceptional","p":"adj.","d":"unusually good","c":"傑出的；異常的","s":"Her exceptional talent for drawing was clear when she was only five, and she now studies art in Paris.","t":"她傑出的繪畫天分在五歲時就很明顯，現在她在巴黎學藝術。"},{"w":"exhaust","p":"v.","d":"to make someone very tired; to use something up completely","c":"使筋疲力盡；耗盡","s":"Climbing the mountain in the summer heat will exhaust you quickly, so bring plenty of water and rest often.","t":"在夏天的酷熱中爬山會很快讓你筋疲力盡，所以要帶足夠的水並常常休息。","h":1},{"w":"exhaust","p":"n.","d":"the waste gas that comes out of a vehicle","c":"廢氣","s":"The exhaust from thousands of cars and scooters makes the air in the city dirty, especially during rush hour.","t":"成千上萬汽機車排放的廢氣讓城市的空氣變髒，尤其是在尖峰時段。"},{"w":"exhausted","p":"adj.","d":"extremely tired","c":"筋疲力盡的","s":"After running the whole marathon, she was so exhausted that she fell asleep on the bus before it left the parking lot.","t":"跑完整場馬拉松後，她筋疲力盡，公車還沒開出停車場她就睡著了。"},{"w":"exhausting","p":"adj.","d":"making you extremely tired","c":"令人筋疲力盡的","s":"Looking after three small children all day is exhausting work, so my aunt is always asleep by nine o'clock.","t":"整天照顧三個小孩是令人筋疲力盡的工作，所以我阿姨總是九點前就睡著了。"},{"w":"exhaustion","p":"n.","d":"the state of being extremely tired","c":"筋疲力盡","s":"Two of the hikers were taken to the hospital with exhaustion after they walked for fourteen hours without enough food.","t":"兩名登山客在沒有足夠食物的情況下走了十四小時後，因筋疲力盡被送往醫院。"},{"w":"exhibit","p":"v.","d":"to show something in a public place","c":"展示；展出","s":"The gallery will exhibit paintings by local high school students for two weeks, and entry is free for everyone.","t":"畫廊將展出本地高中生的畫作兩週，所有人免費入場。","h":1},{"w":"exhibit","p":"n.","d":"an object or a collection shown in a museum","c":"展覽品；展覽","s":"The most popular exhibit at the science museum is a real dinosaur bone that visitors are allowed to touch.","t":"科學博物館最受歡迎的展覽品是一根真的恐龍骨頭，參觀者可以觸摸。"},{"w":"exhibition","p":"n.","d":"a public show of art or other objects","c":"展覽","s":"My art class is holding an exhibition in the school hall next week, and my painting of the sea will be in it.","t":"我的美術班下週將在學校禮堂舉辦展覽，我畫的海也會在其中。"},{"w":"expand","p":"v.","d":"to become larger or make something larger","c":"擴大；擴張","s":"The small coffee shop has done so well that the owner plans to expand it by adding a second floor next year.","t":"這家小咖啡店生意很好，老闆計畫明年加蓋二樓來擴大它。","h":1},{"w":"expansion","p":"n.","d":"the process of becoming larger","c":"擴大；擴張","s":"The rapid expansion of the city means that farms which were here ten years ago are now covered with apartment buildings.","t":"城市的快速擴張意味著十年前還在這裡的農田，現在已經蓋滿了公寓大樓。","h":1},{"w":"expand into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start doing business in a new area or field","c":"擴展到…","s":"The bubble tea company first opened in Taichung and later expanded into Japan, Korea, and several cities in Europe.","t":"這家珍珠奶茶公司最初在台中開業，後來擴展到日本、韓國和歐洲的幾個城市。","a":"expanded into"},{"w":"experimental","p":"adj.","d":"new and being tested; connected with experiments","c":"實驗性的；實驗的","s":"The experimental medicine helped many patients in the study, but doctors say more tests are needed before it goes on sale.","t":"這種實驗性的藥物在研究中幫助了許多病患，但醫生說上市前還需要更多測試。","h":1},{"w":"experiment","p":"n.","d":"a scientific test done to learn something","c":"實驗","s":"In today's chemistry class, we did an experiment to find out which liquid makes an egg float the best.","t":"在今天的化學課上，我們做了一個實驗，看看哪種液體最能讓雞蛋浮起來。"},{"w":"experiment","p":"v.","d":"to try new ideas or methods to see what happens","c":"做實驗；嘗試","s":"The chef likes to experiment with unusual ingredients, so last week he made ice cream with green tea and black beans.","t":"這位主廚喜歡用不尋常的食材做嘗試，所以上週他用綠茶和黑豆做了冰淇淋。"},{"w":"explanation","p":"n.","d":"a reason or description that makes something clear","c":"解釋；說明","s":"The teacher's clear explanation of the math problem helped everyone understand it, even the students who had failed the quiz.","t":"老師對這道數學題清楚的解釋幫助每個人都理解了，連小考不及格的學生也懂了。","h":1},{"w":"explain","p":"v.","d":"to make something clear by giving details or reasons","c":"解釋；說明","s":"Could you explain how this washing machine works? The buttons are all in Japanese, and I cannot read them.","t":"你能解釋一下這台洗衣機怎麼用嗎？按鈕全是日文，我看不懂。"},{"w":"give an explanation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell someone the reason for something","c":"給出解釋","s":"You were two hours late for dinner, and you need to give an explanation before your mother gets even more worried.","t":"你晚餐遲到了兩個小時，你需要給個解釋，免得你媽媽更擔心。"}]},{"unit":16,"theme":"explosion – finance","cards":[{"w":"explosion","p":"n.","d":"a sudden loud burst when something like a bomb blows up","c":"爆炸","s":"The explosion at the fireworks factory was so loud that people living ten kilometers away heard it and called the police.","t":"煙火工廠的爆炸聲太大了，住在十公里外的人都聽到並打電話報警。","h":1},{"w":"explosive","p":"adj.","d":"able to explode; likely to blow up","c":"爆炸性的；易爆的","s":"Passengers may not carry explosive materials such as fireworks onto the plane, so the officer checked every bag carefully.","t":"乘客不可攜帶像煙火這類易爆的物品上飛機，所以官員仔細檢查了每個袋子。","h":1},{"w":"explosive","p":"n.","d":"a substance that can explode","c":"爆裂物；炸藥","s":"Workers used a small amount of explosive to break the rock, and then trucks carried the pieces away from the mountain road.","t":"工人用少量炸藥炸開岩石，然後卡車把碎石從山路運走。"},{"w":"explode","p":"v.","d":"to burst with a loud noise; to blow up","c":"爆炸","s":"The old gas tank might explode if you leave it in the hot sun, so please move it to a cool, shady place.","t":"如果你把舊瓦斯桶放在烈日下，它可能會爆炸，所以請把它移到涼爽有陰影的地方。"},{"w":"a population explosion","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very fast increase in the number of people","c":"人口爆炸","s":"Many big cities in Asia experienced a population explosion in the last century, and now they do not have enough homes for everyone.","t":"亞洲許多大城市在上個世紀經歷了人口爆炸，現在沒有足夠的房子給所有人住。"},{"w":"expose","p":"v.","d":"to show something that was hidden; to make the truth known","c":"暴露；揭露","s":"The reporter wanted to expose the truth about the factory, so she secretly took photos of the dirty water it was pouring into the river.","t":"記者想揭露那家工廠的真相，所以她偷偷拍下它排入河裡的髒水照片。","h":1},{"w":"exposure","p":"n.","d":"the state of being in a place where something can affect you","c":"暴露；接觸；曝光","s":"Too much exposure to the sun can damage your skin, so doctors suggest wearing a hat and sunscreen at the beach.","t":"過度暴露在陽光下會傷害皮膚，所以醫生建議在海邊戴帽子並塗防曬乳。","h":1},{"w":"be exposed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be put in a situation where something can affect you","c":"暴露於；接觸到","s":"Children who are exposed to two languages from birth often learn both without any special lessons or extra effort.","t":"從出生就接觸兩種語言的孩子，常常不需要任何特別課程或額外努力就能學會兩種語言。","a":"are exposed to"},{"w":"exposed","p":"adj.","d":"not covered or protected","c":"無遮蔽的；暴露的","s":"The small house on the hill is very exposed to the wind, so the family planted a row of tall trees to protect it.","t":"山丘上的小房子完全暴露在風中，所以這家人種了一排高大的樹來保護它。"},{"w":"extend","p":"v.","d":"to make something longer or larger; to last longer","c":"延長；擴展","s":"The library decided to extend its opening hours during exam week, so students can now study there until eleven at night.","t":"圖書館決定在考試週延長開放時間，所以學生現在可以在那裡讀到晚上十一點。","h":1},{"w":"extent","p":"n.","d":"how large, important, or serious something is","c":"程度；範圍","s":"After the typhoon passed, officials flew over the island to see the extent of the damage to roads and bridges.","t":"颱風過後，官員飛越全島查看道路和橋梁受損的程度。","h":1},{"w":"extend a deadline","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give more time to finish something","c":"延長期限","s":"Because half of the class was sick last week, the teacher agreed to extend the deadline for the science report by three days.","t":"因為上週班上一半的人生病了，老師同意將科學報告的期限延長三天。","a":"extend the deadline"},{"w":"to some extent","p":"phr.","d":"partly; in some way","c":"在某種程度上","s":"I agree with you to some extent, but I still think we should ask the teacher before we change the plan.","t":"我在某種程度上同意你，但我還是認為改變計畫前應該先問老師。"},{"w":"extension","p":"n.","d":"extra time given; a part added to make something longer","c":"延期；延長；擴建部分","s":"She asked her boss for a two-day extension because her computer broke down before she could finish the report.","t":"她向老闆要求延期兩天，因為電腦在她完成報告之前壞了。"},{"w":"extensive","p":"adj.","d":"covering a large area or amount","c":"廣泛的；大範圍的","s":"The fire caused extensive damage to the old market, and it will take at least a year to rebuild all the shops.","t":"這場火災對舊市場造成大範圍的損害，至少要一年才能重建所有店面。"},{"w":"facial","p":"adj.","d":"of or on the face","c":"臉部的","s":"Babies cannot talk, but their facial expressions tell parents clearly whether they are happy, hungry, or tired.","t":"嬰兒不會說話，但他們的臉部表情清楚地告訴父母他們是快樂、飢餓還是疲倦。","h":1},{"w":"face","p":"n.","d":"the front part of the head","c":"臉","s":"After running in the cold wind for an hour, his face was bright red, and his lips were almost blue.","t":"在冷風中跑了一個小時後，他的臉紅通通的，嘴唇幾乎發紫。"},{"w":"face","p":"v.","d":"to deal with a difficult situation","c":"面對","s":"Instead of running away from the problem, you should face it bravely and talk to your parents about what happened.","t":"與其逃避問題，你應該勇敢地面對它，並告訴父母發生了什麼事。"},{"w":"face to face","p":"phr.","d":"meeting someone in person, not online or by phone","c":"面對面","s":"We had talked online for two years, so it felt strange to finally meet face to face at the airport last Saturday.","t":"我們在網路上聊了兩年，所以上週六終於在機場面對面見面時感覺很奇妙。"},{"w":"facility","p":"n.","d":"a place, building, or equipment for a special purpose","c":"設施","s":"The new sports facility near our school has a swimming pool, a gym, and two basketball courts that anyone can use.","t":"我們學校附近新的運動設施有游泳池、健身房和兩個任何人都能使用的籃球場。","h":1},{"w":"facilities","p":"n.","d":"rooms, equipment, or services provided for people to use","c":"設備；設施（複數）","s":"The hotel is cheap, but its facilities are excellent, including free Wi-Fi, a laundry room, and a kitchen for guests.","t":"這家旅館很便宜，但設施很棒，包括免費 Wi-Fi、洗衣房和給客人用的廚房。"},{"w":"facilitate","p":"v.","d":"to make something easier","c":"促進；使容易","s":"Clear road signs facilitate travel for visitors, so the city put up new signs in English and Japanese before the festival.","t":"清楚的路標有助於遊客的旅行，所以市政府在節慶前設立了新的英文和日文標示。"},{"w":"faithful","p":"adj.","d":"always loyal and supporting someone or something","c":"忠實的；忠誠的","s":"The old dog stayed faithful to its owner for fifteen years and waited by the door every evening until he came home.","t":"那隻老狗十五年來一直對主人很忠心，每天傍晚都在門邊等到他回家。","h":1},{"w":"faithfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a loyal way; exactly as the original","c":"忠實地","s":"The movie follows the novel faithfully, so fans of the book were happy that nothing important was changed.","t":"這部電影忠實地按照小說拍攝，所以書迷很高興沒有重要的情節被改動。"},{"w":"faith","p":"n.","d":"strong belief or trust in someone or something","c":"信念；信任；信仰","s":"Even after the team lost five games in a row, the coach never lost faith in his young players.","t":"即使球隊連輸五場，教練也從未對他年輕的球員失去信心。"},{"w":"have faith in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to trust or believe in someone","c":"對…有信心","s":"My parents have faith in me, so they let me travel to Japan alone for the first time last summer.","t":"我父母對我有信心，所以去年夏天他們第一次讓我獨自去日本旅行。"},{"w":"unfaithful","p":"adj.","d":"not loyal to a partner or friend","c":"不忠的","s":"She ended the relationship because her boyfriend had been unfaithful to her, and she could no longer trust him at all.","t":"她結束了這段關係，因為男友對她不忠，她再也無法信任他。"},{"w":"fame","p":"n.","d":"the state of being known by many people","c":"名聲；名氣","s":"The young singer found fame overnight after her video was watched by millions of people around the world.","t":"這位年輕歌手的影片被全球數百萬人觀看後，一夜之間獲得了名聲。","h":1},{"w":"famous","p":"adj.","d":"known by many people","c":"有名的","s":"Taiwan is famous for its night markets, where visitors can try hundreds of delicious snacks at very low prices.","t":"台灣以夜市聞名，遊客可以在那裡用很低的價格品嚐數百種美味小吃。"},{"w":"rise to fame","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become famous","c":"成名","s":"The actor rose to fame after playing a brave doctor in a popular TV drama, and now he appears in many films.","t":"這位演員在一部熱門電視劇中演出一位勇敢的醫生後成名，現在他出現在許多電影裡。","a":"rose to fame"},{"w":"fame and fortune","p":"n.phr.","d":"being famous and rich","c":"名利","s":"Many young people move to the big city dreaming of fame and fortune, but only a few of them ever become stars.","t":"許多年輕人搬到大城市夢想著名利，但只有少數人真的成為明星。"},{"w":"fantastic","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; wonderful","c":"極好的；棒極了","s":"We had a fantastic time at the beach yesterday because the weather was perfect and the water was warm and clear.","t":"我們昨天在海邊度過了超棒的時光，因為天氣完美，海水溫暖又清澈。","h":1},{"w":"fantasy","p":"n.","d":"a story or idea about magic and imaginary worlds","c":"幻想；奇幻作品","s":"Harry Potter is a popular fantasy series, and millions of readers love its world of magic, dragons, and flying brooms.","t":"《哈利波特》是一套受歡迎的奇幻系列作品，數百萬讀者喜愛它的魔法、龍和飛天掃帚的世界。","h":1},{"w":"fantastic","p":"adj.","d":"strange and imaginary, like in a dream","c":"奇幻的；想像出來的","s":"The artist's paintings are full of fantastic creatures, such as flying fish with butterfly wings and trees that can walk.","t":"這位藝術家的畫作充滿了奇幻的生物，像是長著蝴蝶翅膀的飛魚和會走路的樹。"},{"w":"fantasize","p":"v.","d":"to imagine something you would like to happen","c":"幻想","s":"During the long boring lesson, he began to fantasize about becoming a famous football player and scoring the winning goal.","t":"在漫長無聊的課堂上，他開始幻想成為一名有名的足球員，踢進致勝的一球。"},{"w":"fantastically","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; wonderfully","c":"極其；非常棒地","s":"The new restaurant has done fantastically well since it opened, and now you need to book a table two weeks ahead.","t":"這家新餐廳開業以來生意非常好，現在你得提前兩週訂位。"},{"w":"farewell","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying goodbye","c":"告別","s":"Before our exchange teacher returned to Canada, the whole class threw a farewell party for her with cake and songs.","t":"在交換老師回加拿大之前，全班為她舉辦了一場有蛋糕和歌曲的告別派對。","h":1},{"w":"say farewell to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say goodbye to someone","c":"向…道別","s":"At the end of the trip, we said farewell to our host family and promised to write to them as soon as we got home.","t":"旅行結束時，我們向接待家庭道別，並承諾一回家就寫信給他們。","a":"said farewell to"},{"w":"farewell speech","p":"n.phr.","d":"a speech given when someone leaves a job or place","c":"告別演說","s":"The retiring principal gave a moving farewell speech that made many teachers and students cry at the graduation ceremony.","t":"即將退休的校長在畢業典禮上發表了一場感人的告別演說，讓許多師生流下眼淚。"},{"w":"fasten","p":"v.","d":"to close or fix something firmly","c":"繫緊；扣上；固定","s":"Please fasten your seat belt and turn off your phone, because the plane is going to take off in a few minutes.","t":"請繫好安全帶並關掉手機，因為飛機幾分鐘後就要起飛了。","h":1},{"w":"unfasten","p":"v.","d":"to open or undo something that was fastened","c":"解開","s":"Wait until the bus has completely stopped before you unfasten your seat belt and stand up to get off.","t":"等公車完全停下來後，再解開安全帶起身下車。"},{"w":"fastener","p":"n.","d":"a button, zip, or clip used to join things together","c":"扣件；扣子","s":"The fastener on my backpack broke this morning, so all my books fell out onto the floor of the MRT.","t":"我背包的扣子今天早上壞了，所以我所有的書都掉到捷運車廂的地板上。"},{"w":"fatal","p":"adj.","d":"causing death","c":"致命的","s":"Drinking and driving can lead to a fatal accident, so the police stop cars every weekend to check drivers.","t":"酒後駕車可能導致致命的意外，所以警察每個週末都攔車檢查駕駛人。","h":1},{"w":"fatal","p":"adj.","d":"causing complete failure","c":"致命的；毀滅性的（錯誤）","s":"Forgetting to save the file was a fatal mistake, because the computer crashed and three hours of work disappeared.","t":"忘了存檔是個致命的錯誤，因為電腦當機，三小時的工作全部消失了。"},{"w":"fatally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that causes death","c":"致命地","s":"Two people were fatally injured in the fire last night, and several others are still in the hospital.","t":"昨晚的火災中有兩人受了致命傷，另有數人仍在醫院。"},{"w":"fate","p":"n.","d":"the things that will happen to a person; destiny","c":"命運","s":"Nobody knows what fate has planned for us, so we should enjoy every day and be kind to the people around us.","t":"沒有人知道命運為我們安排了什麼，所以我們應該享受每一天，善待身邊的人。"},{"w":"favorable","p":"adj.","d":"good and helpful; showing approval","c":"有利的；贊同的","s":"The weather report is favorable for Saturday, so the school sports day will go ahead as planned on the playground.","t":"星期六的天氣預報是有利的，所以學校運動會將按計畫在操場舉行。","h":1},{"w":"do sb a favor","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something kind to help someone","c":"幫某人一個忙","s":"Could you do me a favor and water my plants while I am away next week? I will bring you a gift from Japan.","t":"下週我不在時，你能幫我一個忙幫我的植物澆水嗎？我會從日本帶禮物給你。","a":"do me a favor"},{"w":"in favor of","p":"phr.","d":"supporting an idea or plan","c":"支持；贊成","s":"Most students voted in favor of having a longer lunch break, so the school will try the new schedule next month.","t":"大多數學生投票贊成延長午休時間，所以學校下個月會試行新的時間表。"},{"w":"favorite","p":"adj.","d":"liked more than any other","c":"最喜愛的","s":"Chocolate ice cream has been my favorite dessert since I was a little child, and I still order it every summer.","t":"巧克力冰淇淋從我小時候起就是我最喜愛的甜點，我現在每年夏天還是會點。"},{"w":"unfavorable","p":"adj.","d":"not good or helpful","c":"不利的","s":"Because of unfavorable weather conditions, the ferry to Green Island was canceled, and all the tourists had to wait another day.","t":"由於天氣狀況不利，前往綠島的渡輪被取消，所有遊客必須再等一天。"},{"w":"fax","p":"n.","d":"a copy of a document sent through a phone line","c":"傳真","s":"Although email is faster, some old offices still send important documents by fax because they need a signed copy.","t":"雖然電子郵件比較快，但有些老舊的辦公室仍用傳真寄送重要文件，因為他們需要有簽名的副本。","h":1},{"w":"fax","p":"v.","d":"to send a document by fax","c":"傳真","s":"Please fax the signed form to our office before Friday, or your application for the course cannot be accepted.","t":"請在星期五前把簽好的表格傳真到我們辦公室，否則你的課程申請無法受理。"},{"w":"fax machine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine that sends and receives faxes","c":"傳真機","s":"The fax machine in the teachers' office is so old that it takes five minutes to send a single page.","t":"教師辦公室的傳真機太舊了，寄一頁要花五分鐘。"},{"w":"feast","p":"n.","d":"a large special meal for many people","c":"盛宴；大餐","s":"On Chinese New Year's Eve, my grandmother prepares a huge feast with fish, chicken, dumplings, and at least ten other dishes.","t":"除夕夜，奶奶會準備一頓有魚、雞、水餃和至少十道其他菜的豐盛大餐。","h":1},{"w":"feast","p":"v.","d":"to eat a lot of good food with enjoyment","c":"盡情享用；大吃","s":"After the long hike, the hungry students feasted on fried chicken and pizza until not a single piece was left.","t":"長途健行後，飢餓的學生們大吃炸雞和披薩，直到一塊都不剩。","a":"feasted"},{"w":"a feast for the eyes","p":"n.phr.","d":"something very beautiful to look at","c":"視覺盛宴","s":"The fireworks over the river were a feast for the eyes, and thousands of people stood on the bridge taking photos.","t":"河上的煙火是一場視覺盛宴，數千人站在橋上拍照。"},{"w":"feedback","p":"n.","d":"comments about how well someone has done something","c":"回饋意見","s":"The teacher gave us helpful feedback on our speeches, and she told me to speak more slowly and look at the audience.","t":"老師針對我們的演講給了有用的回饋，她告訴我要說慢一點並看著觀眾。","h":1},{"w":"give feedback","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell someone what you think about their work","c":"給予回饋","s":"Customers can give feedback on the new menu by scanning the QR code on the table, and the restaurant reads every comment.","t":"顧客可以掃描桌上的 QR code 對新菜單給予回饋，餐廳會閱讀每一則意見。"},{"w":"feed","p":"v.","d":"to give food to a person or animal","c":"餵","s":"Visitors are not allowed to feed the animals at the zoo because human food can make them very sick.","t":"遊客不可以在動物園餵動物，因為人類的食物可能讓它們生重病。"},{"w":"feed on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to eat a particular food (used of animals)","c":"以…為食","s":"Pandas feed on bamboo almost all day long, eating up to forty kilograms of it every single day.","t":"熊貓幾乎整天都以竹子為食，每天吃掉多達四十公斤。"},{"w":"be fed up with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be tired and annoyed by something","c":"對…感到厭煩；受夠了","s":"I am fed up with the noise from the construction site next door, so I have decided to study at the library instead.","t":"我受夠了隔壁工地的噪音，所以決定改到圖書館讀書。","a":"am fed up with"},{"w":"ferry","p":"n.","d":"a boat that carries people and cars across water regularly","c":"渡輪","s":"We took the ferry from Donggang to Little Liuqiu, and the trip across the sea took about twenty-five minutes.","t":"我們從東港搭渡輪到小琉球，橫越海面的航程大約二十五分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"ferry","p":"v.","d":"to carry people or things between two places","c":"運送；渡運","s":"Small boats ferry tourists between the islands every hour, so you do not need to book a ticket in advance.","t":"小船每小時在島與島之間運送遊客，所以你不需要事先訂票。"},{"w":"ferry terminal","p":"n.phr.","d":"the building where ferries leave and arrive","c":"渡輪碼頭","s":"The ferry terminal was crowded with families on the holiday morning, and the line for tickets went all the way out the door.","t":"假日早上渡輪碼頭擠滿了全家出遊的人，買票的隊伍一直排到門外。"},{"w":"fertile","p":"adj.","d":"(of land) good for growing plants","c":"肥沃的","s":"The land near the river is very fertile, so farmers there can grow rice, vegetables, and fruit all year round.","t":"河邊的土地非常肥沃，所以那裡的農民一年四季都能種稻米、蔬菜和水果。","h":1},{"w":"fertile","p":"adj.","d":"able to produce many new ideas","c":"豐富的（想像力）；富有創造力的","s":"She has a fertile imagination and can turn an ordinary trip to the supermarket into an exciting adventure story.","t":"她有豐富的想像力，能把一趟普通的超市之旅變成刺激的冒險故事。"},{"w":"fertilizer","p":"n.","d":"a substance put on land to help plants grow","c":"肥料","s":"My grandfather adds natural fertilizer made from leaves and vegetable waste to his garden instead of buying chemicals.","t":"我爺爺在菜園裡加入用樹葉和蔬菜廢料做的天然肥料，而不是購買化學藥品。"},{"w":"fertility","p":"n.","d":"the ability of land to grow plants well","c":"肥沃度；生育力","s":"Volcanic ash improves the fertility of the soil, which is why so many farms are found near Indonesia's volcanoes.","t":"火山灰能提高土壤的肥沃度，這就是為什麼印尼火山附近有這麼多農場。"},{"w":"fetch","p":"v.","d":"to go and get something and bring it back","c":"拿來；取回","s":"Could you fetch me a glass of water from the kitchen? I have a terrible headache and do not want to stand up.","t":"你能從廚房拿一杯水給我嗎？我頭痛得厲害，不想站起來。","h":1},{"w":"fetch","p":"v.","d":"to be sold for a particular price","c":"賣得（某價格）","s":"The old painting is expected to fetch more than one million dollars at the auction next month in Hong Kong.","t":"這幅舊畫預計在下個月香港的拍賣會上能賣得超過一百萬元。"},{"w":"play fetch","p":"v.phr.","d":"to throw a stick or ball for a dog to bring back","c":"玩你丟我撿","s":"Every morning in the park, the little boy plays fetch with his dog, who never gets tired of running after the ball.","t":"每天早上在公園，小男孩都和他的狗玩你丟我撿，那隻狗永遠不會厭倦追球。","a":"plays fetch"},{"w":"fiction","p":"n.","d":"books and stories about imaginary people and events","c":"小說；虛構作品","s":"My sister reads mostly fiction, but I prefer true stories about real people, science, and history.","t":"我姐姐大多讀小說，但我比較喜歡關於真實人物、科學和歷史的真實故事。","h":1},{"w":"science fiction","p":"n.phr.","d":"stories about the future, space, and imaginary science","c":"科幻小說","s":"Science fiction movies about robots and space travel were popular long before people actually landed on the moon.","t":"關於機器人和太空旅行的科幻電影，早在人類真正登陸月球之前就很受歡迎。","a":"Science fiction"},{"w":"fictional","p":"adj.","d":"imaginary; not real","c":"虛構的","s":"Sherlock Holmes is a fictional detective, but so many fans write to him that London has an office to answer the letters.","t":"福爾摩斯是一位虛構的偵探，但寫信給他的粉絲太多了，倫敦還有一間辦公室回覆這些信。"},{"w":"nonfiction","p":"n.","d":"books about real facts, events, and people","c":"非小說類作品","s":"The library moved all the nonfiction books about animals and science to the second floor, where there is more space.","t":"圖書館把所有關於動物和科學的非小說類書籍移到二樓，那裡空間比較大。"},{"w":"fierce","p":"adj.","d":"very angry and violent; likely to attack","c":"兇猛的","s":"Do not go near that dog because it looks fierce and has already bitten two people in our neighborhood this year.","t":"不要靠近那隻狗，因為它看起來很兇猛，今年已經咬了我們社區兩個人。","h":1},{"w":"fierce","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or intense","c":"激烈的；猛烈的","s":"There is fierce competition for places at the top universities, so students start preparing for the exam years in advance.","t":"頂尖大學的入學競爭很激烈，所以學生好幾年前就開始準備考試。"},{"w":"fiercely","p":"adv.","d":"in a very strong or violent way","c":"激烈地；猛烈地","s":"The two teams fought fiercely for the championship, and the final score was decided in the last ten seconds.","t":"兩隊為了冠軍激烈地奮戰，最後比數在最後十秒才決定。"},{"w":"finance","p":"n.","d":"the management of money, especially by governments or companies","c":"金融；財務","s":"She studied finance at university and now works in a bank, helping companies decide how to spend their money wisely.","t":"她在大學讀金融，現在在銀行工作，幫助公司決定如何明智地花錢。","h":1},{"w":"finances","p":"n.","d":"the money a person or organization has","c":"財務狀況；資金","s":"After losing his job, he had to look carefully at his finances and stop eating out at restaurants every weekend.","t":"失業後，他必須仔細檢視自己的財務狀況，不再每個週末上餐廳吃飯。"},{"w":"finance","p":"v.","d":"to provide money for something","c":"提供資金；資助","s":"The city will finance the new library with money from a special tax, so the building should be finished in two years.","t":"市政府將用一項特別稅收資助新圖書館，所以建築應該兩年內完工。"},{"w":"financial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with money","c":"財務的；金融的","s":"Many families had financial problems during the pandemic because shops closed and parents could not go to work.","t":"疫情期間許多家庭有財務問題，因為商店關門，父母無法去上班。"},{"w":"financially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with money","c":"在財務上；經濟上","s":"Although she is only twenty-two, she is already financially independent and pays all her own bills without help from her parents.","t":"雖然她才二十二歲，但已經經濟上獨立，不需父母幫忙就能自己付所有帳單。"}]},{"unit":17,"theme":"financial – frustrate","cards":[{"w":"financial","p":"adj.","d":"connected with money","c":"財務的；金融的","s":"Many young couples have financial problems in their first year of marriage because they spend more than they earn.","t":"許多年輕夫妻在結婚第一年會有財務問題，因為他們花的比賺的多。","h":1},{"w":"finance","p":"n.","d":"the management of money by companies, banks, or governments","c":"金融；財務","s":"He works in finance, so he spends his days helping companies decide where to invest their money safely.","t":"他從事金融業，所以他每天都在幫公司決定該把錢安全地投資在哪裡。"},{"w":"financially","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with money","c":"在財務上；經濟上","s":"After she got her first full-time job, she became financially independent and moved out of her parents' house.","t":"找到第一份全職工作後，她在經濟上變得獨立，搬出了父母的家。"},{"w":"financial crisis","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when banks and businesses suddenly lose a lot of money","c":"金融危機","s":"During the financial crisis of 2008, many banks lost huge amounts of money, and thousands of people lost their jobs.","t":"在2008年的金融危機期間，許多銀行損失了大量金錢，數千人失去工作。"},{"w":"fireplace","p":"n.","d":"a place in a wall of a room where a fire is made","c":"壁爐","s":"On cold winter nights, the whole family sits around the fireplace in the living room and drinks hot chocolate together.","t":"在寒冷的冬夜，全家人會圍坐在客廳的壁爐旁一起喝熱巧克力。","h":1},{"w":"fire","p":"n.","d":"flames and heat that burn things","c":"火；火災","s":"The fire started in the kitchen when nobody was watching the stove, and it spread to the whole house in minutes.","t":"火是在沒人看著爐子時從廚房燒起來的，幾分鐘內就蔓延到整棟房子。"},{"w":"catch fire","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start burning","c":"著火","s":"Dry leaves can catch fire very easily in summer, so you should never throw a cigarette out of the car window.","t":"乾燥的樹葉在夏天很容易著火，所以你絕對不能把香菸丟出車窗。"},{"w":"fireworks","p":"n.","d":"things that explode in the sky with colored lights and loud noises","c":"煙火","s":"Thousands of people gathered by the river on New Year's Eve to watch the fireworks light up the night sky.","t":"除夕夜，數千人聚集在河邊觀看煙火照亮夜空。"},{"w":"flatter","p":"v.","d":"to praise someone too much because you want something from them","c":"奉承；諂媚","s":"Some salespeople flatter their customers by saying how smart they look, hoping that they will buy more expensive clothes.","t":"有些售貨員會奉承顧客，說他們看起來多麼有型，希望他們買更貴的衣服。","h":1},{"w":"flattery","p":"n.","d":"praise that is not sincere","c":"奉承話；諂媚","s":"Do not believe everything he says about your singing, because his flattery is only a way to borrow money from you.","t":"別相信他對你歌聲的每一句話，因為他的奉承只是為了向你借錢。"},{"w":"flattering","p":"adj.","d":"making someone look or seem better than usual","c":"使人顯得好看的；討好的","s":"That blue dress is very flattering; it makes you look taller and goes perfectly with the color of your eyes.","t":"那件藍色洋裝非常襯你，它讓你看起來更高，也和你的眼睛顏色很搭。"},{"w":"be flattered","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel pleased because someone praised you","c":"感到受寵若驚","s":"I was flattered when the famous writer said she had read my short story and enjoyed it very much.","t":"當那位知名作家說她讀過我的短篇故事而且非常喜歡時，我受寵若驚。","a":"was flattered"},{"w":"flea","p":"n.","d":"a very small jumping insect that bites animals and people","c":"跳蚤","s":"Our dog kept scratching his ears all night, and in the morning we found a tiny flea jumping on his bed.","t":"我們的狗整晚一直抓耳朵，早上我們在牠的床上發現一隻小跳蚤在跳。","h":1},{"w":"flea market","p":"n.phr.","d":"an outdoor market that sells old or used things cheaply","c":"跳蚤市場","s":"Every Sunday morning, my mother and I visit the flea market near the river to look for old books and cheap furniture.","t":"每個星期天早上，我和媽媽會去河邊的跳蚤市場找舊書和便宜的家具。"},{"w":"have fleas","p":"v.phr.","d":"(of an animal) to be covered with fleas","c":"長跳蚤","s":"Our cat has fleas again, so we have to wash her bed and give her the medicine from the vet.","t":"我們的貓又長跳蚤了，所以我們得洗她的床並給她吃獸醫開的藥。","a":"has fleas"},{"w":"flee, fled, fled","p":"v.","d":"to run away from danger","c":"逃跑；逃離","s":"When the fire alarm rang, hundreds of shoppers tried to flee the building through the same narrow exit at once.","t":"火警警報響起時，數百名購物者試圖同時從同一個狹窄出口逃離大樓。","a":"flee","h":1},{"w":"flee from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to run away from a person, place, or danger","c":"從…逃走","s":"The deer fled from the hunters and hid in the deep forest, where the thick trees kept it safe until night.","t":"那隻鹿逃離獵人，躲進深林裡，茂密的樹木讓牠安全直到夜晚。","a":"fled from"},{"w":"flee the country","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave your country quickly to escape danger","c":"逃離國家；出逃","s":"After the war began, many families fled the country with only the clothes they were wearing and a few photos.","t":"戰爭開始後，許多家庭只帶著身上穿的衣服和幾張照片就逃離國家。","a":"fled the country"},{"w":"flexible","p":"adj.","d":"able to change easily to suit new situations","c":"有彈性的；可變通的","s":"My new job has flexible hours, so I can start at ten and leave at six whenever I need to.","t":"我的新工作時間很有彈性，所以我需要時可以十點上班六點下班。","h":1},{"w":"flexible","p":"adj.","d":"able to bend easily without breaking","c":"柔軟的；易彎曲的","s":"Yoga keeps my body flexible, and after six months of practice I can finally touch my toes without bending my knees.","t":"瑜珈讓我的身體保持柔軟，練習六個月後我終於可以不彎膝蓋就摸到腳趾。"},{"w":"flexibility","p":"n.","d":"the ability to change or bend easily","c":"彈性；靈活性","s":"The company offers its workers a lot of flexibility, including the choice to work from home two days every week.","t":"這家公司給員工很大的彈性，包括每週可以選擇在家工作兩天。"},{"w":"inflexible","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to change","c":"死板的；不知變通的","s":"The old manager was so inflexible that he refused to change the meeting time even when half the team could not come.","t":"那位老經理非常死板，即使團隊一半的人不能來，他也拒絕更改會議時間。"},{"w":"flex","p":"v.","d":"to bend or tighten a part of your body","c":"彎曲；活動（肌肉）","s":"Before the race, the runners flexed their legs and arms to warm up their muscles and avoid getting hurt.","t":"比賽前，跑者們活動腿部和手臂的肌肉來熱身，以免受傷。","a":"flexed"},{"w":"fluent","p":"adj.","d":"able to speak a language easily and well","c":"流利的","s":"After living in Japan for three years, she became fluent in Japanese and could even understand jokes on TV.","t":"在日本住了三年後，她的日語變得很流利，甚至能聽懂電視上的笑話。","h":1},{"w":"fluently","p":"adv.","d":"in a smooth and easy way","c":"流利地","s":"He speaks English fluently because his mother is from Canada and they have always talked in English at home.","t":"他英語說得很流利，因為他媽媽來自加拿大，他們在家一直用英語交談。"},{"w":"fluency","p":"n.","d":"the ability to speak a language easily and well","c":"流利；流暢度","s":"The best way to build fluency in a foreign language is to talk with native speakers every day, even if you make mistakes.","t":"培養外語流利度最好的方法是每天和母語人士交談，即使你會犯錯。"},{"w":"be fluent in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak a language very well","c":"精通（某語言）","s":"Our tour guide is fluent in four languages, so she could answer questions from the Korean, French, and Thai visitors easily.","t":"我們的導遊精通四種語言，所以她能輕鬆回答韓國、法國和泰國遊客的問題。","a":"is fluent in"},{"w":"flush","p":"v.","d":"to clean a toilet by making water run through it","c":"沖水","s":"Please remember to flush the toilet after you use it, and wash your hands with soap for at least twenty seconds.","t":"請記得使用馬桶後要沖水，並用肥皂洗手至少二十秒。","h":1},{"w":"flush","p":"v.","d":"to become red in the face","c":"臉紅","s":"Her cheeks began to flush when the teacher praised her essay in front of the whole class.","t":"當老師在全班面前稱讚她的作文時，她的臉頰開始泛紅。"},{"w":"flush","p":"n.","d":"a red color that appears on the face","c":"紅暈","s":"A flush of excitement spread across his face when he saw his name at the top of the list of winners.","t":"當他看到自己的名字在得獎名單最上面時，一股興奮的紅暈掠過他的臉。"},{"w":"flushed","p":"adj.","d":"red in the face","c":"臉紅的","s":"After running up ten floors because the elevator was broken, she arrived at the office flushed and out of breath.","t":"因為電梯壞了，她爬了十層樓後滿臉通紅、上氣不接下氣地到達辦公室。"},{"w":"foam","p":"n.","d":"a mass of small bubbles on top of a liquid","c":"泡沫","s":"When you pour the soda too fast, white foam rises to the top of the glass and spills over the side.","t":"當你倒汽水倒得太快，白色的泡沫會升到杯子頂端並溢出來。","h":1},{"w":"foam","p":"v.","d":"to produce a mass of small bubbles","c":"起泡沫","s":"The waves foam and crash against the rocks during a typhoon, and nobody is allowed to walk along the beach.","t":"颱風期間海浪起泡拍打岩石，沒有人可以在海灘上行走。"},{"w":"foam mattress","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soft bed made of light rubber-like material","c":"泡棉床墊","s":"My back stopped hurting after I bought a foam mattress, because it is much softer than the old wooden bed.","t":"買了泡棉床墊後我的背就不痛了，因為它比舊木床軟得多。"},{"w":"foamy","p":"adj.","d":"full of small bubbles","c":"起泡的；泡沫狀的","s":"The barista made a cup of foamy milk for my coffee, and she drew a little heart on top of it.","t":"咖啡師為我的咖啡做了一杯起泡的牛奶，還在上面畫了一個小愛心。"},{"w":"forbid, forbade, forbidden","p":"v.","d":"to order someone not to do something","c":"禁止","s":"The school rules forbid students from using phones during class, so everyone must keep them in their bags.","t":"校規禁止學生上課使用手機，所以每個人都必須把手機放在包包裡。","a":"forbid","h":1},{"w":"forbidden","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed","c":"被禁止的","s":"Smoking is forbidden in all restaurants in Taiwan, and anyone who breaks the rule can be fined up to ten thousand dollars.","t":"台灣所有餐廳都禁止吸菸，任何違規的人可被罰款最高一萬元。"},{"w":"forbid sb to do","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell someone that they must not do something","c":"禁止某人做…","s":"My parents forbid me to ride a scooter until I turn eighteen, even though most of my classmates already have one.","t":"我父母禁止我騎機車直到我滿十八歲，雖然我大多數同學已經有機車了。","a":"forbid me to"},{"w":"forecast","p":"n.","d":"a statement about what will probably happen, especially the weather","c":"預報；預測","s":"According to the weather forecast, it will rain heavily this weekend, so we should move the picnic to next Saturday.","t":"根據天氣預報，這個週末會下大雨，所以我們應該把野餐改到下星期六。","h":1},{"w":"forecast","p":"v.","d":"to say what will probably happen in the future","c":"預測；預報","s":"Experts forecast that the price of rice will rise next year because the dry weather has damaged many farms.","t":"專家預測明年米價會上漲，因為乾旱的天氣損害了許多農田。"},{"w":"weather forecast","p":"n.phr.","d":"a report that says what the weather will be like","c":"天氣預報","s":"I always check the weather forecast on my phone before I leave home, so I know whether to bring an umbrella.","t":"我出門前總是用手機查看天氣預報，這樣就知道要不要帶傘。"},{"w":"forecaster","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to say what the weather will be like","c":"氣象預報員","s":"The TV forecaster warned that the typhoon would reach the east coast by Thursday night, so schools decided to close early.","t":"電視氣象預報員警告颱風會在星期四晚上抵達東岸，所以學校決定提早放學。"},{"w":"formation","p":"n.","d":"the process of starting or making something","c":"形成；組成","s":"The formation of a new volcano under the sea surprised scientists, who are now watching the area with special cameras.","t":"海底新火山的形成讓科學家們感到驚訝，他們現在正用特殊相機監視那個區域。","h":1},{"w":"formation","p":"n.","d":"the way a group of people or things is arranged","c":"隊形；排列","s":"The birds flew south in a V-shaped formation, with the strongest bird at the front to break the wind.","t":"鳥群以 V 字隊形向南飛，最強壯的鳥在前面擋風。"},{"w":"form","p":"v.","d":"to make or start something; to arrange into a shape","c":"形成；組成；排成","s":"Please form a line at the door and wait quietly until the teacher tells you to enter the classroom.","t":"請在門口排成一列，安靜等候直到老師叫你們進教室。"},{"w":"form","p":"n.","d":"a paper with spaces for writing information","c":"表格","s":"To join the library, you need to fill in this form with your name, address, and phone number.","t":"要加入圖書館，你需要在這張表格填寫姓名、地址和電話號碼。"},{"w":"formal","p":"adj.","d":"following official rules; serious and polite","c":"正式的","s":"You should wear a suit to the wedding because it is a formal event, and jeans would not be acceptable.","t":"你應該穿西裝去婚禮，因為那是個正式的場合，牛仔褲是不被接受的。"},{"w":"informal","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and friendly; not official","c":"非正式的","s":"The meeting with the new teacher was quite informal, so we just sat on the grass and chatted about our hobbies.","t":"和新老師的見面相當非正式，所以我們只是坐在草地上聊聊我們的嗜好。"},{"w":"formula","p":"n.","d":"a rule written with numbers and letters in math or science","c":"公式","s":"Our math teacher gave us a simple formula to find the area of a circle, and now the homework takes only ten minutes.","t":"數學老師給我們一個簡單的公式來計算圓面積，現在作業只要十分鐘就能完成。","h":1},{"w":"formula for success","p":"n.phr.","d":"a way of doing things that leads to success","c":"成功的公式／方法","s":"Hard work, good sleep, and a little luck are her formula for success, she told the students at graduation.","t":"她在畢業典禮上告訴學生，努力、充足的睡眠和一點運氣是她的成功公式。"},{"w":"formulate","p":"v.","d":"to make a plan or idea carefully","c":"制定；構想","s":"The government is trying to formulate a plan to help poor families pay their electricity bills during the hot summer.","t":"政府正試圖制定一項計畫，幫助貧困家庭在炎熱的夏天支付電費。"},{"w":"fort","p":"n.","d":"a strong building used by soldiers to protect a place","c":"堡壘；要塞","s":"The old fort on the hill was built by the Dutch four hundred years ago to protect the harbor from enemy ships.","t":"山丘上的古老堡壘是荷蘭人四百年前建造的，用來保護港口不受敵船攻擊。","h":1},{"w":"fortress","p":"n.","d":"a large strong building or town that is hard to attack","c":"要塞；堡壘","s":"The castle looks like a fortress, with thick stone walls, small windows, and a deep ditch filled with water around it.","t":"這座城堡看起來像一座要塞，有厚厚的石牆、小窗戶，周圍還有一條裝滿水的深溝。"},{"w":"fortify","p":"v.","d":"to make a place stronger against attack","c":"加固；設防","s":"The soldiers worked all night to fortify the town with high walls before the enemy army arrived the next morning.","t":"士兵們徹夜工作，在敵軍隔天早上抵達前用高牆加固城鎮。"},{"w":"fortunate","p":"adj.","d":"lucky","c":"幸運的","s":"We were very fortunate to find a hotel room at the last minute, because the whole town was full of tourists for the festival.","t":"我們非常幸運能在最後一刻找到飯店房間，因為整個小鎮都擠滿了來參加節慶的遊客。","h":1},{"w":"fortunately","p":"adv.","d":"luckily","c":"幸運地；幸好","s":"Fortunately, nobody was hurt when the tree fell on the car, because the family had gone into the shop a minute earlier.","t":"幸運的是，樹倒在車上時沒有人受傷，因為那家人一分鐘前走進了商店。","a":"Fortunately"},{"w":"unfortunately","p":"adv.","d":"unluckily; sadly","c":"不幸地；遺憾地","s":"Unfortunately, the concert tickets were sold out in ten minutes, so we will have to watch the show online instead.","t":"不幸的是，演唱會門票在十分鐘內就賣完了，所以我們只好改在線上看表演。","a":"Unfortunately"},{"w":"fortune","p":"n.","d":"luck; a very large amount of money","c":"運氣；財富","s":"I had the good fortune to sit next to a kind old man on the train, and he told me many stories about the city.","t":"我很幸運在火車上坐在一位和善的老先生旁邊，他告訴我許多關於這座城市的故事。"},{"w":"make a fortune","p":"v.phr.","d":"to earn a very large amount of money","c":"賺大錢；發財","s":"He made a fortune by selling bubble tea in Europe, and now he owns more than fifty shops in ten countries.","t":"他靠在歐洲賣珍珠奶茶賺了一大筆錢，現在在十個國家擁有超過五十家店。","a":"made a fortune"},{"w":"misfortune","p":"n.","d":"bad luck; an unlucky event","c":"不幸","s":"It was a great misfortune that the family lost their house in the fire just two weeks before Chinese New Year.","t":"那家人在農曆新年前兩週因火災失去房子，真是一大不幸。"},{"w":"fossil","p":"n.","d":"the remains of a very old plant or animal kept in rock","c":"化石","s":"The children found a fossil of a small fish in the rock, and the museum said it was over one hundred million years old.","t":"孩子們在岩石裡發現一個小魚的化石，博物館說它有超過一億年的歷史。","h":1},{"w":"fossil fuel","p":"n.phr.","d":"coal, oil, or gas formed from dead plants and animals long ago","c":"化石燃料","s":"Burning fossil fuels such as coal and oil puts a lot of carbon dioxide into the air, which makes the earth warmer.","t":"燃燒像煤和石油這樣的化石燃料會把大量二氧化碳排入空氣中，使地球變暖。","a":"fossil fuels"},{"w":"fossilized","p":"adj.","d":"turned into a fossil","c":"化石化的","s":"Scientists discovered fossilized footprints of a dinosaur in the dry riverbed, and each one was bigger than a car tire.","t":"科學家在乾涸的河床上發現了恐龍的化石化的腳印，每一個都比汽車輪胎還大。"},{"w":"foundation","p":"n.","d":"the strong base under a building","c":"地基；基礎","s":"Workers spent two months building a strong foundation for the tower, because the ground near the river is soft and wet.","t":"工人花了兩個月為這座塔建造堅固的地基，因為河邊的地面又軟又濕。","h":1},{"w":"founder","p":"n.","d":"a person who starts a company, school, or organization","c":"創辦人","s":"The founder of the company started it in his garage thirty years ago with only two friends and one old computer.","t":"這家公司的創辦人三十年前只和兩個朋友及一台舊電腦在他的車庫裡創業。","h":1},{"w":"foundation","p":"n.","d":"an organization that gives money to help people","c":"基金會","s":"The foundation gives money to poor students every year so that they can finish high school and go to university.","t":"這個基金會每年提供經費給貧困學生，讓他們能完成高中學業並上大學。"},{"w":"found, founded, founded","p":"v.","d":"to start a company, school, or organization","c":"創立；建立","s":"The school was founded in 1920 by a group of teachers who believed that every girl deserved a good education.","t":"這所學校是在1920年由一群相信每個女孩都應該受良好教育的老師所創立的。","a":"founded"},{"w":"lay the foundation for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to prepare the base that makes later success possible","c":"為…奠定基礎","s":"Learning to read early can lay the foundation for success in every other school subject, so parents should read with their children.","t":"早期學會閱讀能為其他每一門學科的成功奠定基礎，所以父母應該和孩子一起閱讀。"},{"w":"fragile","p":"adj.","d":"easily broken or damaged","c":"易碎的","s":"Please be careful with that box because the glasses inside are very fragile and will break if you drop it.","t":"請小心那個箱子，因為裡面的玻璃杯非常易碎，掉下去就會破。","h":1},{"w":"fragile","p":"adj.","d":"weak and easily harmed","c":"脆弱的（健康、關係）","s":"After the long illness, my grandfather's health is still fragile, so the doctor told him to rest for another month.","t":"久病之後，我爺爺的健康仍然很脆弱，所以醫生要他再休息一個月。"},{"w":"fragility","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being easily broken or harmed","c":"脆弱性；易碎性","s":"The fragility of the old painting means it cannot be moved, so visitors must travel to the small museum to see it.","t":"這幅古畫的脆弱性意味著它不能被移動，所以參觀者必須前往那座小博物館才能看到它。"},{"w":"frame","p":"n.","d":"the hard structure that holds or supports something","c":"框架；車架；骨架","s":"The bicycle has a light aluminum frame, so even a small child can lift it and carry it up the stairs.","t":"這台腳踏車有輕巧的鋁合金車架，所以連小孩也能抬起來搬上樓梯。","h":1},{"w":"frame","p":"v.","d":"to put a picture inside a frame","c":"裱框；加框","s":"She decided to frame the photo of her grandparents' wedding and hang it on the wall in the living room.","t":"她決定把祖父母婚禮的照片裱框，掛在客廳的牆上。"},{"w":"picture frame","p":"n.phr.","d":"a border that holds a picture or photo","c":"相框","s":"I bought a wooden picture frame at the night market for my mother's birthday and put our family photo inside it.","t":"我在夜市買了一個木製相框當媽媽的生日禮物，並把我們的全家福放進去。"},{"w":"framework","p":"n.","d":"a set of ideas or rules used to plan something","c":"架構；框架","s":"The teacher gave us a clear framework for the essay, with one paragraph for each of the three main ideas.","t":"老師給了我們一個清楚的作文架構，三個主要想法各寫一段。"},{"w":"frame of mind","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way you feel at a particular time","c":"心境；心情","s":"You should not make big decisions when you are in an angry frame of mind; wait until tomorrow and think again calmly.","t":"你不應該在生氣的心境下做重大決定；等到明天再冷靜地想一想。"},{"w":"frequency","p":"n.","d":"how often something happens","c":"頻率；次數","s":"The frequency of buses on this route has increased, so now there is one every five minutes during rush hour.","t":"這條路線公車的班次頻率增加了，現在尖峰時段每五分鐘就有一班。","h":1},{"w":"frequent","p":"adj.","d":"happening often","c":"頻繁的；經常的","s":"Heavy rain is frequent in Taipei during May and June, so most people carry an umbrella with them every day.","t":"五、六月台北經常下大雨，所以大多數人每天都隨身帶著雨傘。"},{"w":"frequently","p":"adv.","d":"often","c":"經常地","s":"My grandmother frequently forgets where she put her glasses, so we bought her a chain to hang them around her neck.","t":"我奶奶經常忘記眼鏡放在哪裡，所以我們買了一條鍊子讓她掛在脖子上。"},{"w":"infrequent","p":"adj.","d":"not happening often","c":"不常發生的；稀少的","s":"Trains to the small mountain village are infrequent, with only two in the morning and one in the late afternoon.","t":"到那個山區小村的火車班次很少，早上只有兩班，傍晚一班。"},{"w":"freshman","p":"n.","d":"a student in the first year of high school or university","c":"新生；一年級學生","s":"As a freshman at the university, he found it hard to make friends until he joined the hiking club in October.","t":"身為大學新生，他覺得很難交到朋友，直到十月加入登山社。","h":1},{"w":"fresh","p":"adj.","d":"new; recently made, picked, or caught","c":"新鮮的","s":"My mother goes to the market early every morning because the vegetables and fish are fresh and cheaper at that time.","t":"我媽媽每天一早就去市場，因為那時蔬菜和魚比較新鮮也比較便宜。"},{"w":"freshly","p":"adv.","d":"recently; just now","c":"剛剛；新近","s":"There is nothing better than the smell of freshly baked bread coming from the bakery on a cold morning.","t":"在寒冷的早晨，沒有什麼比得上從麵包店飄來剛出爐麵包的香味。"},{"w":"refresh","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel less tired or less hot","c":"使恢復精神；使清爽","s":"A cold shower will refresh you after the long hike, and then we can go out for dinner at the night market.","t":"長途健行後沖個冷水澡會讓你恢復精神，然後我們可以去夜市吃晚餐。"},{"w":"frost","p":"n.","d":"a thin white layer of ice that forms when it is very cold","c":"霜","s":"When we woke up in the mountains, there was white frost on the grass, and the car windows were covered with ice.","t":"我們在山上醒來時，草地上有白色的霜，車窗也覆蓋著冰。","h":1},{"w":"frosty","p":"adj.","d":"very cold, with frost","c":"結霜的；嚴寒的","s":"It was a frosty morning in January, so the children put on their thick coats and gloves before walking to school.","t":"那是一月一個結霜的早晨，所以孩子們走路上學前穿上了厚外套和手套。"},{"w":"frostbite","p":"n.","d":"damage to fingers, toes, or ears caused by extreme cold","c":"凍傷","s":"Climbers must cover their fingers and ears on high mountains, because frostbite can damage the skin in less than an hour.","t":"登山者在高山上必須遮住手指和耳朵，因為凍傷可能在不到一小時內傷害皮膚。"},{"w":"defrost","p":"v.","d":"to let frozen food become soft again","c":"解凍","s":"Take the chicken out of the freezer in the morning so it can defrost before you cook it for dinner.","t":"早上把雞肉從冷凍庫拿出來，這樣它在你煮晚餐前就能解凍。"},{"w":"frown","p":"v.","d":"to make an angry or unhappy face by moving your eyebrows together","c":"皺眉","s":"The teacher began to frown when she saw that half the class had not finished the homework she gave last week.","t":"老師看到班上一半的人沒完成她上週出的作業時開始皺眉。","h":1},{"w":"frown","p":"n.","d":"an angry or unhappy look on the face","c":"皺眉；不悅的表情","s":"He read the letter with a deep frown on his face, and we knew at once that the news was not good.","t":"他臉上帶著深深的皺眉讀那封信，我們立刻知道消息不好。"},{"w":"frown on/upon","p":"v.phr.","d":"to disapprove of something","c":"不贊成；反對","s":"Many older people frown on eating on the MRT, even though there is no rule against it in some cities.","t":"許多年長的人不贊成在捷運上吃東西，雖然有些城市並沒有禁止的規定。","a":"frown on"},{"w":"frustrate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel annoyed because they cannot do what they want","c":"使挫折；使沮喪","s":"Slow internet can really frustrate students who are trying to upload their homework before the midnight deadline.","t":"緩慢的網路真的會讓想在午夜截止前上傳作業的學生感到挫折。","h":1},{"w":"frustrated","p":"adj.","d":"feeling annoyed because you cannot do what you want","c":"感到挫折的；沮喪的","s":"I felt so frustrated when the computer crashed for the third time that I almost threw it out of the window.","t":"當電腦第三次當機時，我沮喪到幾乎想把它丟出窗外。"},{"w":"frustrating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel annoyed and helpless","c":"令人沮喪的","s":"It is very frustrating to wait forty minutes for a bus and then watch three of them arrive at the same time.","t":"等公車等了四十分鐘，然後看到三輛同時到站，真是令人沮喪。"},{"w":"frustration","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being annoyed because you cannot do something","c":"挫折感","s":"In her frustration, she tore up the drawing she had worked on for hours and started again from the beginning.","t":"在挫折中，她撕掉了花了好幾個小時畫的圖，從頭再來。"}]},{"unit":18,"theme":"frustration – glorious","cards":[{"w":"frustration","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being upset because you cannot do or get something","c":"挫折感；灰心","s":"After trying to fix the printer for an hour without success, Mark finally hit the desk in frustration and went outside for some air.","t":"試了一個小時還是修不好印表機後，馬克終於在挫折感中拍了桌子，走到外面透透氣。","h":1},{"w":"frustrate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone feel upset because they cannot do something","c":"使灰心；使受挫","s":"The slow internet at the hotel began to frustrate the students, who needed to upload their project before the deadline at midnight.","t":"飯店緩慢的網路開始讓學生們感到挫折，他們必須在午夜截止前上傳專題作業。"},{"w":"frustrated","p":"adj.","d":"feeling upset because you cannot do something","c":"感到挫折的；灰心的","s":"I felt so frustrated when the bus left just as I reached the stop, because it was the last one of the night.","t":"當我剛到站牌公車就開走時，我覺得非常挫折，因為那是當晚最後一班車。"},{"w":"frustrating","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel upset or annoyed","c":"令人沮喪的","s":"It is really frustrating to study hard for a test and then forget everything the moment you see the first question.","t":"用功準備考試，卻在看到第一題的那一刻忘光一切，真的令人沮喪。"},{"w":"fulfill","p":"v.","d":"to do what you promised or what is needed; to make a dream come true","c":"履行；實現；達成","s":"Grandpa worked for forty years to fulfill his dream of owning a small farm, and he finally bought one last spring.","t":"爺爺工作了四十年來實現擁有一座小農場的夢想，去年春天他終於買了一座。","h":1},{"w":"fulfillment","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being happy because you achieved something","c":"成就感；滿足；實現","s":"Teaching in a small village school gave her a deep sense of fulfillment that a higher salary in the city never could.","t":"在小村莊的學校教書帶給她一種深深的成就感，那是城市裡更高的薪水永遠無法給予的。"},{"w":"fulfill a promise","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do what you said you would do","c":"履行承諾","s":"My father always says that a good man must fulfill his promise, so he drove three hours to attend my game as he had said.","t":"我爸爸總是說好男人必須履行承諾，所以他如他所說的開了三小時的車來看我的比賽。","a":"fulfill his promise"},{"w":"fulfill the requirements","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have or do everything that is needed","c":"符合要求","s":"Students who want to join the exchange program must fulfill the requirements, including a high English score and a teacher's letter.","t":"想參加交換計畫的學生必須符合要求，包括英文高分和一封老師的推薦信。"},{"w":"fulfilling","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel happy and satisfied","c":"令人滿足的；有意義的","s":"Being a nurse is tiring but very fulfilling, because you can see how your care helps people get better every day.","t":"當護士很累但非常令人滿足，因為你每天都能看到自己的照顧如何幫助人們好起來。"},{"w":"functional","p":"adj.","d":"working properly; made to be useful rather than beautiful","c":"功能性的；可運作的","s":"The old elevator in our building is still functional, but the landlord has promised to replace it with a newer one next year.","t":"我們大樓的舊電梯仍然可以運作，但房東已承諾明年換一台新的。","h":1},{"w":"function","p":"n.","d":"the purpose or job of a thing or person","c":"功能；作用","s":"The main function of the heart is to pump blood around the body, and it does this about one hundred thousand times a day.","t":"心臟的主要功能是把血液輸送到全身，它每天大約做這件事十萬次。"},{"w":"function","p":"v.","d":"to work in the correct way","c":"運作；起作用","s":"My laptop stopped working after I spilled coffee on it, but luckily it began to function again after it dried for two days.","t":"我的筆電在我把咖啡灑在上面後就不能用了，但幸運的是，晾乾兩天後它又開始運作了。"},{"w":"function as","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work or be used as something","c":"當作…使用；充當","s":"When guests come to stay, the sofa in our living room can function as a bed, so nobody has to sleep on the floor.","t":"當有客人來住時，我們客廳的沙發可以當作床使用，所以沒有人需要睡地板。"},{"w":"fundamental","p":"adj.","d":"very basic and important","c":"基本的；根本的","s":"Reading and writing are fundamental skills, so elementary schools spend a lot of time on them before teaching anything else.","t":"讀和寫是基本的技能，所以小學在教其他任何東西之前會花很多時間在這上面。","h":1},{"w":"fundamentals","p":"n.","d":"the most basic and important parts of something","c":"基礎；基本功；基本原理","s":"Before you try to play a whole song on the guitar, you should learn the fundamentals, such as how to hold it and change chords.","t":"在你嘗試用吉他彈完整首歌之前，應該先學會基本功，例如怎麼拿吉他和換和弦。"},{"w":"fundamentally","p":"adv.","d":"in a very basic and important way","c":"根本上；基本上","s":"Although the two phones look similar, they are fundamentally different inside, so their prices are also very different.","t":"雖然這兩支手機看起來相似，但它們內部根本上不同，所以價格也差很多。"},{"w":"fund","p":"n.","d":"an amount of money saved or collected for a special purpose","c":"基金；資金","s":"The students started a fund to help a classmate whose house was damaged in the fire, and they collected 50,000 dollars.","t":"學生們成立了一個基金來幫助一位房子在火災中受損的同學，他們募集了五萬元。"},{"w":"funeral","p":"n.","d":"a ceremony for a person who has died","c":"葬禮；喪禮","s":"Hundreds of people came to the old teacher's funeral to say goodbye, and many of them had been her students fifty years ago.","t":"數百人來到這位老教師的葬禮道別，其中許多人五十年前曾是她的學生。","h":1},{"w":"attend a funeral","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go to the ceremony for a person who has died","c":"參加葬禮","s":"My uncle flew back from Japan to attend the funeral of his best friend, who had passed away suddenly after a short illness.","t":"我叔叔從日本飛回來參加他最好朋友的葬禮，那位朋友在短暫生病後突然過世了。","a":"attend the funeral"},{"w":"funeral home","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where funerals are prepared and held","c":"殯儀館","s":"The family gathered at the funeral home early in the morning to prepare flowers and photos for the ceremony.","t":"家人一早就聚集在殯儀館，為儀式準備花和照片。"},{"w":"furious","p":"adj.","d":"extremely angry","c":"狂怒的；氣得要命的","s":"Mom was furious when she found out that I had used her credit card to buy games without asking her first.","t":"當媽媽發現我沒先問她就用她的信用卡買遊戲時，她氣得要命。","h":1},{"w":"fury","p":"n.","d":"very strong anger","c":"怒火；狂怒","s":"The coach could not hide his fury after the referee made a third unfair call against his team in one game.","t":"裁判在一場比賽中第三次對他的球隊做出不公判決後，教練無法掩飾自己的怒火。"},{"w":"furiously","p":"adv.","d":"in a very angry way; very fast and with a lot of energy","c":"狂怒地；猛烈地","s":"The dog barked furiously at the stranger who tried to open our gate, and the man ran away quickly.","t":"那隻狗對試圖打開我們大門的陌生人猛烈地吠叫，那個人很快就跑掉了。"},{"w":"be furious with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be extremely angry at someone","c":"對…大發雷霆","s":"Our teacher was furious with the boys who had drawn on the new desks, and she made them clean every desk in the room.","t":"老師對在新桌子上亂畫的男生們大發雷霆，她要他們把教室裡每張桌子都清乾淨。","a":"was furious with"},{"w":"furnish","p":"v.","d":"to put furniture into a room or house","c":"為…配備家具；佈置","s":"The young couple spent a whole month trying to furnish their new apartment because they wanted every room to feel warm and comfortable.","t":"這對年輕夫妻花了整整一個月為新公寓添置家具，因為他們希望每個房間都溫暖舒適。","h":1},{"w":"furniture","p":"n.","d":"things like tables, chairs, and beds","c":"家具","s":"We bought some second-hand furniture for the student dorm, including two desks, a bookshelf, and a comfortable old chair.","t":"我們為學生宿舍買了一些二手家具，包括兩張桌子、一個書架和一張舒適的舊椅子。"},{"w":"furnished","p":"adj.","d":"with furniture already in it","c":"附家具的","s":"The apartment is fully furnished, so you only need to bring your clothes and books when you move in next week.","t":"這間公寓是附全套家具的，所以下週搬進來時你只需要帶衣服和書。"},{"w":"furnish sb with sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give someone something they need","c":"提供某人某物","s":"The travel agency will furnish you with a map and a list of good restaurants before you leave for Kyoto.","t":"旅行社會在你出發去京都前提供你一張地圖和一份好餐廳的清單。","a":"furnish you with"},{"w":"furthermore","p":"adv.","d":"in addition; also","c":"此外；而且","s":"The new library is close to the MRT station; furthermore, it stays open until ten, so students can study there after school.","t":"新圖書館離捷運站很近；此外，它開放到十點，所以學生放學後可以在那裡讀書。","h":1},{"w":"further","p":"adj.","d":"more; additional","c":"更進一步的；額外的","s":"If you have any further questions about the trip, please ask Ms. Lin before Friday, because she will be away next week.","t":"如果你對這次旅行還有任何進一步的問題，請在星期五之前問林老師，因為她下週會不在。"},{"w":"further","p":"v.","d":"to help something develop or succeed","c":"促進；增進","s":"She took evening classes in Japanese to further her career, since many companies in Taiwan trade with Japan.","t":"她上日文夜間課程來促進自己的職涯，因為台灣許多公司都和日本做生意。"},{"w":"gallery","p":"n.","d":"a room or building where art is shown","c":"畫廊；美術館","s":"The new gallery downtown is showing paintings by young Taiwanese artists, and the entrance is free on weekday afternoons.","t":"市中心新開的畫廊正在展出台灣年輕藝術家的畫作，平日下午免費入場。","h":1},{"w":"art gallery","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where paintings and other art are shown","c":"美術館；畫廊","s":"On rainy days, my grandmother likes to visit the art gallery near her home and sit quietly in front of her favorite painting.","t":"下雨天時，我奶奶喜歡去她家附近的美術館，安靜地坐在她最愛的畫前。"},{"w":"gallery","p":"n.","d":"the highest seats in a theater, far from the stage","c":"樓座；頂層看台","s":"Our seats were up in the gallery, far from the stage, but we could still hear every word the actors said.","t":"我們的座位在高處的樓座，離舞台很遠，但我們仍能聽到演員說的每一個字。"},{"w":"gaze","p":"v.","d":"to look at something for a long time","c":"凝視；注視","s":"The children lay on the grass and gazed at the stars for hours, trying to count them before falling asleep.","t":"孩子們躺在草地上凝視星星好幾個小時，想在睡著前數完它們。","a":"gazed","h":1},{"w":"gaze","p":"n.","d":"a long, steady look","c":"凝視；目光","s":"The little boy was shy, so he lowered his gaze and looked at his shoes when the teacher asked him a question.","t":"小男孩很害羞，所以當老師問他問題時，他垂下目光看著自己的鞋子。"},{"w":"gaze at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look at something steadily for a long time","c":"凝視著","s":"The couple sat by the lake and gazed at the sunset, forgetting about their phones for the first time all week.","t":"這對情侶坐在湖邊凝視著夕陽，一整個星期以來第一次忘了手機。","a":"gazed at"},{"w":"gear","p":"n.","d":"the equipment or clothes you need for an activity","c":"裝備；用具","s":"Before the hike, the guide checked everyone's gear, including boots, raincoats, and enough water for the whole day.","t":"出發爬山前，導遊檢查了每個人的裝備，包括登山鞋、雨衣和一整天足夠的水。","h":1},{"w":"gear","p":"n.","d":"a wheel with teeth in a machine; the speed setting of a car or bike","c":"齒輪；排檔","s":"The driver changed to a lower gear as the car climbed the steep mountain road toward Alishan.","t":"當車子爬上通往阿里山的陡峭山路時，司機換到較低的排檔。"},{"w":"gear up for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get ready for something","c":"為…做準備","s":"The whole school is starting to gear up for the sports day next month, and students practice running every afternoon.","t":"全校正開始為下個月的運動會做準備，學生每天下午都練習跑步。"},{"w":"be geared toward","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be designed for a particular purpose or group","c":"針對…而設計","s":"This English course is geared toward senior high school students who want to pass the GSAT, so it focuses on reading and vocabulary.","t":"這門英文課是針對想通過學測的高中生而設計的，所以它著重閱讀和單字。","a":"is geared toward"},{"w":"gender","p":"n.","d":"the fact of being male or female","c":"性別","s":"The survey asked people to write their age and gender, but they did not need to give their names or addresses.","t":"這份問卷要求人們填寫年齡和性別，但不需要寫姓名或地址。","h":1},{"w":"gender equality","p":"n.phr.","d":"treating men and women in the same fair way","c":"性別平等","s":"Many companies now talk about gender equality, but women still earn less money than men for doing the same job in many countries.","t":"許多公司現在都在談性別平等，但在許多國家，做同樣工作的女性賺的錢仍比男性少。"},{"w":"gender gap","p":"n.phr.","d":"a difference between men and women in pay, scores, or chances","c":"性別差距","s":"The report shows that the gender gap in math scores is getting smaller, and girls now do as well as boys in most schools.","t":"報告顯示數學成績的性別差距正在縮小，現在大多數學校的女生表現和男生一樣好。"},{"w":"gene","p":"n.","d":"a part of a cell that controls what you get from your parents","c":"基因","s":"Scientists have found a gene that may explain why some people can eat a lot without gaining weight.","t":"科學家發現一個基因，可能解釋為什麼有些人吃很多卻不會變胖。","h":1},{"w":"genetic","p":"adj.","d":"related to genes; passed from parents to children","c":"基因的；遺傳的","s":"Some diseases are genetic, which means they can be passed from parents to their children through the family line.","t":"有些疾病是遺傳的，意思是它們可以透過家族血脈從父母傳給子女。"},{"w":"genetics","p":"n.","d":"the study of genes and how they are passed on","c":"遺傳學","s":"My cousin studies genetics at university because she wants to understand why she looks exactly like her grandmother.","t":"我表姐在大學讀遺傳學，因為她想了解為什麼自己長得和奶奶一模一樣。"},{"w":"genetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is related to genes","c":"基因上；遺傳上","s":"These tomatoes have been genetically changed so that they stay fresh for two weeks longer than ordinary ones.","t":"這些番茄經過基因改造，所以比普通番茄多保鮮兩個星期。"},{"w":"generation","p":"n.","d":"all the people born at about the same time; one step in a family","c":"世代；一代","s":"My grandfather often says that the younger generation spends too much time on their phones and too little time talking face to face.","t":"我爺爺常說年輕世代花太多時間在手機上，太少時間面對面聊天。","h":1},{"w":"generation gap","p":"n.phr.","d":"the difference in ideas between young and old people","c":"代溝；世代差距","s":"There is a big generation gap between my parents and me when it comes to music, since they have never heard of my favorite singers.","t":"在音樂方面，我和父母之間有很大的代溝，因為他們從沒聽過我最喜歡的歌手。"},{"w":"generate","p":"v.","d":"to produce or create something, especially power or money","c":"產生；創造","s":"The solar panels on the school roof generate enough electricity to power all the classroom lights during the day.","t":"學校屋頂的太陽能板產生足夠的電力，可以供應白天所有教室的燈。"},{"w":"generator","p":"n.","d":"a machine that produces electricity","c":"發電機","s":"When the typhoon cut off the power, the hospital turned on its generator so that the machines in every room kept working.","t":"颱風切斷電力時，醫院啟動了發電機，讓每個房間的機器都能繼續運作。"},{"w":"from generation to generation","p":"phr.","d":"passed on from parents to children over many years","c":"代代相傳","s":"The recipe for this rice cake has been passed down from generation to generation in our family for more than one hundred years.","t":"這個米糕的食譜在我們家代代相傳了一百多年。"},{"w":"generosity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of giving money, time, or help freely","c":"慷慨；大方","s":"Thanks to the generosity of local shop owners, every child at the orphanage received a new coat and a gift this winter.","t":"多虧了當地店家的慷慨，孤兒院的每個孩子今年冬天都收到一件新外套和一份禮物。","h":1},{"w":"generous","p":"adj.","d":"giving more than is expected; large","c":"慷慨的；大方的","s":"My aunt is so generous that she always brings a gift for every single person when she comes back from a trip.","t":"我阿姨非常大方，每次旅行回來總是帶禮物給每一個人。"},{"w":"generously","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind way that gives a lot","c":"慷慨地","s":"The restaurant owner generously offered free lunches to the firefighters who had worked all night to put out the fire next door.","t":"餐廳老闆慷慨地提供免費午餐給整夜撲滅隔壁火災的消防員。"},{"w":"be generous with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give a lot of something freely","c":"對…很大方；不吝惜","s":"Our teacher is generous with her time and always stays after class to help any student who does not understand the lesson.","t":"我們老師對她的時間很大方，總是下課後留下來幫助任何聽不懂的學生。","a":"is generous with"},{"w":"genius","p":"n.","d":"a person who is extremely intelligent or talented","c":"天才","s":"Einstein is often called a genius, but he said that hard work and curiosity mattered more than natural talent.","t":"愛因斯坦常被稱為天才，但他說努力和好奇心比天生的才能更重要。","h":1},{"w":"genius","p":"n.","d":"great natural ability","c":"天賦；才華","s":"She has a genius for making friends, and within a week of moving to the new school, she knew everyone's name.","t":"她有交朋友的天賦，搬到新學校不到一週，她就知道了每個人的名字。"},{"w":"a stroke of genius","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very clever idea","c":"絕妙的想法；天才之舉","s":"Putting the night market next to the new MRT station was a stroke of genius, because thousands of people now pass by every evening.","t":"把夜市設在新捷運站旁邊真是絕妙的想法，因為現在每天晚上有數千人經過。"},{"w":"ingenious","p":"adj.","d":"very clever and original","c":"巧妙的；有創意的","s":"The student came up with an ingenious way to keep her lunch cool, using a frozen water bottle inside her bag.","t":"這位學生想出一個巧妙的方法讓午餐保持涼爽，就是在包包裡放一瓶冷凍的水。"},{"w":"genuine","p":"adj.","d":"real, not fake","c":"真正的；真品的","s":"The shop promises that every bag it sells is genuine leather, and it gives customers a card to prove it.","t":"這家店保證它賣的每個包包都是真正的皮革，並給顧客一張卡片證明。","h":1},{"w":"genuine","p":"adj.","d":"honest and sincere","c":"真誠的","s":"Her smile was so genuine that even the shy new students felt welcome on their first day at school.","t":"她的笑容如此真誠，連害羞的新生在開學第一天也感到受歡迎。"},{"w":"genuinely","p":"adv.","d":"really; in a sincere way","c":"真誠地；確實","s":"I am genuinely sorry for forgetting your birthday, so please let me take you out for dinner this weekend.","t":"我真的很抱歉忘了你的生日，所以請讓我這個週末帶你出去吃晚餐。"},{"w":"germ","p":"n.","d":"a very small living thing that can make you sick","c":"細菌；病菌","s":"Wash your hands with soap for at least twenty seconds to kill the germs you pick up on buses and in public places.","t":"用肥皂洗手至少二十秒，以殺死你在公車和公共場所沾到的細菌。","a":"germs","h":1},{"w":"germ","p":"n.","d":"the first small beginning of an idea","c":"萌芽；起源","s":"The germ of her first novel came from a strange dream she had during a long train ride across the country.","t":"她第一本小說的萌芽來自一次橫越全國的長途火車旅程中做的奇怪夢。"},{"w":"germinate","p":"v.","d":"to begin to grow from a seed","c":"發芽","s":"In warm, wet weather, the bean seeds will germinate in just three or four days, so check the pot every morning.","t":"在溫暖潮濕的天氣下，豆子種子只要三、四天就會發芽，所以每天早上檢查花盆。"},{"w":"gifted","p":"adj.","d":"having a special natural ability","c":"有天賦的；資優的","s":"The school has a special class for gifted students, who finish the regular lessons quickly and need more difficult work.","t":"這所學校有一個為資優學生開設的特殊班，他們很快就完成一般課程，需要更難的作業。","h":1},{"w":"gift","p":"n.","d":"a natural ability; something you give to someone","c":"天賦；禮物","s":"Winning the piano contest showed that she has a real gift for music, even though she only started lessons two years ago.","t":"贏得鋼琴比賽顯示她對音樂有真正的天賦，雖然她兩年前才開始上課。"},{"w":"be gifted with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a special natural ability","c":"天生具有…","s":"My brother is gifted with a wonderful memory, so he can remember every phone number he has ever heard.","t":"我哥哥天生具有超強的記憶力，所以能記住他聽過的每一個電話號碼。","a":"is gifted with"},{"w":"gift shop","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop that sells small presents and souvenirs","c":"禮品店","s":"Before leaving the museum, we stopped at the gift shop to buy postcards and a small model of the famous painting.","t":"離開博物館前，我們在禮品店停下來買明信片和那幅名畫的小模型。"},{"w":"gigantic","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large","c":"巨大的","s":"A gigantic wave hit the beach after the storm, and it carried away two boats that had been tied to the dock.","t":"暴風雨後一個巨大的浪打上海灘，捲走了兩艘綁在碼頭的船。","h":1},{"w":"giant","p":"n.","d":"a very large person or creature, especially in stories","c":"巨人","s":"In the old story, a giant lived at the top of the mountain and shook the ground every time he walked.","t":"在這個古老的故事裡，一個巨人住在山頂，每次走路都讓地面震動。"},{"w":"giant","p":"adj.","d":"very large","c":"巨大的","s":"The night market sells giant fried chicken that is bigger than your face, and tourists line up for an hour to try it.","t":"這個夜市賣比你臉還大的巨大炸雞排，觀光客排一小時隊就為了嚐一口。"},{"w":"giggle","p":"v.","d":"to laugh in a silly, nervous, or quiet way","c":"傻笑；咯咯笑","s":"The girls began to giggle when the teacher accidentally called the principal by the wrong name in front of the whole class.","t":"當老師在全班面前不小心叫錯校長的名字時，女孩們開始傻笑。","h":1},{"w":"giggle","p":"n.","d":"a silly or nervous laugh","c":"傻笑；咯咯笑聲","s":"A nervous giggle spread across the classroom when the new student said he had never eaten stinky tofu.","t":"當新同學說他從沒吃過臭豆腐時，一陣緊張的傻笑傳遍教室。"},{"w":"burst into giggles","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly start laughing in a silly way","c":"突然咯咯笑起來","s":"Every time my little sister sees a cat video, she bursts into giggles and cannot stop laughing for several minutes.","t":"每次我妹妹看到貓的影片，她就突然咯咯笑起來，好幾分鐘都停不下來。","a":"bursts into giggles"},{"w":"ginger","p":"n.","d":"a root with a hot taste used in cooking","c":"薑","s":"My mother always adds a few slices of ginger to the fish soup because it takes away the strong smell and keeps us warm.","t":"我媽媽總是在魚湯裡加幾片薑，因為它能去除腥味，還讓我們身體暖和。","h":1},{"w":"ginger tea","p":"n.phr.","d":"a hot drink made with ginger","c":"薑茶","s":"When I come home wet and cold on a rainy winter day, Grandma makes me a cup of hot ginger tea with brown sugar.","t":"在下雨的冬日我又濕又冷地回到家時，奶奶會為我泡一杯加黑糖的熱薑茶。"},{"w":"gingerbread","p":"n.","d":"a sweet cake or cookie made with ginger","c":"薑餅","s":"Every December, our class bakes gingerbread men and decorates them with icing and candy for the Christmas party.","t":"每年十二月，我們班都會烤薑餅人，用糖霜和糖果裝飾，為聖誕派對做準備。"},{"w":"ginger","p":"adj.","d":"orange-brown in color, especially hair or fur","c":"薑黃色的；橘色的","s":"The ginger cat that lives behind the school is so friendly that students bring it food every day after lunch.","t":"住在學校後面的那隻薑黃色的貓非常友善，學生每天午餐後都會帶食物給它。"},{"w":"glimpse","p":"n.","d":"a quick, short look","c":"一瞥；一眼","s":"We only caught a glimpse of the famous singer as her car drove past, but the fans still screamed with excitement.","t":"當名歌手的車開過時，我們只瞥見了她一眼，但粉絲們仍興奮地尖叫。","h":1},{"w":"glimpse","p":"v.","d":"to see something for a very short time","c":"瞥見","s":"Through the trees, the hikers glimpsed a deer drinking from the stream before it noticed them and ran away.","t":"透過樹林，登山客瞥見一隻鹿在溪邊喝水，然後它就發現了他們並跑掉了。","a":"glimpsed"},{"w":"catch a glimpse of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to see someone or something for a very short time","c":"瞥見；看上一眼","s":"Thousands of people waited outside the temple for hours, hoping to catch a glimpse of the Mazu statue as it passed by.","t":"數千人在廟外等了好幾個小時，希望在媽祖神像經過時能看上一眼。"},{"w":"globe","p":"n.","d":"the world; a round model of the Earth","c":"地球；地球儀","s":"The teacher spun the globe on her desk and asked us to find Taiwan, which is so small that some students missed it.","t":"老師轉動她桌上的地球儀，要我們找出台灣，它小到有些學生沒看到。","h":1},{"w":"around the globe","p":"phr.","d":"in every part of the world","c":"全世界；全球各地","s":"K-pop songs are now popular around the globe, and fans from Brazil to Taiwan learn Korean just to sing along.","t":"韓國流行歌曲現在在全世界都很受歡迎，從巴西到台灣的粉絲為了跟著唱而學韓文。"},{"w":"global","p":"adj.","d":"of or affecting the whole world","c":"全球的","s":"Climate change is a global problem, so every country must work together instead of waiting for others to act first.","t":"氣候變遷是一個全球性的問題，所以每個國家都必須合作，而不是等別人先行動。"},{"w":"globally","p":"adv.","d":"in or across the whole world","c":"全球地；在全世界","s":"The company sells its bubble tea globally, with more than two thousand shops in forty different countries.","t":"這家公司在全球販售珍珠奶茶，在四十個不同國家有兩千多家店。"},{"w":"globalization","p":"n.","d":"the process by which the world's businesses and cultures become connected","c":"全球化","s":"Because of globalization, you can buy the same brand of shoes in Taipei, Paris, and New York at almost the same price.","t":"由於全球化，你可以在台北、巴黎和紐約以幾乎相同的價格買到同一品牌的鞋子。"},{"w":"glorious","p":"adj.","d":"very beautiful or wonderful; deserving great praise","c":"燦爛的；輝煌的；光榮的","s":"After a week of rain, we finally woke up to a glorious sunny morning and decided to go to the beach.","t":"下了一週的雨後，我們終於在一個燦爛的晴朗早晨醒來，決定去海邊。","h":1},{"w":"glory","p":"n.","d":"great honor and praise that you win by doing something important","c":"榮耀；光榮","s":"The team returned home in glory after winning the national championship for the first time in thirty years.","t":"球隊在三十年來首次贏得全國冠軍後，帶著榮耀回到家鄉。"},{"w":"glorify","p":"v.","d":"to make something seem better or more important than it really is","c":"美化；頌揚","s":"Some movies glorify war and make it look exciting, but soldiers who have really fought say it is nothing like that.","t":"有些電影美化戰爭，讓它看起來很刺激，但真正打過仗的士兵說完全不是那樣。"},{"w":"gloriously","p":"adv.","d":"in a very beautiful or wonderful way","c":"燦爛地；輝煌地","s":"The sun set gloriously over the sea, painting the whole sky orange and pink as the fishing boats came home.","t":"太陽燦爛地落入海中，在漁船返航時把整個天空染成橘色和粉紅色。"}]},{"unit":19,"theme":"goods – hardship","cards":[{"w":"goods","p":"n.","d":"things that are made to be sold","c":"商品；貨物","s":"The small shop sells all kinds of goods, from fresh vegetables to school supplies, so the neighbors rarely need to go to the supermarket.","t":"這家小店賣各式各樣的商品，從新鮮蔬菜到學校用品，所以鄰居們很少需要去超市。","h":1},{"w":"household goods","p":"n.phr.","d":"things used in a home, such as pots, towels, and cleaning tools","c":"家庭用品","s":"After moving into the new apartment, we spent the whole weekend buying household goods like pans, towels, and a broom.","t":"搬進新公寓後，我們花了整個週末購買家庭用品，像是平底鍋、毛巾和掃帚。"},{"w":"goods and services","p":"n.phr.","d":"the things people buy and the work others do for them","c":"商品與服務","s":"When prices of goods and services go up every year, families find that their money buys less and less than before.","t":"當商品與服務的價格每年上漲，家庭會發現他們的錢能買到的東西越來越少。"},{"w":"deliver the goods","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do what you promised or what people expect","c":"交出成果；不負期望","s":"The new coach talked a lot about winning, but he failed to deliver the goods, and the team finished last again this season.","t":"新教練說了很多關於贏球的話，但他沒能交出成果，球隊這一季又墊底了。"},{"w":"gown","p":"n.","d":"a long dress worn on special occasions; a long loose piece of clothing","c":"長禮服；長袍","s":"The actress walked down the red carpet in a silver gown that shone under the lights and touched the floor behind her.","t":"那位女演員穿著一件銀色長禮服走過紅毯，禮服在燈光下閃閃發亮，裙擺拖在身後的地板上。","h":1},{"w":"wedding gown","p":"n.phr.","d":"the dress a woman wears at her wedding","c":"婚紗","s":"My sister tried on more than twenty dresses before she found a wedding gown that made her feel like a princess.","t":"我姐姐試穿了二十多件禮服，才找到一件讓她覺得自己像公主的婚紗。"},{"w":"evening gown","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long formal dress worn at night events","c":"晚禮服","s":"Every guest at the charity dinner wore an evening gown or a black suit, so I felt a little out of place in my jeans.","t":"慈善晚宴上的每位客人都穿著晚禮服或黑色西裝，所以我穿牛仔褲覺得有點格格不入。"},{"w":"cap and gown","p":"n.phr.","d":"the hat and long robe worn at a graduation ceremony","c":"學士帽與學士服；畢業服","s":"The students put on their cap and gown and lined up outside the hall, waiting for the graduation ceremony to begin.","t":"學生們穿上學士帽與學士服，在禮堂外排好隊，等待畢業典禮開始。"},{"w":"grace","p":"n.","d":"a smooth, beautiful way of moving; polite and kind behavior","c":"優雅；風度","s":"The old ballet teacher still walks with such grace that people in the street stop to watch her pass by.","t":"那位年長的芭蕾老師走路仍然如此優雅，街上的人都會停下來看她經過。","h":1},{"w":"graceful","p":"adj.","d":"moving in a smooth and beautiful way","c":"優美的；優雅的","s":"The skater's jumps were so graceful that the judges gave her the highest score of the whole competition.","t":"那位滑冰選手的跳躍如此優美，評審給了她整場比賽的最高分。","h":1},{"w":"gracious","p":"adj.","d":"polite, kind, and generous, especially to people of lower position","c":"親切有禮的；寬厚的","s":"Although the famous writer was very busy, she was gracious enough to sign every book and chat with each young fan.","t":"雖然那位名作家非常忙碌，但她親切有禮地為每本書簽名，並和每位年輕粉絲聊天。","h":1},{"w":"gracefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a smooth and beautiful way; politely","c":"優雅地；有風度地","s":"The champion accepted her loss gracefully, hugging the winner and telling reporters that the better player had won.","t":"那位冠軍有風度地接受了失敗，擁抱贏家，並告訴記者是更強的選手獲勝了。"},{"w":"graciously","p":"adv.","d":"in a polite and kind way","c":"親切有禮地","s":"The host graciously invited the late guests to sit down and brought them hot soup even though dinner was almost over.","t":"主人親切地請遲到的客人坐下，即使晚餐快結束了，還是為他們端來熱湯。"},{"w":"say grace","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say a short prayer of thanks before a meal","c":"飯前禱告","s":"In my grandmother's house, nobody picks up a fork until Grandpa has finished saying grace and everyone has said amen.","t":"在我奶奶家，直到爺爺飯前禱告完、大家都說了阿們之後，才有人拿起叉子。","a":"saying grace"},{"w":"graduation","p":"n.","d":"the act of finishing your studies at a school or university; the ceremony for this","c":"畢業；畢業典禮","s":"After graduation, many of my classmates moved to Taipei for work, but we still meet up every summer at our old school.","t":"畢業後，我的許多同學搬到台北工作，但我們每年夏天仍會在母校聚會。","h":1},{"w":"graduate","p":"v.","d":"to finish your studies at a school or university","c":"畢業","s":"My cousin will graduate from medical school next June, and then she plans to work in a hospital in Hualien.","t":"我表姐明年六月將從醫學院畢業，之後她打算在花蓮的一家醫院工作。"},{"w":"graduate","p":"n.","d":"a person who has finished school or university","c":"畢業生","s":"The company prefers to hire a graduate with some work experience rather than a student who has never had a job.","t":"這家公司比較喜歡聘用有一些工作經驗的畢業生，而不是從未工作過的學生。"},{"w":"graduation ceremony","p":"n.phr.","d":"the event where students receive their diplomas","c":"畢業典禮","s":"Parents cried and took hundreds of photos at the graduation ceremony as each student walked across the stage to receive a diploma.","t":"在畢業典禮上，當每位學生走過舞台領取畢業證書時，家長們又哭又拍了數百張照片。"},{"w":"graduate from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finish your studies at a particular school","c":"從…畢業","s":"Both of my parents graduated from the same university, where they met in a chemistry class more than thirty years ago.","t":"我父母都畢業於同一所大學，三十多年前他們在那裡的化學課上相識。","a":"graduated from"},{"w":"grammar","p":"n.","d":"the rules for putting words together in a language","c":"文法","s":"Learning grammar is important, but you also need to listen and speak a lot if you want to use English naturally.","t":"學文法很重要，但如果你想自然地使用英文，也需要大量聽和說。","h":1},{"w":"grammatical","p":"adj.","d":"relating to grammar; correct according to the rules of grammar","c":"文法的；合乎文法的","s":"The sentence sounds strange to native speakers even though it is grammatical, so the teacher suggested a more natural way to say it.","t":"這個句子雖然合乎文法，但母語人士聽起來覺得奇怪，所以老師建議了一個更自然的說法。","h":1},{"w":"grammatically","p":"adv.","d":"according to the rules of grammar","c":"在文法上","s":"Your email is grammatically correct, but it sounds a little too formal for a message to a close friend.","t":"你的電子郵件在文法上是正確的，但對於寫給好朋友的訊息來說，聽起來有點太正式了。"},{"w":"grammatical error","p":"n.phr.","d":"a mistake in grammar","c":"文法錯誤","s":"The teacher circled every grammatical error in red and asked us to rewrite the sentences correctly before the next class.","t":"老師用紅筆圈出每一個文法錯誤，要我們在下次上課前把句子改正重寫。"},{"w":"graph","p":"n.","d":"a drawing that uses lines or bars to show how numbers are related","c":"圖表；曲線圖","s":"The graph on the screen showed that the number of tourists visiting Taiwan has doubled over the past ten years.","t":"螢幕上的圖表顯示，過去十年來台灣的觀光客人數增加了一倍。","h":1},{"w":"bar graph","p":"n.phr.","d":"a graph that uses bars of different heights to compare amounts","c":"長條圖","s":"Our group made a bar graph to compare how many hours students in each grade sleep on school nights.","t":"我們這組做了一張長條圖，比較各年級學生在上學日晚上睡幾個小時。"},{"w":"graph","p":"v.","d":"to show information in a graph","c":"繪製圖表","s":"For homework, we had to graph the temperature of the water every two minutes as it slowly came to a boil.","t":"作業是我們必須每兩分鐘把水溫畫成圖表，記錄它慢慢煮沸的過程。"},{"w":"graphic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with drawings or pictures; described in a very clear, detailed way","c":"圖像的；生動的","s":"My brother studies graphic design because he wants to create posters and book covers for a living.","t":"我哥哥讀平面設計，因為他想以製作海報和書籍封面為生。"},{"w":"graphics","p":"n.","d":"pictures and images made by a computer","c":"電腦圖像；繪圖","s":"The new game is popular not only for its exciting story but also for its beautiful graphics that look almost like a movie.","t":"這款新遊戲受歡迎不只因為刺激的故事，也因為它幾乎像電影一樣漂亮的畫面。"},{"w":"grateful","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that you want to thank someone","c":"感激的；感謝的","s":"I am very grateful to my English teacher, who stayed after school every day for a month to help me prepare for the speech contest.","t":"我非常感激我的英文老師，她一個月來每天放學後留下來幫我準備演講比賽。","h":1},{"w":"gratitude","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being thankful","c":"感激；感謝","s":"The villagers showed their gratitude to the doctor by bringing her fresh fruit and vegetables from their farms every week.","t":"村民每週從農場帶新鮮的水果和蔬菜給醫生，以表達他們的感激。","h":1},{"w":"be grateful for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel thankful for something","c":"對…心存感激","s":"After the typhoon destroyed so many homes, our family was grateful for the simple fact that our house was still standing.","t":"颱風摧毀了那麼多房子後，我們全家感激我們的房子還好好站著這個簡單的事實。","a":"was grateful for"},{"w":"gratefully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you are thankful","c":"感激地","s":"The tired hikers gratefully accepted the hot tea that the old farmer offered them at the foot of the mountain.","t":"疲憊的登山客感激地接受了老農夫在山腳下請他們喝的熱茶。"},{"w":"ungrateful","p":"adj.","d":"not showing thanks for what others do for you","c":"不知感恩的；忘恩負義的","s":"It would be ungrateful to complain about the gift, because your aunt spent two months knitting that sweater for you.","t":"抱怨這份禮物會顯得不知感恩，因為你阿姨花了兩個月為你織那件毛衣。"},{"w":"express gratitude","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say or show that you are thankful","c":"表達感謝","s":"At the end of the year, the students wrote cards to express their gratitude to the school cooks who had prepared their lunches every day.","t":"年底時，學生們寫卡片向每天為他們準備午餐的學校廚師表達感謝。","a":"express their gratitude"},{"w":"grave","p":"n.","d":"the place in the ground where a dead person is buried","c":"墳墓","s":"Every year during Tomb Sweeping Day, our whole family visits my great-grandfather's grave to clean it and offer flowers.","t":"每年清明節，我們全家都會去曾祖父的墳墓清掃並獻花。","h":1},{"w":"grave","p":"adj.","d":"very serious and worrying","c":"嚴重的；重大的","s":"Drinking and driving is a grave mistake that can cost not only your own life but also the lives of others.","t":"酒後駕車是一個嚴重的錯誤，可能不只賠上自己的生命，也賠上他人的性命。"},{"w":"gravely","p":"adv.","d":"in a very serious way","c":"嚴重地；嚴肅地","s":"The doctor spoke gravely to the family, explaining that the old man might not live through the night.","t":"醫生嚴肅地對家屬說話，解釋老先生可能撐不過今晚。"},{"w":"graveyard","p":"n.","d":"an area of land where dead people are buried","c":"墓地；墓園","s":"The children dared each other to walk through the old graveyard at night, but none of them was brave enough to do it.","t":"孩子們互相激對方晚上走過那座老墓園，但沒有一個人有足夠的勇氣去做。"},{"w":"gravestone","p":"n.","d":"a stone placed over a grave with the dead person's name on it","c":"墓碑","s":"The gravestone was so old that we could hardly read the name carved on it, but the date showed the year 1890.","t":"那塊墓碑太古老了，我們幾乎看不清刻在上面的名字，但日期顯示是一八九〇年。"},{"w":"greasy","p":"adj.","d":"covered with or containing a lot of oil or fat","c":"油膩的","s":"The fried noodles at that stand are too greasy for my grandmother, so she always orders the vegetable soup instead.","t":"那個攤子的炒麵對我奶奶來說太油膩了，所以她總是改點蔬菜湯。","h":1},{"w":"grease","p":"n.","d":"thick oil or fat, especially from cooking or in machines","c":"油脂；潤滑油","s":"After cooking bacon, my mother wipes the grease off the pan with a paper towel before washing it in the sink.","t":"煎完培根後，我媽媽會先用紙巾把鍋子上的油脂擦掉，再放到水槽裡洗。"},{"w":"grease","p":"v.","d":"to put oil or fat on something so it moves or cooks easily","c":"給…上油；塗油","s":"Remember to grease the baking pan before you pour in the cake mix, or the cake will stick to the bottom.","t":"記得在倒入蛋糕麵糊前先為烤盤塗油，否則蛋糕會黏在底部。"},{"w":"greeting","p":"n.","d":"something you say or do when you meet someone","c":"問候；招呼","s":"A warm smile and a friendly greeting at the door can make customers feel welcome before they even look at the menu.","t":"門口一個溫暖的微笑和友善的問候，能讓顧客在看菜單之前就感到受歡迎。","h":1},{"w":"greetings","p":"n.","d":"a friendly message sent to someone, often for a holiday","c":"問候語；祝賀","s":"Grandma still mails New Year greetings to all her old friends, even though most of them now use their phones.","t":"奶奶仍然寄新年問候卡給她所有的老朋友，雖然他們大多數現在都用手機了。"},{"w":"greet","p":"v.","d":"to welcome someone with words or actions","c":"迎接；打招呼","s":"Our dog runs to the door to greet every member of the family, wagging his tail so hard that his whole body shakes.","t":"我們的狗會跑到門口迎接家裡的每一個人，尾巴搖得整個身體都在晃。"},{"w":"greeting card","p":"n.phr.","d":"a card with a message for a birthday, holiday, or special event","c":"賀卡","s":"The bookstore sells a greeting card for almost every occasion, from birthdays and weddings to passing an exam.","t":"這家書店幾乎每種場合的賀卡都有賣，從生日、婚禮到通過考試。"},{"w":"grief","p":"n.","d":"great sadness, especially when someone dies","c":"悲傷；悲痛","s":"After her husband passed away, the old woman was so full of grief that she did not leave the house for weeks.","t":"丈夫過世後，那位老婦人充滿悲傷，好幾個星期都沒有出門。","h":1},{"w":"grieve","p":"v.","d":"to feel very sad, especially because someone has died","c":"悲傷；哀悼","s":"People grieve in different ways; some want to talk about the person they lost, while others prefer to be alone.","t":"人們哀悼的方式各不相同；有些人想談論他們失去的人，有些人則比較喜歡獨處。"},{"w":"grieve for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel deep sadness because of someone's death","c":"為…哀悼","s":"The whole town grieved for the young firefighter who lost his life saving a family from the burning building.","t":"整個小鎮都為那位年輕消防員哀悼，他為了從火場中救出一家人而失去生命。","a":"grieved for"},{"w":"grieving","p":"adj.","d":"feeling very sad because someone has died","c":"悲傷的；哀悼中的","s":"Friends brought meals to the grieving family every evening so that they would not have to think about cooking.","t":"朋友們每天晚上送餐給哀悼中的那家人，讓他們不必去想煮飯的事。"},{"w":"grind, ground, ground","p":"v.","d":"to break something into very small pieces or powder by crushing it","c":"磨碎；研磨","s":"The coffee shop will grind the beans for you right before you pay, so the coffee smells fresh when you get home.","t":"咖啡店會在你付錢前幫你把咖啡豆磨碎，這樣你回到家時咖啡聞起來還很新鮮。","a":"grind","h":1},{"w":"ground","p":"adj.","d":"broken into very small pieces or powder","c":"磨碎的；絞碎的","s":"This recipe needs 300 grams of ground pork, two eggs, and a little ginger to make the dumpling filling.","t":"這個食譜需要三百克的絞豬肉、兩顆蛋和一點薑來做水餃餡。"},{"w":"grinder","p":"n.","d":"a machine for breaking something into small pieces or powder","c":"研磨機；磨豆機","s":"My father bought an electric coffee grinder last month, and now the whole kitchen smells wonderful every morning.","t":"我爸爸上個月買了一台電動咖啡磨豆機，現在整個廚房每天早上都香味四溢。"},{"w":"the daily grind","p":"n.phr.","d":"the boring, tiring work you have to do every day","c":"日常的苦差事；每天單調的工作","s":"After ten years of the daily grind in a bank, he quit his job and opened a small surf shop by the beach.","t":"在銀行做了十年日復一日的單調工作後，他辭職在海邊開了一家小衝浪用品店。"},{"w":"grind one's teeth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to rub your top and bottom teeth together, often while sleeping","c":"磨牙","s":"The dentist said that I grind my teeth at night, which explains why my jaw hurts every morning when I wake up.","t":"牙醫說我晚上會磨牙，這解釋了為什麼我每天早上醒來下巴都會痛。","a":"grind my teeth"},{"w":"guarantee","p":"v.","d":"to promise that something will certainly happen or be done","c":"保證","s":"The restaurant owner guarantees that every dish is made with fresh vegetables bought from the market that same morning.","t":"餐廳老闆保證每道菜都是用當天早上從市場買來的新鮮蔬菜做的。","a":"guarantees","h":1},{"w":"guarantee","p":"n.","d":"a promise that something will be done; a written promise to repair or replace a product","c":"保證；保固","s":"The new washing machine comes with a three-year guarantee, so the company will fix it for free if anything goes wrong.","t":"這台新洗衣機附有三年保固，所以如果有任何問題，公司會免費修理。"},{"w":"money-back guarantee","p":"n.phr.","d":"a promise to return your money if you are not happy with a product","c":"退款保證","s":"The online shop offers a thirty-day money-back guarantee, which is why I felt safe ordering the shoes without trying them on.","t":"這家網路商店提供三十天退款保證，這就是為什麼我不用試穿就能放心訂購那雙鞋。"},{"w":"guaranteed","p":"adj.","d":"certain to happen or be received","c":"有保證的；必定的","s":"Winning the city contest means a guaranteed place in the national final, so the team is practicing harder than ever.","t":"贏得市賽代表保證能進入全國決賽，所以隊伍比以往更努力練習。"},{"w":"be guaranteed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be certain to do or cause something","c":"必定會…","s":"This comedy movie is guaranteed to make you laugh, even if you have had the worst day of your life.","t":"這部喜劇電影必定會讓你笑出來，即使你今天過得糟透了。","a":"is guaranteed to"},{"w":"guardian","p":"n.","d":"a person who is legally responsible for a child; someone who protects something","c":"監護人；守護者","s":"Since Mia's parents work abroad, her grandmother is her legal guardian and signs all the forms from school.","t":"由於米亞的父母在國外工作，她的奶奶是她的法定監護人，負責簽學校所有的表格。","h":1},{"w":"guard","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to protect a place or people","c":"警衛；守衛","s":"The security guard at the bank asked me to take off my helmet before I walked through the front door.","t":"銀行的保全警衛要我在走進大門前先脫下安全帽。"},{"w":"guard","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone or something from danger","c":"守衛；保護","s":"Two big dogs guard the farm at night, and they bark loudly whenever a stranger comes near the gate.","t":"兩隻大狗晚上守衛農場，每當有陌生人靠近大門，牠們就大聲吠叫。"},{"w":"guard against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to prevent something bad from happening","c":"防範；預防","s":"Wearing a mask and washing your hands often are simple ways to guard against catching a cold in winter.","t":"戴口罩和勤洗手是冬天預防感冒的簡單方法。"},{"w":"legal guardian","p":"n.phr.","d":"the person the law says is responsible for a child","c":"法定監護人","s":"Children under eighteen need a legal guardian to sign the form before they can join the overseas study program.","t":"十八歲以下的兒童需要法定監護人簽署表格，才能參加海外遊學計畫。"},{"w":"guilt","p":"n.","d":"the bad feeling you have when you know you have done something wrong; the fact of having broken a law","c":"罪惡感；內疚；有罪","s":"Tom was filled with guilt after he lied to his best friend, so he called her the next morning to tell the truth.","t":"湯姆對好朋友說謊後充滿罪惡感，所以第二天早上他打電話告訴她實話。","h":1},{"w":"guilty","p":"adj.","d":"having broken a law; feeling bad because you have done something wrong","c":"有罪的；內疚的","s":"I felt guilty about eating the last piece of cake, because I knew my little brother had been saving it.","t":"我對吃掉最後一塊蛋糕感到內疚，因為我知道我弟弟一直留著它。","h":1},{"w":"feel guilty about","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel bad because you have done something wrong","c":"對…感到內疚","s":"She still feels guilty about missing her grandfather's birthday party, even though she had to work that day.","t":"她仍然對錯過爺爺的生日派對感到內疚，雖然那天她必須工作。","a":"feels guilty about"},{"w":"be found guilty of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be judged in court to have done a crime","c":"被判犯有…罪","s":"The driver was found guilty of causing the accident, and the judge took away his license for two years.","t":"那名駕駛被判犯有造成車禍的罪，法官吊銷了他兩年的駕照。","a":"was found guilty of"},{"w":"gulf","p":"n.","d":"a large area of sea that is partly surrounded by land","c":"海灣","s":"Many small fishing villages lie along the gulf, where the water is calm and full of fish for most of the year.","t":"許多小漁村沿著海灣分布，那裡的海水平靜，一年中大部分時間都有很多魚。","h":1},{"w":"gulf","p":"n.","d":"a large difference between two groups or ideas","c":"鴻溝；巨大差距","s":"There is a growing gulf between rich and poor families in the city, and the government is trying to narrow it.","t":"這座城市裡富裕家庭和貧窮家庭之間的鴻溝越來越大，政府正試圖縮小它。"},{"w":"a gulf between","p":"n.phr.","d":"a big difference between two people or things","c":"…之間的鴻溝","s":"After years of not talking, there was a gulf between the two brothers that even their mother could not bridge.","t":"多年不說話之後，這兩兄弟之間有一道鴻溝，連他們的母親都無法跨越。"},{"w":"habitual","p":"adj.","d":"done regularly as a habit; usual","c":"習慣性的；慣常的","s":"His habitual lateness finally cost him his job, because the manager could no longer trust him to open the shop on time.","t":"他習慣性的遲到終於讓他丟了工作，因為經理再也無法信任他會準時開店。","h":1},{"w":"habit","p":"n.","d":"something you do often and regularly, sometimes without thinking","c":"習慣","s":"Reading for twenty minutes before bed is a good habit that helps me relax and fall asleep more quickly.","t":"睡前閱讀二十分鐘是個好習慣，能幫助我放鬆並更快入睡。"},{"w":"habitually","p":"adv.","d":"regularly, as a habit","c":"習慣性地","s":"My uncle habitually checks the weather report before breakfast, even on days when he has no plans to go outside.","t":"我叔叔習慣性地在早餐前查看天氣預報，即使那天他沒打算出門。"},{"w":"be in the habit of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something regularly","c":"有…的習慣","s":"Grandpa is in the habit of walking around the park every morning at six, so all the neighbors know him well.","t":"爺爺有每天早上六點繞公園散步的習慣，所以鄰居們都很熟悉他。","a":"is in the habit of"},{"w":"break a habit","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop doing something you have done regularly for a long time","c":"戒掉習慣","s":"It took my father almost a year to break the habit of smoking, but he has not touched a cigarette since last spring.","t":"我爸爸花了將近一年才戒掉抽菸的習慣，但從去年春天起他就沒碰過香菸。","a":"break the habit"},{"w":"halt","p":"v.","d":"to stop moving or stop something from continuing","c":"停止；使停止","s":"The police had to halt the parade for twenty minutes because a child had been separated from her parents.","t":"警方不得不讓遊行暫停二十分鐘，因為有個小孩和父母走散了。","h":1},{"w":"halt","p":"n.","d":"a stop","c":"停止；中止","s":"Heavy snow brought the whole city to a halt, with buses, trains, and even taxis unable to move for hours.","t":"大雪讓整座城市陷入停擺，公車、火車甚至計程車都好幾個小時動彈不得。"},{"w":"come to a halt","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop moving or stop happening","c":"停下來","s":"The old bus came to a halt in the middle of the road, and all the passengers had to get off and wait for the next one.","t":"那輛舊公車在路中間停了下來，所有乘客都得下車等下一班。","a":"came to a halt"},{"w":"bring sth to a halt","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make something stop","c":"使…停止","s":"Work in the factory was brought to a halt by the sudden power cut, and the workers sat in the dark for almost two hours.","t":"工廠的工作因突然停電而被迫停止，工人們在黑暗中坐了將近兩個小時。","a":"was brought to a halt"},{"w":"handwriting","p":"n.","d":"the way a person writes with a pen or pencil","c":"筆跡；書寫","s":"The doctor's handwriting was so messy that the nurse had to call him to ask what medicine he had written down.","t":"醫生的筆跡太潦草了，護士得打電話問他寫的是什麼藥。","h":1},{"w":"handwritten","p":"adj.","d":"written by hand, not typed or printed","c":"手寫的","s":"In a world of emails and text messages, a handwritten letter from an old friend feels especially warm and personal.","t":"在電子郵件和簡訊的世界裡，一封來自老朋友的手寫信感覺特別溫暖而有人情味。"},{"w":"handwriting on the wall","p":"phr.","d":"clear signs that something bad is going to happen","c":"不祥之兆","s":"When the company stopped hiring and cut everyone's hours, the workers saw the handwriting on the wall and started looking for new jobs.","t":"當公司停止招人並削減每個人的工時，員工們看出了不祥之兆，開始找新工作。"},{"w":"hardship","p":"n.","d":"something that makes life difficult, such as not having enough money or food","c":"困苦；艱難","s":"My grandparents went through great hardship during the war, when they often had nothing but sweet potatoes to eat.","t":"我的祖父母在戰爭期間經歷了極大的困苦，那時他們常常只有番薯可以吃。","h":1},{"w":"hard","p":"adj.","d":"difficult; full of problems or suffering","c":"艱難的；困難的","s":"It was a hard year for the farmers, because the typhoon destroyed their rice just a week before the harvest.","t":"對農民來說那是艱難的一年，因為颱風在收割前一週摧毀了他們的稻米。"},{"w":"harden","p":"v.","d":"to become hard; to make someone less kind or less easily hurt","c":"變硬；使堅強；使冷酷","s":"Leave the clay in the sun for a few hours to let it harden, and then you can paint your bowl any color you like.","t":"把黏土放在太陽下幾個小時讓它變硬，然後你就可以把碗漆成任何你喜歡的顏色。"},{"w":"hardly","p":"adv.","d":"almost not; only just","c":"幾乎不","s":"The room was so dark that I could hardly see my own hands, so I used my phone as a flashlight to find the door.","t":"房間太暗了，我幾乎看不見自己的手，所以我用手機當手電筒找到門。"},{"w":"endure hardship","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suffer difficult conditions over a long time","c":"忍受困苦","s":"The early settlers had to endure hardship for many years, building their homes by hand and growing all their own food.","t":"早期的拓荒者必須忍受困苦許多年，親手建造家園並自己種植所有的食物。"}]},{"unit":20,"theme":"hardware – identical","cards":[{"w":"hardware","p":"n.","d":"the physical parts of a computer; tools and metal things for the home","c":"硬體；五金","s":"Our school bought new computer hardware last month, so the machines in the lab now run much faster than before.","t":"我們學校上個月買了新的電腦硬體，所以電腦教室的機器現在跑得比以前快多了。","h":1},{"w":"hardware store","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop that sells tools, nails, and things for fixing a house","c":"五金行","s":"My father went to the hardware store to buy some nails and a new hammer because he wanted to fix the broken shelf.","t":"我爸爸去五金行買一些釘子和一把新鎚子，因為他想修理壞掉的架子。"},{"w":"software","p":"n.","d":"the programs that run on a computer","c":"軟體","s":"Before you install the new software on your laptop, make sure you have enough space and a good Internet connection.","t":"在你的筆電上安裝新軟體之前，請確認你有足夠的空間和良好的網路連線。"},{"w":"hardware engineer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who designs the physical parts of computers","c":"硬體工程師","s":"My cousin works as a hardware engineer in Hsinchu, where she designs small chips that go inside smartphones and cameras.","t":"我表姊在新竹當硬體工程師，她在那裡設計放進智慧型手機和相機裡的小晶片。"},{"w":"harmony","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which people live or work together peacefully","c":"和諧","s":"In our small village, people of different religions have lived together in harmony for more than a hundred years.","t":"在我們的小村莊裡，不同宗教的人們已經和諧地共同生活了一百多年。","h":1},{"w":"in harmony with","p":"phr.","d":"working or living well together with something","c":"與…和諧一致","s":"The new wooden house was built in harmony with the forest around it, so it looks like part of nature.","t":"這間新的木屋蓋得與周圍的森林和諧一致，所以它看起來像大自然的一部分。"},{"w":"harmonious","p":"adj.","d":"friendly and peaceful; sounding pleasant together","c":"和諧的；和睦的","s":"The two families have a harmonious relationship, and they often share meals and help each other with the farm work.","t":"這兩家人關係和睦，他們常常一起吃飯，並在農事上互相幫忙。"},{"w":"harmonize","p":"v.","d":"to go well together; to sing or play notes that sound good together","c":"使和諧；和聲","s":"The singers practiced for weeks so that their voices would harmonize perfectly during the final song of the concert.","t":"歌手們練習了好幾個星期，好讓他們的聲音在音樂會的最後一首歌中完美和聲。"},{"w":"live in harmony","p":"v.phr.","d":"to live together peacefully","c":"和諧共處","s":"Humans and wild animals can live in harmony if we protect the forests and do not take all the land for ourselves.","t":"如果我們保護森林，不把所有土地都佔為己有，人類和野生動物就能和諧共處。"},{"w":"harsh","p":"adj.","d":"cruel, unkind, or too strict; very difficult or unpleasant","c":"嚴厲的；殘酷的；惡劣的","s":"The coach was too harsh with the young players, and several of them cried after he shouted at them during practice.","t":"教練對年輕球員太嚴厲了，有幾個人在練習時被他大吼之後哭了。","h":1},{"w":"harshly","p":"adv.","d":"in a cruel or very strict way","c":"嚴厲地","s":"The manager spoke so harshly to the new worker that everyone in the office felt uncomfortable and stopped talking.","t":"經理對新員工說話如此嚴厲，辦公室裡的每個人都覺得不舒服而停止交談。"},{"w":"harsh winter","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very cold and difficult winter","c":"嚴冬","s":"After a long and harsh winter, the farmers were happy to see the first green leaves appear on the trees in March.","t":"經過漫長的嚴冬之後，農民們很高興在三月看到樹上長出第一批綠葉。"},{"w":"harshness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being cruel, strict, or unpleasant","c":"嚴厲；嚴酷","s":"The harshness of the desert climate makes it hard for most plants to grow, so only a few kinds of cactus survive there.","t":"沙漠氣候的嚴酷使大多數植物難以生長，所以只有少數幾種仙人掌能在那裡存活。"},{"w":"haste","p":"n.","d":"great speed in doing something, often because you have too little time","c":"匆忙；急忙","s":"In her haste to catch the early train, Lisa left her wallet on the kitchen table and had no money for a ticket.","t":"莉莎匆忙趕早班火車，把皮夾忘在廚房桌上，結果沒錢買票。","h":1},{"w":"hasten","p":"v.","d":"to hurry; to make something happen sooner","c":"趕快；加速","s":"When the dark clouds appeared, the farmers had to hasten to bring in the rice before the heavy rain destroyed it.","t":"當烏雲出現時，農民們必須趕快把稻米收進來，以免大雨把它毀了。","h":1},{"w":"in haste","p":"phr.","d":"quickly and without careful thought","c":"匆忙地","s":"The letter was written in haste, so it had several spelling mistakes and the writer even forgot to sign his name.","t":"這封信寫得很匆忙，所以有好幾個拼字錯誤，寫信的人甚至忘了簽名。"},{"w":"hasty","p":"adj.","d":"done too quickly without enough thought","c":"倉促的；草率的","s":"Buying a car on the first day you see it is a hasty decision, so take a week to compare prices first.","t":"看到車的第一天就買下來是個倉促的決定，所以先花一個星期比較價格吧。"},{"w":"hastily","p":"adv.","d":"too quickly and without care","c":"匆忙地；草率地","s":"The students hastily packed their bags when the bell rang, and two of them left their homework on the desks.","t":"鐘聲響起時學生們匆忙地收拾書包，有兩個人把作業留在桌上了。"},{"w":"make haste","p":"v.phr.","d":"to hurry","c":"趕快","s":"\"Make haste, children, or we will miss the last bus home,\" Grandma called from the door as she put on her coat.","t":"「趕快，孩子們，不然我們會錯過回家的最後一班公車。」奶奶一邊穿外套一邊在門口喊道。","a":"Make haste"},{"w":"hatred","p":"n.","d":"a very strong feeling of not liking someone or something","c":"仇恨；憎恨","s":"The old man was full of hatred for the soldiers who had burned his village and taken his family away when he was young.","t":"那位老人對那些在他年輕時燒毀他的村莊、帶走他家人的士兵充滿仇恨。","h":1},{"w":"hate","p":"v.","d":"to dislike someone or something very much","c":"討厭；恨","s":"I really hate getting up early on cold winter mornings, but I have to catch the school bus at six thirty.","t":"我真的很討厭在寒冷的冬天早晨早起，但我必須趕六點半的校車。"},{"w":"hateful","p":"adj.","d":"very unkind and cruel; causing hate","c":"可惡的；充滿惡意的","s":"Leaving hateful comments under other people's photos online is a form of bullying, and the school will not allow it.","t":"在網路上別人的照片下留下惡意的評論是一種霸凌，學校不會容許這種行為。"},{"w":"hate speech","p":"n.phr.","d":"words that attack a group of people because of their race, religion, etc.","c":"仇恨言論","s":"Many websites now remove hate speech quickly because such words can hurt people and even lead to violence in real life.","t":"許多網站現在會很快刪除仇恨言論，因為這類話語會傷害人，甚至在現實生活中導致暴力。"},{"w":"hawk","p":"n.","d":"a large bird that hunts small animals","c":"鷹；隼","s":"High above the fields, a hawk circled slowly in the sky, watching for a mouse or a small bird to catch.","t":"在田野高空，一隻鷹在天上慢慢盤旋，尋找可以抓的老鼠或小鳥。","h":1},{"w":"watch sb like a hawk","p":"v.phr.","d":"to watch someone very carefully so they cannot do anything wrong","c":"緊盯著某人","s":"During the exam, the teacher watched him like a hawk because he had copied answers from a classmate the last time.","t":"考試期間老師緊盯著他，因為他上次抄了同學的答案。","a":"watched him like a hawk"},{"w":"hawk-eyed","p":"adj.","d":"able to notice small details quickly","c":"目光敏銳的","s":"Our hawk-eyed librarian noticed at once that one book was missing from the shelf, even though there were hundreds of books there.","t":"我們目光敏銳的圖書館員立刻注意到架上少了一本書，即使那裡有好幾百本書。"},{"w":"helicopter","p":"n.","d":"an aircraft with large turning blades on top that can fly straight up","c":"直升機","s":"When the hikers got lost in the mountains, a rescue helicopter flew over the forest for hours until it found them.","t":"當登山客在山裡迷路時，一架救援直升機在森林上空飛了好幾個小時，直到找到他們。","h":1},{"w":"by helicopter","p":"phr.","d":"traveling in a helicopter","c":"搭直升機","s":"The injured climber was taken to the hospital by helicopter because the mountain road was blocked by fallen rocks.","t":"受傷的登山者搭直升機被送到醫院，因為山路被落石堵住了。"},{"w":"helicopter pilot","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who flies a helicopter","c":"直升機駕駛員","s":"My uncle is a helicopter pilot who carries doctors and medicine to small islands when the sea is too rough for boats.","t":"我叔叔是一位直升機駕駛員，當海上風浪太大船無法出航時，他載醫生和藥品到小島上。"},{"w":"helicopter parent","p":"n.phr.","d":"a parent who watches and controls their child too closely","c":"直升機父母","s":"Some teachers say that a helicopter parent does so much for the child that he or she never learns to solve problems alone.","t":"有些老師說，直升機父母為孩子做太多事，以至於孩子永遠學不會自己解決問題。"},{"w":"herd","p":"n.","d":"a large group of animals of one kind that live together","c":"牧群；獸群","s":"A large herd of cows was crossing the road slowly, so all the cars had to stop and wait for ten minutes.","t":"一大群牛正慢慢地過馬路，所以所有車子都得停下來等十分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"herd","p":"v.","d":"to make animals or people move together as a group","c":"放牧；把…趕在一起","s":"Every evening the old farmer and his dog herd the sheep back into the barn before the sun goes down.","t":"每天傍晚，老農夫和他的狗在太陽下山前把羊趕回畜棚。"},{"w":"a herd of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of large animals such as cows or elephants","c":"一群…","s":"On our trip to Africa, we saw a herd of elephants walking to the river to drink water in the early morning.","t":"在非洲旅行時，我們看到一群大象在清晨走到河邊喝水。"},{"w":"follow the herd","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do what most other people do without thinking","c":"隨波逐流；盲從","s":"Instead of choosing the popular major just to follow the herd, you should study the subject that you truly love.","t":"與其只是為了隨波逐流而選擇熱門科系，你應該讀自己真正喜愛的科目。"},{"w":"hesitation","p":"n.","d":"a pause before you do or say something because you are not sure","c":"猶豫；躊躇","s":"After a moment of hesitation, the boy jumped into the cold pool, and his friends cheered loudly from the side.","t":"猶豫了一會兒之後，男孩跳進冰冷的泳池，他的朋友們在池邊大聲歡呼。","h":1},{"w":"hesitate","p":"v.","d":"to pause before doing something because you are not sure","c":"猶豫","s":"If you have any questions about the homework, please do not hesitate to ask me after class or send me an email.","t":"如果你對作業有任何問題，請不要猶豫，下課後來問我或寄電子郵件給我。"},{"w":"hesitant","p":"adj.","d":"slow to act or speak because you are not sure","c":"猶豫的；遲疑的","s":"Amy was hesitant about joining the dance club at first, but now she practices with the team three times a week.","t":"艾咪起初對加入舞蹈社感到猶豫，但現在她每週和隊員一起練習三次。"},{"w":"without hesitation","p":"phr.","d":"immediately, without stopping to think","c":"毫不猶豫地","s":"When the little girl fell into the river, the young man jumped in without hesitation and pulled her safely to the bank.","t":"當小女孩掉進河裡時，年輕人毫不猶豫地跳下去，把她安全地拉上岸。"},{"w":"hesitate to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be slow or unwilling to do something","c":"遲遲不…；不敢…","s":"Many students hesitate to speak English in class because they are afraid of making mistakes in front of their friends.","t":"許多學生在課堂上遲遲不敢說英文，因為他們害怕在朋友面前出錯。"},{"w":"hive","p":"n.","d":"a box or structure where bees live and make honey","c":"蜂巢；蜂箱","s":"The farmer keeps twenty hives behind his house, and each one gives him several bottles of honey every summer.","t":"農夫在房子後面養了二十個蜂箱，每個蜂箱每年夏天都能給他好幾瓶蜂蜜。","a":"hives","h":1},{"w":"beehive","p":"n.","d":"a hive where bees are kept","c":"蜂巢","s":"Do not throw stones at the beehive in that tree, or hundreds of angry bees will fly out and chase you.","t":"不要對那棵樹上的蜂巢丟石頭，否則幾百隻生氣的蜜蜂會飛出來追你。"},{"w":"a hive of activity","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place full of busy people","c":"繁忙熱鬧的地方","s":"The night market becomes a hive of activity after seven o'clock, with cooks shouting, music playing, and crowds moving everywhere.","t":"夜市在七點以後變成一個熱鬧繁忙的地方，廚師在叫喊、音樂在播放、人群四處走動。"},{"w":"homeland","p":"n.","d":"the country where you were born","c":"祖國；家鄉","s":"After living abroad for thirty years, my grandfather finally returned to his homeland to spend his last years near the sea.","t":"在國外住了三十年之後，我爺爺終於回到他的祖國，在海邊度過他的晚年。","h":1},{"w":"hometown","p":"n.","d":"the town where you were born or grew up","c":"家鄉；故鄉","s":"Every Lunar New Year, millions of people travel back to their hometown to eat dinner with their parents and grandparents.","t":"每年農曆新年，數百萬人回到家鄉，和父母與祖父母一起吃晚餐。"},{"w":"homesick","p":"adj.","d":"sad because you are away from home","c":"想家的","s":"During her first month in London, Mei felt so homesick that she called her mother in Taiwan every single night.","t":"在倫敦的第一個月，小美想家想得厲害，每天晚上都打電話給在台灣的媽媽。"},{"w":"homeless","p":"adj.","d":"without a home to live in","c":"無家可歸的","s":"The typhoon destroyed hundreds of houses, and many homeless families had to sleep in the school gym for two weeks.","t":"颱風摧毀了數百間房屋，許多無家可歸的家庭不得不在學校體育館睡了兩個星期。"},{"w":"homemade","p":"adj.","d":"made at home, not bought in a shop","c":"自製的","s":"My grandmother's homemade dumplings taste much better than the frozen ones from the supermarket, so we always ask her to make more.","t":"我奶奶自製的水餃比超市的冷凍水餃好吃多了，所以我們總是請她多做一些。"},{"w":"honeymoon","p":"n.","d":"a holiday taken by a newly married couple","c":"蜜月","s":"After the wedding, the happy couple spent their honeymoon on a quiet island in Thailand, far away from work and phones.","t":"婚禮之後，這對幸福的新人在泰國一座安靜的小島上度蜜月，遠離工作和電話。","h":1},{"w":"honeymoon","p":"v.","d":"to take a holiday after getting married","c":"度蜜月","s":"My parents honeymooned in Japan twenty-five years ago, and they still keep the photos of the cherry blossoms on the wall.","t":"我父母二十五年前在日本度蜜月，他們至今仍把櫻花的照片掛在牆上。","a":"honeymooned"},{"w":"honeymooner","p":"n.","d":"a person who is on their honeymoon","c":"度蜜月的人","s":"The hotel by the beach is popular with honeymooners, so it offers romantic dinners and flowers in every room.","t":"這家海邊的飯店很受度蜜月的人歡迎，所以每個房間都提供浪漫晚餐和鮮花。","a":"honeymooners"},{"w":"go on honeymoon","p":"v.phr.","d":"to travel somewhere for a honeymoon","c":"去度蜜月","s":"Where would you like to go on honeymoon if you could choose any place in the world without worrying about money?","t":"如果你可以不用擔心錢而選擇世界上任何地方，你想到哪裡去度蜜月？"},{"w":"hook","p":"n.","d":"a curved piece of metal or plastic for hanging or catching things","c":"鉤子；掛鉤","s":"Please hang your wet coat on the hook behind the door so that the water does not drip onto the floor.","t":"請把你濕的外套掛在門後的掛鉤上，這樣水就不會滴到地板上。","h":1},{"w":"hook","p":"v.","d":"to catch a fish with a hook; to fasten something with a hook","c":"鉤住；釣到","s":"After waiting by the river for three hours, my brother finally managed to hook a big fish and pulled it onto the bank.","t":"在河邊等了三個小時之後，我哥哥終於釣到一條大魚，把它拉上岸。"},{"w":"be hooked on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to like something so much that you cannot stop doing it","c":"迷上；對…上癮","s":"My little sister is hooked on a new cartoon series, and she watches at least two episodes every evening after dinner.","t":"我妹妹迷上了一部新的卡通系列，她每天晚餐後至少看兩集。","a":"is hooked on"},{"w":"off the hook","p":"phr.","d":"no longer in trouble or no longer having to do something","c":"脫身；擺脫麻煩","s":"Tom thought he was off the hook when the teacher forgot to collect the homework, but she asked for it the next morning.","t":"老師忘了收作業時，湯姆以為自己脫身了，但她第二天早上就要大家交。"},{"w":"unhook","p":"v.","d":"to remove something from a hook","c":"取下；解開（鉤子）","s":"Be careful when you unhook the fish, because the sharp metal can easily cut your fingers if you pull too hard.","t":"把魚從鉤子上取下來時要小心，因為如果你拉得太用力，尖銳的金屬很容易割傷你的手指。"},{"w":"horizon","p":"n.","d":"the line where the sky seems to meet the land or sea","c":"地平線；水平線","s":"We sat on the beach and watched the sun slowly sink below the horizon until the whole sky turned orange and pink.","t":"我們坐在沙灘上看著太陽慢慢沉到地平線下，直到整個天空變成橘色和粉紅色。","h":1},{"w":"on the horizon","p":"phr.","d":"likely to happen soon","c":"即將來臨；在望","s":"With the final exams on the horizon, the library is full of students every night, and the quiet study rooms are always taken.","t":"期末考即將來臨，圖書館每晚都坐滿學生，安靜的自習室總是被佔滿。"},{"w":"broaden one's horizons","p":"v.phr.","d":"to learn new things and gain wider experience","c":"開拓視野","s":"Studying abroad for a year helped me broaden my horizons, and I made friends from more than ten different countries.","t":"出國讀書一年幫助我開拓了視野，我結交了來自十多個不同國家的朋友。","a":"broaden my horizons"},{"w":"horizontal","p":"adj.","d":"flat and level; going from side to side","c":"水平的；橫的","s":"Draw a horizontal line across the middle of the page, and then write the English words above it and the Chinese below.","t":"在頁面中間畫一條水平線，然後把英文字寫在線的上面，中文寫在下面。"},{"w":"horrify","p":"v.","d":"to shock someone very much; to make someone feel great fear","c":"使驚駭；使震驚","s":"The news of the plane crash will horrify the whole country, because more than two hundred people were on board.","t":"飛機失事的消息將會震驚全國，因為機上有兩百多人。","h":1},{"w":"horrified","p":"adj.","d":"feeling great shock and fear","c":"感到驚駭的","s":"The parents were horrified when they saw their little son standing on the edge of the roof, so they ran upstairs at once.","t":"父母看到小兒子站在屋頂邊緣時嚇壞了，所以立刻跑上樓。"},{"w":"horrifying","p":"adj.","d":"very shocking and frightening","c":"令人驚駭的","s":"The film shows horrifying pictures of the war, so the teacher warned us that some scenes would be hard to watch.","t":"這部影片呈現了令人驚駭的戰爭畫面，所以老師警告我們有些場景會很難看下去。"},{"w":"horror","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great shock and fear","c":"恐怖；驚恐","s":"To her horror, Jane realized that she had sent the private message to the whole class instead of to her best friend.","t":"讓珍驚恐的是，她發現自己把私人訊息傳給了全班，而不是傳給最好的朋友。"},{"w":"horrible","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or unpleasant; frightening","c":"可怕的；糟透的","s":"The weather was horrible during our trip to the mountains, so we stayed inside the cabin and played cards for two days.","t":"我們去山上旅行時天氣糟透了，所以我們待在小木屋裡玩了兩天的紙牌。"},{"w":"horror movie","p":"n.phr.","d":"a film made to frighten people","c":"恐怖片","s":"My friends love watching a horror movie late at night, but I always cover my eyes during the scary parts.","t":"我的朋友們喜歡在深夜看恐怖片，但我在可怕的部分總是遮住眼睛。"},{"w":"hose","p":"n.","d":"a long rubber or plastic tube that carries water","c":"水管；軟管","s":"On hot summer afternoons, the children love to run through the water from the garden hose to cool down.","t":"在炎熱的夏日午後，孩子們喜歡跑過花園水管噴出的水來消暑。","h":1},{"w":"hose down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to wash something with water from a hose","c":"用水管沖洗","s":"After the muddy football game, Dad made us hose down our boots in the yard before we could come into the house.","t":"泥濁的足球賽之後，爸爸要我們先在院子裡用水管沖洗鞋子，才能進屋。"},{"w":"fire hose","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large hose used by firefighters","c":"消防水帶","s":"The firefighters pulled a long fire hose from the truck and sprayed water on the burning roof for almost an hour.","t":"消防員從消防車上拉出一條長長的消防水帶，對著燃燒的屋頂噴水將近一個小時。"},{"w":"household","p":"n.","d":"all the people who live together in one house","c":"家庭；一家人","s":"In a traditional Taiwanese household, grandparents, parents, and children often lived under the same roof and ate together.","t":"在傳統的台灣家庭裡，祖父母、父母和孩子常常住在同一個屋頂下一起吃飯。","h":1},{"w":"household","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a house and the people in it","c":"家用的；家庭的","s":"The supermarket sells household products such as soap, toilet paper, and light bulbs on the second floor near the elevator.","t":"這間超市在二樓電梯旁販售肥皂、衛生紙和燈泡等家用產品。"},{"w":"household chores","p":"n.phr.","d":"jobs that need to be done regularly at home","c":"家事","s":"In our family, everyone shares the household chores: I wash the dishes, my sister sweeps the floor, and Dad cooks dinner.","t":"在我們家，每個人都分擔家事：我洗碗，妹妹掃地，爸爸煮晚餐。"},{"w":"household name","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person or thing that almost everyone knows","c":"家喻戶曉的人／事物","s":"After winning the gold medal at the Olympics, the young swimmer became a household name in Taiwan almost overnight.","t":"在奧運贏得金牌後，這位年輕的游泳選手幾乎一夜之間在台灣成了家喻戶曉的人物。"},{"w":"housework","p":"n.","d":"the work of cleaning and cooking in a house","c":"家事；家務","s":"My mother does most of the housework on weekends, so my brother and I try to help her by cleaning our own rooms.","t":"我媽媽週末做大部分的家事，所以我和哥哥會打掃自己的房間來幫她。","h":1},{"w":"do the housework","p":"v.phr.","d":"to clean, wash, and tidy the house","c":"做家事","s":"Since both of my parents work long hours, we all do the housework together on Saturday morning before going out.","t":"因為我父母工時都很長，所以我們星期六早上出門前會一起做家事。"},{"w":"housewife","p":"n.","d":"a woman who stays at home to take care of the house and family","c":"家庭主婦","s":"My aunt was a housewife for ten years, and then she opened a small bakery when her children started high school.","t":"我阿姨當了十年家庭主婦，然後在孩子上高中時開了一間小麵包店。"},{"w":"housekeeper","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to clean and manage a house or hotel","c":"管家；房務人員","s":"The hotel housekeeper changes the sheets and towels every day, and she always leaves a small chocolate on the pillow.","t":"飯店的房務人員每天更換床單和毛巾，而且總是在枕頭上留一塊小巧克力。"},{"w":"humanity","p":"n.","d":"all people in the world","c":"人類","s":"Climate change is one of the biggest problems facing humanity today, and every country must work together to solve it.","t":"氣候變遷是當今人類面臨的最大問題之一，每個國家都必須合作解決它。","h":1},{"w":"humanity","p":"n.","d":"kindness and care for other people","c":"人性；仁慈","s":"The doctor treated the poor patients for free, showing a deep sense of humanity that everyone in the town respected.","t":"這位醫生免費為窮苦病人看病，展現出鎮上每個人都敬重的深厚仁慈之心。"},{"w":"human","p":"adj.","d":"connected with people","c":"人的；人類的","s":"The human body needs about eight hours of sleep a night, but many high school students get only five or six.","t":"人體每晚需要大約八小時的睡眠，但許多高中生只睡五、六個小時。"},{"w":"humane","p":"adj.","d":"kind and showing care, especially to people or animals who are suffering","c":"人道的；仁慈的","s":"The new law requires farms to keep animals in humane conditions, with enough space, clean water, and fresh air.","t":"新法律要求農場以人道的方式飼養動物，提供足夠的空間、乾淨的水和新鮮空氣。"},{"w":"humankind","p":"n.","d":"all human beings as a group","c":"全人類","s":"The invention of writing changed the history of humankind, because people could finally keep records of what they knew.","t":"文字的發明改變了全人類的歷史，因為人們終於能把所知的事記錄下來。"},{"w":"humidity","p":"n.","d":"the amount of water in the air","c":"濕度","s":"The humidity in Taipei is very high in summer, so clothes take a long time to dry even on sunny days.","t":"台北夏天的濕度很高，所以即使在晴天，衣服也要很久才會乾。","h":1},{"w":"humid","p":"adj.","d":"warm and wet (of air or weather)","c":"潮濕的","s":"The weather was so hot and humid that my shirt was wet after I walked only two blocks to the MRT station.","t":"天氣又熱又潮濕，我才走兩個街區到捷運站，襯衫就濕了。"},{"w":"dehumidifier","p":"n.","d":"a machine that takes water out of the air in a room","c":"除濕機","s":"We turn on the dehumidifier in the bedroom every night during the rainy season to keep the walls free of mold.","t":"雨季期間，我們每晚都在臥室開除濕機，讓牆壁不長黴。"},{"w":"high humidity","p":"n.phr.","d":"a lot of water in the air","c":"高濕度","s":"Because of the high humidity in the storeroom, the old books began to smell and some of their pages stuck together.","t":"由於儲藏室濕度高，舊書開始發出味道，有些書頁還黏在一起。"},{"w":"hurricane","p":"n.","d":"a violent storm with very strong winds, especially in the Atlantic","c":"颶風","s":"When the hurricane hit the coast of Florida, thousands of people had to leave their homes and move to safer places inland.","t":"當颶風襲擊佛羅里達海岸時，數千人不得不離開家園，搬到內陸較安全的地方。","h":1},{"w":"hurricane season","p":"n.phr.","d":"the months when hurricanes usually happen","c":"颶風季","s":"Hotels on the islands are much cheaper during the hurricane season, but your holiday may be ruined by heavy storms.","t":"颶風季期間島上的飯店便宜許多，但你的假期可能會被強烈風暴毀掉。"},{"w":"hurricane warning","p":"n.phr.","d":"an official message that a hurricane is coming","c":"颶風警報","s":"As soon as the hurricane warning was announced on TV, people rushed to the supermarket to buy water, bread, and batteries.","t":"電視一宣布颶風警報，人們就衝到超市買水、麵包和電池。"},{"w":"hush","p":"n.","d":"a sudden silence","c":"寂靜；安靜","s":"A hush fell over the crowd as the judge stood up to announce the winner of the singing contest.","t":"當評審站起來宣布歌唱比賽的優勝者時，人群中一片寂靜。","h":1},{"w":"hush","p":"v.","d":"to make someone quiet; to become quiet","c":"使安靜；噓","s":"The mother tried to hush her crying baby on the train, but the little boy kept screaming for another ten minutes.","t":"媽媽試著讓火車上哭鬧的寶寶安靜下來，但小男孩又尖叫了十分鐘。"},{"w":"hush up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep something secret so that people do not find out","c":"掩蓋；隱瞞","s":"The company tried to hush up the accident at the factory, but a worker told the newspaper what had really happened.","t":"公司試圖掩蓋工廠的事故，但一名工人把真正發生的事告訴了報社。"},{"w":"hushed","p":"adj.","d":"quiet; in a low voice","c":"低聲的；寂靜的","s":"The visitors spoke in hushed voices as they walked through the old temple, because a group of monks was praying inside.","t":"遊客走過古寺時用低聲交談，因為一群和尚正在裡面祈禱。"},{"w":"hydrogen","p":"n.","d":"the lightest gas, which has no color or smell","c":"氫","s":"Water is made of two kinds of atoms, hydrogen and oxygen, and this is why scientists write it as H2O.","t":"水是由兩種原子氫和氧組成的，這就是科學家把它寫成 H2O 的原因。","h":1},{"w":"hydrogen bomb","p":"n.phr.","d":"an extremely powerful nuclear bomb","c":"氫彈","s":"A single hydrogen bomb could destroy a whole city, so many countries have signed agreements never to use such weapons.","t":"一顆氫彈就能摧毀整座城市，所以許多國家簽署了協議，承諾永不使用這類武器。"},{"w":"hydrogen fuel","p":"n.phr.","d":"hydrogen used to power cars and machines","c":"氫燃料","s":"Some new buses in the city run on hydrogen fuel instead of gasoline, so they produce only water and no dirty smoke.","t":"市區有些新公車用氫燃料而不是汽油行駛，所以只排出水，不會排放髒煙。"},{"w":"identical","p":"adj.","d":"exactly the same","c":"完全相同的","s":"The two paintings look identical at first, but if you look closely, one of them has a tiny bird in the corner.","t":"這兩幅畫起初看起來完全相同，但如果你仔細看，其中一幅角落裡有一隻小鳥。","h":1},{"w":"identical twins","p":"n.phr.","d":"two brothers or sisters born at the same time who look exactly alike","c":"同卵雙胞胎","s":"Ken and Ben are identical twins, so even their teachers sometimes call them by the wrong names in class.","t":"阿肯和阿班是同卵雙胞胎，所以連老師有時也會在課堂上叫錯他們的名字。"},{"w":"identical to","p":"adj.phr.","d":"exactly the same as","c":"與…完全相同","s":"The bag she bought at the night market is identical to the one in the department store, but it cost only one third of the price.","t":"她在夜市買的包包與百貨公司的那個一模一樣，但價格只有三分之一。"},{"w":"identically","p":"adv.","d":"in exactly the same way","c":"完全相同地","s":"The two sisters were dressed identically in red skirts and white shirts, so people thought they were twins.","t":"這兩姊妹穿得一模一樣，都是紅裙子和白襯衫，所以大家以為她們是雙胞胎。"},{"w":"identity","p":"n.","d":"who a person is; the qualities that make a person or group different from others","c":"身分；特性","s":"The police asked the man to show his ID card to prove his identity before they let him into the building.","t":"警察要求那名男子出示身分證以證明他的身分，然後才讓他進入大樓。"}]},{"unit":21,"theme":"identification – infant","cards":[{"w":"identification","p":"n.","d":"proof of who you are, such as a passport; the act of recognizing someone or something","c":"身分證明；辨認","s":"You need to show some form of identification, such as a passport or a student card, before you can pick up the package.","t":"你必須出示某種身分證明，例如護照或學生證，才能領取包裹。","h":1},{"w":"identify","p":"v.","d":"to recognize someone or something and say who or what they are","c":"辨認；確認","s":"The police asked the shop owner to identify the thief from a group of photos, and she picked him out at once.","t":"警察請店主從一組照片中指認小偷，她立刻就認出他了。","h":1},{"w":"ID card","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small official card that proves who you are","c":"身分證","s":"Everyone in Taiwan must carry an ID card after the age of fourteen, and you need it to open a bank account.","t":"在台灣，每個人年滿十四歲後都必須持有身分證，開銀行帳戶也需要它。"},{"w":"identify with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel that you understand and share the feelings of someone","c":"認同；對…產生共鳴","s":"Many teenagers identify with the main character of the novel because she also feels lonely and misunderstood at school.","t":"許多青少年認同小說的主角，因為她在學校也感到孤單、不被理解。"},{"w":"identifiable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be recognized","c":"可辨認的","s":"The school uniform makes students easily identifiable on the street, so shop owners know which school they come from.","t":"校服讓學生在街上很容易被辨認出來，所以店家知道他們來自哪所學校。"},{"w":"idiom","p":"n.","d":"a group of words whose meaning is different from the meanings of the separate words","c":"成語；慣用語","s":"\"It is raining cats and dogs\" is an English idiom that means it is raining very heavily, not that animals are falling.","t":"「It is raining cats and dogs」是一個英文成語，意思是雨下得很大，而不是動物從天上掉下來。","h":1},{"w":"idiomatic","p":"adj.","d":"using words in a natural way that sounds like a native speaker","c":"慣用的；道地的","s":"After living in Australia for five years, my cousin speaks very idiomatic English and even tells jokes like a local.","t":"在澳洲住了五年後，我表哥說著非常道地的英文，甚至能像當地人一樣講笑話。"},{"w":"idiomatic expression","p":"n.phr.","d":"a phrase with a special meaning that native speakers often use","c":"慣用語","s":"\"Break a leg\" is an idiomatic expression that actors use to wish each other good luck before a show.","t":"「Break a leg」是演員在演出前用來互相祝好運的慣用語。"},{"w":"idle","p":"adj.","d":"not working or being used; lazy","c":"閒置的；懶散的","s":"The old factory has stood idle for ten years, and now the city wants to turn it into a park with a museum.","t":"這座舊工廠已經閒置十年，現在市政府想把它改成有博物館的公園。","h":1},{"w":"idle","p":"v.","d":"to spend time doing nothing; (of an engine) to run slowly without moving","c":"閒混；（引擎）空轉","s":"Please do not let the car engine idle in the parking lot, because it wastes gas and makes the air dirty.","t":"請不要讓汽車引擎在停車場空轉，因為這會浪費汽油又污染空氣。"},{"w":"idle away","p":"v.phr.","d":"to waste time doing nothing useful","c":"虛度（時光）","s":"Instead of studying for the test, my brother idled away the whole afternoon playing games on his phone.","t":"我弟弟沒有準備考試，反而整個下午都用手機玩遊戲虛度了。","a":"idled away"},{"w":"idly","p":"adv.","d":"without doing anything; without a real purpose","c":"無所事事地；懶散地","s":"We sat idly by the river for an hour, watching the boats go by and talking about nothing in particular.","t":"我們懶散地在河邊坐了一個小時，看著船隻經過，隨意聊天。"},{"w":"idleness","p":"n.","d":"the state of doing nothing or not working","c":"閒散；無所事事","s":"After a week of idleness during the holiday, I was actually happy to go back to school and see my friends again.","t":"假期無所事事了一個星期之後，我其實很高興回到學校再見到朋友。"},{"w":"idol","p":"n.","d":"a famous person who is loved and admired very much; a statue that people pray to","c":"偶像","s":"Thousands of fans waited outside the airport for hours just to see their idol walk past for a few seconds.","t":"數千名粉絲在機場外等了好幾個小時，只為了看他們的偶像走過幾秒鐘。","h":1},{"w":"pop idol","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very popular singer, especially one loved by young people","c":"流行偶像","s":"My sister dreams of becoming a pop idol, so she practices singing and dancing in front of the mirror every night.","t":"我妹妹夢想成為流行偶像，所以她每晚都在鏡子前練習唱歌和跳舞。"},{"w":"idolize","p":"v.","d":"to love and admire someone very much, often too much","c":"崇拜","s":"Many young players idolize the famous basketball star, and they copy his hairstyle and even the way he walks.","t":"許多年輕球員崇拜這位著名的籃球明星，他們模仿他的髮型，甚至走路的方式。"},{"w":"ignorance","p":"n.","d":"lack of knowledge or information about something","c":"無知","s":"Many people throw batteries into the normal trash out of ignorance, not knowing that they can poison the soil and water.","t":"許多人因為無知把電池丟進一般垃圾，不知道電池會毒害土壤和水。","h":1},{"w":"ignorant","p":"adj.","d":"not knowing about something; not educated","c":"無知的；不知道的","s":"I was completely ignorant about the history of my own city until our teacher took us on a walking tour last month.","t":"直到上個月老師帶我們徒步導覽，我對自己城市的歷史一直完全一無所知。","h":1},{"w":"ignore","p":"v.","d":"to pay no attention to someone or something","c":"忽視；不理會","s":"If your classmates say unkind things, the best thing is to ignore them and tell a teacher instead of fighting back.","t":"如果同學說不友善的話，最好的做法是不理會他們並告訴老師，而不是反擊。"},{"w":"be ignorant of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not know about something","c":"不知道…","s":"Most tourists are ignorant of the local custom, so they wear shoes inside the temple without realizing it is rude.","t":"大多數遊客不知道當地的習俗，所以他們穿著鞋子進入寺廟，沒意識到這很失禮。","a":"are ignorant of"},{"w":"in ignorance of","p":"prep.","d":"without knowing about","c":"不知道…；不了解…","s":"The family continued their picnic in ignorance of the typhoon warning, because nobody had checked the news that morning.","t":"這家人不知道颱風警報，繼續他們的野餐，因為那天早上沒有人看新聞。"},{"w":"illustrate","p":"v.","d":"to explain something by giving examples; to draw pictures for a book","c":"說明；舉例說明；為…畫插圖","s":"To illustrate how plants drink water, the teacher put a white flower in a glass of blue water and let us watch it change.","t":"為了說明植物如何吸水，老師把一朵白花放進一杯藍色的水裡，讓我們觀察它的變化。","h":1},{"w":"illustration","p":"n.","d":"a picture in a book; an example that explains something","c":"插圖；例證","s":"The children's book is full of colorful illustrations, so even kids who cannot read yet enjoy looking at every page.","t":"這本童書充滿了色彩豐富的插圖，所以連還不識字的孩子也喜歡看每一頁。","a":"illustrations","h":1},{"w":"illustrator","p":"n.","d":"a person who draws pictures for books or magazines","c":"插畫家","s":"Jimmy Liao is a famous Taiwanese illustrator whose gentle pictures of lonely children have been loved by readers around the world.","t":"幾米是著名的台灣插畫家，他筆下孤單孩子的溫柔圖畫深受世界各地讀者喜愛。"},{"w":"illustrated","p":"adj.","d":"having pictures in it","c":"有插圖的","s":"My grandfather gave me an illustrated book about birds, and I spent the whole weekend trying to find them in the park.","t":"爺爺送我一本有插圖的鳥類書籍，我整個週末都在公園裡試著找出那些鳥。"},{"w":"imaginary","p":"adj.","d":"existing only in your mind, not real","c":"想像的；虛構的","s":"When my little brother was four, he had an imaginary friend named Bobo who always sat next to him at dinner.","t":"我弟弟四歲時有一個名叫波波的想像朋友，吃晚餐時總是坐在他旁邊。","h":1},{"w":"imaginative","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing new and interesting ideas","c":"富有想像力的","s":"The art teacher praised Lily for her imaginative painting, which showed a city floating in the sky above a forest of giant mushrooms.","t":"美術老師稱讚莉莉富有想像力的畫作，畫中一座城市漂浮在巨型蘑菇森林上方的天空中。","h":1},{"w":"imagine","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture or idea of something in your mind","c":"想像","s":"Close your eyes and imagine that you are lying on a warm beach, listening to the waves and feeling the soft sand.","t":"閉上眼睛，想像你正躺在溫暖的海灘上，聽著海浪，感受柔軟的沙子。"},{"w":"imagination","p":"n.","d":"the ability to form pictures and ideas in your mind","c":"想像力","s":"Writing stories is a great way for children to use their imagination, and it also helps them learn new words.","t":"寫故事是孩子運用想像力的好方法，也能幫助他們學習新單字。"},{"w":"imaginary friend","p":"n.phr.","d":"a friend that a child invents in their mind","c":"想像中的朋友","s":"Having an imaginary friend is normal for young children, and doctors say it may even help them learn to talk and share.","t":"有想像中的朋友對幼童來說很正常，醫生說這甚至可能幫助他們學習說話和分享。"},{"w":"use one's imagination","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think of new ideas instead of copying","c":"發揮想像力","s":"The teacher told us to use our imagination and design a machine that could help old people carry heavy bags up the stairs.","t":"老師要我們發揮想像力，設計一台能幫助老人提重物上樓的機器。","a":"use our imagination"},{"w":"imitate","p":"v.","d":"to copy the way someone speaks or acts","c":"模仿","s":"Babies learn to talk by trying to imitate the sounds and words that they hear from their parents every day.","t":"嬰兒透過試著模仿每天從父母那裡聽到的聲音和字詞來學說話。","h":1},{"w":"imitation","p":"n.","d":"a copy of something, often not as good as the real thing; the act of copying","c":"仿製品；模仿","s":"The watch looked expensive, but it was only a cheap imitation that stopped working after two weeks.","t":"這只手錶看起來很貴，但它只是個便宜的仿製品，兩個星期後就不走了。","h":1},{"w":"in imitation of","p":"prep.","d":"copying the style or actions of","c":"模仿…","s":"The new shopping mall was built in imitation of an old European town, with narrow streets and small colorful houses.","t":"這座新購物中心是模仿歐洲古鎮建造的，有狹窄的街道和色彩繽紛的小房子。"},{"w":"imitation leather","p":"n.phr.","d":"a material made to look like leather","c":"仿皮；人造皮","s":"This bag is made of imitation leather, so it costs much less than a real one but looks almost the same from a distance.","t":"這個包包是仿皮做的，所以價格比真皮便宜很多，但從遠處看幾乎一樣。"},{"w":"immigrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who comes to live in a foreign country","c":"移民（移入者）","s":"Many of the workers at the restaurant are immigrants from Vietnam, and they cook the most delicious noodle soup in town.","t":"餐廳裡的許多員工是來自越南的移民，他們煮的湯麵是鎮上最好吃的。","a":"immigrants","h":1},{"w":"immigrate","p":"v.","d":"to come into a foreign country in order to live there","c":"移民（移入）","s":"My grandparents decided to immigrate to Canada in 1990 because they wanted their children to study in English.","t":"我的祖父母在1990年決定移民到加拿大，因為他們希望孩子用英文學習。","h":1},{"w":"immigration","p":"n.","d":"the process of coming to live in a foreign country; the office at an airport that checks passports","c":"移民；入境檢查處","s":"After the long flight, we waited forty minutes at immigration while the officer checked our passports and asked a few questions.","t":"長途飛行之後，我們在入境檢查處等了四十分鐘，官員檢查我們的護照並問了幾個問題。","h":1},{"w":"immigrate to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move to a country in order to live there","c":"移民到…","s":"Thousands of people immigrate to Australia every year, hoping to find better jobs and a quieter life near the sea.","t":"每年有數千人移民到澳洲，希望找到更好的工作和海邊更安靜的生活。"},{"w":"emigrate","p":"v.","d":"to leave your own country to live in another one","c":"移居國外（移出）","s":"My uncle plans to emigrate from Taiwan next year, and he is already selling his house and learning German.","t":"我叔叔計畫明年從台灣移居國外，他已經在賣房子和學德文了。"},{"w":"migrant","p":"n.","d":"a person who moves from one place to another to find work","c":"移工；遷徙者","s":"During the harvest season, hundreds of migrant workers arrive in the valley to help pick fruit on the big farms.","t":"收成季節期間，數百名移工來到山谷，幫忙在大農場採摘水果。"},{"w":"impact","p":"n.","d":"a strong effect that something has on someone or something","c":"影響；衝擊","s":"Smartphones have had a huge impact on the way teenagers talk to each other, both at school and at home.","t":"智慧型手機對青少年在學校和家裡彼此交談的方式產生了巨大的影響。","h":1},{"w":"impact","p":"n.","d":"the force of one thing hitting another","c":"撞擊；衝擊力","s":"The car hit the wall at high speed, and the impact was so strong that the front of the car was completely crushed.","t":"汽車高速撞上牆壁，撞擊力道強到車頭完全被壓扁。"},{"w":"impact","p":"v.","d":"to have a strong effect on something","c":"影響；衝擊","s":"Rising sea levels will impact millions of people who live in low coastal cities over the next fifty years.","t":"海平面上升將在未來五十年內衝擊數百萬住在低窪沿海城市的人。"},{"w":"have an impact on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to affect something strongly","c":"對…有影響","s":"The new bike lanes have had an impact on the city, because many people now ride to work instead of driving.","t":"新的自行車道對這座城市產生了影響，因為現在許多人騎車上班而不開車。","a":"have had an impact on"},{"w":"imply","p":"v.","d":"to suggest something without saying it directly","c":"暗示；意味著","s":"When the teacher said that some students had not tried their best, she seemed to imply that she was talking about us.","t":"當老師說有些學生沒有盡力時，她似乎在暗示她說的是我們。","h":1},{"w":"implication","p":"n.","d":"something that is suggested but not said directly; a possible result","c":"暗示；含意；影響","s":"The implication of the report is clear: if we keep wasting water, the city will face serious shortages within ten years.","t":"這份報告的含意很清楚：如果我們繼續浪費水，這座城市十年內就會面臨嚴重缺水。"},{"w":"implied","p":"adj.","d":"suggested but not said directly","c":"暗示的；含蓄的","s":"There was an implied warning in the coach's words: anyone who missed practice again would not play in the final game.","t":"教練的話裡有一個含蓄的警告：再缺席練習的人就不能參加決賽。"},{"w":"implicit","p":"adj.","d":"understood without being said directly","c":"不言明的；隱含的","s":"In our family there is an implicit rule that nobody uses a phone at the dinner table, even though Mom never said it aloud.","t":"在我們家有個不言明的規矩：餐桌上沒有人用手機，雖然媽媽從沒大聲說過。"},{"w":"impose","p":"v.","d":"to force a rule, tax, or punishment on people","c":"強制實施；徵收","s":"The government decided to impose a new tax on sugary drinks to encourage people to choose water or tea instead.","t":"政府決定對含糖飲料徵收新稅，以鼓勵人們改選水或茶。","h":1},{"w":"impose on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause trouble for someone by asking too much of them; to force something on someone","c":"打擾；把…強加於","s":"I do not want to impose on you, but could I stay at your apartment for two nights while my house is being painted?","t":"我不想打擾你，但我家在粉刷時，可以在你的公寓住兩晚嗎？"},{"w":"imposing","p":"adj.","d":"large and impressive","c":"雄偉的；壯觀的","s":"The imposing building at the end of the street used to be a bank, and its stone columns are over twenty meters high.","t":"街尾那棟雄偉的建築以前是銀行，它的石柱超過二十公尺高。"},{"w":"imposition","p":"n.","d":"the act of forcing a rule or payment on people; an unreasonable request","c":"強制實施；強加；過分的要求","s":"Many drivers felt that the sudden imposition of a parking fee in the old town was unfair, so they wrote letters to the mayor.","t":"許多駕駛認為在老城區突然強制收取停車費不公平，所以他們寫信給市長。"},{"w":"impression","p":"n.","d":"an idea or feeling you have about someone or something","c":"印象","s":"The new student made a very good impression on the class by helping to clean the room on her very first day.","t":"這位新同學第一天就幫忙打掃教室，給全班留下了很好的印象。","h":1},{"w":"impress","p":"v.","d":"to make someone admire or respect you","c":"使印象深刻；使欽佩","s":"Ken tried to impress the judges by playing the hardest piece on the piano, but he made several mistakes in the middle.","t":"阿肯試圖彈奏最難的鋼琴曲來讓評審印象深刻，但他在中間出了好幾個錯。"},{"w":"impressive","p":"adj.","d":"causing admiration because it is very good or large","c":"令人印象深刻的","s":"Taipei 101 is still an impressive sight at night, especially on New Year's Eve when fireworks shoot from its sides.","t":"台北101在夜晚仍是令人印象深刻的景象，尤其是跨年夜煙火從大樓側面射出時。"},{"w":"make a good impression","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make people like and respect you when they first meet you","c":"留下好印象","s":"If you want to make a good impression at the job interview, arrive early, dress neatly, and smile when you shake hands.","t":"如果你想在面試時留下好印象，要提早到、穿著整齊，握手時面帶微笑。"},{"w":"be under the impression that","p":"v.phr.","d":"to believe something, often wrongly","c":"以為…","s":"I was under the impression that the test was next Friday, so I was shocked when the teacher handed out the papers this morning.","t":"我以為考試是下星期五，所以今天早上老師發考卷時我嚇了一跳。","a":"was under the impression that"},{"w":"incident","p":"n.","d":"something that happens, especially something unusual or unpleasant","c":"事件；事故","s":"The school called the parents after the incident in the playground, in which two boys were hurt during a fight.","t":"操場上發生兩個男孩打架受傷的事件後，學校打電話給家長。","h":1},{"w":"without incident","p":"phr.","d":"without anything unusual or bad happening","c":"平安無事地","s":"The long bus ride through the mountains passed without incident, and we arrived at the hotel just before dinner.","t":"穿越山區的長途巴士之旅平安無事，我們在晚餐前剛好抵達飯店。"},{"w":"incidental","p":"adj.","d":"happening by chance or as a small, less important part of something","c":"附帶的；偶然的","s":"The hotel price includes breakfast, but incidental costs such as drinks and phone calls must be paid separately.","t":"飯店價格包含早餐，但飲料和電話等附帶的費用必須另外支付。"},{"w":"incidentally","p":"adv.","d":"used to add something that is not the main point; by the way","c":"順帶一提","s":"Incidentally, the restaurant we are going to tonight is the same one where my parents had their first date thirty years ago.","t":"順帶一提，我們今晚要去的餐廳就是我父母三十年前第一次約會的那家。","a":"Incidentally"},{"w":"including","p":"prep.","d":"having something as part of a group or total","c":"包括","s":"The trip to Japan costs 35,000 dollars, including the plane ticket, the hotel, and breakfast every morning.","t":"日本之旅的費用是三萬五千元，包括機票、飯店和每天早餐。","h":1},{"w":"include","p":"v.","d":"to have something as a part; to put something in a group","c":"包括；包含","s":"Does the price of the meal include a drink, or do we have to pay extra for the tea and the juice?","t":"餐點的價格包含飲料嗎？還是茶和果汁要另外付費？"},{"w":"inclusion","p":"n.","d":"the act of including someone or something; making everyone feel part of a group","c":"納入；包容","s":"The inclusion of students with disabilities in regular classes helps everyone in the school learn to respect differences.","t":"將身心障礙學生納入普通班級，有助於學校裡的每個人學會尊重差異。"},{"w":"inclusive","p":"adj.","d":"including everyone or everything","c":"包容的；包含一切的","s":"The club tries to be inclusive, so students of every age, ability, and background are welcome to join its activities.","t":"這個社團努力做到包容，所以各年齡、能力和背景的學生都歡迎參加它的活動。"},{"w":"excluding","p":"prep.","d":"not including","c":"不包括","s":"The hotel room costs 3,000 dollars a night excluding breakfast, which you can add for 300 dollars per person.","t":"飯店房間一晚三千元，不包括早餐，早餐可以每人加三百元。"},{"w":"exclude","p":"v.","d":"to keep someone or something out; to not include","c":"排除；不包括","s":"The coach decided to exclude two players from the team because they had missed practice five times without a reason.","t":"教練決定把兩名球員排除在隊伍之外，因為他們無故缺席練習五次。"},{"w":"incredible","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good, large, or surprising; amazing","c":"驚人的；極好的","s":"The view from the top of the mountain was incredible, and we could see the whole city and the sea beyond it.","t":"從山頂看到的景色美得驚人，我們能看到整座城市和它後面的大海。","h":1},{"w":"incredible","p":"adj.","d":"impossible or very hard to believe","c":"難以置信的","s":"It seems incredible that a ten-year-old boy swam across the river alone, but three people saw him do it.","t":"一個十歲男孩獨自游過那條河似乎難以置信，但有三個人親眼看到他做到了。"},{"w":"incredibly","p":"adv.","d":"extremely; in a way that is hard to believe","c":"極其；難以置信地","s":"The new phone is incredibly thin, and it weighs less than a small bar of chocolate, so you hardly feel it in your pocket.","t":"這款新手機極其輕薄，重量比一小條巧克力還輕，所以放在口袋裡幾乎感覺不到。"},{"w":"credible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be believed or trusted","c":"可信的","s":"The news story did not seem credible to me, because the website gave no names and no proof for its claims.","t":"這則新聞對我來說似乎不太可信，因為那個網站沒有提供任何姓名或證據。"},{"w":"indication","p":"n.","d":"a sign that shows something is true or is happening","c":"跡象；指標","s":"Dark clouds and a sudden cold wind are usually a clear indication that a heavy rainstorm is on its way.","t":"烏雲和突然的冷風通常是暴雨即將來臨的明顯跡象。","h":1},{"w":"indicate","p":"v.","d":"to show or point to something; to be a sign of","c":"指出；顯示；表明","s":"The red light on the machine will indicate that the water is hot enough, so please wait until you see it.","t":"機器上的紅燈會顯示水已經夠熱了，所以請等到你看到紅燈亮起。"},{"w":"indicator","p":"n.","d":"something that shows what a situation is like or how it is changing","c":"指標；指示器","s":"The number of tourists is a good indicator of how well the city's economy is doing this year.","t":"觀光客人數是今年這座城市經濟狀況好壞的一個很好的指標。"},{"w":"give an indication of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show roughly what something is like","c":"顯示；透露…的情況","s":"The first ten minutes of a movie usually give an indication of whether it is going to be exciting or boring.","t":"電影的前十分鐘通常能透露它會是精彩還是無聊。"},{"w":"infant","p":"n.","d":"a baby or very young child","c":"嬰兒；幼兒","s":"The nurse showed the new parents how to hold the infant safely and how to give her a bath without getting water in her eyes.","t":"護士教新手父母如何安全地抱嬰兒，以及如何幫她洗澡而不讓水進到眼睛。","h":1},{"w":"infancy","p":"n.","d":"the time when you are a baby","c":"嬰兒期","s":"My grandmother says I hardly ever cried in infancy, but my mother remembers many sleepless nights.","t":"我奶奶說我在嬰兒時期幾乎不哭，但我媽媽記得許多個不眠之夜。"},{"w":"in its infancy","p":"phr.","d":"at a very early stage of development","c":"處於初期階段","s":"Electric flying taxis are still in their infancy, but some companies hope to carry passengers across cities within ten years.","t":"電動飛行計程車仍處於初期階段，但有些公司希望十年內能載客跨越城市。","a":"in their infancy"},{"w":"infantile","p":"adj.","d":"behaving like a small child; childish","c":"幼稚的","s":"Throwing your controller on the floor when you lose a game is infantile behavior for a sixteen-year-old boy.","t":"輸了遊戲就把控制器摔在地上，對一個十六歲男孩來說是幼稚的行為。"}]},{"unit":22,"theme":"infection – intensive","cards":[{"w":"infection","p":"n.","d":"an illness caused by germs getting into the body","c":"感染","s":"The doctor said the cut on my hand had a small infection, so I need to clean it and take medicine for a week.","t":"醫生說我手上的傷口有輕微感染，所以我需要清潔傷口並吃一週的藥。","h":1},{"w":"infect","p":"v.","d":"to pass a disease or germs to a person, animal, or thing","c":"感染；傳染","s":"If you cough without covering your mouth, you may infect the people around you, especially on a crowded bus.","t":"如果你咳嗽時不遮住嘴巴，可能會傳染給周圍的人，尤其是在擠滿人的公車上。"},{"w":"infectious","p":"adj.","d":"able to spread from one person to another","c":"傳染性的","s":"The flu is highly infectious, so students with a fever should stay home instead of coming to school.","t":"流感具有高度傳染性，所以發燒的學生應該待在家裡，而不是來上學。"},{"w":"be infected with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a disease because germs have entered your body","c":"感染（某種疾病）","s":"After drinking the dirty water, several hikers were infected with a stomach virus and had to visit the hospital that night.","t":"喝了髒水之後，幾位登山客感染了腸胃病毒，當晚不得不去醫院。","a":"were infected with"},{"w":"inflation","p":"n.","d":"a general rise in prices over time","c":"通貨膨脹","s":"Because of inflation, a bowl of beef noodles that cost 100 dollars five years ago now costs almost 150.","t":"由於通貨膨脹，五年前一碗一百元的牛肉麵現在要將近一百五十元。","h":1},{"w":"inflate","p":"v.","d":"to fill something with air; to make prices or numbers go up","c":"使充氣；使上漲","s":"Before the party, we used a small pump to inflate fifty balloons, and the whole room looked colorful and fun.","t":"派對開始前，我們用一個小打氣筒充氣五十個氣球，整個房間看起來五彩繽紛又有趣。"},{"w":"inflation rate","p":"n.phr.","d":"the speed at which prices rise, shown as a percent","c":"通貨膨脹率","s":"The news reported that the inflation rate reached three percent this year, so many families are spending less on eating out.","t":"新聞報導今年的通貨膨脹率達到百分之三，所以許多家庭減少了外食的花費。"},{"w":"influential","p":"adj.","d":"having the power to change how people think or act","c":"有影響力的","s":"She is one of the most influential teachers in our school because many students chose their careers after taking her class.","t":"她是我們學校最有影響力的老師之一，因為許多學生上了她的課後決定了自己的職業。","h":1},{"w":"influence","p":"n.","d":"the power to change someone or something","c":"影響；影響力","s":"Parents have a strong influence on their children, so kids often copy the way their mother and father speak and eat.","t":"父母對孩子有很大的影響，所以孩子常常模仿爸媽說話和吃東西的方式。"},{"w":"influence","p":"v.","d":"to change the way someone thinks or acts","c":"影響","s":"Advertisements on social media can influence teenagers to buy things they do not really need, such as expensive sneakers.","t":"社群媒體上的廣告可能會影響青少年去買他們其實不需要的東西，例如昂貵的球鞋。"},{"w":"have an influence on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to affect someone or something","c":"對…有影響","s":"The weather can have an influence on our mood, and many people feel sad and tired after several days of heavy rain.","t":"天氣會對我們的心情有影響，許多人在連續幾天大雨之後會覺得難過又疲倦。"},{"w":"informative","p":"adj.","d":"giving a lot of useful facts and information","c":"資訊豐富的；有教育性的","s":"The museum guide was so informative that we learned more about Taiwan's history in one hour than in a whole semester.","t":"博物館導覽員講解得非常有知識性，我們在一小時內學到的台灣歷史比整個學期還多。","h":1},{"w":"inform","p":"v.","d":"to tell someone about something officially","c":"通知；告知","s":"The school will inform parents by text message if classes are canceled because of the typhoon tomorrow morning.","t":"如果明天早上因颱風停課，學校會用簡訊通知家長。"},{"w":"information","p":"n.","d":"facts or details about something","c":"資訊；訊息","s":"You can find all the information about the school trip, including the price and the date, on the notice board.","t":"你可以在公告欄上找到關於學校旅行的所有資訊，包括價格和日期。"},{"w":"inform sb of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to tell someone about something","c":"告知某人某事","s":"The airline sent an email to inform us of the change in our flight time, so we arrived at the airport two hours later.","t":"航空公司寄了電子郵件告知我們航班時間的變更，所以我們晚了兩小時才到機場。","a":"inform us of"},{"w":"ingredient","p":"n.","d":"one of the foods you use to make a dish","c":"（食物的）成分；材料","s":"Flour, eggs, and sugar are the main ingredients of this cake, so you probably already have everything in your kitchen.","t":"麵粉、雞蛋和糖是這個蛋糕的主要材料，所以你的廚房裡可能已經有所有東西了。","a":"ingredients","h":1},{"w":"ingredient","p":"n.","d":"a quality that is needed to make something successful","c":"（成功的）要素","s":"Hard work is an important ingredient of success, but good friends and a little luck also help a lot.","t":"努力是成功的重要要素，但好朋友和一點運氣也很有幫助。"},{"w":"key ingredient","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most important thing needed for something","c":"關鍵成分；關鍵要素","s":"Fresh ginger is the key ingredient in my grandmother's soup, and without it the soup tastes completely different.","t":"新鮮的薑是我奶奶那道湯的關鍵材料，少了它湯的味道就完全不一樣。"},{"w":"initial","p":"adj.","d":"happening at the beginning; first","c":"最初的；開始的","s":"My initial plan was to study medicine, but after one year at university I decided to become a teacher instead.","t":"我最初的計畫是讀醫學，但在大學讀了一年後，我決定改當老師。","h":1},{"w":"initially","p":"adv.","d":"at the beginning; at first","c":"起初；最初","s":"Initially, I did not like my new roommate because he was very quiet, but now we are the best of friends.","t":"起初我不喜歡我的新室友，因為他很安靜，但現在我們是最好的朋友。","a":"Initially"},{"w":"initial","p":"n.","d":"the first letter of a name","c":"（姓名的）首字母","s":"Please write your initials in the box at the bottom of each page to show that you have read it.","t":"請在每一頁底部的方框裡寫上你的姓名首字母，表示你已經讀過了。","a":"initials"},{"w":"initiate","p":"v.","d":"to make something start","c":"開始；發起","s":"The city government decided to initiate a recycling program that gives small rewards to families who sort their trash.","t":"市政府決定發起一項回收計畫，給垃圾分類做得好的家庭小獎勵。"},{"w":"initiative","p":"n.","d":"a new plan to solve a problem; the ability to act without being told","c":"新方案；主動性","s":"Instead of waiting for the teacher's instructions, Amy took the initiative and started cleaning the classroom by herself.","t":"艾咪沒有等老師的指示，而是主動自己開始打掃教室。"},{"w":"injure","p":"v.","d":"to hurt a person or animal, especially in an accident","c":"傷害；使受傷","s":"Wear a helmet when you ride a scooter, because a simple fall can seriously injure your head and neck.","t":"騎機車時要戴安全帽，因為一次簡單的摔倒就可能嚴重傷害你的頭部和頸部。","h":1},{"w":"injury","p":"n.","d":"harm done to a person's body","c":"傷害；受傷","s":"The basketball player had a knee injury last season, so he could not play in the final game of the year.","t":"那位籃球員上個球季膝蓋受傷，所以他無法參加年度最後一場比賽。"},{"w":"injured","p":"adj.","d":"hurt; having a wound or broken bone","c":"受傷的","s":"After the car accident, the injured driver was taken to the hospital, but luckily he only had a broken arm.","t":"車禍之後，受傷的駕駛被送往醫院，幸運的是他只有手臂骨折。"},{"w":"the injured","p":"n.","d":"people who have been hurt in an accident","c":"傷者","s":"After the earthquake, doctors and nurses worked all night to take care of the injured in the small town.","t":"地震過後，醫生和護士整夜工作，照顧小鎮上的傷者。"},{"w":"innocence","p":"n.","d":"the fact of not being guilty of a crime; lack of experience","c":"無辜；清白；純真","s":"The young man kept saying that he was not the thief, and a video from the store finally proved his innocence.","t":"那個年輕人一直說他不是小偷，店裡的影片最後證明了他的清白。","h":1},{"w":"innocent","p":"adj.","d":"not guilty of a crime; without experience of bad things","c":"無辜的；天真的","s":"The police later found that the man was innocent, so they let him go home and said sorry to his family.","t":"警方後來發現那名男子是無辜的，所以放他回家並向他的家人道歉。"},{"w":"innocently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows no bad intention or experience","c":"無辜地；天真地","s":"The little girl innocently asked why the moon follows our car, and everyone in the family laughed warmly.","t":"小女孩天真地問為什麼月亮一直跟著我們的車，全家人都溫暖地笑了。"},{"w":"prove one's innocence","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show that you did not do something wrong","c":"證明某人的清白","s":"The lawyer worked for two years to prove his innocence, and in the end the court agreed that he had done nothing wrong.","t":"律師努力了兩年來證明他的清白，最後法庭同意他沒有做錯任何事。","a":"prove his innocence"},{"w":"input","p":"n.","d":"information that is put into a computer or system","c":"輸入（的資料）","s":"The program could not run because of a mistake in the input, so the engineer checked every number again.","t":"程式因為輸入資料有錯誤而無法運行，所以工程師又把每個數字檢查了一遍。","h":1},{"w":"input","p":"v.","d":"to put information into a computer","c":"輸入","s":"You need to input your student number and password before you can see your test scores on the school website.","t":"你需要先輸入學號和密碼，才能在學校網站上看到你的考試成績。"},{"w":"input","p":"n.","d":"ideas or help that you give to make something better","c":"意見；貢獻","s":"Thank you for your input at the meeting; your ideas about the school fair will make the event much better.","t":"感謝你在會議上的意見；你關於校慶園遊會的想法會讓活動好很多。"},{"w":"insert","p":"v.","d":"to put something inside something else","c":"插入；放入","s":"To use the machine, insert a coin into the slot, press the green button, and wait for your drink to come out.","t":"要使用這台機器，請把硬幣投入投幣口，按下綠色按鈕，然後等飲料出來。","h":1},{"w":"insertion","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting something inside something else","c":"插入","s":"The insertion of one short sentence at the beginning of the paragraph made the whole story much clearer to readers.","t":"在段落開頭插入一個短句，讓整個故事對讀者來說清楚得多。"},{"w":"insert A into B","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put one thing inside another","c":"把A插入B","s":"The nurse carefully inserted the needle into the patient's arm and told him that it would hurt for only a second.","t":"護士小心地把針插入病人的手臂，並告訴他只會痛一秒鐘。","a":"inserted"},{"w":"inspection","p":"n.","d":"a careful check to see if something is correct or safe","c":"檢查；視察","s":"The restaurant passed the health inspection with a perfect score, so the owner put the report on the wall by the door.","t":"這家餐廳以滿分通過了衛生檢查，所以老闆把報告貼在門邊的牆上。","h":1},{"w":"inspect","p":"v.","d":"to look at something carefully to check it","c":"檢查；審視","s":"Before you buy a used bike, inspect the brakes and the tires carefully, or you may have to pay for repairs later.","t":"買二手腳踏車之前，請仔細檢查煞車和輪胎，否則你以後可能得付修理費。"},{"w":"inspector","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to check things or places","c":"檢查員；督察","s":"An inspector from the city visited our factory this morning to make sure the workers were wearing safety equipment.","t":"今天早上一位市政府的檢查員來我們工廠，確認工人都有穿戴安全裝備。"},{"w":"carry out an inspection","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do an official check","c":"進行檢查","s":"Firefighters carried out an inspection of the old apartment building and found that half of the fire alarms did not work.","t":"消防員對那棟老公寓進行了檢查，發現一半的火災警報器都不能用。","a":"carried out an inspection"},{"w":"inspiration","p":"n.","d":"a person or thing that gives you new ideas or makes you want to do something","c":"靈感；啟發","s":"The artist said that the mountains near her hometown were the inspiration for most of the paintings in this show.","t":"這位藝術家說，她家鄉附近的山是這次展覽中大部分畫作的靈感來源。","h":1},{"w":"inspire","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something good or creative","c":"啟發；激勵","s":"Her story about learning to read at the age of sixty will inspire many people who think it is too late to study.","t":"她六十歲學會讀書的故事將激勵許多認為讀書太遲的人。","h":1},{"w":"inspiring","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel excited and able to do something","c":"激勵人心的","s":"The coach gave such an inspiring speech before the game that every player ran onto the court full of energy.","t":"教練在比賽前發表了一段非常激勵人心的演講，每位球員都充滿活力地衝上球場。"},{"w":"inspired","p":"adj.","d":"full of good ideas; feeling excited and creative","c":"受到啟發的；有靈感的","s":"After visiting the science museum, the children felt so inspired that they built their own small robot at home.","t":"參觀科學博物館後，孩子們深受啟發，於是在家裡做了一個自己的小機器人。"},{"w":"inspire sb to do sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone want to do something","c":"激勵某人去做某事","s":"My grandfather's garden inspired me to grow my own vegetables, so now I have tomatoes and peppers on my balcony.","t":"我爺爺的花園激勵我自己種蔬菜，所以現在我的陽台上有番茄和辣椒。","a":"inspired me to"},{"w":"install","p":"v.","d":"to put a machine or program in place so it can be used","c":"安裝","s":"The worker came to install a new air conditioner in our classroom, and now summer afternoons are much more comfortable.","t":"工人來我們教室安裝一台新冷氣，現在夏天的下午舒服多了。","h":1},{"w":"installation","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting a machine or system in place","c":"安裝","s":"The installation of the solar panels on the roof took three days, but now the family pays almost nothing for electricity.","t":"屋頂上太陽能板的安裝花了三天，但現在這家人幾乎不用付電費。"},{"w":"installment","p":"n.","d":"one of several regular payments for something","c":"分期付款（的一期）","s":"My brother bought his laptop in twelve monthly installments, so he only pays about two thousand dollars each month.","t":"我哥哥用十二期分期付款買了他的筆電，所以他每個月只要付大約兩千元。","a":"installments"},{"w":"instinct","p":"n.","d":"a natural way of behaving or feeling that you are born with","c":"本能；直覺","s":"Birds build their nests by instinct; nobody teaches them, yet every spring they know exactly what to do.","t":"鳥類靠本能築巢；沒有人教它們，但每年春天它們都清楚知道該怎麼做。","h":1},{"w":"instinctive","p":"adj.","d":"done naturally without thinking","c":"本能的；直覺的","s":"Closing your eyes when something flies toward your face is an instinctive reaction that protects you from getting hurt.","t":"當有東西朝你的臉飛來時閉上眼睛，是一種保護你不受傷的本能反應。"},{"w":"instinctively","p":"adv.","d":"in a natural way, without thinking first","c":"本能地；直覺地","s":"When the baby started to fall off the chair, the mother instinctively reached out and caught him just in time.","t":"當寶寶開始從椅子上掉下來時，媽媽本能地伸手及時接住了他。"},{"w":"have an instinct for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be naturally good at something","c":"對…有天生的才能","s":"Even as a child, my cousin had an instinct for business, selling homemade cookies to the neighbors every weekend.","t":"我表哥小時候就對做生意有天生的才能，每個週末都把自製餅乾賣給鄰居。","a":"had an instinct for"},{"w":"instruct","p":"v.","d":"to teach someone or tell them officially what to do","c":"教導；指示","s":"The lifeguard will instruct the children on how to swim safely before they are allowed to enter the deep pool.","t":"救生員會先教導孩子們如何安全游泳，然後才允許他們進入深水池。","h":1},{"w":"instructor","p":"n.","d":"a person who teaches a skill or sport","c":"教練；指導員","s":"Our yoga instructor always reminds us to breathe slowly, and she walks around the room to correct our positions.","t":"我們的瑜珈教練總是提醒我們慢慢呼吸，她會在教室裡走動糾正我們的姿勢。","h":1},{"w":"instruction","p":"n.","d":"teaching; information on how to do something","c":"教學；指導","s":"Students in this class receive two hours of instruction in English every day, and they practice speaking with partners.","t":"這個班的學生每天接受兩小時的英語教學，並和同伴練習口說。"},{"w":"follow the instructions","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do what the written or spoken directions tell you","c":"遵照說明","s":"If you follow the instructions on the box step by step, you can put the bookshelf together in less than an hour.","t":"如果你一步一步遵照盒子上的說明，不到一小時就可以把書架組裝好。"},{"w":"instructive","p":"adj.","d":"giving useful information or knowledge","c":"有教育意義的","s":"The documentary about ocean pollution was both interesting and instructive, so our teacher showed it to every class.","t":"那部關於海洋污染的紀錄片既有趣又有教育意義，所以我們老師放給每個班看。"},{"w":"insult","p":"v.","d":"to say or do something rude that hurts someone's feelings","c":"侮辱；辱罵","s":"You should never insult your classmates because of their looks, since words can hurt much more than you think.","t":"你永遠不應該因為同學的外表而侮辱他們，因為言語造成的傷害比你想的大得多。","h":1},{"w":"insult","p":"n.","d":"a rude remark or action","c":"侮辱","s":"Calling someone stupid in front of the whole class is a serious insult, and the teacher asked him to apologize.","t":"在全班面前說某人笨是一種嚴重的侮辱，老師要他道歉。"},{"w":"insulting","p":"adj.","d":"rude and hurting someone's feelings","c":"侮辱的；無禮的","s":"The comedian's jokes about old people were so insulting that many members of the audience stood up and left.","t":"那位喜劇演員拿老人開的玩笑太無禮了，許多觀眾起身離席。"},{"w":"insurance","p":"n.","d":"an agreement in which you pay money and a company pays if something bad happens","c":"保險","s":"Travel insurance is not expensive, but it can save you thousands of dollars if you get sick or lose your bag abroad.","t":"旅遊保險並不貴，但如果你在國外生病或掉了包包，它可以幫你省下好幾千元。","h":1},{"w":"insure","p":"v.","d":"to buy insurance for something","c":"為…投保","s":"Most people insure their cars against accidents, so the insurance company pays for repairs after a crash.","t":"大多數人會為他們的汽車投保意外險，所以撞車後由保險公司支付修理費。"},{"w":"insurance company","p":"n.phr.","d":"a business that sells insurance","c":"保險公司","s":"After the typhoon damaged our roof, my father called the insurance company, and they sent someone to check the house the next day.","t":"颱風毀壞我們的屋頂後，我爸爸打電話給保險公司，他們隔天就派人來檢查房子。"},{"w":"health insurance","p":"n.phr.","d":"insurance that pays for medical care","c":"健康保險；健保","s":"Thanks to the national health insurance system, a visit to the doctor in Taiwan usually costs only a few hundred dollars.","t":"多虧了全民健康保險制度，在台灣看一次醫生通常只要幾百元。"},{"w":"intellectual","p":"adj.","d":"connected with thinking and understanding ideas","c":"智力的；知識的","s":"Reading a good novel is an intellectual activity that makes your brain work much harder than watching short videos does.","t":"閱讀一本好小說是一種智力活動，比看短影片更能讓你的大腦努力運作。","h":1},{"w":"intellectual","p":"n.","d":"a well-educated person who enjoys thinking about ideas","c":"知識分子","s":"In the old days, many intellectuals met in coffee shops to talk about politics, art, and the future of their country.","t":"在過去，許多知識分子在咖啡館聚會，談論政治、藝術和國家的未來。","a":"intellectuals"},{"w":"intellect","p":"n.","d":"the ability to think and understand ideas","c":"智力；才智","s":"The scientist was famous not only for her sharp intellect but also for her kindness toward young students.","t":"這位科學家不僅以敏銳的才智聞名，也以她對年輕學生的親切著稱。"},{"w":"intellectual property","p":"n.phr.","d":"ideas or creations that legally belong to a person or company","c":"智慧財產","s":"Copying a song from the Internet without paying breaks intellectual property laws, so the website was closed down last month.","t":"不付費就從網路上複製歌曲違反了智慧財產法，所以那個網站上個月被關閉了。"},{"w":"intelligence","p":"n.","d":"the ability to learn, understand, and think","c":"智力；智慧","s":"Dolphins show great intelligence; they can learn tricks quickly and even seem to talk to each other with sounds.","t":"海豚展現出極高的智力；它們能快速學會技巧，甚至似乎能用聲音互相交談。","h":1},{"w":"intelligent","p":"adj.","d":"good at learning and understanding things; clever","c":"聰明的","s":"My dog is so intelligent that he brings me his bowl when he is hungry and waits quietly by the door for his walk.","t":"我的狗非常聰明，餓的時候會把碗拿給我，想散步時會安靜地在門邊等。"},{"w":"intelligently","p":"adv.","d":"in a clever and thoughtful way","c":"聰明地","s":"The young player answered the reporter's hard questions intelligently, and the coach smiled proudly beside him.","t":"那位年輕球員聰明地回答了記者的刁鑽問題，教練在他身旁自豪地微笑。"},{"w":"artificial intelligence","p":"n.phr.","d":"computer systems that can think and learn like people","c":"人工智慧","s":"Many phones now use artificial intelligence to understand your voice, so you can send a message just by speaking to them.","t":"現在許多手機使用人工智慧來理解你的聲音，所以你只要對它說話就能發送訊息。"},{"w":"intend","p":"v.","d":"to plan to do something","c":"打算；意圖","s":"We intend to visit our grandparents in Tainan this weekend, but we will stay home if the typhoon comes closer.","t":"我們打算這個週末去台南看爺爺奶奶，但如果颱風更接近，我們就會待在家。","h":1},{"w":"intend to do sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a plan to do something","c":"打算做某事","s":"I intended to finish my homework before dinner, but my friend called and we talked for almost two hours.","t":"我打算在晚餐前做完功課，但我朋友打電話來，我們聊了將近兩小時。","a":"intended to"},{"w":"intended","p":"adj.","d":"planned; meant for a particular person or purpose","c":"預期的；為…準備的","s":"This book is intended for young children, so the pictures are large and each page has only one short sentence.","t":"這本書是為幼兒準備的，所以圖片很大，每頁只有一個短句。"},{"w":"intention","p":"n.","d":"something you plan or want to do","c":"意圖；打算","s":"I had no intention of hurting your feelings when I joked about your haircut, and I am truly sorry.","t":"我拿你的髮型開玩笑時，完全沒有傷害你感情的意圖，我真的很抱歉。"},{"w":"intentional","p":"adj.","d":"done on purpose, not by accident","c":"故意的","s":"The referee decided that the push was intentional, so the player received a red card and had to leave the field.","t":"裁判判定那一推是故意的，所以該球員收到紅牌，必須離場。"},{"w":"intense","p":"adj.","d":"very strong or extreme","c":"強烈的；劇烈的","s":"The heat was so intense at noon that we had to stop playing basketball and rest in the shade for an hour.","t":"中午的熱氣非常強烈，我們不得不停止打籃球，在陰涼處休息一小時。","h":1},{"w":"intensity","p":"n.","d":"the strength or power of something","c":"強度；強烈","s":"The intensity of the earthquake surprised everyone, and books fell off the shelves in houses across the whole city.","t":"這次地震的強度讓每個人都很驚訝，全市住家的書都從書架上掉了下來。","h":1},{"w":"intensive","p":"adj.","d":"involving a lot of work or effort in a short time","c":"密集的；加強的","s":"Before the big exam, Tom took an intensive English course that met for four hours every day for two weeks.","t":"大考之前，湯姆上了一門密集英語課程，連續兩週每天上四小時。","h":1},{"w":"intensify","p":"v.","d":"to become stronger or make something stronger","c":"加強；增強","s":"The rain began to intensify in the afternoon, so the school sent all the students home two hours early.","t":"下午雨勢開始增強，所以學校提早兩小時讓所有學生回家。"},{"w":"intensely","p":"adv.","d":"very strongly; extremely","c":"強烈地；極度地","s":"She stared intensely at the chessboard for ten minutes before she finally moved her queen and won the game.","t":"她專注地盯著棋盤十分鐘，才終於移動皇后，贏得了比賽。"}]},{"unit":23,"theme":"intention – laboratorylab","cards":[{"w":"intention","p":"n.","d":"something you plan or want to do","c":"意圖；打算","s":"My intention was to study for only one hour, but the chapter was so interesting that I read until midnight.","t":"我的打算是只讀一小時，但那一章太有趣了，我一直讀到半夜。","h":1},{"w":"intend","p":"v.","d":"to plan to do something","c":"打算；意圖","s":"We intend to open the new coffee shop in March, but the furniture arrived late, so we moved the date to May.","t":"我們打算在三月開新咖啡店，但家具晚到了，所以我們把日期改到五月。"},{"w":"intentional","p":"adj.","d":"done on purpose, not by accident","c":"故意的","s":"The teacher believed that the broken window was not intentional, so she only asked the boys to be more careful next time.","t":"老師相信窗戶不是故意打破的，所以她只要求男孩們下次更小心。"},{"w":"intentionally","p":"adv.","d":"on purpose","c":"故意地","s":"Some players intentionally fall down during a soccer game so that the referee will give them a free kick.","t":"有些球員在足球比賽中故意跌倒，好讓裁判判給他們一個自由球。"},{"w":"have no intention of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not plan to do something at all","c":"完全沒有…的打算","s":"My grandfather has no intention of retiring, and he still goes to his small shop every morning at seven o'clock.","t":"我爺爺完全沒有退休的打算，他仍然每天早上七點去他的小店。","a":"has no intention of"},{"w":"interact","p":"v.","d":"to talk to and do things with other people","c":"互動；交流","s":"Shy children often find it hard to interact with new classmates, so the teacher uses group games on the first day.","t":"害羞的孩子常常覺得很難和新同學互動，所以老師在第一天會用小組遊戲。","h":1},{"w":"interaction","p":"n.","d":"the activity of talking and doing things together","c":"互動；交流","s":"Playing with other kids at the park gives a child the social interaction that watching cartoons at home cannot provide.","t":"在公園和其他孩子玩，能給孩子在家看卡通無法提供的社交互動。","h":1},{"w":"interact with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to communicate or work together with someone or something","c":"與…互動","s":"Modern robots can interact with people by answering questions, and some of them even tell jokes to make customers laugh.","t":"現代機器人可以藉由回答問題與人互動，有些甚至會講笑話逗顧客笑。"},{"w":"interactive","p":"adj.","d":"allowing people and machines to communicate with each other","c":"互動的","s":"The museum has an interactive map that lights up and plays sounds when visitors touch different parts of the screen.","t":"博物館有一張互動式地圖，當參觀者觸碰螢幕的不同部分時會發光並播放聲音。"},{"w":"interfere","p":"v.","d":"to get involved in a situation where you are not wanted","c":"干涉；干擾","s":"My aunt loves to interfere in other people's business, so nobody in the family tells her their secrets anymore.","t":"我阿姨喜歡干涉別人的事，所以家裡再也沒有人告訴她秘密了。","h":1},{"w":"interfere with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop something from happening in the normal way","c":"妨礙；干擾","s":"Playing video games late at night can interfere with your sleep, which makes it hard to pay attention in class.","t":"深夜玩電動會干擾你的睡眠，讓你上課時很難專心。"},{"w":"interference","p":"n.","d":"the act of getting involved where you are not wanted; noise that disturbs a signal","c":"干涉；干擾","s":"Teenagers often complain about their parents' interference in their lives, but most of them still ask for advice when they need it.","t":"青少年常抱怨父母對他們生活的干涉，但大多數人需要時仍會尋求建議。"},{"w":"intermediate","p":"adj.","d":"between the beginning level and the advanced level","c":"中級的；中間的","s":"After passing the beginner's test, Jenny moved up to the intermediate swimming class, where she learned to swim longer distances.","t":"通過初級考試後，珍妮升到中級游泳班，在那裡她學會游更長的距離。","h":1},{"w":"intermediate","p":"n.","d":"a learner who is at the middle level","c":"中級學習者","s":"This textbook is written for intermediates, so beginners may find the stories a little too hard to understand.","t":"這本教科書是為中級學習者寫的，所以初學者可能會覺得故事有點難懂。","a":"intermediates"},{"w":"intermediate level","p":"n.phr.","d":"the middle level of skill in a subject","c":"中級程度","s":"To join the study tour in Japan, students need Japanese at the intermediate level, which means they can order food and ask for directions.","t":"要參加日本遊學團，學生需要中級程度的日語，也就是能點餐和問路。"},{"w":"interpret","p":"v.","d":"to explain the meaning of something; to change spoken words into another language","c":"解釋；口譯","s":"People often interpret the same painting in different ways; some see a happy family, while others see a lonely child.","t":"人們常常以不同的方式解讀同一幅畫；有些人看到幸福的家庭，有些人卻看到孤單的孩子。","h":1},{"w":"interpretation","p":"n.","d":"an explanation of the meaning of something","c":"解釋；詮釋","s":"The actor's interpretation of the old king was so powerful that the audience stood up and clapped for five minutes.","t":"這位演員對老國王的詮釋非常有力，觀眾起立鼓掌了五分鐘。"},{"w":"interpreter","p":"n.","d":"a person who changes spoken words into another language","c":"口譯員","s":"During the meeting with the Japanese company, an interpreter sat between the two managers and translated every sentence.","t":"與日本公司開會時，一位口譯員坐在兩位經理中間，翻譯每一句話。"},{"w":"misinterpret","p":"v.","d":"to understand something in the wrong way","c":"誤解","s":"It is easy to misinterpret a short text message, because you cannot hear the other person's voice or see their face.","t":"簡短的文字訊息很容易被誤解，因為你聽不到對方的聲音，也看不到他們的表情。"},{"w":"interruption","p":"n.","d":"something that stops an activity for a short time","c":"中斷；打擾","s":"The speaker asked everyone to turn off their phones so that she could finish her talk without any interruption.","t":"講者請大家把手機關掉，好讓她能在沒有任何打擾的情況下完成演講。","h":1},{"w":"interrupt","p":"v.","d":"to stop someone while they are speaking or doing something","c":"打斷；中斷","s":"Please do not interrupt me while I am on the phone with the doctor; I will answer your question in a few minutes.","t":"我和醫生講電話時請不要打斷我；幾分鐘後我就會回答你的問題。"},{"w":"without interruption","p":"phr.","d":"continuously, with no stops","c":"不間斷地","s":"The old clock in the hall has been running without interruption for over fifty years, and my grandfather still winds it every Sunday.","t":"大廳裡的老時鐘已經不間斷地走了五十多年，我爺爺仍然每個星期天幫它上發條。"},{"w":"intimate","p":"adj.","d":"very close and friendly; private and personal","c":"親密的；私人的","s":"Lisa and I have been intimate friends since kindergarten, so she knows all my secrets and I know hers.","t":"麗莎和我從幼兒園起就是親密的朋友，所以她知道我所有的秘密，我也知道她的。","h":1},{"w":"intimacy","p":"n.","d":"a close and loving relationship","c":"親密；親近","s":"Eating dinner together every evening without phones builds intimacy between family members, even if the meal is simple.","t":"每天晚上一起吃晚餐、不用手機，即使餐點簡單，也能建立家人之間的親密感。"},{"w":"intimate friend","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very close friend","c":"知己；密友","s":"Everyone needs at least one intimate friend to talk to when life becomes difficult and nobody else seems to understand.","t":"每個人都需要至少一位知己，在生活變得艱難、似乎沒有人理解時可以傾訴。"},{"w":"intimately","p":"adv.","d":"in a very close or detailed way","c":"親密地；詳細地","s":"The old fisherman knows the coast intimately, so he can find his way home even on the darkest and foggiest night.","t":"那位老漁夫非常熟悉這片海岸，所以即使在最黑暗、霧最濃的夜晚，他也能找到回家的路。"},{"w":"intuition","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that you know something without thinking about it","c":"直覺","s":"My mother's intuition told her that something was wrong, and she called me just as I was about to get lost.","t":"我媽媽的直覺告訴她有事不對勁，就在我快要迷路時她打電話給我。","h":1},{"w":"intuitive","p":"adj.","d":"based on feelings rather than facts; easy to understand without instructions","c":"直覺的；易懂的","s":"The new phone has an intuitive design, so even my eighty-year-old grandmother learned to use it in one afternoon.","t":"這支新手機的設計很直覺，所以連我八十歲的奶奶也在一個下午就學會使用了。"},{"w":"intuitively","p":"adv.","d":"by feeling, without thinking carefully first","c":"直覺地","s":"The experienced nurse intuitively knew which patient needed help first, even before she had read any of the reports.","t":"那位經驗豐富的護士憑直覺就知道哪位病人需要優先幫助，甚至在她讀任何報告之前。"},{"w":"invade","p":"v.","d":"to enter a country or place by force","c":"入侵；侵略","s":"In the movie, aliens invade the Earth, and a small group of students must find a way to save their city.","t":"在電影中，外星人入侵地球，一小群學生必須想辦法拯救他們的城市。","h":1},{"w":"invasion","p":"n.","d":"the act of entering a place by force","c":"入侵；侵略","s":"The museum shows how the island's people fought bravely against the invasion of foreign soldiers four hundred years ago.","t":"博物館展示了四百年前島上的人民如何勇敢對抗外國士兵的入侵。","h":1},{"w":"invader","p":"n.","d":"a person, army, or thing that enters a place by force","c":"入侵者","s":"The farmers built a high wall around the village to keep out invaders, and parts of it are still standing today.","t":"農民們在村莊周圍築起高牆以阻擋入侵者，其中一部分至今仍然屹立。","a":"invaders"},{"w":"invade sb's privacy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look into someone's private life without permission","c":"侵犯某人的隱私","s":"Reading your sister's diary without asking invades her privacy, and she will be very angry if she finds out.","t":"未經詢問就看你妹妹的日記是侵犯她的隱私，如果她發現了會非常生氣。","a":"invades her privacy"},{"w":"invention","p":"n.","d":"a new thing that someone has made or designed","c":"發明","s":"The smartphone is probably the most important invention of the past twenty years, and few people can live without one now.","t":"智慧型手機可能是過去二十年最重要的發明，現在很少有人能離開它。","h":1},{"w":"invent","p":"v.","d":"to make or design something completely new","c":"發明","s":"Nobody knows exactly who first learned to invent paper, but we do know it was made in China about two thousand years ago.","t":"沒有人確切知道是誰最早發明了紙，但我們知道它是大約兩千年前在中國製造的。"},{"w":"inventor","p":"n.","d":"a person who makes or designs new things","c":"發明家","s":"Thomas Edison was a famous inventor who tried thousands of materials before he finally made a light bulb that worked.","t":"湯瑪斯·愛迪生是一位著名的發明家，他試了數千種材料才終於做出能用的燈泡。"},{"w":"inventive","p":"adj.","d":"good at thinking of new ideas","c":"有創造力的","s":"My little brother is very inventive; he turned an old shoe box and some straws into a small house for his hamster.","t":"我弟弟非常有創意；他把一個舊鞋盒和一些吸管變成了倉鼠的小房子。"},{"w":"invest","p":"v.","d":"to put money into something to make more money later","c":"投資","s":"My parents decided to invest part of their savings in a small apartment, which they now rent to a young couple.","t":"我父母決定把一部分積蓄投資在一間小公寓上，現在他們把它租給一對年輕夫婦。","h":1},{"w":"investment","p":"n.","d":"money put into something to make a profit; the act of investing","c":"投資","s":"Buying a good dictionary is a small investment that will help you with every English class for the next six years.","t":"買一本好字典是一項小投資，它會在接下來六年的每一堂英文課上幫助你。"},{"w":"investor","p":"n.","d":"a person or company that puts money into a business","c":"投資者","s":"The young designer found an investor who gave her enough money to open her first clothing store in Taichung.","t":"這位年輕設計師找到了一位投資者，給了她足夠的錢在台中開第一家服飾店。"},{"w":"invest in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spend money or time on something useful","c":"投資於…","s":"Experts say that countries should invest in education, because well-educated people create stronger economies in the future.","t":"專家表示各國應該投資於教育，因為受過良好教育的人會在未來創造更強的經濟。"},{"w":"investigation","p":"n.","d":"an official attempt to find out the truth about something","c":"調查","s":"The police began an investigation into the fire at the factory, and they soon discovered that an old machine had caused it.","t":"警方開始對工廠火災進行調查，很快就發現是一台舊機器引起的。","h":1},{"w":"investigate","p":"v.","d":"to try to find out the truth about something","c":"調查","s":"Scientists are working to investigate why so many fish died in the river last week, and they are testing the water every day.","t":"科學家正在努力調查上週河裡為什麼有這麼多魚死亡，他們每天都在檢測水質。"},{"w":"investigator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to find out the truth about something","c":"調查員","s":"A private investigator followed the man for three days and found out that he was secretly meeting with the company's rival.","t":"一位私家調查員跟蹤那名男子三天，發現他正秘密與公司的競爭對手會面。"},{"w":"under investigation","p":"phr.","d":"being officially examined","c":"在調查中","s":"The cause of the accident is still under investigation, so the police have asked drivers to avoid that road for a few days.","t":"事故原因仍在調查中，所以警方已請駕駛人這幾天避開那條路。"},{"w":"involve","p":"v.","d":"to include something as a necessary part; to make someone take part","c":"涉及；使參與","s":"The job will involve a lot of travel, so the company is looking for someone who does not mind being away from home.","t":"這份工作會涉及大量出差，所以公司正在尋找不介意離家的人。","h":1},{"w":"involvement","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in something","c":"參與；涉入","s":"The school thanked the parents for their involvement in the sports day, since more than fifty of them helped at the event.","t":"學校感謝家長們對運動會的參與，因為有五十多位家長在活動中幫忙。"},{"w":"be involved in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take part in something; to be connected with something","c":"參與；捲入","s":"My cousin was involved in a car accident last month, but luckily nobody was hurt and only the mirror was broken.","t":"我表哥上個月捲入一場車禍，但幸運的是沒有人受傷，只有後照鏡壞了。","a":"was involved in"},{"w":"involved","p":"adj.","d":"complicated; difficult to understand","c":"複雜的","s":"The rules of the card game were so involved that we spent half an hour reading them before we could start playing.","t":"這個紙牌遊戲的規則太複雜了，我們花了半小時讀規則才能開始玩。"},{"w":"isolate","p":"v.","d":"to keep a person or thing separate from others","c":"隔離；孤立","s":"Doctors had to isolate the sick patients in a separate room so that the virus would not spread to other people.","t":"醫生必須把生病的病人隔離在另一個房間，以免病毒傳染給其他人。","h":1},{"w":"isolation","p":"n.","d":"the state of being separate from other people or things","c":"隔離；孤立","s":"After returning from abroad during the pandemic, travelers had to stay in isolation at home for fourteen days.","t":"疫情期間從國外回來後，旅客必須在家隔離十四天。","h":1},{"w":"isolated","p":"adj.","d":"far away from other places; feeling alone","c":"偏遠的；孤立的","s":"The village is so isolated that the nearest hospital is three hours away by car along a narrow mountain road.","t":"這個村莊非常偏遠，最近的醫院開車要沿著狹窄的山路走三小時。"},{"w":"in isolation","p":"phr.","d":"separately, without considering other things","c":"單獨地；孤立地","s":"You cannot judge a student's ability by one test in isolation; you also need to look at homework and class performance.","t":"你不能單獨憑一次考試判斷學生的能力；你還需要看作業和課堂表現。"},{"w":"issue","p":"n.","d":"an important subject or problem that people discuss","c":"議題；問題","s":"Air pollution is a serious issue in many big cities, and governments are trying to reduce the number of cars on the roads.","t":"空氣污染是許多大城市的嚴重問題，各國政府正努力減少路上的汽車數量。","h":1},{"w":"issue","p":"n.","d":"one of a series of magazines or newspapers","c":"（期刊的）一期","s":"The latest issue of the science magazine has a long article about black holes, which my brother read twice.","t":"這本科學雜誌的最新一期有一篇關於黑洞的長文，我哥哥讀了兩遍。"},{"w":"issue","p":"v.","d":"to give something officially; to announce","c":"發給；發布","s":"The government will issue a warning to the public if the typhoon gets stronger, so please keep watching the news.","t":"如果颱風增強，政府將向大眾發布警報，所以請持續關注新聞。"},{"w":"jealousy","p":"n.","d":"the unhappy feeling you have when someone has what you want","c":"嫉妒；妒忌","s":"When her best friend won the prize, Amy felt a little jealousy, but she still smiled and said congratulations.","t":"當她最好的朋友贏得獎項時，艾咪感到一絲嫉妒，但她仍然微笑著說恭喜。","h":1},{"w":"jealous","p":"adj.","d":"unhappy because someone has what you want","c":"嫉妒的；吃醋的","s":"My dog gets jealous whenever I play with the neighbor's cat, and he pushes his way between us.","t":"每當我和鄰居的貓玩，我的狗就會吃醋，牠會擠進我們中間。"},{"w":"be jealous of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel unhappy because of what someone else has","c":"嫉妒…","s":"There is no reason to be jealous of your sister's new phone; your own phone still works perfectly well.","t":"沒有理由嫉妒你姐姐的新手機；你自己的手機還能用得好好的。"},{"w":"jealously","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you do not want to share something","c":"嫉妒地；小心守護地","s":"The old man jealously guarded his secret recipe and never let anyone, not even his son, into the kitchen while he cooked.","t":"老先生小心翼翼地守護著他的秘密食譜，做菜時從不讓任何人（連他兒子也不行）進廚房。"},{"w":"keen","p":"adj.","d":"very interested in something; eager","c":"熱衷的；渴望的","s":"Tom is a keen photographer who gets up before sunrise every weekend to take pictures of birds in the park.","t":"湯姆是個熱愛攝影的人，每個週末日出前就起床到公園拍鳥。","h":1},{"w":"keen","p":"adj.","d":"sharp; very good at noticing things","c":"敏銳的","s":"Dogs have a keen sense of smell, which is why the police use them to find lost people in the mountains.","t":"狗有敏銳的嗅覺，這就是為什麼警察用牠們在山裡尋找失蹤的人。"},{"w":"be keen on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to like something very much","c":"熱衷於；很喜歡","s":"My sister is keen on Korean dramas, so she stays up late every night watching one more episode.","t":"我姐姐很喜歡韓劇，所以她每晚都熬夜再看一集。","a":"is keen on"},{"w":"keenly","p":"adv.","d":"very much; strongly","c":"強烈地；敏銳地","s":"The whole class keenly felt the loss when their favorite teacher moved to another school last summer.","t":"去年夏天他們最喜歡的老師調到另一所學校時，全班都深深地感受到失落。"},{"w":"kettle","p":"n.","d":"a container with a handle used for boiling water","c":"水壺；茶壺","s":"Fill the kettle with cold water and wait for it to boil before you pour the water over the tea leaves.","t":"把水壺裝滿冷水，等它煮沸後再把水倒在茶葉上。","h":1},{"w":"electric kettle","p":"n.phr.","d":"a kettle that boils water using electricity","c":"電熱水壺","s":"An electric kettle is the most useful thing in my dorm room, because I use it to make tea, coffee, and instant noodles.","t":"電熱水壺是我宿舍房間裡最有用的東西，因為我用它泡茶、泡咖啡和泡泡麵。"},{"w":"put the kettle on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start boiling water for tea or coffee","c":"燒水（泡茶）","s":"When guests arrive at my grandmother's house, the first thing she does is put the kettle on and bring out her best cookies.","t":"客人到我奶奶家時，她做的第一件事就是燒水泡茶，並拿出她最好的餅乾。"},{"w":"kneel, knelt, knelt","p":"v.","d":"to be on your knees, or to go down onto your knees","c":"跪；跪下","s":"The gardener had to kneel on the wet grass for an hour to plant all the flowers before the rain started.","t":"園丁必須在濕草地上跪一小時，趕在下雨前種完所有的花。","a":"kneel","h":1},{"w":"kneel down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go down onto your knees","c":"跪下","s":"The young man decided to kneel down in front of everyone at the party and ask his girlfriend to marry him.","t":"那位年輕男子決定在派對上當著大家的面跪下，向女友求婚。"},{"w":"knee","p":"n.","d":"the joint in the middle of your leg where it bends","c":"膝蓋","s":"She hurt her knee when she fell off her bike, so she could not join the dance practice for two weeks.","t":"她從腳踏車上摔下來時傷到了膝蓋，所以兩週不能參加舞蹈練習。"},{"w":"knob","p":"n.","d":"a round handle or button that you turn","c":"旋鈕；圓形把手","s":"Turn the knob on the left to make the water hotter, and turn the one on the right to make it colder.","t":"把左邊的旋鈕轉一下可以讓水更熱，轉右邊那個可以讓水更冷。","h":1},{"w":"doorknob","p":"n.","d":"a round handle on a door","c":"門把","s":"The doorknob was so old and loose that it came off in my hand when I tried to open the bathroom door.","t":"那個門把又舊又鬆，我想開浴室門時它竟然掉在我手裡。"},{"w":"turn the knob","p":"v.phr.","d":"to twist a round handle to open or control something","c":"轉動旋鈕","s":"To change the channel on this old radio, you have to turn the knob slowly until the music sounds clear and loud.","t":"要在這台老收音機上換頻道，你必須慢慢轉動旋鈕，直到音樂聽起來清楚又大聲。"},{"w":"labor","p":"n.","d":"hard physical work","c":"勞動；勞力","s":"Building the old stone bridge took years of hard labor, since the workers had no machines and carried every rock by hand.","t":"建造那座古老的石橋花了多年的辛苦勞動，因為工人沒有機器，每塊石頭都是用手搬的。","h":1},{"w":"labor","p":"n.","d":"workers as a group","c":"勞工","s":"The factory moved to another country because labor was cheaper there, and many local workers lost their jobs.","t":"那家工廠搬到另一個國家，因為那裡的勞工比較便宜，許多本地工人因此失業。"},{"w":"labor","p":"v.","d":"to work very hard","c":"辛苦工作","s":"The farmers labor in the fields from early morning until sunset during the rice harvest every June.","t":"每年六月稻米收割期間，農民從一大早到日落都在田裡辛苦工作。"},{"w":"Labor Day","p":"n.phr.","d":"a public holiday that honors workers","c":"勞動節","s":"In Taiwan, Labor Day is on May 1st, so most offices and factories are closed and workers enjoy a day off.","t":"在台灣，勞動節是五月一日，所以大多數辦公室和工廠都休息，勞工享有一天假期。"},{"w":"laborer","p":"n.","d":"a person who does hard physical work","c":"勞工；工人","s":"My grandfather worked as a laborer on the railway for thirty years, and his hands were rough but strong.","t":"我爺爺在鐵路當了三十年的工人，他的手粗糙但有力。"},{"w":"laboratory","p":"n.","d":"a room or building where scientists do experiments","c":"實驗室","s":"Students must wear safety glasses in the chemistry laboratory, because some of the liquids there can burn your eyes.","t":"學生在化學實驗室裡必須戴護目鏡，因為那裡有些液體會灼傷眼睛。","h":1},{"w":"lab","p":"n.","d":"a laboratory (short form)","c":"實驗室（簡稱）","s":"Our biology teacher took us to the school lab to look at plant cells under a microscope for the first time.","t":"我們的生物老師帶我們到學校的實驗室，第一次用顯微鏡觀察植物細胞。"},{"w":"language lab","p":"n.phr.","d":"a room with computers and headphones for practicing languages","c":"語言教室","s":"Every Friday we go to the language lab, where we put on headphones and practice our English listening and speaking.","t":"每個星期五我們都去語言教室，戴上耳機練習英語聽力和口說。"},{"w":"lab coat","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long white coat worn by scientists or doctors","c":"實驗袍","s":"The scientist put on her white lab coat and gloves before she started mixing the chemicals on the table.","t":"科學家穿上白色實驗袍並戴上手套，然後才開始混合桌上的化學藥品。"}]},{"unit":24,"theme":"lag – lobster","cards":[{"w":"lag","p":"v.","d":"to move or develop more slowly than others","c":"落後","s":"Our team started well, but we began to lag behind in the second half because everyone was tired and thirsty.","t":"我們隊一開始表現不錯，但下半場開始落後，因為每個人都又累又渴。","h":1},{"w":"lag behind","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be slower or less successful than others","c":"落後於…","s":"Students who miss many classes often lag behind their classmates, so the teacher gives them extra homework to catch up.","t":"缺很多課的學生常常落後同學，所以老師會給他們額外的作業來趕上進度。"},{"w":"jet lag","p":"n.phr.","d":"the tired feeling you get after a long flight across time zones","c":"時差（不適）","s":"After the long flight from Taipei to New York, my father suffered from terrible jet lag and woke up at three every morning.","t":"從台北飛到紐約的長途飛行之後，我爸爸飽受嚴重時差之苦，每天早上三點就醒來。"},{"w":"time lag","p":"n.phr.","d":"a delay between two things that happen","c":"時間差；延遲","s":"There is a short time lag between the moment you press the button and the moment the video starts to play.","t":"從你按下按鈕到影片開始播放之間，有一小段時間差。"},{"w":"landmark","p":"n.","d":"a famous building or place that is easy to see and recognize","c":"地標","s":"Taipei 101 is the most famous landmark in the city, and visitors use it to find their way when they are lost.","t":"台北101是這座城市最有名的地標，遊客迷路時會用它來辨認方向。","h":1},{"w":"landmark","p":"n.","d":"an important event that marks a big change","c":"里程碑","s":"The invention of the smartphone was a landmark in modern history because it changed the way people talk, shop, and learn.","t":"智慧型手機的發明是現代史上的一個里程碑，因為它改變了人們交談、購物和學習的方式。"},{"w":"land","p":"n.","d":"the part of the earth that is not covered by water","c":"陸地；土地","s":"After three weeks at sea, the sailors were so happy to see land that some of them began to cry with joy.","t":"在海上三個星期之後，水手們看到陸地高興得不得了，有些人甚至喜極而泣。"},{"w":"landlord","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns a house or room and rents it to others","c":"房東","s":"Our landlord is very kind; when the air conditioner broke last summer, he sent someone to fix it the very next day.","t":"我們的房東人很好；去年夏天冷氣壞掉時，他隔天就派人來修理。"},{"w":"landscape","p":"n.","d":"everything you can see when you look across a large area of land","c":"風景；地貌","s":"From the top of the mountain, we enjoyed a beautiful landscape of green fields, small villages, and a long silver river.","t":"從山頂上，我們欣賞到綠色田野、小村莊和一條銀色長河組成的美麗風景。","h":1},{"w":"landscape","p":"v.","d":"to make a garden or park look more beautiful with plants and paths","c":"美化（庭園）；造景","s":"The school hired a company to landscape the area around the new library, so there are now flowers and trees everywhere.","t":"學校請了一家公司來美化新圖書館周圍的區域，所以現在到處都是花和樹。"},{"w":"landscape painting","p":"n.phr.","d":"a picture of the countryside, mountains, or sea","c":"風景畫","s":"My grandmother loves landscape painting, and she has hung several pictures of mountains and lakes on the walls of her living room.","t":"我奶奶很喜歡風景畫，她在客廳牆上掛了好幾幅山和湖的畫。"},{"w":"landscape","p":"n.","d":"the general situation in an area of activity","c":"（某領域的）局面；態勢","s":"Online shopping has completely changed the business landscape, so many small shops now sell their products on the Internet, too.","t":"網路購物徹底改變了商業局面，所以許多小店現在也在網路上賣東西。"},{"w":"largely","p":"adv.","d":"mostly; mainly","c":"大部分地；主要地","s":"The success of the school play was largely due to the hard work of the students who stayed late to practice every day.","t":"學校戲劇演出的成功主要歸功於那些每天留到很晚練習的學生的努力。","h":1},{"w":"large","p":"adj.","d":"big in size or amount","c":"大的","s":"We ordered a large pizza for the party, but it was gone in ten minutes because everyone was so hungry.","t":"我們為派對訂了一個大披薩，但十分鐘就被吃光了，因為大家都好餓。"},{"w":"at large","p":"phr.","d":"free and not yet caught; as a whole","c":"在逃；整體而言","s":"The police warned that the thief was still at large, so people in the area should lock their doors and windows carefully.","t":"警方警告小偷仍在逃，所以該地區的居民應該仔細鎖好門窗。"},{"w":"enlarge","p":"v.","d":"to make something bigger","c":"放大；擴大","s":"The photo shop can enlarge this small picture so that we can hang it on the wall of our living room.","t":"照相館可以把這張小照片放大，這樣我們就能把它掛在客廳的牆上。"},{"w":"launch","p":"v.","d":"to send a rocket or ship into the sky or water; to start selling or doing something new","c":"發射；推出","s":"The company plans to launch its new phone next month, and many fans have already lined up to order one online.","t":"這家公司計畫下個月推出新手機，許多粉絲已經在網路上排隊預訂了。","h":1},{"w":"launch","p":"n.","d":"the act of starting something new or sending a rocket into space","c":"發射；上市","s":"Thousands of people watched the launch of the rocket on TV as it rose slowly into the blue morning sky.","t":"成千上萬的人在電視上觀看火箭發射，看著它慢慢升入藍色的晨空。"},{"w":"launch a campaign","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start a series of planned activities for a goal","c":"發起（宣傳）活動","s":"The students decided to launch a campaign to stop food waste, and they put up posters in every classroom and the cafeteria.","t":"學生們決定發起一項停止浪費食物的活動，他們在每間教室和餐廳都貼了海報。"},{"w":"launch into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly start saying or doing something with a lot of energy","c":"突然開始（滔滔不絕地說）","s":"As soon as my uncle sat down, he launched into a long story about his trip to Japan last winter.","t":"我叔叔一坐下來，就開始滔滔不絕地講他去年冬天去日本旅行的長篇故事。","a":"launched into"},{"w":"lawful","p":"adj.","d":"allowed by law","c":"合法的","s":"It is lawful to ride a scooter at the age of eighteen in Taiwan, but you must pass a test and get a license first.","t":"在台灣十八歲騎機車是合法的，但你必須先通過考試並取得駕照。","h":1},{"w":"unlawful","p":"adj.","d":"not allowed by law","c":"不合法的；非法的","s":"Parking in front of a fire station is unlawful, and the police will give you a heavy fine if they catch you.","t":"把車停在消防隊前面是不合法的，警察抓到會重罰。"},{"w":"lawfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is allowed by law","c":"合法地","s":"The land was lawfully bought by the farmer's grandfather eighty years ago, so nobody can take it away from the family now.","t":"這塊地是農夫的祖父八十年前合法買下的，所以現在沒有人能從這家人手中奪走它。"},{"w":"law","p":"n.","d":"the rules of a country that everyone must follow","c":"法律","s":"According to the new law, everyone in the back seat of a car must wear a seat belt or pay a fine.","t":"根據新法律，汽車後座的每個人都必須繫安全帶，否則要罰款。"},{"w":"lawyer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to help people with the law","c":"律師","s":"My aunt is a lawyer who helps poor families when they have problems with their landlords or their bosses.","t":"我阿姨是一位律師，當貧窮家庭和房東或老闆發生問題時，她會幫助他們。"},{"w":"break the law","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something that the law does not allow","c":"違法；犯法","s":"People who break the law by driving after drinking alcohol may lose their license and even go to prison.","t":"喝酒後開車而違法的人可能會被吊銷駕照，甚至坐牢。"},{"w":"lean","p":"v.","d":"to bend your body or rest against something","c":"傾斜；倚靠","s":"Do not lean against that old wall because the bricks are loose and might fall on you at any moment.","t":"不要倚靠那面舊牆，因為磚頭鬆了，隨時可能掉下來砸到你。","h":1},{"w":"lean on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to depend on someone for help and support","c":"依靠；依賴","s":"When I failed the exam, I could always lean on my best friend, who listened to me and helped me study.","t":"當我考試不及格時，我總是可以依靠我最好的朋友，他會聽我說話並幫我讀書。"},{"w":"lean","p":"adj.","d":"thin and healthy; with little or no fat","c":"精瘦的；（肉）瘦的","s":"Doctors suggest eating lean meat such as chicken breast instead of fatty pork if you want to stay healthy and fit.","t":"醫生建議，如果想保持健康和好身材，就吃雞胸肉這類的瘦肉，而不是肥豬肉。"},{"w":"lean forward","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move the top part of your body toward the front","c":"身體向前傾","s":"The students all leaned forward in their seats when the teacher began to tell a ghost story in a quiet voice.","t":"當老師開始用低沉的聲音講鬼故事時，學生們全都在座位上向前傾。","a":"leaned forward"},{"w":"learned","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of knowledge from study","c":"博學的；有學問的","s":"The old professor is a very learned man who can read five languages and has written more than twenty books.","t":"這位老教授是個非常博學的人，他能讀五種語言，還寫了二十多本書。","h":1},{"w":"learn","p":"v.","d":"to get knowledge or a skill by studying or practicing","c":"學習；學會","s":"Many people want to learn a new language, but few of them practice every day, so they give up after a few months.","t":"很多人想學一種新語言，但很少人每天練習，所以幾個月後就放棄了。"},{"w":"learner","p":"n.","d":"a person who is learning something","c":"學習者","s":"This dictionary is designed for young learners of English, so the explanations are short and the examples are easy.","t":"這本字典是為年輕的英語學習者設計的，所以解釋簡短，例句也簡單。","a":"learners"},{"w":"learn sth by heart","p":"v.phr.","d":"to memorize something so you can say it without reading","c":"背誦；熟記","s":"Instead of just reading the poem once, you should learn it by heart so that you can recite it in front of the class tomorrow.","t":"與其只讀一遍這首詩，你應該把它背起來，這樣明天才能在全班面前朗誦。","a":"learn it by heart"},{"w":"learning","p":"n.","d":"the process of getting knowledge","c":"學習","s":"Online learning became very popular during the pandemic because students could not go to school for several months.","t":"線上學習在疫情期間變得非常流行，因為學生好幾個月都不能去學校。"},{"w":"lecture","p":"n.","d":"a long talk given to a group of students or people","c":"演講；講課","s":"The lecture on climate change lasted two hours, but nobody felt bored because the speaker showed many interesting photos.","t":"這場關於氣候變遷的演講持續了兩小時，但沒有人覺得無聊，因為講者展示了許多有趣的照片。","h":1},{"w":"lecturer","p":"n.","d":"a person who gives lectures, especially at a university","c":"講師","s":"My cousin works as a lecturer at a university in Taichung, where she teaches English literature to first-year students.","t":"我表姐在台中一所大學當講師，教一年級學生英國文學。","h":1},{"w":"lecture","p":"v.","d":"to give a long talk; to scold someone at length","c":"講課；訓話","s":"My mother always lectures me about keeping my room clean whenever she finds dirty socks under my bed.","t":"每當媽媽在我床底下發現髒襪子，她總是訓我一頓，要我保持房間整潔。","a":"lectures"},{"w":"give a lecture","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak to an audience about a subject","c":"發表演講","s":"The famous writer will give a lecture at our school next Friday, so the library has already prepared three hundred seats.","t":"這位知名作家下週五將在我們學校發表演講，所以圖書館已經準備了三百個座位。"},{"w":"attend a lecture","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go to a lecture and listen","c":"聽講；出席演講","s":"University students are expected to attend a lecture every morning and then discuss what they heard in small groups in the afternoon.","t":"大學生每天早上都要聽一場講課，然後下午分組討論他們聽到的內容。"},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"an old story from the past that may not be true","c":"傳說","s":"According to an old Chinese legend, a beautiful woman named Chang'e flew to the moon after drinking a magic medicine.","t":"根據一個古老的中國傳說，一位名叫嫦娥的美女喝下仙藥後飛到了月亮上。","h":1},{"w":"legend","p":"n.","d":"a very famous person who is admired by many people","c":"傳奇人物","s":"Many baseball fans consider Chien-Ming Wang a legend because he was one of the first Taiwanese pitchers to succeed in the US.","t":"許多棒球迷認為王建民是個傳奇人物，因為他是最早在美國成功的台灣投手之一。"},{"w":"legendary","p":"adj.","d":"very famous and admired; from a legend","c":"傳奇的；傳說中的","s":"The legendary singer gave her last concert in Taipei, and tickets were sold out in less than five minutes.","t":"這位傳奇歌手在台北舉辦了最後一場演唱會，門票不到五分鐘就賣光了。"},{"w":"urban legend","p":"n.phr.","d":"a modern story that many people believe but that is not true","c":"都市傳說","s":"The story about the ghost in the school bathroom is just an urban legend, but many younger students still believe it.","t":"學校廁所鬧鬼的故事只是個都市傳說，但許多低年級學生仍然相信。"},{"w":"leisurely","p":"adj.","d":"relaxed and not hurried","c":"悠閒的；從容的","s":"On Sunday mornings, my parents like to take a leisurely walk along the river before they have breakfast at a small café.","t":"星期天早上，我父母喜歡沿著河邊悠閒地散步，然後再到小咖啡館吃早餐。","h":1},{"w":"leisurely","p":"adv.","d":"in a slow and relaxed way","c":"悠閒地","s":"We ate leisurely by the lake, talking and laughing, because nobody had to go to work or school that day.","t":"我們在湖邊悠閒地吃東西，邊聊邊笑，因為那天沒有人要上班或上學。"},{"w":"leisure","p":"n.","d":"free time when you are not working or studying","c":"休閒；空閒","s":"Since he retired last year, my grandfather has had a lot of leisure time, so he has started painting and fishing.","t":"自從去年退休後，我爺爺有很多空閒時間，所以他開始畫畫和釣魚。"},{"w":"leisure activities","p":"n.phr.","d":"things people do for fun in their free time","c":"休閒活動","s":"Hiking and cycling are popular leisure activities in Taiwan because the island has many beautiful mountains and well-built bike paths.","t":"健行和騎自行車是台灣受歡迎的休閒活動，因為這座島有許多美麗的山脈和完善的自行車道。"},{"w":"at leisure","p":"phr.","d":"with no hurry; when you have free time","c":"從容地；有空時","s":"There is no deadline for this report, so you can read the materials at leisure and write it whenever you have time.","t":"這份報告沒有截止日期，所以你可以從容地閱讀資料，有空時再寫。"},{"w":"lengthen","p":"v.","d":"to make something longer or to become longer","c":"加長；延長","s":"The tailor can lengthen these pants by two centimeters because my brother has grown a lot since last summer.","t":"裁縫師可以把這條褲子加長兩公分，因為我弟弟從去年夏天以來長高了不少。","h":1},{"w":"length","p":"n.","d":"how long something is from one end to the other","c":"長度","s":"The length of the swimming pool is fifty meters, so you need to swim twenty times to finish one kilometer.","t":"這座游泳池的長度是五十公尺，所以你需要游二十趟才能游完一公里。"},{"w":"lengthy","p":"adj.","d":"very long, often too long","c":"冗長的","s":"After a lengthy meeting that lasted four hours, everyone was tired and hungry, and nothing had really been decided.","t":"開了一場長達四小時的冗長會議之後，大家又累又餓，而且什麼都沒真正決定。"},{"w":"at length","p":"phr.","d":"for a long time and in detail","c":"詳細地；長時間地","s":"The doctor explained the problem at length so that my grandmother would understand exactly how to take her new medicine.","t":"醫生詳細地解釋了這個問題，好讓我奶奶清楚知道該怎麼服用新藥。"},{"w":"go to great lengths","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try very hard to do something","c":"不遺餘力；竭盡全力","s":"My parents went to great lengths to find my lost dog, putting up posters all over town and calling every animal shelter.","t":"我父母竭盡全力尋找我走失的狗，在全鎮張貼海報，還打電話給每一間動物收容所。","a":"went to great lengths"},{"w":"liar","p":"n.","d":"a person who tells lies","c":"說謊的人；騙子","s":"Nobody trusts him anymore because he has been caught telling lies so many times that everyone calls him a liar.","t":"再也沒有人相信他了，因為他被抓到說謊太多次，大家都叫他騙子。","h":1},{"w":"lie, lied, lied","p":"v.","d":"to say something that is not true","c":"說謊","s":"Please do not lie to your parents about your test scores, because they will find out the truth sooner or later.","t":"請不要對父母說謊隱瞞你的考試成績，因為他們遲早會知道真相。","a":"lie"},{"w":"lie","p":"n.","d":"something you say that you know is not true","c":"謊言","s":"He told a small lie about being sick so that he could stay home and play video games all day.","t":"他撒了個小謊說自己生病，好讓自己能待在家裡玩一整天的電玩。"},{"w":"white lie","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small, harmless lie that you tell to be polite or kind","c":"善意的謊言","s":"When my aunt asked if I liked her cooking, I told a white lie and said it was delicious because I did not want to hurt her feelings.","t":"當阿姨問我喜不喜歡她做的菜時，我說了個善意的謊言，說很好吃，因為我不想傷她的心。"},{"w":"tell a lie","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say something that is not true","c":"說謊","s":"It is better to admit a mistake than to tell a lie, because one lie usually leads to another and another.","t":"承認錯誤比說謊好，因為一個謊言通常會引來一個又一個的謊言。"},{"w":"librarian","p":"n.","d":"a person who works in a library and helps people find books","c":"圖書館員","s":"If you cannot find the book you need, ask the librarian at the front desk, and she will help you look it up.","t":"如果你找不到需要的書，就問櫃檯的圖書館員，她會幫你查。","h":1},{"w":"library","p":"n.","d":"a place where books are kept for people to read or borrow","c":"圖書館","s":"Our school library stays open until nine in the evening, so many students go there to study after dinner.","t":"我們學校的圖書館開放到晚上九點，所以很多學生晚餐後會去那裡讀書。"},{"w":"library card","p":"n.phr.","d":"a card that lets you borrow books from a library","c":"借書證","s":"You need to show your library card at the counter before you can borrow more than three books at one time.","t":"你需要在櫃檯出示借書證，才能一次借三本以上的書。"},{"w":"license","p":"n.","d":"an official paper that allows you to do or own something","c":"執照；許可證","s":"You have to pass both a written test and a driving test before you can get a driver's license in Taiwan.","t":"在台灣，你必須通過筆試和路考，才能拿到駕照。","h":1},{"w":"license","p":"v.","d":"to give someone official permission to do something","c":"發給執照；批准","s":"The city government will only license restaurants that pass a careful kitchen check, so customers can eat safely.","t":"市政府只會發執照給通過嚴格廚房檢查的餐廳，這樣顧客才能吃得安心。"},{"w":"licensed","p":"adj.","d":"having official permission to do something","c":"有執照的；領有許可的","s":"Make sure your electrician is licensed before you let him change the wires in your house, or it could be very dangerous.","t":"在讓電工更換你家電線之前，務必確認他是有執照的，否則可能非常危險。"},{"w":"license plate","p":"n.phr.","d":"the metal sign with numbers and letters on a car","c":"車牌","s":"The witness could not remember the whole license plate of the car, but she knew it started with the letters AB.","t":"目擊者記不得那輛車完整的車牌，但她知道是以字母AB開頭。"},{"w":"lifeguard","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to save swimmers who are in danger","c":"救生員","s":"The lifeguard blew his whistle loudly when he saw two children swimming too far from the beach.","t":"救生員看到兩個小孩游得離海灘太遠時，大聲吹響了哨子。","h":1},{"w":"guard","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to protect a place or people","c":"警衛；守衛","s":"A security guard stands at the gate of the factory all night to make sure that nobody enters without permission.","t":"一名保全警衛整夜站在工廠大門口，確保沒有人未經許可進入。"},{"w":"guard","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone or something from danger","c":"守衛；保護","s":"Two big dogs guard the farm at night, and they bark loudly whenever a stranger comes near the gate.","t":"兩隻大狗夜裡守衛著農場，只要有陌生人靠近大門，牠們就大聲吠叫。"},{"w":"life jacket","p":"n.phr.","d":"a jacket that helps you float in the water","c":"救生衣","s":"Everyone on the boat must wear a life jacket because the sea can become rough very quickly in the afternoon.","t":"船上的每個人都必須穿救生衣，因為下午海面可能很快就變得波濤洶湧。"},{"w":"limitation","p":"n.","d":"a rule or fact that limits something; a weakness","c":"限制；侷限","s":"One limitation of this phone is its small battery, which does not last a whole day if you watch a lot of videos.","t":"這支手機的一個侷限是電池太小，如果你看很多影片，撐不了一整天。","h":1},{"w":"limit","p":"n.","d":"the greatest amount or level that is allowed","c":"限制；上限","s":"The speed limit on this road is fifty kilometers an hour, so please slow down before the camera takes your picture.","t":"這條路的速限是每小時五十公里，所以請在測速照相機拍到你之前減速。"},{"w":"limit","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from going above a certain amount","c":"限制","s":"Doctors advise parents to limit their children's screen time to two hours a day so their eyes can rest.","t":"醫生建議父母把孩子的螢幕時間限制在每天兩小時，好讓眼睛休息。"},{"w":"limited","p":"adj.","d":"not very great in amount or number","c":"有限的","s":"We only have a limited number of tickets for the concert, so please buy yours before they are all sold out.","t":"我們演唱會的票數量有限，所以請在全部賣完之前買好你的票。"},{"w":"unlimited","p":"adj.","d":"without any limit","c":"無限的；不限量的","s":"This phone plan gives you unlimited data every month, so you can watch videos anywhere without worrying about the bill.","t":"這個手機方案每個月給你無限流量，所以你可以在任何地方看影片，不用擔心帳單。"},{"w":"linen","p":"n.","d":"a strong, cool cloth made from a plant","c":"亞麻布","s":"In summer my mother wears light linen dresses because the cloth keeps her cool and dries very quickly after washing.","t":"夏天我媽媽穿輕薄的亞麻布洋裝，因為這種布料讓她保持涼爽，洗完也乾得很快。","h":1},{"w":"bed linen","p":"n.phr.","d":"sheets and pillowcases for a bed","c":"床單寢具","s":"The hotel changes the bed linen every day, so the sheets and pillowcases always smell fresh and clean when you go to bed.","t":"這家飯店每天更換床單寢具，所以你上床時床單和枕頭套總是聞起來清新乾淨。"},{"w":"table linen","p":"n.phr.","d":"tablecloths and napkins made of cloth","c":"桌巾餐巾","s":"For the wedding dinner, the restaurant used white table linen and fresh flowers to make every table look elegant.","t":"為了這場婚宴，餐廳用白色桌巾餐巾和鮮花讓每一桌看起來都很高雅。"},{"w":"lipstick","p":"n.","d":"a colored stick that you use to color your lips","c":"口紅","s":"My sister put on some red lipstick before the party, and then she checked her face in the mirror one last time.","t":"我姐姐在派對前塗了些紅色口紅，然後對著鏡子最後檢查了一次臉。","h":1},{"w":"lip","p":"n.","d":"one of the two soft edges of your mouth","c":"嘴唇","s":"She bit her lower lip nervously while she waited for the teacher to hand back the test papers.","t":"她在等老師發回考卷時，緊張地咬著下唇。"},{"w":"stick","p":"n.","d":"a thin piece of wood","c":"棍子；棒子","s":"The old man used a wooden stick to help him walk up the steep steps to the temple on the hill.","t":"老先生用一根木棍幫助自己走上通往山丘寺廟的陡峭階梯。"},{"w":"stick, stuck, stuck","p":"v.","d":"to fix something with glue; to become unable to move","c":"黏貼；卡住","s":"The elevator got stuck between the fifth and sixth floors, and we had to wait twenty minutes for help.","t":"電梯卡在五樓和六樓之間，我們只好等了二十分鐘才有人來救援。","a":"stuck"},{"w":"liquor","p":"n.","d":"strong alcoholic drink such as whisky","c":"烈酒","s":"In Taiwan, stores are not allowed to sell beer, wine, or liquor to anyone under the age of eighteen.","t":"在台灣，商店不得販賣啤酒、葡萄酒或烈酒給未滿十八歲的人。","h":1},{"w":"liquid","p":"n.","d":"a substance like water that flows and is not solid or gas","c":"液體","s":"Water turns from a liquid into ice when the temperature drops below zero degrees Celsius on a cold winter night.","t":"在寒冷的冬夜，當溫度降到攝氏零度以下時，水會從液體變成冰。"},{"w":"liquid","p":"adj.","d":"in the form of a liquid","c":"液態的；液體的","s":"Liquid soap is easier to use than a bar of soap because you can just press the pump with one hand.","t":"液態肥皂比肥皂塊更好用，因為你只要用一隻手按壓壓頭就好。","a":"Liquid"},{"w":"liquor store","p":"n.phr.","d":"a shop that sells alcoholic drinks","c":"酒類專賣店","s":"My uncle runs a small liquor store near the night market, and he checks every young customer's ID card very carefully.","t":"我叔叔在夜市附近經營一家小酒類專賣店，他會非常仔細地檢查每位年輕顧客的身分證。"},{"w":"literary","p":"adj.","d":"connected with literature or writing","c":"文學的","s":"She won first prize in a literary contest for a short story about her grandmother's life in a small fishing village.","t":"她以一篇描寫奶奶在小漁村生活的短篇故事，在文學比賽中獲得首獎。","h":1},{"w":"literature","p":"n.","d":"written works such as novels, poems, and plays","c":"文學","s":"My brother is studying English literature at university, so he reads novels by Dickens and plays by Shakespeare every week.","t":"我哥哥在大學讀英國文學，所以他每週都讀狄更斯的小說和莎士比亞的戲劇。","h":1},{"w":"literate","p":"adj.","d":"able to read and write","c":"識字的；有讀寫能力的","s":"A hundred years ago, only a small number of people in the village were literate, so letters were read aloud by the teacher.","t":"一百年前，村裡只有少數人識字，所以信件都由老師大聲唸出來。"},{"w":"literacy","p":"n.","d":"the ability to read and write","c":"識字能力；讀寫能力","s":"The government opened night classes to improve adult literacy in the countryside, and hundreds of farmers learned to read.","t":"政府開設夜間課程以提升鄉村成人的識字能力，數百位農民因此學會了閱讀。"},{"w":"literal","p":"adj.","d":"following the exact, basic meaning of the words","c":"字面上的","s":"The literal meaning of \"break a leg\" sounds terrible, but actors actually say it to wish each other good luck.","t":"「break a leg」的字面意思聽起來很可怕，但演員其實是用它來互相祝好運。"},{"w":"literally","p":"adv.","d":"exactly as the words say; really","c":"字面上地；確實地","s":"We literally ran all the way to the station, but the last train had already left when we arrived.","t":"我們真的一路跑到車站，但我們到達時，最後一班火車已經開走了。"},{"w":"loan","p":"n.","d":"money that you borrow and must pay back, usually with interest","c":"貸款","s":"My parents took out a loan from the bank to buy our apartment, and they will pay it back over twenty years.","t":"我父母向銀行申請了貸款來買我們的公寓，他們將在二十年內還清。","h":1},{"w":"loan","p":"v.","d":"to lend something, especially money or valuable things","c":"借出；貸給","s":"The museum agreed to loan several famous paintings to a gallery in Japan for a special exhibition next spring.","t":"博物館同意把幾幅名畫出借給日本的一家美術館，供明年春天的特展使用。"},{"w":"student loan","p":"n.phr.","d":"money that a student borrows to pay for university","c":"學生貸款；就學貸款","s":"Many graduates spend years paying back their student loan, so some people choose cheaper public universities to save money.","t":"許多畢業生要花好幾年償還學生貸款，所以有些人選擇比較便宜的公立大學來省錢。"},{"w":"lend, lent, lent","p":"v.","d":"to give something to someone for a short time","c":"借給；借出","s":"Could you lend me your umbrella for the afternoon? I will return it to you as soon as the rain stops.","t":"你可以借我雨傘用一個下午嗎？雨一停我就馬上還給你。","a":"lend"},{"w":"on loan","p":"phr.","d":"borrowed for a period of time","c":"借出中；暫借的","s":"This painting is on loan from a museum in Paris, so it will go back to France at the end of the year.","t":"這幅畫是從巴黎一家博物館借來的，所以年底就會送回法國。"},{"w":"lobster","p":"n.","d":"a sea animal with a hard shell and two large claws, eaten as food","c":"龍蝦","s":"The restaurant by the harbor is famous for its fresh lobster, which is cooked with butter and garlic and served hot.","t":"港邊那家餐廳以新鮮龍蝦聞名，用奶油和大蒜烹調後趁熱上桌。","h":1},{"w":"seafood","p":"n.","d":"fish and other sea animals that people eat","c":"海鮮","s":"Kaohsiung is a great place for seafood lovers because the fish, shrimp, and crabs come straight from the boats every morning.","t":"高雄是海鮮愛好者的好地方，因為魚、蝦和螃蟹每天早上直接從漁船送來。"},{"w":"shellfish","p":"n.","d":"sea animals with shells, such as crabs and shrimp","c":"貝類；甲殼類海鮮","s":"Some people are allergic to shellfish, so the cook always asks customers before adding shrimp or crab to a dish.","t":"有些人對甲殼類海鮮過敏，所以廚師在菜裡加蝦或蟹之前總會先問顧客。"},{"w":"shrimp","p":"n.","d":"a small sea animal with a shell that turns pink when cooked","c":"蝦","s":"My favorite night-market snack is fried shrimp with a little salt and pepper, served hot in a paper bag.","t":"我最喜歡的夜市小吃是撒上一點鹽和胡椒的炸蝦，裝在紙袋裡熱騰騰地上桌。"}]},{"unit":25,"theme":"logic – memorial","cards":[{"w":"logic","p":"n.","d":"a way of thinking carefully using clear reasons","c":"邏輯；道理","s":"I could not follow the logic of his argument, because he jumped from one idea to another without explaining anything.","t":"我跟不上他論點的邏輯，因為他從一個想法跳到另一個想法，什麼都沒解釋。","h":1},{"w":"logical","p":"adj.","d":"sensible and based on clear reasons","c":"合邏輯的；合理的","s":"It is logical to bring an umbrella today, since the weather report says there is an eighty percent chance of rain.","t":"今天帶雨傘是合理的，因為氣象報告說降雨機率有百分之八十。","h":1},{"w":"logically","p":"adv.","d":"in a sensible and reasonable way","c":"邏輯上；有條理地","s":"Instead of getting angry, try to think logically about the problem and write down every possible solution you can find.","t":"與其生氣，不如試著有條理地思考這個問題，並寫下你能想到的每一個可能的解決方法。"},{"w":"illogical","p":"adj.","d":"not sensible or reasonable","c":"不合邏輯的；不合理的","s":"It seems illogical to buy a bigger car when gas prices are rising and you only drive to work alone.","t":"在油價上漲、而且你只是一個人開車上班的情況下買更大的車，似乎不合理。"},{"w":"loosen","p":"v.","d":"to make something less tight, or to become less tight","c":"鬆開；放鬆","s":"After the long dinner, my father had to loosen his belt because he had eaten far too much of my mother's cooking.","t":"吃完那頓漫長的晚餐後，我爸爸不得不鬆開皮帶，因為他吃了太多我媽媽做的菜。","h":1},{"w":"loose","p":"adj.","d":"not tight; not firmly fixed","c":"鬆的；寬鬆的","s":"This shirt is too loose for me, so I will exchange it for a smaller size at the store tomorrow morning.","t":"這件襯衫對我來說太寬鬆了，所以我明天早上要去店裡換小一號的。"},{"w":"loosely","p":"adv.","d":"not tightly; not exactly","c":"鬆鬆地；大致上","s":"The movie is loosely based on a true story, but the director changed many details to make it more exciting.","t":"這部電影大致上是根據真實故事改編的，但導演改了許多細節讓它更刺激。"},{"w":"come loose","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become no longer firmly fixed","c":"鬆脫","s":"One of the wheels on my old bike came loose while I was riding home, so I had to push it the rest of the way.","t":"我騎舊腳踏車回家時，其中一個輪子鬆脫了，所以剩下的路我只好用推的。","a":"came loose"},{"w":"lousy","p":"adj.","d":"very bad or of very poor quality","c":"糟糕的；差勁的","s":"The hotel room was lousy: the bed was hard, the shower was cold, and we could hear traffic noise all night.","t":"那間飯店房間很糟糕：床很硬、淋浴的水是冷的，而且整晚都聽得到車聲。","h":1},{"w":"feel lousy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel ill or unhappy","c":"感覺很糟；很不舒服","s":"I felt lousy this morning because I stayed up until two o'clock finishing my history report.","t":"我今天早上感覺很糟，因為我熬夜到兩點才寫完歷史報告。","a":"felt lousy"},{"w":"lousy at","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very bad at doing something","c":"很不擅長…","s":"My brother is lousy at cooking, so whenever my parents are away, we just order pizza or eat instant noodles.","t":"我哥哥很不擅長烹飪，所以每當父母不在家，我們就只能叫披薩或吃泡麵。"},{"w":"loyal","p":"adj.","d":"always supporting someone or something","c":"忠誠的；忠實的","s":"A dog is a loyal friend that will stay by your side even when everyone else has left you.","t":"狗是忠實的朋友，即使其他人都離開了你，牠仍會守在你身邊。","h":1},{"w":"loyalty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of always supporting someone or something","c":"忠誠；忠心","s":"The company rewards the loyalty of its workers by giving a bonus to anyone who has stayed for more than ten years.","t":"這家公司為了獎勵員工的忠誠，會發獎金給任職超過十年的人。","h":1},{"w":"disloyal","p":"adj.","d":"not loyal; not supporting your friends or group","c":"不忠的；背叛的","s":"It was disloyal of him to tell our secret plan to the other team just before the big game.","t":"他在大賽前把我們的秘密計畫告訴對方球隊，真是不忠。"},{"w":"loyal customer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a customer who keeps buying from the same shop or company","c":"忠實顧客","s":"Mrs. Lin has been a loyal customer of this bakery for twenty years, so the owner always gives her a free cookie.","t":"林太太二十年來一直是這家麵包店的忠實顧客，所以老闆總是送她一片免費的餅乾。"},{"w":"luxurious","p":"adj.","d":"very comfortable, beautiful, and expensive","c":"豪華的；奢華的","s":"The luxurious hotel has a swimming pool on the roof, a private beach, and a restaurant with a famous French chef.","t":"這家豪華飯店有屋頂游泳池、私人海灘，還有一間由名法國主廚主持的餐廳。","h":1},{"w":"luxury","p":"n.","d":"great comfort from expensive things; something expensive that you enjoy but do not need","c":"奢華；奢侈品","s":"For my grandmother, who grew up very poor, a hot bath every night was a luxury that she never took for granted.","t":"對從小家境貧困的奶奶來說，每晚泡個熱水澡是她從不視為理所當然的奢侈享受。","h":1},{"w":"luxury hotel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very expensive and comfortable hotel","c":"豪華飯店","s":"The movie star stayed in a luxury hotel near the beach, where one night costs more than my father earns in a month.","t":"那位電影明星住在海邊的一家豪華飯店，那裡住一晚的費用比我爸爸一個月賺的還多。"},{"w":"live in luxury","p":"v.phr.","d":"to live with great comfort and expensive things","c":"過奢華的生活","s":"After winning the lottery, the man lived in luxury for a few years, but he spent everything and ended up poor again.","t":"中了樂透之後，那個人過了幾年奢華的生活，但他花光了一切，最後又變得一貧如洗。","a":"lived in luxury"},{"w":"machinery","p":"n.","d":"machines, especially large ones, as a group","c":"機器（總稱）；機械","s":"The factory bought new machinery from Germany last year, so it can now produce twice as many bicycles every day.","t":"這家工廠去年從德國買了新機器，所以現在每天能生產兩倍數量的腳踏車。","h":1},{"w":"machine","p":"n.","d":"a piece of equipment with moving parts that does a particular job","c":"機器","s":"This machine can wash, dry, and fold the clothes by itself, so my mother has much more free time now.","t":"這台機器能自己洗、烘、摺衣服，所以我媽媽現在有更多的空閒時間。"},{"w":"washing machine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine for washing clothes","c":"洗衣機","s":"Our old washing machine finally stopped working last week, so we had to take all our dirty clothes to the laundry.","t":"我們家的舊洗衣機上週終於壞了，所以我們只好把髒衣服全部拿去洗衣店。"},{"w":"vending machine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine that sells drinks or snacks when you put in money","c":"自動販賣機","s":"If you get thirsty during the hike, there is a vending machine near the entrance of the trail that sells cold drinks.","t":"如果你健行時口渴了，步道入口附近有一台賣冷飲的自動販賣機。"},{"w":"magnetic","p":"adj.","d":"able to attract iron; having a strong power to attract people","c":"磁性的；有吸引力的","s":"The magnetic strip on the back of your credit card stores your information, so keep it away from your phone.","t":"你信用卡背面的磁條儲存了你的資料，所以要讓它遠離手機。","h":1},{"w":"magnet","p":"n.","d":"a piece of iron or metal that attracts other metal objects","c":"磁鐵","s":"My little sister collects a magnet from every city she visits and sticks them all on the door of our refrigerator.","t":"我妹妹每到一個城市都會收集一個磁鐵，然後全部貼在我們家冰箱的門上。"},{"w":"magnetic field","p":"n.phr.","d":"the area around a magnet where its force can be felt","c":"磁場","s":"Birds can feel the Earth's magnetic field, which helps them fly thousands of kilometers in the right direction every winter.","t":"鳥類能感受到地球的磁場，這幫助牠們每年冬天朝正確方向飛行數千公里。"},{"w":"magnetism","p":"n.","d":"the power of a magnet; a strong personal charm","c":"磁性；（個人）魅力","s":"The young teacher has a kind of magnetism that makes even the laziest students sit up and listen to her lessons.","t":"這位年輕老師有一種魅力，連最懶散的學生都會坐直身子聽她上課。"},{"w":"magnificent","p":"adj.","d":"extremely beautiful or impressive","c":"壯麗的；宏偉的","s":"From the hotel window we had a magnificent view of the whole bay, with fishing boats and islands shining in the sunset.","t":"從飯店窗戶望出去，我們看到整個海灣壯麗的景色，漁船和島嶼在夕陽下閃閃發光。","h":1},{"w":"magnificently","p":"adv.","d":"in an extremely beautiful or impressive way","c":"壯麗地；出色地","s":"The old temple has been magnificently restored, and its red roof and golden dragons look exactly as they did three hundred years ago.","t":"這座古廟被出色地修復了，它的紅色屋頂和金龍看起來和三百年前一模一樣。"},{"w":"magnificence","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being extremely beautiful or impressive","c":"壯麗；宏偉","s":"Visitors are often silent for a moment when they first see the magnificence of the Grand Canyon from the edge of the cliff.","t":"遊客第一次從懸崖邊看到大峽谷的壯麗時，常常會沉默片刻。"},{"w":"makeup","p":"n.","d":"colored substances that you put on your face to look more attractive","c":"化妝品；化妝","s":"My mother only wears a little makeup to work, but she puts on more for weddings and other special occasions.","t":"我媽媽上班只化淡妝，但參加婚禮和其他特殊場合時會化得濃一點。","h":1},{"w":"put on makeup","p":"v.phr.","d":"to apply makeup to your face","c":"化妝","s":"Some girls in my class put on makeup on the bus every morning because they do not have time at home.","t":"我們班有些女生每天早上在公車上化妝，因為她們在家沒有時間。"},{"w":"make up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to invent a story or excuse that is not true","c":"編造；捏造","s":"Tom did not do his homework, so he tried to make up a story about his dog eating his notebook.","t":"湯姆沒寫作業，所以他試圖編造一個他的狗把筆記本吃掉的故事。"},{"w":"make up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to form something as its parts","c":"組成；構成","s":"Students from Vietnam and Indonesia make up almost half of the class in the evening Chinese course at our school.","t":"來自越南和印尼的學生占了我們學校夜間中文課班上將近一半的人數。"},{"w":"make up for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something good to balance something bad","c":"彌補；補償","s":"He bought his sister a big ice cream to make up for forgetting her birthday last week.","t":"他買了一個大冰淇淋給妹妹，以彌補上週忘了她的生日。"},{"w":"make up with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become friends again with someone after a fight","c":"和（某人）和好","s":"After a week of not talking, the two best friends finally made up with each other and went to the movies together.","t":"一個星期沒說話之後，這兩個最好的朋友終於和好了，一起去看電影。","a":"made up with"},{"w":"manual","p":"n.","d":"a book that explains how to use or do something","c":"手冊；使用說明書","s":"Before you use the new camera, read the manual carefully so that you know what every button does.","t":"在使用新相機之前，請仔細閱讀使用手冊，這樣你才知道每個按鈕的功能。","h":1},{"w":"manual","p":"adj.","d":"done with the hands; operated by hand rather than by machine","c":"手工的；手動的","s":"My grandfather still prefers manual tools in his garden because he says they are quieter and more reliable than electric ones.","t":"我爺爺在花園裡仍然偏愛手動工具，因為他說它們比電動的更安靜、更可靠。"},{"w":"manually","p":"adv.","d":"by hand, not by machine","c":"手動地；人工地","s":"When the power went out, the staff had to open the heavy gate manually to let the cars leave the parking lot.","t":"停電時，工作人員必須手動打開沉重的大門，讓車子離開停車場。"},{"w":"manual labor","p":"n.phr.","d":"hard physical work done with the hands","c":"體力勞動","s":"Farming used to require a lot of manual labor, but today machines do most of the planting and harvesting.","t":"農業以前需要大量的體力勞動，但今天大部分的種植和收割都由機器完成。"},{"w":"manufacture","p":"v.","d":"to make goods in large numbers in a factory","c":"製造；生產","s":"The company will manufacture its electric scooters in Taiwan and then sell them to customers in Europe and Japan.","t":"這家公司將在台灣製造電動機車，然後賣給歐洲和日本的顧客。","h":1},{"w":"manufacturer","p":"n.","d":"a company that makes goods in large numbers","c":"製造商；廠商","s":"If the phone stops working within one year, the manufacturer promises to repair it for free or give you a new one.","t":"如果手機在一年內故障，製造商承諾免費維修或換一支新的給你。","h":1},{"w":"manufacture","p":"n.","d":"the making of goods in large numbers","c":"製造（業）","s":"The manufacture of bicycles has been an important industry in Taichung for more than forty years.","t":"腳踏車的製造四十多年來一直是台中的重要產業。"},{"w":"manufacturing","p":"n.","d":"the business of making goods in factories","c":"製造業","s":"Many young people now prefer jobs in computer science to jobs in manufacturing, so some factories cannot find enough workers.","t":"現在許多年輕人寧願從事電腦科學的工作，而不是製造業的工作，所以有些工廠找不到足夠的工人。"},{"w":"marathon","p":"n.","d":"a running race of about 42 kilometers","c":"馬拉松","s":"My aunt finished her first marathon in under five hours, and the whole family was waiting for her at the finish line.","t":"我阿姨在五小時內跑完她的第一場馬拉松，全家人都在終點線等她。","h":1},{"w":"run a marathon","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take part in a marathon race","c":"跑馬拉松","s":"If you want to run a marathon next spring, you should start training now by running at least three times a week.","t":"如果你想明年春天跑馬拉松，現在就應該開始訓練，每週至少跑三次。"},{"w":"half marathon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a running race of about 21 kilometers","c":"半程馬拉松","s":"A half marathon is a good first goal for new runners because it is long enough to be a challenge but not too hard.","t":"半程馬拉松對新手跑者來說是不錯的第一個目標，因為它長到足以構成挑戰，但又不會太難。"},{"w":"marathon runner","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who runs marathons","c":"馬拉松跑者","s":"A good marathon runner eats a lot of rice and noodles the night before a race to give the body enough energy.","t":"優秀的馬拉松跑者會在比賽前一晚吃很多飯和麵，讓身體有足夠的能量。"},{"w":"margin","p":"n.","d":"the empty space at the edge of a page","c":"頁邊空白","s":"Our teacher asks us to write our comments in the margin of the page so that the main text stays clean and easy to read.","t":"老師要我們把評語寫在頁面的空白邊緣，這樣正文才能保持乾淨、容易閱讀。","h":1},{"w":"margin","p":"n.","d":"the difference between two amounts, especially in a contest","c":"差距","s":"Our school won the basketball final by a margin of only two points, so the last minute of the game was very exciting.","t":"我們學校以僅僅兩分的差距贏得籃球決賽，所以比賽的最後一分鐘非常刺激。"},{"w":"profit margin","p":"n.phr.","d":"the difference between the cost of making something and its selling price","c":"利潤率","s":"The profit margin on bubble tea is very high because the ingredients are cheap but customers are happy to pay sixty dollars a cup.","t":"珍珠奶茶的利潤率非常高，因為原料便宜，但顧客樂意為一杯付六十元。"},{"w":"marginal","p":"adj.","d":"very small and not important","c":"微小的；邊緣的","s":"The new medicine made only a marginal difference to the patients, so the doctors decided to try something else.","t":"新藥對病人只產生了微小的差別，所以醫生決定嘗試其他方法。"},{"w":"by a narrow margin","p":"phr.","d":"by only a small difference","c":"以些微差距","s":"She was elected class leader by a narrow margin, winning by just three votes more than her closest rival.","t":"她以些微差距當選班長，只比最接近的對手多三票。"},{"w":"maturity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being fully grown or of behaving like a sensible adult","c":"成熟","s":"Although he is only sixteen, he showed great maturity by staying calm and calling for help when his grandfather fell.","t":"雖然他只有十六歲，但在爺爺跌倒時他保持冷靜並呼救，表現出極大的成熟。","h":1},{"w":"mature","p":"adj.","d":"fully grown; behaving in a sensible, adult way","c":"成熟的","s":"My younger sister is very mature for her age; she saves her pocket money and never fights with her friends.","t":"我妹妹就她的年齡來說非常成熟；她會存零用錢，而且從不和朋友吵架。"},{"w":"mature","p":"v.","d":"to become fully grown or fully developed","c":"成熟；長成","s":"These cheeses need to mature for at least six months in a cool, dark room before they are ready to be sold.","t":"這些起司需要在陰涼黑暗的房間裡熟成至少六個月，才可以出售。"},{"w":"immature","p":"adj.","d":"behaving like a child; not fully developed","c":"不成熟的；幼稚的","s":"It was immature of the boys to laugh at the new student just because he spoke with a different accent.","t":"那些男孩只因為新同學口音不同就嘲笑他，真是幼稚。"},{"w":"maximum","p":"adj.","d":"the largest possible or allowed","c":"最大的；最高的","s":"The maximum number of people allowed in the elevator is twelve, so please wait for the next one if it is full.","t":"電梯允許的最多人數是十二人，所以如果滿了，請等下一班。","h":1},{"w":"maximum","p":"n.","d":"the largest amount or number that is possible or allowed","c":"最大量；最大限度","s":"You can borrow a maximum of five books from the library at one time, and you must return them within two weeks.","t":"你一次最多可以從圖書館借五本書，而且必須在兩週內歸還。"},{"w":"maximize","p":"v.","d":"to make something as large or as good as possible","c":"使最大化","s":"To maximize your chances of passing the test, review your notes every evening instead of studying everything the night before.","t":"為了最大化你通過考試的機會，每天晚上複習筆記，而不是考前一晚才讀完所有東西。"},{"w":"to the maximum","p":"phr.","d":"as much as possible","c":"到極限；最大程度地","s":"The young players pushed themselves to the maximum during the final, and several of them could hardly walk after the game.","t":"年輕球員在決賽中把自己逼到極限，賽後有好幾個人幾乎走不動。"},{"w":"measurable","p":"adj.","d":"large enough to be noticed or measured","c":"可測量的；顯著的","s":"After three months of daily practice, there was a measurable improvement in her English speaking, and her teacher noticed it right away.","t":"每天練習三個月後，她的英語口說有了顯著的進步，老師馬上就注意到了。","h":1},{"w":"measure","p":"n.","d":"an action taken to deal with a problem (often plural: measures)","c":"措施；手段（常用複數 measures）","s":"The school introduced a new safety measure: every visitor must sign in at the gate and wear a name card inside.","t":"學校推出了一項新的安全措施：每位訪客都必須在大門登記，並在校內佩戴名牌。","h":1},{"w":"measure","p":"v.","d":"to find the size, amount, or degree of something","c":"測量","s":"The nurse will measure your height and weight first, and then the doctor will check your eyes and ears.","t":"護士會先測量你的身高和體重，然後醫生會檢查你的眼睛和耳朵。"},{"w":"measurement","p":"n.","d":"the size or amount found by measuring; the act of measuring","c":"測量；尺寸","s":"The tailor took my measurements carefully before he started making the suit for my cousin's wedding next month.","t":"裁縫師在開始為我做參加表哥下個月婚禮的西裝之前，仔細量了我的尺寸。","a":"measurements"},{"w":"take measures","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do things in order to deal with a problem","c":"採取措施","s":"The government has taken measures to reduce air pollution, such as offering free rides on electric buses during rush hour.","t":"政府已採取措施減少空氣污染，例如在尖峰時段提供免費搭乘電動公車。","a":"taken measures"},{"w":"mechanic","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to repair cars or machines","c":"技工；修車師傅","s":"The mechanic looked under the car for ten minutes and then told us that the brakes needed to be replaced.","t":"修車師傅在車底下看了十分鐘，然後告訴我們煞車需要更換。","h":1},{"w":"mechanical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with machines; done without thinking","c":"機械的；機械式的","s":"The plane could not take off on time because of a mechanical problem with one of its engines.","t":"飛機因為其中一具引擎的機械問題而無法準時起飛。","h":1},{"w":"mechanism","p":"n.","d":"a part of a machine that does a particular job; a way of doing something","c":"機械裝置；機制","s":"The mechanism inside the old clock is so delicate that only one man in the city knows how to repair it.","t":"這座老時鐘裡的機械裝置非常精細，全市只有一個人知道怎麼修理。"},{"w":"mechanically","p":"adv.","d":"by machine; without thinking about what you are doing","c":"機械地；呆板地","s":"The tired worker answered every question mechanically, without even looking up from his desk or changing his voice.","t":"那位疲憊的員工機械地回答每個問題，甚至沒有從桌前抬起頭或改變語氣。"},{"w":"mechanics","p":"n.","d":"the science of how forces act on objects; the way something works","c":"力學；運作方式","s":"In physics class this week we are studying mechanics, which explains why a ball falls faster the longer it drops.","t":"這週物理課我們在學力學，它解釋了為什麼球掉得越久就掉得越快。"},{"w":"memorable","p":"adj.","d":"worth remembering; special","c":"難忘的；值得紀念的","s":"Our graduation trip to Green Island was truly memorable; we swam with sea turtles and watched the stars all night.","t":"我們的綠島畢業旅行真的很難忘；我們和海龜一起游泳，還整晚看星星。","h":1},{"w":"memorial","p":"n.","d":"a building or statue built to remember a person or event","c":"紀念碑；紀念館","s":"Thousands of visitors come to the war memorial every year to lay flowers and remember the soldiers who died.","t":"每年有成千上萬的遊客來到戰爭紀念碑獻花，緬懷陣亡的士兵。","h":1},{"w":"memorial","p":"adj.","d":"made or held in order to remember a person or event","c":"紀念的；追悼的","s":"The school will hold a memorial service for the old principal, who taught here for forty years before he passed away.","t":"學校將為老校長舉行追悼會，他在過世前曾在這裡任教四十年。"},{"w":"memory","p":"n.","d":"the ability to remember things; something that you remember","c":"記憶力；回憶","s":"My grandmother has a wonderful memory for names, and she can still tell you about every student she taught.","t":"我奶奶對名字的記憶力非常好，她還能告訴你她教過的每一個學生的事。"},{"w":"memorize","p":"v.","d":"to learn something so that you can remember it exactly","c":"記住；背誦","s":"You do not need to memorize every date in the history book, but you should understand why each event happened.","t":"你不需要背歷史課本裡的每一個日期，但你應該理解每個事件發生的原因。"},{"w":"in memory of","p":"phr.","d":"as a way of remembering someone who has died","c":"為了紀念…","s":"The park was built in memory of the firefighters who lost their lives while saving people from the burning building.","t":"這座公園是為了紀念那些在燃燒的大樓裡救人而喪生的消防員而建的。"}]},{"unit":26,"theme":"memorize – monitor","cards":[{"w":"memorize","p":"v.","d":"to learn something so that you can remember it exactly","c":"記住；背誦","s":"Our English teacher asks us to memorize ten new words every day, and she gives us a short quiz on Friday.","t":"我們的英文老師要我們每天背十個新單字，然後星期五給我們一個小考。","h":1},{"w":"memory","p":"n.","d":"the ability to remember things; something that you remember","c":"記憶力；回憶","s":"My grandfather has a wonderful memory for faces, but he often forgets where he left his glasses and keys.","t":"我爺爺對臉孔的記憶力很好，但他常常忘記把眼鏡和鑰匙放在哪裡。"},{"w":"memorization","p":"n.","d":"the act of learning something by heart","c":"背誦；記憶","s":"Learning a language is not only about memorization of word lists; you also need to use the words in real conversations.","t":"學語言不只是單字表的背誦；你還需要在真實的對話中使用這些字。"},{"w":"learn by heart","p":"v.phr.","d":"to memorize something completely","c":"背下來；熟記","s":"Before the speech contest, Amy had to learn by heart a two-page speech, so she practiced it in front of the mirror every night.","t":"演講比賽前，艾咪必須把兩頁的講稿背下來，所以她每晚在鏡子前練習。"},{"w":"merchant","p":"n.","d":"a person who buys and sells goods in large amounts","c":"商人","s":"Hundreds of years ago, a rich merchant from Venice sailed to Asia to buy silk and spices, which he then sold in Europe.","t":"數百年前，一位來自威尼斯的富有商人航行到亞洲購買絲綢和香料，然後在歐洲販售。","h":1},{"w":"merchandise","p":"n.","d":"goods that are for sale in a shop","c":"商品","s":"The new department store sells all kinds of merchandise, from cheap socks to expensive watches and designer handbags.","t":"這家新的百貨公司販賣各式各樣的商品，從便宜的襪子到昂貴的手錶和名牌包。"},{"w":"merchant ship","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large ship that carries goods, not passengers","c":"商船","s":"The merchant ship left Kaohsiung harbor at dawn, carrying thousands of containers full of bicycles and computer parts.","t":"那艘商船在黎明時離開高雄港，載著數千個裝滿腳踏車和電腦零件的貨櫃。"},{"w":"commerce","p":"n.","d":"the buying and selling of goods, especially between countries","c":"商業；貿易","s":"Taiwan's economy depends heavily on international commerce, so a trade war between big countries can hurt many local companies.","t":"台灣的經濟高度依賴國際貿易，所以大國之間的貿易戰可能傷害許多本地公司。"},{"w":"mercy","p":"n.","d":"kindness shown to someone you could punish or hurt","c":"憐憫；慈悲","s":"The soldier begged the king for mercy, and the king decided to send him home instead of putting him in prison.","t":"那名士兵向國王乞求憐憫，國王決定讓他回家，而不是把他關進監獄。","h":1},{"w":"show mercy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be kind to someone instead of punishing them","c":"表現慈悲；饒恕","s":"The teacher showed mercy to the boy who broke the window because he told the truth right away and offered to pay for it.","t":"老師饒恕了打破窗戶的那個男孩，因為他立刻說了實話，還主動提出要賠償。","a":"showed mercy"},{"w":"at the mercy of","p":"phr.","d":"in a situation that is controlled by something you cannot stop","c":"任由…擺布；受制於","s":"Without a map or a phone, the lost hikers were at the mercy of the weather, and dark clouds were gathering above the mountain.","t":"沒有地圖也沒有手機，迷路的登山客只能任由天氣擺布，而山頂上方正聚集著烏雲。"},{"w":"merciful","p":"adj.","d":"kind and forgiving towards people","c":"仁慈的；寬容的","s":"The merciful judge gave the young man a second chance because it was his first mistake and he was truly sorry.","t":"這位仁慈的法官給了那個年輕人第二次機會，因為那是他第一次犯錯，而且他真心感到抱歉。"},{"w":"merciless","p":"adj.","d":"showing no kindness or pity","c":"無情的；殘忍的","s":"The merciless summer sun beat down on the farmers all afternoon, and several of them had to stop working and rest in the shade.","t":"無情的夏日烈陽整個下午照在農夫身上，好幾個人不得不停下工作，到樹蔭下休息。"},{"w":"mere","p":"adj.","d":"used to say that something is small or not important","c":"僅僅的；只不過的","s":"The famous painting was sold for a mere two hundred dollars fifty years ago, but today it is worth millions.","t":"這幅名畫五十年前僅以兩百美元售出，但今天它價值數百萬。","h":1},{"w":"merely","p":"adv.","d":"only; just","c":"僅僅；只是","s":"I was not angry at you yesterday; I was merely tired after working twelve hours, so please do not take it personally.","t":"我昨天不是在生你的氣；我只是工作了十二小時太累了，所以請不要往心裡去。"},{"w":"a mere child","p":"n.phr.","d":"only a child, too young to do something","c":"只是個孩子","s":"When his father died, Tom was a mere child of eight, but he had to help his mother take care of his two younger sisters.","t":"父親過世時，湯姆只是個八歲的孩子，但他必須幫忙媽媽照顧兩個妹妹。"},{"w":"merit","p":"n.","d":"a good quality that deserves praise","c":"優點；價值","s":"Each plan has its own merit, so the committee will need more time to compare them carefully before making a final decision.","t":"每個計畫都有自己的優點，所以委員會需要更多時間仔細比較，才能做出最後決定。","h":1},{"w":"merit","p":"v.","d":"to deserve something","c":"值得；應得","s":"Her brave action during the fire merited a special award from the mayor, who praised her at the city hall ceremony.","t":"她在火災中的勇敢行為值得市長頒發特別獎，市長在市政府的典禮上表揚了她。","a":"merited"},{"w":"on merit","p":"phr.","d":"according to how good someone or something is, not for other reasons","c":"憑實力；論功","s":"The company promises that every worker will be judged on merit, not on how long they have been with the company or who they know.","t":"公司承諾每位員工都將憑實力被評斷，而不是看他們在公司待了多久或認識誰。"},{"w":"meritorious","p":"adj.","d":"deserving praise or reward","c":"值得讚揚的","s":"The firefighter received a medal for meritorious service after he saved three children from a burning apartment last winter.","t":"那位消防員去年冬天從燃燒的公寓救出三個孩子後，因值得讚揚的服務獲頒獎章。"},{"w":"messenger","p":"n.","d":"a person who carries a message or delivers things","c":"信差；送信者","s":"In ancient times, a messenger might ride a horse for days to bring an important letter from the king to a distant city.","t":"古時候，信差可能要騎馬好幾天，才能把國王的重要信件送到遙遠的城市。","h":1},{"w":"message","p":"n.","d":"a piece of information sent to someone","c":"訊息；留言","s":"Mom left a message on the kitchen table saying that dinner was in the fridge and she would be home late.","t":"媽媽在餐桌上留了一張留言，說晚餐在冰箱裡，她會晚點回家。"},{"w":"text message","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short written message sent by phone","c":"簡訊","s":"I sent my friend a text message to tell her I was running late, but she did not read it until after the movie started.","t":"我傳了一則簡訊告訴朋友我會遲到，但她直到電影開演後才看到。"},{"w":"get the message","p":"v.phr.","d":"to understand what someone really means","c":"明白意思；領會","s":"After I yawned three times during his long story, Jack finally got the message and said goodnight.","t":"在他講長篇故事時我打了三次哈欠，傑克終於明白了意思，說了晚安。","a":"got the message"},{"w":"messy","p":"adj.","d":"dirty or untidy","c":"凌亂的；髒亂的","s":"My brother's room is so messy that you cannot see the floor; there are clothes, books, and snack bags everywhere.","t":"我哥哥的房間凌亂到看不見地板；到處都是衣服、書本和零食袋。","h":1},{"w":"mess","p":"n.","d":"a dirty or untidy state","c":"雜亂；一團糟","s":"After the birthday party, the living room was a complete mess, with paper cups and cake all over the carpet.","t":"生日派對結束後，客廳一團糟，地毯上到處是紙杯和蛋糕。"},{"w":"mess up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make something dirty, untidy, or to do something badly","c":"弄亂；搞砸","s":"I was so nervous during the piano recital that I messed up the last part of the song, but the audience still clapped warmly.","t":"鋼琴演奏會上我太緊張了，以致於搞砸了曲子的最後一段，但觀眾還是熱情地鼓掌。","a":"messed up"},{"w":"make a mess","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a place dirty or untidy","c":"弄得一團亂","s":"The children made a mess in the kitchen while trying to bake cookies, but the cookies tasted surprisingly good.","t":"孩子們試著烤餅乾時把廚房弄得一團亂，但餅乾出乎意料地好吃。","a":"made a mess"},{"w":"mess around","p":"v.phr.","d":"to waste time doing silly things","c":"鬼混；瞎混","s":"Stop messing around with your phone and finish your homework, or you will have to stay up late again tonight.","t":"別再玩手機瞎混了，快把作業寫完，否則今晚又得熬夜。","a":"messing around"},{"w":"microscope","p":"n.","d":"an instrument that makes very small things look much bigger","c":"顯微鏡","s":"In biology class, we looked at a drop of pond water under the microscope and were amazed by the tiny living things moving around.","t":"生物課上，我們用顯微鏡觀察一滴池塘水，對裡面游來游去的微小生物感到驚奇。","h":1},{"w":"microscopic","p":"adj.","d":"so small that it can only be seen with a microscope","c":"微小的；顯微鏡下才可見的","s":"Although the kitchen looked clean, the scientist found millions of microscopic germs living on the sponge next to the sink.","t":"雖然廚房看起來很乾淨，科學家卻在水槽旁的海綿上發現了數百萬個微小的細菌。"},{"w":"telescope","p":"n.","d":"an instrument that makes distant objects look closer","c":"望遠鏡","s":"On clear nights, my uncle sets up his telescope on the balcony so that we can look at the rings of Saturn and the moon's craters.","t":"晴朗的夜晚，叔叔會在陽台架起望遠鏡，讓我們看土星環和月球上的坑洞。"},{"w":"microwave","p":"n.","d":"an oven that cooks food very quickly using special waves","c":"微波爐","s":"When I get home late, I just put the leftover rice in the microwave for two minutes instead of cooking a new meal.","t":"我晚回家時，就把剩飯放進微波爐加熱兩分鐘，而不是重新煮一餐。"},{"w":"mild","p":"adj.","d":"not strong, serious, or severe; gentle","c":"溫和的；輕微的","s":"The doctor said my cold was mild and that I only needed to rest and drink plenty of warm water for a few days.","t":"醫生說我的感冒很輕微，只需要休息幾天並多喝溫開水。","h":1},{"w":"mild","p":"adj.","d":"(of weather) not too hot or too cold","c":"（天氣）溫和的","s":"Taipei has a mild winter compared to Korea or Japan, so we rarely see snow in the city.","t":"和韓國或日本相比，台北的冬天很溫和，所以我們在市區很少看到雪。"},{"w":"mildly","p":"adv.","d":"slightly; in a gentle way","c":"輕微地；溫和地","s":"She was only mildly interested in the movie, so she kept checking her phone and left before the ending.","t":"她對那部電影只有些微興趣，所以一直看手機，電影還沒結束就離開了。"},{"w":"mildness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being gentle or not severe","c":"溫和；輕微","s":"Many tourists visit Kenting in winter because of the mildness of the weather and the warm, sunny beaches.","t":"許多遊客冬天到墾丁旅遊，是因為天氣的溫和以及溫暖、陽光普照的海灘。"},{"w":"mill","p":"n.","d":"a building with machines for grinding grain into flour; a factory","c":"磨坊；工廠","s":"The old mill by the river used to grind wheat into flour for the whole village, but now it is a museum.","t":"河邊那座老磨坊以前為全村人把小麥磨成麵粉，但現在是一座博物館。","h":1},{"w":"mill","p":"v.","d":"to grind grain into flour or powder","c":"磨碎；碾磨","s":"The farmers mill their rice right after the harvest, and the fresh rice flour is then sold at the weekend market.","t":"農夫們在收成後立刻碾磨稻米，新鮮的米粉隨後在週末市集販售。"},{"w":"windmill","p":"n.","d":"a tall building or machine with large blades turned by the wind","c":"風車","s":"The Netherlands is famous for its tulips and the hundreds of windmills that once pumped water out of the low land.","t":"荷蘭以鬱金香和數百座曾經把低地的水抽出來的風車聞名。","a":"windmills"},{"w":"miller","p":"n.","d":"a person who owns or works in a mill","c":"磨坊主人","s":"In the old story, the poor miller told the king that his daughter could turn straw into gold, which got her into trouble.","t":"在那個古老的故事裡，貧窮的磨坊主人告訴國王他的女兒能把稻草變成黃金，這讓她惹上麻煩。"},{"w":"millionaire","p":"n.","d":"a very rich person who has at least a million dollars","c":"百萬富翁","s":"The young man became a millionaire at twenty-five after he sold his small game company to a famous Japanese firm.","t":"那個年輕人二十五歲時把自己的小遊戲公司賣給一家著名的日本公司，成了百萬富翁。","h":1},{"w":"million","p":"n.","d":"the number 1,000,000","c":"百萬","s":"More than two million people live in Taichung, and the city is still growing because many young families move there.","t":"超過兩百萬人住在台中，而且這座城市還在成長，因為許多年輕家庭搬到那裡。"},{"w":"billionaire","p":"n.","d":"a person who has at least a billion dollars","c":"億萬富翁","s":"The billionaire promised to give away most of his money to schools and hospitals before he dies.","t":"那位億萬富翁承諾在過世前把大部分的錢捐給學校和醫院。"},{"w":"millions of","p":"phr.","d":"a very large number of","c":"數百萬的；無數的","s":"Every year, millions of people watch the fireworks at Taipei 101 on New Year's Eve, either in person or on television.","t":"每年跨年夜，數百萬人親自或透過電視觀看台北101的煙火。"},{"w":"miner","p":"n.","d":"a person who works in a mine digging coal, gold, or other materials","c":"礦工","s":"The miner worked deep underground for ten hours a day, and his face was always black with coal dust when he came home.","t":"那位礦工每天在地底深處工作十小時，回家時臉上總是沾滿黑色的煤灰。","h":1},{"w":"mineral","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance such as coal, salt, or gold that is found in the ground","c":"礦物","s":"Taiwan has few natural minerals of its own, so it must import oil, coal, and iron from other countries.","t":"台灣本身的天然礦物很少，所以必須從其他國家進口石油、煤和鐵。","a":"minerals","h":1},{"w":"mine","p":"n.","d":"a deep hole or tunnel in the ground where coal, gold, etc. are dug out","c":"礦場；礦坑","s":"The old gold mine in Jiufen closed many years ago, but tourists still visit the town for its tea houses and views.","t":"九份的舊金礦多年前就關閉了，但遊客仍會來這個小鎮喝茶、看風景。"},{"w":"mining","p":"n.","d":"the industry of digging coal, gold, etc. out of the ground","c":"採礦業","s":"Mining was once the main industry in this mountain town, but today most families earn their living from tourism.","t":"採礦業曾是這個山城的主要產業，但今天大多數家庭靠觀光業維生。","a":"Mining"},{"w":"mineral water","p":"n.phr.","d":"water from a natural spring that contains minerals, sold in bottles","c":"礦泉水","s":"The restaurant charges three dollars for a bottle of mineral water, so I usually ask for free tap water instead.","t":"這家餐廳一瓶礦泉水要價三美元，所以我通常改要免費的白開水。"},{"w":"minimum","p":"adj.","d":"the smallest possible or allowed","c":"最小的；最低的","s":"The minimum age for getting a driver's license in Taiwan is eighteen, so my brother has to wait one more year.","t":"在台灣考駕照的最低年齡是十八歲，所以我哥哥還要再等一年。","h":1},{"w":"minimum","p":"n.","d":"the smallest amount or number that is possible or allowed","c":"最小量；最低限度","s":"You need to spend a minimum of five hundred dollars to get free delivery from this online shop.","t":"你在這家網路商店至少要消費五百元，才能享有免運費。"},{"w":"minimize","p":"v.","d":"to make something as small as possible","c":"使減到最少；最小化","s":"Wearing a helmet when you ride a scooter can minimize the risk of serious head injury in an accident.","t":"騎機車時戴安全帽，可以把發生事故時頭部重傷的風險減到最低。"},{"w":"minimal","p":"adj.","d":"very small in amount or degree","c":"極少的；最低限度的","s":"The typhoon caused only minimal damage to our town, with a few fallen trees and some broken signs.","t":"這次颱風對我們鎮上只造成極小的損害，只有幾棵樹倒下和幾個招牌損壞。"},{"w":"keep to a minimum","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep something as small as possible","c":"盡量減少","s":"During the exam period, I try to keep to a minimum my time on social media so that I can focus on studying.","t":"考試期間，我試著把花在社群媒體上的時間盡量減少，這樣才能專心讀書。"},{"w":"minister","p":"n.","d":"a senior member of a government in charge of a department","c":"部長","s":"The education minister announced that all senior high school students will have free lunches starting next September.","t":"教育部長宣布，從明年九月開始所有高中生都能享有免費午餐。","h":1},{"w":"ministry","p":"n.","d":"a government department","c":"（政府的）部","s":"The Ministry of Health has asked everyone to wash their hands often and stay home if they have a fever.","t":"衛生部呼籲大家勤洗手，如果發燒就待在家裡。","a":"Ministry","h":1},{"w":"prime minister","p":"n.phr.","d":"the leader of the government in some countries","c":"首相；總理","s":"The British prime minister lives and works at 10 Downing Street, a famous address that many tourists photograph.","t":"英國首相在唐寧街十號生活和工作，那是許多遊客拍照的著名地址。"},{"w":"minister","p":"n.","d":"a priest in some Christian churches","c":"牧師","s":"The minister spoke kindly to the family at the funeral and reminded everyone of the happy years they had shared.","t":"牧師在葬禮上親切地對家屬說話，提醒大家曾共度的快樂歲月。"},{"w":"administer","p":"v.","d":"to manage or organize something; to give medicine","c":"管理；施用（藥物）","s":"The nurse will administer the vaccine in your left arm, and you should stay in the waiting room for fifteen minutes afterward.","t":"護士會在你的左手臂施打疫苗，之後你應該在候診室待十五分鐘。"},{"w":"mischief","p":"n.","d":"bad behavior, especially by children, that is annoying but not serious","c":"惡作劇；淘氣","s":"The twins are full of mischief; yesterday they hid their grandmother's glasses and watched her search the whole house.","t":"這對雙胞胎充滿淘氣；昨天他們把奶奶的眼鏡藏起來，看著她找遍整間屋子。","h":1},{"w":"mischievous","p":"adj.","d":"enjoying playing tricks and annoying people","c":"淘氣的；愛惡作劇的","s":"My mischievous little cousin put salt in the sugar bowl, so everyone's tea tasted terrible at breakfast this morning.","t":"我愛惡作劇的小表弟把鹽放進糖罐裡，所以今天早餐大家的茶都難喝極了。"},{"w":"get into mischief","p":"v.phr.","d":"to behave badly and cause trouble","c":"調皮搗蛋；惹麻煩","s":"Whenever the teacher leaves the classroom, the boys in the back row get into mischief and start throwing paper balls.","t":"每當老師離開教室，後排的男生就開始調皮搗蛋，丟起紙團。"},{"w":"make mischief","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause trouble between people on purpose","c":"挑撥離間；搗亂","s":"Some people on the Internet like to make mischief by spreading rumors about famous singers and actors.","t":"網路上有些人喜歡散播有關知名歌手和演員的謠言來搗亂。"},{"w":"miserable","p":"adj.","d":"very unhappy or uncomfortable","c":"悲慘的；痛苦的","s":"I felt miserable all weekend because I had a high fever and could not go to my best friend's birthday party.","t":"我整個週末都覺得很痛苦，因為我發高燒，無法參加最好朋友的生日派對。","h":1},{"w":"misery","p":"n.","d":"great suffering or unhappiness","c":"痛苦；悲慘","s":"The earthquake brought great misery to the village, and many families lost their homes and had to live in tents.","t":"地震為這個村莊帶來巨大的痛苦，許多家庭失去家園，必須住在帳篷裡。"},{"w":"miserably","p":"adv.","d":"in a very unhappy way; very badly","c":"悲慘地；糟糕地","s":"Our team failed miserably in the final game, losing by thirty points to a school we had beaten twice before.","t":"我們的球隊在決賽中慘敗，以三十分之差輸給一所我們之前贏過兩次的學校。"},{"w":"make someone's life a misery","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause someone a lot of trouble or unhappiness","c":"讓某人生活痛苦不堪","s":"The noisy construction next door has made our life a misery for months, so we cannot open the windows or sleep late.","t":"隔壁吵鬧的工程好幾個月來讓我們的生活痛苦不堪，我們既不能開窗也不能睡晚一點。","a":"made our life a misery"},{"w":"misfortune","p":"n.","d":"bad luck, or an unlucky event","c":"不幸；厄運","s":"After a year of misfortune, in which he lost his job and broke his leg, Mr. Wang finally found a new position at a good company.","t":"經過一年的不幸，他失去工作又摔斷了腿，王先生終於在一家好公司找到新職位。","h":1},{"w":"fortune","p":"n.","d":"luck; a very large amount of money","c":"運氣；財富","s":"The old man made a fortune selling bubble tea and then opened twenty more shops across the country.","t":"那位老先生靠賣珍珠奶茶賺了一大筆財富，然後在全國開了二十多家店。"},{"w":"fortunate","p":"adj.","d":"lucky","c":"幸運的","s":"We were fortunate to find a parking space right in front of the restaurant on such a busy Saturday night.","t":"在這麼忙碌的週六晚上，我們很幸運能在餐廳正前方找到停車位。"},{"w":"unfortunately","p":"adv.","d":"used to say that something is sad or disappointing","c":"不幸地；遺憾地","s":"I wanted to see the concert, but unfortunately, all the tickets were sold out within ten minutes of going on sale.","t":"我想去看那場演唱會，但遺憾的是，所有門票在開賣十分鐘內就賣光了。"},{"w":"have the misfortune to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be unlucky enough to experience something","c":"不幸地…","s":"On our trip to Japan, we had the misfortune to lose our passports on the first day and had to spend hours at the police station.","t":"我們去日本旅行時，不幸地在第一天就弄丟護照，必須在警察局耗上好幾個小時。","a":"had the misfortune to"},{"w":"mislead, misled, misled","p":"v.","d":"to make someone believe something that is not true","c":"誤導","s":"The advertisement misled many customers into thinking the drink was healthy, when in fact it was full of sugar.","t":"那則廣告誤導許多顧客，讓他們以為這種飲料很健康，事實上它含有大量的糖。","a":"misled","h":1},{"w":"misleading","p":"adj.","d":"giving the wrong idea or impression","c":"誤導的；令人誤解的","s":"The title of the news report was misleading; the actor was not really hurt, he only had a small cut on his finger.","t":"那則新聞報導的標題很誤導人；那位演員並沒有真的受傷，只是手指上有一道小傷口。"},{"w":"lead, led, led","p":"v.","d":"to show someone the way; to be in charge of a group","c":"帶領；領導","s":"The tour guide led us through the narrow streets of the old town and told us stories about every building.","t":"導遊帶領我們穿過老城區狹窄的街道，並講述每棟建築的故事。","a":"led"},{"w":"leader","p":"n.","d":"a person who leads a group or country","c":"領導者；領袖","s":"A good leader listens to the ideas of everyone on the team before making a decision that affects them all.","t":"好的領導者在做出影響所有人的決定前，會先聽取團隊中每個人的想法。"},{"w":"misunderstand, misunderstood, misunderstood","p":"v.","d":"to not understand someone or something correctly","c":"誤解","s":"I think you misunderstood me; I did not say the party was canceled, I said it was moved to Saturday.","t":"我想你誤解我了；我不是說派對取消了，我是說改到星期六。","a":"misunderstood","h":1},{"w":"misunderstanding","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which someone does not understand something correctly","c":"誤會","s":"There was a misunderstanding about the meeting time, so half of the group arrived an hour early and had to wait outside.","t":"關於開會時間有個誤會，所以一半的人提早一小時到，只好在外面等。"},{"w":"understand, understood, understood","p":"v.","d":"to know the meaning of something","c":"理解；明白","s":"At first I did not understand the math problem, but after the teacher drew a picture on the board, it became clear.","t":"一開始我不明白那道數學題，但老師在黑板上畫了一張圖後，就變得清楚了。","a":"understand"},{"w":"understanding","p":"adj.","d":"kind and willing to forgive other people's problems","c":"體諒的；善解人意的","s":"My boss was very understanding when my mother was in the hospital, and she let me leave work early every day that week.","t":"我媽媽住院時，老闆非常體諒，那一週她每天都讓我提早下班。"},{"w":"misunderstand each other","p":"v.phr.","d":"to each fail to understand what the other means","c":"彼此誤會","s":"People who speak different languages often misunderstand each other at first, but patience and a smile can solve most problems.","t":"說不同語言的人一開始常常彼此誤會，但耐心和微笑可以解決大部分的問題。"},{"w":"moderate","p":"adj.","d":"not too much and not too little; average","c":"適度的；中等的","s":"Doctors say that moderate exercise, such as walking thirty minutes a day, is enough to keep most people healthy.","t":"醫生說適度的運動，例如每天走路三十分鐘，就足以讓大多數人保持健康。","h":1},{"w":"moderate","p":"v.","d":"to make something less extreme; to lead a discussion","c":"緩和；主持（討論）","s":"A well-known journalist was invited to moderate the debate between the three candidates for city mayor.","t":"一位知名記者受邀主持三位市長候選人之間的辯論。"},{"w":"moderately","p":"adv.","d":"to an average degree; not very","c":"適度地；中等地","s":"The new Korean restaurant is moderately priced, so students can afford to eat there once or twice a month.","t":"這家新的韓式餐廳價格適中，所以學生每個月可以負擔得起去吃一兩次。"},{"w":"moderation","p":"n.","d":"the quality of doing something without going too far","c":"適度；節制","s":"Eating sweets in moderation is fine, but having three pieces of cake every day is bad for your teeth and your health.","t":"適度吃甜食是沒問題的，但每天吃三塊蛋糕對牙齒和健康都不好。"},{"w":"modest","p":"adj.","d":"not talking proudly about your own abilities or success","c":"謙虛的","s":"Although he won first prize in the national science fair, Kevin remained modest and thanked his teammates and teachers.","t":"雖然在全國科展中獲得第一名，凱文仍然很謙虛，感謝他的隊友和老師。","h":1},{"w":"modesty","p":"n.","d":"the quality of not talking proudly about yourself","c":"謙虛；謙遜","s":"The famous singer is known for her modesty; she always says that her success is because of her fans and her family.","t":"這位知名歌手以她的謙虛聞名；她總是說自己的成功是因為粉絲和家人。","h":1},{"w":"modest","p":"adj.","d":"not very large in size or amount; simple","c":"不大的；樸素的","s":"The family lives in a modest apartment near the night market, with only two small bedrooms and a tiny kitchen.","t":"這家人住在夜市附近一間樸素的公寓裡，只有兩間小臥室和一個小廚房。"},{"w":"modestly","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is not proud or showy","c":"謙虛地；適度地","s":"When reporters praised his goal, the young player modestly replied that the whole team deserved the credit.","t":"當記者稱讚他的進球時，這位年輕球員謙虛地回答，功勞應該屬於整個球隊。"},{"w":"immodest","p":"adj.","d":"talking too proudly about yourself","c":"不謙虛的；自大的","s":"It would be immodest of me to say I am the best student in class, but I did get the highest score on this test.","t":"說自己是班上最好的學生會顯得不謙虛，但我這次考試確實拿到最高分。"},{"w":"monitor","p":"n.","d":"a screen that shows information from a computer or camera","c":"螢幕；監視器","s":"The security guard watches six monitors at the same time, so he can see every entrance and parking area of the building.","t":"警衛同時看著六個監視器，所以他能看到大樓的每個入口和停車區。","a":"monitors","h":1},{"w":"monitor","p":"v.","d":"to watch and check something carefully over a period of time","c":"監測；監控","s":"The nurses will monitor your heart rate and blood pressure every hour during the night after the operation.","t":"手術後的夜裡，護士每小時會監測你的心跳和血壓。"},{"w":"monitor","p":"n.","d":"a student chosen to help the teacher with small jobs","c":"班長；值日生","s":"As the class monitor this week, Lisa has to collect the homework and turn off the lights when we leave the room.","t":"身為這週的班級值日生，麗莎必須收作業，並在我們離開教室時關燈。"},{"w":"monitoring","p":"n.","d":"the act of watching and checking something regularly","c":"監測；監控","s":"Careful monitoring of air quality helps the city decide when to warn people to stay indoors on polluted days.","t":"對空氣品質的仔細監測有助於城市決定何時在污染的日子警告民眾待在室內。"}]},{"unit":27,"theme":"monument – nursery","cards":[{"w":"monument","p":"n.","d":"a statue or building made to remember a famous person or event","c":"紀念碑；紀念建築","s":"In the center of the square stands a tall stone monument built to honor the soldiers who died in the war a century ago.","t":"廣場中央矗立著一座高大的石造紀念碑，是為了紀念一百年前在戰爭中陣亡的士兵而建的。","h":1},{"w":"monumental","p":"adj.","d":"very big, important, or impressive","c":"巨大的；重要的","s":"Cleaning up the whole beach after the typhoon was a monumental task, but two hundred volunteers finished it in a single weekend.","t":"颱風過後清理整個海灘是一項巨大的工作，但兩百名志工在一個週末內就完成了。"},{"w":"historic monument","p":"n.phr.","d":"an old building or place that is protected because of its history","c":"歷史古蹟","s":"The Red House in Ximending is a historic monument that was built in 1908, and today it hosts art shows and small shops.","t":"西門町的紅樓是建於1908年的歷史古蹟，如今那裡舉辦藝術展覽，也有小商店。"},{"w":"memorial","p":"n.","d":"a building or statue built to remember a person or event","c":"紀念碑；紀念館","s":"Every spring, thousands of people visit the memorial to lay flowers and remember the victims of the earthquake.","t":"每年春天，成千上萬的人到紀念碑獻花，緬懷地震的罹難者。"},{"w":"moreover","p":"adv.","d":"in addition; what is more","c":"此外；而且","s":"The new apartment is close to the MRT station; moreover, the rent is five thousand dollars cheaper than our old place.","t":"新公寓離捷運站很近；此外，租金比我們舊家便宜五千元。","h":1},{"w":"furthermore","p":"adv.","d":"in addition; moreover","c":"此外；再者","s":"Riding a bike to school saves money and keeps you fit; furthermore, it does not pollute the air like a scooter does.","t":"騎腳踏車上學省錢又能保持健康；此外，它不像機車那樣污染空氣。"},{"w":"what's more","p":"phr.","d":"used to add something surprising or important","c":"更重要的是；而且","s":"The restaurant serves the best beef noodles in town, and what's more, every bowl costs less than one hundred dollars.","t":"這家餐廳供應全城最好吃的牛肉麵，而且，每碗都不到一百元。"},{"w":"in addition","p":"phr.","d":"also; as well","c":"此外；另外","s":"Students must hand in a written report; in addition, each group will give a five-minute talk in front of the class.","t":"學生必須繳交書面報告；此外，每組還要在全班面前做五分鐘的口頭報告。"},{"w":"motivate","p":"v.","d":"to make someone want to do something or work hard","c":"激勵；促使","s":"A good coach knows how to motivate the players before a big game, so that they give their best even when they are tired.","t":"好的教練知道如何在大賽前激勵球員，讓他們即使疲倦也能全力以赴。","h":1},{"w":"motivation","p":"n.","d":"the reason or desire that makes you want to do something","c":"動機；動力","s":"My main motivation for learning Japanese is that I want to talk to my grandmother's old friends in Osaka without a translator.","t":"我學日文的主要動機是想不透過翻譯，直接和奶奶在大阪的老朋友聊天。","h":1},{"w":"motivated","p":"adj.","d":"very keen to do something or to succeed","c":"有動力的；積極的","s":"After she visited the hospital, Judy became highly motivated to study medicine and started reading science books every night.","t":"參觀醫院之後，茱蒂變得非常有動力要念醫學，開始每晚讀科學書籍。"},{"w":"motive","p":"n.","d":"the reason why someone does something, especially something bad","c":"動機；目的","s":"The police still do not know the motive for the robbery, because the thief took only an old photo and left the money.","t":"警方仍不知道這起搶案的動機，因為小偷只拿走一張舊照片，把錢留了下來。"},{"w":"lack of motivation","p":"n.phr.","d":"not having a strong desire to do something","c":"缺乏動力","s":"Many students fail not because they are not smart but because of a lack of motivation, so teachers try to make lessons more interesting.","t":"許多學生失敗不是因為不聰明，而是因為缺乏動力，所以老師設法讓課程更有趣。"},{"w":"mountainous","p":"adj.","d":"having many mountains","c":"多山的","s":"Taiwan is a mountainous island, and more than two hundred of its peaks are higher than three thousand meters.","t":"台灣是一座多山的島嶼，有兩百多座山峰超過三千公尺。","h":1},{"w":"mountain","p":"n.","d":"a very high hill","c":"山","s":"Climbing Jade Mountain, the highest mountain in Taiwan, takes two days, and you need a permit to enter the park.","t":"攀登台灣最高的山玉山需要兩天，而且你需要許可證才能進入園區。"},{"w":"mountain climbing","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sport of climbing mountains","c":"登山","s":"My uncle took up mountain climbing after he retired, and now he spends almost every weekend on a trail somewhere in Taiwan.","t":"我叔叔退休後開始從事登山，現在他幾乎每個週末都在台灣某條步道上。"},{"w":"mountain range","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long line of mountains","c":"山脈","s":"The Central Mountain Range runs down the middle of Taiwan like a backbone and separates the east coast from the west.","t":"中央山脈像脊椎一樣貫穿台灣中部，把東海岸與西部隔開。","a":"Mountain Range"},{"w":"muddy","p":"adj.","d":"covered in mud or full of mud","c":"泥濘的；沾滿泥的","s":"After the heavy rain, the path to the waterfall was so muddy that our shoes sank into the ground with every step.","t":"大雨過後，通往瀑布的小路非常泥濘，我們每走一步鞋子就陷進土裡。","h":1},{"w":"mud","p":"n.","d":"wet, soft earth","c":"泥巴；泥土","s":"The children came home covered in mud from head to toe after playing football in the rain all afternoon.","t":"孩子們在雨中踢了一下午的足球後，從頭到腳沾滿泥巴回家。"},{"w":"muddy","p":"v.","d":"to make something dirty with mud; to make something less clear","c":"弄髒；使混濁","s":"The cows walked through the stream and muddied the clear water, so we had to wait before filling our bottles.","t":"牛群走過小溪，弄濁了清澈的溪水，所以我們得等一下才能裝水瓶。","a":"muddied"},{"w":"mudslide","p":"n.","d":"a large amount of mud sliding down a hill","c":"土石流","s":"The typhoon caused a mudslide that blocked the mountain road, so the village was cut off for three days.","t":"颱風引發的土石流堵住了山路，所以村莊與外界隔絕了三天。"},{"w":"mule","p":"n.","d":"an animal whose parents are a horse and a donkey, used for carrying things","c":"騾子","s":"In the mountains, the farmers still use a mule to carry heavy bags of tea leaves down the narrow, rocky trail.","t":"在山區，農夫們仍然用騾子把沉重的茶葉袋沿著狹窄多石的小徑運下山。","h":1},{"w":"as stubborn as a mule","p":"adj.phr.","d":"very stubborn; refusing to change your mind","c":"固執得像頭騾子","s":"My grandfather is as stubborn as a mule; once he decides to walk home in the rain, nobody can make him take a taxi.","t":"我爺爺固執得像頭騾子；一旦他決定冒雨走路回家，沒人能叫他搭計程車。"},{"w":"donkey","p":"n.","d":"an animal like a small horse with long ears","c":"驢子","s":"The little donkey carried the tourists' bags up the hill while they walked slowly behind it, taking photos of the view.","t":"小驢子馱著遊客的包包上山，遊客則慢慢走在牠後面拍風景照。"},{"w":"multiple","p":"adj.","d":"involving many people or things; more than one","c":"多種的；多重的","s":"The driver was taken to the hospital with multiple injuries after his car hit a tree on the mountain road last night.","t":"昨晚那名駕駛的車在山路上撞樹後，身上帶著多處傷被送往醫院。","h":1},{"w":"multiple-choice","p":"adj.","d":"(of a test) giving several answers from which you choose the correct one","c":"選擇題的","s":"The first part of the English exam is multiple-choice, and the second part asks you to write a short passage about your weekend.","t":"英文考試的第一部分是選擇題，第二部分要你寫一篇關於週末的短文。"},{"w":"multiply","p":"v.","d":"to add a number to itself a certain number of times; to increase greatly","c":"乘；大量增加","s":"If you multiply the length by the width, you get the area of the rectangle, which is all you need for this math problem.","t":"如果你把長乘以寬，就會得到長方形的面積，這道數學題只需要這樣。"},{"w":"multiply","p":"v.","d":"to increase greatly in number","c":"繁殖；倍增","s":"Mosquitoes multiply quickly in warm weather, so you should empty any pots or cans that hold rainwater near your house.","t":"蚊子在溫暖的天氣中繁殖得很快，所以你應該把家附近積雨水的花盆或罐子倒空。"},{"w":"murderer","p":"n.","d":"a person who kills someone on purpose","c":"兇手；殺人犯","s":"After months of searching, the police finally caught the murderer in a small town hundreds of kilometers from the city.","t":"經過數月的搜尋，警方終於在離城市數百公里的小鎮抓到了那名兇手。","h":1},{"w":"murder","p":"n.","d":"the crime of killing someone on purpose","c":"謀殺","s":"The detective story is about a murder that happened on a train, and every passenger seems to have a secret.","t":"這部偵探小說講的是一樁發生在火車上的謀殺案，每位乘客似乎都有秘密。"},{"w":"murder","p":"v.","d":"to kill someone on purpose","c":"謀殺","s":"In the play, the king is murdered by his own brother, who wants to take the throne and marry the queen.","t":"在這齣戲裡，國王被自己的弟弟謀殺，弟弟想奪取王位並娶皇后。","a":"murdered"},{"w":"get away with murder","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something very bad without being punished","c":"為非作歹卻不受懲罰","s":"The teacher is so kind that some students think they can get away with murder, but she keeps careful notes about everything they do.","t":"這位老師太和善了，有些學生以為可以為所欲為而不受懲罰，但她把他們做的每件事都仔細記下來。"},{"w":"murmur","p":"v.","d":"to say something very quietly","c":"低語；輕聲說","s":"The old man murmured a few words in his sleep, and his daughter leaned closer to hear what he was trying to say.","t":"老先生在睡夢中低聲說了幾句話，女兒靠近一點想聽清楚他想說什麼。","a":"murmured","h":1},{"w":"murmur","p":"n.","d":"a soft, low sound made by people speaking or by water, wind, etc.","c":"低語聲；潺潺聲","s":"We fell asleep to the gentle murmur of the stream outside our tent and woke up to the sound of birds.","t":"我們在帳篷外小溪輕柔的潺潺聲中入睡，在鳥鳴聲中醒來。"},{"w":"whisper","p":"v.","d":"to speak very quietly using your breath rather than your voice","c":"低聲說；耳語","s":"The two girls kept whispering during the movie, so the man behind them finally asked them to be quiet.","t":"那兩個女孩在電影播放時一直竊竊私語，所以後面的男子終於請她們安靜。","a":"whispering"},{"w":"mutter","p":"v.","d":"to speak quietly and unclearly, often because you are annoyed","c":"咕噥；嘀咕","s":"When the bus was late again, the man next to me muttered something angry under his breath and checked his watch.","t":"公車又誤點時，我旁邊的男子低聲嘀咕了幾句氣話，然後看了看手錶。","a":"muttered"},{"w":"mutual","p":"adj.","d":"felt or done by two or more people towards each other","c":"相互的；彼此的","s":"A good marriage is built on mutual respect, which means that both people listen to each other and share the housework.","t":"美好的婚姻建立在相互尊重之上，也就是說雙方都傾聽對方並分擔家務。","h":1},{"w":"mutual friend","p":"n.phr.","d":"a friend that two people both have","c":"共同的朋友","s":"My parents met at a party through a mutual friend, who later became the best man at their wedding.","t":"我父母在派對上透過一位共同的朋友認識，那位朋友後來成了他們婚禮上的伴郎。"},{"w":"mutually","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that affects or involves both sides","c":"相互地；彼此地","s":"The two companies signed a mutually beneficial agreement: one provides the design, and the other builds the product.","t":"兩家公司簽了一份彼此有利的協議：一家負責設計，另一家負責製造產品。"},{"w":"by mutual agreement","p":"phr.","d":"with both sides agreeing","c":"經雙方同意","s":"The singer and the record company ended their contract by mutual agreement, so there was no fight in court and no angry statements.","t":"這位歌手和唱片公司經雙方同意結束合約，所以沒有對簿公堂，也沒有發表憤怒的聲明。"},{"w":"mysterious","p":"adj.","d":"strange and not understood or explained","c":"神秘的；難以理解的","s":"A mysterious light appeared over the mountain every night for a week, and nobody in the village could explain where it came from.","t":"一道神秘的光連續一週每晚出現在山上空，村裡沒有人能解釋它從哪裡來。","h":1},{"w":"mystery","p":"n.","d":"something that cannot be explained or understood","c":"謎；神秘的事","s":"How the ancient people moved such huge stones without machines is still a mystery to scientists today.","t":"古代人如何在沒有機器的情況下搬動這麼巨大的石頭，對今日的科學家來說仍是個謎。"},{"w":"mysteriously","p":"adv.","d":"in a strange way that cannot be explained","c":"神秘地；不可思議地","s":"My keys mysteriously disappeared from the table and then turned up inside the fridge, next to the milk, two days later.","t":"我的鑰匙神秘地從桌上消失，兩天後卻出現在冰箱裡的牛奶旁邊。"},{"w":"mystery novel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a story about a crime or strange event that is solved at the end","c":"推理小說","s":"I love reading a good mystery novel on a rainy weekend and trying to guess who the criminal is before the detective does.","t":"我喜歡在下雨的週末讀一本好的推理小說，試著在偵探之前猜出誰是罪犯。"},{"w":"namely","p":"adv.","d":"used to give exact details of something you have just mentioned","c":"即；也就是","s":"Only two students in our class have been abroad, namely Peter and Lisa, and both of them went to Japan with their parents.","t":"我們班上只有兩個學生出過國，也就是彼得和麗莎，而且他們都是和父母去日本。","h":1},{"w":"name","p":"v.","d":"to give a name to someone or something; to say the name of","c":"命名；說出名字","s":"The couple decided to name their baby daughter after her grandmother, who had taken care of them for many years.","t":"這對夫妻決定用奶奶的名字為女兒命名，奶奶多年來一直照顧他們。"},{"w":"that is to say","p":"phr.","d":"in other words; namely","c":"也就是說","s":"The museum is closed on public holidays, that is to say, you cannot visit it this Friday because it is the Dragon Boat Festival.","t":"博物館在國定假日休館，也就是說，這個星期五因為是端午節，你無法參觀。"},{"w":"name after","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give someone the same name as another person","c":"以…的名字命名","s":"The new library was named after a famous writer who was born in this town and wrote most of her novels here.","t":"新圖書館以一位在這個小鎮出生、並在此寫下大部分小說的知名作家的名字命名。","a":"named after"},{"w":"nationality","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a citizen of a particular country","c":"國籍","s":"The form asks for your name, date of birth, and nationality, so remember to bring your passport when you go to the office.","t":"表格要填你的姓名、出生日期和國籍，所以去辦公室時記得帶護照。","h":1},{"w":"nation","p":"n.","d":"a country, especially when thought of as its people and government","c":"國家；民族","s":"The whole nation watched the baseball final on television, and people cheered in the streets when the home team won.","t":"全國都透過電視觀看棒球決賽，主隊獲勝時人們在街上歡呼。"},{"w":"national","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a whole country","c":"全國的；國家的","s":"The national park protects thousands of rare plants and animals, so visitors are not allowed to pick flowers or feed the monkeys.","t":"這座國家公園保護數千種稀有動植物，所以遊客不可以摘花或餵猴子。"},{"w":"international","p":"adj.","d":"involving two or more countries","c":"國際的","s":"Our school is holding an international food fair next month, and students from Vietnam, Japan, and France will cook dishes from home.","t":"我們學校下個月將舉辦國際美食節，來自越南、日本和法國的學生會烹煮家鄉菜。"},{"w":"nationwide","p":"adj.","d":"happening in every part of a country","c":"全國性的","s":"The government started a nationwide campaign to encourage people to use their own cups instead of plastic ones.","t":"政府發起一項全國性的活動，鼓勵民眾自備杯子取代塑膠杯。"},{"w":"needy","p":"adj.","d":"very poor; not having enough money, food, or clothes","c":"貧困的；需要幫助的","s":"Every winter, our church collects warm coats and blankets for needy families who cannot afford to heat their homes.","t":"每年冬天，我們教會都會為付不起暖氣費的貧困家庭募集保暖外套和毛毯。","h":1},{"w":"need","p":"n.","d":"something that you must have; a situation in which something is necessary","c":"需要；需求","s":"There is an urgent need for clean water in the villages hit by the flood, so the army is sending trucks today.","t":"受洪水侵襲的村莊迫切需要乾淨的水，所以軍方今天派出卡車運送。"},{"w":"the needy","p":"n.phr.","d":"poor people as a group","c":"窮人；貧困者","s":"The restaurant owner gives free meals to the needy every Sunday evening, and many volunteers come to help him cook and serve.","t":"這位餐廳老闆每週日晚上免費供餐給窮人，許多志工來幫他烹飪和上菜。"},{"w":"in need","p":"phr.","d":"not having enough money or help","c":"處於困境；需要幫助","s":"A friend in need is a friend indeed; the people who stay with you during hard times are the ones who truly care.","t":"處於困境時的朋友才是真正的朋友；在艱難時刻陪在你身邊的人才是真正關心你的人。"},{"w":"needless","p":"adj.","d":"not necessary","c":"不必要的","s":"Buying a new phone every year is a needless expense when your old one still works perfectly well.","t":"當舊手機還能正常使用時，每年買新手機是一筆不必要的開銷。"},{"w":"neglect","p":"v.","d":"to fail to take care of someone or something; to not give enough attention to","c":"忽視；疏忽","s":"If you neglect your plants for two weeks in summer, they will dry out and die, so ask a neighbor to water them while you travel.","t":"如果你在夏天忽略植物兩個星期，它們會乾枯而死，所以旅行時請鄰居幫忙澆水。","h":1},{"w":"neglect","p":"n.","d":"the failure to take care of someone or something","c":"疏忽；忽視","s":"The old temple suffered years of neglect, and its roof finally fell in during last summer's typhoon.","t":"這座古廟多年來遭到忽視，屋頂終於在去年夏天的颱風中塌了下來。"},{"w":"neglected","p":"adj.","d":"not receiving enough care or attention","c":"被忽視的；無人照料的","s":"The neglected garden behind the school was full of weeds until the gardening club decided to turn it into a vegetable patch.","t":"學校後面那座無人照料的花園長滿雜草，直到園藝社決定把它變成菜園。"},{"w":"negligent","p":"adj.","d":"not careful enough in doing your job or duty","c":"疏忽的；怠忽職守的","s":"The court found the driver negligent because he was looking at his phone when his car hit the cyclist.","t":"法院判定那名駕駛有過失，因為他的車撞上自行車騎士時，他正在看手機。"},{"w":"neglect to do","p":"v.phr.","d":"to forget or fail to do something","c":"忘記做；疏於做","s":"My brother neglected to lock the back door last night, and this morning we found that our two bicycles were gone.","t":"我哥哥昨晚忘了鎖後門，今天早上我們發現兩台腳踏車不見了。","a":"neglected to"},{"w":"negotiate","p":"v.","d":"to discuss something in order to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"The workers' union will negotiate with the company next week, hoping to get higher pay and two more days of holiday a year.","t":"工會下週將與公司談判，希望爭取更高的薪資和每年多兩天假期。","h":1},{"w":"negotiation","p":"n.","d":"a formal discussion to reach an agreement","c":"談判；協商","s":"After three days of negotiation, the two countries agreed to lower the taxes on each other's cars and fruit.","t":"經過三天的談判，兩國同意降低彼此汽車和水果的關稅。"},{"w":"negotiator","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in negotiations","c":"談判者；協商者","s":"The police sent a trained negotiator to talk to the man on the roof, and after two hours he agreed to come down safely.","t":"警方派了一位受過訓練的談判專家去和屋頂上的男子交談，兩小時後他同意安全下來。"},{"w":"negotiate a price","p":"v.phr.","d":"to discuss and agree on how much something will cost","c":"議價","s":"At the night market, you can often negotiate a price with the seller, especially if you buy more than one item.","t":"在夜市你常常可以和攤販議價，特別是當你買不只一件商品的時候。"},{"w":"nevertheless","p":"adv.","d":"in spite of that; however","c":"然而；儘管如此","s":"The weather report said it would rain all day; nevertheless, we decided to go to the beach, and the sun came out at noon.","t":"氣象報告說會下一整天的雨；儘管如此，我們還是決定去海邊，結果中午太陽出來了。","h":1},{"w":"nonetheless","p":"adv.","d":"in spite of that; nevertheless","c":"儘管如此；但是","s":"The movie is almost three hours long; nonetheless, nobody in the theater looked bored, and some people even cried at the end.","t":"這部電影將近三小時；儘管如此，戲院裡沒有人看起來無聊，有些人甚至在結尾時哭了。"},{"w":"however","p":"adv.","d":"used to add a fact or idea that is surprising after what you have just said","c":"然而；不過","s":"I usually take the bus to school; this morning, however, my father drove me because I had to carry a big science project.","t":"我通常搭公車上學；然而今天早上爸爸開車送我，因為我得帶一個大型科學作品。"},{"w":"all the same","p":"phr.","d":"in spite of that; nevertheless","c":"儘管如此；還是","s":"I know you are busy with exams, but all the same, you should call your grandmother on her birthday this Sunday.","t":"我知道你忙著考試，但儘管如此，這個星期日奶奶生日你還是應該打電話給她。"},{"w":"nightmare","p":"n.","d":"a very frightening dream","c":"惡夢","s":"After watching the horror movie, my little sister had a nightmare and crawled into my parents' bed in the middle of the night.","t":"看完那部恐怖片後，我妹妹做了惡夢，半夜爬到爸媽的床上。","h":1},{"w":"nightmare","p":"n.","d":"a very unpleasant or difficult experience","c":"惡夢般的經歷；噩夢","s":"Moving house in the middle of a typhoon was a complete nightmare; the boxes got wet, and the truck arrived four hours late.","t":"在颱風中搬家簡直是一場噩夢；箱子都濕了，貨車也晚了四個小時才到。"},{"w":"have a nightmare","p":"v.phr.","d":"to experience a frightening dream","c":"做惡夢","s":"I had a nightmare about failing all my exams last night, so I got up early this morning and reviewed my notes again.","t":"我昨晚做了惡夢，夢到所有考試都不及格，所以今天早上提早起床，又複習了一次筆記。","a":"had a nightmare"},{"w":"daydream","p":"n.","d":"pleasant thoughts that make you forget what you are doing","c":"白日夢","s":"Ben was lost in a daydream about winning the lottery when the teacher suddenly called his name and asked for the answer.","t":"班正沉浸在中樂透的白日夢裡，老師突然叫他的名字，問他答案。"},{"w":"noble","p":"adj.","d":"having or showing high moral qualities, such as honesty and courage","c":"高尚的；崇高的","s":"Giving up his seat on the lifeboat to a mother and her baby was a truly noble act that people still talk about today.","t":"把救生艇上的座位讓給一位母親和她的嬰兒，是真正高尚的行為，人們至今仍在談論。","h":1},{"w":"noble","p":"n.","d":"a person of the highest social class, such as a duke or a count","c":"貴族","s":"In the old days, only a noble could own land near the castle, while farmers had to pay him part of their harvest.","t":"在過去，只有貴族可以擁有城堡附近的土地，而農民必須把部分收成交給他。"},{"w":"nobility","p":"n.","d":"the people of the highest social class; the quality of being noble","c":"貴族階級；高貴","s":"The palace was once home to the French nobility, who held huge parties there while most people in the country were starving.","t":"這座宮殿曾是法國貴族的家，他們在那裡舉辦盛大的宴會，而全國大多數人卻在挨餓。"},{"w":"nobly","p":"adv.","d":"in a noble, brave, or generous way","c":"高尚地；高貴地","s":"The captain nobly stayed on the sinking ship until every passenger had been placed safely in a lifeboat.","t":"船長高尚地留在沉船上，直到每位乘客都安全地登上救生艇。"},{"w":"nonsense","p":"n.","d":"words or ideas that are silly or have no meaning","c":"胡說；廢話","s":"My brother told me that eating carrots would let me see in the dark, but my science teacher said that was complete nonsense.","t":"我哥哥告訴我吃紅蘿蔔能讓我在黑暗中看見東西，但科學老師說那完全是胡說。","h":1},{"w":"talk nonsense","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say silly or untrue things","c":"胡說八道","s":"Do not listen to him when he has had too much to drink; he always starts to talk nonsense about ghosts and aliens.","t":"他喝太多的時候別聽他的；他總是開始胡說八道，講些鬼和外星人的事。"},{"w":"sense","p":"n.","d":"good understanding and judgment; a natural ability","c":"理智；感覺；感官","s":"Jenny has a good sense of direction, so she never gets lost even in a city she is visiting for the first time.","t":"珍妮的方向感很好，所以即使在第一次造訪的城市也從不迷路。"},{"w":"make sense","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be clear and easy to understand; to be a reasonable thing to do","c":"有道理；講得通","s":"It does not make sense to buy a car in Taipei when the MRT and buses can take you almost everywhere cheaply.","t":"在台北買車不合理，因為捷運和公車幾乎能便宜地帶你到任何地方。"},{"w":"sensible","p":"adj.","d":"showing good judgment; practical","c":"明智的；理智的","s":"Bringing a raincoat was a sensible decision, because the sky turned dark and it poured for an hour during our hike.","t":"帶雨衣是個明智的決定，因為健行時天空變暗，下了一個小時的大雨。"},{"w":"nowadays","p":"adv.","d":"at the present time, compared with the past","c":"現今；如今","s":"Nowadays, most teenagers read the news on their phones, while thirty years ago families waited for the morning newspaper.","t":"如今大多數青少年用手機看新聞，而三十年前家家戶戶都在等早報。","a":"Nowadays","h":1},{"w":"these days","p":"phr.","d":"at the present time; nowadays","c":"最近；現在","s":"It is hard to find a public phone these days, since almost everyone carries a mobile phone in their pocket.","t":"現在很難找到公共電話，因為幾乎每個人口袋裡都有手機。"},{"w":"in the old days","p":"phr.","d":"a long time ago, in the past","c":"從前；以前","s":"In the old days, people in this village washed their clothes in the river, but now every house has a washing machine.","t":"從前這個村子裡的人在河邊洗衣服，但現在每戶人家都有洗衣機。","a":"In the old days"},{"w":"up to date","p":"adj.phr.","d":"modern; including the latest information","c":"最新的；現代的","s":"Make sure your phone's software is up to date before the trip, because the old version of the map app may not work abroad.","t":"出發前確認你手機的軟體是最新的，因為舊版的地圖應用程式在國外可能無法使用。"},{"w":"nuclear","p":"adj.","d":"relating to the energy produced when atoms are split or joined","c":"核能的；核子的","s":"Some people support nuclear power because it produces little carbon dioxide, while others worry about the dangerous waste it leaves behind.","t":"有些人支持核能，因為它排放的二氧化碳很少，而另一些人則擔心它留下的危險廢料。","h":1},{"w":"nuclear power plant","p":"n.phr.","d":"a factory that makes electricity from nuclear energy","c":"核能發電廠","s":"The old nuclear power plant on the north coast will be closed next year, and the government plans to build more wind farms instead.","t":"北海岸那座舊的核能發電廠明年將關閉，政府計畫改建更多風力發電場。"},{"w":"nuclear weapon","p":"n.phr.","d":"a bomb that uses nuclear energy to cause huge destruction","c":"核子武器","s":"Many countries have signed an agreement promising never to build a nuclear weapon, because one bomb can destroy an entire city.","t":"許多國家簽署了協議，承諾永不製造核子武器，因為一顆炸彈就能摧毀整座城市。"},{"w":"nuclear family","p":"n.phr.","d":"a family consisting of parents and their children only","c":"核心家庭；小家庭","s":"My grandparents lived with three generations under one roof, but today most of my friends grow up in a nuclear family.","t":"我的祖父母是三代同堂，但現在我大多數朋友都在小家庭中長大。"},{"w":"numerous","p":"adj.","d":"many; a large number of","c":"許多的；為數眾多的","s":"The singer has received numerous awards over the past ten years, but she says the love of her fans matters more than any prize.","t":"這位歌手過去十年獲得了許多獎項，但她說粉絲的愛比任何獎都重要。","h":1},{"w":"number","p":"n.","d":"a word or symbol that shows an amount; a quantity","c":"數字；數量","s":"The number of foreign tourists visiting Taiwan has grown every year since the airport opened its new terminal.","t":"自從機場新航廈啟用以來，來台的外國遊客人數每年都在成長。"},{"w":"a number of","p":"phr.","d":"several; some","c":"一些；若干","s":"A number of students complained that the classroom was too hot, so the school finally installed air conditioners last month.","t":"一些學生抱怨教室太熱，所以學校上個月終於裝了冷氣。","a":"A number of"},{"w":"innumerable","p":"adj.","d":"too many to be counted","c":"無數的","s":"On a clear night in the mountains, far from the city lights, you can see innumerable stars shining across the sky.","t":"在山上晴朗的夜晚，遠離城市燈光，你可以看到無數的星星在天空中閃耀。"},{"w":"outnumber","p":"v.","d":"to be larger in number than another group","c":"數量上超過","s":"At the concert, the girls in the audience outnumbered the boys by about five to one, and they sang along with every song.","t":"演唱會上，觀眾中的女生人數大約是男生的五倍，而且每首歌她們都跟著唱。","a":"outnumbered"},{"w":"nursery","p":"n.","d":"a place where young children are cared for while their parents are at work","c":"托兒所；幼兒園","s":"My aunt drops her two-year-old son at the nursery at eight every morning and picks him up after work at six.","t":"我阿姨每天早上八點把兩歲的兒子送到托兒所，下班後六點再去接他。","h":1},{"w":"nursery","p":"n.","d":"a place where young plants and trees are grown and sold","c":"苗圃","s":"We bought three small lemon trees at a plant nursery outside the city and planted them along the fence in our backyard.","t":"我們在城外的植物苗圃買了三棵小檸檬樹，種在後院的圍籬旁。"},{"w":"nurse","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to care for sick or injured people","c":"護士；護理師","s":"The nurse checked my temperature and gave me a cup of warm water while I waited for the doctor to arrive.","t":"護士幫我量了體溫，給我一杯溫水，讓我等醫生來。"},{"w":"nurse","p":"v.","d":"to take care of someone who is ill or injured","c":"照顧；護理","s":"Grandma nursed my little brother back to health with hot soup and plenty of sleep when he caught the flu last winter.","t":"去年冬天我弟弟得流感時，奶奶用熱湯和充足的睡眠照顧他恢復健康。","a":"nursed"},{"w":"nursery rhyme","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short traditional song or poem for young children","c":"童謠；兒歌","s":"My mother used to sing the same nursery rhyme to me every night, and now I sing it to my own daughter before she sleeps.","t":"我媽媽以前每晚都唱同一首童謠給我聽，現在我在女兒睡前唱給她聽。"}]},{"unit":28,"theme":"nutritious – oval","cards":[{"w":"nutritious","p":"adj.","d":"full of the things your body needs to stay healthy","c":"有營養的","s":"Brown rice and fresh vegetables are more nutritious than instant noodles, so my mother cooks them for dinner almost every night.","t":"糙米和新鮮蔬菜比泡麵更有營養，所以我媽媽幾乎每天晚餐都煮這些。","h":1},{"w":"nutrition","p":"n.","d":"the food you eat and the way it keeps your body healthy","c":"營養","s":"Good nutrition is important for teenagers because their bodies are still growing and need enough protein and vitamins every day.","t":"良好的營養對青少年很重要，因為他們的身體仍在成長，每天都需要足夠的蛋白質和維生素。"},{"w":"nutrient","p":"n.","d":"a substance in food that living things need to grow","c":"養分；營養素","s":"Plants take in water and nutrients from the soil through their roots, which is why farmers add fertilizer to their fields.","t":"植物透過根部從土壤中吸收水分和養分，這就是為什麼農夫要在田裡施肥。","a":"nutrients"},{"w":"nutritional","p":"adj.","d":"connected with nutrition","c":"營養的；營養方面的","s":"Read the nutritional information on the package before you buy snacks, because some of them contain a lot of sugar and salt.","t":"買零食前先看包裝上的營養標示，因為有些零食含有大量的糖和鹽。"},{"w":"obedience","p":"n.","d":"doing what you are told to do","c":"服從；順從","s":"Soldiers are trained to show complete obedience to their officers, so they follow every order quickly without asking any questions.","t":"士兵被訓練要對長官完全服從，所以他們會迅速執行每個命令而不多問。","h":1},{"w":"obedient","p":"adj.","d":"doing what you are told to do","c":"聽話的；順從的","s":"Our new puppy is very obedient; it sits down, stays, and comes back as soon as my sister calls its name.","t":"我們的新小狗非常聽話；只要我妹妹叫牠的名字，牠就會坐下、待著不動，然後跑回來。","h":1},{"w":"obediently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you do what you are told","c":"順從地","s":"The children lined up obediently behind their teacher and walked quietly to the school bus without pushing anyone.","t":"孩子們順從地在老師身後排好隊，安靜地走向校車，沒有推擠任何人。"},{"w":"obey","p":"v.","d":"to do what a person, law, or rule tells you to do","c":"服從；遵守","s":"Students must obey the school rules, and anyone who breaks them more than twice will have to stay after class.","t":"學生必須遵守校規，任何違反超過兩次的人都得在放學後留下來。"},{"w":"disobey","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to do what you are told to do","c":"違抗；不服從","s":"If you disobey your coach and skip practice again, you will not be allowed to play in the final game next week.","t":"如果你再違抗教練、不來練習，下週的決賽你就不能上場。"},{"w":"disobedient","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to do what you are told","c":"不聽話的","s":"The disobedient child refused to turn off the TV when his parents told him to, so he lost his screen time for a week.","t":"那個不聽話的孩子在父母叫他關電視時拒絕照做，所以他一個星期不能看螢幕。"},{"w":"objection","p":"n.","d":"a reason you give for not agreeing with something","c":"反對；異議","s":"Does anyone have an objection to moving the meeting to Friday afternoon, when more members of the team will be free?","t":"有人對把會議改到星期五下午有異議嗎？那時候會有更多團隊成員有空。","h":1},{"w":"objective","p":"n.","d":"something you are trying to achieve","c":"目標；目的","s":"The main objective of this program is to help students read faster, so we practice with a short article every morning.","t":"這個課程的主要目標是幫助學生讀得更快，所以我們每天早上都用一篇短文練習。","h":1},{"w":"objective","p":"adj.","d":"based on facts, not on personal feelings","c":"客觀的","s":"A good judge must stay objective and decide every case by the facts, not by his personal feelings about the people involved.","t":"好的法官必須保持客觀，根據事實而不是對當事人的個人感受來判決每個案件。"},{"w":"objectively","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is based on facts, not feelings","c":"客觀地","s":"Try to look at your own essay objectively, as if a stranger had written it, and you will find mistakes you missed before.","t":"試著客觀地看你自己的作文，就像它是陌生人寫的一樣，你會發現以前沒注意到的錯誤。"},{"w":"object","p":"v.","d":"to say that you do not agree with something","c":"反對","s":"Many residents object to the plan for a new factory because they are worried about air pollution and heavy traffic.","t":"許多居民反對興建新工廠的計畫，因為他們擔心空氣污染和交通壅塞。"},{"w":"raise an objection","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say officially that you do not agree","c":"提出異議","s":"Nobody raised an objection when the manager suggested starting work an hour earlier in summer, so the new schedule began the next Monday.","t":"經理建議夏天提早一小時上班時，沒有人提出異議，所以新的時間表從下週一開始實施。","a":"raised an objection"},{"w":"subjective","p":"adj.","d":"based on your own feelings and ideas, not on facts","c":"主觀的","s":"Which movie is the best is a subjective question, because different people enjoy very different kinds of stories and actors.","t":"哪部電影最好是個主觀的問題，因為不同的人喜歡的故事類型和演員都大不相同。"},{"w":"observation","p":"n.","d":"the act of watching something carefully","c":"觀察","s":"After three days of careful observation, the doctor decided that the patient was well enough to go home and rest.","t":"經過三天仔細的觀察，醫生判斷病人已經好到可以回家休養了。","h":1},{"w":"observe","p":"v.","d":"to watch something carefully; to follow a rule or custom","c":"觀察；遵守","s":"Scientists observe the behavior of birds in the park every morning to find out how city noise affects them.","t":"科學家每天早上觀察公園裡鳥類的行為，想找出城市噪音對牠們有什麼影響。"},{"w":"observer","p":"n.","d":"a person who watches something","c":"觀察者；旁觀者","s":"As an observer at the chess match, you may watch the players closely, but you must not talk or give them any hints.","t":"身為西洋棋比賽的觀察者，你可以仔細看選手下棋，但不能說話或給他們任何提示。"},{"w":"under observation","p":"phr.","d":"being watched carefully, especially in a hospital","c":"接受觀察中","s":"The baby was kept under observation in the hospital overnight because she had a high fever that did not go down.","t":"那個嬰兒因為高燒不退，被留在醫院觀察了一整晚。"},{"w":"obstacle","p":"n.","d":"something that makes it difficult to do or reach something","c":"障礙；阻礙","s":"The biggest obstacle to learning English well is the fear of making mistakes, so do not be afraid to speak up in class.","t":"學好英文最大的障礙是害怕犯錯，所以在課堂上不要怕開口。","h":1},{"w":"overcome obstacles","p":"v.phr.","d":"to deal with difficulties and succeed","c":"克服障礙","s":"Successful people learn to overcome obstacles instead of giving up, and they often say that each failure taught them something useful.","t":"成功的人學會克服障礙而不是放棄，他們常說每次失敗都教了他們一些有用的東西。"},{"w":"obstacle course","p":"n.phr.","d":"a race track with walls, ropes, and other things to climb over","c":"障礙賽跑道","s":"At the sports camp, the kids ran through an obstacle course with ropes, tires, and walls, and everyone finished covered in mud.","t":"在運動營裡，孩子們跑過一條有繩索、輪胎和牆的障礙賽跑道，每個人最後都沾滿了泥巴。"},{"w":"obtain","p":"v.","d":"to get something, especially by asking or working for it","c":"獲得；取得","s":"You need to obtain a permit from the city office before you can sell food at the night market on weekends.","t":"你必須先向市政府取得許可證，才能在週末的夜市賣食物。","h":1},{"w":"obtainable","p":"adj.","d":"possible to get","c":"可獲得的；可取得的","s":"Fresh mangoes are easily obtainable in Taiwan during summer, but in winter you can only find them at a very high price.","t":"夏天在台灣很容易買得到新鮮芒果，但冬天只能以很高的價格找到。"},{"w":"obtain permission","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get the right to do something from someone in charge","c":"取得許可","s":"Students who want to leave school early must obtain permission from their homeroom teacher and sign out at the front office.","t":"想提早離校的學生必須向導師取得許可，並在前門辦公室簽退。"},{"w":"occasional","p":"adj.","d":"happening sometimes but not often","c":"偶爾的","s":"Apart from an occasional cold in winter, my grandfather has been very healthy, and he still walks five kilometers every morning.","t":"除了冬天偶爾感冒之外，我爺爺一直很健康，他每天早上還是走五公里。","h":1},{"w":"occasionally","p":"adv.","d":"sometimes but not often","c":"偶爾","s":"We occasionally eat out at a nice restaurant on weekends, but most of the time my parents prefer to cook at home.","t":"我們偶爾會在週末去好餐廳吃飯，但大多數時候我父母比較喜歡在家煮。"},{"w":"occasion","p":"n.","d":"a special time or event","c":"場合；時刻","s":"A wedding is a special occasion, so most guests wear their best clothes and bring a gift for the new couple.","t":"婚禮是個特別的場合，所以大多數賓客都會穿上最好的衣服，並帶禮物給新人。"},{"w":"on occasion","p":"phr.","d":"sometimes but not often","c":"偶爾；有時","s":"My uncle lives in Kaohsiung, but on occasion he drives up to Taipei to visit us and take us out for dinner.","t":"我叔叔住在高雄，但偶爾他會開車上台北來看我們，帶我們出去吃晚餐。"},{"w":"occupation","p":"n.","d":"a person's job","c":"職業","s":"Please write your name, address, and occupation on the form, and then hand it to the nurse at the front desk.","t":"請在表格上寫下你的姓名、地址和職業，然後交給櫃檯的護理師。","h":1},{"w":"occupy","p":"v.","d":"to fill a space or time; to live or work in a place","c":"佔據；佔用","s":"The large sofa and the piano occupy most of the living room, so there is hardly any space left for a dining table.","t":"大沙發和鋼琴佔據了客廳大部分的空間，所以幾乎沒有地方放餐桌。","h":1},{"w":"be occupied with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be busy doing something","c":"忙於","s":"My father is occupied with his new project these days, so he often comes home after we have already gone to bed.","t":"我爸爸這陣子忙於他的新專案，所以他常常在我們已經睡了之後才回家。","a":"is occupied with"},{"w":"occupied","p":"adj.","d":"being used; having someone inside","c":"使用中的；有人的","s":"All the seats on the train were occupied, so the old man had to stand for almost an hour until Taichung.","t":"火車上所有的座位都有人坐了，所以那位老先生必須站將近一個小時直到台中。"},{"w":"occupant","p":"n.","d":"a person who lives or works in a room, house, or car","c":"居住者；佔用者","s":"The occupant of the apartment next door moved out last week, and now the landlord is looking for someone new.","t":"隔壁公寓的住戶上週搬走了，現在房東正在找新的房客。"},{"w":"offend","p":"v.","d":"to make someone angry or upset by what you say or do","c":"冒犯；得罪","s":"I did not mean to offend you with my joke, and I am truly sorry if it made you feel uncomfortable.","t":"我無意用我的笑話冒犯你，如果它讓你不舒服，我真的很抱歉。","h":1},{"w":"offense","p":"n.","d":"a crime; the act of making someone upset","c":"罪行；冒犯","s":"Driving after drinking is a serious offense, and anyone caught doing it can lose his license for at least one year.","t":"酒後開車是嚴重的罪行，任何被抓到的人至少會被吊銷駕照一年。","h":1},{"w":"offensive","p":"adj.","d":"rude in a way that makes people upset or angry","c":"無禮的；冒犯的","s":"Some people found the advertisement offensive because it made fun of older people, so the company removed it the next day.","t":"有些人覺得那則廣告很冒犯人，因為它取笑老年人，所以公司第二天就把它撤掉了。","h":1},{"w":"take offense","p":"phr.","d":"to feel upset or angry because of what someone said or did","c":"生氣；見怪","s":"Please do not take offense at what she said; she was tired and did not really mean to criticize your work.","t":"請不要因為她說的話而生氣；她只是累了，並不是真的想批評你的工作。"},{"w":"no offense","p":"phr.","d":"used before saying something that might upset someone","c":"無意冒犯","s":"No offense, but I think your plan needs more time and money than our small club can afford this year.","t":"無意冒犯，但我認為你的計畫需要的時間和錢，比我們這個小社團今年能負擔的還多。","a":"No offense"},{"w":"offender","p":"n.","d":"a person who has broken the law","c":"違法者；罪犯","s":"The judge gave the young offender a second chance because it was his first time breaking the law and he was truly sorry.","t":"法官給了那個年輕的違法者第二次機會，因為這是他第一次犯法，而且他真心悔過。"},{"w":"opera","p":"n.","d":"a play in which most of the words are sung to music","c":"歌劇","s":"My grandmother loves Taiwanese opera, and she still goes to the temple square to watch it whenever a group performs there.","t":"我奶奶很愛台灣歌仔戲，只要有劇團在廟口演出，她還是會去看。","h":1},{"w":"opera house","p":"n.phr.","d":"a theater where operas are performed","c":"歌劇院","s":"The Sydney Opera House is one of the most famous buildings in the world, and millions of tourists take photos of it every year.","t":"雪梨歌劇院是世界上最有名的建築之一，每年有數百萬遊客為它拍照。","a":"Opera House"},{"w":"soap opera","p":"n.phr.","d":"a TV drama about the daily lives of a group of people, shown many times a week","c":"肥皂劇；連續劇","s":"My aunt never misses her favorite soap opera at eight o'clock, even though the story has been going on for five years.","t":"我阿姨從不錯過她最愛的八點檔連續劇，即使這個故事已經演了五年。"},{"w":"oppose","p":"v.","d":"to disagree with something and try to stop it","c":"反對","s":"Many parents oppose the plan to start school an hour earlier because their children already do not get enough sleep.","t":"許多家長反對提早一小時上學的計畫，因為他們的孩子已經睡眠不足了。","h":1},{"w":"be opposed to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to disagree strongly with something","c":"反對","s":"My grandfather is opposed to using credit cards because he believes people should only spend the money they actually have.","t":"我爺爺反對使用信用卡，因為他認為人們只應該花自己真正擁有的錢。","a":"is opposed to"},{"w":"opposite","p":"adj.","d":"completely different; on the other side","c":"相反的；對面的","s":"The post office is on the opposite side of the street from the bank, right next to the small bakery.","t":"郵局在銀行對面那一側的街上，就在小麵包店旁邊。"},{"w":"opposition","p":"n.","d":"strong disagreement with a plan or idea","c":"反對；反對勢力","s":"The new tax faced strong opposition from shop owners, who said it would force many small stores to close.","t":"新稅制遭到店家強烈反對，他們說這會迫使許多小商店倒閉。"},{"w":"opponent","p":"n.","d":"a person you play or fight against","c":"對手","s":"Our team lost the final match, but we shook hands with our opponents and congratulated them on their great performance.","t":"我們隊輸了決賽，但我們和對手握手，並祝賀他們精彩的表現。","a":"opponents"},{"w":"option","p":"n.","d":"one of the things you can choose","c":"選擇；選項","s":"If the tickets for Saturday are sold out, another option is to watch the concert online for a much lower price.","t":"如果星期六的票賣完了，另一個選擇是用低很多的價格在線上看演唱會。","h":1},{"w":"optional","p":"adj.","d":"something you can choose to do or not do","c":"可選擇的；非必修的","s":"The school trip is optional, so students who do not want to go can stay at school and study in the library.","t":"校外教學是自由參加的，所以不想去的學生可以留在學校的圖書館讀書。"},{"w":"have no option but to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have to do something because there is no other choice","c":"別無選擇只能","s":"When the last bus left without us, we had no option but to walk home in the rain for nearly an hour.","t":"最後一班公車沒載到我們就開走了，我們別無選擇只能在雨中走將近一小時回家。","a":"had no option but to"},{"w":"opt","p":"v.","d":"to choose one thing instead of another","c":"選擇","s":"More and more young people opt to rent an apartment in the city rather than buy a house far from their jobs.","t":"越來越多年輕人選擇在市區租公寓，而不是買離工作地點很遠的房子。"},{"w":"orbit","p":"n.","d":"the curved path of a planet or satellite around a star or planet","c":"軌道","s":"The satellite was put into orbit around the Earth last year, and it sends back weather pictures every thirty minutes.","t":"那顆衛星去年被送入環繞地球的軌道，每三十分鐘就會傳回氣象照片。","h":1},{"w":"orbit","p":"v.","d":"to move around a planet or star in a curved path","c":"繞軌道運行","s":"The Moon takes about twenty-seven days to orbit the Earth, which is why we see a full moon roughly once a month.","t":"月球大約需要二十七天繞行地球一圈，這就是為什麼我們大約每個月會看到一次滿月。"},{"w":"in orbit","p":"phr.","d":"moving around a planet in space","c":"在軌道上","s":"There are thousands of pieces of old rockets and broken satellites still in orbit around our planet, and they can damage new spacecraft.","t":"還有成千上萬塊舊火箭和壞掉的衛星碎片仍在軌道上環繞著我們的星球，它們可能會損壞新的太空船。"},{"w":"orchestra","p":"n.","d":"a large group of musicians who play classical music together","c":"管弦樂團","s":"My cousin plays the violin in the school orchestra, and they will give a free concert in the city hall next month.","t":"我表妹在學校管弦樂團拉小提琴，他們下個月將在市政廳舉行免費音樂會。","h":1},{"w":"orchestral","p":"adj.","d":"written for or played by an orchestra","c":"管弦樂的","s":"The movie's orchestral music was recorded by more than eighty musicians, and it makes every battle scene feel much more exciting.","t":"這部電影的管弦樂配樂由八十多位音樂家錄製，讓每個戰鬥場面都更加刺激。"},{"w":"conductor","p":"n.","d":"a person who stands in front of an orchestra and directs the music","c":"指揮","s":"The conductor raised his hands, the hall became silent, and then the whole orchestra began to play the first note together.","t":"指揮舉起雙手，大廳安靜下來，接著整個管弦樂團一起奏出第一個音。"},{"w":"musician","p":"n.","d":"a person who plays a musical instrument or writes music","c":"音樂家","s":"Every musician in the band practices at least three hours a day, which explains why their performances always sound so perfect.","t":"樂團裡的每位音樂家每天至少練習三小時，這說明了為什麼他們的演出總是如此完美。"},{"w":"orientation","p":"n.","d":"a meeting or course that helps new people get used to a place","c":"新生訓練；適應指導","s":"New students must attend the orientation on the first day, where teachers will explain the school rules and show them around the campus.","t":"新生第一天必須參加新生訓練，老師會在那裡說明校規並帶他們參觀校園。","h":1},{"w":"orient","p":"v.","d":"to help someone get used to a new place or situation","c":"使適應；使熟悉","s":"It took the new workers a few weeks to orient themselves to the busy schedule and the company's way of doing things.","t":"新員工花了幾個星期才讓自己適應忙碌的工作時程和公司的做事方式。"},{"w":"oriental","p":"adj.","d":"from or connected with East Asia","c":"東方的","s":"The museum has a special room of oriental art, with old paintings and pottery from China, Japan, and Korea.","t":"博物館有一間東方藝術特展室，陳列來自中國、日本和韓國的古老繪畫和陶器。"},{"w":"orphan","p":"n.","d":"a child whose parents are dead","c":"孤兒","s":"After the earthquake, many children became orphans, and families across the country offered to give them a new home.","t":"地震後，許多孩子成了孤兒，全國各地的家庭都表示願意給他們一個新家。","a":"orphans","h":1},{"w":"orphan","p":"v.","d":"to make a child an orphan","c":"使成為孤兒","s":"The war orphaned thousands of children, who had to grow up without parents to take care of them.","t":"戰爭使成千上萬的孩子成了孤兒，他們必須在沒有父母照顧的情況下長大。","a":"orphaned"},{"w":"orphanage","p":"n.","d":"a home for children whose parents are dead","c":"孤兒院","s":"Every Christmas, our class collects toys and books and takes them to the orphanage in the next town.","t":"每年聖誕節，我們班都會收集玩具和書，送到隔壁鎮上的孤兒院。"},{"w":"otherwise","p":"adv.","d":"if not; or else","c":"否則","s":"Set your alarm clock for six tomorrow; otherwise, you will miss the early train and be late for the interview.","t":"明天把鬧鐘設在六點；否則你會錯過早班火車，面試遲到。","h":1},{"w":"otherwise","p":"adv.","d":"apart from that; in other ways","c":"除此之外；在其他方面","s":"The soup was a little too salty, but otherwise the dinner at the new restaurant was excellent and the service was friendly.","t":"湯有點太鹹，但除此之外新餐廳的晚餐很棒，服務也很親切。"},{"w":"or otherwise","p":"phr.","d":"or not; or the opposite","c":"或其他；或相反","s":"All suggestions, useful or otherwise, should be written on the paper and put in the box before Friday.","t":"所有的建議，不論有用與否，都應該寫在紙上，並在星期五前投進箱子裡。"},{"w":"outcome","p":"n.","d":"the result of an action or event","c":"結果","s":"Nobody could predict the outcome of the election, because the two candidates had almost the same number of supporters.","t":"沒有人能預測選舉的結果，因為兩位候選人的支持者人數幾乎一樣多。","h":1},{"w":"turn out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to happen in a particular way in the end","c":"結果是；最後變成","s":"The weather turned out to be perfect for the picnic, even though the forecast had said it might rain all afternoon.","t":"天氣結果非常適合野餐，儘管氣象預報說整個下午可能會下雨。","a":"turned out"},{"w":"come out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be produced or published; to become known","c":"上市；出版；結果","s":"The new phone will come out in September, and many fans are already saving money to buy it on the first day.","t":"新手機將在九月上市，許多粉絲已經在存錢準備第一天就買。"},{"w":"outstanding","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good; much better than others","c":"傑出的；優秀的","s":"She won the prize for outstanding service to the community after she spent ten years teaching free English classes to children.","t":"她在為孩子們免費教了十年英文後，獲得了社區傑出服務獎。","h":1},{"w":"outstanding","p":"adj.","d":"not yet paid or finished","c":"未付的；未解決的","s":"You still have an outstanding payment of two thousand dollars, so please pay it before the end of this month.","t":"你還有一筆兩千元未付的款項，請在這個月底前付清。"},{"w":"stand out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be easy to see or notice because of being different","c":"突出；顯眼","s":"Her red jacket made her stand out in the crowd, so we found her easily at the busy train station.","t":"她的紅夾克讓她在人群中很顯眼，所以我們在繁忙的火車站很容易就找到了她。"},{"w":"oval","p":"adj.","d":"shaped like an egg","c":"橢圓形的","s":"The dining table in my grandmother's house is oval, so eight people can sit around it comfortably during family dinners.","t":"我奶奶家的餐桌是橢圓形的，所以家庭聚餐時八個人可以舒服地圍坐在一起。","h":1},{"w":"oval","p":"n.","d":"a shape like an egg","c":"橢圓形","s":"Draw an oval on the paper first, and then add two circles for eyes to turn it into a simple cartoon face.","t":"先在紙上畫一個橢圓形，然後加上兩個圓圈當眼睛，把它變成一張簡單的卡通臉。"},{"w":"the Oval Office","p":"n.phr.","d":"the office of the President of the United States","c":"美國總統辦公室（橢圓形辦公室）","s":"The President of the United States works in the Oval Office, which gets its name from its unusual shape.","t":"美國總統在橢圓形辦公室工作，它的名字來自它不尋常的形狀。"}]},{"unit":29,"theme":"overcoat – permanent","cards":[{"w":"overcoat","p":"n.","d":"a long, warm coat worn over other clothes in cold weather","c":"大衣","s":"It was snowing hard in Seoul, so my father put on his thick wool overcoat before we went out to find a restaurant.","t":"首爾下著大雪，所以我爸爸在我們出門找餐廳之前穿上了他厚厚的羊毛大衣。","h":1},{"w":"coat","p":"n.","d":"a piece of clothing with sleeves that you wear over other clothes","c":"外套","s":"Take a coat with you tonight, because the weather report says the temperature will drop to ten degrees after sunset.","t":"今晚帶件外套出門，因為氣象報告說日落後氣溫會降到十度。"},{"w":"raincoat","p":"n.","d":"a coat that keeps you dry in the rain","c":"雨衣","s":"The students who rode scooters to school all wore a yellow raincoat, since it had been raining heavily since early morning.","t":"騎機車上學的學生都穿著黃色雨衣，因為從清晨開始就一直下著大雨。"},{"w":"a coat of paint","p":"n.phr.","d":"a thin layer of paint","c":"一層漆","s":"The old wooden door looked brand new after my uncle gave it a coat of paint on Saturday afternoon.","t":"我叔叔星期六下午給那扇舊木門上了一層漆之後，它看起來就像全新的一樣。"},{"w":"overcome, overcame, overcome","p":"v.","d":"to succeed in dealing with a problem or feeling","c":"克服","s":"With the support of her family, she was able to overcome her fear of water and finally learned to swim at thirty.","t":"在家人的支持下，她克服了對水的恐懼，終於在三十歲時學會了游泳。","a":"overcome","h":1},{"w":"be overcome by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be made weak or unable to act by smoke, gas, or a strong feeling","c":"被…壓倒；被…嗆倒","s":"The firefighters were overcome by smoke inside the burning building, so they had to come out for fresh air.","t":"消防員在燃燒的建築物裡被濃煙嗆倒，所以他們不得不出來呼吸新鮮空氣。","a":"overcome by"},{"w":"overcome difficulties","p":"v.phr.","d":"to deal with problems successfully","c":"克服困難","s":"Learning to overcome difficulties on your own is an important part of growing up, and your parents will not always be there to help.","t":"學會自己克服困難是成長的重要一部分，你的父母不會永遠在身邊幫忙。"},{"w":"overlook","p":"v.","d":"to fail to notice something","c":"忽略；沒注意到","s":"The manager was in a hurry and seemed to overlook several mistakes in the report, which caused problems later that week.","t":"經理很匆忙，似乎忽略了報告裡的幾個錯誤，這在那週稍後造成了問題。","h":1},{"w":"overlook","p":"v.","d":"to have a view of something from above","c":"俯瞰","s":"Our hotel room overlooked the harbor, so every morning we could watch the fishing boats sail out to sea.","t":"我們的旅館房間俯瞰港口，所以每天早上我們都能看漁船出海。","a":"overlooked"},{"w":"look over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to check something quickly","c":"檢查；瀏覽","s":"Could you look over my essay before I hand it in and tell me if any of the sentences sound strange?","t":"你能在我交作文之前幫我看一下，告訴我有沒有句子聽起來怪怪的嗎？"},{"w":"overnight","p":"adv.","d":"for or during the whole night; very suddenly","c":"整夜；一夜之間","s":"We decided to stay overnight at my aunt's house in Tainan because the last train to Taipei had already left.","t":"我們決定在台南阿姨家過夜，因為往台北的末班火車已經開走了。","h":1},{"w":"overnight","p":"adj.","d":"happening or lasting through the night","c":"夜間的；一夜的","s":"Please take the overnight bus to Kenting; it leaves at eleven and arrives early in the morning, so you save a hotel night.","t":"請搭夜間巴士去墾丁；它十一點出發，清晨抵達，這樣你可以省下一晚旅館費。"},{"w":"overnight success","p":"n.phr.","d":"someone or something that becomes famous very suddenly","c":"一夜成名","s":"The singer looked like an overnight success, but in fact she had sung in small cafes for ten years before anyone noticed her.","t":"這位歌手看起來像是一夜成名，但其實在有人注意到她之前，她已經在小咖啡館唱了十年。"},{"w":"overthrow, overthrew, overthrown","p":"v.","d":"to remove a leader or government from power by force","c":"推翻","s":"In 1911, the people rose up to overthrow the Qing government, and the Republic of China was born the next year.","t":"一九一一年，人民起義推翻清朝政府，中華民國在隔年誕生。","a":"overthrow","h":1},{"w":"throw, threw, thrown","p":"v.","d":"to send something through the air with your hand","c":"丟；扔","s":"Please do not throw your trash on the ground; there is a garbage can right beside the entrance of the park.","t":"請不要把垃圾丟在地上；公園入口旁邊就有一個垃圾桶。","a":"throw"},{"w":"throw away","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get rid of something you do not want","c":"丟掉；扔掉","s":"Before you throw away those old magazines, check whether the school library would like to have them for the reading corner.","t":"在你丟掉那些舊雜誌之前，先問問學校圖書館的閱讀角要不要。"},{"w":"oxygen","p":"n.","d":"the gas in the air that people and animals need to breathe","c":"氧氣","s":"Climbers who go to the top of Mount Everest usually carry bottles of oxygen because the air there is extremely thin.","t":"攀登聖母峰頂的登山者通常會帶著氧氣瓶，因為那裡的空氣極為稀薄。","h":1},{"w":"oxygen mask","p":"n.phr.","d":"a cover for the face that gives you oxygen to breathe","c":"氧氣罩","s":"If the air pressure in the cabin drops, an oxygen mask will fall from above your seat, and you should put it on at once.","t":"如果機艙內的氣壓下降，氧氣罩會從你座位上方掉下來，你應該立刻戴上。"},{"w":"hydrogen","p":"n.","d":"the lightest gas, which burns easily","c":"氫","s":"Water is made of two kinds of gas, hydrogen and oxygen, which is why scientists write it as H2O.","t":"水是由兩種氣體組成的，氫和氧，這就是為什麼科學家把它寫成 H2O。"},{"w":"carbon dioxide","p":"n.phr.","d":"the gas that people breathe out and that plants take in","c":"二氧化碳","s":"Trees take in carbon dioxide and give out oxygen, so planting more of them helps to clean the air in our cities.","t":"樹木吸收二氧化碳並釋放氧氣，所以多種樹有助於淨化我們城市的空氣。"},{"w":"pace","p":"n.","d":"the speed at which someone walks, runs, or does something","c":"步伐；速度","s":"The old man walked at a slow pace, so it took him almost twenty minutes to reach the bus stop at the corner.","t":"那位老先生走路的步伐很慢，所以他花了將近二十分鐘才走到轉角的公車站。","h":1},{"w":"pace","p":"v.","d":"to walk up and down because you are worried","c":"踱步","s":"The nervous father paced up and down the hospital hallway while he waited for news about his wife and the baby.","t":"那位緊張的父親在醫院走廊來回踱步，等待他妻子和寶寶的消息。","a":"paced"},{"w":"keep pace with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move or change as fast as someone or something else","c":"跟上","s":"Small shops find it hard to keep pace with big online stores, which can sell the same products at much lower prices.","t":"小商店很難跟上大型網路商店，因為後者能以低很多的價格賣同樣的產品。"},{"w":"at one's own pace","p":"phr.","d":"at the speed that suits you","c":"以自己的步調","s":"In this online course, students can learn at their own pace, watching each video again whenever they do not understand something.","t":"在這門線上課程裡，學生可以以自己的步調學習，只要有不懂的地方就可以再看一次影片。","a":"at their own pace"},{"w":"panel","p":"n.","d":"a flat board with controls or instruments on it","c":"面板；控制板","s":"The pilot checked every light on the control panel before the plane left the gate and rolled toward the runway.","t":"飛機離開登機門滑向跑道之前，機師檢查了控制面板上的每一個燈。","h":1},{"w":"panel","p":"n.","d":"a small group of people chosen to judge or discuss something","c":"專家小組；評審團","s":"A panel of three judges will listen to all the speeches and choose the winner of the English contest.","t":"由三位評審組成的評審團將聽完所有演講，選出英語比賽的優勝者。"},{"w":"solar panel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a flat board that turns sunlight into electricity","c":"太陽能板","s":"My uncle put a solar panel on the roof of his house, and now his electricity bill is almost half of what it used to be.","t":"我叔叔在他家屋頂裝了太陽能板，現在他的電費幾乎只有以前的一半。"},{"w":"panel discussion","p":"n.phr.","d":"a talk in which a group of experts discuss a topic in front of an audience","c":"座談會","s":"After the movie, there was a panel discussion in which the director and two actors answered questions from the audience.","t":"電影結束後有一場座談會，導演和兩位演員在會中回答觀眾的提問。"},{"w":"parachute","p":"n.","d":"a large piece of cloth that lets a person fall slowly from a plane","c":"降落傘","s":"The pilot jumped from the burning plane, and his parachute opened just in time to carry him safely to the ground.","t":"機師從燃燒的飛機跳下，他的降落傘及時打開，把他安全地帶到地面。","h":1},{"w":"parachute","p":"v.","d":"to jump from a plane using a parachute","c":"跳傘","s":"For his fortieth birthday, my uncle decided to parachute from a plane, and he said it was the most exciting minute of his life.","t":"為了慶祝四十歲生日，我叔叔決定從飛機上跳傘，他說那是他一生中最刺激的一分鐘。"},{"w":"parachuting","p":"n.","d":"the sport of jumping from a plane with a parachute","c":"跳傘運動","s":"Parachuting is popular with people who love excitement, but it is expensive and you need several lessons before your first jump.","t":"跳傘運動很受愛刺激的人歡迎，但它很貴，而且在第一次跳之前你需要上好幾堂課。","a":"Parachuting"},{"w":"paragraph","p":"n.","d":"a group of sentences about one idea, starting on a new line","c":"段落","s":"Your essay should have an opening paragraph that tells the reader clearly what you are going to write about.","t":"你的作文應該有一個開頭段落，清楚地告訴讀者你要寫什麼。","h":1},{"w":"topic sentence","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sentence that gives the main idea of a paragraph","c":"主題句","s":"Every paragraph needs a topic sentence that states its main idea, and the other sentences should support it with details.","t":"每個段落都需要一個說明主旨的主題句，其他句子則應該用細節來支持它。"},{"w":"graph","p":"n.","d":"a drawing that uses lines or bars to show how numbers change","c":"圖表","s":"The graph on page ten shows that the number of visitors to the museum has doubled over the past five years.","t":"第十頁的圖表顯示，過去五年來博物館的參觀人數增加了一倍。"},{"w":"photograph","p":"n.","d":"a picture taken with a camera","c":"照片","s":"My grandmother keeps an old black-and-white photograph of her wedding day on the table beside her bed.","t":"我奶奶在她床邊的桌上放著一張她婚禮當天的黑白老照片。"},{"w":"partial","p":"adj.","d":"not complete; only a part","c":"部分的","s":"The company offered only a partial refund, so the customer got back half of the money she had paid for the broken chair.","t":"公司只提供部分退款，所以那位顧客只拿回她為那張壞椅子付的一半錢。","h":1},{"w":"partially","p":"adv.","d":"not completely; partly","c":"部分地","s":"The road was partially blocked by a fallen tree after the typhoon, so cars had to drive slowly around it.","t":"颱風過後，道路被一棵倒下的樹部分堵住，所以車輛必須慢慢繞過它。"},{"w":"part","p":"n.","d":"one piece of something; not the whole","c":"部分","s":"I have only read the first part of the novel, so please do not tell me how the story ends.","t":"我只讀了這本小說的第一部分，所以請不要告訴我故事的結局。"},{"w":"partly","p":"adv.","d":"to some degree, but not completely","c":"部分地；某種程度上","s":"The accident was partly my fault because I was looking at my phone when I stepped onto the road.","t":"那起意外有一部分是我的錯，因為我走上馬路時正在看手機。"},{"w":"be partial to","p":"phr.","d":"to like something very much","c":"偏愛","s":"My grandfather is partial to sweet food, so there is always a box of pineapple cakes somewhere in his kitchen.","t":"我爺爺偏愛甜食，所以他的廚房裡總是有一盒鳳梨酥放在某個角落。","a":"is partial to"},{"w":"participation","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking part in an activity","c":"參與","s":"Class participation counts for twenty percent of your final grade, so make sure you join every discussion and activity.","t":"課堂參與佔你期末成績的百分之二十，所以務必加入每一次討論和活動。","h":1},{"w":"participate","p":"v.","d":"to take part in an activity","c":"參加；參與","s":"All students are encouraged to participate in at least one club so that they can make friends and learn new skills.","t":"我們鼓勵所有學生至少參加一個社團，這樣他們可以交朋友並學習新技能。"},{"w":"participate in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take part in something","c":"參加…","s":"More than two thousand runners participated in the city marathon last Sunday despite the cold rain that fell all morning.","t":"儘管整個早上下著冷雨，上週日仍有兩千多名跑者參加了城市馬拉松。","a":"participated in"},{"w":"participant","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in something","c":"參與者","s":"Each participant in the cooking class receives an apron and a recipe book, and everyone takes home the dishes they make.","t":"烹飪課的每位參與者都會拿到一件圍裙和一本食譜，而且每個人都能把自己做的菜帶回家。"},{"w":"partnership","p":"n.","d":"a relationship between people or companies that work together","c":"合夥；合作關係","s":"The two small companies formed a partnership last year, and together they now sell their products in five countries.","t":"這兩家小公司去年建立了合作關係，現在他們一起在五個國家銷售產品。","h":1},{"w":"partner","p":"n.","d":"a person you do an activity with or run a business with","c":"夥伴；搭檔；合夥人","s":"My tennis partner broke her arm last month, so I have been practicing alone against the wall ever since.","t":"我的網球搭檔上個月手臂骨折了，所以從那時起我一直一個人對著牆練習。"},{"w":"partner with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work together with a person or company","c":"與…合作","s":"The school decided to partner with a local farm so that students can learn how rice is grown and harvested.","t":"學校決定與當地一座農場合作，讓學生能學習稻米是如何種植和收割的。"},{"w":"in partnership with","p":"phr.","d":"working together with someone","c":"與…合作","s":"The concert was organized in partnership with the city government, which provided the park and the sound equipment for free.","t":"這場音樂會是與市政府合作舉辦的，市政府免費提供了公園場地和音響設備。"},{"w":"passive","p":"adj.","d":"accepting what happens without trying to change it","c":"被動的；消極的","s":"Do not be a passive learner who only listens; ask questions, take notes, and try to use the new words in your own sentences.","t":"不要當一個只聽講的被動學習者；要提問、做筆記，並試著在自己的句子裡使用新單字。","h":1},{"w":"passively","p":"adv.","d":"without doing anything to change what happens","c":"被動地","s":"Many people sit passively in front of the TV for hours every evening instead of going out and doing something active.","t":"許多人每天晚上被動地坐在電視前好幾個小時，而不是出門做點積極的事。"},{"w":"the passive voice","p":"n.phr.","d":"the verb form used when the subject receives the action","c":"被動語態","s":"In the sentence 'The window was broken by the ball,' the verb is in the passive voice, because the window did not do the action.","t":"在「The window was broken by the ball」這個句子裡，動詞是被動語態，因為窗戶不是做動作的人。"},{"w":"passive smoking","p":"n.phr.","d":"breathing in smoke from other people's cigarettes","c":"二手菸","s":"Doctors warn that passive smoking can harm children's lungs, so parents should never smoke inside the house or the car.","t":"醫生警告二手菸會傷害孩子的肺，所以父母絕不應該在屋內或車內抽菸。"},{"w":"pasta","p":"n.","d":"Italian food made from flour and water, such as spaghetti","c":"義大利麵","s":"My little brother could eat pasta every day; his favorite is spaghetti with tomato sauce and lots of cheese on top.","t":"我弟弟可以每天吃義大利麵；他最愛的是加番茄醬和很多起司的義大利細麵。","h":1},{"w":"spaghetti","p":"n.","d":"long, thin pasta","c":"義大利細麵","s":"The restaurant is famous for its spaghetti with seafood, and on weekends you often have to wait thirty minutes for a table.","t":"這家餐廳以海鮮義大利細麵聞名，週末常常要等三十分鐘才有位子。"},{"w":"noodle","p":"n.","d":"a long, thin piece of food made from flour, cooked in soup or with sauce","c":"麵條","s":"Beef noodle soup is one of the most famous dishes in Taiwan, and tourists line up for hours at the best shops.","t":"牛肉麵是台灣最有名的菜餚之一，觀光客會在最好的店前排隊好幾個小時。"},{"w":"paste","p":"n.","d":"a soft, thick, wet mixture","c":"糊；膏；醬","s":"Mix the flour with a little water to make a thick paste, and then use it to stick the paper onto the wall.","t":"把麵粉和一點水混合成濃稠的糊，然後用它把紙黏到牆上。"},{"w":"paw","p":"n.","d":"the foot of an animal such as a cat, dog, or bear","c":"爪子；腳掌","s":"The cat lifted one paw and touched the fish in the tank, but it jumped back as soon as it felt the cold water.","t":"那隻貓抬起一隻腳掌碰了碰水缸裡的魚，但一感覺到冷水就馬上跳開了。","h":1},{"w":"paw","p":"v.","d":"to touch or scratch something with a paw","c":"用爪子抓","s":"The dog will paw at the door every morning at six, which is his way of telling us that he wants to go out.","t":"那隻狗每天早上六點都會用爪子抓門，這是牠告訴我們牠想出去的方式。"},{"w":"claw","p":"n.","d":"the sharp, curved nail on an animal's foot","c":"爪","s":"The eagle held the fish tightly in its sharp claws and flew back to its nest high in the tree.","t":"老鷹用牠銳利的爪緊緊抓著魚，飛回樹上高處的巢。","a":"claws"},{"w":"paw print","p":"n.phr.","d":"the mark left by an animal's foot","c":"爪印；腳印","s":"We knew a cat had walked across the wet floor because there was a line of small paw prints leading to the kitchen.","t":"我們知道有隻貓走過濕地板，因為有一排小小的爪印通往廚房。","a":"paw prints"},{"w":"peculiar","p":"adj.","d":"strange or unusual","c":"奇特的；古怪的","s":"There was a peculiar smell in the kitchen this morning, and later we found a rotten egg behind the refrigerator.","t":"今天早上廚房裡有一股奇怪的味道，後來我們在冰箱後面發現一顆壞掉的蛋。","h":1},{"w":"peculiarly","p":"adv.","d":"in a strange way; especially","c":"奇怪地；特別地","s":"The dog was behaving peculiarly all evening, hiding under the bed and refusing to eat, so we took him to the vet.","t":"那隻狗整個晚上表現得很奇怪，躲在床底下又不肯吃東西，所以我們帶牠去看獸醫。"},{"w":"be peculiar to","p":"phr.","d":"to belong only to one person, place, or thing","c":"為…所特有","s":"This kind of fruit is peculiar to the island, so you will not find it growing anywhere else in the world.","t":"這種水果是這座島特有的，所以你在世界上其他任何地方都找不到它生長。","a":"is peculiar to"},{"w":"peep","p":"v.","d":"to look at something quickly and secretly","c":"偷看；窺視","s":"The children tried to peep through the window to see what their birthday present was before the party started.","t":"孩子們想在派對開始前從窗戶偷看他們的生日禮物是什麼。","h":1},{"w":"peep","p":"n.","d":"a quick, secret look","c":"偷看一眼","s":"Take a quick peep inside the box, but do not tell your sister what is in it until she opens it herself.","t":"快速偷看一下盒子裡面，但在你妹妹自己打開之前，不要告訴她裡面有什麼。"},{"w":"peek","p":"v.","d":"to look quickly, often at something you should not see","c":"偷看；瞥一眼","s":"I could not wait until Christmas, so I peeked at the presents under the tree while my parents were out.","t":"我等不到聖誕節，所以趁父母出門時偷看了聖誕樹下的禮物。","a":"peeked"},{"w":"peer","p":"n.","d":"a person who is the same age or has the same position as you","c":"同儕；同輩","s":"Teenagers often care more about what their peers think than about what their parents say, which can lead to risky choices.","t":"青少年往往比較在意同儕的看法而不是父母的話，這可能導致冒險的選擇。","a":"peers","h":1},{"w":"peer","p":"v.","d":"to look very carefully, especially when it is hard to see","c":"凝視；仔細看","s":"The old woman peered at the small letters on the medicine bottle, but she could not read them without her glasses.","t":"那位老太太仔細看著藥瓶上的小字，但沒有眼鏡她看不清楚。","a":"peered"},{"w":"peer pressure","p":"n.phr.","d":"the feeling that you must do what people of your age are doing","c":"同儕壓力","s":"Many students start smoking because of peer pressure; they do not want to look different from their friends.","t":"許多學生因為同儕壓力而開始抽菸；他們不想看起來和朋友不一樣。"},{"w":"penalty","p":"n.","d":"a punishment for breaking a law or rule","c":"處罰；罰款","s":"The penalty for parking in a space for disabled people is a fine of twelve hundred dollars, and your car may be towed away.","t":"在身心障礙車位停車的處罰是罰款一千兩百元，而且你的車可能會被拖走。","h":1},{"w":"penalty","p":"n.","d":"in sports, a free kick or shot given because the other team broke a rule","c":"罰球","s":"In the last minute of the match, our team won a penalty, and the captain kicked the ball straight into the goal.","t":"比賽最後一分鐘，我們隊獲得一次罰球，隊長把球直接踢進了球門。"},{"w":"death penalty","p":"n.phr.","d":"the punishment of being killed for a very serious crime","c":"死刑","s":"Some countries have ended the death penalty because they believe that no court should have the power to take a life.","t":"有些國家已經廢除死刑，因為他們認為任何法院都不該有奪走生命的權力。"},{"w":"penalize","p":"v.","d":"to punish someone for breaking a rule","c":"處罰","s":"The referee will penalize any player who pushes another player, so keep your hands to yourself during the game.","t":"裁判會處罰任何推人的球員，所以比賽中不要動手推別人。"},{"w":"percent","p":"n.","d":"one part in every hundred","c":"百分之…","s":"Only about thirty percent of the students passed the first test, so the teacher decided to review the chapter again.","t":"只有大約百分之三十的學生通過第一次考試，所以老師決定再複習一次這一章。","h":1},{"w":"percentage","p":"n.","d":"an amount expressed as a part of a hundred","c":"百分比；比例","s":"A high percentage of the people in this town are over sixty, so the hospital is always busy and the schools are getting smaller.","t":"這個鎮上有很高比例的人超過六十歲，所以醫院總是很忙，而學校越來越小。","h":1},{"w":"per","p":"prep.","d":"for each","c":"每","s":"The speed limit on this road is fifty kilometers per hour, so slow down before the camera near the school.","t":"這條路的速限是每小時五十公里，所以在學校附近的照相機前要減速。"},{"w":"cent","p":"n.","d":"a small coin; one hundredth of a dollar","c":"分","s":"In the United States, a quarter is a coin worth twenty-five cents, and you can use it in many parking meters.","t":"在美國，quarter 是一枚價值二十五分的硬幣，你可以在許多停車計時器上使用它。","a":"cents"},{"w":"perfection","p":"n.","d":"the state of being perfect, without any mistakes","c":"完美","s":"The chef cooked the steak to perfection; it was brown outside, pink inside, and so soft that you hardly needed a knife.","t":"主廚把牛排煎得完美；外面焦黃、裡面粉紅，而且軟到幾乎不需要用刀。","h":1},{"w":"perfect","p":"adj.","d":"as good as possible; without any mistakes","c":"完美的","s":"The weather was perfect for our trip to the beach—sunny, warm, and with a gentle wind coming off the sea.","t":"我們去海邊那天的天氣很完美——晴朗、溫暖，還有從海上吹來的微風。"},{"w":"perfect","p":"v.","d":"to make something as good as possible","c":"使完美；改進","s":"She spent the whole summer trying to perfect her English pronunciation by listening to podcasts and repeating every sentence.","t":"她花了整個夏天聽播客並跟讀每個句子，努力改進她的英文發音。"},{"w":"perfectly","p":"adv.","d":"completely; in a perfect way","c":"完全地；完美地","s":"The dress fits her perfectly, so she does not need to have it changed before her cousin's wedding next month.","t":"這件洋裝完全合她的身，所以在下個月她表姐的婚禮前不需要修改。"},{"w":"perfectionist","p":"n.","d":"a person who wants everything to be perfect","c":"完美主義者","s":"My sister is a perfectionist who rewrites every essay five times, so she often stays up past midnight before a deadline.","t":"我姐姐是個完美主義者，每篇作文都要重寫五次，所以她在截止日前常常熬到半夜。"},{"w":"perfume","p":"n.","d":"a liquid with a pleasant smell that you put on your skin","c":"香水","s":"My mother only wears perfume on special occasions, and the smell of roses always reminds me of her birthday dinners.","t":"我媽媽只在特殊場合擦香水，玫瑰的香味總是讓我想起她的生日晚餐。","h":1},{"w":"perfume","p":"v.","d":"to fill a place with a pleasant smell","c":"使充滿香氣","s":"In May, the white flowers of the tung tree perfume the whole mountain path, and visitors come from far away to see them.","t":"五月時，油桐樹的白花讓整條山路充滿香氣，遊客從遠方前來觀賞。"},{"w":"fume","p":"n.","d":"strong-smelling gas or smoke that is bad to breathe","c":"煙；濃煙；廢氣","s":"Thick fumes from the factory chimney made the people in the nearby village cough all afternoon.","t":"工廠煙囪冒出的濃煙讓附近村莊的人咳了一整個下午。","a":"fumes"},{"w":"permanent","p":"adj.","d":"lasting for a very long time or forever","c":"永久的；固定的","s":"After working at the company for a year on a short contract, she was finally offered a permanent job with a higher salary.","t":"在公司以短期合約工作一年後，她終於獲得一份薪水更高的正式工作。","h":1},{"w":"permanently","p":"adv.","d":"forever; for all time","c":"永久地","s":"The old bridge was damaged so badly in the flood that it has been permanently closed, and a new one will be built next year.","t":"舊橋在洪水中損壞得太嚴重，已經永久封閉，明年將興建一座新橋。"},{"w":"permanent resident","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is allowed to live in a country for as long as they want","c":"永久居民","s":"My aunt became a permanent resident of Canada five years ago, but she still flies back to Taiwan every Lunar New Year.","t":"我阿姨五年前成為加拿大的永久居民，但她每年農曆新年還是會飛回台灣。"},{"w":"temporary","p":"adj.","d":"lasting only for a short time","c":"暫時的","s":"The road closure is only temporary; workers will finish fixing the water pipe by Friday, and buses will return to their normal route.","t":"道路封閉只是暫時的；工人會在星期五前修好水管，公車也會恢復正常路線。"}]},{"unit":30,"theme":"persuasion – possess","cards":[{"w":"persuasion","p":"n.","d":"the act of making someone agree to do something by giving good reasons","c":"說服；勸說","s":"It took a lot of persuasion before my parents finally agreed to let me go camping with my friends.","t":"經過一番勸說，我爸媽終於同意讓我和朋友去露營。","h":1},{"w":"persuasive","p":"adj.","d":"good at making people agree with you","c":"有說服力的","s":"Her speech was so persuasive that even the students who hated the idea at first voted for it in the end.","t":"她的演講非常有說服力，連一開始討厭這個想法的學生最後都投票支持。","h":1},{"w":"persuade","p":"v.","d":"to make someone agree to do something by giving good reasons","c":"說服","s":"My sister tried to persuade me to join the dance club, but I prefer to spend my free time drawing.","t":"我姐姐試著說服我加入舞蹈社，但我比較喜歡把空閒時間花在畫畫上。"},{"w":"persuade sb to do sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make someone agree to do something","c":"說服某人做某事","s":"After an hour of talking, we finally persuaded her to see a doctor about the pain in her back.","t":"談了一個小時後，我們終於說服她去看醫生，檢查她背部的疼痛。","a":"persuaded her to"},{"w":"pessimistic","p":"adj.","d":"always expecting bad things to happen","c":"悲觀的","s":"Do not be so pessimistic about the exam; you have studied hard every night, and I am sure you will pass.","t":"別對考試這麼悲觀；你每天晚上都用功讀書，我相信你一定會及格。","h":1},{"w":"pessimism","p":"n.","d":"the feeling that bad things will happen","c":"悲觀；悲觀主義","s":"After losing three games in a row, there was a lot of pessimism among the fans, but the coach still believed in his team.","t":"連輸三場比賽後，球迷之間瀰漫著悲觀的氣氛，但教練仍然相信他的球隊。"},{"w":"pessimist","p":"n.","d":"a person who always expects the worst","c":"悲觀的人","s":"My uncle is such a pessimist that he brings an umbrella every day, even when the sky is completely clear.","t":"我叔叔是個十足的悲觀主義者，即使天空萬里無雲，他每天都帶著雨傘。"},{"w":"optimistic","p":"adj.","d":"expecting good things to happen","c":"樂觀的","s":"Although the company lost money this year, the manager is optimistic that sales will grow again next spring.","t":"雖然公司今年虧損，經理仍樂觀認為明年春天銷售會再成長。"},{"w":"pest","p":"n.","d":"an insect or small animal that damages crops or food","c":"害蟲","s":"Farmers in the village lost half of their rice crop this year because of a tiny pest that eats the young plants.","t":"村裡的農民今年損失了一半的稻米收成，因為一種會吃幼苗的小害蟲。","h":1},{"w":"pest","p":"n.","d":"an annoying person, especially a child","c":"討厭的人；討厭鬼","s":"My little brother can be a real pest when he follows me around and asks the same question twenty times.","t":"我弟弟跟著我到處走、同一個問題問二十次的時候，真是個討厭鬼。"},{"w":"pesticide","p":"n.","d":"a chemical used to kill insects that damage plants","c":"殺蟲劑；農藥","s":"Many customers now pay more for vegetables that are grown without any pesticide, because they worry about their health.","t":"許多顧客現在願意多花錢買不使用任何農藥種植的蔬菜，因為他們擔心健康。"},{"w":"pest control","p":"n.phr.","d":"the job of killing insects, rats, and other pests","c":"害蟲防治","s":"After we saw two rats in the kitchen, my father called a pest control company to come and check the whole house.","t":"我們在廚房看到兩隻老鼠後，我爸爸打電話請害蟲防治公司來檢查整間房子。"},{"w":"phenomenon","p":"n.","d":"something that happens or exists, especially something unusual","c":"現象","s":"A rainbow is a beautiful natural phenomenon that appears when sunlight shines through drops of rain in the air.","t":"彩虹是一種美麗的自然現象，當陽光穿過空氣中的雨滴時就會出現。","h":1},{"w":"phenomena","p":"n.","d":"more than one phenomenon (plural form)","c":"現象（複數）","s":"Earthquakes, typhoons, and volcanoes are natural phenomena that scientists in Taiwan study very carefully every year.","t":"地震、颱風和火山是台灣科學家每年都仔細研究的自然現象。"},{"w":"social phenomenon","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that happens in society and affects many people","c":"社會現象","s":"Young people staying single until their thirties has become a common social phenomenon in many big cities around the world.","t":"年輕人到三十幾歲仍單身，在世界許多大城市已成為常見的社會現象。"},{"w":"phenomenal","p":"adj.","d":"extremely good or great","c":"驚人的；非凡的","s":"The young singer's success has been phenomenal; her first album sold a million copies in only two weeks.","t":"這位年輕歌手的成功十分驚人；她的第一張專輯只花兩週就賣了一百萬張。"},{"w":"philosopher","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies and thinks about the meaning of life","c":"哲學家","s":"Confucius was a great Chinese philosopher whose ideas about respect and learning are still taught in schools today.","t":"孔子是偉大的中國哲學家，他關於尊重和學習的思想至今仍在學校裡教授。","h":1},{"w":"philosophical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with philosophy; about the meaning of life","c":"哲學的；哲學性的","s":"After dinner, my grandfather often asks us philosophical questions like \"What makes a person truly happy?\"","t":"晚餐後，我爺爺常問我們哲學性的問題，例如「什麼讓一個人真正快樂？」","h":1},{"w":"philosophy","p":"n.","d":"the study of ideas about life, truth, and how to think","c":"哲學","s":"She chose to study philosophy at university because she loves asking big questions that have no easy answers.","t":"她選擇在大學讀哲學，因為她喜歡問那些沒有簡單答案的大問題。","h":1},{"w":"philosophy","p":"n.","d":"a person's way of thinking about life","c":"人生觀；人生哲學","s":"My grandmother's philosophy is simple: work hard, be kind to others, and never go to bed angry.","t":"我奶奶的人生哲學很簡單：努力工作、善待他人，而且絕不帶著怒氣上床睡覺。"},{"w":"philosophically","p":"adv.","d":"in a calm way that accepts difficult things","c":"豁達地；達觀地","s":"He took the bad news philosophically, saying that losing one job might open the door to a better one.","t":"他豁達地接受了這個壞消息，說失去一份工作也許會為更好的工作打開大門。"},{"w":"photography","p":"n.","d":"the art or job of taking photos","c":"攝影","s":"My cousin studied photography for three years, and now she takes wedding pictures for a living in Taichung.","t":"我表姐學了三年攝影，現在她在台中以拍婚禮照片為生。","h":1},{"w":"photograph","p":"n.","d":"a picture taken with a camera","c":"照片","s":"This old photograph shows my grandparents on their wedding day, standing in front of the temple in 1965.","t":"這張舊照片是我祖父母結婚那天拍的，他們站在廟前，那是 1965 年。"},{"w":"photographer","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes photos, especially as a job","c":"攝影師","s":"The photographer asked everyone to move closer together and smile before he took the class picture.","t":"攝影師請大家靠近一點並微笑，然後才拍班級合照。"},{"w":"photographic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with photography","c":"攝影的","s":"He has a photographic memory, so he can remember every page of a book after reading it only once.","t":"他有攝影般的記憶力，所以一本書只讀一次就能記住每一頁。"},{"w":"take a photograph","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use a camera to make a picture","c":"拍照","s":"Visitors are not allowed to take a photograph inside the museum because the bright light can damage the old paintings.","t":"參觀者不可以在博物館裡拍照，因為強光會損壞古老的畫作。"},{"w":"physical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the body","c":"身體的","s":"Doctors say that thirty minutes of physical exercise every day can help teenagers sleep better and feel less stressed.","t":"醫生說每天三十分鐘的身體運動能幫助青少年睡得更好、壓力更少。","h":1},{"w":"physical","p":"adj.","d":"real; able to be touched","c":"實體的；物質的","s":"Many students prefer physical books to e-books because they like to write notes on the pages.","t":"許多學生偏好實體書而不是電子書，因為他們喜歡在書頁上寫筆記。"},{"w":"physically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with the body","c":"身體上","s":"The marathon was physically very hard, but crossing the finish line made every painful step worth it.","t":"這場馬拉松在身體上非常辛苦，但跨過終點線讓每一個痛苦的步伐都值得。"},{"w":"physical education (PE)","p":"n.phr.","d":"sports and exercise classes at school","c":"體育課","s":"Our school has physical education twice a week, and most students say it is their favorite class.","t":"我們學校每週有兩次體育課，大多數學生說那是他們最喜歡的課。","a":"physical education"},{"w":"physician","p":"n.","d":"a doctor, especially one who does not do operations","c":"醫師；內科醫生","s":"If the fever does not go down by tomorrow, you should see a physician instead of just taking more medicine.","t":"如果到明天燒還沒退，你應該去看醫生，而不是只吃更多的藥。","h":1},{"w":"physicist","p":"n.","d":"a scientist who studies physics","c":"物理學家","s":"Albert Einstein, the famous physicist, changed the way people all over the world understand time, light, and energy.","t":"著名的物理學家愛因斯坦改變了全世界的人對時間、光和能量的理解。","h":1},{"w":"physics","p":"n.","d":"the science of energy, forces, and matter","c":"物理學","s":"In physics class today, we learned why a heavy ball and a light ball fall to the ground at the same speed.","t":"今天物理課上，我們學到為什麼重球和輕球會以同樣的速度落到地面。","h":1},{"w":"family physician","p":"n.phr.","d":"a doctor who takes care of all the members of a family","c":"家庭醫師","s":"Our family physician has known me since I was a baby, so she always notices right away when something is wrong.","t":"我們的家庭醫師從我還是嬰兒時就認識我，所以她總是能馬上注意到哪裡不對勁。"},{"w":"pickle","p":"n.","d":"a vegetable kept in salt water or vinegar","c":"泡菜；醃菜","s":"My grandmother makes her own pickles every winter by keeping cabbage in big jars with salt and chili.","t":"我奶奶每年冬天都自己做泡菜，把高麗菜放在大罐子裡加鹽和辣椒醃。","a":"pickles","h":1},{"w":"pickle","p":"v.","d":"to keep food in salt water or vinegar","c":"醃製","s":"In the past, people had to pickle vegetables in the autumn so that they would have something to eat all winter.","t":"以前的人必須在秋天醃製蔬菜，這樣整個冬天才有東西吃。"},{"w":"pickled","p":"adj.","d":"kept in salt water or vinegar","c":"醃製的","s":"The night market stand sells pickled cucumbers that taste sour, sweet, and a little spicy at the same time.","t":"那個夜市攤位賣的醃黃瓜吃起來又酸又甜，還有一點辣。"},{"w":"in a pickle","p":"phr.","d":"in a difficult situation","c":"陷入困境","s":"We were really in a pickle when the car broke down on the mountain road at night with no phone signal.","t":"當車子在夜裡拋錨在山路上又沒有手機訊號時，我們真的陷入了困境。"},{"w":"pioneer","p":"n.","d":"one of the first people to do or study something new","c":"先驅；拓荒者","s":"Marie Curie was a pioneer in the study of radiation, and she was the first woman to win a Nobel Prize.","t":"居禮夫人是輻射研究的先驅，她也是第一位獲得諾貝爾獎的女性。","h":1},{"w":"pioneer","p":"v.","d":"to be the first to do or develop something new","c":"開創；開拓","s":"The small Taiwanese company pioneered a new way to make bicycles lighter, and now factories around the world copy it.","t":"這家台灣小公司開創了讓腳踏車更輕的新方法，現在世界各地的工廠都在模仿。","a":"pioneered"},{"w":"pioneering","p":"adj.","d":"new and leading the way for others","c":"開創性的","s":"Her pioneering work on ocean plastic has inspired thousands of young people to clean up beaches in their own towns.","t":"她在海洋塑膠方面的開創性研究，激勵了成千上萬的年輕人去清理自己家鄉的海灘。"},{"w":"plentiful","p":"adj.","d":"existing in large amounts; more than enough","c":"豐富的；充足的","s":"Fish were once plentiful in this river, but now you can wait all day without catching a single one.","t":"這條河裡的魚曾經很豐富，但現在你可以等一整天也釣不到一條。","h":1},{"w":"plenty","p":"pron./n.","d":"a large amount; as much as you need","c":"很多；充足","s":"There is no need to hurry, because we have plenty of time before the train leaves at six o'clock.","t":"不用急，因為火車六點才開，我們有很多時間。"},{"w":"plenty of","p":"phr.","d":"a lot of; enough","c":"很多的；充足的","s":"Make sure you drink plenty of water during the hike, because the sun will be very strong in the afternoon.","t":"健行時一定要喝大量的水，因為下午的太陽會非常強。"},{"w":"plot","p":"n.","d":"the story of a book, film, or play","c":"情節","s":"The plot of the movie was so confusing that my friends and I argued about the ending for an hour.","t":"這部電影的情節太令人困惑了，我和朋友為了結局爭論了一個小時。","h":1},{"w":"plot","p":"n.","d":"a secret plan to do something bad","c":"陰謀","s":"The police discovered a plot to steal the famous painting from the museum during the New Year holiday.","t":"警方發現了一個在新年假期期間從博物館偷走名畫的陰謀。"},{"w":"plot","p":"v.","d":"to make a secret plan to do something bad","c":"密謀","s":"In the story, the king's brother plotted with the enemy to take the throne while the king was away at war.","t":"在故事中，國王的弟弟和敵人密謀，想趁國王出征時奪取王位。","a":"plotted"},{"w":"plot","p":"n.","d":"a small piece of land","c":"一小塊地","s":"My grandfather grows tomatoes and beans on a small plot of land behind his house in the countryside.","t":"我爺爺在鄉下房子後面的一小塊地上種番茄和豆子。"},{"w":"plum","p":"n.","d":"a soft round fruit with a stone in the middle","c":"李子；梅子","s":"In summer, my aunt sends us a box of sweet purple plums from her farm in the mountains of Nantou.","t":"夏天時，我阿姨從她在南投山上的農場寄給我們一箱甜甜的紫色李子。","a":"plums","h":1},{"w":"plum blossom","p":"n.phr.","d":"the flower of the plum tree; the national flower of the R.O.C.","c":"梅花","s":"Every January, tourists drive to the mountains to see the white plum blossoms that open even in the cold wind.","t":"每年一月，遊客開車上山看即使在寒風中也會綻放的白色梅花。","a":"plum blossoms"},{"w":"dried plum","p":"n.phr.","d":"a plum that has been dried and salted as a snack","c":"話梅；梅乾","s":"My grandmother always keeps a bag of dried plums in her purse and gives me one when I feel carsick.","t":"我奶奶的皮包裡總是放著一袋話梅，我暈車時她就給我一顆。","a":"dried plums"},{"w":"plumber","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to fix water pipes","c":"水管工","s":"Water was dripping from the ceiling all night, so we called a plumber first thing in the morning.","t":"整個晚上天花板都在滴水，所以我們一大早就打電話找水管工。","h":1},{"w":"plumbing","p":"n.","d":"the pipes that carry water in a building","c":"水管系統","s":"The old house looks lovely, but its plumbing needs to be replaced before anyone can live there safely.","t":"這棟老房子看起來很美，但它的水管系統需要更換，之後才能安全入住。"},{"w":"call a plumber","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask a plumber to come and fix the pipes","c":"找水管工來修","s":"If the toilet keeps running after you flush it, you had better call a plumber before the water bill gets too high.","t":"如果馬桶沖水後一直流個不停，你最好在水費變太高之前找水管工來修。"},{"w":"poisonous","p":"adj.","d":"containing poison; able to kill or harm you","c":"有毒的","s":"Some wild mushrooms in the forest are poisonous, so never eat one unless an expert tells you it is safe.","t":"森林裡有些野生蘑菇是有毒的，所以除非專家說它安全，否則絕對不要吃。","h":1},{"w":"poison","p":"n.","d":"a substance that can kill or harm you if you eat or touch it","c":"毒；毒藥","s":"Keep the rat poison on a high shelf where small children and pets cannot reach it.","t":"把老鼠藥放在高架子上，讓小孩和寵物都拿不到。"},{"w":"poison","p":"v.","d":"to kill or harm someone or something with poison","c":"毒害；下毒","s":"Chemicals from the old factory poisoned the river, and thousands of fish died within a few days.","t":"老工廠排出的化學物質毒害了河流，幾天內就有成千上萬條魚死亡。","a":"poisoned"},{"w":"food poisoning","p":"n.phr.","d":"an illness caused by eating bad food","c":"食物中毒","s":"Three students got food poisoning after eating the chicken sandwiches, so the school closed the cafeteria for a week.","t":"三名學生吃了雞肉三明治後食物中毒，所以學校把餐廳關閉了一週。"},{"w":"polish","p":"v.","d":"to rub something to make it shine","c":"擦亮；拋光","s":"Before the ceremony, every soldier had to polish his boots until he could see his face in them.","t":"典禮前，每位士兵都必須把靴子擦亮，直到能在靴子上看見自己的臉。","h":1},{"w":"polish","p":"n.","d":"a substance you rub on something to make it shine","c":"亮光劑；鞋油","s":"My father keeps a tin of shoe polish by the door and shines his leather shoes every Sunday night.","t":"我爸爸在門邊放著一罐鞋油，每個星期天晚上都把他的皮鞋擦亮。"},{"w":"polished","p":"adj.","d":"shiny after being rubbed","c":"擦亮的；光亮的","s":"The floor of the hotel lobby was so polished that I could see the lights of the ceiling in it.","t":"飯店大廳的地板擦得發亮，我可以在上面看到天花板的燈光。"},{"w":"polish up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to improve a skill by practicing","c":"加強；改進","s":"I need to polish up my Japanese before the trip, so I am watching a Japanese drama every evening.","t":"旅行前我需要加強我的日文，所以我每天晚上都看一部日劇。"},{"w":"popularity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being liked by many people","c":"受歡迎；人氣","s":"The singer's popularity grew so fast that her concert tickets sold out in less than ten minutes.","t":"這位歌手的人氣成長得太快，她的演唱會門票不到十分鐘就賣光了。","h":1},{"w":"popular","p":"adj.","d":"liked by many people","c":"受歡迎的","s":"Bubble tea is so popular in Taiwan that you can find a tea shop on almost every street corner.","t":"珍珠奶茶在台灣非常受歡迎，幾乎每個街角都能找到一家茶飲店。"},{"w":"popularize","p":"v.","d":"to make something known and liked by many people","c":"推廣；使普及","s":"The TV show helped to popularize hiking among young people, and now the mountain trails are crowded every weekend.","t":"這個電視節目幫助在年輕人之間推廣健行，現在山路每個週末都擠滿了人。"},{"w":"gain popularity","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become liked by more and more people","c":"越來越受歡迎","s":"Electric scooters have gained popularity in the city because they are quiet, clean, and cheap to charge.","t":"電動機車在這座城市越來越受歡迎，因為它們安靜、乾淨，而且充電便宜。","a":"gained popularity"},{"w":"portable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to carry or move","c":"可攜帶的；便攜式的","s":"My father bought a portable speaker so that we can listen to music on the beach and in the park.","t":"我爸爸買了一個便攜式喇叭，這樣我們在海灘和公園都能聽音樂。","h":1},{"w":"portable charger","p":"n.phr.","d":"a small battery you carry to charge your phone","c":"行動電源","s":"Always bring a portable charger on a long trip, because your phone battery will die before you find a plug.","t":"長途旅行時一定要帶行動電源，因為在找到插座之前你的手機電池就會沒電。"},{"w":"portability","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being easy to carry","c":"可攜性","s":"The main selling point of this laptop is its portability; it weighs less than a kilogram and fits in a small bag.","t":"這台筆電最大的賣點是它的可攜性；它不到一公斤重，而且放得進小包包。"},{"w":"portray","p":"v.","d":"to show or describe someone or something in a particular way","c":"描繪；描述","s":"The movie portrays the famous scientist as a lonely man who cared only about his work.","t":"這部電影把這位著名的科學家描繪成一個只在乎工作的孤獨男人。","a":"portrays","h":1},{"w":"portray","p":"v.","d":"to act the part of a character in a film or play","c":"扮演","s":"In the school play, Jason will portray an old king who loses everything because he trusts the wrong people.","t":"在學校話劇中，傑森將扮演一位因為信錯人而失去一切的老國王。"},{"w":"portrait","p":"n.","d":"a painting, drawing, or photo of a person","c":"肖像；人像","s":"A large portrait of my great-grandfather hangs in the living room, and everyone says I have his eyes.","t":"客廳裡掛著一幅我曾祖父的大肖像，每個人都說我的眼睛像他。"},{"w":"portrayal","p":"n.","d":"the way someone or something is shown in a film, book, or picture","c":"描繪；刻畫","s":"Critics praised the actor's portrayal of the blind musician, saying it was the best performance of the year.","t":"評論家稱讚這位演員對盲人音樂家的刻畫，說那是年度最佳表演。"},{"w":"possess","p":"v.","d":"to have or own something","c":"擁有；具有","s":"Anyone who wants to be a good teacher must possess patience, because students do not learn everything the first time.","t":"想成為好老師的人必須具有耐心，因為學生不會第一次就學會所有東西。","h":1},{"w":"possession","p":"n.","d":"the state of having or owning something","c":"擁有；持有","s":"The police found the stolen bicycle in the possession of a man who said he had bought it online.","t":"警方發現失竊的腳踏車在一名男子的持有中，他說他是在網路上買的。"},{"w":"possessions","p":"n.","d":"the things that you own","c":"財產；所有物","s":"After the fire, the family lost almost all of their possessions, but luckily nobody was hurt.","t":"火災後，這家人幾乎失去了所有的財物，但幸運的是沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"possessive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to keep someone or something only for yourself","c":"佔有慾強的","s":"My dog is very possessive about his toys, and he growls if another dog comes near them.","t":"我的狗對牠的玩具佔有慾很強，如果別的狗靠近牠就會低吼。"},{"w":"take possession of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start to own or control something","c":"取得…的所有權；接管","s":"The new owners will take possession of the house next month, after the old family moves out.","t":"舊住戶搬走後，新屋主下個月將取得這棟房子的所有權。"}]},{"unit":31,"theme":"possession – promising","cards":[{"w":"possession","p":"n.","d":"the state of having or owning something","c":"擁有；持有","s":"When the police stopped the car, they found that the driver was in possession of a knife and a large amount of cash.","t":"警察攔下車子時，發現駕駛持有一把刀和大量現金。","h":1},{"w":"possessions","p":"n.","d":"the things that you own","c":"財產；所有物","s":"The old man did not have many possessions, but he said his books and his garden were all he needed.","t":"那位老先生沒有很多財物，但他說他的書和花園就是他所需要的一切。"},{"w":"possess","p":"v.","d":"to have or own something","c":"擁有；具有","s":"Few people possess the courage to speak the truth when everyone around them is saying something different.","t":"很少人擁有在周圍所有人都說不同話時說出真相的勇氣。"},{"w":"possessive","p":"adj.","d":"wanting to keep someone or something only for yourself","c":"佔有慾強的","s":"Her boyfriend was so possessive that he got upset whenever she spent an evening with her other friends.","t":"她的男朋友佔有慾太強，每當她和其他朋友共度一個晚上他就會不高興。"},{"w":"take possession of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start to own or control something","c":"取得…的所有權；接管","s":"The new owners will take possession of the restaurant next month and plan to change the menu completely.","t":"新老闆下個月將接管這家餐廳，並計畫完全更換菜單。"},{"w":"postage","p":"n.","d":"the money you pay to send a letter or package","c":"郵資","s":"Sending a small gift to Japan is easy, but the postage can be higher than the price of the gift itself.","t":"寄小禮物到日本很容易，但郵資可能比禮物本身的價格還高。","h":1},{"w":"post","p":"v.","d":"to send a letter or package by mail","c":"寄；郵寄","s":"Please post this letter on your way to school, because the application must arrive at the office by Friday.","t":"請在上學路上寄這封信，因為申請書必須在星期五前送到辦公室。"},{"w":"post office","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where you buy stamps and send letters and packages","c":"郵局","s":"My grandmother goes to the post office every month to pay her bills and send a package to my uncle in Tainan.","t":"我奶奶每個月都去郵局繳帳單，並寄包裹給我在台南的叔叔。"},{"w":"postcard","p":"n.","d":"a card with a picture on one side that you send without an envelope","c":"明信片","s":"Whenever my aunt travels abroad, she sends me a postcard with a picture of a famous building on the front.","t":"每當我阿姨出國旅行，她都會寄給我一張正面印著著名建築圖片的明信片。"},{"w":"potential","p":"adj.","d":"possible in the future; that may become something","c":"潛在的；可能的","s":"The company is looking at the small town as a potential site for its new factory, which could bring hundreds of jobs.","t":"這家公司正把這個小鎮視為新工廠的潛在地點，可能帶來數百個工作機會。","h":1},{"w":"potential","p":"n.","d":"the ability to become good or successful in the future","c":"潛力","s":"The coach believes the young swimmer has the potential to win a medal at the Olympic Games one day.","t":"教練相信這位年輕的游泳選手有朝一日能在奧運贏得獎牌的潛力。"},{"w":"potentially","p":"adv.","d":"possibly, in a way that may happen in the future","c":"潛在地；可能地","s":"Leaving a candle burning in an empty room is potentially dangerous, so always blow it out before you go to bed.","t":"讓蠟燭在空房間裡燃燒可能很危險，所以睡前一定要吹熄它。"},{"w":"reach one's full potential","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become as good as you can possibly be","c":"充分發揮潛力","s":"A good teacher helps every student reach their full potential, not just the ones who already get high grades.","t":"好老師幫助每個學生充分發揮潛力，而不只是那些已經拿高分的學生。","a":"reach their full potential"},{"w":"precise","p":"adj.","d":"exact and correct in every detail","c":"精確的；準確的","s":"The doctor needs the precise time you took the medicine, so please check the message on your phone.","t":"醫生需要你吃藥的確切時間，所以請查看你手機上的訊息。","h":1},{"w":"precisely","p":"adv.","d":"exactly","c":"精確地；正好","s":"The train leaves at precisely 8:15 every morning, so if you arrive one minute late, you will miss it.","t":"火車每天早上準八點十五分開，所以如果你晚到一分鐘，就會錯過它。"},{"w":"precision","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being exact and correct","c":"精確；精準","s":"Watchmakers must work with great precision, because even a tiny mistake can stop the whole watch from working.","t":"鐘錶匠必須非常精準地工作，因為即使是微小的錯誤也可能讓整隻錶停擺。"},{"w":"to be precise","p":"phr.","d":"used to give exact information","c":"確切地說","s":"The trip will take about three hours, or to be precise, two hours and fifty minutes if there is no traffic.","t":"這趟車程大約三小時，確切地說，如果沒有塞車是兩小時五十分鐘。"},{"w":"predict","p":"v.","d":"to say what will happen in the future","c":"預測；預言","s":"Nobody can predict exactly when the next big earthquake will hit, so every family should prepare an emergency bag.","t":"沒有人能預測下一次大地震確切會在何時發生，所以每個家庭都應該準備緊急避難包。","h":1},{"w":"prediction","p":"n.","d":"a statement about what will happen in the future","c":"預測；預言","s":"The weather prediction for the weekend is sunny and warm, so we are planning a picnic by the river.","t":"週末的天氣預測是晴朗溫暖，所以我們計畫去河邊野餐。","h":1},{"w":"predictable","p":"adj.","d":"happening in a way that you can expect","c":"可預測的；意料中的","s":"The ending of the movie was so predictable that I guessed who the thief was in the first ten minutes.","t":"這部電影的結局太可預測了，我在前十分鐘就猜到誰是小偷。"},{"w":"unpredictable","p":"adj.","d":"changing often, so that you cannot know what will happen","c":"難以預測的","s":"Mountain weather is unpredictable; it can be sunny at noon and then pour with rain an hour later.","t":"山區的天氣難以預測；中午可能是晴天，一小時後就下起傾盆大雨。"},{"w":"make a prediction","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say what you think will happen","c":"做出預測","s":"Before the game, the sports reporter made a prediction that the home team would win by at least ten points.","t":"比賽前，體育記者做出預測，認為主隊會贏至少十分。","a":"made a prediction"},{"w":"pregnancy","p":"n.","d":"the time when a woman has a baby growing inside her","c":"懷孕；孕期","s":"During her pregnancy, my sister stopped drinking coffee and went to the doctor for a check-up every month.","t":"懷孕期間，我姐姐不再喝咖啡，並且每個月去醫生那裡做檢查。","h":1},{"w":"pregnant","p":"adj.","d":"having a baby growing inside the body","c":"懷孕的","s":"A young man stood up on the bus and gave his seat to a pregnant woman who was holding a heavy bag.","t":"一位年輕男子在公車上站起來，把座位讓給一位提著重袋子的懷孕婦女。","h":1},{"w":"get pregnant","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start having a baby growing inside the body","c":"懷孕","s":"My aunt and uncle were married for five years before she got pregnant with their first child.","t":"我阿姨和姨丈結婚五年後，她才懷了他們的第一個孩子。","a":"got pregnant"},{"w":"presentation","p":"n.","d":"a talk in which you show and explain something to a group","c":"簡報；報告","s":"Each group will give a ten-minute presentation about a country in Asia, using pictures, maps, and music.","t":"每一組將做一個十分鐘的簡報，介紹一個亞洲國家，使用圖片、地圖和音樂。","h":1},{"w":"give a presentation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak to a group to explain something","c":"做簡報","s":"I was nervous about having to give a presentation in English, but my classmates clapped loudly when I finished.","t":"我對要用英文做簡報感到緊張，但我講完時同學們大聲鼓掌。"},{"w":"present","p":"v.","d":"to show or give something to people formally","c":"發表；呈現","s":"The scientist will present her new research at the meeting in Tokyo next month in front of experts from twenty countries.","t":"這位科學家下個月將在東京的會議上，在來自二十個國家的專家面前發表她的新研究。"},{"w":"presenter","p":"n.","d":"a person who introduces a TV or radio program, or gives a talk","c":"主持人；報告者","s":"The presenter of the morning news show has such a warm voice that my grandmother watches it every day.","t":"晨間新聞節目的主持人聲音很溫暖，我奶奶每天都看。"},{"w":"preservation","p":"n.","d":"the act of keeping something safe or in good condition","c":"保存；保護","s":"The preservation of the old forest is important because many rare birds build their nests there every spring.","t":"這片古老森林的保護很重要，因為每年春天許多稀有鳥類都在那裡築巢。","h":1},{"w":"preserve","p":"v.","d":"to keep something safe or in good condition","c":"保存；保護","s":"Grandma uses sugar to preserve the strawberries from her garden so that we can eat jam all winter long.","t":"奶奶用糖來保存她花園裡的草莓，這樣我們整個冬天都能吃到果醬。","h":1},{"w":"preservative","p":"n.","d":"a chemical added to food to keep it from going bad","c":"防腐劑","s":"This bread has no preservative in it, so you should eat it within two days or keep it in the fridge.","t":"這種麵包不含防腐劑，所以你應該在兩天內吃完，或放進冰箱保存。"},{"w":"well-preserved","p":"adj.","d":"kept in good condition over a long time","c":"保存良好的","s":"The well-preserved temple looks almost the same as it did three hundred years ago, thanks to careful repairs.","t":"這座保存良好的寺廟看起來幾乎和三百年前一樣，這要歸功於細心的修繕。"},{"w":"prevention","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping something bad from happening","c":"預防","s":"Fire prevention is everyone's job, so never leave the stove on when you go out, even for a few minutes.","t":"火災預防是每個人的責任，所以出門時絕不要讓爐火開著，即使只是幾分鐘。","h":1},{"w":"prevent","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from happening","c":"防止；預防","s":"Brushing your teeth twice a day helps prevent tooth decay, which is why dentists keep reminding us to do it.","t":"每天刷牙兩次有助於預防蛀牙，這就是為什麼牙醫一直提醒我們要刷牙。"},{"w":"prevent sb from doing","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop someone from doing something","c":"阻止某人做某事","s":"The heavy snow prevented us from getting to the airport, so we missed our flight to Hokkaido.","t":"大雪使我們無法到達機場，所以我們錯過了飛往北海道的班機。","a":"prevented us from"},{"w":"preventive","p":"adj.","d":"done to stop something bad from happening","c":"預防性的","s":"A yearly health check is a preventive measure that can find small problems before they become serious illnesses.","t":"每年的健康檢查是一種預防性措施，能在小問題變成嚴重疾病前發現它們。"},{"w":"prime","p":"adj.","d":"most important; of the best quality","c":"主要的；最好的","s":"Heavy traffic is the prime reason why many people in Taipei choose to ride the MRT instead of driving.","t":"交通擁擠是許多台北人選擇搭捷運而不開車的主要原因。","h":1},{"w":"prime minister","p":"n.phr.","d":"the leader of the government in some countries","c":"首相；總理","s":"The prime minister of Japan will visit three countries in Europe next week to talk about trade and energy.","t":"日本首相下週將訪問歐洲三個國家，討論貿易和能源問題。"},{"w":"primary","p":"adj.","d":"most important; main; first","c":"主要的；初級的","s":"Her primary goal this year is to pass the English test, so she practices listening for an hour every day.","t":"她今年的主要目標是通過英文檢定，所以她每天練習聽力一小時。"},{"w":"in one's prime","p":"phr.","d":"at the time of life when you are strongest or most successful","c":"在全盛時期","s":"The singer was in her prime in the 1990s, when every one of her albums sold more than a million copies.","t":"這位歌手在 1990 年代正值全盛時期，當時她每張專輯都賣超過一百萬張。","a":"in her prime"},{"w":"primitive","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to a very early stage of human history","c":"原始的","s":"Scientists found tools made by primitive people in a cave in the mountains, along with drawings of animals on the walls.","t":"科學家在山上的一個洞穴裡發現了原始人類製作的工具，還有牆上的動物圖畫。","h":1},{"w":"primitive","p":"adj.","d":"very simple and basic, without modern comforts","c":"簡陋的；簡單的","s":"The cabin was quite primitive, with no electricity or running water, but the view of the lake was wonderful.","t":"這間小屋相當簡陋，沒有電也沒有自來水，但湖景美極了。"},{"w":"primitive society","p":"n.phr.","d":"a human group living in a very early and simple way","c":"原始社會","s":"In a primitive society, people hunted animals and gathered fruit instead of growing food on farms.","t":"在原始社會裡，人們打獵和採集水果，而不是在農場種植食物。"},{"w":"priority","p":"n.","d":"something that is more important than other things","c":"優先事項；優先","s":"Safety is our first priority, so every worker must wear a helmet before entering the building site.","t":"安全是我們的第一優先事項，所以每位工人進入工地前都必須戴安全帽。","h":1},{"w":"top priority","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most important thing to do","c":"首要任務","s":"Finding clean water for the villagers became the top priority after the typhoon destroyed the pipes.","t":"颱風摧毀水管後，為村民找到乾淨的水成了首要任務。"},{"w":"give priority to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to treat something as more important than other things","c":"優先考慮；優先處理","s":"Hospitals must give priority to patients whose lives are in danger, even if other people have waited longer.","t":"醫院必須優先處理生命有危險的病人，即使其他人等得比較久。"},{"w":"prior","p":"adj.","d":"happening or existing before something else","c":"先前的；事先的","s":"You cannot enter the laboratory without prior permission from the professor, so please send her an email first.","t":"沒有教授事先的許可，你不能進入實驗室，所以請先寄電子郵件給她。"},{"w":"prioritize","p":"v.","d":"to decide which things are most important and do them first","c":"優先處理；排定優先順序","s":"When you have too much homework, learn to prioritize and finish the most difficult subject while your mind is still fresh.","t":"當你功課太多時，要學會排定優先順序，趁頭腦還清醒時先完成最難的科目。"},{"w":"privacy","p":"n.","d":"the state of being alone and not watched or bothered by others","c":"隱私","s":"Teenagers need some privacy, so my parents always knock on my door before they come into my room.","t":"青少年需要一些隱私，所以我爸媽進我房間前總是會先敲門。","h":1},{"w":"private","p":"adj.","d":"for one person or group only; not public","c":"私人的；私密的","s":"This is a private beach, so only the people who live in the apartments nearby are allowed to swim here.","t":"這是私人海灘，所以只有住在附近公寓的人可以在這裡游泳。"},{"w":"in private","p":"phr.","d":"with nobody else present","c":"私下地","s":"The teacher asked to speak with Tom in private after class, because she did not want to embarrass him in front of everyone.","t":"老師要求下課後私下和湯姆談談，因為她不想在大家面前讓他難堪。"},{"w":"privately","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is not public","c":"私下地；私人地","s":"The two leaders talked privately for an hour before they walked out to answer questions from the reporters.","t":"兩位領導人私下談了一小時，然後才走出來回答記者的問題。"},{"w":"privilege","p":"n.","d":"a special right or advantage that only some people have","c":"特權；殊榮","s":"In the past, only rich families had the privilege of sending their children to school, while poor children worked.","t":"過去只有富裕家庭才有送孩子上學的特權，而貧窮的孩子則要工作。","h":1},{"w":"privileged","p":"adj.","d":"having special rights or advantages","c":"享有特權的；優渥的","s":"Students from privileged families often have private tutors, so they get extra help with difficult subjects.","t":"來自優渥家庭的學生常有家教，所以他們在困難科目上能獲得額外幫助。"},{"w":"have the privilege of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be lucky enough to be able to do something special","c":"有幸做某事","s":"Last year our class had the privilege of meeting a famous writer who answered all of our questions about her books.","t":"去年我們班有幸見到一位著名的作家，她回答了我們關於她作品的所有問題。","a":"had the privilege of"},{"w":"procedure","p":"n.","d":"the correct or usual way of doing something","c":"程序；步驟","s":"Follow the safety procedure carefully: put on your goggles first, and never touch the chemicals with your bare hands.","t":"請仔細遵守安全程序：先戴上護目鏡，而且絕對不要用手直接碰化學藥品。","h":1},{"w":"proceed","p":"v.","d":"to continue doing something; to go on","c":"繼續進行；前進","s":"After the short break, the judge told everyone to sit down so that the meeting could proceed.","t":"短暫休息後，法官請大家坐下，好讓會議可以繼續進行。","h":1},{"w":"proceed with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to continue with a plan or action","c":"繼續進行（某事）","s":"Even though it was raining, the school decided to proceed with the sports day as planned.","t":"儘管下著雨，學校還是決定按原計畫繼續舉行運動會。"},{"w":"process","p":"n.","d":"a series of actions done to achieve something","c":"過程；流程","s":"Learning a language is a slow process, so do not be upset if you still make mistakes after a year.","t":"學習語言是一個緩慢的過程，所以如果一年後你還會犯錯，別難過。"},{"w":"process","p":"v.","d":"to deal with information or materials in a series of steps","c":"處理；加工","s":"It takes the office about two weeks to process a passport application, so apply early if you travel in July.","t":"辦公室大約需要兩週來處理護照申請，所以如果你七月要旅行，請提早申請。"},{"w":"productive","p":"adj.","d":"making or achieving a lot","c":"多產的；有效率的","s":"I am most productive early in the morning, so I do my hardest homework before breakfast.","t":"我在清晨最有效率，所以我在早餐前做最難的功課。","h":1},{"w":"productivity","p":"n.","d":"the rate at which work is done or things are made","c":"生產力","s":"The factory's productivity doubled after the new machines were installed, so the workers finished early most days.","t":"新機器安裝後，工廠的生產力倍增，所以工人大多數日子都提早完工。"},{"w":"produce","p":"v.","d":"to make or grow something","c":"生產；製造","s":"This small farm in Yunlin can produce enough rice every year to feed about five hundred families.","t":"雲林這座小農場每年能生產足夠餵飽大約五百個家庭的稻米。"},{"w":"product","p":"n.","d":"something that is made or grown to be sold","c":"產品","s":"The company's newest product is a water bottle that keeps drinks cold for twenty-four hours, even in summer.","t":"這家公司最新的產品是一個即使在夏天也能讓飲料保冷二十四小時的水瓶。"},{"w":"production","p":"n.","d":"the process of making or growing things in large amounts","c":"生產；製作","s":"The production of electric cars has grown quickly, and the company now builds a thousand of them every day.","t":"電動車的生產快速成長，這家公司現在每天製造一千輛。"},{"w":"profession","p":"n.","d":"a job that needs special training, such as teaching or medicine","c":"職業；專業","s":"Nursing is a caring profession, and my cousin says helping sick people get better makes her long hours worth it.","t":"護理是一個充滿關懷的職業，我表姐說幫助病人康復讓她漫長的工時變得值得。","h":1},{"w":"professional","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a job that needs special training; done for money","c":"專業的；職業的","s":"You should get professional advice from a lawyer before you sign a contract for the new apartment.","t":"在簽新公寓的合約之前，你應該先向律師尋求專業建議。","h":1},{"w":"professional","p":"n.","d":"a person who does a job that needs special training; a paid player","c":"專業人士；職業選手","s":"After winning several big tournaments, the young golfer decided to become a professional at the age of eighteen.","t":"贏得幾場大型錦標賽後，這位年輕的高爾夫選手決定在十八歲時成為職業選手。"},{"w":"professionally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows skill and training","c":"專業地","s":"The waiter handled the angry customer very professionally, staying calm and polite until the problem was solved.","t":"服務生非常專業地應對那位生氣的顧客，保持冷靜有禮直到問題解決。"},{"w":"professor","p":"n.","d":"a teacher of the highest rank at a university","c":"教授","s":"My chemistry professor explains difficult ideas so clearly that even students who hate science enjoy her class.","t":"我的化學教授把困難的概念解釋得很清楚，連討厭科學的學生都喜歡她的課。"},{"w":"profitable","p":"adj.","d":"making money; bringing an advantage","c":"有利可圖的；獲利的","s":"The night market stand was so profitable that the owner opened a second one on the other side of town.","t":"這個夜市攤位非常有利可圖，老闆在城市另一邊開了第二家。","h":1},{"w":"profit","p":"n.","d":"the money you make after paying your costs","c":"利潤","s":"The students sold cookies at the fair and made a profit of three thousand dollars for the animal shelter.","t":"學生們在園遊會賣餅乾，為動物收容所賺到三千元的利潤。"},{"w":"profit from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get an advantage or money from something","c":"從…獲益","s":"Everyone in the class can profit from reading more English stories, not just the students who plan to study abroad.","t":"班上每個人都能從多讀英文故事中獲益，不只是打算出國留學的學生。"},{"w":"make a profit","p":"v.phr.","d":"to earn more money than you spend","c":"獲利；賺錢","s":"The new café did not make a profit in its first year, but the owner believes business will improve this summer.","t":"新咖啡館第一年沒有獲利，但老闆相信今年夏天生意會好轉。"},{"w":"prominent","p":"adj.","d":"important and well known","c":"著名的；重要的","s":"Several prominent doctors spoke at the meeting about the dangers of sitting too long in front of screens.","t":"幾位著名的醫生在會議上談到長時間坐在螢幕前的危險。","h":1},{"w":"prominent","p":"adj.","d":"easy to see; sticking out","c":"顯眼的；突出的","s":"The red lighthouse is the most prominent building in the harbor, and sailors can see it from miles away.","t":"這座紅色燈塔是港口裡最顯眼的建築，水手們從幾英里外就能看到它。"},{"w":"prominence","p":"n.","d":"the state of being important or well known","c":"卓越；顯著；聲望","s":"The young actor rose to prominence after his first movie became a surprise hit across Asia.","t":"這位年輕演員在他的第一部電影意外在亞洲大受歡迎後聲名大噪。"},{"w":"promising","p":"adj.","d":"likely to be successful in the future","c":"有前途的；有希望的","s":"The doctors say the new treatment looks promising, and patients in the first test group are already feeling better.","t":"醫生說這種新療法看起來很有希望，第一組測試的病人已經感覺好多了。","h":1},{"w":"promise","p":"n.","d":"a statement that you will certainly do something","c":"承諾；諾言","s":"My father made a promise to take us to the beach this weekend if we finished all our homework by Friday.","t":"我爸爸做了一個承諾，如果我們星期五前做完所有功課，週末就帶我們去海邊。"},{"w":"promise","p":"v.","d":"to say that you will certainly do something","c":"承諾；答應","s":"I promise to call my grandmother every Sunday evening, and I have not missed a single week since March.","t":"我答應每個星期天晚上打電話給奶奶，從三月以來我沒有漏掉任何一週。"},{"w":"keep a promise","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do what you said you would do","c":"信守承諾","s":"A good friend always tries to keep a promise, even when it is not easy or convenient.","t":"好朋友總是努力信守承諾，即使那並不容易或方便。"}]},{"unit":32,"theme":"promotion – raisin","cards":[{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"a move to a higher or more important job","c":"晉升；升職","s":"After working hard for five years, my father finally got a promotion and became the manager of his department.","t":"努力工作五年後，我爸爸終於獲得晉升，成為他部門的經理。","h":1},{"w":"promotion","p":"n.","d":"an activity that helps sell a product","c":"促銷；宣傳活動","s":"The supermarket is running a special promotion this week, so you can buy two bottles of juice for the price of one.","t":"超市這週正在舉辦特別促銷活動，所以你可以用一瓶的價錢買兩瓶果汁。"},{"w":"promote","p":"v.","d":"to give someone a higher job; to help something grow or sell","c":"晉升；促進；宣傳","s":"The company decided to promote Ms. Lin to sales director because her team sold more than anyone else last year.","t":"公司決定晉升林小姐為業務總監，因為她的團隊去年的銷售量比其他人都多。"},{"w":"get a promotion","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be moved up to a better job","c":"獲得升職","s":"If you want to get a promotion next year, you should learn new skills and show your boss that you can lead a team.","t":"如果你想在明年獲得升職，你應該學習新技能，並讓老闆看到你能帶領團隊。"},{"w":"promotional","p":"adj.","d":"made to advertise or sell something","c":"促銷的；宣傳的","s":"The store handed out promotional flyers at the MRT station, and hundreds of people came to the opening sale that afternoon.","t":"那家店在捷運站發放宣傳傳單，當天下午有數百人來參加開幕特賣。"},{"w":"prompt","p":"adj.","d":"done quickly and without delay","c":"迅速的；及時的","s":"Thank you for your prompt reply to my email; now we can finish the report before the meeting on Friday.","t":"謝謝你迅速回覆我的電子郵件；現在我們可以在星期五開會前完成報告了。","h":1},{"w":"prompt","p":"v.","d":"to make someone decide to do something","c":"促使；引起","s":"The terrible traffic jam every morning finally prompted the city government to build a new MRT line.","t":"每天早上可怕的塞車終於促使市政府興建一條新的捷運路線。","a":"prompted"},{"w":"prompt","p":"n.","d":"words or a sign that help you remember what to say or do","c":"提示","s":"The actor forgot his lines on stage, but a quiet prompt from behind the curtain helped him continue the scene.","t":"那位演員在台上忘了台詞，但幕後一聲輕輕的提示幫助他繼續演下去。"},{"w":"promptly","p":"adv.","d":"quickly; at exactly the right time","c":"迅速地；準時地","s":"The train left promptly at 8:00, so the students who arrived two minutes late had to wait for the next one.","t":"火車準時在八點出發，所以晚到兩分鐘的學生必須等下一班。"},{"w":"pronunciation","p":"n.","d":"the way a word is said","c":"發音","s":"Her English pronunciation improved a lot after she started listening to podcasts and repeating every sentence aloud.","t":"自從她開始聽播客並大聲跟讀每個句子後，她的英文發音進步很多。","h":1},{"w":"pronounce","p":"v.","d":"to make the sound of a word","c":"發音；念","s":"Many students do not know how to pronounce the word \"colonel,\" because it is spelled very differently from the way it sounds.","t":"許多學生不知道怎麼念colonel 這個字，因為它的拼法和發音差很多。"},{"w":"mispronounce","p":"v.","d":"to say a word in the wrong way","c":"發錯音","s":"Foreign visitors often mispronounce the names of Taiwanese cities, but local people are always happy to help them say the names correctly.","t":"外國遊客常常把台灣城市的名字念錯，但當地人總是樂意幫他們正確地說出來。"},{"w":"pronounced","p":"adj.","d":"very easy to notice; strong","c":"明顯的；顯著的","s":"Since my grandmother moved to the countryside, there has been a pronounced improvement in her health, and she walks every morning.","t":"自從奶奶搬到鄉下後，她的健康有了明顯的改善，她每天早上都散步。"},{"w":"proposal","p":"n.","d":"a plan or idea that is suggested to others","c":"提議；提案","s":"The students wrote a proposal to the principal asking for more water fountains, and the school agreed to install three new ones.","t":"學生們寫了一份提案給校長，要求增設飲水機，學校同意安裝三台新的。","h":1},{"w":"proposal","p":"n.","d":"the act of asking someone to marry you","c":"求婚","s":"He planned a surprise proposal on the beach at sunset, and she said yes before he had even finished speaking.","t":"他計畫在日落時分的海灘上來一場驚喜求婚，他話還沒說完她就答應了。"},{"w":"propose","p":"v.","d":"to suggest a plan or idea; to ask someone to marry you","c":"提議；求婚","s":"I would like to propose that we hold the class party on Saturday afternoon, since everyone is free then.","t":"我想提議我們在星期六下午舉辦班級派對，因為那時大家都有空。"},{"w":"make a proposal","p":"v.phr.","d":"to formally suggest a plan","c":"提出提案","s":"The engineer will make a proposal to the city council next week about building a bike path along the river.","t":"那位工程師下週將向市議會提出提案，內容是沿著河邊興建自行車道。"},{"w":"proposed","p":"adj.","d":"suggested but not yet decided or built","c":"被提議的；擬議中的","s":"Many residents are against the proposed shopping mall because they worry it will bring too much traffic to their quiet neighborhood.","t":"許多居民反對這座擬議中的購物中心，因為他們擔心它會給安靜的社區帶來太多車流。"},{"w":"prosper","p":"v.","d":"to be successful, especially by making money","c":"繁榮；興旺","s":"Small restaurants near the new university have begun to prosper, because thousands of hungry students eat out every day.","t":"新大學附近的小餐館開始興旺起來，因為每天有數千名飢腸轆轆的學生外食。","h":1},{"w":"prosperity","p":"n.","d":"the state of being successful and having a lot of money","c":"繁榮；富裕","s":"The discovery of oil brought great prosperity to the small country, and new schools and hospitals were built everywhere.","t":"石油的發現為這個小國帶來極大的繁榮，到處都興建了新的學校和醫院。","h":1},{"w":"prosperous","p":"adj.","d":"rich and successful","c":"繁榮的；富裕的","s":"Fifty years ago this was a poor fishing village, but today it is a prosperous city with tall buildings and busy shops.","t":"五十年前這裡是個貧窮的漁村，但今天它是一座有高樓和熱鬧商店的繁榮城市。","h":1},{"w":"economic prosperity","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when a country's business and money are doing well","c":"經濟繁榮","s":"Taiwan enjoyed rapid economic prosperity in the 1980s, when its factories exported products to countries all over the world.","t":"台灣在一九八〇年代享有快速的經濟繁榮，當時它的工廠將產品外銷到世界各國。"},{"w":"prosper in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do well and succeed in a place or kind of work","c":"在…中興旺／成功","s":"Companies that listen to their customers usually prosper in any market, while those that ignore complaints slowly lose business.","t":"傾聽顧客的公司通常能在任何市場中興旺，而忽視抱怨的公司則會慢慢失去生意。"},{"w":"protein","p":"n.","d":"a substance in food such as meat, eggs, and beans that helps your body grow","c":"蛋白質","s":"Athletes need plenty of protein to build strong muscles, so they often eat eggs, chicken, and beans after training.","t":"運動員需要大量的蛋白質來鍛鍊強壯的肌肉，所以他們訓練後常吃蛋、雞肉和豆類。","h":1},{"w":"high in protein","p":"adj.phr.","d":"containing a lot of protein","c":"富含蛋白質","s":"Tofu is high in protein and low in fat, which is why many vegetarians eat it almost every day instead of meat.","t":"豆腐富含蛋白質且脂肪低，這就是為什麼許多素食者幾乎每天用它代替肉。"},{"w":"protein shake","p":"n.phr.","d":"a drink made with protein powder, often used by people who exercise","c":"蛋白飲；高蛋白奶昔","s":"My brother drinks a protein shake right after the gym because he says it helps his body recover faster.","t":"我哥哥健身後會馬上喝一杯高蛋白奶昔，因為他說這能幫助身體更快恢復。"},{"w":"protest","p":"n.","d":"a strong public complaint against something","c":"抗議","s":"Thousands of workers joined a protest outside the factory because the company had not paid them for two months.","t":"數千名工人加入了工廠外的抗議，因為公司已經兩個月沒付他們薪水。","h":1},{"w":"protest","p":"v.","d":"to say or show strongly that you do not agree with something","c":"抗議；反對","s":"Students gathered in front of the school to protest against the plan to cut down the old trees on campus.","t":"學生聚集在校門口抗議砍掉校園裡老樹的計畫。"},{"w":"protester","p":"n.","d":"a person who takes part in a protest","c":"抗議者","s":"The protesters held up signs and sang songs, and the police made sure that everything stayed peaceful.","t":"抗議者舉著標語唱歌，警察則確保一切保持和平。","a":"protesters"},{"w":"in protest","p":"phr.","d":"as a way of showing that you disagree","c":"以示抗議","s":"When the restaurant raised its prices again, many regular customers stopped eating there in protest.","t":"當那家餐廳再次漲價時，許多常客不再去那裡用餐以示抗議。"},{"w":"psychological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the mind and the way people think and feel","c":"心理的","s":"Losing a pet can cause real psychological pain, so parents should talk with their children about their feelings.","t":"失去寵物可能造成真正的心理痛苦，所以父母應該和孩子談談他們的感受。","h":1},{"w":"psychologist","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies the mind and helps people with their feelings","c":"心理學家；心理師","s":"The school psychologist talked with the boy every week, and slowly he started to make friends and enjoy class again.","t":"學校心理師每週和那個男孩談話，慢慢地他開始交朋友，再次喜歡上課。","h":1},{"w":"psychology","p":"n.","d":"the study of the mind and how people behave","c":"心理學","s":"My sister is studying psychology at university because she wants to understand why people make the choices they do.","t":"我姐姐在大學讀心理學，因為她想了解人們為什麼會做出那些選擇。","h":1},{"w":"psychologically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with the mind","c":"心理上","s":"The long exam period was hard on the students psychologically, so the teachers planned a fun day at the beach afterwards.","t":"漫長的考試期間對學生來說在心理上很辛苦，所以老師們在考後安排了一天快樂的海灘活動。"},{"w":"psychiatrist","p":"n.","d":"a medical doctor who treats mental illness","c":"精神科醫師","s":"Unlike a psychologist, a psychiatrist is a doctor who can give patients medicine to help them sleep or feel calmer.","t":"和心理師不同，精神科醫師是能開藥幫助病人入睡或感到平靜的醫生。"},{"w":"child psychology","p":"n.phr.","d":"the study of how children think, feel, and grow","c":"兒童心理學","s":"Every kindergarten teacher in our city must take a course in child psychology so that they understand why young children behave the way they do.","t":"我們市裡每位幼兒園老師都必須修一門兒童心理學課程，以便了解幼童為什麼會有那樣的行為。"},{"w":"publication","p":"n.","d":"the act of printing a book or article so people can read it; a book or magazine","c":"出版；出版品","s":"The publication of her first novel changed her life, and within a year she had readers in more than ten countries.","t":"她第一本小說的出版改變了她的人生，一年內她在十幾個國家都有了讀者。","h":1},{"w":"publicity","p":"n.","d":"attention from newspapers, TV, and the public","c":"宣傳；公眾的注意","s":"The small bakery got a lot of free publicity after a famous singer posted a photo of its cakes online.","t":"一位知名歌手在網路上貼出那家小麵包店蛋糕的照片後，店家獲得了許多免費的宣傳。","h":1},{"w":"publish","p":"v.","d":"to print a book, magazine, or article for people to buy or read","c":"出版；發表","s":"The newspaper decided to publish the student's letter about school lunches, and many parents wrote in to agree with her.","t":"報社決定刊登那位學生關於營養午餐的投書，許多家長寫信表示贊同。","h":1},{"w":"publisher","p":"n.","d":"a company or person that prints and sells books","c":"出版社；出版商","s":"After twenty publishers said no to his book, the twenty-first one finally said yes, and it became a bestseller.","t":"在二十家出版社拒絕他的書之後，第二十一家終於答應了，而這本書成了暢銷書。","a":"publishers","h":1},{"w":"publicize","p":"v.","d":"to make something known to the public","c":"宣傳；公布","s":"The club used posters and social media to publicize the charity concert, and all the tickets were sold in three days.","t":"社團利用海報和社群媒體來宣傳這場慈善音樂會，所有門票三天內就賣光了。"},{"w":"publishing","p":"n.","d":"the business of producing books, magazines, and newspapers","c":"出版業","s":"My aunt has worked in publishing for twenty years, and she says that e-books have completely changed the way people read.","t":"我阿姨在出版業工作了二十年，她說電子書徹底改變了人們閱讀的方式。"},{"w":"in public","p":"phr.","d":"where other people can see or hear you","c":"公開地；在公共場合","s":"My little brother is very shy and never sings in public, but at home he sings loudly in the shower every night.","t":"我弟弟很害羞，從不在公共場合唱歌，但在家裡他每晚洗澡時都大聲唱。"},{"w":"pursue","p":"v.","d":"to try hard to achieve something over a long time","c":"追求；從事","s":"After graduation, she moved to Taipei to pursue her dream of becoming a professional dancer, even though her parents worried.","t":"畢業後，她搬到台北追求成為職業舞者的夢想，儘管父母很擔心。","h":1},{"w":"pursue","p":"v.","d":"to follow or chase someone in order to catch them","c":"追趕；追捕","s":"The police officer continued to pursue the thief through the night market until he was finally caught near the exit.","t":"警察在夜市裡持續追捕小偷，直到他終於在出口附近被抓到。","h":1},{"w":"pursuit","p":"n.","d":"the act of trying to achieve or get something","c":"追求","s":"In the pursuit of higher grades, some students sleep only five hours a night, which is actually bad for their memory.","t":"為了追求更高的成績，有些學生每晚只睡五小時，這其實對記憶力有害。"},{"w":"in pursuit of","p":"phr.","d":"trying to get or achieve something","c":"為了追求…","s":"Many young people leave their small hometowns in pursuit of better jobs, so the villages are now full of elderly people.","t":"許多年輕人為了追求更好的工作而離開小鎮家鄉，所以村子裡現在到處都是老年人。"},{"w":"pursue a career","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work toward a particular job over time","c":"從事某種職業","s":"My cousin decided to pursue a career in medicine, so he will spend at least seven more years studying at university.","t":"我表哥決定從事醫學方面的職業，所以他將在大學至少再花七年讀書。"},{"w":"quarrel","p":"n.","d":"an angry argument between people","c":"爭吵；口角","s":"The two sisters had a loud quarrel over who should use the computer first, and their mother finally turned it off.","t":"兩姊妹為了誰先用電腦而大聲爭吵，最後媽媽把電腦關掉了。","h":1},{"w":"quarrel","p":"v.","d":"to argue angrily with someone","c":"爭吵","s":"My parents rarely quarrel about money, but they sometimes disagree about where to go on vacation.","t":"我父母很少為錢爭吵，但有時候會對去哪裡度假意見不合。"},{"w":"quarrel with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have an angry argument with someone","c":"和…爭吵","s":"I did not want to quarrel with my best friend over such a small thing, so I said sorry first and we made up.","t":"我不想為這麼小的事和我最好的朋友爭吵，所以我先道歉，然後我們就和好了。"},{"w":"quarrelsome","p":"adj.","d":"often starting arguments with people","c":"愛爭吵的","s":"The quarrelsome old man complained about everything in the neighborhood, so most people tried to avoid talking to him.","t":"那個愛爭吵的老人抱怨社區裡的每件事，所以大多數人都盡量避免和他說話。"},{"w":"quilt","p":"n.","d":"a thick warm cover for a bed made of layers of cloth sewn together","c":"被子；拼布被","s":"On cold winter nights, my grandmother always puts a thick quilt on my bed so that I can sleep warmly.","t":"在寒冷的冬夜，奶奶總是在我床上放一條厚被子，讓我可以睡得暖和。","h":1},{"w":"quilt","p":"v.","d":"to sew layers of cloth together to make a thick cover","c":"縫被子；縫製拼布","s":"My aunt likes to quilt in her free time, and she has made a colorful blanket for every baby in our family.","t":"我阿姨閒暇時喜歡縫製拼布，她為我們家每個寶寶都做了一條彩色毯子。"},{"w":"patchwork quilt","p":"n.phr.","d":"a quilt made from many small pieces of different cloth","c":"拼布被","s":"The patchwork quilt on the wall was made from pieces of my grandfather's old shirts, so it holds many family memories.","t":"牆上那條拼布被是用我爺爺舊襯衫的布片做成的，所以它承載著許多家族回憶。"},{"w":"quilted","p":"adj.","d":"made of two layers of cloth with soft material in between","c":"絎縫的；夾棉的","s":"She wore a quilted jacket on the mountain trip, and it kept her warm even when the wind became very strong.","t":"她在登山旅行時穿了一件夾棉外套，即使風變得很強也讓她保持溫暖。"},{"w":"quotation","p":"n.","d":"a sentence or phrase taken from a book or speech","c":"引文；引述","s":"The teacher began her speech with a famous quotation from Confucius, and then she explained what it means for students today.","t":"老師以一句孔子的著名引文開始演講，然後解釋它對今天的學生有什麼意義。","h":1},{"w":"quotation","p":"n.","d":"a written statement of how much a job or service will cost","c":"報價單","s":"Before we fix the roof, we should ask at least three companies for a quotation and compare their prices carefully.","t":"在修屋頂之前，我們應該至少向三家公司索取報價單，並仔細比較價格。"},{"w":"quote","p":"v.","d":"to repeat the exact words that someone else said or wrote","c":"引用；引述","s":"In your essay, you should quote the author's exact words and then explain the idea in your own language.","t":"在你的作文裡，你應該引用作者的原話，然後用自己的語言解釋那個想法。"},{"w":"quotation marks","p":"n.phr.","d":"the marks \" \" used in writing to show the words someone said","c":"引號","s":"When you write down what a person said, remember to put the words inside quotation marks so readers know they are not yours.","t":"當你寫下某人說的話時，記得把那些字放在引號裡，讓讀者知道那不是你的話。"},{"w":"radar","p":"n.","d":"a system that uses radio waves to find the position of planes, ships, or storms","c":"雷達","s":"The airport radar showed a large storm moving toward the city, so all flights were delayed for two hours.","t":"機場的雷達顯示一個大風暴正朝城市移動，所以所有航班都延誤了兩小時。","h":1},{"w":"radar screen","p":"n.phr.","d":"the screen on which radar shows positions","c":"雷達螢幕","s":"The pilot watched a small dot appear on the radar screen and realized that another plane was flying too close.","t":"飛行員看著雷達螢幕上出現一個小點，意識到另一架飛機飛得太近了。"},{"w":"under the radar","p":"phr.","d":"without being noticed by people","c":"不被注意地；低調地","s":"The small coffee shop stayed under the radar for years, but now it is famous after a travel blogger wrote about it.","t":"那家小咖啡店多年來一直不被注意，但在一位旅遊部落客寫到它之後，現在它出名了。"},{"w":"speed radar","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine that measures how fast cars are going","c":"測速雷達","s":"Drivers slow down when they see the speed radar on the highway, because a ticket for speeding costs thousands of dollars.","t":"駕駛人看到高速公路上的測速雷達時會減速，因為超速罰單要好幾千元。"},{"w":"rage","p":"n.","d":"very strong anger that is hard to control","c":"盛怒；狂怒","s":"When he saw the scratch on his new car, his face turned red with rage, and he shouted at the parking attendant.","t":"當他看到新車上的刮痕時，氣得滿臉通紅，盛怒之下對停車場管理員大吼。","h":1},{"w":"rage","p":"v.","d":"to continue with great force; to be very angry","c":"肆虐；發怒","s":"The storm raged all night, and in the morning we found trees lying across the road and the power still off.","t":"暴風雨肆虐了一整夜，早上我們發現樹木橫倒在路上，而且電力還沒恢復。","a":"raged"},{"w":"fly into a rage","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suddenly become extremely angry","c":"勃然大怒","s":"My uncle usually stays calm, but he flew into a rage when he found out that someone had stolen his bicycle again.","t":"我叔叔通常很冷靜，但當他發現有人又偷了他的腳踏車時，他勃然大怒。","a":"flew into a rage"},{"w":"road rage","p":"n.phr.","d":"violent anger shown by a driver toward other drivers","c":"路怒症","s":"Cases of road rage are increasing in big cities, so the police warn drivers to take a deep breath instead of fighting.","t":"大城市的路怒症案件正在增加，所以警方提醒駕駛人深呼吸而不要打架。"},{"w":"outrage","p":"n.","d":"a strong feeling of shock and anger","c":"憤慨；義憤","s":"There was public outrage when the news showed the factory pouring dirty water directly into the river.","t":"當新聞播出那家工廠直接把髒水倒進河裡時，引起了民眾的憤慨。"},{"w":"outrageous","p":"adj.","d":"very shocking and unfair","c":"離譜的；令人髮指的","s":"It is outrageous that the hotel charged us 500 dollars for a bottle of water that costs 20 dollars in a store.","t":"飯店向我們收了五百元買一瓶商店只賣二十元的水，這真是離譜。"},{"w":"rainfall","p":"n.","d":"the amount of rain that falls in a place during a period of time","c":"降雨量","s":"The rainfall this summer was only half of the normal amount, so farmers are worried about their rice fields.","t":"今年夏天的降雨量只有正常的一半，所以農民很擔心他們的稻田。","h":1},{"w":"heavy rainfall","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large amount of rain","c":"豪雨；大量降雨","s":"The weather bureau warned of heavy rainfall in the mountains, and hikers were told to leave the trails before noon.","t":"氣象局警告山區將有豪雨，登山客被告知要在中午前離開步道。"},{"w":"rainy","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of rain","c":"多雨的；下雨的","s":"Keelung is famous for its rainy weather, so people who live there always carry an umbrella in their bags.","t":"基隆以多雨的天氣聞名，所以住在那裡的人總是在包包裡帶著雨傘。"},{"w":"rainstorm","p":"n.","d":"a storm with very heavy rain","c":"暴風雨","s":"A sudden rainstorm hit the city during rush hour, and many streets were under water within thirty minutes.","t":"一場突如其來的暴風雨在尖峰時間襲擊城市，許多街道在三十分鐘內就淹水了。"},{"w":"raisin","p":"n.","d":"a dried grape, often used in cakes and bread","c":"葡萄乾","s":"My mother adds a handful of raisins to the oatmeal every morning because they make it sweet without any sugar.","t":"我媽媽每天早上在燕麥粥裡加一把葡萄乾，因為它們不用加糖就能讓粥變甜。","a":"raisins","h":1},{"w":"raisin bread","p":"n.phr.","d":"bread with raisins baked inside it","c":"葡萄乾麵包","s":"The bakery on the corner sells warm raisin bread every morning at seven, and it is usually sold out by nine.","t":"轉角那家麵包店每天早上七點賣熱騰騰的葡萄乾麵包，通常九點前就賣光了。"},{"w":"grape","p":"n.","d":"a small round green or purple fruit that grows in bunches","c":"葡萄","s":"In autumn, farmers in Changhua pick grapes from the vines, and some of them are dried in the sun to make raisins.","t":"秋天時，彰化的農民從藤上採收葡萄，其中一些會在太陽下曬乾製成葡萄乾。","a":"grapes"},{"w":"dried fruit","p":"n.phr.","d":"fruit that has had its water removed so it keeps for a long time","c":"果乾","s":"Instead of candy, the teacher gave each student a small bag of dried fruit, such as raisins and dried mango.","t":"老師沒有發糖果，而是給每位學生一小袋果乾，例如葡萄乾和芒果乾。"}]},{"unit":33,"theme":"realistic – relaxation","cards":[{"w":"realistic","p":"adj.","d":"sensible and based on what is really possible","c":"實際的；務實的","s":"Running ten kilometers on your first day is not a realistic goal, so start with two kilometers and add more each week.","t":"第一天就跑十公里不是一個實際的目標，所以從兩公里開始，每週再增加一些。","h":1},{"w":"realistic","p":"adj.","d":"looking or seeming like real life","c":"逼真的；寫實的","s":"The dinosaurs in the movie looked so realistic that my little sister hid behind the seat and refused to watch.","t":"電影裡的恐龍看起來太逼真了，我妹妹躲在座位後面不敢看。"},{"w":"unrealistic","p":"adj.","d":"not sensible; not based on what is really possible","c":"不切實際的","s":"It is unrealistic to expect a beginner to speak perfect English after only one month of lessons.","t":"期待一個初學者只上一個月課就能說完美的英文是不切實際的。"},{"w":"realistically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that accepts what is really possible","c":"實際地；現實地","s":"Realistically, we cannot finish the whole project by Friday, so let's ask the teacher for a few more days.","t":"實際上，我們無法在星期五前完成整個專案，所以我們向老師多要幾天吧。","a":"Realistically"},{"w":"reality","p":"n.","d":"the way things really are, not the way you imagine them","c":"現實","s":"In his dreams he was a famous singer, but in reality he worked at a convenience store and sang only in the shower.","t":"在夢裡他是個知名歌手，但在現實中他在便利商店工作，只在洗澡時唱歌。"},{"w":"rebel","p":"n.","d":"a person who fights against the government or refuses to follow rules","c":"叛軍；反叛者","s":"The rebels hid in the mountains for years and attacked government soldiers whenever they passed through the valley.","t":"叛軍在山裡躲了好幾年，每當政府軍經過山谷時就發動攻擊。","a":"rebels","h":1},{"w":"rebel","p":"v.","d":"to fight against or refuse to obey people in power","c":"反叛；反抗","s":"Teenagers often rebel against their parents' rules, but most of them understand those rules better when they grow up.","t":"青少年常常反抗父母的規定，但大多數人長大後會更理解那些規定。"},{"w":"rebel against","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fight against or refuse to accept something","c":"反抗…","s":"The workers decided to rebel against the new schedule because it forced them to work twelve hours a day without a break.","t":"工人們決定反抗新的班表，因為它強迫他們每天工作十二小時而且沒有休息。"},{"w":"rebellion","p":"n.","d":"an organized attempt to change the government by force","c":"叛亂；起義","s":"The rebellion began when farmers could no longer pay the high taxes, and it spread to the capital within a month.","t":"當農民再也付不起高額稅金時，叛亂開始了，並在一個月內蔓延到首都。"},{"w":"rebellious","p":"adj.","d":"refusing to obey rules or people in power","c":"叛逆的","s":"My rebellious cousin dyed his hair green and skipped school for a week, which made my aunt extremely worried.","t":"我那叛逆的表哥把頭髮染成綠色，還翹課一週，讓我阿姨非常擔心。"},{"w":"recall","p":"v.","d":"to remember something from the past","c":"回想；記起","s":"I can still recall the smell of my grandmother's kitchen, even though she passed away more than ten years ago.","t":"我仍然能回想起奶奶廚房的味道，即使她已經過世十多年了。","h":1},{"w":"recall","p":"v.","d":"to ask people to return a product because something is wrong with it","c":"召回","s":"The car company had to recall 50,000 cars after drivers reported that the brakes sometimes stopped working.","t":"在駕駛人反映煞車有時會失靈之後，那家汽車公司不得不召回五萬輛車。"},{"w":"recall","p":"n.","d":"the ability to remember things","c":"記憶力；回想","s":"My grandfather has an amazing recall of names and dates, and he can tell you what happened on any day of his youth.","t":"我爺爺對名字和日期有驚人的記憶力，他能告訴你他年輕時任何一天發生的事。"},{"w":"product recall","p":"n.phr.","d":"the act of a company taking back a product that is not safe","c":"產品召回","s":"After the product recall, customers could return the toy to any store and get their money back without a receipt.","t":"產品召回之後，顧客可以把玩具拿到任何一家店退回，不需要收據就能拿回錢。"},{"w":"reception","p":"n.","d":"a formal party to welcome someone or celebrate something","c":"歡迎會；喜宴","s":"The wedding reception was held in a hotel by the sea, and more than two hundred guests enjoyed the dinner and dancing.","t":"婚禮喜宴在海邊的一家飯店舉行，兩百多位賓客享用了晚餐並跳舞。","h":1},{"w":"reception","p":"n.","d":"the area in a hotel or office where visitors are welcomed","c":"接待處；櫃檯","s":"Please leave your key at reception when you go out, and the staff will keep it safe until you come back.","t":"外出時請把鑰匙放在櫃檯，工作人員會替你保管到你回來。"},{"w":"reception","p":"n.","d":"the quality of radio, TV, or phone signals","c":"收訊","s":"The phone reception in the mountains is very poor, so we could not call home until we reached the village.","t":"山區的手機收訊很差，所以我們直到抵達村子才能打電話回家。"},{"w":"receptionist","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to welcome visitors at a hotel or office","c":"接待員；櫃檯人員","s":"The receptionist smiled and asked for our passports, and then she gave us the key to a room on the tenth floor.","t":"接待員微笑著要我們出示護照，然後給了我們十樓一間房的鑰匙。"},{"w":"receive","p":"v.","d":"to get something that is given or sent to you","c":"收到；接受","s":"Did you receive the package I sent last Monday, or should I call the post office and ask what happened?","t":"你收到我上週一寄的包裹了嗎？還是我應該打電話去郵局問發生了什麼事？"},{"w":"in receipt of","p":"prep.","d":"having received something (formal)","c":"已收到…","s":"The letter says, \"We are in receipt of your application and will contact you within two weeks about the interview.\"","t":"信上寫著：「我們已收到您的申請，將在兩週內與您聯絡面試事宜。」"},{"w":"recipe","p":"n.","d":"a set of instructions for cooking a dish","c":"食譜","s":"My mother found a simple recipe for beef noodles online, and the whole family said it tasted better than the restaurant's.","t":"我媽媽在網路上找到一個簡單的牛肉麵食譜，全家人都說比餐廳的還好吃。","h":1},{"w":"follow a recipe","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cook by doing exactly what the instructions say","c":"照著食譜做","s":"If you follow a recipe carefully and measure everything, even a beginner can bake a delicious chocolate cake.","t":"如果你仔細照著食譜做並把所有材料量好，即使是初學者也能烤出美味的巧克力蛋糕。"},{"w":"a recipe for disaster","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that is very likely to cause big problems","c":"災難的根源；必定出問題的做法","s":"Leaving three young children alone with a box of matches is a recipe for disaster, so the babysitter took the box away.","t":"讓三個小孩單獨和一盒火柴在一起必定會出事，所以保母把火柴盒拿走了。"},{"w":"recipe book","p":"n.phr.","d":"a book full of instructions for cooking different dishes","c":"食譜書","s":"My aunt gave me a recipe book with fifty easy dinners, and I have already tried the curry and the fried rice.","t":"我阿姨送我一本有五十道簡易晚餐的食譜書，我已經試做過咖哩和炒飯了。"},{"w":"recognition","p":"n.","d":"the act of knowing who or what something is because you have seen it before","c":"認出；辨識","s":"The new phone uses face recognition to unlock the screen, so you do not have to type a password every time.","t":"這支新手機用臉部辨識來解鎖螢幕，所以你不必每次都輸入密碼。","h":1},{"w":"recognition","p":"n.","d":"public respect and thanks for something a person has done","c":"表彰；肯定","s":"The nurse finally received the recognition she deserved when the city gave her an award for thirty years of service.","t":"當市政府頒獎表揚那位護士三十年的服務時，她終於獲得了應有的肯定。"},{"w":"recognize","p":"v.","d":"to know who or what someone or something is because you have seen them before","c":"認出；承認","s":"I did not recognize my old classmate at first because he had grown a beard and lost a lot of weight.","t":"我一開始沒有認出我的老同學，因為他留了鬍子，而且瘦了很多。"},{"w":"recognizable","p":"adj.","d":"easy to recognize","c":"容易辨認的","s":"The singer's voice is so recognizable that people know it is her after hearing only the first two words of a song.","t":"那位歌手的聲音非常容易辨認，人們只要聽到歌的前兩個字就知道是她。"},{"w":"in recognition of","p":"prep.","d":"as a way of showing thanks or respect for something","c":"為了表彰…","s":"The school named the new library after Mr. Chen in recognition of his forty years of teaching and his gift of ten thousand books.","t":"學校以陳先生的名字為新圖書館命名，以表彰他四十年的教學和捐贈的一萬本書。"},{"w":"recovery","p":"n.","d":"the process of getting better after an illness or injury","c":"康復；復原","s":"The doctor said her recovery would take about six weeks, so she will miss the basketball season this year.","t":"醫生說她的康復大約需要六週，所以她今年會錯過籃球賽季。","h":1},{"w":"recovery","p":"n.","d":"the process of returning to a normal state after a difficult time","c":"復甦；恢復","s":"The economic recovery after the storm was slow, and many shops along the beach did not reopen for a whole year.","t":"暴風雨後的經濟復甦很緩慢，海灘沿線的許多商店整整一年都沒有重新開業。"},{"w":"recover","p":"v.","d":"to become well again after an illness or injury; to get something back","c":"康復；取回","s":"It took my father two months to recover from the operation, but now he walks three kilometers every morning.","t":"我爸爸花了兩個月才從手術中康復，但現在他每天早上走三公里。"},{"w":"recover from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to get better after an illness, a shock, or a bad experience","c":"從…恢復","s":"The team needed a long time to recover from the painful loss in the final, but they came back stronger the next season.","t":"球隊需要很長的時間才能從決賽的痛苦失利中恢復，但下一個賽季他們變得更強了。"},{"w":"make a full recovery","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become completely well again","c":"完全康復","s":"The puppy was very weak when we found it, but the vet says it will make a full recovery if it eats well and rests.","t":"我們發現那隻小狗時牠非常虛弱，但獸醫說只要牠好好吃飯休息，就會完全康復。"},{"w":"recreation","p":"n.","d":"activities that you do for enjoyment when you are not working","c":"娛樂；休閒活動","s":"The city built a large park by the river for recreation, and families now go there to ride bikes and have picnics.","t":"市政府在河邊建了一座大公園供休閒之用，家庭們現在會去那裡騎腳踏車和野餐。","h":1},{"w":"recreational","p":"adj.","d":"done for enjoyment rather than for work","c":"休閒的；娛樂的","s":"Swimming is her favorite recreational activity, so she goes to the public pool every Saturday morning with her friends.","t":"游泳是她最喜歡的休閒活動，所以她每週六早上都和朋友去公共泳池。"},{"w":"recreation center","p":"n.phr.","d":"a public building where people can do sports and other activities for fun","c":"活動中心；休閒中心","s":"The new recreation center has a gym, a pool, and a music room, and students can use all of them for free after school.","t":"新的活動中心有健身房、游泳池和音樂教室，學生放學後可以免費使用。"},{"w":"recreate","p":"v.","d":"to make something exist or happen again","c":"重現；再現","s":"The museum tried to recreate a street from 1920s Taipei, with old shops, bicycles, and even the sounds of the market.","t":"博物館試圖重現一九二〇年代台北的一條街道，有老商店、腳踏車，甚至市場的聲音。"},{"w":"recycle","p":"v.","d":"to treat used materials so that they can be used again","c":"回收；再利用","s":"Our school asks students to recycle paper, bottles, and cans, and the money from them pays for new library books.","t":"我們學校要求學生回收紙張、瓶子和罐子，賣得的錢用來買新的圖書館藏書。","h":1},{"w":"recycling","p":"n.","d":"the process of treating used materials so they can be used again","c":"資源回收","s":"Recycling is now part of daily life in Taiwan, and the garbage truck plays music so that people know when to bring out their bags.","t":"資源回收現在是台灣日常生活的一部分，垃圾車會播放音樂讓人們知道何時把袋子拿出來。","a":"Recycling"},{"w":"recyclable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be recycled","c":"可回收的","s":"Most plastic bottles are recyclable, but you should wash them and remove the caps before putting them in the blue bin.","t":"大多數塑膠瓶是可回收的，但你應該先洗乾淨並拿掉瓶蓋，再放進藍色回收桶。"},{"w":"recycling bin","p":"n.phr.","d":"a container for things that will be recycled","c":"回收桶","s":"Please put the empty cans in the recycling bin next to the door instead of throwing them into the regular trash.","t":"請把空罐子放進門邊的回收桶，而不要丟進一般垃圾桶。"},{"w":"reduction","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something smaller or less","c":"減少；降低","s":"The city reported a 20 percent reduction in traffic accidents after it lowered the speed limit near schools.","t":"市政府報告，在調降學校附近的速限後，交通事故減少了百分之二十。","h":1},{"w":"reduce","p":"v.","d":"to make something smaller or less","c":"減少；降低","s":"To reduce the amount of sugar in your diet, try drinking water instead of soda and eating fruit instead of candy.","t":"要減少飲食中的糖分，試著以水代替汽水，以水果代替糖果。"},{"w":"price reduction","p":"n.phr.","d":"a lowering of the price of something","c":"降價","s":"The store announced a big price reduction on winter coats in March, so I finally bought the one I had wanted for months.","t":"那家店在三月宣布冬季外套大降價，所以我終於買了想要好幾個月的那一件。"},{"w":"reduced","p":"adj.","d":"smaller or less than before","c":"減少的；降價的","s":"Students can buy movie tickets at a reduced price on weekdays if they show their student ID at the counter.","t":"學生在平日出示學生證，就能以優惠價格購買電影票。"},{"w":"refer","p":"v.","d":"to mention or talk about someone or something","c":"提到；指","s":"When the teacher said \"someone in this class,\" we all knew she was referring to Jason, who had not done his homework again.","t":"當老師說「這班上的某個人」時，我們都知道她指的是又沒寫功課的傑森。","a":"referring","h":1},{"w":"reference","p":"n.","d":"a mention of something; a book or source used to find information","c":"提及；參考資料","s":"The speaker made a short reference to her childhood in Tainan, and then she talked about her work as a scientist.","t":"講者簡短地提到她在台南的童年，然後談起她身為科學家的工作。","h":1},{"w":"refer to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look at a book or document for information","c":"查閱；參考","s":"If you are not sure how to spell a word, you can always refer to the dictionary on the shelf behind you.","t":"如果你不確定一個字怎麼拼，你隨時可以查閱你身後架子上的字典。"},{"w":"refer sb to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to send someone to a person or place that can help them","c":"把某人轉介給…","s":"The family doctor decided to refer my mother to a heart specialist at the big hospital in Taipei.","t":"家庭醫生決定把我媽媽轉介給台北大醫院的心臟專科醫師。","a":"refer"},{"w":"reference","p":"n.","d":"a letter from a former teacher or boss saying that you are good at your work","c":"推薦信；推薦人","s":"When you apply for the job, you will need a reference from your teacher, so ask her for one as early as possible.","t":"當你申請那份工作時，你需要老師的推薦信，所以儘早請她幫你寫一封。"},{"w":"reference book","p":"n.phr.","d":"a book such as a dictionary that you look at for information","c":"參考書；工具書","s":"You cannot borrow a reference book from the library, but you can read it at the tables on the second floor.","t":"你不能從圖書館借出工具書，但你可以在二樓的桌子上閱讀。"},{"w":"referee","p":"n.","d":"the person who makes sure players follow the rules in a game","c":"裁判","s":"The referee blew his whistle and showed the player a red card, so the team had to finish the game with ten men.","t":"裁判吹哨並向那名球員出示紅牌，所以球隊必須以十人完成比賽。"},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to send back light, heat, or an image from a surface","c":"反射；映照","s":"The calm lake reflected the mountains so clearly that our photos looked like two pictures joined together.","t":"平靜的湖面清楚地映照出群山，我們的照片看起來就像兩張圖片接在一起。","a":"reflected","h":1},{"w":"reflection","p":"n.","d":"an image that you see in a mirror, glass, or water","c":"倒影；鏡中影像","s":"The cat saw its own reflection in the window and jumped back, thinking there was another cat outside.","t":"那隻貓看到窗戶上自己的倒影就往後跳，以為外面有另一隻貓。","h":1},{"w":"reflect","p":"v.","d":"to show or be a sign of something","c":"反映；顯示","s":"Your test scores do not always reflect how hard you have studied, so do not feel too sad about one bad grade.","t":"你的考試分數不一定能反映你有多用功，所以不要為一次不好的成績太難過。"},{"w":"reflect on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think carefully about something","c":"反思；仔細思考","s":"At the end of the year, our teacher asks us to reflect on what we have learned and what we want to do better.","t":"年底時，老師要我們反思這一年學到了什麼，以及想要改進什麼。"},{"w":"reflection","p":"n.","d":"careful thought about something","c":"反思；深思","s":"After some reflection, he decided to apologize to his friend because he realized the argument had been his fault.","t":"經過一番反思後，他決定向朋友道歉，因為他意識到那場爭吵是他的錯。"},{"w":"reflective","p":"adj.","d":"able to reflect light; thinking quietly and deeply","c":"反光的；深思的","s":"Cyclists should wear reflective clothing at night so that drivers can see them from far away on dark roads.","t":"騎自行車的人晚上應該穿反光衣物，這樣駕駛人在暗路上就能從遠處看到他們。"},{"w":"reform","p":"n.","d":"a change made to a system or law to make it better","c":"改革","s":"The new education reform means that high school students will have fewer exams and more time for group projects.","t":"新的教育改革意味著高中生會有較少的考試和較多的小組專題時間。","h":1},{"w":"reform","p":"v.","d":"to change a system or law to make it better","c":"改革；改善","s":"The government promised to reform the tax system so that rich people and large companies pay their fair share.","t":"政府承諾改革稅制，讓富人和大公司繳納公平的份額。"},{"w":"reformer","p":"n.","d":"a person who works to change and improve a system","c":"改革者","s":"She is remembered as a great reformer who fought for twenty years until every girl in the country could go to school.","t":"她被人們記得是一位偉大的改革者，奮鬥了二十年，直到全國每個女孩都能上學。"},{"w":"educational reform","p":"n.phr.","d":"changes made to improve schools and teaching","c":"教育改革","s":"Many parents welcomed the educational reform because it gave children more time for art, music, and sports at school.","t":"許多家長歡迎這項教育改革，因為它讓孩子在學校有更多時間學習美術、音樂和運動。"},{"w":"refugee","p":"n.","d":"a person who has to leave their country because of war or danger","c":"難民","s":"The refugees arrived with nothing but the clothes they were wearing, and local families offered them food and warm beds.","t":"難民抵達時除了身上穿的衣服什麼都沒有，當地家庭提供他們食物和溫暖的床。","a":"refugees","h":1},{"w":"refuge","p":"n.","d":"a safe place that protects you from danger or bad weather","c":"避難所；庇護","s":"During the typhoon, the old temple became a refuge for people whose homes were near the rising river.","t":"颱風期間，那座古廟成了住家靠近上漲河水的人們的避難所。"},{"w":"take refuge","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go somewhere safe to escape danger","c":"避難；躲避","s":"When the rain suddenly became heavy, the hikers had to take refuge in a small cave until the storm passed.","t":"當雨突然變大時，登山客不得不在一個小山洞裡避難，直到暴風雨過去。"},{"w":"refugee camp","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where refugees live, usually in tents","c":"難民營","s":"Volunteers from Taiwan spent the summer teaching English to children in a refugee camp near the border.","t":"來自台灣的志工整個夏天都在邊境附近的一座難民營教孩子們英文。"},{"w":"refund","p":"n.","d":"money that is given back to you because you are not happy with something","c":"退款","s":"The shoes were too small, so I took them back to the store and asked for a refund instead of a different size.","t":"那雙鞋太小了，所以我把它們拿回店裡，要求退款而不是換尺寸。","h":1},{"w":"refund","p":"v.","d":"to give someone their money back","c":"退還（錢）","s":"The concert was canceled because of the typhoon, and the company promised to refund every ticket within ten days.","t":"演唱會因颱風取消，公司承諾在十天內退還每一張票的錢。"},{"w":"get a refund","p":"v.phr.","d":"to receive your money back","c":"拿到退款","s":"You can get a refund only if you bring the receipt and return the item within seven days of buying it.","t":"只有在你帶著收據並在購買後七天內退回商品的情況下，才能拿到退款。"},{"w":"refundable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be given back as money","c":"可退款的","s":"The deposit for the apartment is fully refundable if you leave the rooms clean and nothing is broken.","t":"如果你把房間打掃乾淨而且沒有東西損壞，公寓的押金是全額可退還的。"},{"w":"non-refundable","p":"adj.","d":"not able to be given back as money","c":"不可退款的","s":"The cheap plane ticket is non-refundable, so think carefully before you book it, because you cannot get your money back.","t":"那張便宜的機票是不可退款的，所以訂票前要仔細考慮，因為你無法拿回錢。"},{"w":"refusal","p":"n.","d":"the act of saying that you will not do or accept something","c":"拒絕","s":"Her refusal to join the trip surprised everyone, because she had been the first person to suggest the idea.","t":"她拒絕參加這趟旅行讓大家都很驚訝，因為她是第一個提出這個主意的人。","h":1},{"w":"refuse","p":"v.","d":"to say that you will not do or accept something","c":"拒絕","s":"The little boy refused to eat his vegetables, so his mother hid the carrots inside his favorite dumplings.","t":"那個小男孩拒絕吃蔬菜，所以他媽媽把胡蘿蔔藏進他最喜歡的水餃裡。","a":"refused"},{"w":"refuse to do","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say firmly that you will not do something","c":"拒絕做…","s":"The workers refused to do the dangerous job until the company gave them helmets and safety ropes.","t":"工人們拒絕做那份危險的工作，直到公司給他們安全帽和安全繩。","a":"refused to do"},{"w":"flat refusal","p":"n.phr.","d":"a clear and direct no","c":"斷然拒絕","s":"When I asked my boss for a day off during the busiest week, I got a flat refusal, so I had to change my plans.","t":"當我在最忙的那週向老闆請一天假時，遭到斷然拒絕，所以我必須改變計畫。"},{"w":"regarding","p":"prep.","d":"about; concerning","c":"關於","s":"The principal sent a letter to all parents regarding the new rules for mobile phones, which will begin next month.","t":"校長寄了一封信給所有家長，關於下個月開始實施的手機新規定。","h":1},{"w":"regard ... as","p":"v.phr.","d":"to think of someone or something in a particular way","c":"把…視為","s":"Most people in the village regard the old doctor as a hero because he saved so many lives during the flood.","t":"村裡大多數人把那位老醫生視為英雄，因為他在水災期間救了許多人。","a":"regard"},{"w":"regard","p":"n.","d":"respect or care for someone","c":"尊重；敬重","s":"The students have great regard for their coach, who stays after practice every day to help the weaker players.","t":"學生們非常敬重他們的教練，他每天練習後都留下來幫助較弱的球員。"},{"w":"regardless of","p":"prep.","d":"without being affected by something","c":"不管；不論","s":"The marathon will take place on Sunday regardless of the weather, so bring a raincoat if the forecast says rain.","t":"馬拉松將在星期日舉行，不論天氣如何，所以如果預報說會下雨就帶件雨衣。"},{"w":"with regard to","p":"prep.","d":"about; concerning (formal)","c":"關於；至於","s":"With regard to your question about the schedule, the first class will start at nine instead of eight from next week.","t":"關於你對課表的問題，從下週起第一堂課將在九點而不是八點開始。","a":"With regard to"},{"w":"register","p":"v.","d":"to put your name on an official list","c":"登記；註冊","s":"New students must register for classes before August 20, or they will not be able to choose the courses they want.","t":"新生必須在八月二十日前登記選課，否則他們將無法選到想要的課程。","h":1},{"w":"registration","p":"n.","d":"the act of putting a name on an official list","c":"登記；註冊","s":"Registration for the summer camp opens on Monday, and the places usually fill up within the first two days.","t":"夏令營的報名將在星期一開放，名額通常在前兩天內就會額滿。","a":"Registration","h":1},{"w":"register","p":"n.","d":"an official list or book of names","c":"登記簿；名冊","s":"The hotel keeps a register of every guest, so the police could check who had stayed there on the night of the theft.","t":"飯店保有每位房客的登記簿，所以警方能查出竊案當晚誰住在那裡。"},{"w":"register for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put your name down for a course or event","c":"報名參加…","s":"I decided to register for the Japanese course at the community center because I want to travel to Tokyo next year.","t":"我決定報名參加社區中心的日文課程，因為我明年想去東京旅行。"},{"w":"registered","p":"adj.","d":"officially recorded on a list","c":"登記過的；註冊的","s":"Only registered voters can take part in the election, so make sure your name is on the list before voting day.","t":"只有登記過的選民才能參加選舉，所以在投票日前要確認你的名字在名冊上。"},{"w":"registration form","p":"n.phr.","d":"a paper or online form you fill in to put your name on a list","c":"報名表；登記表","s":"Please fill in the registration form with your name, phone number, and emergency contact, and hand it to the office by Friday.","t":"請在報名表上填寫你的姓名、電話和緊急聯絡人，並在星期五前交到辦公室。"},{"w":"regulate","p":"v.","d":"to control something by rules or laws","c":"管制；規範；調節","s":"The government plans to regulate online games more strictly so that children under twelve cannot play late at night.","t":"政府計畫更嚴格地管制線上遊戲，讓十二歲以下的兒童不能在深夜玩。","h":1},{"w":"regulation","p":"n.","d":"an official rule that controls how something is done","c":"規定；法規","s":"A new regulation says that every scooter rider must wear a helmet, and the fine for breaking it is 500 dollars.","t":"一項新規定指出每位機車騎士都必須戴安全帽，違規的罰款是五百元。","h":1},{"w":"regulator","p":"n.","d":"a person or organization that checks that rules are followed","c":"監管機構；調節器","s":"The food regulator closed the factory for a month after it found dirty water being used to wash the vegetables.","t":"食品監管機構發現該工廠用髒水洗菜後，勒令它停業一個月。"},{"w":"regular","p":"adj.","d":"happening at the same time or in the same way again and again","c":"規律的；定期的","s":"Regular exercise, such as a thirty-minute walk every day, can help you sleep better and feel less stressed.","t":"規律的運動，例如每天散步三十分鐘，可以幫助你睡得更好，壓力更小。","a":"Regular"},{"w":"regularly","p":"adv.","d":"often, at the same times or in the same way","c":"定期地；經常地","s":"My grandmother visits the doctor regularly to check her blood pressure, and she has not missed a visit in five years.","t":"我奶奶定期去看醫生檢查血壓，五年來從未錯過任何一次。"},{"w":"rules and regulations","p":"n.phr.","d":"the official rules of a place or organization","c":"規章制度","s":"Before you start working at the factory, you must read the rules and regulations and sign a paper saying you understand them.","t":"在你開始到工廠工作之前，必須先閱讀規章制度，並簽署一份表示你已了解的文件。"},{"w":"rejection","p":"n.","d":"the act of refusing to accept someone or something","c":"拒絕；退回","s":"After three years of rejection from different companies, she finally got a job offer and cried with happiness.","t":"經過三年被不同公司拒絕之後，她終於收到一份工作邀約，高興得哭了。","h":1},{"w":"reject","p":"v.","d":"to refuse to accept, believe, or use something","c":"拒絕；否決","s":"The city council decided to reject the plan for a new parking lot because the land is needed for a park.","t":"市議會決定否決興建新停車場的計畫，因為那塊地要用來蓋公園。"},{"w":"rejection letter","p":"n.phr.","d":"a letter telling you that you have not been accepted","c":"拒絕信；未錄取通知","s":"He received a rejection letter from his first-choice university, but a week later his second choice accepted him.","t":"他收到了第一志願大學的未錄取通知，但一週後他的第二志願錄取了他。"},{"w":"be rejected","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not be accepted","c":"被拒絕；遭否決","s":"Her first story was rejected by ten magazines, but she kept writing, and today her books are sold around the world.","t":"她的第一篇故事被十家雜誌拒絕，但她持續寫作，如今她的書在世界各地販售。","a":"was rejected"},{"w":"relaxation","p":"n.","d":"the activity of resting and doing things that make you feel calm","c":"放鬆；休閒","s":"For relaxation, my father likes to sit in the garden with a cup of tea and listen to the birds after dinner.","t":"為了放鬆，我爸爸喜歡晚餐後坐在花園裡喝杯茶，聽鳥叫。","h":1},{"w":"relax","p":"v.","d":"to rest and become calm and less worried","c":"放鬆","s":"After the long exam week, the students went to the beach to relax and forget about books for a few days.","t":"漫長的考試週結束後，學生們到海邊放鬆，有幾天不去想書本的事。"},{"w":"relaxed","p":"adj.","d":"calm and not worried","c":"放鬆的；輕鬆的","s":"The teacher was so relaxed and friendly that even the shyest students felt brave enough to ask questions.","t":"那位老師非常輕鬆友善，連最害羞的學生都有勇氣提問。"},{"w":"relaxing","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel calm and rested","c":"令人放鬆的","s":"A hot bath with soft music is the most relaxing way to end a busy day, according to my mother.","t":"根據我媽媽的說法，泡個熱水澡配上輕柔的音樂是結束忙碌一天最令人放鬆的方式。"}]},{"unit":34,"theme":"relevant – retain","cards":[{"w":"relevant","p":"adj.","d":"closely connected with what is being talked about","c":"相關的；切題的","s":"Please keep your questions relevant to today's topic, because we only have twenty minutes left before the bell rings.","t":"請讓你的問題與今天的主題相關，因為離鐘響只剩二十分鐘了。","h":1},{"w":"relevance","p":"n.","d":"the way something is connected to the matter being discussed","c":"相關性；關聯","s":"I don't see the relevance of your story to our discussion, so could you please explain how it is connected?","t":"我看不出你的故事和我們的討論有什麼關聯，可以請你解釋一下它們是怎麼連在一起的嗎？"},{"w":"irrelevant","p":"adj.","d":"not connected to the matter; not important here","c":"不相關的；離題的","s":"The lawyer told the witness that his comments about the weather were irrelevant and asked him to answer the question.","t":"律師告訴證人，他關於天氣的評論不相關，並要他回答問題。"},{"w":"be relevant to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be connected to or useful for something","c":"與…有關","s":"The skills you learn in this computer class are relevant to almost every job you might want to do in the future.","t":"你在這堂電腦課學到的技能與你未來可能想做的幾乎每一種工作有關。","a":"are relevant to"},{"w":"relieve","p":"v.","d":"to make pain or a bad feeling less strong","c":"緩解；減輕","s":"The doctor gave my grandmother some medicine to relieve the pain in her back, and she felt much better by the evening.","t":"醫生給我奶奶一些藥來緩解她背部的疼痛，到了晚上她覺得好多了。","h":1},{"w":"relief","p":"n.","d":"the good feeling you have when worry or pain goes away","c":"寬慰；解脫","s":"It was a great relief to hear that everyone on the bus was safe after the accident on the mountain road.","t":"聽到山路上那場事故後公車上的每個人都平安，真是一大寬慰。"},{"w":"relieved","p":"adj.","d":"feeling happy because something bad did not happen","c":"感到寬慰的；鬆了一口氣的","s":"I was so relieved when I found my lost wallet under the car seat, because all my ID cards were inside it.","t":"當我在車座下找到遺失的錢包時，我鬆了一口氣，因為我所有的證件都在裡面。"},{"w":"relieve stress","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make yourself feel less worried or tired","c":"紓解壓力","s":"Many students listen to music or play sports to relieve stress after a long week of tests and homework.","t":"許多學生在考試和作業滿滿的一週之後，會聽音樂或運動來紓解壓力。"},{"w":"to one's relief","p":"phr.","d":"used to say that someone felt better after a worry ended","c":"令某人寬慰的是","s":"To my relief, the typhoon changed direction last night and the school trip to Kenting can still take place this weekend.","t":"令我寬慰的是，颱風昨晚改變了方向，這個週末的墾丁校外教學仍然可以照常舉行。","a":"To my relief"},{"w":"reluctant","p":"adj.","d":"not wanting to do something and slow to do it","c":"不情願的；勉強的","s":"My little brother was reluctant to go to the dentist, so my mother promised him an ice cream after the visit.","t":"我弟弟不情願去看牙醫，所以我媽媽答應看完牙後給他一支冰淇淋。","h":1},{"w":"reluctantly","p":"adv.","d":"in a slow, unwilling way","c":"不情願地；勉強地","s":"He reluctantly turned off the video game and started his homework after his father warned him for the third time.","t":"在爸爸第三次警告他之後，他不情願地關掉電動，開始寫功課。"},{"w":"reluctance","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of not wanting to do something","c":"不情願；勉強","s":"The students showed great reluctance to clean the classroom on such a hot day, but the teacher insisted that they finish it.","t":"在這麼熱的天氣打掃教室，學生們表現出極大的不情願，但老師堅持要他們完成。"},{"w":"be reluctant to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not want to do something","c":"不願意…","s":"Many people are reluctant to try new food when they travel abroad, so they often end up eating at fast-food restaurants.","t":"許多人出國旅行時不願意嘗試新食物，所以他們常常最後都在速食店用餐。","a":"are reluctant to"},{"w":"remark","p":"n.","d":"something that you say; a comment","c":"評論；話語","s":"The coach made a kind remark about my hard work, and it gave me the confidence to keep practicing every day.","t":"教練對我的努力說了一句親切的評語，這給了我每天持續練習的信心。","h":1},{"w":"remarkable","p":"adj.","d":"so good or unusual that people notice it","c":"卓越的；非凡的；值得注意的","s":"It is remarkable that a twelve-year-old girl could swim across the lake, which is more than three kilometers wide.","t":"一個十二歲的女孩竟能游過這座寬度超過三公里的湖，真是了不起。","h":1},{"w":"remark","p":"v.","d":"to say something as a comment","c":"說；評論","s":"My aunt remarked that the soup needed more salt, so my father quickly added some before the guests arrived.","t":"我阿姨說湯需要多加點鹽，所以我爸爸在客人到達前趕快加了一些。","a":"remarked"},{"w":"remarkably","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is surprising or unusual","c":"非常；顯著地","s":"The weather was remarkably warm for December, so we had lunch outside in the park instead of staying indoors.","t":"以十二月來說天氣異常地溫暖，所以我們在公園戶外吃午餐，而不是待在室內。"},{"w":"make a remark","p":"v.phr.","d":"to say a comment about something","c":"發表評論","s":"It is rude to make a remark about someone's weight, even if you are only joking with a close friend.","t":"對別人的體重發表評論是不禮貌的，即使你只是在和好朋友開玩笑。"},{"w":"remedy","p":"n.","d":"a medicine or a way to make a problem better","c":"治療法；補救辦法","s":"My grandmother believes that hot ginger tea is the best remedy for a cold, and she makes it for us every winter.","t":"我奶奶相信熱薑茶是治感冒最好的療方，她每年冬天都會煮給我們喝。","h":1},{"w":"remedy","p":"v.","d":"to fix or improve a bad situation","c":"補救；改正","s":"The company promised to remedy the problem with the new phones by giving every customer a free battery.","t":"該公司承諾送每位顧客一顆免費電池，以補救新手機的問題。"},{"w":"home remedy","p":"n.phr.","d":"a simple treatment made at home, not from a doctor","c":"民間療法；居家療法","s":"Honey with lemon is a popular home remedy for a sore throat, and many families in Taiwan still use it today.","t":"蜂蜜加檸檬是治喉嚨痛很受歡迎的居家療法，台灣許多家庭至今仍在使用。"},{"w":"remedial","p":"adj.","d":"meant to help students who are behind","c":"補救的；補習的","s":"Students who failed the math test must attend remedial classes after school until their scores improve.","t":"數學考試不及格的學生必須在放學後上補救課程，直到成績進步為止。"},{"w":"renew","p":"v.","d":"to make something continue for more time; to make new again","c":"更新；續約；重新開始","s":"I need to renew my library card before Friday, or I will not be able to borrow books during the summer vacation.","t":"我需要在星期五前更新我的借書證，否則暑假期間就無法借書了。","h":1},{"w":"renewal","p":"n.","d":"the act of making something continue or new again","c":"更新；續約","s":"The renewal of your passport takes about two weeks, so please apply early if you plan to travel in July.","t":"護照換發大約需要兩週，所以如果你打算七月出國，請提早申請。"},{"w":"renewable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be replaced naturally and never used up","c":"可再生的","s":"Solar and wind power are renewable energy sources because they will never run out, unlike oil and coal.","t":"太陽能和風力是可再生的能源，因為它們永遠不會用完，不像石油和煤。"},{"w":"renewable energy","p":"n.phr.","d":"power from the sun, wind, or water that does not run out","c":"再生能源","s":"Taiwan is building more wind farms along the west coast because the government wants to use more renewable energy in the future.","t":"台灣正在西海岸興建更多風力發電場，因為政府希望未來使用更多再生能源。"},{"w":"renew a contract","p":"v.phr.","d":"to agree to continue a work or business agreement","c":"續約","s":"The basketball star decided to renew his contract with his team for three more years because he loves playing in this city.","t":"這位籃球明星決定和他的球隊再續約三年，因為他熱愛在這座城市打球。","a":"renew his contract"},{"w":"repetition","p":"n.","d":"doing or saying the same thing again and again","c":"重複","s":"Learning a new language takes a lot of repetition, so do not worry if you have to say the same word twenty times.","t":"學習新語言需要大量的重複，所以如果你得把同一個字說二十次，也不用擔心。","h":1},{"w":"repeat","p":"v.","d":"to say or do something again","c":"重複；重說","s":"Could you please repeat the address slowly, because the line is bad and I could not hear it clearly the first time?","t":"可以請你慢慢重複一次地址嗎？因為線路不好，我第一次沒有聽清楚。"},{"w":"repeated","p":"adj.","d":"happening again and again","c":"一再的；反覆的","s":"After repeated warnings from the teacher, the boy finally stopped talking and paid attention to the lesson.","t":"在老師一再警告之後，那個男孩終於停止說話，專心上課。"},{"w":"repeatedly","p":"adv.","d":"many times; again and again","c":"一再地；反覆地","s":"The little girl repeatedly asked her father when they would arrive, and he patiently answered her every time.","t":"小女孩一再地問爸爸他們什麼時候會到，而他每次都耐心地回答她。"},{"w":"repetitive","p":"adj.","d":"doing the same thing many times in a boring way","c":"重複的；單調的","s":"Working on the factory line is repetitive because you do the same simple action hundreds of times every day.","t":"在工廠生產線工作很單調重複，因為你每天要做同一個簡單動作好幾百次。"},{"w":"representation","p":"n.","d":"a picture or description that shows what something is like","c":"表現；描繪；代表","s":"The painting is a beautiful representation of life in a small fishing village a hundred years ago.","t":"這幅畫美麗地描繪了一百年前小漁村的生活。","h":1},{"w":"represent","p":"v.","d":"to act or speak for a person or group","c":"代表","s":"Two students from each class will represent our school at the city speech contest next month.","t":"每班將有兩名學生在下個月的全市演講比賽中代表我們學校。"},{"w":"representative","p":"n.","d":"a person chosen to speak or act for others","c":"代表","s":"The class chose Amy as their representative because she is good at explaining everyone's ideas to the teachers.","t":"全班選艾美當他們的代表，因為她擅長向老師說明大家的想法。"},{"w":"representative","p":"adj.","d":"typical of a group or a place","c":"有代表性的；典型的","s":"Night markets are a representative part of Taiwanese culture, so every foreign visitor should try one at least once.","t":"夜市是台灣文化中具代表性的一部分，所以每位外國遊客至少都該逛一次。"},{"w":"reputation","p":"n.","d":"the opinion people have about how good someone or something is","c":"名聲；聲譽","s":"The restaurant has a good reputation for fresh seafood, so you should book a table a week before you go.","t":"這家餐廳以新鮮海鮮享有好名聲，所以你應該在去的一週前先訂位。","h":1},{"w":"have a reputation for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be known for a certain quality","c":"以…聞名","s":"The small bakery has a reputation for the best pineapple cakes in town, and tourists line up outside it every morning.","t":"這家小麵包店以鎮上最好吃的鳳梨酥聞名，每天早上都有遊客在外面排隊。","a":"has a reputation for"},{"w":"reputable","p":"adj.","d":"known to be good and honest","c":"聲譽良好的","s":"Buy your laptop from a reputable store so that you can get good service if something goes wrong with it later.","t":"請在聲譽良好的商店購買筆電，這樣日後出問題時才能得到好的服務。"},{"w":"ruin one's reputation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to destroy the good opinion people have of someone","c":"毀掉某人的名聲","s":"One careless post on social media can ruin your reputation in a single day, so think carefully before you click \"share.\"","t":"社群媒體上一則不小心的貼文可能在一天之內毀掉你的名聲，所以按下「分享」前要仔細想清楚。","a":"ruin your reputation"},{"w":"rescue","p":"v.","d":"to save someone from danger","c":"救援；營救","s":"Firefighters worked for six hours to rescue the workers who were trapped under the fallen building after the earthquake.","t":"消防員努力了六個小時，營救地震後被困在倒塌建築下的工人。","h":1},{"w":"rescue","p":"n.","d":"the act of saving someone from danger","c":"救援","s":"The rescue of the lost hikers took all night because heavy fog made it hard for the helicopter to see them.","t":"對迷路登山客的救援花了一整夜，因為濃霧讓直升機很難看到他們。"},{"w":"come to sb's rescue","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help someone who is in trouble","c":"前來救援；解圍","s":"When my bike broke down on the mountain road, a kind farmer came to my rescue and drove me back to town in his truck.","t":"當我的腳踏車在山路上壞掉時，一位好心的農夫前來救我，用他的卡車載我回鎮上。","a":"came to my rescue"},{"w":"rescue team","p":"n.phr.","d":"a group of people trained to save others","c":"救難隊","s":"A rescue team with trained dogs arrived at the village early in the morning to search for people under the mud.","t":"一支帶著搜救犬的救難隊一大早抵達村莊，搜尋泥土下的人。"},{"w":"research","p":"n.","d":"careful study to find out new facts","c":"研究","s":"Scientists are doing research on how sleep affects memory, and their early results show that teenagers need at least eight hours.","t":"科學家正在進行睡眠如何影響記憶的研究，初步結果顯示青少年至少需要八小時的睡眠。","h":1},{"w":"researcher","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to study something carefully","c":"研究員；研究人員","s":"My cousin works as a researcher at a university lab, where she studies how plants grow in very dry places.","t":"我表姐在大學實驗室擔任研究員，她在那裡研究植物如何在非常乾燥的地方生長。","h":1},{"w":"research","p":"v.","d":"to study something carefully to learn about it","c":"研究；調查","s":"Before you buy a used car, you should research its history online to make sure it has never been in a serious accident.","t":"在購買二手車之前，你應該上網調查它的歷史，確認它從未發生過嚴重事故。"},{"w":"do research on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to study a subject carefully","c":"做…的研究","s":"For our science project, we decided to do research on the water quality of the river that runs behind our school.","t":"為了我們的科學專題，我們決定研究流經學校後方那條河的水質。"},{"w":"research paper","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long piece of writing that reports a study","c":"研究論文；研究報告","s":"Every senior student must write a research paper on a topic they choose, and the best ones are printed in the school magazine.","t":"每位高三學生都必須就自選的題目寫一篇研究報告，最好的幾篇會刊登在校刊上。"},{"w":"resemble","p":"v.","d":"to look like or be similar to someone or something","c":"像；類似","s":"My little sister resembles our mother so much that people often think they are looking at an old photo of Mom.","t":"我妹妹非常像我們的媽媽，人們常以為他們看到的是媽媽的舊照片。","a":"resembles","h":1},{"w":"resemblance","p":"n.","d":"the fact of looking like someone or something","c":"相似；相像","s":"There is a strong resemblance between the two paintings, so experts believe they were made by the same artist.","t":"這兩幅畫之間有強烈的相似之處，所以專家認為它們出自同一位畫家。"},{"w":"bear a resemblance to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look like something or someone","c":"與…相似","s":"The new shopping mall bears a resemblance to a giant ship, which is why people in the city call it \"the boat.\"","t":"這座新購物中心很像一艘巨大的船，這就是為什麼城裡的人叫它「那艘船」。","a":"bears a resemblance to"},{"w":"reservation","p":"n.","d":"an arrangement to keep a seat, room, or table for you","c":"預訂；預約","s":"I made a reservation for four people at the Italian restaurant, so we should arrive there before seven o'clock.","t":"我在那家義大利餐廳訂了四個人的位子，所以我們應該在七點前到達那裡。","h":1},{"w":"reserve","p":"v.","d":"to arrange to keep something for a later time","c":"預訂；保留","s":"You can reserve a seat on the train through the app, which saves you from waiting in line at the station.","t":"你可以透過 App預訂火車座位，這樣就不用在車站排隊等候了。"},{"w":"reserved","p":"adj.","d":"kept for a particular person or purpose","c":"已預訂的；保留的","s":"Those front seats are reserved for the parents of the graduates, so please find a place in the rows behind them.","t":"前排那些座位是保留給畢業生家長的，所以請在後面幾排找位子。"},{"w":"make a reservation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to book a table, room, or seat ahead of time","c":"預訂；訂位","s":"If you want to eat at that famous hot-pot place on Saturday, you must make a reservation at least a week ahead.","t":"如果你想在星期六去那家有名的火鍋店吃飯，你必須至少提前一週訂位。"},{"w":"reservation","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of doubt about a plan or idea","c":"保留；疑慮","s":"I have some reservations about the plan, because it costs a lot of money and nobody has tried it before.","t":"我對這個計畫有些疑慮，因為它要花很多錢，而且以前沒有人試過。","a":"reservations"},{"w":"resign","p":"v.","d":"to leave your job by telling your boss","c":"辭職","s":"After ten years at the company, Mr. Lin decided to resign and open a small coffee shop near the beach.","t":"在公司待了十年後，林先生決定辭職，在海邊附近開一家小咖啡店。","h":1},{"w":"resignation","p":"n.","d":"the act of leaving a job; the letter that says you are leaving","c":"辭職；辭呈","s":"The manager handed in her resignation on Monday, and the whole office was surprised because she had seemed so happy.","t":"經理星期一遞交了辭呈，整個辦公室都很驚訝，因為她看起來一直很開心。","h":1},{"w":"resign from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave a particular job or position","c":"從…辭職","s":"He plans to resign from his job as a bank clerk next month so that he can take care of his sick father.","t":"他打算下個月辭去銀行職員的工作，以便照顧生病的父親。"},{"w":"resign oneself to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to accept something bad because you cannot change it","c":"聽天由命；無奈地接受","s":"When the last bus left without us, we resigned ourselves to walking home in the rain for over an hour.","t":"當末班公車沒載到我們就開走時，我們只好無奈地接受在雨中走一個多小時回家。","a":"resigned ourselves to"},{"w":"resistance","p":"n.","d":"the act of fighting against or refusing something","c":"反抗；抵抗；阻力","s":"The new rule about school uniforms met with strong resistance from students, who said they wanted to choose their own clothes.","t":"新的校服規定遭到學生強烈反抗，他們說想要自己選擇衣服。","h":1},{"w":"resist","p":"v.","d":"to fight against something; to stop yourself from doing something","c":"抵抗；忍住","s":"I could not resist the smell of fresh bread from the bakery, so I bought two loaves on my way home.","t":"我無法抗拒麵包店飄來的新鮮麵包香味，所以回家路上買了兩條。"},{"w":"resistant","p":"adj.","d":"not easily hurt or changed by something","c":"抵抗的；耐…的","s":"This new phone is resistant to water and dust, so you do not have to worry about using it on the beach.","t":"這支新手機耐水又耐灰塵，所以你不用擔心在海灘上使用它。"},{"w":"resist the temptation","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop yourself from doing something you want to do","c":"抵抗誘惑","s":"It is hard to resist the temptation to check your phone when you study, so put it in another room until you finish.","t":"讀書時很難抵抗查看手機的誘惑，所以把它放到另一個房間，直到你讀完為止。"},{"w":"resolution","p":"n.","d":"a firm decision to do something","c":"決心；決議","s":"Every January, my father makes a New Year's resolution to exercise more, but he usually gives up before March.","t":"每年一月，我爸爸都會立下多運動的新年決心，但他通常在三月前就放棄了。","h":1},{"w":"resolve","p":"v.","d":"to find an answer to a problem or an argument","c":"解決","s":"The two neighbors finally agreed to resolve their argument about the fence by talking to each other calmly.","t":"這兩位鄰居終於同意透過冷靜地對談來解決他們對圍籬的爭執。","h":1},{"w":"resolve","p":"n.","d":"strong determination to do something","c":"決心","s":"Losing the first game only made the team's resolve stronger, and they won every match for the rest of the season.","t":"輸掉第一場比賽只讓球隊的決心更堅定，他們在本季剩下的每場比賽都獲勝。"},{"w":"resolution","p":"n.","d":"the act of solving a problem or ending a disagreement","c":"解決；化解","s":"Both sides hope to find a peaceful resolution to the problem before it turns into a bigger fight.","t":"雙方都希望在問題演變成更大的衝突前，找到和平的解決方法。"},{"w":"resolve to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to decide firmly that you will do something","c":"下定決心…","s":"After failing the test twice, she resolved to study English for an hour every single day until she passed.","t":"考試兩次不及格之後，她下定決心每天讀一小時英文，直到通過為止。","a":"resolved to"},{"w":"resolute","p":"adj.","d":"very determined and not changing your mind","c":"堅決的；堅定的","s":"The young nurse remained resolute in her decision to help in the countryside, even though her parents wanted her to stay.","t":"這位年輕護士對到鄉下服務的決定仍然很堅定，即使她的父母希望她留下來。"},{"w":"respectable","p":"adj.","d":"good enough to be respected by people","c":"可敬的；體面的","s":"Mr. Wang is a respectable businessman who has given money to the local school for over twenty years.","t":"王先生是一位可敬的商人，二十多年來一直捐錢給當地的學校。","h":1},{"w":"respectful","p":"adj.","d":"showing respect to others; polite","c":"恭敬的；有禮貌的","s":"Students should be respectful to their teachers, but good teachers also treat their students with the same respect.","t":"學生應該對老師恭敬，但好老師也會以同樣的尊重對待學生。","h":1},{"w":"respect","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that someone is important and should be admired","c":"尊敬；尊重","s":"I have great respect for doctors who work through the night to save the lives of people they have never met.","t":"我非常敬佩那些徹夜工作、拯救素未謀面的人的生命的醫生。"},{"w":"respect","p":"v.","d":"to admire someone; to treat something as important","c":"尊重；尊敬","s":"We should respect other people's opinions even when we do not agree with them, especially during class discussions.","t":"即使我們不同意別人的意見，也應該尊重，尤其是在課堂討論時。"},{"w":"disrespectful","p":"adj.","d":"rude; not showing respect","c":"無禮的；不尊重的","s":"It is disrespectful to play with your phone while someone older is talking to you, so put it away during dinner.","t":"長輩跟你說話時玩手機是不禮貌的，所以晚餐時請把手機收起來。"},{"w":"show respect for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to act in a way that shows you admire someone","c":"對…表示尊重","s":"In Taiwan, people show respect for their elders by letting them sit first and serving them food before everyone else.","t":"在台灣，人們讓長輩先坐、先為他們夾菜，以此表示對長輩的尊重。"},{"w":"restore","p":"v.","d":"to bring something back to the way it was before","c":"恢復；修復","s":"Workers are trying to restore electricity to the mountain villages after the typhoon blew down the power lines last night.","t":"颱風昨晚吹倒電線後，工人正努力恢復山區村莊的供電。","h":1},{"w":"restoration","p":"n.","d":"the work of repairing something old so it looks new again","c":"修復；恢復","s":"The restoration of the old temple took five years, but now its colors look as bright as they did two hundred years ago.","t":"這座古廟的修復花了五年，但現在它的色彩看起來和兩百年前一樣鮮豔。"},{"w":"restore order","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a place calm and under control again","c":"恢復秩序","s":"The police arrived quickly to restore order after the concert crowd pushed through the gates and knocked down the fences.","t":"演唱會人潮衝過閘門、推倒圍欄後，警察迅速趕到恢復秩序。"},{"w":"restriction","p":"n.","d":"a rule that limits what you can do","c":"限制；規定","s":"There is a weight restriction of twenty kilograms for each bag on this flight, so you may have to pay extra for the second one.","t":"這班飛機每件行李有二十公斤的重量限制，所以你的第二件行李可能要額外付費。","h":1},{"w":"restrict","p":"v.","d":"to limit something; to keep it small","c":"限制","s":"Doctors advise parents to restrict screen time to one hour a day for children under the age of six.","t":"醫生建議家長把六歲以下兒童的螢幕時間限制在每天一小時。"},{"w":"restricted","p":"adj.","d":"limited; open only to certain people","c":"受限的；限制進入的","s":"This is a restricted area, so only workers with a special card are allowed to enter the building after dark.","t":"這是一個管制區域，所以天黑後只有持特殊通行證的工作人員才能進入大樓。"},{"w":"restrictive","p":"adj.","d":"limiting people too much","c":"限制性的；過於嚴格的","s":"Some students think the school's rules about hair are too restrictive, and they have asked the principal to change them.","t":"有些學生認為學校關於髮型的規定太嚴格，他們已經要求校長修改。"},{"w":"retain","p":"v.","d":"to keep something; to continue to have it","c":"保留；保持","s":"Even after living abroad for thirty years, my uncle has managed to retain his Taiwanese accent and his love of stinky tofu.","t":"即使在國外住了三十年，我叔叔仍然保留著他的台灣口音和對臭豆腐的熱愛。","h":1},{"w":"retention","p":"n.","d":"the ability to keep or remember something","c":"保留；記憶力","s":"Reading aloud improves your retention of new words, so try saying each one three times before you move on.","t":"朗讀可以提高你對新單字的記憶，所以在往下學之前，試著把每個字說三遍。"},{"w":"retain heat","p":"v.phr.","d":"to keep something warm for a long time","c":"保溫","s":"This cup is made of a special material that can retain heat for six hours, so your coffee stays warm all morning.","t":"這個杯子用一種能保溫六小時的特殊材料製成，所以你的咖啡整個早上都是溫的。"}]},{"unit":35,"theme":"retirement – scoop","cards":[{"w":"retire","p":"v.","d":"to stop working because you have reached a certain age","c":"退休","s":"My grandfather plans to retire from his job at the post office next year, and he wants to spend more time fishing.","t":"我爺爺打算明年從郵局的工作退休，他想花更多時間釣魚。","h":1},{"w":"retirement","p":"n.","d":"the time of life after you stop working","c":"退休；退休生活","s":"After forty years of teaching, Mrs. Lee is looking forward to her retirement, when she can finally travel around the world.","t":"教了四十年書之後，李老師很期待她的退休生活，到時她終於可以環遊世界。"},{"w":"retired","p":"adj.","d":"no longer working because of age","c":"退休的","s":"Our neighbor is a retired police officer, so he still gets up at five every morning and takes a long walk.","t":"我們的鄰居是一位退休的警察，所以他仍然每天早上五點起床，去散很久的步。"},{"w":"retirement home","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where old people live and are cared for","c":"養老院；安養中心","s":"My great-aunt moved into a retirement home last year, where nurses help her with meals and she has many new friends.","t":"我的姑婆去年搬進了一間養老院，那裡有護士幫她準備餐點，她也交了許多新朋友。"},{"w":"retirement age","p":"n.phr.","d":"the age at which people usually stop working","c":"退休年齡","s":"In many countries the retirement age is sixty-five, but some people choose to keep working because they enjoy their jobs.","t":"在許多國家，退休年齡是六十五歲，但有些人因為喜歡自己的工作而選擇繼續工作。"},{"w":"retreat","p":"v.","d":"to move back or away from danger","c":"撤退；退避","s":"When the storm got worse, the climbers decided to retreat to the camp at the bottom of the mountain and wait.","t":"當暴風雨變得更強時，登山者決定撤退到山腳下的營地等候。","h":1},{"w":"retreat","p":"n.","d":"the act of moving back from danger; a quiet place to rest","c":"撤退；靜修處","s":"The army's retreat across the river saved thousands of soldiers, although they had to leave their heavy guns behind.","t":"軍隊渡河撤退救了數千名士兵，儘管他們不得不丟下沉重的大砲。"},{"w":"beat a retreat","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave a place quickly to avoid trouble","c":"趕緊撤退；溜走","s":"As soon as the big dog started barking, the two boys beat a retreat and ran back to the safety of the street.","t":"大狗一開始吠叫，兩個男孩就趕緊撤退，跑回安全的街上。"},{"w":"reunion","p":"n.","d":"a meeting of people who have not seen each other for a long time","c":"團聚；重聚","s":"Every Lunar New Year, my whole family has a big reunion at my grandmother's house, and more than thirty people come.","t":"每年農曆新年，我們全家人都會在奶奶家舉行盛大的團聚，來的人超過三十位。","h":1},{"w":"reunite","p":"v.","d":"to bring people together again after a long time","c":"使重聚；使團圓","s":"The lost dog was finally reunited with its owner after a kind student found it and posted a photo online.","t":"一位好心的學生找到那隻走失的狗並在網路上貼了照片後，牠終於和主人重聚了。","a":"reunited"},{"w":"class reunion","p":"n.phr.","d":"a party for people who were in the same class at school","c":"同學會","s":"At our class reunion last month, I was surprised to see that my quiet classmate had become a famous singer.","t":"在上個月的同學會上，我很驚訝地發現我那位安靜的同學已經成了知名歌手。"},{"w":"family reunion","p":"n.phr.","d":"a gathering of all the members of a family","c":"家庭團聚","s":"The Mid-Autumn Festival is a time for family reunion, so trains and highways are always crowded with people going home.","t":"中秋節是家庭團聚的時刻，所以火車和高速公路總是擠滿了返鄉的人。"},{"w":"revenge","p":"n.","d":"something you do to hurt someone because they hurt you","c":"復仇；報復","s":"The movie is about a man who seeks revenge on the people who destroyed his family's farm twenty years ago.","t":"這部電影講的是一個男人向二十年前毀掉他家農場的人報仇的故事。","h":1},{"w":"take revenge on","p":"v.phr.","d":"to hurt someone because they hurt you first","c":"向…報仇","s":"She wanted to take revenge on the classmate who had spread lies about her, but her mother told her to forgive him instead.","t":"她想向那個散播關於她的謊言的同學報仇，但媽媽告訴她應該原諒他。"},{"w":"revenge","p":"v.","d":"to punish someone for a wrong done to you or your family","c":"替…報仇","s":"In the old story, the young prince swore to revenge his father's death, and he trained with a sword for years.","t":"在那個古老的故事裡，年輕的王子發誓要為父親的死報仇，他練了多年的劍。"},{"w":"out of revenge","p":"phr.","d":"because you want to hurt someone back","c":"出於報復","s":"The angry worker broke the office windows out of revenge after the company fired him without giving any reason.","t":"公司沒給任何理由就解雇他之後，那名憤怒的員工出於報復打破了辦公室的窗戶。"},{"w":"revise","p":"v.","d":"to change something to make it better or more correct","c":"修訂；修改","s":"The teacher asked me to revise my essay because some of my ideas were good but the order of the paragraphs was confusing.","t":"老師要我修改作文，因為我有些想法不錯，但段落的順序令人困惑。","h":1},{"w":"revision","p":"n.","d":"a change made to make something better; a new version","c":"修訂；修改；修訂版","s":"The second revision of the book fixed many mistakes, and the new edition will be in stores next spring.","t":"這本書的第二次修訂改正了許多錯誤，新版明年春天就會在書店上架。","h":1},{"w":"revised","p":"adj.","d":"changed and improved","c":"修訂過的；更新的","s":"Please check the revised schedule on the school website, because the sports day has been moved to Friday.","t":"請查看學校網站上修訂後的時間表，因為運動會已改到星期五。"},{"w":"make revisions","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make changes to improve a piece of writing","c":"做修改","s":"Writers often make revisions to their stories many times before the book is finally printed and sold.","t":"作家在書最終印刷出售之前，常常會對故事做許多次修改。"},{"w":"revolution","p":"n.","d":"a time when people change the government by force; a complete change","c":"革命；大變革","s":"The French Revolution of 1789 changed the country forever, and people still celebrate it every July.","t":"一七八九年的法國大革命永遠改變了這個國家，人們至今每年七月仍會慶祝它。","a":"Revolution","h":1},{"w":"revolutionary","p":"adj.","d":"completely new and causing great change","c":"革命性的","s":"The smartphone was a revolutionary invention because it put a camera, a map, and a phone into one small device.","t":"智慧型手機是一項革命性的發明，因為它把相機、地圖和電話放進了一個小小的裝置裡。","h":1},{"w":"revolutionary","p":"n.","d":"a person who fights to change the government","c":"革命分子；革命者","s":"The museum tells the story of a young revolutionary who fought to end the king's rule and give power to the people.","t":"這座博物館講述一位年輕革命者的故事，他為了結束國王的統治、把權力交給人民而奮鬥。"},{"w":"revolve","p":"v.","d":"to move in a circle around something","c":"旋轉；繞轉","s":"The earth takes one year to revolve around the sun, which is why we have four different seasons.","t":"地球繞太陽轉一圈需要一年，這就是為什麼我們有四個不同的季節。"},{"w":"revolutionize","p":"v.","d":"to change something completely","c":"徹底改變","s":"The internet has revolutionized the way we shop, since we can now buy almost anything without leaving our homes.","t":"網路徹底改變了我們購物的方式，因為現在我們不用出門幾乎什麼都能買到。","a":"revolutionized"},{"w":"industrial revolution","p":"n.phr.","d":"the time in history when machines and factories changed work","c":"工業革命","s":"During the Industrial Revolution, many farmers moved to the cities to work in the new factories that were built there.","t":"在工業革命期間，許多農民搬到城市，到那裡新建的工廠工作。","a":"Industrial Revolution"},{"w":"reward","p":"n.","d":"something good you get for doing something well or helpful","c":"報酬；獎賞；酬金","s":"The police are offering a reward of fifty thousand dollars to anyone who can help them find the stolen painting.","t":"警方提供五萬元的酬金給任何能幫助他們找到被偷畫作的人。","h":1},{"w":"reward","p":"v.","d":"to give someone something good for what they have done","c":"獎勵；酬謝","s":"My parents promised to reward me with a trip to Japan if I could get into my first-choice university.","t":"我父母答應，如果我能考上第一志願的大學，就獎勵我去日本旅行。"},{"w":"rewarding","p":"adj.","d":"giving you a good feeling because it is useful or important","c":"有意義的；值得做的","s":"Teaching children to read is hard work, but my aunt says it is the most rewarding job she has ever had.","t":"教孩子閱讀是件辛苦的工作，但我阿姨說這是她做過最有意義的工作。"},{"w":"as a reward for","p":"phr.","d":"as a prize or thanks for something","c":"作為…的獎賞","s":"The teacher gave the class a pizza party as a reward for their excellent behavior during the school trip.","t":"老師辦了一場披薩派對，作為全班在校外教學期間表現優良的獎賞。"},{"w":"rhyme","p":"n.","d":"a word that ends with the same sound as another; a short poem with such words","c":"押韻；韻腳；押韻短詩","s":"Little children learn words faster when the words are in a rhyme, which is why so many songs are written for them.","t":"小孩子在字詞押韻時學得比較快，這就是為什麼有這麼多歌是為他們寫的。","h":1},{"w":"rhyme","p":"v.","d":"to end with the same sound as another word","c":"押韻","s":"In this poem, \"night\" is supposed to rhyme with \"light,\" so please read the two lines again and listen to the sound.","t":"在這首詩裡，night 應該和 light押韻，所以請再讀一次這兩行，聽聽它們的聲音。"},{"w":"nursery rhyme","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short old song or poem for young children","c":"童謠","s":"\"Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star\" is a famous nursery rhyme that almost every child in the world can sing.","t":"〈一閃一閃亮晶晶〉是一首著名的童謠，世界上幾乎每個孩子都會唱。"},{"w":"rhythm","p":"n.","d":"a regular repeated pattern of sounds or movements","c":"節奏；韻律","s":"The drummer kept a steady rhythm while the dancers moved across the stage in their bright costumes.","t":"鼓手保持穩定的節奏，舞者們穿著鮮豔的服裝在舞台上移動。","h":1},{"w":"rhythmic","p":"adj.","d":"having a regular repeated pattern","c":"有節奏的","s":"The rhythmic sound of the waves on the beach made me so sleepy that I fell asleep under the umbrella.","t":"海灘上有節奏的海浪聲讓我好想睡，結果我在傘下睡著了。"},{"w":"rhythmically","p":"adv.","d":"in a regular repeated pattern","c":"有節奏地","s":"The children clapped rhythmically to the music while the teacher played the piano and sang the song.","t":"老師彈鋼琴唱歌時，孩子們隨著音樂有節奏地拍手。"},{"w":"have a good sense of rhythm","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be able to feel and follow the beat of music easily","c":"節奏感很好","s":"My cousin has a good sense of rhythm, so she picked up the new dance after watching the video only twice.","t":"我表妹節奏感很好，所以她只看了兩次影片就學會了新舞步。","a":"has a good sense of rhythm"},{"w":"riddle","p":"n.","d":"a question that is hard to answer and is asked as a game","c":"謎語","s":"My little brother loves asking me the same riddle: \"What has hands but cannot clap?\" The answer is a clock.","t":"我弟弟很愛問我同一個謎語：「什麼東西有手卻不能拍手？」答案是時鐘。","h":1},{"w":"solve a riddle","p":"v.phr.","d":"to find the answer to a riddle","c":"解謎；猜出謎語","s":"It took the whole class ten minutes to solve the riddle that the teacher had written on the board.","t":"全班花了十分鐘才猜出老師寫在黑板上的那個謎語。","a":"solve the riddle"},{"w":"speak in riddles","p":"v.phr.","d":"to talk in a way that is hard to understand","c":"說話打啞謎","s":"Please stop speaking in riddles and just tell me clearly whether you are coming to the party or not.","t":"請別再打啞謎了，直接清楚告訴我你到底來不來參加派對。","a":"speaking in riddles"},{"w":"robber","p":"n.","d":"a person who steals money or things, often using force","c":"強盜；搶匪","s":"The robber ran out of the bank with a bag of money, but the police caught him two streets away.","t":"那名搶匪帶著一袋錢跑出銀行，但警察在兩條街外就抓到了他。","h":1},{"w":"rob","p":"v.","d":"to steal money or things from a person or place","c":"搶劫；盜取","s":"Two men tried to rob the convenience store at midnight, but the brave clerk pressed the alarm button right away.","t":"兩名男子半夜試圖搶劫便利商店，但勇敢的店員立刻按下了警鈴。"},{"w":"robbery","p":"n.","d":"the crime of stealing from a person or place","c":"搶案；搶劫","s":"There was a robbery at the jewelry shop last night, and the thieves took rings worth over a million dollars.","t":"珠寶店昨晚發生了一起搶案，小偷拿走了價值超過一百萬元的戒指。"},{"w":"rob sb of sth","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take something from someone by force","c":"搶走某人的…","s":"The thief tried to rob her of her purse and phone while she was waiting for the bus in the dark.","t":"她在黑暗中等公車時，小偷試圖搶走她的皮包和手機。","a":"rob her of"},{"w":"romance","p":"n.","d":"a love story; a relationship between two people in love","c":"愛情；戀愛；愛情故事","s":"My grandparents' romance began in 1965 when they met on a crowded train from Taipei to Kaohsiung.","t":"我祖父母的愛情始於一九六五年，當時他們在一班從台北到高雄的擁擠火車上相遇。","h":1},{"w":"romantic","p":"adj.","d":"connected with love; showing feelings of love","c":"浪漫的；愛情的","s":"He planned a romantic dinner on the beach with candles and soft music to celebrate their tenth anniversary.","t":"他在海灘上安排了一頓有蠟燭和輕柔音樂的浪漫晚餐，來慶祝他們結婚十週年。"},{"w":"romance novel","p":"n.phr.","d":"a book about a love story","c":"愛情小說","s":"My sister reads a new romance novel every week, and she always cries at the happy ending.","t":"我姐姐每週都讀一本新的愛情小說，而且她總是在快樂的結局時哭。"},{"w":"romantically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way connected with love","c":"在愛情方面；浪漫地","s":"The two singers were romantically linked in the news for months, but they said they were only good friends.","t":"這兩位歌手被新聞傳了好幾個月的戀情，但他們說自己只是好朋友。"},{"w":"route","p":"n.","d":"the way you go from one place to another","c":"路線","s":"The bus takes a longer route on weekends because it stops at the night market and the river park.","t":"這班公車週末走比較長的路線，因為它會停夜市和河濱公園。","h":1},{"w":"route","p":"v.","d":"to send something or someone along a particular way","c":"按特定路線發送；引導","s":"Because of the road work, the police will route all traffic through the old part of town this weekend.","t":"由於道路施工，警方這個週末會把所有車流引導到舊城區通行。"},{"w":"take a route","p":"v.phr.","d":"to travel along a particular way","c":"走…路線","s":"We decided to take a route along the coast instead of the highway so that we could enjoy the view of the ocean.","t":"我們決定走沿海的路線而不是高速公路，這樣就能欣賞海景。"},{"w":"en route","p":"phr.","d":"on the way to a place","c":"在途中","s":"The package is en route to your house right now, and the delivery man will call you when he arrives.","t":"包裹現在正在送往你家的途中，送貨員到達時會打電話給你。"},{"w":"ruin","p":"v.","d":"to spoil or destroy something completely","c":"毀掉；破壞","s":"Please do not tell me the ending of the movie, or you will ruin it for me before I even see it.","t":"請不要告訴我電影的結局，不然你會在我看之前就把它毀了。","h":1},{"w":"ruin","p":"n.","d":"the state of having lost all your money; complete destruction","c":"毀滅；破產","s":"The company faced ruin after its biggest customer stopped buying, and two hundred workers lost their jobs.","t":"這家公司在最大的客戶停止購買後面臨破產，兩百名員工失去了工作。"},{"w":"ruins","p":"n.","d":"the parts of a building or city that are left after it is destroyed","c":"廢墟；遺跡","s":"Tourists come from all over the world to walk among the ruins of the old city, which was destroyed by an earthquake.","t":"遊客從世界各地前來，漫步在這座被地震摧毀的古城遺跡之中。"},{"w":"in ruins","p":"phr.","d":"badly damaged or destroyed","c":"成為廢墟；毀壞殆盡","s":"After the fire, the old wooden temple lay in ruins, and the villagers cried when they saw the black walls.","t":"火災之後，那座古老的木造寺廟成了廢墟，村民看到燒黑的牆壁時都哭了。"},{"w":"ruined","p":"adj.","d":"destroyed or badly damaged","c":"毀壞的；荒廢的","s":"The ruined castle on the hill is a popular place for photos, even though only two of its walls are still standing.","t":"山丘上那座荒廢的城堡是個熱門的拍照地點，儘管它只剩下兩面牆還立著。"},{"w":"rural","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the countryside, not the city","c":"鄉村的；農村的","s":"Life in a rural area is quieter than in the city, but you may have to drive thirty minutes to buy groceries.","t":"鄉村地區的生活比城市安靜，但你可能得開三十分鐘的車才能買到日用品。","h":1},{"w":"rural area","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place in the countryside","c":"鄉村地區","s":"Doctors are needed in many rural areas of Taiwan, so the government offers extra money to those who work there.","t":"台灣許多鄉村地區都需要醫生，所以政府提供額外津貼給在那裡工作的醫生。","a":"rural areas"},{"w":"rural life","p":"n.phr.","d":"the way people live in the countryside","c":"鄉村生活","s":"Many young people leave rural life behind to find jobs in Taipei, but some return home later to take over their family farms.","t":"許多年輕人離開鄉村生活到台北找工作，但有些人後來會回家接手家裡的農場。"},{"w":"rusty","p":"adj.","d":"covered with rust; old and damaged by water","c":"生鏽的","s":"The old bicycle in the garage is so rusty that the wheels will not turn, so we should throw it away.","t":"車庫裡那台舊腳踏車鏽得連輪子都轉不動，所以我們應該把它丟掉。","h":1},{"w":"rust","p":"n.","d":"the red-brown material that forms on wet iron","c":"鏽","s":"If you leave your tools outside in the rain, rust will form on them and they will become useless.","t":"如果你把工具留在外面淋雨，它們會長鏽，然後就不能用了。"},{"w":"rust","p":"v.","d":"to become covered with rust","c":"生鏽","s":"Iron chairs will rust quickly near the sea because the salty air eats away at the metal day after day.","t":"鐵椅在海邊很快就會生鏽，因為帶鹽的空氣日復一日地侵蝕金屬。"},{"w":"rusty","p":"adj.","d":"not as good as before because you have not practiced","c":"生疏的","s":"My French is a little rusty because I have not used it since I finished college ten years ago.","t":"我的法文有點生疏了，因為我十年前大學畢業後就沒再用過。"},{"w":"sacrifice","p":"n.","d":"giving up something important to help someone or get something better","c":"犧牲","s":"My parents made many sacrifices so that my sister and I could go to good schools and study abroad.","t":"我父母做出了許多犧牲，好讓我和姐姐能上好學校並出國留學。","a":"sacrifices","h":1},{"w":"sacrifice","p":"v.","d":"to give up something important for a good reason","c":"犧牲","s":"The young firefighter was willing to sacrifice his own safety to carry the old man out of the burning house.","t":"年輕的消防員願意犧牲自己的安全，把老人從著火的房子裡背出來。"},{"w":"make a sacrifice","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give up something you want in order to get something more important","c":"做出犧牲","s":"To win the gold medal, the swimmer had to make a sacrifice: she gave up parties, late nights, and even her favorite desserts.","t":"為了贏得金牌，這位游泳選手必須做出犧牲：她放棄了派對、熬夜，甚至是她最愛的甜點。"},{"w":"self-sacrifice","p":"n.","d":"giving up your own needs to help others","c":"自我犧牲","s":"The nurse's self-sacrifice during the long outbreak last year earned her the respect of everyone in the whole hospital.","t":"這位護士在去年漫長的疫情期間的自我犧牲，為她贏得了全醫院每個人的尊敬。"},{"w":"satellite","p":"n.","d":"a machine sent into space that moves around the earth","c":"人造衛星","s":"Weather satellites high above the earth send pictures of clouds to scientists, who use them to predict typhoons.","t":"高掛在地球上空的氣象衛星把雲層的照片傳給科學家，他們用這些照片來預測颱風。","a":"satellites","h":1},{"w":"satellite TV","p":"n.phr.","d":"television programs sent through a satellite","c":"衛星電視","s":"My uncle's house in the mountains has satellite TV, so he can watch football games from Europe late at night.","t":"我叔叔山上的房子有衛星電視，所以他可以在深夜收看歐洲的足球比賽。"},{"w":"satellite","p":"n.","d":"a natural object, like the moon, that moves around a planet","c":"衛星（天體）","s":"The moon is the earth's only natural satellite, and it takes about twenty-seven days to go around our planet once.","t":"月球是地球唯一的天然衛星，它繞我們的星球一圈大約需要二十七天。"},{"w":"by satellite","p":"phr.","d":"sent through a satellite in space","c":"透過衛星","s":"The concert was broadcast by satellite to more than fifty countries, so fans everywhere could watch it live.","t":"這場演唱會透過衛星轉播到五十多個國家，所以世界各地的歌迷都能即時收看。"},{"w":"satisfaction","p":"n.","d":"the good feeling you have when you get what you wanted","c":"滿意；滿足","s":"Finishing the thousand-piece puzzle gave my grandmother a deep feeling of satisfaction, and she showed it to every visitor.","t":"完成那幅一千片的拼圖讓我奶奶有深深的滿足感，她把它展示給每位來訪的客人看。","h":1},{"w":"satisfy","p":"v.","d":"to make someone pleased by giving them what they want","c":"使滿意；滿足","s":"It is hard to satisfy every customer, but the restaurant owner always listens carefully when someone complains.","t":"要讓每位顧客都滿意很難，但餐廳老闆總是在有人抱怨時仔細傾聽。"},{"w":"satisfied","p":"adj.","d":"pleased because you got what you wanted","c":"感到滿意的","s":"The teacher was satisfied with our group project, so she gave every member of the team full marks.","t":"老師對我們的小組報告很滿意，所以她給了團隊的每個成員滿分。"},{"w":"satisfying","p":"adj.","d":"making you feel pleased and happy","c":"令人滿足的","s":"There is nothing more satisfying than a bowl of hot beef noodles after a long, cold day of hiking in the mountains.","t":"在山裡健行了漫長寒冷的一天之後，沒有什麼比一碗熱牛肉麵更令人滿足的了。"},{"w":"satisfactory","p":"adj.","d":"good enough; acceptable","c":"令人滿意的；合格的","s":"Your test score is satisfactory, but I know you can do even better if you study a little more each day.","t":"你的考試成績還算令人滿意，但我知道如果你每天多讀一點書，可以考得更好。"},{"w":"satisfactorily","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is good enough","c":"令人滿意地","s":"The problem with the air conditioner was solved satisfactorily by the repairman, so the room is cool again.","t":"冷氣的問題已經被修理工令人滿意地解決了，所以房間又涼快了。"},{"w":"scarcely","p":"adv.","d":"almost not; only just","c":"幾乎不；僅僅","s":"The baby was so quiet that we could scarcely hear her breathing, so my mother checked on her several times.","t":"寶寶安靜到我們幾乎聽不到她的呼吸聲，所以我媽媽去看了她好幾次。","h":1},{"w":"scarce","p":"adj.","d":"not enough; hard to find","c":"稀少的；缺乏的","s":"Fresh water is scarce on the small island, so every family collects rainwater in large tanks on the roof.","t":"小島上淡水稀少，所以每戶人家都在屋頂用大水桶收集雨水。"},{"w":"scarcity","p":"n.","d":"a situation in which there is not enough of something","c":"缺乏；稀少","s":"The scarcity of parking spaces near the night market means many visitors now come by MRT instead of by car.","t":"夜市附近停車位的缺乏，使得許多遊客現在改搭捷運而不開車來。"},{"w":"scarcely ever","p":"phr.","d":"almost never","c":"幾乎從不","s":"My grandfather scarcely ever uses his smartphone, because he still prefers to call people on the old telephone in the hall.","t":"我爺爺幾乎從不用他的智慧型手機，因為他還是比較喜歡用走廊上的舊電話打給別人。"},{"w":"scenery","p":"n.","d":"the natural things you see in the countryside, like mountains and rivers","c":"風景；景色","s":"The train ride along the east coast offers beautiful scenery, with mountains on one side and the ocean on the other.","t":"沿著東海岸的火車之旅有美麗的風景，一邊是山，另一邊是海。","h":1},{"w":"scene","p":"n.","d":"the place where something happens; a part of a movie or play","c":"現場；場景","s":"The police arrived at the scene of the accident within five minutes and quickly moved the cars to the side.","t":"警察在五分鐘內抵達事故現場，並迅速把車輛移到路邊。"},{"w":"scenic","p":"adj.","d":"having beautiful views of nature","c":"風景優美的","s":"We took the scenic road through the mountains instead of the highway, and the trip took two hours longer.","t":"我們走了穿越山區的風景優美的道路而不是高速公路，這趟旅程多花了兩個小時。"},{"w":"behind the scenes","p":"phr.","d":"in private, where people cannot see","c":"幕後","s":"Many people work hard behind the scenes to make a concert happen, even though the audience only sees the singer on stage.","t":"許多人在幕後努力工作才能讓演唱會順利舉行，儘管觀眾只看到台上的歌手。"},{"w":"scold","p":"v.","d":"to speak angrily to someone because they did something wrong","c":"責罵；斥責","s":"My mother did not scold me for breaking the plate, because she could see that it was an accident.","t":"我媽媽沒有因為我打破盤子而責罵我，因為她看得出那是意外。","h":1},{"w":"scolding","p":"n.","d":"angry words said to someone who did something wrong","c":"責罵","s":"The boy got a scolding from his teacher for drawing on the desk, and he had to clean it after school.","t":"那個男孩因為在桌上畫畫而被老師責罵了一頓，放學後還得把桌子清乾淨。"},{"w":"scold sb for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to speak angrily to someone because of something they did","c":"因…責罵某人","s":"The coach scolded him for being late to practice again, and he made him run five extra laps around the field.","t":"教練因為他又練習遲到而責罵他，並要他多跑操場五圈。","a":"scolded him for"},{"w":"scoop","p":"n.","d":"a deep spoon for serving food; the amount it holds","c":"勺；一勺（的量）","s":"Would you like one scoop of ice cream or two, and do you want chocolate or strawberry on top?","t":"你要一球冰淇淋還是兩球？上面要淋巧克力還是草莓？","h":1},{"w":"scoop","p":"v.","d":"to pick up or move something with a spoon or your hands","c":"舀；挖","s":"Use the big spoon to scoop the rice into the bowls, and then put the fish on the table.","t":"用大湯匙把飯舀進碗裡，然後把魚放到桌上。"},{"w":"scoop up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to lift something or someone quickly","c":"舀起；一把抱起","s":"The mother quickly scooped up her little boy before he could run onto the busy road.","t":"媽媽在小男孩跑上繁忙的馬路之前，迅速一把抱起了他。","a":"scooped up"},{"w":"scoop","p":"n.","d":"an important news story that one newspaper reports first","c":"獨家新聞","s":"The young reporter got the biggest scoop of the year when she discovered that the mayor had been taking money.","t":"這位年輕記者發現市長一直在收錢，拿到了年度最大的獨家新聞。"}]},{"unit":36,"theme":"scratch – software","cards":[{"w":"scratch","p":"v.","d":"to rub your skin with your nails; to make a thin mark on a surface","c":"抓；搔；刮傷","s":"The mosquito bite on my arm is so itchy that I want to scratch it all the time, but the doctor said not to.","t":"我手臂上被蚊子咬的地方好癢，我一直想抓它，但醫生說不要抓。","h":1},{"w":"scratch","p":"n.","d":"a thin mark or small cut on a surface or on skin","c":"刮痕；抓痕","s":"There is a long scratch on the side of my father's new car, and he thinks someone hit it in the parking lot.","t":"我爸爸新車的側面有一道長長的刮痕，他認為有人在停車場撞到了它。"},{"w":"from scratch","p":"phr.","d":"from the very beginning, without using anything already made","c":"從頭開始","s":"My grandmother never buys bread from the store because she enjoys making it from scratch with flour, water, and salt.","t":"我奶奶從不在店裡買麵包，因為她喜歡用麵粉、水和鹽從頭做起。"},{"w":"scratch one's head","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be confused and not know what to do","c":"搔頭（感到困惑）","s":"The math problem was so hard that even the teacher scratched his head for a minute before he found a way to solve it.","t":"那道數學題太難了，連老師都搔了搔頭好一會兒，才想到解題的方法。","a":"scratched his head"},{"w":"sculpture","p":"n.","d":"a piece of art made by shaping stone, wood, or metal","c":"雕塑；雕像","s":"In the middle of the park stands a huge bronze sculpture of a horse, and tourists love to take photos next to it.","t":"公園中央矗立著一座巨大的青銅馬雕塑，遊客喜歡在旁邊拍照。","h":1},{"w":"sculptor","p":"n.","d":"an artist who makes sculptures","c":"雕塑家","s":"The famous sculptor spent three years cutting a single piece of marble before the statue was finally finished.","t":"這位著名的雕塑家花了三年時間雕刻一整塊大理石，雕像才終於完成。"},{"w":"sculpt","p":"v.","d":"to make a sculpture by shaping material","c":"雕刻；雕塑","s":"The art students learned to sculpt small animals out of clay, and their teacher put the best ones on display.","t":"美術系學生學習用黏土雕塑小動物，老師把最好的作品拿出來展示。"},{"w":"ice sculpture","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sculpture made of ice","c":"冰雕","s":"At the winter festival in Harbin, visitors walk through a whole city of ice sculptures that shine with colorful lights at night.","t":"在哈爾濱的冬季節慶，遊客穿梭在整座冰雕城市裡，夜晚它們閃耀著彩色燈光。","a":"ice sculptures"},{"w":"secure","p":"adj.","d":"safe and protected; not likely to fail or be lost","c":"安全的；穩固的","s":"Keep your passport in a secure place while you travel, because getting a new one abroad takes a lot of time.","t":"旅行時把護照放在安全的地方，因為在國外補辦護照要花很多時間。","h":1},{"w":"secure","p":"v.","d":"to get or achieve something after effort; to make something safe","c":"獲得；使安全","s":"After months of hard work, our team finally managed to secure a contract with the biggest supermarket chain in Taiwan.","t":"經過幾個月的努力，我們團隊終於獲得了與台灣最大連鎖超市的合約。"},{"w":"security","p":"n.","d":"the state of being safe; the people who guard a place","c":"安全；保全","s":"Airport security has become much stricter in recent years, so passengers are asked to arrive at least two hours early.","t":"近年來機場安檢變得嚴格許多，所以乘客被要求至少提前兩小時到達。"},{"w":"security guard","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose job is to protect a building or people","c":"警衛；保全人員","s":"The security guard at the front gate checks every visitor's ID card before letting them walk into the building.","t":"大門口的警衛在讓訪客進入大樓之前，會檢查每個人的身分證。"},{"w":"securely","p":"adv.","d":"in a safe and firm way","c":"牢固地；安全地","s":"Make sure the bike is securely locked to the pole, or it may be stolen while you are shopping in the market.","t":"確定腳踏車牢牢地鎖在柱子上，否則你在市場購物時它可能會被偷。"},{"w":"insecure","p":"adj.","d":"not confident; not safe or firm","c":"沒有安全感的；不穩固的","s":"He felt insecure about his English, so he kept quiet in class even when he knew the answers to the questions.","t":"他對自己的英文沒有信心，所以即使知道答案，上課時也保持沉默。"},{"w":"seize","p":"v.","d":"to take hold of something suddenly and firmly","c":"抓住；奪取","s":"When the little boy ran toward the busy road, his mother quickly ran after him and managed to seize his arm.","t":"小男孩跑向車水馬龍的馬路時，媽媽趕緊追上去，及時抓住了他的手臂。","h":1},{"w":"seize the opportunity","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use a chance quickly before it goes away","c":"抓住機會","s":"If a company offers you a job in Japan, you should seize the opportunity because such chances do not come every day.","t":"如果有公司提供你在日本的工作，你應該抓住機會，因為這樣的機會不是天天有。"},{"w":"seize control of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take power over something by force","c":"奪取…的控制權","s":"The soldiers tried to seize control of the radio station, but the people of the city stood in the streets to stop them.","t":"士兵們試圖奪取廣播電台的控制權，但這座城市的人民站在街頭阻止他們。"},{"w":"seizure","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking something by force or by law","c":"查獲；扣押","s":"The police announced the seizure of two hundred fake designer bags at the port, the largest case this year.","t":"警方宣布在港口查獲兩百個假名牌包，是今年最大的案件。"},{"w":"settler","p":"n.","d":"a person who goes to live in a new place where few people have lived before","c":"移民者；開拓者","s":"The first settlers in this valley built their houses near the river, because they needed water for their crops.","t":"這個山谷的第一批開拓者把房子蓋在河邊，因為他們的農作物需要水。","a":"settlers","h":1},{"w":"settle","p":"v.","d":"to go and live in a place; to end an argument or a problem","c":"定居；解決","s":"After traveling around Asia for two years, my uncle decided to settle in Taichung and open a small coffee shop.","t":"在亞洲旅行了兩年之後，我叔叔決定在台中定居，開一家小咖啡店。"},{"w":"settle down","p":"v.phr.","d":"to start living a quiet, steady life; to become calm","c":"安定下來；平靜下來","s":"The teacher waited for the noisy students to settle down before she began to explain the rules of the science experiment.","t":"老師等吵鬧的學生安靜下來，才開始解釋科學實驗的規則。"},{"w":"settlement","p":"n.","d":"an official agreement that ends an argument; a place where people have come to live","c":"和解；協議；聚落","s":"The two companies finally reached a settlement after a year in court, so neither side had to pay any more money.","t":"這兩家公司在法院纏訟一年後終於達成和解，所以雙方都不必再付錢。"},{"w":"severe","p":"adj.","d":"very bad, serious, or extreme","c":"嚴重的；劇烈的","s":"The patient had such a severe headache that she could not open her eyes, so the doctor sent her for a brain scan.","t":"病人頭痛得非常劇烈，連眼睛都睜不開，所以醫生安排她做腦部掃描。","h":1},{"w":"severely","p":"adv.","d":"very badly or seriously","c":"嚴重地；嚴厲地","s":"The old bridge was severely damaged by the earthquake, and engineers say it will take a year to repair it.","t":"這座舊橋在地震中受到嚴重損壞，工程師說要花一年才能修好。"},{"w":"severity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being very serious or extreme","c":"嚴重性；嚴厲","s":"Because of the severity of the storm, all schools and offices in the city were closed for two full days.","t":"由於暴風雨的嚴重程度，市內所有學校和辦公室整整關閉了兩天。"},{"w":"severe weather","p":"n.phr.","d":"very bad weather such as storms or heavy snow","c":"惡劣天氣","s":"The airline canceled dozens of flights because of severe weather, and hundreds of passengers had to sleep at the airport.","t":"航空公司因為惡劣天氣取消了數十個航班，數百名乘客不得不睡在機場。"},{"w":"sew, sewed, sewn","p":"v.","d":"to join pieces of cloth together with a needle and thread","c":"縫；縫製","s":"My grandmother taught me how to sew a button back onto my shirt, and now I can fix my own clothes.","t":"我奶奶教我怎麼把鈕扣縫回襯衫上，現在我可以自己修補衣服了。","a":"sew","h":1},{"w":"sewing","p":"n.","d":"the activity of making or repairing things with a needle and thread","c":"縫紉","s":"She keeps all her needles and thread in a small sewing box that her mother gave her thirty years ago.","t":"她把所有針線都放在一個小針線盒裡，那是她媽媽三十年前送給她的。"},{"w":"sewing machine","p":"n.phr.","d":"a machine used to sew cloth quickly","c":"縫紉機","s":"With a sewing machine, my aunt can make a whole dress in one afternoon, which would take days by hand.","t":"用縫紉機，我阿姨一個下午就能做好一整件洋裝，手工縫要花好幾天。"},{"w":"sew up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to close or repair something by sewing","c":"縫合；縫好","s":"The doctor had to sew up the deep cut on his knee with six stitches after he fell off his bike.","t":"他從腳踏車上摔下來後，醫生必須用六針縫合他膝蓋上的深傷口。"},{"w":"shade","p":"n.","d":"an area that is darker and cooler because the sun cannot reach it","c":"陰涼處；樹蔭","s":"It was so hot at noon that the workers sat in the shade of a big tree and drank cold water during their break.","t":"中午太熱了，工人們休息時坐在大樹的樹蔭下喝冰水。","h":1},{"w":"shady","p":"adj.","d":"protected from the sun; dishonest or not to be trusted","c":"陰涼的；可疑的","s":"We picked a shady spot by the lake for our picnic so that the children would not get sunburned.","t":"我們在湖邊挑了一個陰涼的地方野餐，這樣孩子們就不會曬傷。","h":1},{"w":"shade","p":"v.","d":"to protect something from direct light or heat","c":"遮蔽；遮蔭","s":"She used her hand to shade her eyes from the bright sun while she looked for her friend on the beach.","t":"她在海灘上找朋友時，用手遮住眼睛，擋住刺眼的陽光。"},{"w":"shade","p":"n.","d":"a particular form of a color, lighter or darker than others","c":"色調；色度","s":"The walls of the bedroom are painted a soft shade of blue, which makes the whole room feel calm and cool.","t":"臥室的牆壁漆成柔和的藍色調，讓整個房間感覺平靜又涼爽。"},{"w":"in the shade","p":"phr.","d":"in a place out of the sunlight","c":"在陰涼處","s":"The temperature reached thirty-eight degrees today, even in the shade, so the city opened cooling centers for older people.","t":"今天連在陰涼處氣溫都達到三十八度，所以市政府為長者開放了避暑中心。"},{"w":"sunshade","p":"n.","d":"something that protects you from the sun, like an umbrella","c":"遮陽傘；遮陽板","s":"Every car in the parking lot had a silver sunshade on the front window to keep the seats from getting too hot.","t":"停車場裡每輛車的前窗都放了銀色的遮陽板，免得座椅變得太燙。"},{"w":"shameful","p":"adj.","d":"so bad that people should feel ashamed of it","c":"可恥的；丟臉的","s":"It is shameful that some people throw their trash into the river when there is a garbage can only ten meters away.","t":"有些人明明十公尺外就有垃圾桶，卻把垃圾丟進河裡，這真是可恥。","h":1},{"w":"shame","p":"n.","d":"the bad feeling you have when you have done something wrong","c":"羞愧；羞恥","s":"His face turned red with shame when the teacher found out that he had copied his homework from a classmate.","t":"當老師發現他抄同學的作業時，他的臉因羞愧而漲紅。"},{"w":"What a shame!","p":"phr.","d":"used to say that something is disappointing","c":"真可惜！","s":"\"What a shame that you cannot come to the concert with us,\" said Amy, \"because the tickets were really hard to get.\"","t":"艾咪說：「你不能和我們一起去聽演唱會真可惜，因為票真的很難買。」","a":"What a shame"},{"w":"ashamed","p":"adj.","d":"feeling bad because of something you did","c":"感到羞愧的","s":"I feel ashamed of the way I shouted at my little sister yesterday, so I bought her a cake to say sorry.","t":"我對昨天對妹妹大吼的方式感到羞愧，所以我買了蛋糕向她道歉。"},{"w":"shameless","p":"adj.","d":"not feeling ashamed even though you should","c":"無恥的；厚顏的","s":"The shameless salesman kept calling my grandmother every day even after she had told him many times to stop.","t":"那個無恥的推銷員即使在我奶奶多次要他停止之後，仍然每天打電話給她。"},{"w":"shave","p":"v.","d":"to cut hair off your face or body with a razor","c":"刮（鬍子）；剃","s":"My father gets up ten minutes earlier than the rest of us because he needs time to shave before he goes to work.","t":"我爸爸比我們其他人早十分鐘起床，因為他上班前需要時間刮鬍子。","h":1},{"w":"shave","p":"n.","d":"the act of shaving","c":"刮臉；剃鬚","s":"After a quick shave and a hot shower, he looked ten years younger and was ready for the job interview.","t":"快速刮了鬍子並洗了熱水澡之後，他看起來年輕了十歲，準備好去面試了。"},{"w":"shaver","p":"n.","d":"an electric tool used for shaving","c":"電動刮鬍刀","s":"He packed his electric shaver in his suitcase, but he forgot the charger, so it stopped working after two days.","t":"他把電動刮鬍刀放進行李箱，卻忘了帶充電器，所以兩天後它就沒電了。"},{"w":"shaving cream","p":"n.phr.","d":"a soft cream put on the skin before shaving","c":"刮鬍泡；刮鬍膏","s":"If you put some shaving cream on your face first, the razor will move more smoothly and will not hurt your skin.","t":"如果先在臉上塗一些刮鬍泡，刮鬍刀會滑得更順，也不會傷到皮膚。"},{"w":"shelter","p":"n.","d":"a place that protects you from bad weather or danger","c":"避難所；庇護所","s":"During the typhoon, the school gym was used as a shelter for families whose homes were close to the flooded river.","t":"颱風期間，學校體育館被當作避難所，收容住家靠近氾濫河流的家庭。","h":1},{"w":"shelter","p":"v.","d":"to protect someone from bad weather or danger","c":"遮蔽；保護","s":"The thick trees along the road shelter the small houses from the strong winds that blow in from the sea.","t":"路邊茂密的樹木保護著小屋，擋住從海上吹來的強風。"},{"w":"take shelter","p":"v.phr.","d":"to go to a place where you are protected","c":"躲避；避難","s":"When the thunder started, the hikers ran to take shelter under a rock, and they waited there until the rain stopped.","t":"雷聲響起時，登山客跑到岩石下躲避，在那裡一直等到雨停。"},{"w":"animal shelter","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place that takes care of animals that have no home","c":"動物收容所","s":"My family adopted our dog from an animal shelter two years ago, and she has become the happiest member of our home.","t":"我們家兩年前從動物收容所領養了我們的狗，她已成為家裡最快樂的成員。"},{"w":"sheltered","p":"adj.","d":"protected from bad weather or from difficult experiences","c":"受到保護的；有遮蔽的","s":"The boats are kept in a sheltered bay where the high cliffs on both sides keep out the wind and the big waves.","t":"這些船停在一個有遮蔽的海灣，兩側的高崖擋住了風和大浪。"},{"w":"shift","p":"v.","d":"to move or change something from one place or position to another","c":"移動；轉移；改變","s":"Could you help me shift this heavy desk closer to the window so that I can get more light while I study?","t":"你能幫我把這張重桌子移到靠窗的地方嗎？這樣我讀書時光線會更好。","h":1},{"w":"shift","p":"n.","d":"a period of work time in a place that is open day and night","c":"輪班；班次","s":"Nurses at the hospital work in three groups, and the night shift runs from eleven in the evening to seven in the morning.","t":"醫院的護理師分三組工作，夜班從晚上十一點到早上七點。"},{"w":"shift","p":"n.","d":"a change in the way people think or do things","c":"轉變；改變","s":"There has been a big shift in how people shop, as more and more customers now buy their clothes online.","t":"人們購物的方式有了很大的轉變，越來越多的顧客現在在網路上買衣服。"},{"w":"work the night shift","p":"v.phr.","d":"to work during the night","c":"上夜班","s":"My mother works the night shift at the factory three times a week, so she usually sleeps while we are at school.","t":"我媽媽每週在工廠上夜班三次，所以她通常在我們上學時睡覺。","a":"works the night shift"},{"w":"shift gears","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change what you are doing or how you do it","c":"換檔；改變做法","s":"After an hour of grammar practice, the teacher decided to shift gears and play a vocabulary game with the class.","t":"練習了一小時文法之後，老師決定換個方式，和全班玩單字遊戲。"},{"w":"sightseeing","p":"n.","d":"the activity of visiting famous or interesting places as a tourist","c":"觀光","s":"We spent our first day in Kyoto doing some sightseeing, and we visited three temples before lunch.","t":"我們在京都的第一天去觀光，午餐前就參觀了三座寺廟。","h":1},{"w":"go sightseeing","p":"v.phr.","d":"to visit interesting places as a tourist","c":"去觀光","s":"After the business meeting ended early, my boss and I had a free afternoon to go sightseeing around the old city.","t":"商務會議提早結束後，我和老闆有一個空閒的下午可以在舊城區觀光。"},{"w":"sightseeing tour","p":"n.phr.","d":"a trip organized to show tourists famous places","c":"觀光行程","s":"The hotel offers a half-day sightseeing tour of the city for only five hundred dollars, and lunch is included in the price.","t":"飯店提供半天的城市觀光行程，只要五百元，而且價格包含午餐。"},{"w":"sight","p":"n.","d":"a famous or interesting place that tourists visit; the ability to see","c":"名勝；景象；視力","s":"Taipei 101 is the most famous sight in the city, and thousands of visitors go up to the top floor every day.","t":"台北101是這座城市最著名的景點，每天有數千名遊客上到頂樓。"},{"w":"sightseer","p":"n.","d":"a person who visits interesting places as a tourist","c":"觀光客","s":"On weekends the old street is full of sightseers taking photos, so the local people prefer to shop there on weekdays.","t":"週末老街擠滿了拍照的觀光客，所以當地人比較喜歡平日去那裡購物。","a":"sightseers"},{"w":"signature","p":"n.","d":"your name written by yourself in your own special way","c":"簽名","s":"The form is not valid without your signature at the bottom, so please sign it before you hand it in.","t":"這張表格底部沒有你的簽名就無效，所以請在交出之前先簽名。","h":1},{"w":"signature","p":"adj.","d":"typical of a particular person or place and known for it","c":"招牌的；代表性的","s":"The chef's signature dish is beef noodle soup, and people wait in line for an hour just to taste it.","t":"這位主廚的招牌菜是牛肉麵，人們排隊一小時只為了嚐一嚐。"},{"w":"sign","p":"v.","d":"to write your name on a document to show you agree","c":"簽署；簽名","s":"Before you sign the contract, read every page carefully and ask the company about anything you do not understand.","t":"在你簽合約之前，仔細閱讀每一頁，並向公司詢問任何你不懂的地方。"},{"w":"collect signatures","p":"v.phr.","d":"to ask many people to sign a document to support something","c":"連署；收集簽名","s":"The students stood outside the library to collect signatures for a petition asking the school to open the pool on weekends.","t":"學生們站在圖書館外收集簽名連署，請求學校在週末開放游泳池。"},{"w":"significance","p":"n.","d":"the importance or meaning of something","c":"重要性；意義","s":"The teacher explained the significance of the Dragon Boat Festival, so now we understand why people eat rice dumplings that day.","t":"老師解釋了端午節的意義，所以我們現在明白為什麼人們那天要吃粽子。","h":1},{"w":"significant","p":"adj.","d":"important or large enough to be noticed","c":"重要的；顯著的","s":"There has been a significant drop in the number of people smoking since the government raised the price of cigarettes.","t":"自從政府提高香菸價格以來，吸菸人數有顯著的下降。"},{"w":"significantly","p":"adv.","d":"in an important or noticeable way","c":"顯著地；大幅地","s":"Her test scores improved significantly after she started reviewing her notes for twenty minutes every night before bed.","t":"自從她開始每晚睡前複習筆記二十分鐘後，她的考試成績大幅進步。"},{"w":"signify","p":"v.","d":"to be a sign of something; to mean","c":"表示；意味著","s":"In many Asian countries, a red envelope with money inside is given to signify good luck for the coming year.","t":"在許多亞洲國家，人們會送裝有錢的紅包來表示來年的好運。"},{"w":"insignificant","p":"adj.","d":"too small or unimportant to matter","c":"微不足道的","s":"Do not worry about such an insignificant mistake; nobody noticed that you skipped one word during your speech.","t":"別擔心這麼微不足道的錯誤；沒有人注意到你演講時漏了一個字。"},{"w":"sincerity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being honest and meaning what you say","c":"真誠；誠意","s":"Everyone could feel the sincerity in his voice when he thanked the nurses who had taken care of his mother.","t":"當他感謝照顧他母親的護理師時，每個人都能感受到他聲音中的真誠。","h":1},{"w":"sincere","p":"adj.","d":"honest and really meaning what you say or feel","c":"真誠的；誠懇的","s":"Please accept my sincere apology for missing your birthday dinner; I promise to make it up to you this weekend.","t":"請接受我誠懇的道歉，我錯過了你的生日晚餐；我保證這個週末補償你。"},{"w":"sincerely","p":"adv.","d":"honestly; used at the end of a formal letter","c":"真誠地；敬上","s":"I sincerely hope that your father gets better soon, and please let me know if there is anything I can do.","t":"我衷心希望你父親早日康復，如果有什麼我能幫忙的，請告訴我。"},{"w":"Yours sincerely,","p":"phr.","d":"a polite way to end a formal letter when you know the person's name","c":"敬上（書信結尾）","s":"She finished her letter to the school principal with the words \"Yours sincerely\" and then wrote her full name below.","t":"她在寫給校長的信末寫上「敬上」，然後在下面寫下她的全名。","a":"Yours sincerely"},{"w":"insincere","p":"adj.","d":"not honest; not meaning what you say","c":"不真誠的；虛偽的","s":"His smile looked insincere, and we all knew he did not really want to help us move the furniture.","t":"他的笑容看起來不真誠，我們都知道他並不是真的想幫我們搬家具。"},{"w":"singular","p":"adj.","d":"the form of a word used for one person or thing (grammar)","c":"單數的","s":"In English, the singular form of the noun is \"child,\" but the plural form is \"children,\" not \"childs.\"","t":"在英文裡，這個名詞的單數形式是 child，但複數形式是 children，不是 childs。","h":1},{"w":"singular","p":"n.","d":"the singular form of a word","c":"單數","s":"The word \"sheep\" is the same in the singular and the plural, so you can say one sheep or ten sheep.","t":"sheep 這個字的單數和複數形式相同，所以你可以說 one sheep 或 ten sheep。"},{"w":"singular","p":"adj.","d":"very unusual or remarkable","c":"非凡的；奇特的","s":"The young pianist has a singular talent, and music teachers from around the world have come to hear her play.","t":"這位年輕鋼琴家有非凡的才華，世界各地的音樂老師都來聽她演奏。"},{"w":"single","p":"adj.","d":"only one; not married","c":"單一的；單身的","s":"Not a single student was late for class today, because the teacher had promised a prize for the whole class.","t":"今天一個學生都沒遲到，因為老師答應要給全班獎品。"},{"w":"plural","p":"adj.","d":"the form of a word used for more than one person or thing","c":"複數的","s":"Many students forget to add an \"s\" to make a noun plural, so they write \"two book\" instead of \"two books.\"","t":"許多學生忘了加 s 讓名詞變成複數，所以他們寫 two book 而不是 two books。"},{"w":"site","p":"n.","d":"a place where something is, was, or will be built","c":"地點；場所；遺址","s":"The old train station is now a historic site, and the city has turned the waiting room into a small museum.","t":"舊火車站現在是一處歷史遺址，市政府把候車室改成了一座小博物館。","h":1},{"w":"website","p":"n.","d":"a group of connected pages on the internet","c":"網站","s":"You can check your exam results on the school website after six o'clock tonight by typing in your student number.","t":"今晚六點以後，你可以在學校網站輸入學號查詢考試成績。"},{"w":"construction site","p":"n.phr.","d":"a place where a building is being built","c":"建築工地；施工現場","s":"Workers on the construction site must wear hard hats at all times, because tools and bricks sometimes fall from above.","t":"建築工地的工人必須隨時戴安全帽，因為工具和磚塊有時會從上面掉下來。"},{"w":"on site","p":"phr.","d":"at the place where something happens or is being done","c":"在現場","s":"A doctor is always on site during the marathon, so runners who feel sick can get help within a few minutes.","t":"馬拉松期間總有一位醫生在現場，所以覺得不舒服的跑者幾分鐘內就能得到幫助。"},{"w":"sketch","p":"n.","d":"a quick, simple drawing without many details","c":"素描；草圖","s":"Before painting the picture, the artist made a quick sketch of the mountain in pencil to plan where everything would go.","t":"在畫這幅畫之前，藝術家先用鉛筆畫了一張山的草圖，規劃每樣東西的位置。","h":1},{"w":"sketch","p":"v.","d":"to make a quick, simple drawing of something","c":"畫素描；勾勒","s":"My sister likes to sit by the river and sketch the boats and birds she sees, using only a pencil and a notebook.","t":"我姐姐喜歡坐在河邊，只用一枝鉛筆和一本筆記本素描她看到的船和鳥。"},{"w":"sketchbook","p":"n.","d":"a book of blank pages for drawing","c":"素描本","s":"He carries a small sketchbook everywhere he goes, so he can draw interesting faces he sees on the train.","t":"他走到哪裡都帶著一本小素描本，這樣就能畫下他在火車上看到的有趣面孔。"},{"w":"sketch out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to describe or plan something in a simple, general way","c":"概略說明；草擬","s":"At the first meeting, the manager will sketch out the plan for the new product, and the details will come later.","t":"在第一次會議上，經理會概略說明新產品的計畫，細節稍後再談。"},{"w":"skyscraper","p":"n.","d":"a very tall modern building in a city","c":"摩天大樓","s":"From the top of the skyscraper, you can see the whole city, and at night the lights look like a sea of stars.","t":"從摩天大樓的頂樓可以看到整座城市，晚上燈光看起來像一片星海。","h":1},{"w":"sky","p":"n.","d":"the space above the earth where you see clouds, the sun, and stars","c":"天空","s":"The sky was so clear last night that we could see thousands of stars from the beach without a telescope.","t":"昨晚天空非常清澈，我們在海灘上不用望遠鏡就能看到成千上萬顆星星。"},{"w":"skyline","p":"n.","d":"the shape that tall buildings make against the sky","c":"天際線","s":"The skyline of Kaohsiung has changed a lot in twenty years, with new towers rising up near the harbor every year.","t":"高雄的天際線二十年來改變很大，每年港口附近都有新的高樓拔地而起。"},{"w":"scrape","p":"v.","d":"to rub a hard edge against a surface, often making a noise or a mark","c":"刮；擦","s":"Please do not scrape the chair legs across the floor, because the noise disturbs the family who lives downstairs.","t":"請不要把椅腳在地板上拖刮，因為噪音會打擾住在樓下的那家人。"},{"w":"slight","p":"adj.","d":"small and not important or serious","c":"輕微的；些微的","s":"There was a slight change in the schedule, so the meeting will start at ten instead of nine thirty tomorrow.","t":"時間表有一點些微的變動，所以明天會議將在十點開始，而不是九點半。","h":1},{"w":"slightly","p":"adv.","d":"a little; to a small degree","c":"稍微；略微","s":"The soup tastes slightly too salty for me, but my father says it is perfect and asks for a second bowl.","t":"這湯對我來說稍微太鹹了，但我爸爸說它很完美，還要了第二碗。"},{"w":"not in the slightest","p":"phr.","d":"not at all","c":"一點也不","s":"I was not in the slightest surprised when Tom won the speech contest, because he had practiced every day for a whole month.","t":"湯姆贏得演講比賽時，我一點也不驚訝，因為他整整一個月每天都在練習。"},{"w":"slight","p":"v.","d":"to treat someone as if they are not important","c":"輕視；怠慢","s":"She felt that the manager had slighted her by giving the big project to a new worker with far less experience.","t":"她覺得經理把大型專案交給經驗少得多的新員工，是在輕視她。","a":"slighted"},{"w":"slogan","p":"n.","d":"a short, easy-to-remember phrase used in advertising or politics","c":"口號；標語","s":"The company's new slogan is only three words long, but everyone in the country can repeat it after hearing the ad once.","t":"這家公司的新標語只有三個字，但全國的人聽過廣告一次就能複述。","h":1},{"w":"campaign slogan","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short phrase used by a politician or group during an election","c":"競選口號","s":"The mayor's campaign slogan promised a cleaner city, so voters were angry when the parks stayed dirty after the election.","t":"市長的競選口號承諾一個更乾淨的城市，所以選後公園依然髒亂時，選民很生氣。"},{"w":"advertising slogan","p":"n.phr.","d":"a short phrase that helps people remember a product","c":"廣告標語","s":"A good advertising slogan should be short and fun, like the one the sports brand has used for more than thirty years.","t":"好的廣告標語應該簡短有趣，就像那個運動品牌已經使用三十多年的那句話一樣。"},{"w":"shout slogans","p":"v.phr.","d":"to call out short phrases together, as in a protest","c":"高喊口號","s":"Hundreds of workers marched in front of the government building and shouted slogans asking for a higher minimum wage.","t":"數百名工人在政府大樓前遊行，高喊口號要求提高最低工資。","a":"shouted slogans"},{"w":"socket","p":"n.","d":"a place in a wall where you plug in electrical equipment","c":"插座","s":"There is only one socket in this old hotel room, so we have to take turns charging our phones and laptops.","t":"這間舊飯店房間只有一個插座，所以我們必須輪流幫手機和筆電充電。","h":1},{"w":"socket","p":"n.","d":"a hollow part that something fits into, such as the eye socket","c":"孔；窩；承口","s":"The doctor checked the X-ray and said the bone around his eye socket was not broken, which was a great relief.","t":"醫生看了X光片，說他眼窩周圍的骨頭沒有斷，這真是鬆了一口氣。"},{"w":"plug","p":"n.","d":"the part at the end of a wire that goes into a socket","c":"插頭","s":"When you travel to Japan, remember that the plug of your hair dryer may not fit the sockets in the hotel.","t":"去日本旅行時，記得你吹風機的插頭可能不適合飯店的插座。"},{"w":"plug in","p":"v.phr.","d":"to connect a machine to the electricity supply","c":"插上電源","s":"If the printer does not turn on, first check whether you remembered to plug in the power cable at the back.","t":"如果印表機打不開，先檢查你是否記得把後面的電源線插上。"},{"w":"software","p":"n.","d":"the programs that run on a computer or phone","c":"軟體","s":"You need to update the software on your phone regularly, or some apps may stop working and your data may be less safe.","t":"你需要定期更新手機的軟體，否則有些應用程式可能無法運作，資料也比較不安全。","h":1},{"w":"hardware","p":"n.","d":"the physical parts of a computer, such as the screen and keyboard","c":"硬體","s":"The computer's hardware is five years old, so it cannot run the newest games no matter which programs we install.","t":"這台電腦的硬體已經五年了，所以不管我們安裝什麼程式，都無法執行最新的遊戲。"},{"w":"software engineer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person whose job is to design and write computer programs","c":"軟體工程師","s":"My cousin works as a software engineer in Hsinchu, and she spends most of her day writing code for a new banking app.","t":"我表姐在新竹當軟體工程師，她一天大部分時間都在為一個新的銀行應用程式寫程式碼。"},{"w":"install software","p":"v.phr.","d":"to put a program onto a computer so it can be used","c":"安裝軟體","s":"Before the class starts, every student has to install the software on their laptop so that they can follow the coding lesson.","t":"課程開始前，每位學生都必須在筆電上安裝軟體，才能跟上程式設計課。","a":"install the software"}]},{"unit":37,"theme":"solar – summarize","cards":[{"w":"solar","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the sun or using the sun's energy","c":"太陽的；太陽能的","s":"Our school put solar panels on the roof last year, and now the sun provides half of the electricity we use.","t":"我們學校去年在屋頂裝了太陽能板，現在太陽提供我們一半的用電。","h":1},{"w":"solar energy","p":"n.phr.","d":"power that comes from the sun's light and heat","c":"太陽能","s":"Many families in southern Taiwan use solar energy to heat their water, because the sun shines almost every day there.","t":"台灣南部許多家庭用太陽能來加熱洗澡水，因為那裡幾乎每天都有陽光。"},{"w":"solar system","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sun and all the planets that move around it","c":"太陽系","s":"In science class we built a model of the solar system, with the sun in the middle and eight planets around it.","t":"在自然課上我們做了一個太陽系模型，太陽在中間，八顆行星繞著它。"},{"w":"solar eclipse","p":"n.phr.","d":"a time when the moon passes between the sun and the earth","c":"日蝕","s":"Thousands of people wore special glasses to watch the solar eclipse, which turned the afternoon sky dark for three minutes.","t":"數千人戴著特製眼鏡觀看日蝕，它讓下午的天空暗了三分鐘。"},{"w":"spade","p":"n.","d":"a tool with a flat blade used for digging","c":"鏟子","s":"My grandfather took his old spade out of the shed and began to dig a hole for the new lemon tree.","t":"我爺爺從工具間拿出他的舊鏟子，開始為新的檸檬樹挖洞。","h":1},{"w":"spades","p":"n.","d":"one of the four groups of playing cards, with black pointed shapes","c":"黑桃","s":"In this card game, the ace of spades is the strongest card, so whoever holds it usually wins the round.","t":"在這個紙牌遊戲中，黑桃A是最大的牌，所以拿到它的人通常會贏這一局。"},{"w":"call a spade a spade","p":"phr.","d":"to say exactly what you think, even if it is not polite","c":"直言不諱","s":"My aunt always calls a spade a spade; if she thinks your cooking is bad, she will tell you so to your face.","t":"我阿姨總是直言不諱；如果她覺得你煮的菜難吃，她會當面告訴你。","a":"calls a spade a spade"},{"w":"dig","p":"v.","d":"to make a hole in the ground with a tool or your hands","c":"挖","s":"The dog loves to dig holes in the garden, so my mother finds her flowers pulled out of the ground almost every week.","t":"這隻狗喜歡在花園裡挖洞，所以我媽媽幾乎每週都發現她的花被挖出來。"},{"w":"spare","p":"adj.","d":"extra; not being used and available if needed","c":"備用的；多餘的","s":"Always keep a spare key with a neighbor you trust, so you can get in if you lock yourself out of the house.","t":"一定要把一把備用鑰匙放在你信任的鄰居那裡，這樣把自己鎖在門外時還能進屋。","h":1},{"w":"spare time","p":"n.phr.","d":"time when you are not working or studying","c":"空閒時間","s":"In her spare time, my sister likes to bake cookies and give them to the old people who live alone on our street.","t":"我姐姐在空閒時間喜歡烤餅乾，送給我們這條街上獨居的老人。"},{"w":"spare","p":"v.","d":"to give time or money that you have enough of; to not hurt or punish someone","c":"抽出；撥出；饒恕","s":"Could you spare ten minutes this afternoon to look at my report before I send it to the manager?","t":"你今天下午能抽出十分鐘看一下我的報告嗎？我想在寄給經理前請你看看。"},{"w":"spare tire","p":"n.phr.","d":"an extra wheel kept in a car in case one gets a flat","c":"備胎","s":"When we got a flat on the mountain road, my father calmly took out the spare tire and changed the wheel in fifteen minutes.","t":"我們在山路上爆胎時，爸爸冷靜地拿出備胎，十五分鐘內就換好了輪子。"},{"w":"to spare","p":"phr.","d":"left over; more than you need","c":"剩餘的；多出的","s":"We arrived at the station with twenty minutes to spare, so we bought some hot tea and sat down to wait for the train.","t":"我們到車站時還多出二十分鐘，所以買了熱茶坐下來等火車。"},{"w":"spark","p":"n.","d":"a very small piece of burning material or flash of electricity","c":"火花；火星","s":"A single spark from the campfire landed on the dry grass, and within seconds a small fire had started.","t":"營火的一顆火星掉在乾草上，幾秒鐘內就燒起了一小片火。","h":1},{"w":"spark","p":"v.","d":"to make something start, especially a feeling or an event","c":"引發；激起","s":"The teacher's simple question about dinosaurs managed to spark a lively discussion that lasted the whole class.","t":"老師關於恐龍的一個簡單問題引發了一場熱烈的討論，持續了整堂課。"},{"w":"spark off","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cause something to happen suddenly","c":"引起；觸發","s":"The rise in bus fares sparked off angry protests across the city, and students marched to the city hall on Monday.","t":"公車票價上漲引發了全市的憤怒抗議，學生們星期一遊行到市政府。","a":"sparked off"},{"w":"sparkle","p":"v.","d":"to shine with small bright flashes of light","c":"閃耀；閃爍","s":"The lake began to sparkle in the morning sun, and the whole view looked like a picture from a postcard.","t":"湖面在晨光中開始閃閃發光，整個景色看起來就像明信片上的圖畫。"},{"w":"spear","p":"n.","d":"a long weapon with a sharp point used for hunting or fighting","c":"矛；魚叉","s":"Long before guns were invented, hunters used a long wooden spear to catch fish and large animals in the forest.","t":"在槍發明之前很久，獵人用長木矛在森林裡捕魚和獵捕大型動物。","h":1},{"w":"spear","p":"v.","d":"to push a pointed object through something","c":"用矛刺；叉起","s":"The fisherman stood still in the river and waited for the right moment to spear a fish with one quick move.","t":"漁夫靜靜地站在河裡，等待最佳時機，一個快動作就叉到一條魚。"},{"w":"spearhead","p":"v.","d":"to lead an action or a movement","c":"帶頭；領導","s":"A group of high school students decided to spearhead a campaign to clean up the beach every Saturday morning.","t":"一群高中生決定帶頭發起一項每週六早上淨灘的活動。"},{"w":"spear fishing","p":"n.phr.","d":"catching fish with a spear","c":"魚叉捕魚","s":"On the island, the local people still practice spear fishing the way their grandparents did, holding their breath under the water.","t":"在島上，當地人仍然像祖父母那樣用魚叉捕魚，在水下憋氣。"},{"w":"species","p":"n.","d":"a group of animals or plants that are the same kind","c":"物種","s":"Scientists discovered a new species of frog in the mountains of Taiwan, and it is smaller than a coin.","t":"科學家在台灣的山區發現了一個新的青蛙物種，它比一枚硬幣還小。","h":1},{"w":"endangered species","p":"n.phr.","d":"a kind of animal or plant that may soon disappear","c":"瀕危物種","s":"The Formosan black bear is an endangered species, so hunting it is against the law and can lead to years in prison.","t":"台灣黑熊是瀕危物種，所以獵捕牠是違法的，可能導致多年牢獄。"},{"w":"the human species","p":"n.phr.","d":"all people considered as one kind of living thing","c":"人類","s":"For most of its history, the human species lived by hunting and gathering, and farming began only about ten thousand years ago.","t":"在歷史上大部分時間，人類靠狩獵和採集維生，農業大約在一萬年前才開始。"},{"w":"special","p":"adj.","d":"different from what is usual; important or better","c":"特別的","s":"My mother makes a special dinner every Chinese New Year, with fish, dumplings, and a hot pot for the whole family.","t":"我媽媽每年農曆新年都會做一頓特別的晚餐，有魚、餃子，還有全家人吃的火鍋。"},{"w":"spiritual","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the human spirit or with religion, not with the body","c":"精神的；心靈的；宗教的","s":"Many people climb the mountain not for exercise but for spiritual reasons, since there is an old temple at the top.","t":"許多人爬這座山不是為了運動，而是出於心靈上的理由，因為山頂有一座古老的寺廟。","h":1},{"w":"spirit","p":"n.","d":"the part of a person that is not the body; a mood or attitude","c":"精神；心靈；情緒","s":"Although Grandma is eighty-five, she still has the spirit of a young woman and travels abroad every year.","t":"雖然奶奶已經八十五歲，她仍然有年輕女子的精神，每年都出國旅行。"},{"w":"in high spirits","p":"phr.","d":"very happy and full of energy","c":"興高采烈","s":"The whole team was in high spirits after the game, singing on the bus all the way back to school.","t":"比賽結束後全隊興高采烈，回學校的公車上一路唱歌。"},{"w":"team spirit","p":"n.phr.","d":"the feeling of working together and supporting each other","c":"團隊精神","s":"Our coach says that team spirit matters more than talent, because a team that helps each other can beat stronger players.","t":"我們的教練說團隊精神比天分更重要，因為互相幫助的隊伍能打敗更強的球員。"},{"w":"spiritually","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with the spirit or religion","c":"在精神上；在心靈上","s":"After a week of quiet walks in the countryside, she felt spiritually refreshed and ready to return to her busy job.","t":"在鄉間安靜地散步一週之後，她覺得心靈上煥然一新，準備好回到忙碌的工作。"},{"w":"splendid","p":"adj.","d":"excellent; very beautiful or impressive","c":"極好的；壯麗的","s":"From the hotel window we had a splendid view of the harbor, with hundreds of boats and the mountains behind them.","t":"從飯店的窗戶我們可以看到港口壯麗的景色，有數百艘船和後面的山。","h":1},{"w":"splendidly","p":"adv.","d":"in an excellent or impressive way","c":"極好地；出色地","s":"The students performed splendidly at the concert, and the principal praised every one of them on stage afterwards.","t":"學生們在音樂會上表現出色，之後校長在台上稱讚了他們每一個人。"},{"w":"splendor","p":"n.","d":"great beauty that impresses people","c":"壯麗；輝煌","s":"Visitors to the old palace are always amazed by the splendor of its golden halls and painted ceilings.","t":"參觀舊皇宮的遊客總是對它金色大廳和彩繪天花板的壯麗感到驚嘆。"},{"w":"a splendid idea","p":"n.phr.","d":"an excellent plan or suggestion","c":"好主意","s":"\"Let's have the party in the park instead of the classroom,\" said Lisa, and everyone agreed it was a splendid idea.","t":"麗莎說：「我們在公園而不是教室辦派對吧。」大家都同意這是個好主意。"},{"w":"split, split, split","p":"v.","d":"to divide into parts; to break along a line","c":"分開；分裂；裂開","s":"The teacher asked us to split into groups of four, and each group had to make a poster about one country.","t":"老師要我們分成四人一組，每組要做一張關於一個國家的海報。","a":"split","h":1},{"w":"split","p":"n.","d":"a division between people or groups; a crack","c":"分裂；裂縫","s":"There was a split in the club after the vote, and half of the members decided to start a new club of their own.","t":"投票之後社團出現分裂，一半的成員決定自己成立一個新社團。"},{"w":"split the bill","p":"v.phr.","d":"to share the cost of a meal between people","c":"分攤帳單","s":"When my friends and I eat out together, we usually split the bill so that nobody has to pay for everyone.","t":"我和朋友一起外出吃飯時，我們通常分攤帳單，這樣就不用有人請客。"},{"w":"split up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to end a relationship; to divide into smaller groups","c":"分手；拆散；分開","s":"The famous singer and her husband decided to split up after ten years of marriage, and the news shocked their fans.","t":"這位知名歌手和她的丈夫在結婚十年後決定分手，這個消息震驚了歌迷。"},{"w":"split second","p":"n.phr.","d":"an extremely short moment","c":"一瞬間","s":"The driver stopped the car in a split second when the child ran into the street, and luckily nobody was hurt.","t":"當孩子跑到街上時，司機在一瞬間停下了車，幸好沒有人受傷。"},{"w":"sprinkle","p":"v.","d":"to scatter small drops or pieces of something over a surface","c":"撒；灑","s":"Before you put the pizza in the oven, sprinkle some cheese on top so that it melts into a golden layer.","t":"把披薩放進烤箱之前，在上面撒一些起司，這樣它會融化成金黃色的一層。","h":1},{"w":"sprinkle","p":"n.","d":"a small amount of something scattered; light rain","c":"少量撒的東西；小雨","s":"Add a sprinkle of salt to the soup, taste it, and then decide whether it needs any more before you serve it.","t":"在湯裡加少許鹽，嚐一嚐，然後在上菜前決定是否需要再加。"},{"w":"sprinkler","p":"n.","d":"a device that sprays water over grass or puts out fires","c":"灑水器","s":"The sprinkler in the park turns on every evening at six, so the children love to run through the water on hot days.","t":"公園裡的灑水器每天傍晚六點打開，所以天熱時孩子們喜歡在水裡跑來跑去。"},{"w":"sprinkle with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to cover something lightly with small pieces","c":"在…上撒","s":"The baker sprinkled the cakes with sugar and finished them with a little cream, and the shop sold out before noon.","t":"麵包師在蛋糕上撒糖，再加上一點奶油，店裡的蛋糕中午前就賣完了。","a":"sprinkled the cakes with"},{"w":"stab","p":"v.","d":"to push a knife or sharp object into someone or something","c":"刺；戳","s":"The news said a man tried to stab a shop owner during a robbery, but a brave customer stopped him in time.","t":"新聞說一名男子在搶劫時試圖刺店主，但一位勇敢的顧客及時阻止了他。","h":1},{"w":"stab","p":"n.","d":"an act of pushing a knife into someone; a sudden sharp feeling","c":"刺；戳；一陣（痛）","s":"He felt a sharp stab of pain in his back when he lifted the heavy box, so the doctor told him to rest for a week.","t":"他搬重箱子時感到背部一陣劇痛，所以醫生要他休息一週。"},{"w":"stab sb in the back","p":"v.phr.","d":"to harm someone who trusts you, secretly","c":"暗箭傷人；背叛","s":"I thought he was my friend, but he stabbed me in the back by telling the boss about my mistake to get the promotion himself.","t":"我以為他是我的朋友，但他為了自己升職向老闆告發我的錯誤，在背後捅了我一刀。","a":"stabbed me in the back"},{"w":"take a stab at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to do something, even if you may not succeed","c":"試一試","s":"I have never fixed a bike before, but I am willing to take a stab at it if you show me which tools to use.","t":"我以前從沒修過腳踏車，但如果你告訴我該用哪些工具，我願意試一試。"},{"w":"statistics","p":"n.","d":"numbers that give facts about something; the study of such numbers","c":"統計數據；統計學","s":"The latest statistics show that fewer babies were born in Taiwan last year than in any year before.","t":"最新的統計數據顯示，台灣去年出生的嬰兒比以往任何一年都少。","h":1},{"w":"statistical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with or based on statistics","c":"統計的","s":"The report gives a clear statistical picture of how many students use their phones for more than five hours a day.","t":"這份報告清楚地呈現了每天使用手機超過五小時的學生人數的統計狀況。"},{"w":"statistically","p":"adv.","d":"according to statistics","c":"從統計上來看","s":"Statistically, flying is much safer than driving, even though many people are more afraid of airplanes than of cars.","t":"從統計上來看，搭飛機比開車安全得多，儘管許多人更怕飛機而不是汽車。","a":"Statistically"},{"w":"statistician","p":"n.","d":"a person who studies or works with statistics","c":"統計學家","s":"A statistician at the health department explained why the number of flu cases always rises after the winter holidays.","t":"衛生局的一位統計學家解釋了為什麼流感病例在寒假之後總是增加。"},{"w":"status","p":"n.","d":"a person's social or professional position compared with others","c":"地位；身分","s":"In the past, owning a car was a sign of high status in the village, but today almost every family has one.","t":"過去在村裡擁有汽車是高地位的象徵，但今天幾乎每個家庭都有車。","h":1},{"w":"status","p":"n.","d":"the situation of something at a particular time","c":"狀態；狀況","s":"You can check the status of your package online, and the website will tell you whether it has left the warehouse.","t":"你可以在線上查詢包裹的狀態，網站會告訴你它是否已經離開倉庫。"},{"w":"marital status","p":"n.phr.","d":"whether a person is single, married, or divorced","c":"婚姻狀況","s":"The form asks for your name, date of birth, and marital status, but you do not have to say how much money you earn.","t":"這張表格要填姓名、出生日期和婚姻狀況，但你不必說你賺多少錢。"},{"w":"status symbol","p":"n.phr.","d":"something expensive that shows how rich or important a person is","c":"地位象徵","s":"For some teenagers, the newest phone is a status symbol, and they feel embarrassed to use an older model in front of friends.","t":"對有些青少年來說，最新的手機是一種地位象徵，在朋友面前用舊款會覺得尷尬。"},{"w":"stem","p":"n.","d":"the long thin part of a plant that holds the leaves and flowers","c":"莖；梗","s":"Cut the stem of each rose at an angle before you put it in water, and the flowers will stay fresh longer.","t":"把每朵玫瑰的莖斜著剪一下再放進水裡，花會保持新鮮更久。","h":1},{"w":"stem from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be caused by something; to come from","c":"源於；起因於","s":"Most of the problems between the two brothers stem from the fact that they have to share one small bedroom.","t":"這兩兄弟之間大部分的問題源於他們必須共用一間小臥室。"},{"w":"stem","p":"v.","d":"to stop something from spreading or increasing","c":"阻止；遏止","s":"The government took quick action to stem the spread of the virus, closing schools for two weeks in March.","t":"政府迅速採取行動遏止病毒擴散，三月時關閉學校兩週。"},{"w":"stem cell","p":"n.phr.","d":"a basic cell in the body that can grow into different kinds of cells","c":"幹細胞","s":"Doctors hope that stem cell research will one day help people who have lost the ability to walk after an accident.","t":"醫生希望幹細胞研究有朝一日能幫助在意外後失去行走能力的人。"},{"w":"stereo","p":"n.","d":"a machine for playing music with sound coming from two speakers","c":"立體音響","s":"My father bought an old stereo at the flea market, and he spends every Sunday playing his jazz records on it.","t":"我爸爸在跳蚤市場買了一台舊立體音響，他每個星期天都用它播放爵士唱片。","h":1},{"w":"stereo","p":"adj.","d":"using two speakers so the sound seems to come from different directions","c":"立體聲的","s":"The new headphones give you real stereo sound, so you can hear the guitar on the left and the drums on the right.","t":"這副新耳機能給你真正的立體聲效果，你可以聽到吉他在左邊、鼓在右邊。"},{"w":"in stereo","p":"phr.","d":"with sound coming from two directions","c":"以立體聲","s":"The concert was recorded in stereo, so listening to it at home almost feels like sitting in the front row.","t":"這場演唱會是以立體聲錄製的，所以在家聽幾乎感覺像坐在第一排。"},{"w":"stereotype","p":"n.","d":"a fixed idea about what a type of person is like, often wrong","c":"刻板印象","s":"The movie breaks the old stereotype that girls are bad at science by showing a young woman who builds her own robot.","t":"這部電影透過一位自己製造機器人的年輕女性，打破了女生不擅長科學的舊刻板印象。"},{"w":"stingy","p":"adj.","d":"not willing to spend money or give things to others","c":"小氣的；吝嗇的","s":"My uncle is so stingy that he reuses tea bags three times and never turns on the air conditioner, even in July.","t":"我叔叔小氣到茶包重複用三次，而且即使在七月也從不開冷氣。","h":1},{"w":"stinginess","p":"n.","d":"the quality of not being willing to spend money","c":"小氣；吝嗇","s":"His stinginess became a joke in the office after he brought one small cake for a party of twenty people.","t":"他帶了一個小蛋糕來二十人的派對之後，他的小氣成了辦公室裡的笑話。"},{"w":"be stingy with","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to give very little of something","c":"對…很吝嗇","s":"The new teacher is stingy with praise, so when she says \"good job,\" the students know they have done something really special.","t":"新老師很少給稱讚，所以當她說「做得好」時，學生就知道自己做了很特別的事。","a":"is stingy with"},{"w":"generous","p":"adj.","d":"willing to give more money, time, or help than is expected","c":"慷慨的","s":"Our neighbor is very generous; every Chinese New Year she gives red envelopes to all the children on our street.","t":"我們的鄰居非常慷慨；每年農曆新年她都會發紅包給我們這條街上所有的孩子。"},{"w":"stockings","p":"n.","d":"thin pieces of clothing that cover a woman's feet and legs","c":"長襪；絲襪","s":"She bought a new pair of black stockings to wear with her dress at the wedding, because her old ones had a hole.","t":"她買了一雙新的黑色絲襪搭配婚禮上穿的洋裝，因為舊的那雙破了一個洞。","h":1},{"w":"Christmas stocking","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large sock that children hang up for presents at Christmas","c":"聖誕襪","s":"On Christmas Eve, the children hung a Christmas stocking by the window and found it full of candy and small toys the next morning.","t":"聖誕夜，孩子們把聖誕襪掛在窗邊，第二天早上發現裡面裝滿了糖果和小玩具。"},{"w":"stock","p":"n.","d":"a supply of goods kept in a shop; a share in a company","c":"存貨；庫存；股票","s":"The shop has no more stock of that popular toy, and the manager says the next delivery will not come until next month.","t":"那家店那款熱門玩具已經沒有庫存了，經理說下一批要到下個月才會到。"},{"w":"in stock","p":"phr.","d":"available to buy in a shop","c":"有存貨","s":"I called the bookstore to ask whether the new dictionary was in stock, and they said only two copies were left.","t":"我打電話到書店問新字典是否有貨，他們說只剩兩本了。"},{"w":"strengthen","p":"v.","d":"to make something stronger","c":"加強；增強","s":"Swimming three times a week will strengthen your heart and lungs, and it is also gentle on your knees.","t":"每週游泳三次能強化你的心臟和肺，而且對膝蓋也很溫和。","h":1},{"w":"strength","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being strong; a good quality someone has","c":"力量；優點","s":"It took all his strength to push the broken car to the side of the road, and he had to rest for ten minutes afterwards.","t":"他用盡全身的力氣把壞掉的車推到路邊，之後不得不休息十分鐘。"},{"w":"strong","p":"adj.","d":"having a lot of physical power; not easily broken","c":"強壯的；堅固的","s":"This rope is strong enough to hold two people, so climbers trust it when they go up the steep rock wall.","t":"這條繩子堅固到可以承受兩個人，所以攀登者爬陡峭的岩壁時信任它。"},{"w":"strengths and weaknesses","p":"n.phr.","d":"the good and bad points of a person or thing","c":"優點和缺點","s":"Before the interview, write down your strengths and weaknesses so that you can answer the question honestly and without stopping to think.","t":"面試之前，寫下你的優點和缺點，這樣你就能誠實且不假思索地回答這個問題。"},{"w":"stripe","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow line of color","c":"條紋","s":"The national flag of Thailand has five horizontal stripes of red, white, and blue, with the blue one in the middle.","t":"泰國國旗有五條紅、白、藍的水平條紋，藍色在中間。","a":"stripes","h":1},{"w":"striped","p":"adj.","d":"having stripes","c":"有條紋的","s":"He wore a striped shirt with blue and white lines to the picnic, and it matched his sister's dress by accident.","t":"他穿著一件藍白線條的條紋襯衫去野餐，碰巧和他妹妹的洋裝很搭。"},{"w":"strip","p":"n.","d":"a long narrow piece of something","c":"狹長的一條（片）","s":"Cut the paper into a long strip, write your wish on it, and tie it to the tree like the other visitors have done.","t":"把紙剪成一長條，在上面寫下你的願望，然後像其他遊客一樣把它綁在樹上。"},{"w":"earn one's stripes","p":"v.phr.","d":"to prove by hard work that you deserve a position","c":"靠努力贏得地位","s":"The young cook earned his stripes by working twelve-hour days for two years before the owner finally made him head chef.","t":"這位年輕廚師每天工作十二小時、持續兩年靠努力贏得地位，老闆終於讓他當主廚。","a":"earned his stripes"},{"w":"strive, strove, striven","p":"v.","d":"to try very hard to achieve something","c":"努力；力求","s":"Our school encourages every student to strive for improvement rather than to compare their grades with others.","t":"我們學校鼓勵每位學生努力求進步，而不是和別人比較成績。","a":"strive","h":1},{"w":"strive for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a great effort to get or achieve something","c":"為…而努力","s":"Good writers always strive for clear, simple sentences, because readers should not have to work hard to understand them.","t":"好的作家總是力求寫出清楚、簡單的句子，因為讀者不該費力才能理解。"},{"w":"strive to do","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try hard to do something","c":"努力去做","s":"The city strives to reduce traffic jams by adding bus lanes, but many drivers still refuse to leave their cars at home.","t":"市政府努力透過增設公車專用道來減少塞車，但許多駕駛仍不肯把車留在家裡。","a":"strives to"},{"w":"effort","p":"n.","d":"the energy or hard work you use to do something","c":"努力","s":"She put a lot of effort into the science project, staying up late for a week to finish the model volcano.","t":"她在科學專題上投入了很多努力，熬夜一週完成了火山模型。"},{"w":"stroke","p":"n.","d":"a sudden illness when blood cannot reach part of the brain","c":"中風","s":"My grandfather had a stroke last winter, and he is still learning to walk again with the help of a therapist.","t":"我爺爺去年冬天中風，他仍在治療師的幫助下重新學習走路。","h":1},{"w":"stroke","p":"n.","d":"a movement of your arm in swimming; a single mark made with a pen or brush","c":"划水；一筆；一劃","s":"The swimmer has such a powerful stroke that she can cross the pool in fewer movements than anyone else on the team.","t":"這位泳者的划水非常有力，她過泳池所需的動作比隊上任何人都少。"},{"w":"stroke","p":"v.","d":"to move your hand gently over something, such as an animal","c":"輕撫","s":"The cat closed its eyes and began to purr as soon as the little girl started to stroke its soft fur.","t":"小女孩一開始輕撫貓咪柔軟的毛，牠就閉上眼睛開始發出呼嚕聲。"},{"w":"a stroke of luck","p":"n.phr.","d":"a sudden piece of good luck","c":"一次好運","s":"It was a stroke of luck that we met a farmer on the mountain road, because he gave us a ride just before the storm hit.","t":"我們在山路上遇到一位農夫真是一次好運，因為他在暴風雨來臨前載了我們一程。"},{"w":"submarine","p":"n.","d":"a ship that can travel under the sea","c":"潛水艇","s":"The navy's new submarine can stay under the sea for three months without coming up to the surface for air.","t":"海軍的新潛水艇可以在海底待三個月，不必浮出水面換氣。","h":1},{"w":"submarine","p":"adj.","d":"existing or happening under the sea","c":"海底的","s":"A submarine cable on the ocean floor carries most of the internet traffic between Taiwan and the United States.","t":"一條海底電纜承載了台灣和美國之間大部分的網路流量。"},{"w":"marine","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the sea and the creatures that live in it","c":"海洋的","s":"The new marine park protects the coral and the colorful fish that live around the small island in the south.","t":"新的海洋公園保護了南方小島周圍的珊瑚和色彩繽紛的魚類。"},{"w":"submarine sandwich","p":"n.phr.","d":"a long sandwich made with a whole bread roll","c":"潛艇堡","s":"For lunch we ordered a huge submarine sandwich filled with turkey, cheese, and vegetables, and we cut it into three pieces to share.","t":"午餐我們點了一個巨大的潛艇堡，裡面夾了火雞肉、起司和蔬菜，我們把它切成三塊分著吃。"},{"w":"sue","p":"v.","d":"to take legal action against someone in court","c":"控告；起訴","s":"The woman decided to sue the restaurant after she broke her leg on the wet floor that nobody had cleaned up.","t":"那位女士在沒人清理的濕地板上摔斷腿之後，決定控告那家餐廳。","h":1},{"w":"sue sb for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to take someone to court to get money for a loss","c":"因…控告某人","s":"The singer sued the magazine for a million dollars after the magazine printed a false story about her private life.","t":"在雜誌刊登關於她私生活的不實報導後，這位歌手控告雜誌社要求一百萬美元賠償。","a":"sued the magazine for"},{"w":"lawsuit","p":"n.","d":"a problem or complaint that a person brings to a court of law","c":"訴訟；官司","s":"The company is facing a lawsuit from customers who say the new phone's battery becomes too hot and can burn their hands.","t":"這家公司正面臨顧客的訴訟，他們說新手機的電池會變得太燙，可能燙傷手。"},{"w":"lawyer","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to advise people about the law and speak for them in court","c":"律師","s":"Before signing the contract to buy the house, my parents asked a lawyer to read every page and explain the difficult parts.","t":"在簽買房合約之前，我父母請一位律師讀過每一頁並解釋困難的部分。"},{"w":"suggestion","p":"n.","d":"an idea or plan that you offer for someone to think about","c":"建議；提議","s":"The teacher asked the class for a suggestion about where to go on the school trip, and most students chose the beach.","t":"老師問全班校外教學要去哪裡的建議，大多數學生選擇了海邊。","h":1},{"w":"suggest","p":"v.","d":"to give someone an idea or plan to think about","c":"建議；提議","s":"If you are always tired in the morning, I suggest going to bed an hour earlier and leaving your phone outside the bedroom.","t":"如果你早上總是很累，我建議早一小時上床，並把手機放在臥室外面。"},{"w":"make a suggestion","p":"v.phr.","d":"to offer an idea for others to consider","c":"提出建議","s":"May I make a suggestion? Instead of eating at the same noodle shop again, let's try the new Thai restaurant near the station.","t":"我可以提個建議嗎？與其再去同一家麵店，不如試試車站附近新開的泰式餐廳。"},{"w":"suggestion box","p":"n.phr.","d":"a box where people can leave written ideas for improvement","c":"意見箱","s":"The school put a suggestion box outside the office, and students can write down ideas for making the lunch menu better.","t":"學校在辦公室外放了一個意見箱，學生可以寫下讓午餐菜單更好的點子。"},{"w":"suggestive","p":"adj.","d":"making you think of something; hinting at something","c":"暗示的；引起聯想的","s":"The smell of fresh bread in the kitchen was suggestive of the mornings I spent at my grandmother's house as a child.","t":"廚房裡新鮮麵包的香味讓人聯想到我小時候在奶奶家度過的早晨。"},{"w":"summarize","p":"v.","d":"to give the main points of something in a short form","c":"總結；摘要","s":"After reading the long article, the students had to summarize it in three sentences using their own words.","t":"讀完這篇長文章後，學生必須用自己的話在三句話內總結它。","h":1},{"w":"summary","p":"n.","d":"a short statement of the main points of something","c":"摘要；總結","s":"The report is forty pages long, but there is a one-page summary at the front for people who do not have time to read it all.","t":"這份報告有四十頁，但前面有一頁摘要，給沒時間全部讀完的人看。"},{"w":"in summary","p":"phr.","d":"used to introduce a short statement of the main points","c":"總之；簡而言之","s":"In summary, the new library will be bigger, open later at night, and have free computers for every student to use.","t":"總之，新圖書館會更大、晚上開到更晚，而且有免費電腦供每位學生使用。","a":"In summary"},{"w":"to sum up","p":"phr.","d":"used when you want to give the main points at the end","c":"總而言之","s":"To sum up, our trip was tiring but wonderful, and all of us want to go back to Japan again next winter.","t":"總而言之，我們的旅行很累但很棒，我們所有人都想明年冬天再去日本。","a":"To sum up"}]},{"unit":38,"theme":"surgeon – tolerable","cards":[{"w":"surgeon","p":"n.","d":"a doctor who performs operations","c":"外科醫生","s":"The surgeon explained that the operation on my grandmother's knee would take about two hours and that she could walk again in a month.","t":"外科醫生解釋說，我奶奶的膝蓋手術大約需要兩小時，一個月後她就能再走路。","h":1},{"w":"surgery","p":"n.","d":"medical treatment in which a doctor cuts open the body to repair or remove something","c":"手術；外科","s":"After the car accident, he needed surgery on his broken leg, and the doctors put a metal plate inside to hold the bone.","t":"車禍之後，他斷掉的腿需要動手術，醫生在裡面放了一塊金屬板固定骨頭。","h":1},{"w":"have surgery","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have an operation","c":"動手術","s":"My aunt had surgery on her eyes last week, and now she can read the newspaper without wearing her thick glasses.","t":"我阿姨上週動了眼睛手術，現在不戴厚眼鏡也能看報紙了。","a":"had surgery"},{"w":"surgical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with surgery","c":"外科的；手術的","s":"Everyone in the operating room must wear a surgical mask and gloves so that no germs get into the patient's body.","t":"手術室裡的每個人都必須戴手術口罩和手套，這樣細菌才不會進入病人體內。"},{"w":"plastic surgery","p":"n.phr.","d":"surgery to change or repair the way a person looks","c":"整形手術","s":"The hospital offers free plastic surgery to children who were badly burned, so that they can smile and eat normally again.","t":"這家醫院為嚴重燒傷的兒童提供免費的整形手術，讓他們能再次正常微笑和吃東西。"},{"w":"surrender","p":"v.","d":"to stop fighting and admit that you have lost; to give something up","c":"投降；放棄；交出","s":"After three days without food or water, the soldiers inside the old fort finally agreed to surrender to the enemy.","t":"在沒有食物和水的三天之後，舊堡壘裡的士兵終於同意向敵人投降。","h":1},{"w":"surrender","p":"n.","d":"the act of stopping fighting and admitting defeat","c":"投降","s":"The surrender of the army was announced on the radio, and people in the city ran into the streets to celebrate the end of the war.","t":"軍隊投降的消息在廣播中宣布，城裡的人們跑到街上慶祝戰爭結束。"},{"w":"surrender to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give in to a feeling or to someone stronger","c":"向…屈服；向…投降","s":"The thief realized the police had surrounded the building, so he walked out with his hands up and surrendered to them.","t":"小偷發現警察包圍了大樓，所以他舉起雙手走出來，向他們投降。","a":"surrendered to"},{"w":"never surrender","p":"phr.","d":"to never give up, no matter how hard things are","c":"永不放棄","s":"The coach's favorite words are \"never surrender,\" and the team repeated them together before the final game of the season.","t":"教練最愛說的話是「永不放棄」，球隊在本季最後一場比賽前一起重複這句話。"},{"w":"surroundings","p":"n.","d":"everything that is around you in a place","c":"周圍環境","s":"It took the puppy a few days to get used to its new surroundings, but now it runs happily around every room in the house.","t":"小狗花了幾天才習慣新的周圍環境，但現在牠開心地在家裡每個房間跑來跑去。","h":1},{"w":"surround","p":"v.","d":"to be all around something or someone","c":"圍繞；包圍","s":"Tall green mountains surround the small village, so the only way to get there is by a narrow road along the river.","t":"高大的青山圍繞著這個小村莊，所以到那裡唯一的路是沿河的一條窄路。"},{"w":"be surrounded by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have people or things all around you","c":"被…包圍","s":"The famous singer was surrounded by hundreds of fans the moment she walked out of the airport, and she needed help to reach her car.","t":"這位著名歌手一走出機場就被數百名粉絲包圍，需要協助才能走到她的車。","a":"was surrounded by"},{"w":"surrounding","p":"adj.","d":"all around a particular place","c":"周圍的；附近的","s":"The flood did not only hit the city; many farms in the surrounding villages were also under water for a week.","t":"洪水不只襲擊了城市；周圍村莊的許多農田也淹在水裡一週。"},{"w":"suspicious","p":"adj.","d":"feeling that someone may be doing something wrong; making people feel this way","c":"懷疑的；可疑的","s":"The bank became suspicious when a man tried to take all the money out of an old woman's account in one afternoon.","t":"當一名男子試圖在一個下午把一位老婦人帳戶裡的錢全部領出時，銀行起了懷疑。","h":1},{"w":"be suspicious of","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to not trust someone or something","c":"對…起疑；懷疑","s":"You should be suspicious of any e-mail that asks for your password, even if it looks like it comes from your own bank.","t":"你應該懷疑任何要求你輸入密碼的電子郵件，即使它看起來像來自你自己的銀行。"},{"w":"suspect","p":"v.","d":"to think that something is probably true, especially something bad","c":"懷疑；猜想","s":"The teacher began to suspect that two students had copied each other's homework because every answer was exactly the same.","t":"老師開始懷疑兩個學生互相抄作業，因為每個答案都一模一樣。"},{"w":"suspect","p":"n.","d":"a person the police think may have done a crime","c":"嫌疑犯","s":"The police asked the suspect where he was on Friday night, and he said he had been watching a movie with friends.","t":"警察問嫌疑犯星期五晚上在哪裡，他說他和朋友在看電影。"},{"w":"suspicion","p":"n.","d":"a feeling that someone has done something wrong","c":"懷疑；嫌疑","s":"The manager had a strong suspicion that money was missing from the shop, so he checked the camera recordings every night.","t":"經理強烈懷疑店裡的錢少了，所以他每晚都檢查監視器錄影。"},{"w":"sway","p":"v.","d":"to move slowly from side to side","c":"搖擺；搖晃","s":"The tall palm trees began to sway in the strong wind, and we knew that the typhoon was getting closer to the island.","t":"高大的棕櫚樹在強風中開始搖晃，我們知道颱風正逐漸接近這座島。","h":1},{"w":"sway","p":"v.","d":"to change someone's opinion or decision","c":"影響；左右","s":"The lawyer's emotional speech managed to sway the jury, and in the end they decided that the young man was not guilty.","t":"律師充滿感情的陳述成功左右了陪審團，最後他們判定這名年輕人無罪。"},{"w":"sway","p":"n.","d":"power or influence over people","c":"影響力；支配","s":"That popular video blogger has a lot of sway over teenagers, so companies pay her to talk about their products.","t":"那位人氣影音部落客對青少年有很大的影響力，所以公司付錢請她介紹產品。"},{"w":"sway from side to side","p":"v.phr.","d":"to move back and forth","c":"左右搖擺","s":"The old boat swayed from side to side on the rough sea, and several passengers felt so sick that they could not stand up.","t":"舊船在波濤洶湧的海上左右搖擺，好幾位乘客暈得站不起來。","a":"swayed from side to side"},{"w":"syllable","p":"n.","d":"a unit of sound in a word that has one vowel sound","c":"音節","s":"The word \"banana\" has three syllables, and when you say it, you should put the stress on the second one.","t":"banana 這個字有三個音節，說的時候重音應該放在第二個音節上。","a":"syllables","h":1},{"w":"stressed syllable","p":"n.phr.","d":"the part of a word that is said more strongly","c":"重音節","s":"In the word \"computer,\" the stressed syllable is \"pu,\" so you say it louder and longer than the other two parts.","t":"在 computer 這個字裡，重音節是 pu，所以你要把它說得比其他兩個部分更大聲、更長。"},{"w":"one-syllable word","p":"n.phr.","d":"a word with only one vowel sound, like \"cat\"","c":"單音節字","s":"The teacher asked the children to clap once for every one-syllable word in the poem, such as \"sun,\" \"moon,\" and \"star.\"","t":"老師請孩子們為詩裡的每個單音節字拍一次手，例如 sun、moon 和 star。"},{"w":"pronounce","p":"v.","d":"to make the sound of a word in the correct way","c":"發音","s":"Many students find it hard to pronounce the word \"comfortable,\" because one of the syllables is almost silent in natural speech.","t":"許多學生覺得 comfortable 這個字很難發音，因為在自然的口語中其中一個音節幾乎不發音。"},{"w":"sympathetic","p":"adj.","d":"showing that you understand and care about someone's problems","c":"有同情心的；體諒的","s":"When I told my boss that my mother was in the hospital, she was very sympathetic and told me to take the whole week off.","t":"當我告訴老闆我媽媽住院時，她非常體諒，叫我整個星期都休假。","h":1},{"w":"sympathy","p":"n.","d":"the feeling of being sorry for someone who is in trouble","c":"同情；慰問","s":"Hundreds of people sent cards and flowers to show their sympathy for the families who lost their homes in the fire.","t":"數百人寄送卡片和鮮花，對在火災中失去家園的家庭表達同情。","h":1},{"w":"sympathize with","p":"v.phr.","d":"to understand and feel sorry about someone's problems","c":"同情；體諒","s":"I really sympathize with the new students, because I also felt lost and lonely during my first month at this school.","t":"我真的很同情新生，因為我在這所學校的第一個月也感到迷惘又孤單。"},{"w":"have sympathy for","p":"v.phr.","d":"to feel sorry for someone","c":"對…感到同情","s":"It is hard to have sympathy for a driver who gets a ticket for parking in a space meant for people in wheelchairs.","t":"很難同情一個因為停在輪椅使用者專用車位而被開罰單的駕駛。"},{"w":"sympathetically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that shows you understand someone's feelings","c":"同情地；體諒地","s":"The nurse listened sympathetically as the old man talked about how much he missed his wife, and she held his hand the whole time.","t":"護理師體諒地聽著老先生訴說他多麼想念妻子，整段時間都握著他的手。"},{"w":"systematic","p":"adj.","d":"done according to a careful plan or system","c":"有系統的；有條理的","s":"The police made a systematic search of every room in the building, starting from the roof and working their way down.","t":"警方對大樓裡的每個房間進行有系統的搜索，從屋頂開始逐層往下。","h":1},{"w":"system","p":"n.","d":"a set of connected things or rules that work together","c":"系統；制度","s":"The new MRT system connects the airport to the city center, so travelers can reach their hotels in less than forty minutes.","t":"新的捷運系統連接機場和市中心，所以旅客可以在四十分鐘內到達飯店。"},{"w":"systematically","p":"adv.","d":"in a careful, well-organized way","c":"有系統地","s":"Instead of guessing, she systematically tested each wire in the machine until she found the one that was broken.","t":"她沒有用猜的，而是有系統地測試機器裡的每條電線，直到找到壞掉的那一條。"},{"w":"solar system","p":"n.phr.","d":"the sun and the planets that go around it","c":"太陽系","s":"Jupiter is the largest planet in our solar system, and more than one thousand Earths could fit inside it.","t":"木星是我們太陽系裡最大的行星，一千多個地球可以裝進它裡面。"},{"w":"technician","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to work with or repair machines and equipment","c":"技術人員；技師","s":"A technician from the phone company came this morning to fix our internet connection, and now the Wi-Fi works again.","t":"電話公司的一位技術人員今天早上來修我們的網路連線，現在 Wi-Fi 又能用了。","h":1},{"w":"technique","p":"n.","d":"a particular way of doing something that needs skill","c":"技巧；技術","s":"The swimming coach showed us a new breathing technique that helps you swim longer without feeling tired.","t":"游泳教練教我們一種新的呼吸技巧，能幫助你游得更久而不覺得累。"},{"w":"technical","p":"adj.","d":"connected with the practical use of machines or science","c":"技術上的；專業的","s":"The concert was delayed for half an hour because of a technical problem with the lights and the sound system.","t":"演唱會因為燈光和音響系統的技術問題延後了半小時。"},{"w":"lab technician","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who does practical work in a laboratory","c":"實驗室技術員","s":"The lab technician prepared the blood samples carefully before the doctor came to check the results of the tests.","t":"實驗室技術員在醫生來檢查檢驗結果之前，仔細地準備血液樣本。"},{"w":"technological","p":"adj.","d":"connected with technology","c":"科技的；技術的","s":"The smartphone is probably the greatest technological change of the last twenty years, and few people can live without one now.","t":"智慧型手機可能是過去二十年最大的科技變革，現在很少人能沒有它。","h":1},{"w":"technology","p":"n.","d":"machines and methods based on scientific knowledge","c":"科技；技術","s":"Thanks to modern technology, students in a small village can now take online classes with teachers from around the world.","t":"多虧了現代科技，小村莊的學生現在可以和世界各地的老師上線上課程。"},{"w":"high-tech","p":"adj.","d":"using the most modern machines and methods","c":"高科技的","s":"The new hospital is a high-tech building where robots deliver medicine and computers keep track of every patient.","t":"這家新醫院是一棟高科技建築，機器人送藥，電腦追蹤每位病人的狀況。"},{"w":"technologically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is connected with technology","c":"在科技上","s":"Japan is one of the most technologically advanced countries in the world, yet many people there still prefer to use cash.","t":"日本是世界上科技最先進的國家之一，但那裡許多人仍然偏好使用現金。"},{"w":"telegraph","p":"n.","d":"an old system for sending messages by electric signals along wires","c":"電報（系統）","s":"Before the telephone was invented, the telegraph was the fastest way to send a message from one city to another.","t":"在電話發明之前，電報是把訊息從一個城市傳到另一個城市最快的方式。","h":1},{"w":"telegraph","p":"v.","d":"to send a message by telegraph; to make your plans clear without meaning to","c":"發電報；暴露（意圖）","s":"The boxer lost the fight because he would telegraph every punch, and his opponent could see each one coming.","t":"這位拳擊手輸掉比賽，因為他每一拳都事先暴露，對手都能看出他要出拳。"},{"w":"telegram","p":"n.","d":"a message sent by telegraph","c":"電報","s":"My grandfather still keeps the telegram that told him he had passed the university exam more than sixty years ago.","t":"我爺爺至今還保留著六十多年前通知他通過大學考試的那封電報。"},{"w":"telephone","p":"n.","d":"a machine used to talk to someone in another place","c":"電話","s":"In the 1980s, most families in Taiwan had only one telephone in the living room, so everyone could hear your conversations.","t":"一九八〇年代，台灣大多數家庭客廳裡只有一支電話，所以每個人都能聽到你的談話。"},{"w":"telescope","p":"n.","d":"an instrument shaped like a tube that makes far-away objects look closer","c":"望遠鏡","s":"Through the telescope we could see the rings of Saturn clearly, and my little brother shouted with excitement.","t":"透過望遠鏡我們可以清楚看到土星的環，我弟弟興奮地大叫。","h":1},{"w":"microscope","p":"n.","d":"an instrument that makes very small things look bigger","c":"顯微鏡","s":"Under the microscope, a single drop of pond water was full of tiny living things moving in every direction.","t":"在顯微鏡下，一滴池塘水裡充滿了往四面八方移動的微小生物。"},{"w":"telescope","p":"v.","d":"to make something shorter by pushing its parts into each other","c":"縮短；套疊","s":"The long story was telescoped into a two-minute video, so many important details about the hero's childhood were left out.","t":"這個長篇故事被壓縮成兩分鐘的影片，所以許多關於主角童年的重要細節都被省略了。","a":"telescoped"},{"w":"space telescope","p":"n.phr.","d":"a telescope that is sent into space to look at the universe","c":"太空望遠鏡","s":"The new space telescope has sent back pictures of stars so far away that their light left them billions of years ago.","t":"新的太空望遠鏡傳回了極遠恆星的照片，它們的光在數十億年前就已經出發了。"},{"w":"tendency","p":"n.","d":"the way a person or thing is likely to behave or happen","c":"傾向；趨勢","s":"My brother has a tendency to leave everything until the last minute, so he often stays up all night before an exam.","t":"我哥哥有把所有事情留到最後一刻的傾向，所以他常常在考試前熬夜一整晚。","h":1},{"w":"tend to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to usually do something or to be likely to do it","c":"往往；傾向於","s":"People tend to eat more when they watch TV during dinner, because they do not notice how full they already are.","t":"人們在晚餐時看電視往往會吃得更多，因為他們沒注意到自己已經多飽了。"},{"w":"tend","p":"v.","d":"to take care of something or someone","c":"照料；照顧","s":"My grandmother gets up at five every morning to tend her garden, and her roses are the most beautiful on the street.","t":"我奶奶每天早上五點起床照料她的花園，她的玫瑰是這條街上最美的。"},{"w":"have a tendency to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be likely to do something, often something bad","c":"有…的傾向","s":"Old wooden houses have a tendency to catch fire easily, so the city asks owners to check their electric wires every year.","t":"老舊的木造房屋容易著火，所以市政府要求屋主每年檢查電線。"},{"w":"tense","p":"adj.","d":"nervous and unable to relax; with muscles tight","c":"緊張的；緊繃的","s":"The whole class was tense as the teacher slowly handed back the test papers, and nobody said a single word.","t":"老師慢慢發回考卷時，全班都很緊張，沒有人說一句話。","h":1},{"w":"tension","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of worry that makes it hard to relax; a situation in which people do not trust each other","c":"緊張；緊張關係","s":"There was a lot of tension in the room before the interview started, and some of the applicants kept checking their phones.","t":"面試開始前房間裡充滿了緊張氣氛，有些應徵者一直在看手機。","h":1},{"w":"tense","p":"n.","d":"the form of a verb that shows when an action happens","c":"時態","s":"Remember to use the past tense when you write about your weekend, because all of those things have already happened.","t":"寫你的週末時記得用過去式，因為那些事情都已經發生了。"},{"w":"tense up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to become stiff or nervous","c":"變得緊繃；緊張起來","s":"Try not to tense up when the dentist starts the drill; take slow, deep breaths and the visit will be over soon.","t":"牙醫開始鑽牙時盡量不要緊繃起來；慢慢深呼吸，看診很快就會結束。"},{"w":"ease the tension","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a situation less stressful","c":"緩和緊張氣氛","s":"The host told a funny story about his first day at work to ease the tension before the serious part of the meeting began.","t":"主持人在會議正式開始前講了一個他上班第一天的趣事來緩和緊張氣氛。"},{"w":"terror","p":"n.","d":"a feeling of great fear","c":"恐懼；驚恐","s":"The children screamed in terror when the lights suddenly went out during the ghost story at the summer camp.","t":"夏令營講鬼故事時燈突然熄滅，孩子們驚恐地尖叫。","h":1},{"w":"terrible","p":"adj.","d":"very bad; causing fear or great unhappiness","c":"可怕的；糟糕的","s":"We had a terrible time on the trip because it rained every single day and the hotel room had no hot water.","t":"我們這趟旅行過得很糟糕，因為每天都下雨，而且飯店房間沒有熱水。"},{"w":"terrify","p":"v.","d":"to make someone extremely afraid","c":"使驚恐；嚇壞","s":"Loud fireworks terrify my dog, so on New Year's Eve we keep him inside with the windows closed and the music on.","t":"巨大的煙火聲會嚇壞我的狗，所以除夕夜我們把牠留在屋裡，關上窗戶並放音樂。"},{"w":"terrorist","p":"n.","d":"a person who uses violence to frighten people for political reasons","c":"恐怖分子","s":"The airport increased its checks after the news reported that a terrorist had tried to get on a plane with a weapon.","t":"新聞報導一名恐怖分子試圖帶武器上飛機之後，機場加強了安檢。"},{"w":"in terror","p":"phr.","d":"with a feeling of great fear","c":"驚恐地","s":"The villagers ran in terror toward the hills as the river broke through the wall and rushed into the streets.","t":"河水沖破堤防湧進街道時，村民們驚恐地跑向山丘。"},{"w":"theme","p":"n.","d":"the main subject or idea of a talk, book, or event","c":"主題","s":"The theme of this year's school festival is \"the ocean,\" so every class is decorating its room with fish and waves.","t":"今年校慶的主題是「海洋」，所以每個班級都用魚和海浪裝飾教室。","h":1},{"w":"theme park","p":"n.phr.","d":"a large park with rides and shows based on one idea","c":"主題樂園","s":"We spent the whole day at the theme park, and the roller coaster was so popular that we waited an hour to ride it.","t":"我們在主題樂園待了一整天，雲霄飛車太受歡迎，我們排了一小時才坐到。"},{"w":"theme song","p":"n.phr.","d":"a song that is played at the start of a TV show or film","c":"主題曲","s":"Everyone in my family knows the theme song of that old cartoon, and we still sing it together when it comes on TV.","t":"我們全家都會唱那部老卡通的主題曲，電視上播出時我們還是會一起唱。"},{"w":"main theme","p":"n.phr.","d":"the most important idea in a piece of writing or art","c":"主要主題","s":"The main theme of the novel is friendship, and the writer shows how two boys from different countries learn to trust each other.","t":"這部小說的主要主題是友誼，作者描寫來自不同國家的兩個男孩如何學會信任彼此。"},{"w":"thorough","p":"adj.","d":"done carefully and completely, with attention to every detail","c":"徹底的；仔細的","s":"The doctor gave my father a thorough check-up, testing his heart, blood, and eyes before saying that he was healthy.","t":"醫生為我爸爸做了徹底的檢查，檢測了心臟、血液和眼睛之後才說他很健康。","h":1},{"w":"thoroughly","p":"adv.","d":"completely and carefully","c":"徹底地；完全地","s":"Wash the vegetables thoroughly under running water before you cook them, because there may still be sand and chemicals on them.","t":"烹煮蔬菜前先用流動的水把它們徹底洗乾淨，因為上面可能還有沙子和化學物質。"},{"w":"thoroughness","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being careful and complete","c":"徹底；周密","s":"Her boss praised her thoroughness, because she checked every number in the report twice and found three mistakes nobody else had seen.","t":"老闆稱讚她的周密，因為她把報告裡每個數字都核對了兩次，找到三個別人沒發現的錯誤。"},{"w":"a thorough search","p":"n.phr.","d":"a careful search of every part of a place","c":"徹底的搜查","s":"After a thorough search of the whole house, we finally found the lost cat sleeping inside a box in the garage.","t":"徹底搜查整間屋子之後，我們終於發現失蹤的貓在車庫的箱子裡睡覺。"},{"w":"thoughtful","p":"adj.","d":"kind and thinking about what other people need; quiet and thinking deeply","c":"體貼的；深思的","s":"It was very thoughtful of you to bring soup and medicine when you heard that I had caught a cold.","t":"你聽說我感冒就帶湯和藥來，真是太體貼了。","h":1},{"w":"thoughtfully","p":"adv.","d":"in a kind way; in a way that shows deep thinking","c":"體貼地；若有所思地","s":"The old man looked thoughtfully at the photo of his hometown for a long time before he answered our question.","t":"老先生若有所思地看著家鄉的照片看了很久，才回答我們的問題。"},{"w":"thoughtless","p":"adj.","d":"not thinking about how your actions affect other people","c":"欠考慮的；不體貼的","s":"It was thoughtless of him to play loud music at midnight when he knew his neighbor had to get up at five for work.","t":"他明知道鄰居五點要起床上班，還在半夜放很大聲的音樂，真是不體貼。"},{"w":"thought","p":"n.","d":"an idea or opinion; the act of thinking","c":"想法；思考","s":"I have been giving a lot of thought to your offer, and I have decided to accept the job in Kaohsiung next month.","t":"我對你的提議做了很多思考，決定下個月接受高雄的那份工作。"},{"w":"tickle","p":"v.","d":"to touch someone lightly so that they laugh","c":"搔癢；呵癢","s":"My little sister laughs so hard when I tickle her feet that she can hardly breathe, and then she begs me to stop.","t":"我搔妹妹的腳時她笑得幾乎喘不過氣，然後求我停下來。","h":1},{"w":"tickle","p":"n.","d":"a light touch that makes you laugh; an uncomfortable feeling in the throat","c":"搔癢；喉嚨發癢","s":"I have had a tickle in my throat since this morning, so I am drinking warm honey water to make it feel better.","t":"從今天早上開始我的喉嚨就一直發癢，所以我在喝溫蜂蜜水讓它舒服一點。"},{"w":"ticklish","p":"adj.","d":"laughing easily when touched lightly","c":"怕癢的","s":"My cousin is so ticklish that she starts laughing as soon as you move your hand near her neck.","t":"我表妹非常怕癢，你的手一靠近她的脖子她就開始笑。"},{"w":"be tickled pink","p":"phr.","d":"to be very pleased about something","c":"非常高興","s":"Grandma was tickled pink when all twelve grandchildren came home for her eightieth birthday, and she could not stop smiling.","t":"十二個孫子孫女全都回家為奶奶慶祝八十大壽時，她非常高興，笑得合不攏嘴。","a":"was tickled pink"},{"w":"timetable","p":"n.","d":"a list of the times when classes, buses, or trains happen","c":"時刻表；課表","s":"According to the timetable, the last train to Taipei leaves at eleven thirty, so we must finish dinner before eleven.","t":"根據時刻表，開往台北的最後一班火車十一點半發車，所以我們必須在十一點前吃完晚餐。","h":1},{"w":"class timetable","p":"n.phr.","d":"a list showing when each school lesson takes place","c":"課表","s":"The new class timetable puts PE on Friday afternoon, so students can go home early after the game without changing clothes.","t":"新課表把體育課排在星期五下午，所以學生比賽後不用換衣服就能早點回家。"},{"w":"schedule","p":"n.","d":"a plan of things that will happen and when","c":"時間表；行程","s":"My schedule this week is very full, with three meetings on Monday and a trip to Taichung on Wednesday.","t":"我這週的行程非常滿，星期一有三個會議，星期三要去台中。"},{"w":"on time","p":"phr.","d":"at the correct time; not late","c":"準時","s":"The bus was on time this morning for the first time in a week, so I actually arrived at school before the bell rang.","t":"今天早上公車一週以來第一次準時，所以我真的在鐘響前到了學校。"},{"w":"timid","p":"adj.","d":"shy and easily frightened; not brave","c":"膽小的；羞怯的","s":"The new student was so timid that she did not speak to anyone for a week, but now she has many friends in the class.","t":"新同學非常羞怯，一整週沒跟任何人說話，但現在她在班上有很多朋友。","h":1},{"w":"timidly","p":"adv.","d":"in a shy or frightened way","c":"膽怯地","s":"The little boy timidly raised his hand and asked the famous scientist whether robots could ever feel happy.","t":"小男孩膽怯地舉起手，問那位著名的科學家機器人會不會感到快樂。"},{"w":"timidity","p":"n.","d":"the quality of being shy and easily frightened","c":"膽小；羞怯","s":"Her timidity disappeared the moment she stepped onto the stage, and she sang louder than anyone else in the show.","t":"她一踏上舞台，羞怯就消失了，她唱得比節目裡任何人都大聲。"},{"w":"brave","p":"adj.","d":"not afraid of danger or difficult situations","c":"勇敢的","s":"The brave young man jumped into the cold river to save a child who had fallen in while chasing a ball.","t":"這位勇敢的年輕人跳進冰冷的河裡，救起一個追球時掉進河裡的孩子。"},{"w":"tolerable","p":"adj.","d":"bad but not so bad that you cannot accept it","c":"可忍受的；尚可的","s":"The pain in my tooth was tolerable during the day, but at night it got so bad that I could not sleep at all.","t":"我牙齒的疼痛白天還可以忍受，但到了晚上痛得我完全睡不著。","h":1},{"w":"tolerate","p":"v.","d":"to accept something unpleasant without complaining; to allow","c":"忍受；容忍","s":"Our teacher will not tolerate phones in class, and anyone caught using one has to leave it in her desk until Friday.","t":"我們老師不容忍上課用手機，任何被抓到的人都得把手機放在她桌子裡直到星期五。"},{"w":"tolerance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to accept things you do not like; the willingness to accept different ideas","c":"寬容；容忍","s":"A good city needs tolerance, so that people with different religions and languages can live together in peace.","t":"一個好的城市需要寬容，這樣不同宗教和語言的人才能和平地生活在一起。"},{"w":"tolerant","p":"adj.","d":"willing to accept ideas or behavior different from your own","c":"寬容的","s":"My grandparents are very tolerant of young people's fashion, and they never comment on my brother's pink hair.","t":"我的祖父母對年輕人的時尚非常寬容，他們從不評論我哥哥的粉紅色頭髮。"},{"w":"intolerable","p":"adj.","d":"so bad that you cannot accept it","c":"無法忍受的","s":"The heat in the factory became intolerable in August, so the workers asked the owner to install air conditioning.","t":"八月時工廠裡的高溫變得無法忍受，所以工人要求老闆安裝冷氣。"}]},{"unit":39,"theme":"tolerance – usage","cards":[{"w":"tolerance","p":"n.","d":"the ability to accept people or ideas that are different from yours","c":"寬容；容忍","s":"Our teacher says that tolerance is important in a big city because people from many cultures must live together peacefully.","t":"我們老師說在大城市裡寬容很重要，因為來自許多文化的人必須和平地一起生活。","h":1},{"w":"tolerant","p":"adj.","d":"willing to accept behavior or ideas that you may not like","c":"寬容的；容忍的","s":"My grandmother is very tolerant of noisy children, so she never complains when my cousins run around her house.","t":"我奶奶對吵鬧的孩子非常寬容，所以我表弟妹在她家跑來跑去時她從不抱怨。","h":1},{"w":"tolerate","p":"v.","d":"to accept something unpleasant without complaining or stopping it","c":"容忍；忍受","s":"The new manager will not tolerate people who arrive late, so everyone in the office now comes in before nine.","t":"新經理不會容忍遲到的人，所以辦公室裡的每個人現在都九點前到。","h":1},{"w":"tolerable","p":"adj.","d":"bad but not so bad that you cannot accept it","c":"可以忍受的","s":"The pain in my knee is tolerable when I walk slowly, but it becomes much worse whenever I try to run.","t":"我慢慢走時膝蓋的疼痛還可以忍受，但每當我試著跑步，疼痛就會變得嚴重許多。"},{"w":"intolerable","p":"adj.","d":"so bad or unpleasant that you cannot accept it","c":"無法忍受的","s":"The heat inside the old bus was intolerable in July, and several passengers asked the driver to open all the windows.","t":"七月時舊公車裡的熱氣令人無法忍受，好幾位乘客要求司機把所有窗戶打開。"},{"w":"intolerance","p":"n.","d":"the refusal to accept people or ideas that are different","c":"不寬容；偏狹","s":"Racial intolerance was common in that town fifty years ago, but today people of all backgrounds work and study together there.","t":"五十年前那個鎮上種族不寬容很常見，但今天各種背景的人都在那裡一起工作和讀書。"},{"w":"be tolerant of","p":"adj.phr.","d":"to accept and allow something you may not like","c":"對…寬容","s":"A good coach is tolerant of small mistakes because young players need time to learn and gain confidence.","t":"好教練對小錯誤寬容，因為年輕球員需要時間學習並建立信心。","a":"is tolerant of"},{"w":"zero tolerance","p":"n.phr.","d":"a rule that punishes even the smallest offense","c":"零容忍","s":"The school has a zero tolerance policy on bullying, which means any student who hurts another will be punished at once.","t":"學校對霸凌採取零容忍政策，這表示任何傷害他人的學生都會立刻受到處罰。"},{"w":"tomb","p":"n.","d":"a large grave, often a stone building, where a dead person is buried","c":"墳墓；墓穴","s":"Thousands of tourists visit the ancient tomb every year, but no one is allowed to touch the stone walls inside.","t":"每年有成千上萬的遊客參觀這座古老的墳墓，但沒有人可以碰裡面的石牆。","h":1},{"w":"tombstone","p":"n.","d":"a stone on a grave with the dead person's name on it","c":"墓碑","s":"The old tombstone was covered with grass, so we could hardly read the name and the dates carved on it.","t":"那塊古老的墓碑長滿了草，所以我們幾乎看不清上面刻的名字和日期。"},{"w":"Tomb Sweeping Day","p":"n.phr.","d":"a Chinese holiday when families clean their ancestors' graves","c":"清明節","s":"On Tomb Sweeping Day, my whole family drives to the hills to clean my grandfather's grave and offer him fresh flowers.","t":"清明節那天，我們全家開車到山上清掃爺爺的墳墓，並獻上鮮花。"},{"w":"tortoise","p":"n.","d":"a slow animal with a hard shell that lives on land","c":"陸龜；烏龜","s":"The tortoise in the zoo is over one hundred years old, and it moves so slowly that children often think it is sleeping.","t":"動物園裡的那隻陸龜已經超過一百歲了，牠動作慢到孩子們常以為牠在睡覺。","h":1},{"w":"the tortoise and the hare","p":"n.phr.","d":"a famous story in which a slow animal beats a fast one","c":"龜兔賽跑","s":"Our teacher told us the story of the tortoise and the hare to remind us that working steadily is better than rushing and then giving up.","t":"老師講了龜兔賽跑的故事，提醒我們穩定努力勝過匆忙衝刺然後放棄。"},{"w":"tortoiseshell","p":"n.","d":"a brown and yellow pattern like the shell of a tortoise","c":"玳瑁色；龜甲花紋","s":"She bought a pair of tortoiseshell glasses because the brown and yellow pattern looked warmer than plain black frames.","t":"她買了一副玳瑁色的眼鏡，因為棕黃相間的花紋看起來比純黑的鏡框溫暖。"},{"w":"torture","p":"n.","d":"the act of causing great pain to someone, often as a punishment","c":"酷刑；折磨","s":"In the past, torture was used to make prisoners talk, but today most countries have laws against such cruel treatment.","t":"過去酷刑被用來讓囚犯開口，但今天大多數國家都有法律禁止這種殘忍的對待。","h":1},{"w":"torture","p":"v.","d":"to cause great physical or mental pain to someone","c":"折磨；拷打","s":"Please do not torture your little brother by hiding his favorite toy; he has been crying for almost an hour.","t":"請不要藏起弟弟最愛的玩具來折磨他；他已經哭了快一個小時了。"},{"w":"be tortured by","p":"v.phr.","d":"to suffer great mental pain because of something","c":"飽受…折磨","s":"For years the driver was tortured by guilt because he believed the accident could have been avoided if he had slowed down.","t":"多年來那位司機飽受罪惡感折磨，因為他相信如果他當時減速，意外就可以避免。","a":"was tortured by"},{"w":"torturer","p":"n.","d":"a person who tortures others","c":"施刑者；折磨者","s":"In the movie, the cruel torturer finally feels sorry for what he did and helps the prisoners escape from the castle.","t":"電影裡那個殘忍的施刑者最後對自己的所作所為感到後悔，並幫助囚犯逃出城堡。"},{"w":"tragedy","p":"n.","d":"a very sad event, especially one in which people die","c":"悲劇；慘劇","s":"The fire at the night market was a terrible tragedy, and the whole city held a quiet ceremony for the victims.","t":"夜市那場大火是一場可怕的悲劇，全市為罹難者舉行了安靜的追思儀式。","h":1},{"w":"tragedy","p":"n.","d":"a serious play or story with a sad ending","c":"悲劇（戲劇）","s":"Romeo and Juliet is a famous tragedy by Shakespeare, and our class will perform it in English at the school festival.","t":"《羅密歐與茱麗葉》是莎士比亞著名的悲劇，我們班將在校慶上用英文演出它。","h":1},{"w":"tragic","p":"adj.","d":"very sad, often because someone dies or suffers","c":"悲慘的；悲劇性的","s":"It was tragic that the young singer died in a car crash just one week before her first big concert.","t":"那位年輕歌手在她第一場大型演唱會前一週死於車禍，真是悲慘。"},{"w":"tragically","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is very sad","c":"悲慘地","s":"The story ends tragically when the two best friends are separated by the war and never see each other again.","t":"故事悲慘地結束，兩位最好的朋友被戰爭拆散，再也沒有見到彼此。"},{"w":"end in tragedy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to finish with a very sad event","c":"以悲劇收場","s":"The climbing trip ended in tragedy when a sudden storm hit the mountain and two climbers were lost in the snow.","t":"那次登山之旅以悲劇收場，突如其來的暴風雪襲擊山區，兩名登山者在雪中失蹤。","a":"ended in tragedy"},{"w":"transfer","p":"v.","d":"to move someone or something from one place to another","c":"轉移；調動；轉學","s":"The company decided to transfer my father to its office in Kaohsiung, so we will move there next summer.","t":"公司決定把我爸爸調到高雄的辦公室，所以我們明年夏天會搬去那裡。","h":1},{"w":"transfer","p":"n.","d":"the act of moving from one place, job, or school to another","c":"轉移；轉乘；調動","s":"The MRT map shows that the transfer between the red line and the blue line takes only about three minutes on foot.","t":"捷運地圖顯示紅線和藍線之間的轉乘步行只需大約三分鐘。"},{"w":"transfer to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change to a different bus, train, school, or job","c":"轉乘；轉到","s":"If you want to reach the airport, you need to transfer to the purple line at Sanchong Station and ride four more stops.","t":"如果你要到機場，你需要在三重站轉乘紫線，再搭四站。"},{"w":"transferable","p":"adj.","d":"able to be moved or used in a different place or situation","c":"可轉讓的；可轉移的","s":"The skills you learn in a part-time job, such as teamwork and patience, are transferable to almost any career you choose later.","t":"你在打工中學到的技能，例如團隊合作和耐心，都可轉移到你日後選擇的幾乎任何職業。"},{"w":"bank transfer","p":"n.phr.","d":"a way of sending money directly from one bank account to another","c":"銀行轉帳","s":"My landlord prefers a bank transfer to cash because the record on his phone shows exactly when the rent was paid.","t":"我的房東比較喜歡銀行轉帳而不是現金，因為他手機上的紀錄會清楚顯示房租是什麼時候付的。"},{"w":"transform","p":"v.","d":"to change something completely, usually in a good way","c":"使改變；使轉變","s":"A few trees and some bright paint can transform a grey parking lot into a pleasant place where neighbors like to sit.","t":"幾棵樹和一些鮮豔的油漆就能把灰色的停車場改造成鄰居喜歡坐坐的舒適場所。","h":1},{"w":"transform ... into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to change something into something different","c":"把…變成…","s":"Over ten years, the old factory was transformed into a modern art museum, and now it attracts visitors from all over Asia.","t":"十年間，那座舊工廠被改造成一座現代藝術博物館，現在吸引了來自全亞洲的遊客。","a":"was transformed into"},{"w":"transformation","p":"n.","d":"a complete change in the appearance or character of something","c":"轉變；變化","s":"The transformation of the shy boy into a confident speaker surprised everyone who had known him in junior high school.","t":"那個害羞男孩轉變成自信的演說者，讓所有國中就認識他的人都很驚訝。"},{"w":"transformer","p":"n.","d":"a machine that changes electricity from one voltage to another","c":"變壓器","s":"The lights in our neighborhood went out for two hours after lightning hit the transformer on the pole outside our school.","t":"閃電擊中我們學校外電線桿上的變壓器後，我們社區的燈熄滅了兩個小時。"},{"w":"translate","p":"v.","d":"to change words from one language into another","c":"翻譯","s":"Could you help me translate this letter from my Japanese host family, since I only understand a few simple words?","t":"你能幫我翻譯這封日本寄宿家庭寄來的信嗎？因為我只看得懂幾個簡單的字。","h":1},{"w":"translation","p":"n.","d":"words that have been changed from one language into another","c":"翻譯；譯文","s":"The English translation of the novel was published last month, and reviewers say it keeps the warm style of the original.","t":"這本小說的英文譯本上個月出版了，評論者說它保留了原作溫暖的風格。","h":1},{"w":"translator","p":"n.","d":"a person whose job is to change written words into another language","c":"翻譯者；譯者","s":"My aunt works as a translator for a publishing company, and she has turned more than thirty children's books into Chinese.","t":"我阿姨在一家出版社擔任翻譯，她已經把三十多本童書翻成中文。","h":1},{"w":"be translated into","p":"v.phr.","d":"to be changed into a particular language","c":"被翻譯成…","s":"The Harry Potter books have been translated into more than eighty languages, so children all over the world can enjoy the same story.","t":"《哈利波特》系列已被翻譯成八十多種語言，所以全世界的孩子都能享受同一個故事。","a":"have been translated into"},{"w":"lost in translation","p":"phr.","d":"losing meaning or humor when changed into another language","c":"在翻譯中失真","s":"Many jokes in the movie were lost in translation, so the Taiwanese audience stayed quiet while the American viewers laughed loudly.","t":"電影裡許多笑話在翻譯中失真，所以台灣觀眾安靜地坐著，而美國觀眾卻大聲地笑。"},{"w":"machine translation","p":"n.phr.","d":"translation done automatically by a computer program","c":"機器翻譯","s":"Machine translation is getting better every year, but it still makes funny mistakes with idioms and poems.","t":"機器翻譯每年都在進步，但它在處理成語和詩歌時仍然會犯好笑的錯誤。","a":"Machine translation"},{"w":"transportation","p":"n.","d":"the system of moving people or goods from one place to another","c":"運輸；交通工具","s":"Public transportation in Taipei is so convenient that many families do not feel the need to own a car at all.","t":"台北的大眾運輸非常方便，所以許多家庭完全不覺得需要擁有汽車。","h":1},{"w":"transport","p":"v.","d":"to carry people or goods from one place to another","c":"運送；運輸","s":"Trucks transport fresh fruit from the farms in the south to supermarkets in the north every single night.","t":"卡車每天晚上都把新鮮水果從南部的農場運送到北部的超市。"},{"w":"transport","p":"n.","d":"a vehicle or system for carrying people or goods","c":"交通工具；運輸","s":"The bicycle is still the main form of transport in many small towns because the streets are narrow and parking is hard.","t":"在許多小鎮，腳踏車仍然是主要的交通工具，因為街道狹窄而且停車困難。"},{"w":"public transportation","p":"n.phr.","d":"buses, trains, and other vehicles that everyone can use","c":"大眾運輸","s":"Using public transportation instead of driving saves money and also helps reduce the air pollution in our crowded city.","t":"使用大眾運輸而不是開車可以省錢，也有助於減少我們擁擠城市的空氣污染。"},{"w":"tremble","p":"v.","d":"to shake slightly because you are cold, afraid, or excited","c":"顫抖；發抖","s":"Her hands began to tremble as she opened the envelope, because the letter would tell her whether she had passed the exam.","t":"當她打開信封時，她的手開始顫抖，因為那封信會告訴她是否通過了考試。","h":1},{"w":"tremble","p":"n.","d":"a slight shaking movement","c":"顫抖","s":"There was a tremble in his voice when he thanked the firefighters who had saved his family from the burning house.","t":"當他感謝從燃燒的房子裡救出他家人的消防員時，他的聲音裡帶著一絲顫抖。"},{"w":"tremble with fear","p":"v.phr.","d":"to shake because you are very frightened","c":"害怕得發抖","s":"The little puppy trembled with fear during the thunderstorm, so my sister held it in her arms until the noise stopped.","t":"雷雨期間小狗害怕得發抖，所以我妹妹把牠抱在懷裡直到雷聲停止。","a":"trembled with fear"},{"w":"trembling","p":"adj.","d":"shaking slightly","c":"顫抖的","s":"With trembling fingers, the old man signed the paper that gave his small farm to his youngest daughter.","t":"老人用顫抖的手指簽下文件，把他的小農場交給最小的女兒。"},{"w":"tremendous","p":"adj.","d":"very great in amount, size, or degree","c":"巨大的；極大的","s":"The new MRT line has made a tremendous difference to people in the suburbs, who now reach downtown in twenty minutes.","t":"新的捷運線對郊區居民帶來了巨大的改變，他們現在二十分鐘就能到市中心。","h":1},{"w":"tremendously","p":"adv.","d":"very much; extremely","c":"非常地；極大地","s":"The whole class enjoyed the field trip tremendously, and many students asked whether we could visit the science center again.","t":"全班非常享受這次校外教學，許多學生問我們能不能再去參觀科學中心。"},{"w":"a tremendous amount of","p":"n.phr.","d":"a very large quantity of something","c":"大量的","s":"Preparing for the school fair took a tremendous amount of work, but the smiles on the children's faces made every hour worth it.","t":"為園遊會做準備花了大量的工作，但孩子們臉上的笑容讓每一個小時都值得。"},{"w":"tribal","p":"adj.","d":"connected with a tribe or tribes","c":"部落的；部族的","s":"At the festival, the dancers wore colorful tribal clothing and sang songs that their ancestors had sung for hundreds of years.","t":"在慶典上，舞者穿著色彩繽紛的部落服裝，唱著他們祖先傳唱了數百年的歌曲。","h":1},{"w":"tribe","p":"n.","d":"a group of people with the same language, customs, and leader","c":"部落；部族","s":"The Amis tribe is the largest indigenous group in Taiwan, and its harvest festival attracts many visitors each summer.","t":"阿美族是台灣最大的原住民族群，每年夏天的豐年祭吸引了許多遊客。"},{"w":"tribal culture","p":"n.phr.","d":"the traditions, art, and beliefs of a tribe","c":"部落文化","s":"Our school invited an elder to talk about tribal culture, and he showed us how his people once hunted and built houses.","t":"我們學校邀請一位長老來談部落文化，他向我們展示他的族人過去如何打獵和蓋房子。"},{"w":"triumph","p":"n.","d":"a great success or victory","c":"勝利；成功","s":"Winning the national championship was a great triumph for the small school, which had never reached the final before.","t":"贏得全國冠軍對這所小學校來說是一次偉大的勝利，它以前從未進入過決賽。","h":1},{"w":"triumph","p":"v.","d":"to win a great victory or succeed after a struggle","c":"獲勝；成功","s":"In most fairy tales, kindness and courage triumph in the end, even though the hero faces many dangers along the way.","t":"在大多數童話故事裡，善良和勇氣最後都會獲勝，儘管主角一路上面臨許多危險。"},{"w":"triumph over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to defeat someone or something difficult","c":"戰勝；克服","s":"The young swimmer triumphed over her fear of deep water and finally finished the two-kilometer race in the lake.","t":"這位年輕的游泳選手戰勝了對深水的恐懼，終於完成了湖中兩公里的比賽。","a":"triumphed over"},{"w":"triumphant","p":"adj.","d":"very happy because you have won or succeeded","c":"得意洋洋的；勝利的","s":"The triumphant team ran around the field waving the flag while their parents cheered loudly from the stands.","t":"獲勝的隊伍揮舞著旗幟繞場奔跑，而他們的父母在看台上大聲歡呼。"},{"w":"triumphantly","p":"adv.","d":"in a very happy and proud way after winning","c":"得意洋洋地","s":"After solving the puzzle that nobody else could finish, my little sister held up the paper triumphantly for everyone to see.","t":"解開了沒有人能完成的謎題後，我妹妹得意洋洋地舉起那張紙讓大家看。"},{"w":"troublesome","p":"adj.","d":"causing problems or difficulty","c":"麻煩的；令人困擾的","s":"The old printer in the office is very troublesome because it stops working almost every time we need it most.","t":"辦公室那台舊印表機非常麻煩，因為幾乎每次我們最需要它的時候它就停止運作。","h":1},{"w":"trouble","p":"n.","d":"problems, worry, or difficulty","c":"麻煩；困難","s":"We had some trouble finding the restaurant because the sign was small and the street had no lights at night.","t":"我們找那家餐廳時遇到一些麻煩，因為招牌很小，而且那條街晚上沒有燈。"},{"w":"trouble","p":"v.","d":"to make someone worried or to cause someone difficulty","c":"使煩惱；麻煩","s":"Sorry to trouble you so late, but could you tell me which pages we need to read for tomorrow's history class?","t":"抱歉這麼晚打擾你，但你能告訴我明天歷史課要讀哪幾頁嗎？"},{"w":"in trouble","p":"phr.","d":"in a situation where you may be punished or have problems","c":"有麻煩；惹上麻煩","s":"Tom knew he would be in trouble with his parents when he came home two hours after dinner without calling.","t":"湯姆知道晚餐後兩小時沒打電話就回家，他會惹上父母的麻煩。"},{"w":"troubled","p":"adj.","d":"worried or having many problems","c":"煩惱的；困擾的","s":"She looked troubled all morning, so her best friend finally asked her what was wrong during lunch break.","t":"她整個早上看起來都很煩惱，所以她最好的朋友終於在午休時問她怎麼了。"},{"w":"take the trouble to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a special effort to do something","c":"費心去做；特地去做","s":"Our neighbor took the trouble to water our plants every day while we were traveling, so we brought her a gift from Japan.","t":"我們旅行期間鄰居特地每天幫我們的植物澆水，所以我們從日本帶了禮物給她。","a":"took the trouble to"},{"w":"tumble","p":"v.","d":"to fall suddenly and roll over","c":"跌倒；翻滾","s":"The little boy lost his balance on the wet floor and tumbled down the last three steps, but luckily he was not hurt.","t":"小男孩在濕地板上失去平衡，從最後三階滾了下來，但幸運的是他沒有受傷。","a":"tumbled","h":1},{"w":"tumble","p":"v.","d":"to fall quickly in value or amount","c":"暴跌","s":"Prices of fresh vegetables tumbled after the typhoon season ended, so my mother bought a lot of cabbage last weekend.","t":"颱風季結束後新鮮蔬菜的價格暴跌，所以我媽媽上週末買了很多高麗菜。","a":"tumbled"},{"w":"tumble","p":"n.","d":"a sudden fall","c":"跌倒；摔跤","s":"My grandfather had a bad tumble on the icy road last winter, and he had to use a stick for two months afterwards.","t":"我爺爺去年冬天在結冰的路上重重摔了一跤，之後他必須拄拐杖兩個月。"},{"w":"take a tumble","p":"v.phr.","d":"to fall over; to go down suddenly","c":"跌倒；下跌","s":"The famous actor took a tumble on the stage during the awards show, but he stood up and laughed at himself.","t":"那位知名演員在頒獎典禮的舞台上跌了一跤，但他站起來自嘲地笑了。","a":"took a tumble"},{"w":"twig","p":"n.","d":"a very small, thin branch of a tree or bush","c":"細枝；嫩枝","s":"A twig snapped under my foot as I walked through the forest, and the sound frightened a bird out of the tree.","t":"我走過森林時腳下一根細枝啪地折斷，聲音把一隻鳥從樹上嚇飛了。","h":1},{"w":"dry twigs","p":"n.phr.","d":"small dead branches that burn easily","c":"乾樹枝","s":"We collected dry twigs and leaves to start the campfire, and soon the whole group was warm and roasting sweet potatoes.","t":"我們收集乾樹枝和樹葉來生營火，很快整群人都暖和起來，還烤起了地瓜。"},{"w":"build a nest with twigs","p":"v.phr.","d":"to make a bird's home out of small branches","c":"用細枝築巢","s":"Every spring, the sparrows outside my window build a nest with twigs and grass, and a few weeks later we hear baby birds.","t":"每年春天，我窗外的麻雀會用細枝和草築巢，幾週後我們就會聽到小鳥的叫聲。"},{"w":"universal","p":"adj.","d":"true or existing everywhere or for everyone","c":"普遍的；全體的","s":"Music is often called a universal language because people everywhere can enjoy a beautiful song even without understanding the words.","t":"音樂常被稱為一種世界共通的語言，因為各地的人即使聽不懂歌詞也能欣賞一首美妙的歌。","h":1},{"w":"universe","p":"n.","d":"everything that exists, including all the stars and planets","c":"宇宙","s":"Scientists believe the universe is about fourteen billion years old, and they are still discovering new planets far away.","t":"科學家相信宇宙大約有一百四十億年的歷史，而他們仍在發現遙遠的新行星。"},{"w":"universally","p":"adv.","d":"by everyone; in every case","c":"普遍地；人人皆","s":"The new school lunch menu was universally welcomed by students because it finally included fresh fruit every single day.","t":"新的學校午餐菜單受到學生普遍歡迎，因為它終於每天都有新鮮水果。"},{"w":"university","p":"n.","d":"a place where students study for a degree after high school","c":"大學","s":"My older sister will graduate from university next June, and she hopes to work as an engineer in Hsinchu.","t":"我姐姐明年六月將從大學畢業，她希望在新竹當工程師。"},{"w":"universal truth","p":"n.phr.","d":"something that is true for all people at all times","c":"普世真理","s":"That everyone needs love and respect is a universal truth, no matter where or when a person is born.","t":"每個人都需要愛與尊重是一個普世真理，無論一個人在何時何地出生。"},{"w":"urge","p":"v.","d":"to try hard to persuade someone to do something","c":"敦促；力勸","s":"Doctors urge people to drink more water during the hot summer months, especially when they exercise outdoors.","t":"醫生敦促人們在炎熱的夏季多喝水，特別是在戶外運動時。","h":1},{"w":"urge","p":"n.","d":"a strong wish to do something","c":"衝動；強烈的慾望","s":"Whenever I pass the bakery on my way home, I feel a strong urge to buy a warm loaf of bread.","t":"每當我回家路上經過那家麵包店，我都會有一股想買條熱麵包的強烈衝動。","h":1},{"w":"urge sb to do","p":"v.phr.","d":"to strongly advise someone to do something","c":"力勸某人做…","s":"My teacher urged me to join the speech contest because she thought it would help me become more confident.","t":"我的老師力勸我參加演講比賽，因為她認為那會幫助我變得更有自信。","a":"urged me to"},{"w":"urgent","p":"adj.","d":"needing to be dealt with immediately","c":"緊急的；迫切的","s":"The nurse said the message was urgent, so the doctor left the meeting right away to see the patient.","t":"護士說那則訊息很緊急，所以醫生立刻離開會議去看病人。"},{"w":"urgently","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that needs immediate action","c":"緊急地；迫切地","s":"The hospital urgently needs blood donors of all types after the bus accident on the highway this morning.","t":"今天早上高速公路發生公車事故後，醫院急需各種血型的捐血者。"},{"w":"urgency","p":"n.","d":"the need to act quickly","c":"緊急；迫切","s":"There was a sense of urgency in her voice when she called to say that the river was rising near her house.","t":"她打電話說她家附近的河水正在上漲時，聲音裡帶著一種急迫感。"},{"w":"feel an urge to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to have a strong sudden wish to do something","c":"有股衝動想…","s":"During the long, boring lecture, I felt an urge to stand up and open the window just to feel the fresh air.","t":"在那堂又長又無聊的講課中，我有股衝動想站起來打開窗戶，只為了感受新鮮空氣。","a":"felt an urge to"},{"w":"usage","p":"n.","d":"the way in which words are used in a language","c":"用法","s":"This dictionary gives clear examples of word usage, so students can see how each new word is used in a real sentence.","t":"這本字典提供清楚的單字用法範例，所以學生可以看到每個新單字在真實句子中如何使用。","h":1},{"w":"usage","p":"n.","d":"the amount of something that is used","c":"使用量","s":"Our water usage went up a lot last month because my cousins stayed with us and took long showers every day.","t":"我們上個月的用水量增加了很多，因為表兄弟姐妹住在我們家，每天都洗很久的澡。"},{"w":"use","p":"v.","d":"to do something with a tool or thing for a purpose","c":"使用","s":"You may use a dictionary during the writing test, but phones and tablets must stay inside your bags.","t":"寫作測驗期間你可以使用字典，但手機和平板必須放在書包裡。"},{"w":"use","p":"n.","d":"the act of using something; a purpose for something","c":"使用；用途","s":"The old gym is not in use anymore, so the school plans to turn it into a library with comfortable reading corners.","t":"舊體育館已經不再使用了，所以學校打算把它改成一座有舒適閱讀角落的圖書館。"},{"w":"useful","p":"adj.","d":"helpful for a purpose","c":"有用的","s":"A small flashlight is very useful during a typhoon because the power often goes out for several hours.","t":"小手電筒在颱風期間非常有用，因為電力常常會中斷好幾個小時。"},{"w":"useless","p":"adj.","d":"not helpful at all","c":"沒用的；無用的","s":"The umbrella was useless in the strong wind, so we were completely wet by the time we reached the bus stop.","t":"在強風中那把傘毫無用處，所以我們到公車站時已經全身濕透。"},{"w":"make use of","p":"v.phr.","d":"to use something that is available","c":"利用","s":"Smart students make use of the ten-minute breaks between classes to review the words they have just learned.","t":"聰明的學生利用課間十分鐘的休息時間複習剛學到的單字。"}]},{"unit":40,"theme":"vacancy – youthful","cards":[{"w":"vacancy","p":"n.","d":"a job or a room that is available for someone to take","c":"空缺；空房","s":"The hotel near the beach had only one vacancy left for the holiday weekend, so we booked the room right away.","t":"海邊那家飯店在連假週末只剩一間空房，所以我們立刻就訂了那個房間。","h":1},{"w":"vacancy","p":"n.","d":"a job that nobody is doing and needs to be filled","c":"職缺","s":"There is a vacancy for a part-time English tutor at the community center, and the pay is quite good for students.","t":"社區中心有一個兼職英文家教的職缺，對學生來說薪水相當不錯。"},{"w":"vacant","p":"adj.","d":"empty; not being used or lived in","c":"空著的；閒置的","s":"The seat next to the window was vacant, so I quickly sat down before the bus became crowded again.","t":"靠窗的座位是空的，所以我在公車再度擁擠之前趕快坐了下來。"},{"w":"fill a vacancy","p":"v.phr.","d":"to give an empty job or place to someone","c":"填補空缺","s":"The school needs to fill a vacancy in the music department before September, or the students will have no band teacher.","t":"學校需要在九月前填補音樂科的空缺，否則學生就沒有樂隊老師了。"},{"w":"vain","p":"adj.","d":"too proud of your own looks or abilities","c":"自負的；愛虛榮的","s":"My cousin is so vain that he checks his hair in every shop window we pass on the way to school.","t":"我表哥非常自戀，我們上學途中經過的每扇商店櫥窗他都要照一照頭髮。","h":1},{"w":"vain","p":"adj.","d":"not producing the result you want; useless","c":"徒勞的；無效的","s":"The firefighters made a vain attempt to save the old wooden temple, but the flames were already too strong.","t":"消防員做了徒勞的嘗試想救那座古老的木造寺廟，但火勢已經太猛了。"},{"w":"in vain","p":"phr.","d":"without success; for no result","c":"徒勞地；白費地","s":"We waited at the station for two hours in vain, because the last train had been canceled due to the typhoon.","t":"我們在車站白白等了兩個小時，因為最後一班火車已經因颱風取消了。"},{"w":"vanity","p":"n.","d":"too much pride in your own appearance or importance","c":"虛榮心；自負","s":"Her vanity made her spend half of her salary on designer clothes just to look better than her coworkers.","t":"她的虛榮心讓她把一半薪水花在名牌衣服上，只為了看起來比同事好。"},{"w":"vast","p":"adj.","d":"extremely large in size, amount, or area","c":"廣闊的；巨大的","s":"From the top of the mountain, we could see a vast forest that seemed to stretch all the way to the ocean.","t":"從山頂上，我們可以看到一片廣闊的森林，似乎一路延伸到海邊。","h":1},{"w":"vastly","p":"adv.","d":"very much; to a great degree","c":"極大地；非常","s":"Living in a small town is vastly different from living in Taipei, where the shops stay open until late at night.","t":"住在小鎮和住在台北非常不同，台北的商店開到深夜。"},{"w":"the vast majority of","p":"n.phr.","d":"almost all of a group","c":"絕大多數的","s":"The vast majority of students in our class ride the bus to school, while only three or four come by bicycle every day.","t":"我們班絕大多數的學生搭公車上學，每天只有三四個人騎腳踏車來。","a":"The vast majority of"},{"w":"vegetarian","p":"n.","d":"a person who does not eat meat or fish","c":"素食者","s":"My aunt has been a vegetarian for ten years, so she always orders tofu and vegetables when we eat out together.","t":"我阿姨吃素已經十年了，所以我們一起外食時她總是點豆腐和蔬菜，她是個素食者。","h":1},{"w":"vegetarian","p":"adj.","d":"containing no meat or fish; not eating meat","c":"素食的","s":"The restaurant offers several vegetarian dishes, and even my brother, who loves meat, said the mushroom noodles were delicious.","t":"那家餐廳提供好幾道素食料理，連愛吃肉的哥哥都說香菇麵很好吃。"},{"w":"vegetable","p":"n.","d":"a plant or part of a plant that is eaten as food","c":"蔬菜","s":"Doctors say we should eat at least three kinds of vegetables every day, so my mother always adds broccoli to dinner.","t":"醫生說我們每天應該至少吃三種蔬菜，所以我媽媽晚餐總是加青花菜。","a":"vegetables"},{"w":"vegan","p":"n.","d":"a person who eats no animal products at all, including eggs and milk","c":"純素食者","s":"A vegan does not eat eggs or cheese either, so my friend brought her own snacks to the birthday party.","t":"純素食者連蛋和起司也不吃，所以我朋友自己帶了點心去生日派對。"},{"w":"vessel","p":"n.","d":"a large boat or ship","c":"船艦；船隻","s":"A fishing vessel with twelve people on board was caught in the storm, but the coast guard rescued everyone safely.","t":"一艘載著十二人的漁船被暴風雨困住，但海巡人員安全地救出了所有人。","h":1},{"w":"vessel","p":"n.","d":"a container for holding liquids","c":"容器；器皿","s":"The museum displays a bronze vessel that was used to hold wine more than two thousand years ago.","t":"博物館展出一件兩千多年前用來盛酒的青銅器皿。"},{"w":"blood vessel","p":"n.phr.","d":"one of the tubes that carry blood through your body","c":"血管","s":"Smoking damages every blood vessel in your body, which is why doctors keep telling people to quit as soon as possible.","t":"吸菸會損害你身體裡的每一條血管，這就是為什麼醫生一直勸人儘快戒菸。"},{"w":"violate","p":"v.","d":"to break a law, rule, or agreement","c":"違反；違背","s":"Drivers who violate the speed limit near the school will receive a heavy fine and lose points on their license.","t":"在學校附近違反速限的駕駛將被重罰，駕照也會被扣點。","h":1},{"w":"violation","p":"n.","d":"an action that breaks a law or rule","c":"違反；違規","s":"Parking on the sidewalk is a traffic violation, and the police gave out more than fifty tickets on our street last month.","t":"在人行道上停車是一種交通違規，上個月警察在我們這條街開了五十多張罰單。","h":1},{"w":"violate the rules","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do something that the rules do not allow","c":"違反規定","s":"Any player who violates the rules during the tournament will be sent off the court immediately, no matter how famous he is.","t":"比賽期間任何違反規定的球員都會立刻被趕出球場，不管他多有名。","a":"violates the rules"},{"w":"violence","p":"n.","d":"actions that hurt or kill people","c":"暴力","s":"The movie contains a lot of violence, so parents are advised not to bring children under twelve to the cinema.","t":"這部電影包含大量暴力場面，所以建議家長不要帶十二歲以下的孩子進戲院。"},{"w":"violent","p":"adj.","d":"using force to hurt people; very strong and sudden","c":"暴力的；猛烈的","s":"A violent storm hit the island last night, pulling trees out of the ground and breaking windows all over town.","t":"昨晚一場猛烈的暴風雨襲擊了這座島，把樹連根拔起，打破了全鎮的窗戶。"},{"w":"violently","p":"adv.","d":"with great force; in a way that hurts people","c":"猛烈地；暴力地","s":"The small boat rocked violently in the waves, and several passengers held on to the rails with both hands.","t":"小船在海浪中猛烈地搖晃，好幾位乘客用雙手緊抓著欄杆。"},{"w":"virtue","p":"n.","d":"a good quality in a person's character, such as honesty","c":"美德；優點","s":"Honesty is a virtue my grandfather valued above all others, and he never told a lie even to save money.","t":"誠實是我爺爺最重視的美德，他從不說謊，即使是為了省錢。","h":1},{"w":"virtue","p":"n.","d":"an advantage or good point of something","c":"優點；長處","s":"The main virtue of this phone is its long battery life, which lasts two full days without charging.","t":"這支手機主要的優點是電池續航力長，不充電可以用整整兩天。"},{"w":"virtuous","p":"adj.","d":"behaving in a very honest and moral way","c":"有道德的；品行端正的","s":"In the old story, the virtuous farmer returns the gold he finds, and the king rewards him with a piece of land.","t":"在那個古老的故事裡，品行端正的農夫歸還了他撿到的黃金，國王賞給他一塊土地。"},{"w":"patience is a virtue","p":"phr.","d":"a saying that means waiting calmly is a good quality","c":"耐心是一種美德","s":"Whenever I complain about the long line at the bank, my mother smiles and reminds me that patience is a virtue.","t":"每當我抱怨銀行的隊伍太長，我媽媽就微笑著提醒我耐心是一種美德。"},{"w":"virus","p":"n.","d":"a very small living thing that causes disease","c":"病毒","s":"The doctor said the virus spreads through coughing, so everyone in the office should wear a mask this week.","t":"醫生說這種病毒會透過咳嗽傳播，所以辦公室裡的每個人這週都應該戴口罩。","h":1},{"w":"computer virus","p":"n.phr.","d":"a program that damages a computer or steals information","c":"電腦病毒","s":"My laptop became very slow after I opened a strange email, and the repair shop found a computer virus inside.","t":"我打開一封奇怪的電子郵件後筆電變得很慢，維修店發現裡面有電腦病毒。"},{"w":"viral","p":"adj.","d":"caused by a virus; spreading very fast on the internet","c":"病毒的；瘋傳的","s":"The viral video of the dancing grandmother was watched by ten million people in just three days.","t":"那支跳舞奶奶的瘋傳影片在短短三天內就有一千萬人觀看。"},{"w":"go viral","p":"v.phr.","d":"to spread very quickly on the internet","c":"在網路上瘋傳","s":"The photo of the cat sleeping on the police car went viral within hours, and even the news channels showed it.","t":"那張貓咪睡在警車上的照片幾小時內就在網路上瘋傳，連新聞台都播出了。","a":"went viral"},{"w":"visual","p":"adj.","d":"connected with seeing or sight","c":"視覺的","s":"Charts and pictures give visual support to a speech, so the audience can understand the numbers much more easily.","t":"圖表和圖片為演講提供視覺上的輔助，讓聽眾更容易理解那些數字。","h":1},{"w":"visual aids","p":"n.phr.","d":"pictures, videos, or objects used to help explain something","c":"視覺教具","s":"Our teacher uses visual aids such as maps and short videos, which make the history lessons far more interesting.","t":"我們老師使用地圖和短片等視覺教具，讓歷史課有趣多了。"},{"w":"vision","p":"n.","d":"the ability to see; an idea of what the future could be like","c":"視力；願景","s":"My grandfather's vision is getting worse, so he now needs stronger glasses to read the newspaper every morning.","t":"我爺爺的視力越來越差，所以他現在每天早上需要更厚的眼鏡才能看報紙。"},{"w":"visible","p":"adj.","d":"able to be seen","c":"看得見的；可見的","s":"On a clear night, thousands of stars are visible from the mountain village because there are no city lights nearby.","t":"在晴朗的夜晚，從山村裡看得見成千上萬顆星星，因為附近沒有城市的燈光。"},{"w":"visualize","p":"v.","d":"to form a picture of something in your mind","c":"想像；在腦海中描繪","s":"Before the race, the swimmer closed her eyes to visualize every turn in the pool and the moment she touched the wall.","t":"比賽前，那位游泳選手閉上眼睛在腦海中描繪泳池裡的每一次轉身和她觸壁的那一刻。"},{"w":"vital","p":"adj.","d":"extremely important and necessary","c":"極重要的；不可或缺的","s":"Clean drinking water is vital for the villagers, so the volunteers spent the whole summer building a new well.","t":"乾淨的飲用水對村民來說至關重要，所以志工們花了整個夏天建造一口新井。","h":1},{"w":"vitally","p":"adv.","d":"in a way that is extremely important","c":"極其；至關重要地","s":"It is vitally important to wear a helmet when you ride a scooter, because most head injuries happen in small accidents.","t":"騎機車時戴安全帽極其重要，因為大多數頭部傷害都發生在小事故中。"},{"w":"vitality","p":"n.","d":"energy and strength","c":"活力；生命力","s":"Even at eighty, my grandmother is full of vitality; she walks in the park every morning and dances on weekends.","t":"即使八十歲了，我奶奶仍然充滿活力；她每天早上在公園散步，週末還去跳舞。"},{"w":"vitamin","p":"n.","d":"a natural substance in food that your body needs to stay healthy","c":"維他命；維生素","s":"Oranges are rich in vitamin C, which is why my mother gives me one every morning during the cold winter months.","t":"柳橙富含維他命C，這就是為什麼在寒冷的冬天我媽媽每天早上給我一顆。"},{"w":"voluntary","p":"adj.","d":"done because you want to, not because you are forced or paid","c":"自願的；志願的","s":"Joining the weekend beach cleanup is completely voluntary, but more than half of our class decided to take part.","t":"參加週末淨灘活動完全是自願的，但我們班有超過一半的人決定參加。","h":1},{"w":"volunteer","p":"n.","d":"a person who works without pay to help others","c":"志工；義工","s":"After the earthquake, hundreds of volunteers arrived from all over the island to hand out food, water, and blankets.","t":"地震後，數百名志工從全島各地趕來發放食物、飲水和毛毯。","a":"volunteers","h":1},{"w":"volunteer","p":"v.","d":"to offer to do something without being asked or paid","c":"自願；志願","s":"Nobody wanted to clean the fish tank, so my little sister surprised everyone when she decided to volunteer for the job.","t":"沒有人想清理魚缸，所以當我妹妹決定自願做這件事時，大家都很驚訝。"},{"w":"volunteer to do","p":"v.phr.","d":"to offer to do a task without being forced","c":"自願去做…","s":"When the teacher asked who could carry the heavy boxes, Kevin volunteered to help even though he had hurt his arm last week.","t":"當老師問誰能搬那些重箱子時，凱文自願幫忙，即使他上週傷了手臂。","a":"volunteered to"},{"w":"voluntarily","p":"adv.","d":"by choice, without being forced","c":"自願地","s":"The company said the workers left voluntarily, but many of them told reporters that they had been pushed out.","t":"公司說那些員工是自願離開的，但他們當中許多人告訴記者他們是被逼走的。"},{"w":"volunteer work","p":"n.phr.","d":"unpaid work done to help people or the community","c":"志工服務","s":"Doing volunteer work at the animal shelter taught my brother more about responsibility than any lesson at school.","t":"在動物收容所做志工服務教會了我弟弟更多關於責任的事，勝過學校的任何一堂課。"},{"w":"voyage","p":"n.","d":"a long journey, especially by sea or in space","c":"航行；航程","s":"The voyage from England to Australia took almost three months in the old days, and many sailors became ill on the way.","t":"在過去，從英國到澳洲的航程需要將近三個月，許多水手在途中生病。","h":1},{"w":"voyage","p":"v.","d":"to travel a long way by sea or in space","c":"航行","s":"Hundreds of years ago, brave explorers voyaged across unknown oceans without maps, trusting only the stars above them.","t":"數百年前，勇敢的探險家在沒有地圖的情況下航行越過未知的海洋，只靠頭頂的星星指引。","a":"voyaged"},{"w":"maiden voyage","p":"n.phr.","d":"the first journey of a new ship","c":"處女航；首航","s":"The Titanic sank on its maiden voyage in 1912, and the story of that night is still told in books and movies today.","t":"鐵達尼號在一九一二年的處女航中沉沒，那一夜的故事至今仍在書籍和電影中流傳。"},{"w":"Bon voyage!","p":"phr.","d":"a way of wishing someone a good journey","c":"一路順風！","s":"My whole family came to the airport, hugged me tightly, and shouted \"Bon voyage\" as I walked toward the gate.","t":"我全家人都來到機場，緊緊抱住我，在我走向登機門時大喊「一路順風」。","a":"Bon voyage"},{"w":"waken","p":"v.","d":"to wake up, or to make someone wake up","c":"醒來；喚醒","s":"The loud thunder was enough to waken the whole family at three in the morning, and nobody could fall asleep again.","t":"巨大的雷聲足以在凌晨三點喚醒全家人，之後沒有人能再睡著。","h":1},{"w":"wake, woke, woken","p":"v.","d":"to stop sleeping","c":"醒來；叫醒","s":"I usually wake at six on school days, but on Sundays I love to stay in bed until almost ten.","t":"上學日我通常六點醒來，但星期天我喜歡賴床到將近十點。","a":"wake"},{"w":"wake up","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stop sleeping; to make someone stop sleeping","c":"醒來；叫醒","s":"Please wake up your brother before seven, because the school bus will not wait for him again this week.","t":"請在七點前叫醒你弟弟，因為這週校車不會再等他了。"},{"w":"awake","p":"adj.","d":"not sleeping","c":"醒著的","s":"The baby was still awake at midnight, so her tired parents took turns singing softly until she finally closed her eyes.","t":"午夜時寶寶還醒著，所以她疲倦的父母輪流輕聲唱歌，直到她終於閉上眼睛。"},{"w":"awaken","p":"v.","d":"to wake up; to make someone feel something for the first time","c":"喚醒；使覺醒","s":"The trip to the mountains helped awaken my interest in birds, and now I carry a small guidebook everywhere I go.","t":"那趟山區之旅喚醒了我對鳥類的興趣，現在我走到哪裡都帶著一本小圖鑑。"},{"w":"website","p":"n.","d":"a set of pages on the internet about a person, company, or subject","c":"網站","s":"The school website shows the exam schedule and the lunch menu, so parents can check everything from their phones.","t":"學校網站上有考試時程和午餐菜單，所以家長可以用手機查看所有資訊。","h":1},{"w":"web","p":"n.","d":"the system of connected pages on the internet; a net made by a spider","c":"網路；蜘蛛網","s":"My grandmother learned to search the web for recipes last year, and now she tries a new dish every weekend.","t":"我奶奶去年學會上網搜尋食譜，現在她每個週末都嘗試一道新菜。"},{"w":"web page","p":"n.phr.","d":"one page of information on a website","c":"網頁","s":"This web page takes a long time to load because it contains too many large photos and videos.","t":"這個網頁載入要很久，因為它包含太多大型照片和影片。"},{"w":"browse a website","p":"v.phr.","d":"to look through the pages of a website","c":"瀏覽網站","s":"Instead of doing his homework, my brother spent the whole evening browsing a website that sells video games and comic books.","t":"我弟弟沒有做功課，而是花了整個晚上瀏覽一個賣電玩和漫畫的網站。","a":"browsing a website"},{"w":"welfare","p":"n.","d":"the health, comfort, and happiness of a person or group","c":"福利；幸福","s":"A good teacher cares about the welfare of every student, not only about their test scores at the end of the term.","t":"好老師關心每個學生的幸福，而不只是他們期末的考試成績。","h":1},{"w":"welfare","p":"n.","d":"money given by the government to people who are poor or cannot work","c":"社會福利金","s":"After losing his job in the factory, the man lived on welfare for a year until he found work as a driver.","t":"在工廠失業後，那名男子靠社會福利金生活了一年，直到找到司機的工作。"},{"w":"social welfare","p":"n.phr.","d":"government services that help people in need","c":"社會福利","s":"The city spends a large part of its budget on social welfare, including free lunches for children from poor families.","t":"這座城市將大部分預算用於社會福利，包括為貧困家庭的孩子提供免費午餐。"},{"w":"animal welfare","p":"n.phr.","d":"the protection of animals' health and happiness","c":"動物福利","s":"The new law on animal welfare says that dogs must not be kept on short chains outside all day in the hot sun.","t":"新的動物福利法規定，狗不能整天被用短鏈拴在外面的烈日下。"},{"w":"wink","p":"v.","d":"to close one eye quickly as a friendly or secret signal","c":"眨眼示意","s":"Grandpa likes to wink at me whenever he slips an extra cookie onto my plate when Grandma is not looking.","t":"每當奶奶沒注意時，爺爺偷偷多放一塊餅乾到我盤子裡，他就喜歡對我眨眼。","h":1},{"w":"wink","p":"n.","d":"the act of closing one eye quickly as a signal","c":"眨眼","s":"The waiter gave me a quick wink to show that the birthday cake was ready and hidden in the kitchen.","t":"服務生對我快速眨了一下眼，表示生日蛋糕已經準備好並藏在廚房裡。"},{"w":"wink at","p":"v.phr.","d":"to close one eye quickly to signal to someone","c":"對…眨眼","s":"The actor winked at the camera at the end of the movie, as if he were sharing a secret with every person watching.","t":"電影結尾時那位演員對鏡頭眨眼，彷彿在和每位觀眾分享一個秘密。","a":"winked at"},{"w":"not sleep a wink","p":"v.phr.","d":"to not sleep at all","c":"完全沒睡","s":"I did not sleep a wink last night because the dog next door barked until sunrise, and now I can barely keep my eyes open.","t":"我昨晚完全沒睡，因為隔壁的狗一直叫到天亮，現在我幾乎睜不開眼睛。","a":"did not sleep a wink"},{"w":"wit","p":"n.","d":"the ability to say clever and funny things","c":"機智；風趣","s":"The host of the show is famous for his quick wit, and he can turn any awkward moment into a joke within seconds.","t":"那個節目的主持人以反應快速的機智聞名，他能在幾秒內把任何尷尬的時刻變成笑話。","h":1},{"w":"witty","p":"adj.","d":"clever and funny","c":"機智的；詼諧的","s":"Her witty reply made the whole class laugh, and even the strict teacher could not hide her smile.","t":"她機智的回答讓全班大笑，連嚴格的老師都藏不住笑容。"},{"w":"keep one's wits about one","p":"v.phr.","d":"to stay calm and think clearly in a difficult situation","c":"保持冷靜機警","s":"When the elevator suddenly stopped between floors, the young nurse kept her wits about her and calmly pressed the emergency button.","t":"當電梯突然停在樓層之間時，那位年輕護士保持冷靜機警，沉著地按下緊急按鈕。","a":"kept her wits about her"},{"w":"at one's wits' end","p":"phr.","d":"so worried that you do not know what to do next","c":"束手無策；不知所措","s":"After the baby cried for three hours straight, the new parents were at their wits' end and finally called the doctor.","t":"寶寶連續哭了三個小時後，新手父母束手無策，最後打電話給醫生。","a":"at their wits' end"},{"w":"witch","p":"n.","d":"a woman in stories who has magic powers","c":"女巫","s":"In the fairy tale, the witch lives deep in the forest and turns lost children into animals with a wave of her hand.","t":"在童話故事裡，那個女巫住在森林深處，揮揮手就把迷路的孩子變成動物。","h":1},{"w":"wizard","p":"n.","d":"a man in stories who has magic powers","c":"巫師；魔法師","s":"The old wizard with the long white beard taught the young boy how to use his magic wand carefully and wisely.","t":"那位留著長白鬍子的老巫師教小男孩如何小心而明智地使用魔杖。","h":1},{"w":"witchcraft","p":"n.","d":"the use of magic powers, especially evil ones","c":"巫術","s":"Hundreds of years ago, many innocent women were punished for witchcraft simply because they knew how to use herbs as medicine.","t":"數百年前，許多無辜的女性僅僅因為懂得用草藥治病，就被以巫術的罪名處罰。"},{"w":"a wizard at","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is extremely good at something","c":"…的高手","s":"My classmate is a wizard at math, so everyone asks him for help the night before every important test.","t":"我同學是數學高手，所以每次重要考試的前一晚，大家都找他幫忙。"},{"w":"withdraw, withdrew, withdrawn","p":"v.","d":"to take money out of a bank account","c":"提款；提取","s":"I need to withdraw some cash from the ATM before we go to the night market, because most stands do not take cards.","t":"我們去夜市前我需要從提款機提一些現金，因為大多數攤位不收信用卡。","a":"withdraw","h":1},{"w":"withdraw, withdrew, withdrawn","p":"v.","d":"to stop taking part in something; to move back or away","c":"退出；撤回；撤退","s":"The injured runner had to withdraw from the marathon after only ten kilometers, which made her very disappointed.","t":"那位受傷的跑者在跑了十公里後就不得不退出馬拉松，這讓她非常失望。","a":"withdraw"},{"w":"withdraw from","p":"v.phr.","d":"to leave or stop taking part in an activity or place","c":"退出；從…撤離","s":"Our school team decided to withdraw from the competition because two of the best players were sick with the flu.","t":"我們校隊決定退出比賽，因為兩名最好的球員得了流感。"},{"w":"withdrawal","p":"n.","d":"the act of taking money out; the act of leaving or stopping","c":"提款；撤回；退出","s":"The bank sends a text message to your phone after every withdrawal, so you will know at once if someone uses your card.","t":"銀行在每次提款後都會傳簡訊到你的手機，所以如果有人使用你的卡，你會立刻知道。"},{"w":"withdrawn","p":"adj.","d":"very quiet and not wanting to talk to people","c":"沉默寡言的；孤僻的","s":"After his best friend moved away, the boy became withdrawn and spent most of his lunch breaks reading alone.","t":"在他最好的朋友搬走後，那個男孩變得沉默寡言，大部分的午休時間都獨自看書。"},{"w":"witness","p":"n.","d":"a person who sees an event happen, especially a crime or accident","c":"目擊者；證人","s":"The police are looking for a witness who saw the white car hit the bicycle and then drive away without stopping.","t":"警方正在尋找一位看到白色汽車撞上腳踏車然後逃逸的目擊者。","h":1},{"w":"witness","p":"v.","d":"to see something happen, especially an accident or crime","c":"目擊；親眼看見","s":"Thousands of people gathered on the beach to witness the first sunrise of the new year over the Pacific Ocean.","t":"數千人聚集在海灘上親眼目睹新年第一道從太平洋升起的曙光。"},{"w":"eyewitness","p":"n.","d":"a person who actually saw something happen","c":"目擊證人","s":"According to an eyewitness, the fire started in the kitchen of the restaurant shortly after the last customers left.","t":"根據一位目擊證人的說法，火災是在最後一批客人離開後不久從餐廳的廚房開始的。"},{"w":"bear witness to","p":"v.phr.","d":"to show that something is true or happened","c":"證明；見證","s":"The empty shelves in the supermarket bore witness to how worried people were before the typhoon arrived.","t":"超市裡空蕩蕩的貨架見證了颱風來臨前人們有多麼擔心。","a":"bore witness to"},{"w":"workout","p":"n.","d":"a period of physical exercise","c":"運動；鍛鍊","s":"My father does a thirty-minute workout every morning before breakfast, and he says it gives him energy for the whole day.","t":"我爸爸每天早餐前做三十分鐘的運動，他說這讓他一整天都有精神。","h":1},{"w":"work out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to do physical exercise","c":"健身；運動","s":"She likes to work out at the gym after school because lifting weights helps her forget the stress of exams.","t":"她喜歡放學後去健身房健身，因為舉重能幫她忘掉考試的壓力。"},{"w":"work out","p":"v.phr.","d":"to find the answer to a problem; to happen in a successful way","c":"解決；算出；順利進行","s":"It took me twenty minutes to work out the last math problem, but I felt wonderful when I finally got the right answer.","t":"我花了二十分鐘才算出最後一道數學題，但當我終於得到正確答案時，感覺好極了。"},{"w":"workplace","p":"n.","d":"the place where people work, such as an office or factory","c":"工作場所；職場","s":"A friendly workplace makes people want to stay in their jobs, so the company planted trees and built a small café for its staff.","t":"友善的工作環境讓員工願意留在崗位上，所以公司為員工種了樹並建了一間小咖啡廳。","h":1},{"w":"in the workplace","p":"phr.","d":"at work; in places where people work","c":"在職場上","s":"Good communication skills are highly valued in the workplace, which is why our school now offers a public speaking class.","t":"良好的溝通技巧在職場上備受重視，這就是為什麼我們學校現在開設公開演講課。"},{"w":"workforce","p":"n.","d":"all the people who work in a company or country","c":"勞動力；全體員工","s":"Nearly half of the factory's workforce is made up of women, and the company provides a daycare center for their children.","t":"這家工廠近一半的員工是女性，公司為她們的孩子提供托兒中心。"},{"w":"workload","p":"n.","d":"the amount of work a person has to do","c":"工作量","s":"The nurses complained that their workload had doubled during the winter, when many elderly patients caught the flu.","t":"護士們抱怨冬天她們的工作量增加了一倍，因為許多年長病患得了流感。"},{"w":"wreck","p":"n.","d":"a ship, car, or plane that has been badly damaged","c":"殘骸；失事的船或車","s":"Divers found the wreck of a ship that sank near the island more than two hundred years ago, with old coins still inside.","t":"潛水員發現了一艘兩百多年前在島嶼附近沉沒的船的殘骸，裡面還有古老的錢幣。","h":1},{"w":"wreck","p":"v.","d":"to destroy or badly damage something","c":"毀壞；破壞","s":"The typhoon came so suddenly that it managed to wreck dozens of fishing boats before they could return to the harbor.","t":"颱風來得太突然，在幾十艘漁船回到港口之前就把它們摧毀了。"},{"w":"wreckage","p":"n.","d":"the broken parts of something that has been destroyed","c":"殘骸；碎片","s":"Rescue workers searched the wreckage of the fallen building all night and pulled out five people alive.","t":"救難人員整夜搜尋倒塌建築的殘骸，救出了五名生還者。"},{"w":"shipwreck","p":"n.","d":"an accident in which a ship is destroyed at sea; the destroyed ship","c":"船難；沉船","s":"The only survivor of the shipwreck floated on a wooden door for two days before a fishing boat finally found him.","t":"那場船難唯一的生還者抱著一扇木門漂了兩天，一艘漁船才終於發現他。"},{"w":"a nervous wreck","p":"n.phr.","d":"a person who is extremely worried or nervous","c":"緊張得不得了的人","s":"Before the big piano competition, my sister was a nervous wreck and could not eat anything for breakfast.","t":"大型鋼琴比賽前，我姐姐緊張得不得了，早餐什麼都吃不下。"},{"w":"yawn","p":"v.","d":"to open your mouth wide and breathe in because you are tired or bored","c":"打哈欠","s":"The students began to yawn one after another during the long speech, and some of them nearly fell asleep.","t":"在那場冗長的演講中，學生們一個接一個開始打哈欠，有些人幾乎睡著了。","h":1},{"w":"yawn","p":"n.","d":"the act of opening your mouth wide because you are tired","c":"哈欠","s":"With a big yawn, my father put down his newspaper and said it was time for everyone to go to bed.","t":"我爸爸打了個大哈欠，放下報紙說大家該睡覺了。"},{"w":"stifle a yawn","p":"v.phr.","d":"to try to stop yourself from yawning","c":"忍住哈欠","s":"I tried to stifle a yawn during the meeting, but my boss noticed and asked whether I had stayed up too late again.","t":"開會時我試著忍住哈欠，但老闆注意到了，問我是不是又熬夜了。"},{"w":"youthful","p":"adj.","d":"young, or seeming young and full of energy","c":"年輕的；青春的","s":"Although my grandmother is seventy, she has a youthful smile and still goes hiking with her friends every Saturday.","t":"雖然我奶奶七十歲了，她仍有年輕的笑容，每個星期六還和朋友去爬山。","h":1},{"w":"youth","p":"n.","d":"the time of life when a person is young","c":"青年時期","s":"In his youth, my grandfather worked on a fishing boat, and he still tells us stories about storms at sea.","t":"我爺爺年輕時在漁船上工作，他至今仍會跟我們講海上暴風雨的故事。"},{"w":"youth","p":"n.","d":"young people as a group","c":"年輕人；青年","s":"The new sports center was built for the youth of the town, so teenagers finally have a safe place to play basketball at night.","t":"新的運動中心是為鎮上的年輕人建造的，所以青少年終於有一個晚上打籃球的安全場所。"},{"w":"in one's youth","p":"phr.","d":"when a person was young","c":"在某人年輕時","s":"My mother was a talented singer in her youth, and she still sings beautifully at every family party.","t":"我媽媽年輕時是個有才華的歌手，現在每次家庭聚會她仍然唱得很動聽。","a":"in her youth"}]}];
